INSERT INTO `assignment_questions` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question`, `mark`, `updated_at`, `created_at`, `created_by`, `updated_by`) VALUES
(1, 22, 'Summarize the Patriarch Era, including how, where, and when it started.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(2, 22, 'Discuss the implications of the call of Abraham. How can Abraham?s call to leave his home to go to a new land be seen\r\nas a microcosm of the will of God for all mankind?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(3, 22, 'Describe the Abrahamic Covenant, including its contents, its establishment, and its sign.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(4, 22, 'Someone has stated that the Abrahamic Covenant is the ?glue that holds the Old Testament together.? Explain this\r\nstatement.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(6, 20, 'In your opinion, which of the four theories about the ?day? of Genesis 1 is correct? Explain.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(7, 20, 'Explain the differences in Genesis 1 and Genesis 2, concerning the Creation.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(8, 20, 'What was different in God?s creating procedures when He created man? Explain.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(9, 20, 'Explain the Law of Causality. How does this law support Creationism? Explain.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(10, 1, 'How did the Babylonian captivity influence the Jews? center of worship? Explain.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(11, 1, 'Identify and give the approximate dates of the six major periods in the intertestamental time period\r\nof Israel?s history.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(12, 1, 'Explain how God used the Persians to restore historic Judaism.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(13, 1, 'Who was Maccabeus and how did his leadership reestablish historic Judaism in Jerusalem?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(14, 15, 'The Gospel of John is unique in its presentation of Jesus? genealogy. How?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(15, 15, 'How does the Gospel of John prepare the reader for the Book of Acts? Explain.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(16, 15, 'Discuss the following issues about the Gospel of John:\r\na. Date of writing\r\nb. Location of writing\r\nc. Audience to whom he was writing', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(17, 15, 'How was the Pentecostal movement influenced by the Gospel of John? Include some of the themes\r\nin the Gospel of John which have influenced the Pentecostals? doctrine.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(18, 11, 'In the second division of the Gospel of Mark, discuss the gospel of power. What two themes are found\r\nin the parable of the sower, contained in this division?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(19, 11, 'Discuss the third division of the Gospel of Mark: The Power of Suffering. What are the three\r\npredictions of Jesus? death found within this division?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(20, 11, 'Discuss the passion narrative found in the third division of Mark?s Gospel.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(21, 11, 'Discuss the fourth division of the Gospel of Mark: When the End Is Only the Beginning.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(22, 24, 'Give the structure of the Book of Acts, including the scripture divisions.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(23, 24, 'Give four purposes for the Book of Acts.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(24, 24, 'What is the theme of the Book of Acts? Give a reference to support your answer.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(25, 24, 'Give four reasons why the Book of Acts is important.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(26, 2, 'Define Hellenization and describe its origin in Israel and its influences at the time of Christ.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(27, 2, 'The Jewish people resisted Hellenization. However, there were different ways in which they tried to\r\npreserve their identity. Discuss the methods used by the following groups:\r\na. Sadducees\r\nb. Zealots\r\nc. Pharisees\r\nd. Qumran Community', 50, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(28, 2, 'How can we preserve our identity as Christians in a secular, evil world that is constantly encroaching\r\nupon the church?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(29, 3, 'Who were the Pharisees and what did they believe? Include in your answer a discussion of their three\r\ncentral religious practices. Do we cling to our traditions as the Pharisees did? Is this a good thing?\r\nWhy? How far should we go in the keeping of traditions? Explain.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(30, 3, 'Discuss the origin and beliefs of the Sadducees. When the Sadducees quizzed Jesus (see Luke 20:27-33),\r\nHe responded to them by using examples from the Pentateuch (see Luke 20:37, 38). What does this\r\nsay to us about Jesus? ability to meet us where we are? Explain.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(31, 3, 'Who were the tax collectors of Jesus? day? Why were they so hated? As a general rule, do we feel\r\nthe same way about tax collectors? Why?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(32, 3, 'Describe the Zealots and their ?campaign planks.? In Jesus? response to their taxation question (see\r\nLuke 20:20-26), what was so unique about His answer? What does His answer teach us about paying\r\ntaxes? Do you agree? Why?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(33, 4, 'What is the position taken by the Church of God on the New Testament?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(34, 4, 'Why should we study the origin of the New Testament? Include a scripture basis for your answer.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(35, 4, 'Define the word canon and give a brief history of the word.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(36, 4, 'Discuss the four critical tests for determining the canonicity of the New Testament.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(37, 5, 'Describe how the church?s existence was seriously threatened by gnosticism. Is false doctrine as\r\nthreatening today as it was in the early history of the church? Why?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(38, 5, 'What were the motivations for the production of false writings? Are the motivations the same today,\r\nor are there others? Explain.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(39, 5, 'How can we recognize false writings? Name some writings which Christendom considers false, but\r\non which some religions are based. How can we respond to people of this sort who approach us with\r\ntheir literature? Give examples.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(40, 5, 'What role did the Roman persecution play in the determination of the canon? Explain. Could we say\r\nthat this persecution had a positive aspect? Explain. Can you think of other examples when\r\npersecution had a positive aspect?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(41, 16, 'Define kerygma.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(42, 16, 'Identify and discuss the four basic components of preaching.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(43, 16, 'What are the building blocks of the church? Do these same building blocks apply to the church today?\r\nExplain.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(44, 16, 'Discuss the first Jerusalem Council to which Paul reported (Acts 14:26-28).', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(45, 6, 'Discuss the process of canonization of the New Testament. Include in your discussion the names and\r\ndates of the great councils, as well as their decisions.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(46, 6, 'Explain the difference in the ?church producing the Word of God? and the ?Word producing the\r\nchurch.?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(47, 6, 'During the process of canonization, six books were disputed. Name them and tell why they were\r\ndisputed.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(48, 6, 'If you had been seated on one of the great councils, do you think you would have had a problem\r\naccepting the Book of Revelation? Why? Do people in general have problems understanding the\r\nBook of Revelation? Explain.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(49, 7, 'Discuss the differences in the synoptic Gospels and the Gospel of John. Name the central issue or\r\ntheme of each of the four Gospels.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(50, 7, 'Name and discuss the theme of the Book of Acts. What is unique about this book? Explain.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(51, 7, 'Describe the importance of the Pauline Epistles. Name each of the 13 epistles written by Paul and give\r\nthe theme and a synopsis of each.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(52, 7, 'There are nine General Epistles. Name them, giving the theme and a brief description of each.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(53, 8, 'How does Matthew open his book? Why is this genealogy important? Explain.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(54, 8, 'What is the purpose of the Gospel of Matthew? How is that purpose relevant to us?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(55, 8, 'The Book of Matthew is structured around five of Jesus? sermons or discourses. Name them and state\r\nwhere to find them.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(56, 8, 'The Book of Matthew is outlined into 11 categories. Identify them by name and chapter divisions.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(57, 9, 'Discuss the Book of Matthew in its canonical context.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(58, 9, 'Discuss the Book of Matthew in its original context in the following aspects:\r\na. Authorship c. Place of composition\r\nb. Date d. Occasion', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(59, 9, 'What impact has the Book of Matthew had upon the church world?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(60, 9, 'What impact has the Book of Matthew had upon the Pentecostal doctrine?', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(61, 10, 'Why was it extremely important to record in writing the message of Jesus? Explain.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(62, 10, 'Discuss both the internal and external evidences supporting Markan authorship.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(63, 10, 'Discuss the date of the writing of the Book of Mark.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
(64, 10, 'Divide the Gospel of Mark into four divisions, giving the theme and Scriptural breakdown of each\r\ndivision.', 25, NULL, NULL, 0, 0),
