(683, 236, '1. Discuss rest as indicated in Creation and rest as indicated by the Sabbath.\r\n2. Describe the two anchor points for the day of rest.\r\n3. Explain what spoils rest.', 50, '2017-09-17 01:05:50', '2017-09-16 18:05:50', 1, 1),
(684, 238, 'What is the importance of the study of Apologetics? ', 25, '2018-03-08 02:19:16', '2018-03-07 19:19:16', 1, 1),
(685, 238, 'What are the guidelines from God on how to be an apologist? Explain your answers.', 25, '2018-03-08 02:18:34', '2018-03-07 19:18:34', 1, 1),
(686, 239, 'Knowing that young people today have been raised in a postmodern culture, what differences\r\ndo you see in their attitudes from those raised a few decades earlier? What remains the same?', 25, '2018-03-08 02:20:14', '2018-03-07 19:20:14', 1, 1),
(687, 239, 'Of the guidelines on how to be an apologist listed in Lesson 1, which strikes you the most?\r\nWhy? Which is hardest for you? Easiest? Why? Who do you know who could model for you\r\nstrength in your area of weakness?', 25, '2018-03-08 02:20:54', '2018-03-07 19:20:54', 1, 1),
(688, 240, 'Explain the Absolute proof for the Existence of God. Support your answers with other relevant sources.', 50, '2018-03-08 02:22:34', '2018-03-07 19:22:34', 1, 1),
(689, 241, 'Why do you think people tend to act on very little evidence in most areas, but demand so\r\nproof in religious matters? Is proof enough to convert someone? What examples can you find in\r\nthe ministry of Jesus that would help you answer that question?', 25, '2018-03-08 02:23:55', '2018-03-07 19:23:55', 1, 1),
(690, 241, 'How do the different arguments in Lesson Three speak to the head? How do they speak to the\r\nheart? Which do you find the most convincing? Some of the arguments work best in a classroom\r\nsetting. How might you use each of these if you were having a cup of coffee with a friend who\r\nis considering the case for Christ?', 25, '2018-03-08 02:24:22', '2018-03-07 19:24:22', 1, 1),
(691, 242, 'Explain the concept of Critical Scholarship on Bible\\\'s History. Support your answers with other sources and write the Bibliography for the same.', 50, '2018-03-08 02:26:41', '2018-03-07 19:26:41', 1, 1),
(692, 243, 'Write a paper on the existence of Bible in the History and Defending the authenticity of the Bible.', 50, '2018-03-08 02:29:07', '2018-03-07 19:29:07', 1, 1),
(693, 244, 'Discuss the usage of Bible in its Literal form.', 50, '2018-03-08 02:29:58', '2018-03-07 19:29:58', 1, 1),
(694, 249, 'test question', 10, '2018-04-14 14:11:42', '2018-04-14 07:11:42', 1, 1),
(695, 249, 'test question2', 10, '2018-04-14 15:02:40', '2018-04-14 08:02:40', 1, 1),
(696, 250, '1. Discuss the Authorship with all its details for the Book of Acts. (15 marks)\r\n\r\n2. Explain the Historical settings for the Book of Acts.  (15 Marks)\r\n\r\n3. Write the Theological Background of the Book of Acts (20 marks)\r\n', 50, '2018-05-13 07:08:05', '2018-05-13 00:08:05', 1, 1),
(697, 250, '1. Discuss the explicit and implicit evidence from the Gospel of Luke that strongly suggests that one person wrote both the Gospel of Luke and the book of Acts.\r\n\r\n2. Discuss the historical evidence from the early church that supports the view that the same person wrote the Gospel of Luke and the book of Acts.\r\n\r\n3. Which clues can we gain from the New Testament about the author of Acts? How do these clues support the idea that Luke wrote the book of Acts?\r\n', 50, '2018-07-24 11:03:15', '2018-07-24 04:03:15', 1, 1),
(698, 251, '1. What was Luke’s twofold purpose for writing the book of Acts? How should this purpose impact our reading of Acts?\r\n\r\n2. How and why did Luke use authoritative words and deeds to persuade his readers of the truth of his accounts?\r\n\r\n3. What structural elements reveal the structural pattern of the book of Acts? How does this pattern help us understand the message of the book?', 50, '2018-07-24 11:04:59', '2018-07-24 04:04:59', 1, 1),
(699, 252, '1. Summarize Jesus’ teaching about the Holy Spirit before Pentecost in terms of the purpose and timing of the coming of the Holy Spirit.\r\n\r\n2. Explain the Holy Spirit’s ministry at Pentecost in terms of its significance, the gift of tongues, and the results of these events.\r\n\r\n3. Summarize the Holy Spirit’s work after Pentecost as he continued to empower gospel ministry throughout the book of Acts. Include a discussion of geography and ethnicity.', 50, '2018-07-24 11:06:40', '2018-07-24 04:06:40', 1, 1),
(700, 254, '1.	What is “individual eschatology”? Define the terms “regenerate” and “unregenerate” in the context of the lesson.', 10, '2018-09-11 12:41:45', '2018-09-11 05:41:45', 1, 1),
(701, 254, '2.	Explain the present state of the unregenerate, including a description of spiritual death and Augustine’s states of moral ability before and after the Fall. ', 10, '2018-09-11 12:42:32', '2018-09-11 05:42:32', 1, 1),
(702, 254, '3.	How do unregenerate souls experience the intermediate state? What do the names typically used for “hell” in Scripture teach us about the nature of their situation?', 15, '2018-09-11 12:43:45', '2018-09-11 05:43:45', 1, 1),
(703, 254, '4.	Many people dislike the doctrine of hell and eternal torment. How might you demonstrate the justice of hell to those who object to this biblical teaching? Do you think you should talk about hell in evangelistic conversations? Why or why not?', 15, '2018-09-11 12:44:37', '2018-09-11 05:44:37', 1, 1),
(704, 253, '1.	Define “eschatology.” Broadly understood, what period of time is covered under the term eschatology?', 10, '2018-09-11 12:45:36', '2018-09-11 05:45:36', 1, 1),
(705, 253, '2.	What is the proto-euangelion, and where is it found in Scripture? Why was it necessary? ', 10, '2018-09-11 12:46:35', '2018-09-11 05:46:35', 1, 1),
(706, 253, '3.	What were the two great ages expected by first century Jewish theologians? Given the theological developments that took place between the Old and New Testaments, did Jesus and his apostles confirm or contradict this Jewish expectation? Use specific Scripture references to support your answer.', 15, '2018-09-11 12:47:10', '2018-09-11 05:47:10', 1, 1),
(707, 253, '4.	What does the Great Commission require of churches today? What are some practical ways you can encourage those in your community to “make disciples of all nations”?\r\n\r\n', 15, '2018-09-11 12:47:51', '2018-09-11 05:47:51', 1, 1),
(709, 257, '1.	Define “eschatology.” Broadly understood, what period of time is covered under the term eschatology?\r\n2.	What does the creation account of Genesis 1–2 tell us about our God-ordained roles and responsibilities? How is this related to the “cultural mandate”? \r\n3.	What is the proto-euangelion, and where is it found in Scripture? Why was it necessary? \r\n4.	How are you called to fulfill the cultural mandate? In what ways can you exercise the kingly and priestly role of working and taking care of the things over which God given us authority?\r\n5.	What does the Great Commission require of churches today? What are some practical ways you can encourage those in your community to “make disciples of all nations”?', 50, '2018-09-25 11:10:31', '2018-09-25 04:10:31', 1, 1),
(710, 258, '1.	What is “individual eschatology”? Define the terms “regenerate” and “unregenerate” in the context of the lesson.\r\n2.	How do the regenerate come to experience spiritual life in the present state? How does this affect their moral ability? \r\n3.	How do unregenerate souls experience the intermediate state? What do the names typically used for “hell” in Scripture teach us about the nature of their situation?\r\n4.	Because the unregenerate are not motivated by love for God, even their good deeds do not earn God’s favor. How does this affect your perspective on good works? What role do you think good works play in the Christian life?\r\n5.	Many people dislike the doctrine of hell and eternal torment. How might you demonstrate the justice of hell to those who object to this biblical teaching? Do you think you should talk about hell in evangelistic conversations? Why or why not?\r\n\r\n', 50, '2018-09-25 11:13:29', '2018-09-25 04:13:29', 1, 1),
(711, 259, '1.	What does the Bible teach us about the manner of Christ’s return? What will it look like? How will we recognize him? Use specific Scripture references to support your answer.\r\n2.	Scripture mentions several circumstances that are precursors to Christ’s return. Describe three of the precursors that will precede Jesus’ second advent.\r\n3.	Evangelicals interpret the precursors to Christ’s return using a variety of strategies. List and explain the four main evangelical interpretive strategies associated with the signs of the times.\r\n4.	God’s covenant with Abraham can seem very removed from modern-day Christians. What are some ways that the Abrahamic covenant is still relevant today?\r\n5.	The circumstances that Scripture says will precede Christ’s return create legitimate expectations for how the future may unfold. How do these precursors to the second coming warn and encourage you as you prepare for Christ’s arrival? ', 50, '2018-09-25 11:16:05', '2018-09-25 04:16:05', 1, 1),
(712, 260, '1.	Explain the two predominant first-century schools of thought concerning the resurrection of the dead. Give the rationale for each view. Using Scripture, demonstrate which position Jesus, Paul and the rest of the early church took on this issue.\r\n2.	What is divine authority? Explain the nature of God’s authority in the general resurrection over both hell and heaven.\r\n3.	What effect will the general resurrection have on human beings? Who will be included? What will our resurrected bodies be like?\r\n4.	Read Romans 8:19-23. What do you think Paul meant when he said that creation is “groaning” and that believers “groan inwardly”? What kinds of things cause us to groan as we “wait eagerly for … the redemption of our bodies”?\r\n5.	The final judgment is intended to punish the wicked and reward the righteous. How do you feel about preaching the forgiveness of sins through Christ to murderers and other criminals? Is there anyone who doesn’t deserve to hear the gospel?  Explain your answer', 50, '2018-09-25 11:18:51', '2018-09-25 04:18:51', 1, 1);
