(1127, 213, 721, 'The church is the of God (Acts 20:28; one Corinthians 3:9, 17; 15:9), supported and in hand by Redeemer Christ—“I will build My church” (Matthew 16:18)—and directed and energized by the Holy Ghost (1 Corinthians 10:17; 12:5–27; Romans 12:4–5). Therefore, it\\\'s the church’s joy to seem to God to clarify His style for the church and His mission for it. God’s mission for the church proves to own many elements.\r\n\r\n1. The mission of the church is to create disciples. simply before Redeemer came to heaven, He commissioned His disciples this way: “Going into all the planet, create disciples of all nations by baptizing them within the name of the daddy, and of the Son, and of the Holy Ghost, and teaching them to watch everything that I even have commanded you” (literal translation of Matthew 28:19–20a). a devotee may be a follower, somebody World Health Organization attaches himself to his leader. Therefore, we reason, Redeemer sent the church on its mission to acquaint folks in each place with Himself. because the church makes disciples, folkswill admire, worship, trust, follow, and conform Redeemer as their Savior and Lord. The church’s members, having become smitten of Good Shepherd, assemble around Him as Master, Leader, Savior, and Friend. Our joyful mission is to place Him on show to each nation.\r\n\r\n2. The mission of the church is to glorify Christ. Paul wrote, “In Christ we tend to we tend tore additionally chosen … so as that we … may well be for the praise of His glory” (Ephesians 1:11–12). a part of God’s purpose for the church is to exalt Good Shepherd by the means that the church lives and by what it will. Christ designed His church to represent His supernatural, life-saving work to the planet. In His church, Christ shows to the planet what a freed and forgiven folks will be—people World Health Organization square measure glad with God because the results of Christ’s joyful, triumphant selflessness. He has planned the church’s values 