(1264, 328, 659, 'We believe that God will establish his kingdom in earth , God has special purpose or goal that guided his act revalation ,For from and through him to him all things to be glorify , all creation is done by him, and for him, so jesus teaches to pray thy kingdom come, he wants bring his kingdom to earth, because its for him he made ,whatever is happening in the heaven , the same thing he wants established in earth to glorify him ,', 5, '2019-10-14 17:37:11', '2019-10-22 13:40:48', NULL),
(1265, 331, 692, 'Immutability means God is unchanging in his being, perfections, purposes and promises. God id essentially immutable and relationally mutable. The biblical concept of immutability does not mean that God is inactive, but constantly interacting with his creation in real and meaningful ways. According to traditional Christian theology, there are three critical aspects of immutability.\r\n1. God\'s eternal counsel or ultimate plan for history is immutable. Different traditions understand God\'s eternal plan differently, but all agree that all that God has done, doing and will do are part of a unified plan. God uses his omniscience to direct history towards the ends for which he created it. The immutability of God\'s plan assures us that His will and ways in ancient times accord with his will and ways today. \r\n2. God is immutable in his character. God\'s eternal nature is the same even though he displays different aspects of his nature in different times. This helps us to see that there will be significant connections between the original meaning and modern applications of the scripture. A particular attribute in a passage is understood in the context of God\'s other attributes. Some way modern audience are expected to apply the emphases of every scripture in ways that never disregard any other attribute of God. \r\n3. Covenant promises. When God promises, his word is immutable. God made covenant with Abraham and it remained for ever. If it is not covenant, God changes mind. Eg. His word about the destruction of Nineveh. Every revelation of God in scripture assures that God will keep his covenant promises. The original audience were supposed to understand every passage of scripture in this light, and modern audience should do the same', 8, '2019-10-22 09:46:03', '2019-10-22 13:41:49', NULL),
(1266, 331, 693, 'There are at least three ways in which modern people are very similar to the people who first received the scripture. \r\n1. Sinful images: Human beings created in the image of God, have fallen in to sin. All human despite of period, color or language have totally deprived from God and have a fallen, sinful nature. All human beings are marred in the image of God due to fall. \r\n2. Religious divisions: Since the beginning, the readers of the scriptures fallen in to one of three religious groups: unbelievers, false believers and believers. Unbelievers refuse to submit to God, false believers make superficial commitments to God but not truly redeemed. Believers are people who make faithful commitments to God, redeemed from sin and saved from eternal judgement.\r\nJust as in the past modern applications calls unbelievers to repentance exposing their lost condition. For false believers scripture expose their hypocrisies  and call for repentance. For believers biblical texts were designed to restrain their sin, to warn against failure and to lead them to grateful living. \r\n3. Classes; People are classified on the basis of gender, age, wealth, profession etc. The Bible also speak of people classified on the basis of their background. The same classes of people exist in every age. This forms meaningful connections between the original audience and all subsequent audiences.', 8, '2019-10-22 10:00:23', '2019-10-22 13:41:49', NULL),
(1267, 331, 694, 'It is recognized by the theologians that the progressive nature of God\'s rule over creation has resulted in periodic developments that create discontinuity between the various epochs mentioned in the scripture. Perhaps the most obvious epochal development occurred between the old and New Testaments. \r\nTheologians commonly identified epochs according to God\'s various covenants through out Bible. The laws regarding atoning sacrifice required different things at different points of redemptive history. In patriarchal period, it was family altars; Moses\' period, the Tabernacle; Solomon\'s period, the temple; early NT period Jesus\'s death on the cross and in the later N T, they ceased to be offered altogether. \r\nIt is true that the Old testament and New Testament laws differ in their context and content but they are not contradictory. The animal sacrifice of the OT are not relevant to us, but they are fulfilled in Christ. \r\nBiblical history is like a growing  tree, grows from seed to a sapling and to a fully grown tree. Everything that the tree will become is contained in the seed. But over time tree has to grow and develop to full maturity. \r\nSimilarly redemption has grown and developed through out biblical history. This developmental modal teaches that the whole Bible is relevant and authoritative for us. The older revelations must be applied in the light of the later revelations.', 9, '2019-10-22 10:13:18', '2019-10-22 13:41:49', NULL),
(1268, 331, 695, 'Many theological changes occurred in OT history where God altered his expectations regarding the concepts, behaviors and emotions of his people. When the changes were significant enough, they became basis for identifying epochal divisions. Each epoch is a period of time characterized by substantial and long lasting transitions in OT theology. \r\nThe following are the variety of ways theologians divided OT history. Theologians tend to use theological criteria to describe the epochs. Just as the growth of a tree, some parts of the OT theology advanced slowly, others at a medium pace and others rapidly. \r\nOn the basis of the genealogy of Matthew, the OT history is divided in terms of Abraham to David, David to exile and Exile to Christ. Also on the basis of Romans 5 and 1 Corinthians 15, OT history divided as the period before the law and after the law. \r\nOne of the most popular ways to divide OT history is by associating each epoch with one of God\'s covenants. God\'s covenant with his people always entailed significant theological shifts and there fore provide helpful boundaries for epochal divisions. The covenants are associated with Adam, Moses, David and finally with the New covenant in  Christ. \r\nThese covenants represents times when God moved mightily in history and introduced long lasing theological emphases. Each of God\'s covenant established different ways in which he related to human beings, and each provided his faithful people with new principles to follow in His service.', 9, '2019-10-22 10:28:13', '2019-10-22 13:41:49', NULL),
(1269, 331, 696, 'Old Testament divisions of history shows that God wanted his people to understand and apply theological themes in different ways in different times. Just as it was in the OT period, the NT believers also should never apply the scriptures as if they live in earlier period of history. \r\nA person living in Mosaic period is not supposed to go back to patriarchal period and build altars. A person from Solomon\'s time is not to go back to Mosaic time of Tabernacle. Once God commanded a new way for sacrifice in worship, he expected his people never to return to the old ways. \r\nAs we live in the epoch of New Covenant, we are not supposed to go back to the sacrifice and worship system of the OT. All the OT rituals and practices fulfilled in Jesus Christ and his atonement.\r\nHebrew 8:13 says that the arrival of the New Covenant made the old ways Obsolete, using the Greek term \'palaioo\' which may also be translated \' made old\' or out dated. \r\nThis does not mean that Christians should discard the OT and pay no attention to its teaching. The author of the Hebrews was not telling the OT is irrelevant rather he was saying that we live in a different epoch. we don\'t ignore the old ways, but we should never try to serve God as if we still lived in the old days. \r\nAlso in every age, people need to follow the military leadrership God established for the age. Eg. Judges , Kings etc. We as Christians follow the king Jesus and practice the NT principles of spiritual warfare fighting against the evil forces.\r\nGod has always expected his people to serve him in ways that were appropria', 8, '2019-10-22 10:43:16', '2019-10-22 13:41:49', NULL),
(1270, 333, 660, 'The word symphonic means \"together  in time \"its came from two Greek words, when ever its use for historical events we describe events that took place together in time ,theologian use this word in old testament took sets of events ha pended in same time ,that may be in different books, in different chapters but that will take together ,like a movie is showing pics of parts but its having continuation same way same events in different books, theologian take it together   ,same way we speak some life events ha pend in our life in same time, but we talk about it in one word ,there are many examples in bible, one is about Abraham\'s sacrifice , journey, calling, many things happens with Abraham, but theologian take it as Abraham\'s life, synchronicity means ,taking things together winch happen in same time or continues.', 8, '2019-10-24 16:44:46', '2019-10-29 00:55:56', NULL),
(1271, 333, 661, 'Synthesis is not difficult to understand, its taking different things together as one, or combining different combine or something in to whole, this is what we do when we look at the scripture in sinchronic synthesis in mind ,many critical scholars distinguished critical theology from systematical theology by pointing out logic from each discipline, critical theologians giving much impotent to logic,  from this point of view ,old testament did not focus on logical system,  always looking for historical evidence , an affrimation of logical character of old testament stand on atlist two ground, first kind of contrast between greek and hebrew mind set, second old testament theology display sub stent logic and rational', 9, '2019-10-24 17:00:02', '2019-10-29 00:55:56', NULL),
(1272, 333, 662, 'when we speak about old testament poetry we have in mind some books like psalms, and some wisdom literature, also some old testament poetry have in some other books too,  poet in the old testament were intrested to two differnt world, one is calld \'that world\'means the time he wrote his poem,ore he was focusing on the people who was ther in his time, example in exodus, moses and miryam was singing a song abot God\'s delivering, it was aslo giving a historical evidence what God had done in Red sea , but in other world poet  use different methods in his poem ,contemporary historical information from the writers own time, example psalms 1,who ever read this poem the feel and understand the need of meditating word of God, and hgow God will bless a person who obey word of God and walk according to word of God in any Era, it wat this time world, the person who read this poem its for his time.', 7, '2019-10-24 17:12:19', '2019-10-29 00:55:56', NULL),
