(1276, 340, 666, 'We used the term \'development\' simply  using instead of diachronic change to suggest two main ideas , First, changes in old testament theological structures always move ahead to fully fill the God\'s porous for history ,from one end to the other everything 9in history including developments and shifting of theology was god\'s unfailing plan ,God has a short term plan and long term plan for every creation, he knows everything\'s end in the beginning ,second consider all theological changes only occurs through god provident ion involvement in the history ,Gods divine providence,old testament includes many different changes , but when we looks its seems like one and straight , just like we looks a road from far its seems stragight when we come close or move on its we liaised that it has turn, dissent, ascend , old testament also having the same developments , so we used word development instead of diachronic changes.', 9, '2019-11-07 05:59:20', '2019-11-14 15:33:46', NULL),
(1277, 340, 667, 'There are many ways to divide history in old testament theological period ,the old testament characterize every human relationship based on three covenant dynamic, the display of divine benevolence,the necessity of human loyalty to god , and the consequence of blessing for obedience and curs for disobedience ,old testament covenant falls in main tree categories,universal, national, and new, Firs , \"universal\"the covent with Adam and Noha wa universal, becos they are stand between God and human,thge covenet with adam reffers human and Divin relation, second\'National covenet\"its for special people, especly for isral, God makde covenet with moses, David, abraham,third\"new covent\" its God made with his people throgh prophets abou israels Exile, deliverance israel repnt to sin, god deliverd,new covenet deserned to God\'s people , when they obay hime he will established his kingdom again .', 7, '2019-11-07 06:14:08', '2019-11-14 15:33:46', NULL),
(1278, 340, 668, 'When a christian pastor or teacher teach about the devolpoments of theology in old testament we must learn about typology, it means how writers compare some matters with old testament incidents ,usualy they refers the aspects of the old testament as type of Christ some other aspects of christian faith ,theologians used the word typlogy in may aspects, typeolgy  of worship,typology of doctrin of God etc,biblical typology is the study of dicrhonical developments between theological structur closly associated with significant person and events in criptur ,siply study of types, in bible ther aree many figur of comparisions, and types of speech ,metaphor, simil, analogic, so need of the typological studi is to understand the cambaristions of part of thies scriptur.typologic example- paul comair Christ with Adam , bothe are men, similarities,', 8, '2019-11-07 06:29:11', '2019-11-14 15:33:46', NULL),
(1279, 340, 669, 'New covenant was designed to govern God\'s people, we may speak new covenant as the covenant of the fulfillment\"the covenant given to the israel in exil fullfild in new testament periods, New testament tell us the age of fulfillment was inaugurated first coming of Christ, there are lots of changes happening in the new covenant fulfillment, especially in worship, sacrifice, temple, Passover, it was a dychronical progress,  in old testment Temple was aplace to worship God, but there also may differnt system deveoped accoring to time, God told to moses buld a portable tabrnacle for me, but by Solomen God made an another temple, and system also changed, Esra, Nehemia, zerubabel made anotheer temple worhip style also changed ther e, the same way in new testment after coming of christ , temple is chenged as human heart , also the rits God diven to israle is becme a shadow of Gods plan inthe histroy, traditions change, theological concept about God is devoloed,', 8, '2019-11-07 06:42:34', '2019-11-14 15:33:46', NULL),
(1280, 336, 761, 'According to the scriptures, it teaches that the Son was at the Father\'s side during creation and that that Father created the world by him and through him. This becomes very evident in Colossians 1:16 \"for through him God created everything in the heavenly realms and on earth. He made the things we can see and the things we can\'t see such as thrones, kingdoms, rulers, and authorities in the unseen world. Everything was created through him and for him.\" as well as in Hebrews 1:2, \"And now in the final days, he has spoken to us through his Son. God promised everything to the son as an inheritance and through the Son he created the universe.\"', 7, '2019-11-15 02:14:36', '2019-11-17 05:00:43', NULL),
(1281, 336, 762, 'God\'s external counsel or other words, God\'s plan for the universe with regards to Christ is that what Christ has already accomplished is central to God\'s plan. God ordained salvation in him and Christ wont fail. God had foreknowledge and a purpose in mind. This is clear in Ephesians 1:4,11 \"Even before he made the world, God loved us and chose us in Christ to be holy and without fault in his eyes, furthermore because we are united with Christ, we have received and inheritance from God for he chose us in advance and he makes everything work out according to his plan.\"', 8, '2019-11-15 02:27:32', '2019-11-17 05:00:43', NULL),
(1282, 336, 763, 'God the Father promised to fulfill His kingdom plans for creation and humanity through the Son. The Son promised to become incarnate as a human being descended from God\'s chosen line of Davidic kings and to fulfill all the terms set forth in the prior covenant of redemption. He would die an atoning death for fallen humanity and all those who turned to him in repentance and faith would be redeemed from the presence of corruption and guilt of sin. In addition to these promises, both the Father and the Son agreed to send the Holy Spirit to apply the benefits of salvation to those the Son would save.', 8, '2019-11-15 02:38:26', '2019-11-17 05:00:43', NULL),
(1283, 336, 764, 'There are four things that Jesus specifically did to accomplish redemption for sinners. The 1st is His inauguration of the kingdom of God. Jesus taught that he had brought the kingdom of God to earth in His day. This can be found in Matthew 12:28. Secondly, His obedience to the Father. Jesus lived a life of perfect obedience to the Father, even unto his death on the cross. The third was his resurrection. By rising from the dead, Jesus conquered death itself. Lastly, His ascension. This was important because one, his ascension into heaven showed his enthronement as King and two, it allows Jesus to complete his sacrifice in the heavenly temple and to remain in the Father\'s presence interceding for his people.', 9, '2019-11-15 02:51:43', '2019-11-17 05:00:43', NULL),
(1284, 336, 765, 'At least three crucial events will take place when Jesus initiates the consummation. The first will be the general resurrection. This is where everyone that has died will be resurrected. This includes both the wicked and the righteous and they will be given new bodies. The second event is the last judgement. After the general resurrection has occurred, Jesus will exercise his authority and power as King by destroying all his enemies and blessing all His faithful people at the last judgement. The last event is the renewal of creation. Just as Jesus will judge humanity and purge the unbeliever, he will also purge and renew creation itself.', 8, '2019-11-15 03:04:12', '2019-11-17 05:00:43', NULL),
(1285, 342, 781, '1)Factual background \r\n      Simply put the author recall some historical detail from the Hebrew Scripture and quote a few words. \r\nHeb7: Melchizedek king of Salem\r\nFrom Genesis 14:18 mean king of righteousness and king of peace \r\nThis background then enhanced his comparison between Jesus and Melchizedek \r\n   As another example in Hebrew 12:20 and 21 \r\n\r\n2) Theological outlooks\r\n    In this case rather than nothing simple historical facts, the author focused on Theological believe affiliated by the Hebrew Scripture beliefs about God himself and other \r\nHebrews 1:5  author reference 2 Samuel 7:14 and 1 chronicles 17:13\r\nHeb1:7  Ps 104:4 \r\nIn Hebrew 2:6 he cited Ps 8 : 4-\r\n3) moral obligation \r\n   Hebrew 3:7-15 in indicated Ps 95 : 7-11 \r\nHeb12:5 showed that prob 3:11', 8, '2019-11-17 15:45:43', '2019-12-09 04:03:12', NULL),
(1286, 342, 782, 'The author of Hebrews respond to this challenge in five step\r\n\r\n1) 1:1-4 Audience should follow Jesus because Jesus is God\'s suprem source of divine revelation \r\nJesus brought revelation that was far superior to any revelation given through Angel \r\n2) 1:5-14\r\nJesus Greater than angles because he alone is God\'s messianic son he noted that Jesus fulfilled the ideals for David\'s house \r\nAnd Jesus also fulfilled David\'s predicted of the victory of God\'s messianic son over all of God\'s enemies \r\n3) 2:1-4\r\nHe reminded them that violation message from angles in the past received just punishment from God so his \r\n4) 2:5-9\r\nSupport belief in the supremcy of Christ by explaining that Jesus is now rules over the angel', 9, '2019-11-17 16:00:48', '2019-12-09 04:03:12', NULL),
(1287, 342, 783, 'It is founded on better promise \r\nThes better promise offer the complete transformation of God\'s people and the final enternal forgiveness of their sin \r\nHeb 9;1-28 the author elaborate one the began this section by mentioning the arrangements of Moses earthly Tabernacle, revealing features that resemble God\'s heavenly sanctuary. \r\n\r\n The author also explain why Jesus sacrifice was necessary. He used the example of a will. Ordinary wills are initiated by someone death Moses covenant was initially with death and blood. So the author reasoned that the new covenant also had to be initiated palace . But in this case the inheritance of the will is forgiveness heb9:', 8, '2019-11-17 16:15:52', '2019-12-09 04:03:12', NULL),
