(1427, 426, 630, 'The book of acts present rich theology of the holy spirit, it describe him as the one that empowered the  church to lives transformed lives and evangelized the world , we will foucus on his influence over the church before the Pentecost, spirit in acts before the Pentecost :in Acts 1.3-11 luke records that Jesus spend forty days in the earth after the Resurrection , teaching his apostles, we will touch two aspects of jesus teaching about holy spirit before Pentecost , First we will look at the timing of holy spirit coming, Second we will focus on the purpose of his coming,\r\n  Timing : Jesus announced the coming baptism of the holly spirit   the apostle asked as jesus was about to roster the kingdom of Israel, the expression roster the kingdom to israel is unfamiliure to many modern readers, so we should pause to explain it, \r\nOld testament prophets predicted :because of Israels and judges great sin God would Exel them fro the promis land, and subject tghem to the tyranny of forging rulers based on old testament jews belive God will send messiah to restor his people by forgiving thjre sin, and returing them to the land, ruling over them, the messiah would become king over israel, jesus explain the transiction to glorious kingdom to come, \r\nPurpose:the spirit was poured out to them to empower them, that they may witness bodly,  spirit was act throgh the apostels holy spirit manifested indramatic ways inthem.', 9, '2020-04-23 09:50:05', '2020-04-24 03:40:08', NULL),
(1428, 426, 802, 'The book of acts present rich theology of the holy spirit, it describe him as the one that empowered the  church to lives transformed lives and evangelized the world , we will foucus on his influence over the church before the Pentecost, spirit in acts before the Pentecost :in Acts 1.3-11 luke records that Jesus spend forty days in the earth after the Resurrection , teaching his apostles, we will touch two aspects of jesus teaching about holy spirit before Pentecost , First we will look at the timing of holy spirit coming, Second we will focus on the purpose of his coming,\r\n  Timing : Jesus announced the coming baptism of the holly spirit   the apostle asked as jesus was about to roster the kingdom of Israel, the expression roster the kingdom to israel is unfamiliure to many modern readers, so we should pause to explain it, \r\nOld testament prophets predicted :because of Israels and judges great sin God would Exel them fro the promis land, and subject tghem to the tyranny of forging rulers based on old testament jews belive God will send messiah to restor his people by forgiving thjre sin, and returing them to the land, ruling over them, the messiah would become king over israel, jesus explain the transiction to glorious kingdom to come, \r\nPurpose:the spirit was poured out to them to empower them, that they may witness bodly,  spirit was act throgh the apostels holy spirit manifested indramatic ways inthem.', 0, '2020-04-23 09:57:22', '2020-04-23 09:57:22', NULL),
(1429, 426, 803, 'Apostels witness christ in unique way, the apostels authority is seen in many ways throughout acts , first athority of the appostel\'s can seen in the function of their office, Gods blessing on thier ministry, evident their power of doing miracles, and the revaluation they continue to receive  , \r\nFunction: apostels were comenly used they were messenger, agent and ambasider, missinorys were treated as surrogate of Christjesus deligate his athority to his missionaries , the apostels were athoritive ambasiders form other disciples, they were perpetually  appointed  to the ofice of the church, atherized to speak to the all matters related to the establishment and governments of the Christ church, \r\nBlessings:God gave the apostles convert almost every time they were preached the gospel, in peters one sermon many repented, the external numerical groth of the church was evidence of the grothe of the church, and gods aprovel and power,\r\nMiracles :one of the main porous of the miracle is to prove that God\'s messengers speak the truth and bear god\'s deligated athority, the apstels miracle proved that thier testmany concwering that christ was true.\r\nRevelation:holy spirit always given the guidence to the apostel to preach the word of God , flesh out the truth of the gospel, make disicion for the church as all, sharp stuctural elements thast allowed the church to grow maturly', 8, '2020-04-23 10:15:20', '2020-04-24 03:40:08', NULL),
(1430, 426, 804, 'The arrival of the spirit on the first christian Pentecost  indicate that church had also recived the writing of God\'s law, and equipping the church for the bold witness , out poring of the holy spirit he emphasized it association with Pentecost to indicate the grand significance of what happened. this was not ordinary event, it was mot one miracle among many others , the gift of spirit began to Pentecost the grate harvest of salvation,  \r\n the same way spirit will help us to preach boldly , when the spirit came to deciples they become powerful and they empowerd, same way spirit will empowerd us to do gospelisation , and aslo spirit will transform us from our laziness, fearful, stages, the person who recive the power of holy spirit will change,  i too experienced the holy pirit to share word of god,', 7, '2020-04-23 10:27:51', '2020-04-24 03:40:08', NULL),
(1431, 426, 805, 'There are many ways to the church to continuing the mission to speeding kingdom of God  ,first we can follow the way that apostles did to the early church, that is encourage our people to reaman faith ful to the teaches of the bible, we must teach the word of God to the church, it will help them to stay with God and also they will get empowerment to spread the gospel, \r\n we can improve our effort through encouraging the church to carry out the gospel, and also we should make the provision for them, selecting some elders , decons, youths, leaders, and may othjer things,we must prepare the church to stay in the hard ship, apostels tollarte may problmes , thew were betten up, and jailed, many problem they faced, we also be ready to go throgh any sistuation, \r\nMany wasy i can help my church to expand kingdom of God, i can share the word of God, and i can teach people , and i must be an example for them , i should stay in the hardship ,', 8, '2020-04-23 10:38:23', '2020-04-24 03:40:08', NULL),
(1432, 434, 589, '\"Creation Ordinances\" is moral requirements established by God\'s works of creation. Bible relates the true story of creation in order to explain how humanity was actually designed to function within the world. Creation Ordinances are explicit such as God\'s command to be fruitful and multiply in Genesis 1:28. But others are implicit such as our obligation to keep the sabbath holy. The creation accounts don\'t say explicitly that human being should rest every 7th day, but in the ten commandments in Exodus 20:11, Moses clarified that God\'s pattern of working six days and resting on the seventh obligated human being to do the same. So as we think about the significance and role of humanity is both natural and helpful to start with our creation.', 10, '2020-04-24 16:34:25', '2020-04-24 19:58:39', NULL),
(1433, 434, 590, 'The book of Genesis contains two accounts of creation. One is Genesis 1;1-2:3 and the other is in Genesis 2:4-25. Together these accounts give us a general picture of how and why God created us. In the first creation account in genesis 1:2, we\'re told that the creation was originally formless and empty. Then, in the rest of the chapter we were told that God spent six days forming and filling the universe. A this point, humanity was clearly distinguished from the rest of creation. Human beings were created in God\'s image and given authority over his other creatures.\r\n2. Gen 2:4-25- God;s work on the sixth day when he created the land, animals and humanity. Here, we\'re told that God formed the animals from the dust. He also made the first man Adam in the same way. In order to give him a helper, God created the first women, Eve to be his wife, creating her from his ribs. This made Eve unique amongst all.', 9, '2020-04-24 16:41:17', '2020-04-24 19:58:39', NULL),
(1434, 434, 591, 'The Bible clearly teaches Adam and Eve were created to be superior to the rest of the God\'s earthly creatures. But the real proof of Adam and Eve\'s superiority over the rest of creation is found in the fact that God created them in His image and appointed to rule over creation on his behalf. God created humanity to reflect his glory and his attributes in ways that other creatures couldn\'t. Human beings are likeness of God. Our very existence points to God\'s power and goodness and because no other earthly creature is God\'s image, no other creature carries this much honor or inherent dignity. God appointed our first parents to rule over every other creature he had made. Its our job to administer God\'s rule over the earth. God has delegated the administration of His creation to us, and not to any other animals', 9, '2020-04-24 16:47:03', '2020-04-24 19:58:39', NULL),
(1435, 434, 592, 'Controversy about the origin of human beings continues to rage even today nearly 150 years after the publication of Charles Darwin\'s The origin of Species. Evolutionary explanation for the origin of life is just one of the theories. many other theories include the formation of all living from the Big Bang and one of the other is the Darwin theory of the formation of human from the evolution from the apes.this contrasts the theory of Christian point of view which is what The bible teaches clearly that God created Humans in his own likeness and in his own image from the dust of the earth and all other creatures with the word of his mouth.', 8, '2020-04-24 17:01:53', '2020-04-24 19:58:39', NULL),
(1436, 434, 801, 'Humanity  is still responsible to God for fulfilling the moral obligations that flow from our priestly duties: I as a pastor, fulfills this calling in my life by serving God in  all faithfulness and and worshiping Him in truth and spirit. The aim of my calling is to cultivate the seeds of His word to all nations, proclaim his goodness to the world, render sacrifices of praise and obedience to him and guard the creation that is the sheep of his pasture, which he has held me responsible for, Understanding to turn the whole world into a sanctuary that is absolutely fitting for God\'s awesome presence. This goal and the responsibility upon me burdens and energizes me to work for Him.', 8, '2020-04-24 17:11:07', '2020-04-24 19:58:39', NULL),
(1437, 437, 786, 'Gen 1:27-28- God created man in his own image, in the image of God he created him: male and female he created them. God blessed them and said to them, \"be fruitful and increase in number, fill the earth and subdue it. Rule over the fish and the sea and the birds of the air and over every living creature that moves on the ground\"\r\nRight after the scripture introduces us as images of God, it says that we govern creation. So, at least one important aspect of being God\'s image is that we hold the office of delegated ruler. In theological terms, we are God\'s \"vice-regents\"- his administrative deputies or in ancient near eastern terms, his servant or \"vassal\" kings.', 8, '2020-04-26 16:35:19', '2020-04-29 19:47:38', NULL),
(1438, 437, 787, 'The first thing Scripture says about humanity is that we\'re the image and likeness of God. God formed and ordered the entire world. And on the sixth and last working day of the week as his final act of creation, he made humanity. This is one of the primary ways God thinks about the human race. \"Likeness\"- a statue, a sketch, the appearance or sound of something compared to another: having a similar form. \"image\" and \"likeness\" both describe a model or sketch of greater reality. Scripture affirms that God alone is God. We\'re God\'s images and likenesses because we rule over the earth as God\'s servant kings and are endowed with the necessary qualities and abilities to perform our duties.', 8, '2020-04-26 16:40:58', '2020-04-29 19:47:38', NULL),
(1439, 437, 788, 'Christians have understood that the image of God in human beings includes our capacity to think rationally and process complex emotions. Some of this rational ability was lost in our fall in sin, as evidenced in many biblical passages that speak of human beings being irrational and even insane, such as Ecclesiastes 9:3 and Jeremiah 17:9. The fall damaged our ability to think and understand the world from God\'s perspective but didn\'t destroy it completely: even unbelievers have the rational capacity to know that God exists and to recognize certain aspects of his invisible qualities and divine nature.(Romans 1:19-20)\r\nGod has given believers his holy spirit and the mind of Christ so that we can once again understand reality in the same way that God does( 1 Corin 2:11-16)', 9, '2020-04-26 16:47:20', '2020-04-29 19:47:38', NULL),
(1440, 437, 789, 'God created humanity, he entered into a covenant relationship with us. God\'s covenant with humanity displayed three aspects of our covenant relationship with God that are specific to our role as his images.\r\n1. Reflect God\'s Character: Images of God are intended to reflect his pure, holy and righteous character wherever they appear. Fallen human beings can\'t be utterly holy on our own merit, but we rely on Christ\'s perfect holiness for our standing before God. God still requires us to pursue holiness.\r\n2. Promote Pure worship: Because human beings are real images of God, idols and other non human representations of him are false images. God is our true God, and isn\'t to be treated like the false Gods of the nations\r\n3. Build God\'s kingdom: By God\'s grace we\'re becoming clearer images of him as we pursue holiness and righteousness. God commanded humanity to fill the earth instructing us to place images of himself throughout the world. As God\'s vice regents or servant kings, we carry his rule with us wherever we go.', 9, '2020-04-26 16:55:42', '2020-04-29 19:47:38', NULL),
(1441, 437, 790, 'It is an absolute privilege for being appointed as a vice regent to rule over the creation on God\'s behalf, as we human beings are physical representations that remind all creation of God\'s power, authority and goodness. And through us, he manifests his rule over the world and all its creature. Therefore as a minister it influences my authority,as it says in Luke 10.19, Behold i have given authority to tread on snakes and scorpions, and over all the power of the enemy, and nothing shall hurt you. It opens up new authoritative ministry over demons, over powers of sickness. As God commanded us, He has given us the keys of Kingdom of heaven, whatever you bind on earth will be bound in heaven and whatever you loose on earth will be loosed in heaven, because we are regents of God and the Ambassadors of Christ.', 8, '2020-04-26 17:07:17', '2020-04-29 19:47:38', NULL),
(1442, 429, 816, 'Genesis 4;1-6:8 where Moses described the troubles and violence that took place in the world shortly after humanity\'s fall into sin. In these chapters, Moses described how human being began to fill the world with violence, and how God reacted to those trouble. We will examine three aspects of this portions \r\nMeans subject is \" a world of violence\"\r\nMeans two sections 1) 4:1-5:32\r\n2) 6:1-8 and we have called it \" later violence and hope\"', 7, '2020-04-27 16:13:46', '2020-04-29 19:47:02', NULL),
(1443, 429, 817, '4 -5 chapter divided into four part , and thes part from two parallel seta of narrative and generalloy 4:1 1 7 \r\nSecond 4:22- , 4:17\r\nNarrative and generalloy \r\n1) sinful Cain and Abel \r\n2) Cain murder Abel \r\n3) \r\n\r\nSon of God \r\n6:1-3 \r\nMoses didn\'t explain precisely who these sons of God and daughter of men were. Apparently, he expected his original reader to murder', 4, '2020-04-27 16:24:10', '2020-04-29 19:47:02', NULL),
(1444, 429, 818, 'Moses related thes charter of his primeval history to his contemporary world by descriptionig the violence of earlier human history in ways that closely resembles the experience of violence which Israel had endured by doing so. He point out that the troubles which Israel faced were very similar to the troubles of the primeval world \r\nMoses focused on at least five concern that allows the Israelites to connect this passage to their own day . In the first place, Moses mentioned the occasion of Cain and Abel to create the occasion', 6, '2020-04-27 16:33:36', '2020-04-29 19:47:02', NULL),
(1445, 429, 819, 'No doubt is a Abel .. because he not like violence \r\nCain was a agricultural, a farmer, while abel was a shepherd. In ancient and modern times, it has been common for tension to arise between settled, agricultural backed society and normal Shepard \r\nA second connected between his story ( Cain) and Moses original audience appears the motif of the sacrifice offered by Cain and Abel . \r\nAs Genuine 4 \r\nAble is good on because he always do good work in front of God..', 6, '2020-04-27 16:43:16', '2020-04-29 19:47:02', NULL),
(1446, 429, 820, 'In this light we can see understand how Moses drew another strong connection between this portions of his primeval history and the experience of Israel.\r\nWhen we realize followier of Christ will suffer persecution during the continuation of the kingdom, we can also see the important of maintenance our faith in Christ .the writer of Hebrews touched on this matter in chapter 11\r\n\r\nSo we see that themes of violence and deliverance in the primeval history also apply to following of Christ during the continuation of the kingdom. On one side , we should be ready to suffer \r\nThis hope of final deliver inThe second coming of Christ appears through the new Testament.it express the pin of Christian believe', 7, '2020-04-27 16:56:16', '2020-04-29 19:47:02', NULL),
(1447, 436, 826, 'Our definition of Christian ethics focuses on God and His blessings rather than on terms like good or evil, or right or wrong. Those things that receive God\'s blessings are good and right, whereas those things that do not receive his blessing are wrong and evil.\r\n1.DIVINE NATURE- God himself is the ultimate standard of right and wrong,of good and evil.God is not accountable to any standard outside himself.\r\n2 DIVINE ACTIONS-God\'s actions demonstrates the standard of morality. God shows his approval by bestowing blessings. He shows his hatred by withholding blessings and pouring out curses. Many times the Bible communicates right and wrong by recording God\'s reactions rather that by explicitly labeling things good or evil.', 7, '2020-04-28 00:39:31', '2020-04-29 19:44:11', NULL),
(1448, 436, 827, 'Obedience to God\'s commands must be done with proper motive.Unless a work is done with right motive , it is not a work that God will reward with blessings. \r\n\r\n1.FAITH\r\nOnly believers who are indwelled by the Holy Spirit can do works that God rewards with blessings.\r\nOnly believers have hearts that are purified by faith. Saving faith motivates good works. This is the faith possessed by believers and only by believers. Unless our attempts to seeks God\'s blessings are founded on faith, we cannot please God and therefore cannot be rewarded by Him.\r\n2. LOVE\r\nOur works are useless if they are not motivated by love.\r\nWorks and even spiritual gifts that produce beneficial results merit no reward if they are not motivated by love.\r\nLove is an aspect of every law God requires us to obey . If we do not act in love, no work we do can conform to his standard.Our love mist be both for God and neighbor.', 8, '2020-04-28 00:50:51', '2020-04-29 19:44:11', NULL),
(1449, 436, 828, 'THREEFOLD CRITERIA\r\nWestminister Confession of faith says\" Works done by ungenerate men may be things which God commands and of good use both to themselves and others , yet because they proceed not from an heart purified by faith, nor are done in a right manner , according to the word; nor to a right end , the glory of God;they are therefore sinful and cannot please God.\r\nThe threefold criteria are\r\n1.PROPER MOTIVE\r\nUnless a work is done with right motive , it is not a work that God will reward his blessings.Only believers are hearts are purified by faith. saving faith motivates good works. Our works are useless if they are not motivate by love Our love must be both for God and neighbor\r\n2. PROPER STANDARD\r\nIn order for works to be good , they must be done according to the standard of Word of God, God\'s revelation.All commands of scriptures are designed to guide us.\r\n3. PROPER GOAL\r\nGood works may have any number of innumerate goals. Everything in the Christian life should be done in a way that honors God and brings Him glory. God approves of works intended to bring him glory and He condemns works that disregard or oppose his glory', 9, '2020-04-28 01:05:18', '2020-04-29 19:44:11', NULL),
(1450, 436, 829, 'Ethical judgement involves the applications of God\'s Word to a situation by a person.\r\nEthics should be done from three perspectives:\r\n1.GOD\'S WORD\r\n2.SITUATION\r\n3. PERSON\r\nThe best approach is to do ethics from all three perspectives and to let the insights from each perspective inform and influence the others\r\n1. SITUATIONAL\r\nProblems\r\nconsequences of actions\r\ngoals\r\nwhen our ethical inquiries turn to the problems themselves, or to the consequences of actions or to the goals.\r\n2.Normative- God\'s Word is the norm or standard for ethics . We are doing ethics from the normative perspective when we look to the Bible to tell us what to do\r\n\r\n3. Existential- When we approach ethics by asking questions that are specific to the people involved, we are doing ethics from an existential perspective', 8, '2020-04-28 01:15:33', '2020-04-29 19:44:11', NULL),
(1451, 436, 830, 'God is the absolute judge of morality. He has the ultimate prerogative to determine whether or not particular actions , emotions , and thoughts meet or transgress his moral requirements. And he has the ultimate right and power to ac ton his determinations\r\nGod himself is the highest court in the universe . He will make the ultimate determination of whether or not we have lived morally or not and his judgements will be utterly binding.\r\nIt is God\'s right to judge because he has absolute authority , and His judgements are inescapable because he has absolute power.\r\nGod\'s judgements are perfect , exhibiting flawless insight and wisdom, unfailing fairness and impeccable morality.\r\nGod\'s power and authority to judge obligate his creatures to live according to the standard of his character. Mankind is obligated to obey and to imitate God.', 9, '2020-04-28 01:25:05', '2020-04-29 19:44:11', NULL),
(1452, 436, 831, 'Traditionally , theologians have spoken of God\'s revelation primarily in three categories :\r\n1. GENERAL REVELATION\r\nCreation and history teach us true things about God and his moral requirements. General revelation cannot teach us everything, but it speaks clearly enough to teach us true  things about God.\r\ncomplexity- some aspects of general revelation are common to all people ,but others are restricted to very limited groups of people. Scripture is the supreme form of revelation in our day , but we affirm the validity and binding authority of general revelation. .God \'s revelation in creation and history is clear, but people reject it and convince themselves of falsehood\r\n2.SPECIAL REVELATION-\r\nIT is the norm that is binding in our lives. Most rely on the spoken word or written word ,but all involve GOd communicating with people in ways that transcend the normal workings of creation\r\nThe only universally acknowledged form of current special revelation is Scripture.The Bible is binding on all people at all times\r\n3.EXISTENTIAL REVELATION\r\nGOD uses councils, ancient writers, doctrines of men and private spirits to reveal his will to the people. The external aspects of existential revelation are human existence, human judgement both individual and corporate and human behavior \r\nThe internal aspects  is illumination of the Holy Spirit which is a divine gift of understanding that God gives to believers and even to unbelievers.', 9, '2020-04-28 01:42:30', '2020-04-29 19:44:11', NULL),
(1453, 436, 832, 'Existential revelation is different way of categorizing a portion of general revelation. God uses councils ,ancient writers , doctrines of men and private spirits to reveal His will to his people. Because  we reflect God\'s character, we can learn many things about God by looking at His people.God uses human behavior as an external type of existential revelation. The external aspects of existential revelation include such as human existence,human judgement ,human behavior. we human beings are created in the image of God or we are each a replica of God. Human beings are the image sthat reflect God\'s glory and dignity.\r\ninward leading tends to be more emotive or intuitive which is one of the most common ways in which Holy spirit works within individuals to reveal truth about God\'s character', 7, '2020-04-28 01:54:16', '2020-04-29 19:44:11', NULL),
(1454, 436, 833, '1John 1:5-7 God is not just right and good ,  he is is goodness and rightness themselves.We are obligate to see GOd\'s nature as the standard and model of goodness and rightness. We are forgiven in Christ  so we are obligated to obey God\'s command. goodness is a personal attribute of God.\r\nAs the readers of scripture we are encouraged to measure our own goodness against GOd\'s actions and character.God \'s goodness is the uktimate standard for all goodness.\r\nSo in order to discover the right standard of goodness, we must not strive to learn abstract and ethical principles , rather we must  strive to know the heart of God himself.\r\nsince we are forgiven in Christ and are daily forgiven in Christ, we should also forgive those who hurt us ,according to GOd\'s standards.', 8, '2020-04-28 02:09:19', '2020-04-29 19:44:11', NULL),
(1455, 438, 791, 'Sin is any want of conformity unto or transgression of the law of God. Adam and Eve were created sinless. To continue in God\'s covenant blessings and avoid covenant curses they needed to remain loyal to the terms of God\'s covenants. The serpent tempted eve to eat the forbidden fruit and she gave it to Adam and he ate it. God cursed Adam and Eve because of their disloyalty. \"the fall\"- the events from the serpent\'s temptation through God\'s judgement when Adam and Eve\'s sin caused humanity to fall out of God\'s favor and blessings. Consequences of the fall- Gen 3:16-19- Eve- Pain in childbirth, strife in her relationship with Adam, death\r\nAdam- difficulty subduing and cultivating the earth, death.', 7, '2020-04-29 16:35:14', '2020-04-29 19:43:12', NULL),
(1456, 438, 792, 'The authorship of human sin refers to who is ultimately to blame for it. Adam and Eve tried to blame to someone else for their sin. Adam explicitly blamed Eve and implicitly blamed God who had created her. (Gen 3:12). Eve blamed the serpent. (Gen 3:13). God punished each one.: the serpent for deceiving the women, Eve- for being deceived, eating the fruit and misleading her husband. Adam- for being misled and eating the fruit. \r\nThe serpent was the ultimate author of sin because it was the first to come up with the idea to sin and the first to try to cause humanity to sin. Adam and Eve freely chose to sin and in this sense, authored human sin. God isn\'t culpable or guilty or of compelling anyone to sin. (1 john 1:5). God hates sin and can\'t be tempted by sin.(james 1:13)', 8, '2020-04-29 16:40:59', '2020-04-29 19:43:12', NULL),
(1457, 438, 793, 'In term original sin refers to the consequences of humanity\'s first sin. Original sin- The condition to which Adam\'s natural descendants are born as a result of Adam\'s fall into sin. \r\nCorruption- Humanity\'s relationship to sin: posse non peccare (the ability not to sin)- Adam and Eve\'s original sinless state\r\nnon posse non peccare (the inability not to sin)- Adam and Eve\'s corruption removed their capacity to please God and to merit his blessings. Every part of our human nature has been completely affected by sin, our bodies, our minds, and our hearts.\r\nConcepts- Sin has damaged our capacity for conceptual thought and caused us to believe that false ideas are true.\r\nBehavior- Adam and Eve\'s sin served as the model for all the behavioral sins that have plagued humanity\'s sins. God has given fallen humanity over to its sinful appetites.\r\nEmotions- Sin prevents us from loving God and our neighbors as we should and from manifesting other righteous emotions. Apart from God\'s saving grace, we have no ability to please God.', 8, '2020-04-29 16:49:03', '2020-04-29 19:43:12', NULL),
(1458, 438, 794, 'When Adam rebelled against God, our entire human kingdom fell under the shadow of his guilt and, consequently, under the curse of death(Romans 5:12-17)\r\nAdam died spiritually when he was cursed and his natural descendants are spiritually dead before they come to faith (Eph 2:1-5). We have spiritual life if Christ is in us, but if Christ is not in us, we are spiritually dead. Because of Adam\'s fall into sin, human being suffered immediate spiritual death. Even when we\'re created and eventual physical death. and worse, if we never come to faith in Christ, if we\'re never redeemed from sin\'s curse by God\'s grace, we\'ll continue to suffer both Spiritual and physical death in hell. and just like spiritual death in the present world, it will be a conscious experience. The unredeemed will exists forever, suffering the everlasting curse of sin in both body and soul. The curse of sin is very real, but by God\'s grace, we can struggle against sin\'s influence now and completely escape it in the future.', 8, '2020-04-29 16:55:44', '2020-04-29 19:43:12', NULL),
(1459, 438, 795, 'I would make the person understand the basic concept of God is love, and the loving father won\'t test anyone with evil. He gives us pain, sin and death into the world to once understand the depth of his amazing love and also his care in midst those problems. God allows us pain to bring out his perfect will in our life. As we know trials and tribulations bring us into glory and it works patience, which brings experience, then hope and hope makes us not ashamed because the love of God is shed abroad in our hearts by the Holy Ghost. He will bring out way in between those tribulations bestowing the Love of God. Therefore knowing it is the will of the Loving God, we should accept it in a positive manner and lead a perfect Christian Life and be a role model for those who bear pain and tribulations.', 8, '2020-04-29 17:04:42', '2020-04-29 19:43:12', NULL),
(1460, 433, 589, 'The Bible relates the true story of creation in order to explain how humanity was designed to function within the world. This is why many other parts of the Bible appeal to the creation accounts to prove how the world is supposed to works and what role human beings are morally obligated to play.Theologians often refers to these obligations as creation ordinances.\r\n\r\nCreation ordinances are moral requirements established by God\'s work of creation.\r\nsometimes creation ordinances are explicit.\r\nExplicit ordinances: \r\nexample: be fruitful and multiply  (Genesis 1:28)\r\nImplicit ordinances:\r\nThe creation accounts don\'t say explicitly that human beings should rest every seventh day. But in the Ten commandments it says Moses certified that God\'s pattern of working six days and resting on the seventh day obligated human beings to do the same.\r\nKeep the sabbath holy(Exodus 20:11)', 8, '2020-04-29 18:29:43', '2020-04-29 19:42:34', NULL),
(1461, 433, 590, 'BIBLICAL ACCOUNTS\r\nThere are two accounts of creation given in the Bible; They are:\r\nGENESIS 1:1 TO 2:3\r\nGod spent six days forming and filling the universe:\r\nDay 1: God separated the dark from light.\r\nDay 2: God separated the water above from water below.\r\nDay 3: God separated dry land and sea\r\nDay 4 :God filled the light and darkness with heavenly bodies(sun , moon ,stars)\r\nDay 5- God filled the sky and oceans with birds and sea creatures\r\nDay 6-God filled the dry land with animals and created the human beings to rule over creation\r\nGENESIS 2:4-25\r\nThis account contains more details related to God\'s work on the sixth day.\r\nGod formed the animals from the dust of the earth.\r\nGod made the first man from the dust of the earth and breathed life into him.\r\nAdam look for a suitable helper from among the animals.\r\nGod created Eve, the first woman from Adam\'s rib.\r\nThe two accounts differ in the way that in the second account the details of sixth day is given and about the creation of man and animals from dust. \r\nIn the first account the Human beings were created in God\'s image and given authority over creation.\r\nIn the second account Eve was under Adam \'s authority in their marriage ,but she was equal to him in the tasks God h as assigned them as a race', 9, '2020-04-29 18:45:05', '2020-04-29 19:42:34', NULL),
(1462, 433, 591, 'Adam and Eve were created superior to the rest of God\'s earthly creations.\r\n1.  They were Created on the sixth day, separately from the animals as the culmination of creation .\r\nGenesis 1:27\r\n2. God called them \"very good\" Genesis 1:31\r\n3.Only Adam is said to have his life breathed into him by God. Genesis 2:7\r\n4. God created them in His image , and appointed them to rule over creation on his behalf (genesis 1:27-28, 9:2,Psalms 8:6-8\r\n\r\nGod created humanity to reflect his glory and his attributes in ways that other creature couldn\'t \r\nBecause human beings are likeness of God so our existence pints to his power and goodness and no other creature carries this much honor and inherent dignity \r\nHumanity also has superior role to administer God\'s rule over the earth(Genesis 2:20)\r\nScriptures confirm humanity\'s superiority by putting us almost on the level of angels in the present, and superior to the angels in the future(Psalms 8:5)', 7, '2020-04-29 18:55:49', '2020-04-29 19:42:34', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(1463, 433, 592, 'There had been many common beliefs in the human origins in our culture. Many religions teach different theories of origin of life. Science also has different theories:\r\n1. DARWINISM:- It is a theory of biological evolution which states that all species of organisms arise and develop through the natural selection of small, inherited variations that increase the individual\'s ability to compete , survive and reproduce. It was developed by Charles Darwin.\r\n2. THE BIG BANG THEORY- It is a cosmological model which describes how the universe expanded from an initial state of very density and high temperature and an explosion .\r\n3. SPONTANEOUS GENERATION- It states generation of life from non-living matter .\r\nDarwinism is false according to the Bible as each and every creature was created by God by his word and each of different species and classifications as per his command. \r\nBig band theory is false as earth ,sky , land  and all heavenly bodies and everything in it was created as per His command and not as a result of an explosion.\r\nGod gave his breath and life came to being not out of non-living matter.', 8, '2020-04-29 19:09:52', '2020-04-29 19:42:34', NULL),
(1464, 433, 801, 'God\'s covenant with Adam was and still is binding on all humanity. SO we are still responsible to God for fulfilling the moral obligations that  flow from these priestly duties. 1\r\nHOW TO FULFILL THE PRIESTLY DUTY:( 1 PETER 2:5-9)\r\n1. We are all called to serve God and worship him.\r\n2. to cultivate and guard the creation \r\n3. to turn the whole world into a sanctuary that is fitting for God\'s presence\r\nSo in the /church and in life also we keep on rendering sacrifices of praise in obedience to him and as we get opportunity we proclaim his goodness to the whole world.\r\nHOW TO FULFILL THE ROYAL DUTY\r\n1. Humanity \'s tasks to help God to extend his heavenly kingdom falls on each one of us. This duty energizes to use our skills and our resources to care for and govern his creation.\r\n2. whether we are in lour homes, at our jobs , in the Church or anywhere else. we are called to represent and to serve our great king in everything we do.', 8, '2020-04-29 19:22:03', '2020-04-29 19:42:34', NULL),
(1465, 430, 821, '1) Genesis 6:17-18\r\nGod planning to start over again by delving on man and his family God return Noah after flood and made another Covent\r\n\r\n2)7:1-16 which we have entitled Noah escape from water\" this material is rather straight forward Noah prepare the ark brought animal for every kind into it  and floored begin to Burt into the world but Noah his family and the animal he had gathered were safety sealed in the ark\r\n\r\n3) 8:6-19 It Noah ext to dray land  after the flood had begun to subside, Noah longerd for dray land to appear so that he could leave the ark after a period of wait \r\n\r\n4)', 5, '2020-04-30 16:21:24', '2020-05-05 04:19:31', NULL),
(1466, 430, 822, 'New order 9 to 11 we see in word of God.. Genesis 9:18-10:30 focused on the son of Noah, one the other Genesis 11:1-9 city of Babel. \r\n\r\n1) Son of Noah \r\n   We see two main section 9:18 19 we find Noah tree son and how their distribution all earth \r\n9:20-29 is we see  Canaan the son of Ham Noah pronounced blessing on his other sons Shem and Japheth because they had treated his resspt \r\nMoses included this story in his description of the new order after the flood because the entire human race came from the three sons of Noah \r\n\r\n\r\n2) Defeat of Babel \r\n The story of Babel divided five symmetrical drastic steps first verse 1-2, second 3,4 vers \r\nPlan which the people had they interested to build a city with a great tower reaching to heaven so that they would be famous for all time \r\nFourth 6-7 balance this human plan by report God\'s counter plan God called his heavily army to attack the city \r\nSo we see that account to Moses life after flood was far from the paradise we might have', 6, '2020-04-30 16:39:06', '2020-05-05 04:19:31', NULL),
(1467, 430, 823, '1) we see more than 8 significant connection between Noah and Moses\r\n1) Moses connection between himself and Noah in the motif of violence, \r\nGenesis 6:13 flood come in earth because world was fill with violence \r\nAs Exodus 1-2 see Egyptian had inflicted much violence on the people of Israel prior \r\n\r\n2) Moses use of the team \" ark\" the Hebrew word for Noah ark through Genesis 6-9 is tevah ..this word Moses used only one place is Exodus 2:3- \r\nBoth places Moses\'s mentioned ark \r\n\r\n3) the important of divine covenant also established Noah as a precursor of Moses. As we have seen according to Gen 6:18 and 9:11noah Enter covenant with God \r\nWe see Exodus 19-24 illustrator so well Moses was chosen to lead the people of Israel into a special Covent \r\n\r\n4) connection between two men Genesis 6-9 God delivery Noah and his family by taking them safely through a flood that destroys the wicked of the earth \r\nSame thing Exodus 13-15 when Israel passing red sea then God destroyed the army of Egypt \r\n\r\n5) Genesis 8:1 \r\nAnd we see Exodus 14:12\r\n\r\n6) Gen6:19 \r\nGod brings animal als we see in Exodus many animals \r\n7) gen 8:1 \r\nExodus 6:5', 8, '2020-04-30 16:58:37', '2020-05-05 04:19:31', NULL),
(1468, 430, 824, 'Covenant \r\n  On the hand , Christ brought delivere to his people by means of a covenant that rescue them from the judgment of God as we have seen Noah played a special role as \r\nThe new Testament teache that Christ is our delivers because he mediation a new covenant when he come to this earth \r\nChrist came to the earth when God\'s people were under driven judgment \r\nSo we see that just as Noha delivere from judgment as the mediation of a sign \r\n\r\nVictory \r\n\r\n   In addition to bring a new covenant Jesus earlier ministry fulfilled the theme of victory in holy war . Moses focused on the theme of holy war as a Part of the new order after the flood. \r\n\r\nAs we should expect the new Testament dos not simply relate the themes of Genesis 6:9-11:', 6, '2020-04-30 17:11:45', '2020-05-05 04:19:31', NULL),
(1469, 430, 825, 'We will approach the question of modern application by following the new Testament description of the three stage of Christ kingdom we Wii look first at how the flood of delivering and the resulting new order apply to the inauguration of the kingdom in the first coming of Christ \r\n\r\nIn the inauguration of kingdom, Christ accomplish to the theme Moses emphasis in Genesis 6: 9- 11: \r\nWe can see thse connection in at least two ways . The covenant which Christ mediation, and the victory he accomplished \r\n\r\nIn light of the way the new Testament applies prime history to the inauguration and continuesation of the kingdom, it is not surprising to discover that the consummation of the kingdom is also described in terms of Noah flood and the warfare of the new primeval order', 6, '2020-04-30 17:24:35', '2020-05-05 04:19:31', NULL),
(1470, 440, 796, 'God\'s plan to redeem human beings from the corruption and the consequences of our sin was made before he created the universe. This timing is mentioned in places like Ephe. 3:11, which speaks of God\'s eternal purpose historically accomplished by Jesus. 2 Thess. 2:13, says that we were chosen for salvation from the beginning and 2 timothy 1:9, 10 speaks of grace that was given to us before the beginning of time. God\'s eternal decree of salvation was foreordained or decided before the world began. The word poorizo is also used in places like Romans 8:29,30 and Ephesians 1:5. We can all agree that God\'s decision to save sinners was made as part of eternal counsel before the foundation of the world.', 8, '2020-05-01 16:36:33', '2020-05-05 04:20:34', NULL),
(1471, 440, 797, 'God\'s eternal plan of redemption involves the work of all three persons of the trinity. The Father- originated the agreement because of his desire to redeem fallen human beings from the curse of sin. It was the Father\'s eternal purpose to accomplish our redemption through Christ (Eph. 3:10,11)\r\nThe Son- agreed to add a perfect human nature to his perfect divine nature to die on behalf of sinners. Paul said that we received grace in the Son before the beginning of time( 2 Tim 1:9). and just as God\'s eternal counsel decreed roles fro the Father and the Son, it also determined the Holy Spirit\'s part. The Holy Spirit- agreed to enable and empower the Son\'s work and to apply salvation to those whom the Son redeemed (2 Thess. 2:13).', 7, '2020-05-01 16:40:55', '2020-05-05 04:20:34', NULL),
(1472, 440, 798, 'The covenant of grace fulfills part of God\'s eternal plan for history. The father fulfilled the eternal decree in the covenant of grace by sending the Son and the Spirit to do their work, appointing the Son to the office of Messiah or Christ, giving the son His powerful spirit without limit, preparing the Son\'s perfect human nature. \r\nThe son fulfilled His eternal agreement to redeem humanity by: veiling his divine glory, adding a full human nature to his full divine nature living a perfect life, dying an atoning death. Holy spirit fulfilled his part in God\'s eternal counsel by: enabling and empowering the Son\'s incarnation and subsequent work , empowering Christ\'s death on the cross and His resurrection regenerating our spirits, empowering us to resist sin giving us spiritual gifts, securing our salvation.', 8, '2020-05-01 16:46:03', '2020-05-05 04:20:34', NULL),
(1473, 440, 799, 'God the Son, the second person of the trinity joined the covenant as its mediator. As the mediator, the Son intercedes for God\'s covenant people. He reconciles us to God by taking the blame and punishment for our sins. He preserves the integrity of the covenant and the lives of his people by suffering the covenant curses on our behalf. Similarly, through his obedience to the covenant\'s requirements of human loyalty, the Son earns the covenant blessings for himself. And then shares them with the sinners he redeems. The Son\'s mediation provided forgiveness and salvation for the old testament saints on the basis of his promised future work. The Son\'s mediation of the covenant of grace centered around his incarnation as Jesus his life of perfect faith and obedience, his death on the cross, his resurrection from the dead and his ascension to heaven. As mediator of covenant of grace, he fulfilled the covenant of works on our behalf and guaranteed that we would receive its blessings.', 9, '2020-05-01 16:52:00', '2020-05-05 04:20:34', NULL),
(1474, 440, 800, 'The covenant of grace was administered by various covenant representatives: Adam, Noah, Abraham, Moses, David and Jesus. \r\nAdam: The covenant of grace was instituted with Adam immediately after he fell into sin. The Adamic administration provided humanity the immediate opportunity to reconcile our relationship with God. \r\nNoah: The covenant confirmed with Noah after the flood explicitly incorporated all the terms of Adam\'s administration. The Noahic administration expanded the covenant blessings by adding God\'s promise never again to destroy the earth with flood waters. \r\nAbraham: Under Abraham, the covenant included the previous terms and added God\'s promises to turn Abraham\'s descendants into a mighty nation and to bless all nations through them. IN the Abrahamic administration, the nation of Israel was charged with expanding God\'s kingdom throughout the earth. \r\nMoses: With the Mosaic administration, God confirmed his promises to Abraham provided structure for Israel gave it the first codified version of the law redirected Israel to build his kingdom throughout the world.\r\nDavid: In the Davidic administration God confirmed the Mosaic administration revealed that the greatest covenant blessings would be fulfilled under the kingship of David and his dynastic heirs. \r\nJesus: Jesus\' administration is typically referred to as the \"new covenant\". In it, God established a permanent, unbreakable covenant in which his people would receive all his covenant blessings.', 9, '2020-05-01 17:03:04', '2020-05-05 04:20:34', NULL),
(1475, 439, 834, 'The Bible is divinely inspired , so it carries God\'s authority.\r\n1. CLAIM OF AUTHORITY-\r\nIn the earliest history recorded in the Bible , God spoke directly to humanity and his speech carried authority. All things were created by the power of his word. In the days of Moses  ,God encoded his spoken word in the written form . His spoken word is the basis for his written word. God\'s written word is his authoritative covenant document that his people are obligated to obey. Jesus frequently appealed to scripture to justify and explain his actions. Paul believed that the scriptures are God\'s authoritative word and that they bind New Testament believers.\r\nIMPLICATIONS \r\nBecause Scriptures carries  God\'s authority, we are morally obligated to conform all our choices, actions thoughts and feelings to it. We must keep the breadth of Biblical instruction . We are not to obey what we like and to ignore what we don not like. We all fall into the trap of unconscious selectivity. We must constantly be remind of those commands which we may have forgotten or overlooked. Only when we embrace the Scripture from the heart can we rightly submit to the authority of God\'s word.', 9, '2020-05-02 00:45:43', '2020-05-05 04:21:31', NULL),
(1476, 439, 835, 'When we look at several attributes of Scriptures, we have seen that Scripture is divinely inspires, it is powerful and authoritative. Because it is written for human beings, its is clear , necessary and sufficient. Keeping the attributes of Scripture in mind is helpful to us in many ways  s we study Christian ethics. It reminds us that Bible is indispensable when it comes to answering ethical questions.We must always see its answer because its is authoritative in all aspects of Life and there are many questions which only Bible can answer. Remembering the attributes of scripture is greatly encouraging as it reminds us that God has provided Scripture in order to benefit us about himself and His standards. Finally the attributes of Scriptures give us confidence in our ethical decisions as we are sure that the Bible\'s ethical teachings are both sufficient and clear. So it is important that we rely on the full range of Scriptures attributes as we progress in our study of christian ethics.', 8, '2020-05-02 00:56:19', '2020-05-05 04:21:31', NULL),
(1477, 439, 836, 'God wanted to give his people clear revelation concerning his will and his character in order that we would be better able to conform ourselves to him.Through due use of the ordinary means that is reading and studying we can come to know God\'s will for all areas of life . All scripture is clear enough to be useful. If we apply ourselves sufficiently, we can all come to know God\'s will well enough to conform ourselves to his standard for morality.\r\nPaul says in 2 Timothy 3:16 All scripture is useful  for teaching, rebuking, correcting and training in righteousness. All Scripture is clear enough to useful if we apply ourselves to study it diligently.\r\nIf we rightly under stand the  Bible, we will know God\'s standards sufficiently to make proper decisions', 8, '2020-05-02 01:12:43', '2020-05-05 04:21:31', NULL),
(1478, 439, 837, 'WE see the power of God\'s word through the preaching of his word or Gospel. God works through the preaching of the gospel even when the Preachers are not infallibly inspired. In Romans 1:15-16 Paul directly states that preached Gospel carries God\'s power. The gospel Paul had in mind was not just a set of truths about what Jesus had done, nor the power pf God represented but the statements of the gospel, but Paul meant that the act of preaching the gospel is powerful , because God uses the preaching to brings people to faith.\r\nPeople sometimes count the message of gospel as foolish because they don not believe that its statements are true. TO some it sounds like fanatical tale, but to the people who believes it is the power of God. because it is the means by which God brings them to a saving knowledge of truth.\'So we should also preach the gospel to whomever and wherever and as much as possible, because the act of preaching of gospel is its powerful and God shall bring many to faith, when we do it.', 9, '2020-05-02 01:27:47', '2020-05-05 04:21:31', NULL),
(1479, 439, 838, 'There are different ways ,the various parts and aspects of Scripture communicate God\'s norm to us. Scripture communicates in different ways. It contains statements, questions,offers, curses,threats,advice, commands,summations, desire, love and much more.It includes sarcasm and sincere language.\r\nLanguage \r\nThe bible displays the full range of language that we find in human communication. If we don\'t understand how each type of language communicates, we are likely to understand the Bible.\r\nEXTRAORDINARY-\r\nThose who believe that Bible speaks in extraordinary ways often oversimplify biblical language , developing a system of interpretation that can applied fairly equally to all of scripture. Because the Bible is inspired by God, it communicates in extraordinary ways that can exceed human comprehension. Many Christians also insisted that the Scriptures extraordinary nature makes its language easy to interpret. \r\nORDINARY-\r\nThe Bible communicates in ordinary language using all the normal conventions of human communication.WE have to learn how the ordinary language is used and what was each author\'s intent when he wrote.', 9, '2020-05-02 01:43:18', '2020-05-05 04:21:31', NULL),
(1480, 439, 839, 'Ten commandments have a special primacy over Scriptures\'s other commandments, both historical and theological. \r\nHistorical\r\n1.It was the first written legal code received by the nation of Israel\r\n2. Book of the covenant : the additional laws was received with the Ten Commandments\r\n3. Paul sates that the Ten commandments was the introduction of laws, by receiving it , Israel became a special nation , His own people, A Holy nation\r\nTheological \r\n1.God carved the Ten Commandments in the stone tablets .The giving of the law was attended by thunder and lightening, smoke, clouds and heavenly trumpets. it was given on special occasion with special attention and with /god carving it by himself making it special laws.\r\n2 Moses identified the Ten commandments as God\'s very covenant with his people\r\n3. The Ten commandments were placed within the ark of Covenant.', 8, '2020-05-02 01:55:14', '2020-05-05 04:21:31', NULL),
(1481, 439, 840, 'The various laws of the Old testament has been Categorized into three groups:\r\n1. Moral - God\'s ethical standards: usually identified with the ten Commandments\r\n2. Civil-Provide for the governing of society\r\n3. Ceremonial- Provide instruction for worshipping God\r\nThreefold division  helps us see that the Law regulated all of life and it also reflects a genuine distinction that scripture draws between the three offices that governed Israel\'s theocracy which are 1. Prophet 2.Priest and 3. King\r\nAPPLICATION\r\nGod\'s people are no longer to perform many of the specific behaviors that were required under the Mosaic sacrificial and temple system. The civic and ceremonial laws of the Old Testament have expired in the sense that we are not to return to the old patterns of life.\r\nGod\'s character requires us to learn from the revelation these laws provide. Every law continue to reveal God\'s standard until everything is accomplished. Ceremonial and civic laws are useful for training us in the ways of righteousness.\r\nAs Priest, as King, as prophet Christ fulfills the ceremonial ,civic and moral aspects of law respectively.', 9, '2020-05-02 02:11:26', '2020-05-05 04:21:31', NULL),
(1482, 439, 841, 'Since the death, burial , resurrection and ascension of Christ, we are no longer to perform many of the specific behaviors that were required under the Mosaic sacrificial  and temple system . WE are no longer to maintain the temple or to restrict women and gentiles from access to God\'s holy presence or to sacrifice animals for our sin. The whole categories of laws don\'t apply to modern Christians.\r\nBut I would definitely make it clear to my dear friend that the Civic and the ceremonial laws still guide us as God\'s standard today just as the moral laws do, it is the revelation of who God is and what he is like, And God\'s character has not changed.\r\nMatthew 5:18-19 teaches us the continuing modern application of every old Testament Law, down to the last one. According to Jesus every law will continue to reveal God\'s standard everything is accomplished.\r\nBible consistently teaches us that the law is a unified whole , that it stands together, without regard to distinctions as whole.All of scripture not just some parts is for our moral instruction means that ceremonial and civic laws as well as moral laws have something to teach us about modern ethics.', 9, '2020-05-02 02:27:16', '2020-05-05 04:21:31', NULL),
(1483, 441, 786, 'The office of image of God is rooted in the authority God delegated to humanity. God appointed human beings to rule over his creation on his behalf.\r\nGenesis 1:27-28\r\n\"God created man in His own image........Be fruitful and increase in number, fill the earth and subdue it.........\"\r\nScripture introduces us an image of God, it says that we govern creation.\r\nOne aspect of image of God is that we hold the office of delegated ruler.In theological terms we are \r\n God\'s \"vice-reagents or his administrative deputies or his servant or \'vassals kings.\r\nWe are authorized to fill the earth with God\'s images, to govern all earth\'s creatures and subdue the earth itself.\r\nWe fill the earth by multiplying our numbers, and carrying God\'s representative presence  with us and establishing human culture everywhere we go', 8, '2020-05-04 18:29:03', '2020-05-05 04:16:20', NULL),
(1484, 441, 787, 'The first thing the scripture says about humanity is that we are the image and likeness of God Genesis 1:26\r\nWe are God\'s image and likeness because we rule over the earth as God \'s servant kings and are endowed with the necessary qualities and abilities to perform our duties.\r\nWe are images of God , we rule on His behalf , carry out His will and reflect His glory( 1 Corinthian 11:7)\r\nGenesis 1:27-28\r\n As we hold the office of God we are given the authority to fill the earth with God\'s image , govern all earths\' creature and subdue the earth\r\nOur role or office as image of Go elevates all humanity to the level of royalty.\r\n1 Corinthians 11:7  Man ......is the image and glory of God\r\nWe are still full images of God and not mere shadows , we still rule on his behalf , carry out his will and reflect his glory.', 8, '2020-05-04 18:44:59', '2020-05-05 04:16:20', NULL),
(1485, 441, 788, 'Christians have understood that the image of God in human beings includes our capacity to think rationally and process complex emotions.This rational ability was lost in our fall into sin. We can see it in following passages\r\n1. Ecclesiastes 9:3 and Jeremiah 17:9 here we see human beings being irrational and insane.at times\r\n2.Deuteronomy 29:2,3 where the minds of the Israelite couldn\'t understand the miracles performed by God\r\n3. John 8:43-47 Jesus explained that unbelievers were the children of the devil who is the father of lies and as a result they believed lies and are incapable of accepting the truth.\r\n4 Ephesians 4:17,18 says that our fall into sin damaged our ability to think  and to understand the world from God\'s perspective\r\n\r\nOUR RESTORATION OF RATIONAL CAPABILITIES\r\n1. 1 CORINTHIANS  2:11 says  that God has given us Holy spirit and the mind of Christ so that we can understand reality in the same way the God does.\r\n2. Colossians 3:10 says that the restoration of our rational abilities is an  aspect of the image of God being renewed in us. When we come to faith in Christ , God begins to restore that aspect of his image in us.', 9, '2020-05-04 18:58:12', '2020-05-05 04:16:20', NULL),
(1486, 441, 789, 'When God appointed humanity to the  office of his image , he created a variety of relationships. Three aspects of covenant relationships that are specific to our role as God\' images are:\r\n1. REFLECT GOD\' S CHARACTER:\r\nWe are intended to reflect his character (pure, holy and righteous) wherever they appear(1 Peter 1:15-16, Hebrews 12:14)\r\n 2. PROMOTE PURE WORSHIP\r\nBecause human beings are the real image of God, idols and other non human representation of him are false images.\r\n God is  the true God and is not to be treated like the false gods of the nations (Deuteronomy 4:15,16)\r\n3. BUILD GOD\'S KINGDOM\r\nGod commanded humanity to fill the earth , instructing bus to place image of himself throughout the world (Genesis 1:28)', 8, '2020-05-04 19:12:10', '2020-05-05 04:16:20', NULL),
(1487, 441, 790, 'We are God\'s vice -regent,we are told to fill the earth and subdue it, but it gives us a great responsibility towards all those things which we are given to take care of. Our responsibilities over the earth and its creatures indicate that the world doesn\'t exist empty for our own use. On the contrary it primarily exists for God\'s use.So as His image  its our job to guard and manage those things he called good and to cultivate them, in ways that improve them rather than harm them.\r\nBeing God\'s image we should take care how we relate to God and to other people and the world around us. As God\'s representative on earth, our thoughts, behaviors and emotions reflect on him.\r\nAnd I personally take care to carry out my role in the family, around my home, in the church and ministry given to me as God\'s steward or His faithful  representative, accomplishing his purposes, benefiting his creation and creatures and bringing him glory.', 8, '2020-05-04 19:26:19', '2020-05-05 04:16:20', NULL),
(1488, 447, 771, 'The letter clearly identifies a man named \'James\' as the author. Two men named James had enough authority in the early church to write a letter like this: James, son of Zebedee and James the brother of Jesus- leader of the early church in Jerusalem. Critical scholars still offer at least three arguments for this objection. Three arguments by scholars for\r\n 1) Psuedonymity: No relation to Jesus- there is no mention of the author\'s relation to Jesus but Jude never mentioned his blood ties in his epistle either. \r\n2) Hellenistic culture- the book gives evidence that the author was aware of Greek culture. Many Jews in Palestine had knowledge of Hellenistic philosophy and religion. \r\n3) Inconsistencies- some ideas in the epistle don\'t match James\' theological outlooks in other new Testament books(Acts 21:17-25, Galatians 2:12). James position on the law is actually consistent with his theology in Acts and Galatians.', 8, '2020-05-12 16:38:29', '2020-05-19 01:41:20', NULL),
(1489, 447, 772, 'James identifies his readers as \'\'the twelve tribes scattered among the nation\'\'(1:2) and believers in our glorious Lord Jesus Christ (2:1). These verses indicate that James\' original audience was made up, primarily of Jewish Christians who lived outside of Palestine. It is possible that these were members of the Jerusalem church scattered throughout Judea and Samaria following Stephen\'s Martyrdom. James vocabulary supports the idea that his original readers were Jewish followers of Jesus. \"Synagoge\"- reference to Jewish gatherings. \"Kurios Saboth\"- from a common Old Testament name for God of Israel. There were also many Gentiles converts to Judaism who attended synagogues (Acts 8, 10)', 8, '2020-05-12 16:44:10', '2020-05-19 01:41:20', NULL),
(1490, 447, 773, 'James lived and ministered in Jerusalem until he was martyred in AD 62. His audience was most likely scattered throughout Judea and Samaria, as far as Phoenicia, Antioch and Cyprus. Date- The earliest likely date for the letter\'s composition is AD 44. He became a significant leader of the early church in Jerusalem, by the time Peter was released from prison in AD 44. The latest possible of composition for the epistle is AD 62, when he was matryed. Two reasons to think that the date of composition was earlier in this timeline: James\' use of the word: \'Synagogue\"- James may have written before Christians were forced out of the synagogues. \r\nPurpose- No mention of Jewish- Gentile controversies- it\'s likely that they hadn\'t yet become a factor for James\' audience. He called his audience to pursue wisdom from God, so that they would joy in their trials. These trials appear to have led some to abandon their loyalty to Christ and pursue \"friendship with the world\".', 8, '2020-05-12 16:51:58', '2020-05-19 01:41:20', NULL),
(1491, 447, 774, 'James\' epistle reflects a long history of wisdom literature stemming from the Old Testament; Job, Ecclesiastes, Proverbs.\"wisdom psalms\", prophetic wisdom sayings. James also reflects the contents of influential wisdom books outside of Scripture: (5:11) to promote perseverance. Beyond this, James touched on topics such as speech, the treatment of widows and orphans, poverty, and favoritism. These topics reflect numerous parallels with the content of the book of Proverbs. \r\nThe wisdom of Sirach (e.g James 1:5, and Sirach 1:26). The wisdom of Solomon. In addition to these types of wisdom literature, much of Jesus\' instruction recorded in the Gospels is characteristic of wisdom teaching in Israel. And interpreters have noted a number of similarities between James\' writing and Jesus\' instruction.', 8, '2020-05-12 16:58:51', '2020-05-19 01:41:20', NULL),
(1492, 447, 775, 'First words about the wisdom began with a call to joy. James 1:2- Consider it pure joy, my brothers and sister, whenever you face trials of many kinds. This passage may seem odd to us, especially because it addresses people who were facing \" trials of many kinds\". But James\' appeal to consider this pure joy is not as unusual as we might think. The phrase \"pure joy\" comes from the Greek expression pasan charan that may be translated unmitigated joy.\" This kind of encouragement fits well with other wisdom literature of James\' day. Many times wisdom writings encouraged those who suffered to consider themselves blessed. Jesus, for instance, closed the beatitudes in Matthew 5:12 with the call to \"rejoice and be glad\" in the face of persecution. It\'s often difficult to see the benefits of suffering so James told his readers to pursue wisdom from God(1:5). Wisdom strengthens our confidence that God has ordained for us the blessing of eternal salvation.', 9, '2020-05-12 17:08:06', '2020-05-19 01:41:20', NULL),
(1493, 448, 761, 'Son was at the Father\'s side during creation, and the Father created the world through the Son. Everything that was created by the Father was through the Son. Without the Son, nothing was created.', 6, '2020-05-15 15:07:43', '2020-05-19 01:42:30', NULL),
(1494, 448, 762, 'God\'s eternal counsel regarding Christ was that, Christ was to to be the redeemer of mankind, God\'s eternal counsel was the plan of God for the universe, which was in place even before the foundations of the world was laid. That Jesus would appear in human flesh as both the Son of Man and the Son of God and redeem mankind, after completing the work of redemption, would be resurrected back to life and present Himself before the Heavenly Father and continue His task as the mediator, seated at the right hand of the Father.', 7, '2020-05-15 15:16:25', '2020-05-19 01:42:30', NULL),
(1495, 448, 763, 'God\'s promises are immutable.\r\nCovenant of Redemption. The Trinity promised to redeem fallen mankind. Immediately after the fall of mankind. The Son began to work on on the plan of redemption. The Son began to save sinners.\r\nCovenant of Grace : Arrangement made between the Father & the Son. \r\nAdamic Covenant : Redemption was first offered to mankind\r\nNohaic Covenant : Promise to preserve human beings until Son\'s redeeming work was completed\r\nAbrahamic Covenant : Promise that of the descendants of Abraham, the Redeemer would come into this earth.\r\nMosaic Covenant : Institution of a sacrificial system was introduced\r\nDavidic Covenant : Promise that the Redeemer would be born of the descendants of David\r\nNew Covenant : The workd of redemption was and is being fulfilled', 7, '2020-05-15 15:29:15', '2020-05-19 01:42:30', NULL),
(1496, 448, 764, 'Jesus redeeming work for sinners, consisted of his appearance in the flesh as the redeemer of mankind, in full obedience to the Father\'s will and accomplishing everything in accordance with the Father. Mainly can be categorized as follows :\r\n\r\nInauguration of Kingdom : Jesus brought the Kingdom of God on this earth during His days. Jesus taught and preached about the kingdom of God, sayinv that the Kingdom of God is come unto all, and also invited everyone to be partakers of the kingdom of God. \r\n\r\nJesus fulfilled all the requirements of the law in obedience to the Father, As the first Adam sinned due to disobedience, the second Adam, Jesus through obedience full filled the task of redemption. Jesus life on earth was in perfect obedience to the Father\'s will, even unto death on the cross. And by His obedience, Christ gained the lost blessings back to mankind. \r\n\r\nBible speaks about the passsive obedience wherein his submission  to a life of humiliation and suffering, culminating to His death, fulfilled God\'s requirement as punishment for the sins of mankind. Through the life of Jesus on this earth, His obedience to God, His sufferings and death fulfilled God\'s mandate of judgement for all of mankind. \r\n\r\nAlso there is the Active Obedience - wherein Jesus obeyed the laws of God. Jesus completely obeyed God\'s commandments, life was without sin. Fulfilled God\'s requirement of righteousness, called as forensic righteousness. Hence gave an opportunity for mankind to approach heavenly Father, who looks allows us to approach the throne of grace through His Son Jesus.', 8, '2020-05-15 15:44:47', '2020-05-19 01:42:30', NULL),
(1497, 448, 765, 'The consummation of the heavens and the earth, during Jesus return to the earth, the following will happen with regards to the last judgment :\r\n\r\nDestruction of all God\'s enemes, the blessings of His peop.le and the complete renewal of creation itself, where God\'s redeemed people will dwell forever. \r\n\r\nJesus Return : \r\nJesus return will both be a physical and personal return. He will return the ame way as He ascended to heaven, just like the angels had advised. \r\nIt will be both a public and visible return. Everyone will see Him.\r\nJesus second coming will be triumphant. He will return as a conqueror, as a King of Kings & Lord of Lords. \r\nJesus return will be sudden, like a thief in the night. Only the Father in heaven knows when Christ will return.\r\n\r\nThe events that will take place during Jesus returns.\r\n\r\nGeneral Resurrection : \r\nAll of mankind, who has died will all be resurrected. Both the wicked and righeous. The righteous will be transformed into heavenly bodeis and will live for ever. . But the wicked and unrigheous will face judgement. No one will escape the process. The righteous will receive a uncorruptible body, to live with our God for ever. \r\n\r\nLast Judgement\r\nAll of mankind - wicked and unrigheous will stand before the seat of Judment and will have to give account of their life on the earth. Every aspect & deed will be judged as per the standards of God. \r\nBut those of mankind who received forgiveness by grace will escape the seat of judgement, and they will receive their rewards according to their works during their sojourn on the earth. \r\n\r\nRenewal of Creation \r\nThe present world and creation will be purged of all sins and and will be destroyed with fire. Thereafter God will bring about the New Jerusalem adorned from heaven. There will no more be any sorrow, sickness or pain.  God Himself will be the light. \r\nAll of creation will be restored back to God\'s original plan and everyone will live for ever with God. Everyone will partake from the Tree of Life and worship God forever and ever.', 9, '2020-05-15 16:06:02', '2020-05-19 01:42:30', NULL),
(1498, 449, 776, 'The majority of interpreters reject Pauline authorship. \r\nFirst, Anonymity: this book is anonymous and it was Paul\'s practice to name himself in his epistles. In fact, as 2 Thessalonians 2: 2 makes clear, Paul was deeply concerned that forgeries had spread under his name. So, it seems unlikely that he would have failed to identify himself had he written Hebrews. \r\nSecond. Themes, the book of Hebrews emphasizes subjects that don\'t receive much, if any, attention in Paul\'s letter. For instance, author of Hebrews mentioned Melchizedek three times. He drew attention to the Old Testament tabernacle. And he dealt at length with Christ as the high priest. Taken together, these themes distinguish the book of Hebrews from books that we know were written by Paul. \r\nThird. Generation: the strongest reason for doubting Pauline authorship is the way the writer of Hebrews distanced himself from the first generation of Jesus\' followers.', 9, '2020-05-17 16:37:04', '2020-05-19 01:41:47', NULL),
(1499, 449, 777, 'The author wrote to a specific audience with whom he was personally familiar. \r\n1. Jewish- the author referred to the Old Testament Israelites as \"our forefathers\". It\'s no wonder, that from as early as the time of tertullian, who lived from AD 155-230, the title attached is \"Pros Hebraious\",\"For the Hebrews\". \r\n2. Hellenistic- Hebrews contains theological teachings that were common among Jews living outside of Palestine. The content of Hebrews indicates that the audience was familiar with theological teachings that were more common among Jews living outside of Palestine than among more traditional Jewish circles within Palestine.\r\n3. Immature- The original audience may have remained theologically immature because they didn\'t respect their leaders. In heb 5.11- the author reprimanded his audience for being \'\'slow to learn\'\'. \r\n4. Persecuted- As we read, it is evident that original audience has already faced persecution in the past, some in the present, perhaps more severely in future.\r\n5. Near Apostasy- as the audience faced persecution, some of them were near apostasy. Rather than simply being discouraged or weakened by sufferings, they were in danger of turning away from Christ entirely.', 9, '2020-05-17 16:48:13', '2020-05-19 01:41:47', NULL),
(1500, 449, 778, 'Hebrews employs many literary devices that were associated with persuasive oratory or urgent debate in 1st century:\r\n1. One rhetorical device called synkrisis is a detailed comparison between two or more things designed to convince audience to affirm speaker\'s point of view, For eg, Heb 7:11-28. Rather than asserting his belief, author gave a compelling eight point comparison between Melchizedek and Christ. \r\n2. Another one is exempla. Exempla are lists of illustrations or examples that follow one after the other to build a persuasive argument for a paticular point of view. This technique appears in familiar list of faithful in Heb.11\r\n3. Third is known as Hebrew expression qol wahomer. This expression is well known from both Greco- Roman and rabbinical traditions and can be translated \"light to heavy\" \"less to great\" etc. This argument says that because simple premise is true then surely the more difficult conclusion must also be true.', 8, '2020-05-17 16:56:32', '2020-05-19 01:41:47', NULL),
(1501, 449, 779, 'In Hebrews 5.12 it says of the need of \"milk\" is an expression used for immature believers. The one who needs milk is compared to a spiritual baby and is unskillful in the word of righteousness. Those who are known to the basic principles of the oracles of God, are compared to the one who can have strong meat which is they have their senses exercised to discern both good and evil. \r\nIn my spiritual life, I think need doctrinal progress in the area of sensitive issues like trinity, Christian ethical theology and modern generational cults and keeping up with the new gen theologies like Holy spirit and speaking of tongues etc. I believe in the need to improve the skills and spiritual knowledge to counterattack these, and win over arguments regarding the genuine truth of basic biblical doctrines, with theology and truth.', 8, '2020-05-17 17:12:18', '2020-05-19 01:41:47', NULL),
(1502, 449, 780, 'One of the most recent false teaching I have come across is the questioning of the Baptism of holy spirit and the gift of speaking of tongues. They claimed that there is nothing as such as speaking in tongues and its gifts. The strategy to claim it false was from the scriptures as it says in  1 Corinthians 6.5, where it clearly says that it speaks in tongues edifies himself and speaks to God. \r\nAnother one false teaching was like variety of Gnosticism, that committing sins done by the body won\'t affect the spirit. But the word of God clearly says that our body is the temple of the Living God and the Holy Spirit dwells in it. So we should glorify God with our Body and it should be Holy.', 8, '2020-05-17 17:22:23', '2020-05-19 01:41:47', NULL),
(1503, 451, 654, 'उत्तर = आरंभिक कलीसिया के पास इन चारों समाचारों में अटूट विश्वास के कम से कम तीन कारण थे|\r\n1)पहला -: कलीसीया इस चारो सुसमाचारो को प्रमाणित रूप में ग्रहण किया क्योंकि वह अपने शीर्षक में वे विश्वासयोग्य लेखकों के द्वारा लिखे गए थे।बहुत अधिक संभावना है कि सुसमाचार मूल रूप से नाम रहे थे परंतु संभावना यह भी है कि जब वह पहली बार प्रकाशित किए गए तो उन्हें उन लोगों के द्वारा स्वीकार किया गया जो लेखकों को जानने थे या फिर शायद लेखकों को पहचानते हुए स्रोतों के साथ उन्हें वितरित भी किया और अनामिक समय से ही मसीही लेखकों ने सुसमाचार को मत्ती मरकुस लुका योजना के साथ जोड़ा अर्थात ऐसे चार लोग जो नए नियम में कलीसाई अब वह के साथ अच्छी प्रतिष्ठा में जाने जाते हैं\r\n2)दूसरा -: आरंभिक मसीही कैनन महसूस समाचारों की स्थान के प्रति भी विश्वत थे क्योंकि वह इस बात को जानते थे कि इस पुस्तक को पोर्णित अनुमोदन मिला है मत्ती और यमुना पीड़ित है यीशु के शब्द और कार्यों के गवाते मरकुस के बारे में कहा जाता है कि उसने अपनी कॉपी बातों को पत्र से लिया था जिसे मरकुस के स्रोत से मेरा पुत्र के रूप में संबोधित किया है और हम लुका 1:1-14 मैं पहले ही देख चुके हैं कि लुक्का ने स्पष्ट किया था कि उसने अपने कार्य को गवाह के गुणों पर आधारित किया है\r\nइससे बढ़कर अपनी कृति ैक्लेसियस्टिकल हिस्ट्री में अशुभ या स्नेह दर्शाया कि प्रेरित योजना ने अपना सुसमाचार लिखने से पहले से तीनों सुसमाचार का अनुमोदन किया सुनी अपनी कृति की पुस्तक 3 अध्याय 24 खंड साथ में प्रेरित होना के बारे में  एसुबीएस ने क्या कहा मत्ती मरकुस और लुका के तीनों सुसमाचार सब लोगों के हाथ में आ गए और उनके अपने हाथ में भी वह कहते हैं कि उसने उन्हें स्वीकार किया और उनकी सत्यता की गवाही दी\r\n3)तीसरा -: सभी चारों सुसमाचार पहली सदी की कलीसिया की गवाही से समर्थित है चारों पुस्तके इतनी पुरानी है क्योंकि जीवन और सेव काय के जीवित गवा उनके विवरणों को ठुकरा ने उनकी पुष्टि करने के योग्य थे और ऐसा हुआ भी गवाहों ने बहुत आराम से ही अपनी कविताओं में उन्हें स्वीकार करके उनकी पुष्टि की परमेश्वर अपने वचन में अपनी आवाज की गवाही देता है परंतु हमारी सहायता के लिए हम उन ऐतिहासिक घटनाओं को देख सकते हैं जिनका उल्लेख पवित्र शास्त्र में किया गया और हम देख सकते हैं कि उन बातों से संबंधित है जिन्हें हम इतिहास के रूप में अन्य स्रोतों में जानते हैं\r\nऔर अधिक सामान्य रूप में हम देख सकते हैं कि सामान्य परिस्थितियां राजनीतिक परिस्थितियां भौगोलिक दशा और बाइबिल में उल्लेखित यह सभी अन्य प्रकार की सामान्य बातें वह सब उन सब के स्वरूप है जो उस समय लिखे गए जिन्हें हम ऐतिहासिक समाधि कहते हैं  जिसमें की पहली सदी कपलेश्वर भी शामिल है जब हम सुसमाचार लिखे गए थे परंतु जब हम बाइबिल में विशेष ऐतिहासिक बातों को देखते हैं और जिन ऐतिहासिक दशा और परिस्थितियों का वर्णन करती है तो यहां हमें इस बात को जानने का एक तर्कसंगत धार प्रदान करता है|\r\nकि वे अपने कहे हुए समय में आती है आत्मा की गवाही से हम इस सच्चे विश्वास को प्राप्त करते हैं कि वह परमेश्वर का वचन है अता आरंभिक अलीशा के पहली और दूसरी सर्दियों में कैनन में शामली चारों से समाचारों को कि आज हमारे पास है जो पिरितिया सारे प्रतीकों की स्रोत द्वारा सर्व भूमिक रूप से स्वीकार किया गया और उन्हें यीशु के कार्य और उनके जीवन और उसकी सुचिता ओके विश्वास क्योंकि हम एवं सच्ची साहित्य के रूप में माना गया इस बात पर विश्वास करने के कई कारण है कि सुसमाचार विश्वास नहीं है प्रेरणा प्राप्त है और उनमें ऐसी कई बातें हैं जिन्हें हम सीधी या सरल कह सकते हैं\r\nपरंतु सबसे महत्वपूर्ण बात यह है गांव ने अपनी गवाही को अपने जीवन के साथ प्रमाणित किया आप सोचेंगे कि कोरे खाने पीते जाने का कारावास में डाले जाने क्रूस पर चढ़ाए जाने से पहले किसी एक ने तो कहा होता अरे तुम तो जानते हो ही हो यहां तो बस एक का ही निर्भर है जो उन्होंने कहा उसके लिए उन्होंने अपनी जान दे दी निसंदेह हम जानते हैं कि लोग मरने के लिए तैयार रहते हैं लोकप्रिय झूठ के लिए भी मरते हैं अधिकांश लोग जो छूट के लिए मरते हैं वह नहीं जानते कि वह छूट है बहुत ही कम लोग छूट के बारे में सच्चाई को जानते हुए भी उनके लिए मर जाते हैं यदि वहां उन्हें उनके जीवन काल में अधिकार धनिया वैज्ञानिक प्रदान करता है उन्हें उनमें से कुछ भी नहीं मिलता वे इस दुनिया में कुछ भी नहीं थे वे लगातार भागते रहे वे गरीबों में रहे उन्हें उन्होंने बलिदान किया उन्हें पीटा गया और फिर मर गए उनमें हम पूरी तरह से आश्वस्त हो सकते हैं कि वह सब वास्तव में हुआ था|', 8, '2020-05-20 14:54:12', '2020-06-02 01:57:11', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(1504, 451, 757, 'उत्तर  = जब हम सुसमाचारों के सय्योजन के बारे में बात करते है तो हमारे मन में यहाँ बात है की वे किस प्रकार से लिखे गए है उनके लेखन कोण थे उनोहोने इस पुस्तक को कियु लिखा ? उनोहने इस पुस्तक कैसे लिखी मसीहियों के लिए ें जैसे प्रश्नो को खोजना महत्वपूर्ण है कियुकी अनेक व्याख्याकारों ने ें पुस्तकों के देवीय अधिकर को काम करने के लिए सय्योजन की मानवीय प्रकिर्या पर धयान केन्द्रत किया है परन्तु शुबहा सन्देश या है की सावधानी से ही हुवी जांच हमें इस बात से प्रतीत अवश्य होने का हर कारण प्रदान करती है की सुसमाचार केवल मनुष्य दुवारा लिखी करतिया ही नहीं है बल्कि परमेश्वर का वचन भी है हम सुसमाचार के सयोजन से सबधित तीन विसयो को देखंगे पहला हम भिन्न सुसमाचारिक विवरणों के बिच पाई जाने वाली समानताओं की जांच करंगे दूसरा हम सयोजन के कुछ ऐसे सिद्धन्तो का सर्वेछण करंगे जिनका उदय ें समानताओं को ेस्पस्ट करने के लिए हुवा है और तीसरा हम उन निश्चितता के बिच पाए जाने वाली समानताओं पर धियान देने के दुवारा आरभ करे | \r\nसमानताए-:\r\nचाहे ये अलग अलग लिखे गए हो फिर भी मेथुव मरकुस लुका के सुसमाचार विवरणों को एक साथ रखा जाताहै और उन्हें समदरसी सुसमाचार कहा जाता है शब्द समदर्शी का अर्थ है एक साथ दिखना और इसे इसलिए इनसुसमाचारों पर लागु किया जाता है उनमे अधिकांश एक सामान वार्डन पाए जाते है उन में येशु के शब्दों और कार्यो के अनेक सामान वरदान पाए जाते है और जब वे यीशु के सामान कथनो को बताते है तो वे प्राय: समन सब्दो का भी इस्तेमाल करते है| \r\nउदाहरण के तोर पर लकवे के रोगी को यीशु दुवारा दी गई चंगाई पर ध्यान दीजिये मेथुव ९:६मे हम परभी के वचनो और कार्यो के इस वार्डन को पड़ते है:\r\nपरन्तु इसलिए की तुम जान लो की मनुष्य के पुत्र को पृथवी पर पाप छमा करने का अधिकार है तब उसने लकवे के रोगी से कहा उठ अपनी खाट उठा और अपने घर चलजा मेथुव ९:६ \r\nअब मरकुस २:१०-११ को सुने \r\nपरंति जिसे तुम जान लो की मनुष्य के पुत्र को पृथ्वी पर पाप छमा करने का भी अधिकार है उसने उस लकवे के रोगी से कहा मई तुम से कहता हु उठ खाट उठाकर अपने घर चलजा मरकुस २:१०-११ \r\nऔर फिर लुका ५:२४ \r\nपरन्तु इसलिए की तुम जान लो की मनुष्य के पुत्र को पृथ्वी पर पाप छमा करने का भी अधिकर है उसने उस लकवे के रोगी से कहा मै तुझ से कहता हु उठ और अपनी खाट उठाकर अपने घर चलजा लुका ५:२४  \r\nइस उदाहरण मै हम देखते है की प्रत्येक समदर्शी सुसमाचार में चमत्कार की कहानी का सामान शब्दों में वार्डन पाया जाता है अन्य समानांतर कहानिया तीन में से काम दो समदर्शी सुसमाचारों मै पाए जाती है कोड़ी को चंगा करना कफरनहूम में दुष्टत्मा को निकलना पाट्र्स की सास को चंगा करना झील में आए तूफान को संत करना येर की मर्त लड़की को जीवित करना बारहो को अधिकार देना यीशु का पनो पर चलना सूखे हुवे हाथ के वयक्ति को चंगाई देना कुछ रोटियां और कुछ मछलिया से पांच हजार लोगो को भोजन खिलाना और यीशु का रूपांतर होना |[समदर्शी सुसमाचार के प्रति होना के सुसमाचार का अधिकांश विवरण बिल्कुल अलग है जहां योना ने भी वर्णन किया कि यीशु पानी पर चला उनके 5000 लोगों को भोजन खिलाया वहीं उसने ऐसी घटनाओं का वर्णन भी किया जो समुद्र से समाचार में नहीं पाए जाते\r\n: उहरण के तौर पर युवाओं ने यीशु के के पानी को दहशत में बदलना शामली स्त्री के साथ यीशु के वार्तालाप और मृत्यु में से लार्जर को जीवित करना का विवरण दिया\r\nयीशु की सेव करें और जीवन की कहानी चारों सुसमाचार में भिन्नता से पाई जाती है फिर भी चारों यीशु के बपतिस्मा अपने चेलों के साथ यीशु के अंतिम भोज क्रॉस पर यीशु की मृत्यु और मृत्यु को से यीशु के पुनरुत्थान की गवाही देते हैं   समाचारों में पाई जाने वाली समानता और असमानता होने कई प्रतिष्ठित परिकलन को प्रेरित किया है था आइए अब समाचारों के संयोजन के सिद्धांतों की ओर मुड़ेके\r\nसयोजन के सिद्धांत-:\r\nसमदर्शी सु समाचारों के बीच पाए जाने वाले अनेक समानता ओं के कारण विद्वानों ने उनके संयोजन इतिहास के बारे में कई सिद्धांत विकसित किया है यह सिद्धांत प्रिया काफी जटिल होते हैं और जब हम पहले पहल उनका ध्यान करना आरंभ करते हैं तो वे काफी असमंजस भरे होते हैं हम सबसे लोकप्रिय सिद्धांतों को इस प्रकार से सर्ग भारित कर सकते हैं अधिकांश व्याख्या कार मानते हैं कि मध्य उसका समाचार सबसे पहले लिखा गया था और फिर मत थी और लोका ने मर्ग उसके विवरणों का इस्तेमाल किया\r\nशायद अन्य स्रोतों के विवरणों का भी परंतु अन्य व्याख्या कार मानते हैं कि मध्य पहले लिखा गया था और मरकुस ने मत्ती  के विवरणों का प्रयोग किया और लुका ने मती और मरकुस दोनों की वर्णों का इस्तेमाल किया और अन्य मानते हैं कि मध्य और लुका ऐसे स्रोतों पर आधारित थे जो अब हमारे पास नहीं है और की  मरकुस ने उन दोनों की बिरलोका का इस्तेमाल किया जैसे कि आप देख सकते हैं इन सिद्धांतों की सामान्य विशेषताओं की तुलना करना भी कुछ असमंजस भरा हो सकता है\r\nइसके विपरीत होने का संयोजन काफी सरल है अधिकांश व्याख्या का रस समान होते हैं कि उसने पहली सदी के लगभग अंत में लिखा था और वहां कम से कम एक और शायद सारे समंदर से विवरणों से परिचित था कभी-कभी या सुझाव दिया जाता है कि उसने उन सारे विवरणों को नहीं दोहराया जिनके बारे में वहां जानता था कि वे समदर्शी विवरणों में थे और इसलिए उसने उन अतिरिक्त जानकारी को प्रदान करने का निर्णय किया जो उन समुदायों के लिए सबसे प्रासंगिक थी जिनमें वहां सेवा करता था\r\nसंयोजन के इन सिद्धांतों कमान मन में रखते हुए आइए हम उस अनिश्चितता के बारे में बात करें जिससे हमें पकड़े रहना चाहिए\r\nनिश्चिता-:\r\nआराम से ही हमें यहां पहचान लेना चाहिए कि बाइबल के अनेक लेखकों ने प्रया मौखिक और लिखित परंपराओं का इस्तेमाल किया और इस बात ने उनके प्रणा गया अधिकार से समझौता नहीं किया अतः सिद्धांत रूप से इस बात पर विश्वास करने में कुछ गलत नहीं है कि कोई सुसमाचार लेखक पहले से उपलब्ध स्रोत पर निर्भर था  ऐसा प्रतीत होता है कि बाकी सारे सुसमाचार लेकर के पास भी ऐसा ही स्रोत की पहचान की व्याख्या भी वह स्पष्ट रूप से लुका के समान इसका उल्लेख नहीं करते यदि हम अधिकांश क्या कारों के साथ क्या माल लेकर उसने सबसे पहले सुसमाचार लिखा\r\nतो उसके पास पहले से लिखे सु समाचारों की पहुंच नहीं थी परंतु उसने मौके परंपराओं को निश्चित रूप से इस्तेमाल किया कम से कम अपने गणेश के प्रपत्र से तो अवश्य ही की आलू का और मशीनें शायद एक नमूने के रूप में मरकुस के सुसमाचार का प्रयोग किया इसके अतिरिक्त थी और योजना के पास यीशु के जीवन और उसकी सचिता के अपनी स्मृति थी और सभी चारों सुसमाचार लेखों के पास रहित रूप से पवित्र आत्मा का निर्णय था जैसा कि हम पहले देख चुके हैं\r\nसारांश में हम सो समाचारों के बीच पाए जाने वाले संबंधी विषयों के सिद्धांत की सराहना करते कर सकते हैं परंतु हमें उनके सारे वर्णों को समझने की जरूरत महसूस नहीं करनी चाहिए और ना ही उनमें से किसी एक पर  पूरी तरह निर्भर करना रहना चाहिए यह सिद्धांत में यह बताते हैं कि प्रत्येक सुसमाचार प्रचार 11 के पास अनेक स्रोतों से जानकारी प्राप्त करने और यीशु के जीवन और  शिष्य तारों के विश्वास ने विवरण की रचना करने की योग्यता थी जब हम उनके विवरणों में एक एक समान बातों को पाते हैं तो हमारे पास समाचारों के भिन्न-भिन्न दृष्टिकोण ऊपर ध्यान देने का अवसर होता है तेरे इसका कोई महत्व नहीं रहता कि कौन सा किस से पहले लिखा गया था और जब हम ऐसे विवरण पाको बातें हैं जो केवल एक ही सुसमाचार में पाया जाता है तो हम उसका ध्यान उस उल्लेख के\r\nप्रकाश में कर सकते हैं चारों सुसमाचार के संयोजन पर ध्यान देने के बाद हम उनके प्रमाणिकता को संबोधित करने के लिए तैयार है\r\nप्रमाणिकता-:\r\nअलीशा की आरंभिक सब्जियों में इस विषय में कुछ ऐसा मत याद थी कि वह ऋतिक युग के कौन सी पुस्तक के नए नियम से संबंधित है कुछ आरंभिक लिस्ट आए अब वह ने उन सारी पुस्तकों की पुष्टि नहीं की थी जो आश्रम नए नियम में पाते हैं अन्य लोगों ने माना था कि हमें वर्तमान की 27 पुत्र पुस्तकों से अतिरिक्त पुस्तकों को भी शामिल करना चाहिए परंतु इन विवादों में मस्ती मरकुस लुक्का और योजना की पुस्तकें शामिल नहीं थी इन चारों समाचारों इनके अतिरिक्त कोई और नहीं है को को संडे परमेश्वर की उस वासियों की कल ईशा के द्वारा विशुद्ध और अधिकार पूर्वक रूप से स्वीकार किया गया\r\nउदाहरण के रूप में तीसरी सदी के कल ईशा पूर्व छोरी अगेन जिनका जीवनकाल 185 से 254 ईसवी तक था ने तर्क दिया कि इन्हें नियमित जो 4 समाचार आज हमारे पास है वही प्रमाणित है ऑरिगेन को कलुषित यहां से भी अर्जित का जीवनकाल 263 से 340 ईसवी तक था द्वारा उद्धृत किया गया अपनी कृति ैक्लेसियस्टिकल हिस्ट्री पुस्तक 6 अध्याय 25 का 4 में यूसीबीएस द्वारा ऑरिगेन के लिए कहे गए शब्दों को सुनें आकाश के नीचे परमेश्वर की कलीसिया में केवल चार सुसमाचार ही निवृत्त है\r\nइसके अतिरिक्त एक सदी पूर्व कल ईशा पुरवा एरेनीअस जिसका जीवनकाल 130 से 202 ईसवी तक था ने अपनी तृतीय स्टरेशिया पुस्तक 3 अध्याय 11 खंड 8 में सामूहिक रूप से चार रूप समाचार के बारे में बात की सुनी उसने क्या लिखा था यह संभव नहीं है कि सुसमाचार संख्या में इससे ज्यादा या कम हो जो मनुष्य के सत्ता प्रकट हुआ अर्थात यीशु ने हमें चार पहियों परंतु एक आत्मा के साथ बधावा सुसमाचार दिया है\r\nअरे नियत ने कहा कि वहां ऐसे किसी समय के बारे में नहीं जानता जब चारों में से किसी भी सुसमाचार प्रति कोई विवाद हुआ या फिर इन के अतिरिक्त किसी और से समाचार को कल ईश्वर की आराधना में इस्तेमाल किया गया हो', 8, '2020-05-20 15:13:17', '2020-06-02 01:57:11', NULL),
(1505, 451, 758, 'भिन्नता = इस अध्याय में अब तक हमने सुसमाचारों को उनकी सहित्य विशेषता के आधार पर देखा है कलीसिया में उनके स्तरको देख लिया है और उनकी एक ता पर चर्चा काली है अब हम उस भिन्नता के बारे मई बात करंगे जो उन्हें एक दूसरे से भिन्न करती है जैसा की हम देख चुके है चारो सुसमाचार परमेश्वर के राज्य के आगमन के बारे मई सामान कहानी बताते है परन्तु प्र्तेक ऐसे अपनी ही रूप में बताता है हम दो मुख्य रूपों में इस भिन्नता की खोज करंगे पहला हम सुसमाचार के विवरणों में समाज इस्थापित करने में आने वाली प्रतिहत कठिनाइया को देखेंगे और दूसरा हम प्र्तेक सुसमाचार के भिन्न को देखंगे प्रतिहत कठिनाइया के साथ आरभ करे|\r\n  कठिनाइया  -----;\r\nजब हम सुसंचारो को पड़ते है तो तीर्व प्रभाव हम पते है वह यह है की एक दूसरे के कितना सामान है परन्तु ऐसे के स्थान है जहा सुसमाचार के वार्डन भिन्न भिन्न बाटे कहते प्रतीत होते है निःसन्दे इनमे से अधिकांश भिन्नता इतनी खूब है की उन्हें गभीरता के साथ विरोधभास नहीं कहा जा सकता कुछ भिन्नताऐं अवश्य पाठको को परेशन करती है इसलिए यह महत्वपूर्ण है|\r\n कठिनाइया = की हम कुछ महत्वपूर्ण महत्त्व कठिनाइया पर धियान देजब हम सुसमाचारों को पड़ते है तो तीव्र प्रभाव हम पते है वह यह है की वे एक दूसरे के कितना सामान है परन्तु ऐसे कई स्थान है जह सुसमाचार के वार्डन भिन्न भिन्न बाते कहते प्रतीत होते है निःसंदेह इनमे से अधिकानस भिन्नता इतनी सूछ्म है की उन्हें गभीरता के साथ विरोधभास नहीं कहा जा सकता परन्तु कुछ भिन्नताऐं अवश्य पाठकको परेशन करती है इसलिए यह महत्व पूर्ण है की हम उन कुछ महत्व पूर्ण प्रोतशाह्न कठिनाइयों पर धियान दे\r\n घटनाक्रम-------:\r\n \r\nसबसे आम  बिनता है घटनाक्रम से संबंधित है अर्थात उन क्रम से जिनमें घटनाओं का वर्णन भिंड सुसमाचार में किया गया है जीवन गाथा के विवरणों के रूप में प्रत्येक सुसमाचार एक जैसी आधारभूत समय रेखा का अनुसरण करता है प्रत्येक यीशु के जन्म से आरंभ होती है और उसकी मृत्यु की ओर बढ़ती है और अंत में उसके पुत्र की और परंतु वे यीशु के जीवन की घटना का वर्णन वर्णन क्रम में करते हैं इसका कारण यह है कि सुसमाचार कभी-कभी अपनी प्रमुख अदाओं के अनुसार घटनाओं को एक साथ जोड़ते हैं कि जो की पहली सदी में स्वीकार कर कर योग्यता परंतु शायद वर्तमान की अपेक्षाओं को पूरा ना करें सटीक रूप से घटनाक्रम का नुकसान करने की अपेक्षा का सुसमाचार कभी-कभी विषय या भौगोलिक स्थिति के अनुसार अपने ग्रंथों को बताते हैं उदाहरण के तौर पर मरकुस ने में यीशु के अपने ही गृह नगर में निरादर पाने की कहानी बताई परंतु लुका ने अपनी विवरण में इससे पहले रखा लोकाचार का 4:14 से 30 में जिससे कि यह यीशु कि सार्वजनिक सेवक आई पहली कहानी बनी लुका का सुसमाचार इस कहानी को अमरपुर से अधिक प्रमुखता देता है और यह निरादर के विषय पर अधिक बल देने के लिए यह कहानी के लंबे संस्करण को दर्शाता है सुसमाचार लेखकों की इसमें बहुत ही कम रुचि थी कि वह इस उत्सव का 611 क्रम अनुसार घटनाक्रम को बताएं इसकी अध्यक्षता व उसकी शुचिता और कार्यों में राज्य आगमन को स्पष्टता के साथ बता रहे थे\r\nविलोपन -:\r\n: दूसरे  प्रकार की बनता है एक अधिक सुसमाचार में विवरणों का रुपया अनुपस्थिति है उदाहरण के तौर पर यह ना अपनी सुसमाचार में प्रभु भोज के संस्करण का उल्लेख नहीं करता इस प्रकार के लोगों को कई रूपों में समझा जा सकता है यह शायद भिन्न लेकर द्वारा दिए जाने वाले महत्वपूर्ण फल स्वरुप हो सकते हैं या फिर यहां इसके फल स्वरुप भी हो सकता है कि शायद बाद के सुसमाचार लेखकों ने उन सबों को दोहराने की जरूरत महसूस नहीं की जो पहले सुसमाचार लेखकों की पुस्तकों में उपस्थित थे चाहे जो भी कारण हो विल ओपन ओं का अर्थ सुसमाचार लेखकों के बीच सहमति या विरोधाभास नहीं है आप अपनी किसी वार्तालाप के बारे में सोचें जिसमें अनेक लोग शामिल रहे हो हर व्यक्ति को वहां सब दोहराने की जरूरत नहीं होती जो अन्य लोग पहले से तय चुके हैं इसके अपेक्षित हर एक व्यक्ति आप अपने आस दृष्टिकोण को डालने पर ध्यान देता है शायद कुछ नए विवरणों और ईसाइयत बिन मतों के साथ पवित्र शास्त्र समय-समय पर इसे प्रत्येक रूप में करता है उदाहरण के तौर पर दूसरा इतिहास 9 अध्याय 29 पद में इतिहासकार ने प्रस्तुत रूप में कहा कि वह उन विवरणों को नहीं रख रखा है जिनका वर्णन अन्य लेखकों ने पहले से कर कर दिया है दूसरा इतिहास में तीन अन्य बार ऐसा ही होता है और पहला राजा और दूसरा राजा के पुस्तक में भी पर यहां ऐसा होता है अच्छा यहां देखना अचर्य जनक नहीं होना चाहिए कि किसी एक सुसमाचार लेखक ने उन महत्वपूर्ण विवरणों को नहीं दर्शाया जिनका उल्लेख करने लेखकों ने पहले से ही कर दिया था\r\nभिन्न घटनाएं -:\r\nएक तीसरे प्रकार के प्रस्तुत कठिनाई यीशु मसीह कैसे उगाएं में घटी इन घटनाओं में पाए जाने वाली समानता और से आती है कहने का अर्थ यह है कि कभी-कभी 200 समाचार समान घटना को भिन्न रूपों में दर्शाते प्रतीत होते हैं परंतु वे वास्तव में शायद 21 जैसी पर है परंतु विभिन्न घटनाओं को दिखाते हैं यस आय पर रखना महत्वपूर्ण है कि ईश्वर ब्रह्म शक्ति प्रचारक था अर्थात वहां एक स्थान से दूसरे स्थान पर विचार करता रहा उसने अलग-अलग स्थानों में कई एक जैसे चमत्कार किए कई लोगों को चंगा किया जो अंधे लंगड़े थे और नी संदेशों ने एक ही जैसे कई प्रश्नों और चुनौतियों का बार-बार उत्तर दिया इसके अतिरिक्त विभिन्न अवसरों पर दिए पर लोगों ने असमान रूप में विश्वकप उत्तर दिया लुक्का 7 अध्याय 36 पद और 50 पद और मरकुस 14 अध्याय तीन से 9 पद में यीशु का अभिषेक करने का निर्णय पर ध्यान दीजिए लुक्का में यीशु एक ऋषि के घर में है परंतु मरकुस वहां से शिवखोड़ी के घर में है यह एक ही घटना के दो विरोधाभासी विवरण नहीं है बल्कि भिन घटनाओं के  विवरण है\r\n: भिन्न कथन--:\r\nचौथे प्रकार की कठिनाई समान बातों के भिन्न कतनर द्वारा उत्पन्न किया गया असामाजिक है इसका सबसे सर्वोत्तम ज्ञात उदाहरण मती पांच अध्याय 1 पद और 7 पद 29 पद के यीशु के पहाड़ी उपदेश और लुक्का 6 अध्याय 17 और उन 40 पद में लुका द्वारा दर्शाई गई सामान्य सताए मती पांच अध्याय 1 पद में हमें बताया गया है कि या घटना एक पहाड़ी पर घटित है परंतु हमें बताया गया है कि या घटना एक समतल मैदान में घटी इस समस्या से निपटने के कम से कम 3 तरीके हैं पहला मती लुका दोनों शायद एक ही समान और स्थान पर दिए गए एक ही संदेश के बारे में बात कर रहे हैं गली की झील की दक्षिण पश्चिम की दिशा में उबड़ खाबड़ पहाड़ी नदी है परंतु झील में उठने वाले लहर पहाड़ी है उस उठे हुए स्थान में कई ऐसे छोटे-छोटे भाग भी है जो कि काफी क्षमता ले आता एक ही स्थान को मती के समान पहाड़ी कहा जा सकता है और लुक्का के समान मैदानी कहा जा सकता है परंतु यह सुमित कथनों अर्थात यीशु मसीह द्वारा विभिन्न अवसरों पर कही गई बातों को एक संदेश में समाहित करने की रचना करने की प्राचीन रितिका एक उदाहरण हो सकता है यार यह व्रत रखने के जिन का प्राचीन इतिहास कारों ने भी इस्तेमाल किया और यह इमानदारी या विश्वा नेता के साथ बारे में कोई प्रश्न नहीं उठती तीसरा यहां भी संभव है कि यीशु ने 2 दिन दिनों में दो भिन्न स्थानों एक पहाड़ी और दूसरा एक मैदान में दो बहस की सामान संदेशों का प्रचार किया हो यीशु की सेव काई की शैली के कारण यह मान लेना निश्चित रूप से सतर्क है कि उसने अपनी कई शिक्षकों उन पर नए श्रोताओं के समय दोहराया था जो उन्हें अपरिचित थे सुसमाचार में समाज या बैठक में भिन्न तरीके पर ध्यान देने के द्वारा हम इस बात के प्रति आश्वस्त हो सकते हैं कि यीशु के जीवन और सेव काहे की उनकी संगठित गवाही सच्ची है आस्था विवरणों में बिताए अवश्य है और जब हम पाते हैं कि सुने बिना अवसरों पर एक ही बात को सिखाया तो हम उसकी सेव का और उसके संदेश की निरंतर को देख सकते हैं और हमारे जीवन में उसकी शुचिता को लागू करने के विभिन्न तरीकों को पांच सकते हैं लेखकों में प्रस्तुत कठिनाई के बारे में पूछने के द्वारा हमने चारों सुसमाचार में बिनता को देखने देते हुए आरंभ किया था अतः हम 28 बिंदु पर हम उनके भिन महत्व की जांच करने के द्वारा चारों से समाचारों की विनता को और भी अधिक देखने के लिए तैयार है\r\nभिन्न प्रभाव -:\r\nक्योंकि प्रत्येक सुसमाचार एक दिन लेखक द्वारा लिखी लिखा गया है जिसने यीशु के जीवन और सेवक आई के अपने विवरण में अपने दृष्टिकोण और विषयों को डाला है इसलिए चारों से समाचार में भिन्नता है पाई जाती है यह जानते हैं कि चारों से समाचार पवित्र आत्मा के द्वारा प्रेरणा प्राप्त है हम इस बात के प्रति आश्वस्त है कि हर विवरण  तेरा हित है और इसलिए दूसरे सुसु ब्यूरो का विरोध फांसी नहीं है परंतु इसका अर्थ यह नहीं है कि उनमें कोई मिलता ही नहीं बहुत रात मा ने मानवीय लेखों के के व्यक्तित्व रुचि हो और सेव काय की परिस्थितियों का इस्तेमाल उन भी नेताओं को आकार देने के लिए किया था यदि हम उन सारे रूपों में आशीष पाना चाहते हैं जिनमें पवित्र आत्मा हमें आशीष करना चाहता है तो हमें सुसमाचार को पढ़ते समय प्रत्येक सुसमाचार के विभिन्न प्रभावों पर ध्यान देना होगा जीवन की अनेक परिस्थितियों में हम पाते हैं कि विनलोगबीट लोगों के सम्मान में सत्य के बारे में बात करते हैं हैं जिस किसी ने छोटे बच्चों को खेलते हुए देखा वह जानता है कि एक ही घटना की अनेक संगत व खाए हो सकती है हर बच्चे का अपने द्वारा किए गए खेलों के प्रति अपने दृष्टिकोण होता है खेलों के बारे में उन सब को सुनने के बाद ही पूरी तस्वीर को जोड़ सकते हैं कि वास्तव में क्या हुआ था कोई खिलौना के रंगों के बारे में उत्साह हो सकता है दूसरा शायद उनके द्वारा ही जाने वाली आवाज को बताने में रूचि रखता हो और अन्य कोई उस खिलौने की इधर-उधर भागने का उसे जान के सामर्थ्य का वर्णन करता हो यह दृष्टिकोण एक-दूसरे के विरुद्ध बासी नहीं है परंतु वे आवश्यक दर्शाते हैं कि हर बच्चे के खिलौने के कुछ भागों को दूसरे भागों अधिक रुचि र पाया इसी प्रकार प्रत्येक सुसमाचार लेखक की अपनी रुचियां और अपने विषय सुसमाचार की कहानी के उनके अपने विवरण में छलकते हैं कोई दो विवरण ठीक से एक जैसे प्रदेश नहीं होते हैं नए नियम की सारी सुसमाचार कहानियां एक ही यीशु का वर्णन करती है परंतु वह प्रिया भिन्न रूपों में उनके बारे में बात करती है और उसकी सेव का विभिन्न पहलुओं को सुचिता से दिखाती है सुसमाचार की अनेक भिन्नता विशेषताएं और विषय परंतु इस परिचित आत्मक अध्ययन में हम इस बात पर ध्यान देंगे कि प्रत्येक सुसमाचार 2 प्रश्नों का उत्तर किस प्रकार देता है', 8, '2020-05-20 15:29:42', '2020-06-02 01:57:11', NULL),
(1506, 451, 759, 'उत्तर -:  प्रत्येक सुसमाचार के महत्वपूर्ण बल इस प्रकार से है\r\nमत्ती रचित सुसमाचार-:\r\nसारे सुसमाचार लेखकों में मत्ती ऐसा है जो इस बात को बताने में अधिक रुचि रखता है कि यीशु इजराइल का वह मसीहा रूपी राजा है जिनकी भविष्यवाणी पुराने नियम में की गई थी जैन जगाओ पर मध्य यीशु के राज्यों का उल्लेख करता है उसमें से कुछ यह है 2:2 जहां मजबूरियों ने पूछा कि योगियों का राजा जिसका जन्म हुआ उसे हुए कहां पा सकते हैं जिनमें प्रभु के रूप में यीशु ने कहा कि वह उन सब को स्वर्ग के राज्य में अनुमति नहीं देगा जो उसे प्रभु कहते हैं जब पिरितिया को पूरी होना की माता ने विनती की कि राज्य में उनके पुत्रों की यीशु के साथ उच्च स्थान में विराजमान किया जाए जहां इशू ने अंतिम दिन राजा के रूप में उनको न्याय के विषय में एक दृष्टांत कहा और जहां मदीने व्याख्यात्मक रूप से यहां दर्शन किरूमी सैनिकों ने पुरुष पर यीशु के सिर के ऊपर एक पट्टी का लगाई जिस पर लिखा था या यीशु है याहुदियो का राजा अपेक्षा यहां की गई थी परमेश्वर मसीही रूपी राजा पृथ्वी पर परमेश्वर की महा मसीह रूपी राजा को लाएगा वह इस्राएल को बनवाएं और सके शत्रुओं से छुड़ाए गाबा धार्मिकता के साथ राज्य करेगा और शांति एवं खुशहाली को स्थापित करेगा इशू नहीं आ सब किया परंतु उसने या उस प्रकार से नहीं किया जैसे योगियों ने अपेक्षा की थी यीशु समझ गया था कि उसकी सेव काई को देखने वाले आने की अवधि सोचेंगे कि वह परमेश्वर की व्यवस्था को नष्ट करने कर रहा था पुराने नियम की प्रतिज्ञा को पूरा नहीं कर रहा था इसलिए उसने पूरी स्पष्टता के साथ कहा कि चाहे ऐसा भी जितना होता हो तो भी फिर भी वहां व्यवस्था और वसु कुत्ता ओं की बातों को पूरा कर रहा था\r\nकेवल इस अनुच्छेद में ही नहीं बल्कि बार-बार मति ने दर्शाया कि इसने पुराने नियम के पुत्र शास्त्र की किसी ना किसी पहलू को पूरा किया और इस बात को प्रकट किया कि वास्तव में वही इजरायल का मसीहा रूपी राजा था अच्छा मदीने अनुसार हम यीशु का अनुसरण कैसे करते हैं इसने परमेश्वर की व्यवस्था का सिद्धांत से पालन किया परंतु उसने केवल वही किया उसने कहा कि व्यवस्था की भौतिक भागों को पूरा करना ही पर्याप्त नहीं था परमेश्वर ने अपनी प्रतिज्ञा से सदैव इस बात की मांग की है कि वह हृदय से उसके आज्ञा माने सुसमाचार का शुभ संदेश या है कि राज्य आ चुका है और वह परमेश्वर के लोगों के लिए एक और उधार लाया है और इसने हमें नए और आज्ञाकारी और दे दिए हैं और हमारे परिवर्तन हृदय हमेशा मत और प्रेरणा दोनों देते हैं कि हम पैरा पूर्वक आभारी आनंदित आज्ञाकारी ता के साथ यीशु का अनुसरण करें हम यहां पर देख चुके हैं कि किस प्रकार मध्य का सुसमाचार हमें दो प्रश्नों का उत्तर देता है आइए आप देखें कि मरकुस क्या कहता है\r\nमरकुस रचित सुसमाचार -:            पहले मर पुष्टि अनुसार यीशु कौन है अपने पूरे विवरण में मर कुश ने बल दिया कि यीशु परमेश्वर का दुख उठाने वाला पुत्र था जिसने परमेश्वर के लोगों के शत्रुओं पर विजय प्राप्त की मरकुस निशु के चमत्कारों के अनेक उदाहरण प्रस्तुत किए और उनके द्वारा सृष्टि की शक्तियों पर उनकी सामर्थ को दर्शाया मर्कुस मत्ती और लुक्का के सुसमाचार से काफी छोटा है फिर भी लगभग उतने ही चमत्कारों का वर्णन करता है जो कि सब मिलकर 18 है मर्कुस की सुसमाचार के आरंभ से ही हम देख सकते हैं कि यीशु विजय प्राप्त करने वाला दो उठाने वाला परमेश्वर का पुत्र है अपने पहले अध्याय में योजना बपतिस्मा दाता ने यीशु के आगमन की भविष्यवाणी की और तब यीशु ने अपनी सार्वजनिक सेवा का आरंभ की उसका 32 माह हुआ जंगल में उसकी परीक्षा हुई उसने अपने चेलों को बुलाया दुष्ट आत्मा को निकाला अनेक बीमारियों से लोगों को चंगा क्या बहुत तेजी से चलने वाले और रोमांचक भरे इस विवरण को केवल सतही रूप से पढ़ना इस बात को को दिखाता है कि यीशु परमेश्वर के राज्य के शत्रु पर सामर्थ्य के साथ विजय प्राप्त कर रहा था एक गहन अध्ययन पर यहां भी दिखता है कि मर कुछ नहीं सुको उसकी सेवक आई के आरंभ से ही परमेश्वर के दुख उठाने वाला पुत्र के रूप में चिन्हित किया था अपनी सार्वजनिक सेव का इसके पहले चरण में ही यीशु कितने शैतान के आक्रमणों का सामना किया था और 2 को उठाने वाले सेवक के रूप में यीशु का यह चित्र उनके साथ था और उसके पिता के साथ मर्पित के सुसमाचार में पढ़ना पड़ता चला गया  अमरपुर के अनुसार हमें दुख उठाने वाले विजेता यीशु का अनुसरण कैसे करना चाहिए एक और मरकुस का सुसमाचार मसीह जीवन को एक सरल जीवन के रूप में नहीं दर्शाता है मर कुछ निश्चित या अकेलापन का वर्णन कठिन और प्रिया निरहू कि उक्त प्रक्रिया के रूप में किया है जिनमें हम न केवल दुख उठाने वाले हैं बल्कि गलत क्यों करते हैं असफल भी होते हैं वास्तव में मरकुस के सुसमाचार की एक मुख्य विशेषता यह है कि कितनी बार यीशु के चेले उसे समझने या विश्वास के साथ उत्तर देते देने में सफल हो जाते हैं मर्कुस 4 : 40 में यीशु ने इस बात पर आश्चर्य कि यहां कि उसके चेले बिल्कुल भी विश्वास है या नहीं चलो केहर दे कठोर हो गए थे\r\nयीशु ने अपने चेलों पर नासमझ होने का दोष लगाया क्योंकि वह उसकी  शिष्य को नहीं समझ पाए थे चेले दुष्ट आत्मा को नहीं निकाल पाए चेलों ने गलती से एक दुष्ट आत्मा को निकालने वाले को रोकने का प्रयास किया क्योंकि हुए उसे नहीं जानते थे और एक चेले निशु को अधिकारियों के हाथ पकड़ा दिया एक ने यीशु के साथ अपने पूरे संबंध का इनकार कर दिया और अन्य चेलों ने उसे छोड़ दिया मर्कुस कि सुसमाचार का यह महतो हमें यीशु का अनुसरण करने के बारे में कम से कम दो बातें सिखाता है पहला चेलों के समान हम हमेशा यीशु के समान नहीं पाए वास्तव में हम बाइबल की अनेक बातों को गलत तो रूप में समझ लेते हैं अतः में कितना दिन होने की आवश्यकता है कि हम इस बात को पहचान ले कि हम सब को बहुत कुछ समझना अभी बाकी है इसी भाग के रूप में हमें विश्वास के साथ बाइबल के क्षेत्रों को ग्रहण करना है और यह जानना है कि परमेश्वर का वचन सच्चा है फिर चाहे वह हमें विधि या गलत प्रतीत हो दूसरा कठिनाई और दुख मछलियों के लिए आश्चर्य कार्य है उसका अनुसरण करने से मोड़ने वाले बहुत सारे खतरे हैं परीक्षित आए हैं  इसमें शिकायत है कि हमें उसके प्रति अपने समर्पण में विश्वास क्यों के रहना है हमें यीशु के समान दुख उठाने परीक्षाओं और आत्मिक आक्रमणों के विरुद्ध स्थिर रहने के लिए तैयार रहना है परंतु इस अनुच्छेद में एक और बात पर ध्यान दें यीशु परमेश्वर का केवल दुख उठाने वाला पुत्र ही नहीं है वह परमेश्वर का विजय प्राप्त करने वाला पुत्र भी है वास्तव में वहां अपनी दुख सहने वाली मृत्यु के द्वारा ही विजय प्राप्त करता है और यदि हम राज्य के लिए दुख उठाने के विश्वास योगी के साथ उसका अनुसरण करते हैं तो हम अनंत जीवन के साथ पुरस्कृत किया जाएंगे मत्ती और वर्क उसको मान रखते हुए आइए देखें किस प्रकार लोका ईश्वर उसके अनुयायियों के बारे में हम प्रश्नों का उत्तर देते हैं देता है\r\nलुका रचित सुसमाचार\r\nलुक्का का सुसमाचार यीशु कौन है के प्रश्न का उत्तर यहां घोषणा करने के द्वारा देता है कि वह संसार का करुणामई तरस खाने वाला उद्धार करता है ईश्वर ने अमीरों और ग़रीबों धार्मिक को गुरु और सामाजिक रूप से पिछड़ों को एक समान रूप से बदमाशों का उद्धार प्रदान किया विश्व का शुभ संदेश सब लोगों के लिए था अल्प स्थित और कुछ समझे जाने वाले के लिए भी लोका ने कई रूपों में इस पर बल दिया  यीशु ने मरियम और मारता नामक बहनों को ऐसा सम्मान दिया जब बहुतों से पुरुष स्त्रियों को तुच्छ समझते लुक्का ने ऐसे दृष्टांत और विवरणों को दर्शाया जिन्होंने स्त्रियों बीमार और लंगड़े और गैर योगियों को भी प्रशंसा और अनुसरण के योग्य ठहराया यीशु ने उस विधवा की प्रशंसा की जिसने अपने जीवन की सारी मस्जिद मंदिर में दे दी लुका ने कुछ मांगे गए चुंगी लेने वाले जताई की कहानी बताएं जिसका यीशु के प्रति तनु का के पाठकों के लिए एक नमूना बन गया बार-बार लुका ने उन लोगों के प्रति यीशु की परवाह का वर्णन किया जिन्हें समाज के ठुकरा दिया था या अपेक्षा कर दिया था\r\nपहली सदी के रोमी संसार में एक ही दुआ जिसने अपने पुत्र को खो दिया हो तो उसके पास अपनी जरूरतें पूरी करने के लिए कुछ भी नहीं रहता था और ना ही काम मिलने का कोई अवसर उसे मिलता था उसके लिए यीशु के पत्र पर बल देते हुए लोका ने दर्शाया कि उधर पिता के रूप में प्रभु का कार्य गरीबों और असहाय को के लिए था इस वर्णन के अंत में जैसे लोगों ने टिप्पणी की जरूरतमंदों और निवासियों के प्रति यीशु की सेवा इस बात का प्रमाण थी कि परमेश्वर अपने लोगों की सहायता करने आया है फिर लुका दूसरे प्रश्न का उत्तर किस प्रकार देता है हम यीशु का अनुसरण कैसे करें गरीबों के लिए लुक्का के प्रभाव को देखते हुए एक काम हम कर सकते हैं कि हम दूसरों पर तरस खाए गरीबों की देखभाल करनी चाहिए एवं उनकी जरूरतों को पूरा करने का प्रयास करनी चाहिए हमें उनकी सहायता के लिए हमारी संपत्ति भोजन धन समय देने के लिए तैयार रहना चाहिए वास्तव में जरूरतमंदों की प्रार्थना ओं के उत्तर में परमेश्वर का प्रिय धनी मछलियों को भेजता है जैसा कि लोका ने कहा जब हम उनके लोगों की देखभाल करने के द्वारे विश्वास योगिता के साथ यीशु का अनुसरण करते हैं तो वह एक अनंत विराट के साथ हमारे पुरस्कृत करता है यीशु का अनुसरण करने का एक अन्य तरीका इस प्रतिज्ञा विश्राम करना है कि परमेश्वर हमारी जरूरतों को पूरा करेगा परमेश्वर के राज्य के सदस्य होने के नाते हम इस बात में अध्यक्ष हो सकते हैं कि हमारा महाराजा यीशु मसीह हमारा ध्यान रखेगा और हमारी जरूरतों को पूरा करेगा और हमारा उद्धार करता पर विश्वास करने का यह महत्व लो का सुसमाचार के दो अन्य विश वासियों से बहुत ही घनिष्ट से जुड़ा हुआ है वे विषय है शांति और आनंद उदाहरण के तौर पर लुका के सुसमाचार के आरंभ के पास ही हमारा स्वर्ग दूध की ओर से इस घोषणा को सुनें और 22 अध्याय के बाद लुका ने अपने सुसमाचार का अंत ठीक वैसे ही किया जैसे उसने आराम से लिया था अपनी कहानी के अंत में चेले यीशु का अनुसरण कर रहे थे और उस आनंद का अनुभव कर रहे थे जिसकी भविष्यवाणी यशाया 2 अध्याय में की गई थी\r\nयोहन्ना रचित सुसमाचार\r\nउसके सुसमाचार नहीं होना नहीं सुको परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में चिन्हित किया जो उद्धार के अनंत योजना को पूरा करता है परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में यीशु के पहचान पर बल देते हुए u19 पिता के साथ परमेश्वर के आदित्य संगम के बारे में बात की यीशु अपने पिता का संपूर्ण प्रकाश है और वही एकमात्र है जो उन सब को अनंत जीवन प्रदान कर सकता है जो उन पर अपना भरोसा रखते हैं उदाहरण के लिए जहां अन्य तीन सुषमा चारों ने यीशु के जन्म और प्रति पर उसकी संकाय के साथ अपनी वर्णों को आरंभ किया वहीं योजना ने अपने सुसमाचार का आरंभ यह कहते हुए कहा कि परमेश्वर का पुत्र पिता के साथ सृष्टि रचना में शामिल था और अब पिता अपने पुत्र पुत्र के माध्यम से प्रकट किया जा रहा था यीशु द्वारा कहे गए मैं हूं कथनों के द्वारा यूहन्ना ने एक और तरीके से इस समय मा संदेश को बताएं इन कथनों में ही सुने परमेश्वर की सच्चाई वचायी नमक यह हुआ की ओर संकेत किया स्वयं परमेश्वर निरहुआ नाम को स्पष्ट किया जिसका मूल अर्थ मैं हूं यीशु ने इस नाम की ओर संकेत किया जहां उसने कहा जीवन की रोटी में हूं हम इसे में भी पाते हैं मैं जगत की ज्योति मैं हूं हम पढ़ते हैं द्वार में हूं यहां है पुनरुत्थान और जीवन में हूं मैं अहम पाते हैं सच्चीदा करता मैं हूं इस विश्व में अंतिम घोषणा की मैं हूं इन सारे उदाहरणों में यीशु ने घोषणा की कि परमेश्वर के पुराने नियम के पुत्र नाम को साधारण करने वाला वही है और उसने अपने व्यक्तित्व में परमेश्वर को प्रकट किया उधार की परमेश्वर के अनंत योजना के केंद्र में यीशु का स्थान योजना में यू शिशु की माया जी के प्रार्थना में विशेष रूप से प्रकट होता है इसने अपने अनुयायियों के उद्धार को उस प्रेम के साथ जोड़ा जो पुत्र के लिए पिता के मन में सृष्टि से पहले था उसका कहना था कि हमारा उद्धार यीशु के लिए पिता के प्रेम का उड़ेला जाना है अतः यदि यूनानी यीशु को परमेश्वर के ऐसे पुत्र के रूप में चिन्हित किया जिसे उद्धार के अनंत योजना को पूरा किया तो होना का सुसमाचार हमारे दूसरे प्रश्न का उत्तर कैसे देता है हम यीशु का अनुसरण कैसे कर सकते हैं\r\nयोना के सुसमाचार में यीशु का अनुसरण करने का मुख्य तरीका परमेश्वर के प्रेम को प्राप्त करना और वैसा ही प्रेम दूसरों के प्रति दर्शाना इसने कई तरीकों से हमारे आचरण के लिए इस नमूने को स्थापित किया उदाहरण के तौर पर 17 अध्याय 2326 बाद में इसे देख सकते हैं जहां यीशु ने पुत्र के लिए पिता के लिए प्रेम के बारे में बात की यह पुत्र के लिए पिता का नाम प्रेम ही था जो उस अनंत योजना के पीछे था जिससे इस्सू ने पूरा किया था या अर्थात पूर्व है कि यह नस का सुसमाचार प्रेम के द्वारा चरित्र है जैसा कि यूहन्ना में यीशु ने अपने अन्य अन्य अनुयायियों से कहा योजना के अनुसार हम उसके प्रेम से एक दूसरे से प्रेम करने के द्वारा यीशु का अनुसरण करते हैं इस प्रकार चेल्लप्पन प्रेम से आरंभ होता है और उसी में कार्यरत होता है हमारे लिए परमेश्वर का प्रेम हमारे चेला पन को आरंभ करता है और एक दूसरे के लिए हमारे अध्ययन में परमेश्वर का प्रेम हमारे चेला पनकी अभिव्यक्त है यह हमें समझने में सहायता करता है कि क्यों यूहन्ना ने स्वयं को अपनी उस पूरे सुसमाचार में वहां चेला जो प्रेम करता था के रूप में नहीं बल्कि वह चेला जिसे ईश्वर प्रेम करता था के रूप में प्रकट किया वह जानता था कि दूसरे से प्रेम करने की जो भी योग्यता उसमें थी वहां उसके लिए यीशु के प्रेम की गहराई से आई थी यीशु के अनुयायियों से प्रेम किया गया था तब उन्होंने एक दूसरे से प्रेम करने के लिए बुलाया गया था', 8, '2020-05-20 15:44:15', '2020-06-02 01:57:11', NULL),
(1507, 451, 760, 'उत्तर सुसमाचार में हम के सरे सत्य भट्ना को देख सकते hai kae lo yaha mante hai की येशु  ka आगमन  हो  चूका है  लेकिन  बाइबिल  mai हमें  सुसमाचार  योहानना  14 अधियय  मई  येशु  ने  कहा  माँi अब  सोवर्ग   जातहु  जगह  तैयार  karne  को  ydi  जगह  तैयार  करना pura ho jaye to me sigrh hi tumeh lene ko aa unga es bato se ham jan sakte hai ki yeshu abhi nhi aaya or ham susamacharo ki kitab me kie sare sachae ko dekha sakte hai methuw 28 adhayay mai bhi yeshu ne ka jao sare jagt ke logo ko chela bnao or unhe sab बाटे  मनन  सिखाओ  और  पिता   पुत्र   के  नाम  बप्तिस्मादो  हम    पवित्र  आत्मा  के  विषय  के  बारे  माँ i भी  देखा  सकते  है  अभी  अनुग्र  का  समय  है  ले  किन  एक  दिन  येशु  बदलो  पर  आएगा  हमें  लेने  थिसळुनीकियो  कइ  किताब  मई  देख सकते  है', 6, '2020-05-20 16:01:23', '2020-06-02 01:57:11', NULL),
(1508, 454, 781, '1. Factual Backgrounds- the book of Hebrews quotes refers to or alludes to the old testament nearly 100 times. The author of Hebrews incorporated historical facts into his presentation of the christian faith. (Hb 7:2). \r\n2. Theological outlooks- the author focused on theological beliefs affirmed by the Hebrew scriptures. God\'s son, angels are serving spirits, lower than angels, God\'s oath to Abraham, God as a consuming fire.\r\n3. Moral Obligation- Old testament moral requirements were to remain as standards in New Testament times: not to rebel, not to be discouraged, adhere to righteousness, confidence in God( Hb 13:6)\r\n4. Eschatological Predictions- the author used several old testament eschatological predictions to show that God\'s final judgement and blessings are fulfilled in Christ: angels will worship, current arrangement destroyed, universal sovereignty, royal priesthood from God, no further sacrifices etc.\r\n5. Dynastic ideals- the author referred to a number of dynastic ideals that were established for David\'s lineage in the Psalms. Jesus is the perfect fulfillment of the ideas of David\'s house, royal son to rule nations, vindication shared with Israel, devotion of body to God. (Hb10.5, Ps 40.6-8)', 8, '2020-05-20 16:41:18', '2020-06-02 01:56:32', NULL),
(1509, 454, 782, 'The author of Hebrews wrote that his audience should follow Jesus because Jesus is God\'s supreme source of divine revelation. The author acknowledge that God spoke through angels throughout Old Testament history. But Jesus brought revelation that was far superior to any revelation given through angels. In Hb 1:5-14, Jesus is greater than angels because He alone is God\'s messianic son. Jesus fulfilled ideals for David\'s house, fulfilled David\'s prediction of victory of God\'s messianic son over all God\'s enemies. By Contrast, he noted that angels are nothing more than spirit sent to serve those who inherit salvation in Christ. \r\nIn 2:1-4, the author exhorted of the great message of salvation by Jesus and reminded them that violating messages from angels received punishment from God. \r\nHb. 2:5-9, supports belief in the supremacy of Christ by explaining that Jesus is now ruler over angels and in the future all believers will reign over them with him. And finally, Heb 2:10-18, author demonstrated that Jesus is Abraham\'s descendant. And Jesus will share his Glory with Abraham\'s descendants not with angels.', 8, '2020-05-20 16:49:55', '2020-06-02 01:56:32', NULL),
(1510, 454, 783, 'The author of Hebrews explained the supremacy of Christ as God\'s ordained high priest by discussing how the new covenant is superior to the old. First, Hb 8:1-3 introduces the idea that Jesus mediates the new covenant as the royal high priest in heaven. In Heb. 9:1-28, He elaborated on the fact that Jesus\' heavenly royal priesthood is superior to the Levitical priesthood. He began this section by mentioning the arrangements of Moses earthly tabernacle revealing features that resemble God\'s heavenly sanctuary. Jesus brought final forgiveness of sin. Jesus died as a ransom to set his people free from judgement. The author ends his portion by stating that Christ will return but not to bear sin again. He called his audience to remember the past and not throw away their confidence. He reminded that they had willingly and joyfully suffered in the past because they Knew they had better and lasting possessions in the world to come.', 8, '2020-05-20 16:57:17', '2020-06-02 01:56:32', NULL),
(1511, 454, 784, 'It is of great importance in many ways. \r\nOld testament characters- From Abel to David, influences our faith a lot. Their determination, patience, faith, and the waiting for the promises of God, gives great life lessons and ministerial guidance too.\r\nOld testament prophecies have been fulfilled in many ways, especially about Jesus and His sacrificial death. It inspires us to wait on the promises and prophecies that are yet to happen. Jesus once came to earth for the redemption of sin, died on the cross, and rose up the third day, and ascended to heaven, we believe that He will come back as the King with all glory and that\'s the blessed hope. Jesus\' birth, ministry, death and resurrection was all according to the scriptures and He will return back according to the same scripture.This is the gospel we preach and the ministry we have is to spread this.', 8, '2020-05-20 17:07:38', '2020-06-02 01:56:32', NULL),
(1512, 454, 785, 'In this earth, there\'s only one incarnation that was born without human lineage, but of the spirit of God and that is Jesus Christ. He lived in full human nature without sins. Jesus himself challenged the people who accused him to prove him guilty of sins. He was trialed in five courts, but none could prove him guilty. Even the centurion, who crucified Jesus, agreed that indeed He was a holy man. One who lived without sin can only have the right to forgive sins and there is no other person/God who is sufficient of this, and that is Jesus Christ. There is no other person to show to the world as a role model who overcame sin for the humanity than Jesus. Neither there is salvation in any other for there is none other name under heaven given among men, whereby we must be saved. So, we  can preach confidently and communicate this Good news to our area.', 8, '2020-05-20 17:24:36', '2020-06-02 01:56:32', NULL),
(1513, 452, 796, 'God\'s plan to redeem humanity from the corruption and consequences of sin was made before he created the Universe.\r\n ( Ephesians 1:3-4 ,3:11 which speaks of God\'s eternal purpose historically accomplished by Jesus\r\n 2 Thessalonians 2:13 says that we were chosen for salvation from beginning .\r\n 2 Timothy 1:9,10) speaks of grace that was given to us before the beginning of time.\r\nEphesians 1:11 says that our redemption was determined before the creation of the world.\r\nin Ephesians 1:11,Romans 8:29,30 and Ephesians 1:5 the Greek word \'Proorizo\' is used ,this term is most commonly translated as predestination .\r\nSo from above references we all agree that God\'s decision to save sinners was made as part of his eternal counsel, before the foundation of the world.', 7, '2020-05-22 18:16:06', '2020-06-02 01:57:44', NULL),
(1514, 452, 797, 'God\'s eternal plan of redemption involves the work of all three persons of the Trinity.\r\nTHE FATHER- originated the agreement because of his desire to redeem fallen human beings from the course of sin (Ephesians 3:10,11). According to Paul it was the Father\'s eternal purpose to accomplish our redemption through Christ.\r\nTHE SON- agreed to add a perfect human nature to his perfect divine nature to die on behalf of sinners.(2 Timothy 1:9) Paul said that we received grace in the Son before the beginning of time\r\nTHE HOLY SPIRIT agreed to enable and empower the Son\'s work and to apply salvation to those whom the Son redeemed .(2 Thessalonians 2:13)', 6, '2020-05-22 18:25:58', '2020-06-02 01:57:44', NULL),
(1515, 452, 798, 'COVENANT OF GRACE-The covenant relationship God established with humanity after our fall into sin that provides forgiveness and redemption on the basis of God\'s mercy in Christ\r\nFULFILLMENT-The covenant of grace fulfills part of God\'s eternal plan for history\r\nThe Father fulfilled his eternal decree in to covenant of grace by sending the Son and the/Spirit to work,appointing the son to the office of Messiah(John 5:36), giving the Son his powerful spirit without limit.( John 3:34),and preparing the Son\'s perfect human nature.\r\nThe Son fulfilled his eternal agreement to redeem humanity by veiling his divine glory, adding a full human nature, to his full divine nature,living a perfect life and dying an atoning death(Philippians 2:5-8)\r\nThe Holy Spirit fulfilled His part in God\'s eternal counsel by enabling and empowering the Son\'s incarnation and subsequent work, empowering Christ\'s death on the cross and his resurrection, regenerating our spirit, empowering us to resist sin ,giving us spiritual gift and securing our salvation', 6, '2020-05-22 18:37:55', '2020-06-02 01:57:44', NULL),
(1516, 452, 799, 'God the Son joined the covenant of grace as its mediator as\r\n1. He intercedes for God\'s covenant people\r\n2. He reconciles us to God by taking the blame and punishment for our sins\r\n3. He preserves the integrity of the covenant and the lives of his people by suffering the covenant curses and earning the covenant blessings\r\nThe Son began to mediate the covenant of grace when it was first made, back in the Garden of Eden ,when God first offered redemption to Adam and Eve. And He continues to mediate ever since.\r\nJesus \' role us our fully divine and fully human covenant mediator is what enabled him to atone for our sin  by dying in our place and because this solution to human sin will always be available in the covenant of grace, there will never be a need for divine providence to introduce another covenant, another covenant representative or another mediator.', 8, '2020-05-22 18:50:26', '2020-06-02 01:57:44', NULL),
(1517, 452, 800, 'ADMINISTRATIONS;\r\nThe covenant of grace was administered by various covenant representatives:\r\n1. ADAM-  The Adamic administration provided humanity the immediate opportunity to reconcile our relationships with God(Gen 4:25,26)\r\n2. NOAH- The Noahic administration expanded the covenant blessing by adding God\'s promise never again to destroy the earth with flood waters.\r\n3. ABRAHAM- In the Abrahamic administration the nation of Israel was charged with expanding God\'s kingdom throughout the earth (Romans 4:13)\r\n4. MOSES- In Mosaic administration God confirmed his promise to Abraham,provided structure fir the nation of Israel,gave Israel the first codified version of the law,redirected Israel t build his kingdom through out world .\r\n5. David-In the Davidic administration , the Mosaic administration was confirmed,it was revealed that the greatest covenant blessings would be fulfilled under the kingship of /David and his dynastic heirs.\r\n6. Jesus- In the New Covenant God established a permanent unbreakable covenant in which his people would receive all his covenant blessings.', 8, '2020-05-22 19:05:28', '2020-06-02 01:57:44', NULL),
(1518, 453, 858, 'Love consists of allegiance,action and affection\r\nAllegiance consists of :\r\nLOYALTY is the cornerstone of the concept of love. The most basic responsibility of the people is loyalty to the king.The suzerain\'s love was expressed legally in the form of covenant loyalty to his people:protection,justice,met needs.Vassal\'s love towards the king:obey,support and honor.\r\nJesus is our Lord and king and we are to render love to him through loyal obedience and loyalty to his church.\r\nORIENTATION;\r\nGod and his kingdom must be our highest priorities, the focus of our desire and the center of our world view.\r\nWhen we orient our lives around God and his people, we pursue the agenda of his kingdom and we are motivated ti love in ways that please him.\r\nRESPONSIBILITY\r\nOur loving allegiance to God should motivate us to seek out additional ways that we are responsible to him.When understanding that we are obligated to him in every area of our life, we are in a better position to make decisions that he approves.', 8, '2020-05-24 18:16:04', '2020-06-02 02:02:05', NULL),
(1519, 453, 859, 'All God\'s action are perfect expressions of his character.Scripture exhorts us to pattern our character and actions after God. Scripture teaches that we should love each other in emotion of the love that God has shown for us. The scripture tells us to show the same kind of love for others that God showed to us in the atonement.\r\nCommon grace: God\'s kindness to those who will never be saved Because we love God we should also live the people he loves. It is easy not to have god s kind of love for our enemies, but we should have genuine concern for our enemies well being: be kind to them,pray for them, protect them and provide for them when they are in need', 8, '2020-05-24 18:22:39', '2020-06-02 02:02:05', NULL),
(1520, 453, 860, 'Sincere love towards God motivates me to work in His kingdom.In Colossians 1:5,we learn that hope in our future salvation motivates us to love more greatly and to have stronger faith. And of course , both love and faith are themselves not only good works , but also motive s for good works, So by motivating faith and love, hope is the source of immeasurable good works.\r\nMy outward obedience flows from a heart truly committed to God and His word as Paul taught in Rom,ans 13:9 and Galatians 5:14 that love is so foundation  to all good works that if its not among our motives , our works can never be counted good.', 8, '2020-05-24 18:36:14', '2020-06-02 02:02:05', NULL),
(1521, 453, 861, 'Yes I do remember when I was ten years old I came to saving faith, was not at all changed instantly at that moment , but gradually learnt His ways and followed His faith. This brings a great change in our motives and behaviors. it effects everything that we think about ourselves, our families ,our jobs , lour services and everything else in our lives.Is is an active faith that underlies and motivates our good works.Saving also involves our hearts, it is an inward disposition that cause us to think , speak and act in ways that please God . It involves mental,acts. so saving faith functions a as a motive in my life and enables me to do good works. Earlier my motives were selfish, self centered, but saving faith has influenced my motives and behaviors based on the love of God.', 8, '2020-05-24 18:47:07', '2020-06-02 02:02:05', NULL),
(1522, 453, 862, 'The term imagination refers to our ability to form mental image of thing that are beyond our experience.Imaginations are vital to learning and thinking about God , the world and our ourselves.\r\nCreativity:We can have good degree of confidence in our imagination when we use it carefully and rightly, because the Holy Spirit give  us this faculty as a reliable tool for assessing ethical knowledge\r\nTime:Bible requires us to pursue good goals especially the glorification of God through the triumph of his kingdom, but this goal is in the future. Without our ability to imagine the future ,we would not be able to apply God\'s word to our lives \r\nDistance:\r\nthe information we receive about the distant things is fallible, but we need to rely strongly on the Holy Spirit to help us evaluate our imagination.', 8, '2020-05-24 19:02:53', '2020-06-02 02:02:05', NULL),
(1523, 453, 863, 'Assessing knowledge means to evaluate the information we have received. Our intellect comes from God and His holy Spirit help us to use it rightly . It has an important role to play in our decision making process.\r\nReason is the capacity to make logical inferences and to judge logical consistency. It is also the ability to think and make judgement that accord with biblical patterns of thought.\r\nConscience: God given ability to discern good and evil. The solution to sin\'s corrupting influence is to rely on the power of the Holy Spirit who works within us as we strive to conform our conscience to God\'s word.\r\nEmotions are inner feelings , the effective aspects of our ethical sensitivity.\r\nWe must submit our emotions to the Holy spirit and Gods word and harmonize them with our other God given abilities and capacities.', 8, '2020-05-24 19:16:17', '2020-06-02 02:02:05', NULL),
(1524, 453, 864, 'Will is the capacity for making decisions , volition and ability to make choices. Our will is affected by our fallen nature. For us , the Holy Spirit enables us to make decisions that please God, but our indwelling sin may persuade us to make sinful decisions.\r\nOur will may be active or passive. Our will is involved in each and every thing we choose to think say or do. It is the faculty we use to make every decision in our lives.We must will what God\'s word Command and we must allow the Holy Spirit working within us to influence our will in positive ways', 8, '2020-05-24 19:22:53', '2020-06-02 02:02:05', NULL),
(1525, 453, 865, 'We have many commitments in our lives.We are loyal to various people such us or families, friends and fellow Christians. and we are also committed to organizations  such us churches , companies etc. We are not committed to all these things to the same degree. And for us , one commitment should stand above all others  which is our commitment to God.This commitment should govern the fundamental decision of our entire life and all our other commitments should serve this most basic one. \r\nin Luke 6:45 Jesus referred to our commitments as the things that are store up in our hearts . And our commitments always express themselves in our works. So we express our commitments to God in good works and we express our commitments to sin in evil works. I am fully committed and dedicated to the expansion of the Kingdom of God by giving my time , energy and all resources that I have in my life for His glory.', 8, '2020-05-24 19:33:28', '2020-06-02 02:02:05', NULL),
(1526, 455, 826, 'Ethics is the study of moral right and wrong, the study of what is good and evil. Christian ethics is; theology viewed as a means of determining which human persons acts and attitude receive God\'s blessing and which do not. \r\nOur definition focuses on God and his blessing rather than on terms like good or evil, or right or wrong. Those things that receive God\'s blessings are good and right, whereas those things that do not receive his blessings are wrong and evil. \r\n1. Divine Nature- God himself is the ultimate standard of right or wrong, of good and evil. God is not accountable to any standard outside himself. \r\n2. Divine Action- God\'s actions demonstrate the standard of morality. God shows His approval by bestowing blessings. He shows his hatred by withholding blessings and pouring out curses.', 8, '2020-05-25 16:36:06', '2020-06-02 02:02:43', NULL),
(1527, 455, 827, 'Unless a work is done with a right motive, it is not a work that God will reward with blessings.\r\n1. Faith- Only believers who are indwelled by the Holy Spirit can do works that God rewards with blessings. Only believers have hearts that are purified by faith. Saving faith motivates good works. This is the faith possessed by believers and only by believers.\r\n2. Love- Our works are useless if they are not motivated by love. Works and even spiritual gifts that produce beneficial results merit no reward if they are not motivated by love. Love is an aspect of every law God requires us to obey. If we do not act in love, no work we do can conform to his standard. Our love must be for both God and neighbor.', 8, '2020-05-25 16:40:41', '2020-06-02 02:02:43', NULL),
(1528, 455, 828, 'a. Proper Motive- Unless a work is done with right motive, it is not a work that God will reward with blessings.\r\n Faith- Only believers who are indwelled by the holy spirit can do works that God rewards with blessings and have hearts that are purified by faith, and saving faith motivates good works.\r\n Love- If not with love, our works are useless and our works and spiritual gifts that produce beneficial results will bring no reward.\r\nb. Proper Standard- In order for works to be good, they must be according to the standard of the word of God. \r\n1. Commands- All commands of scripture are designed to guide us. Everyone who sins is guilty of lawlessness so all sin entails lawlessness. All sin violates God\'s law. \r\n2. All Scripture- God\'s word as a whole is a criterion of good works. Paul insisted that all scripture was useful for ethical training, that all scripture places moral demands on us.\r\n3. General Revelation- God\'s revelation given through creation is a part of standard for good works. \r\nc. Proper Goals- Good works may have any number of immediate goals. God approves of works intended to bring him glory and he condemns works that disregard or oppose his glory.', 8, '2020-05-25 16:52:41', '2020-06-02 02:02:43', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(1529, 455, 829, 'Ethical judgement involves the application of God\'s word to a situation by a person. Ethics should be done from three perspectives: -God\'s word -situation -person\r\nThe best approach is to do ethics from all three perspectives and to let the insights from each perspective inform and influence the others.\r\n1. Situational- Problems, Consequences of Actions and Goals. \r\n2. Normative- God\'s word is the norm and standard for ethics. We are doing ethics from the normative perspective when we look to the bible to tell us what to do. \r\n3. Existential- When we approach ethics by asking questions that are specific to the people involved we are doing ethics from an existential perspective.', 8, '2020-05-25 16:57:39', '2020-06-02 02:02:43', NULL),
(1530, 455, 830, 'God has the ultimate prerogative to determine whether or not particular actions, emotions or thoughts meet or transgress his moral requirements. God will make the ultimate determination of whether of not we have lived morally or immorally and his judgement will be utterly binding. As the absolute judge of morality, God consistently applies absolute moral standard of his character in every judgement he makes. His judgement are perfect, exhibiting flawless insight and wisdom, unfailing fairness and impeccable morality.', 8, '2020-05-25 17:01:54', '2020-06-02 02:02:43', NULL),
(1531, 455, 831, 'Traditionally, theologians have spoken of God\'s revelation primarily in two categories: special revelation and general revelation. In the category of special revelation, they have placed direct communication from God such as scripture, prophesy, dreams and visions. \r\nGeneral revelation has been a catchall category to hold everything that is not considered to be special revelation. It cannot teach us everything but it speaks clearly enough to teach us true things about God. \r\nand existential revelation, God\'s revelation in persons, revelation that is often grouped with general revelation but which really deserves to be treated separately.', 8, '2020-05-25 17:07:23', '2020-06-02 02:02:43', NULL),
(1532, 455, 832, 'Existential Revelation is a different way of categorizing a portion of general revelation. God uses councils, ancient writers, doctrines of men and private spirits to reveal his will to his people. Their determinations must be subject to scripture. \r\nA. External aspects- The external aspects of existential revelation include such things as Human existence, Human judgement both individual and corporate, human behavior. Individual and corporate human judgement is closely related to the fact that we are created in God\'s image. God uses human behavior as an external type of existential revelation. \r\nB. Internal Aspects- Illumination of Holy spirit: a divine gift of understanding that God gives to believers and even to unbelievers. God implants in every human being, a basic knowledge of His law. Inward leading of the Holy spirit more emotive and intuitive.', 8, '2020-05-25 17:15:19', '2020-06-02 02:02:43', NULL),
(1533, 455, 833, 'In 1 John 1:7, the passage explains that God is perfectly free from sin by defining sin as that which is foreign to God\'s nature. The metaphor of God as light is primarily a moral evaluation. Darkness is equated with sins and lies, and light is associated with truth and purity from sin. From the moment we confess our sins, till we walk in the light, we are freed from all our sins. If we walk in light, we won\'t sin, and as he himself is in the light, we have fellowship with one another and the blood of Jesus His son, purifies us from all sins.', 8, '2020-05-25 17:29:02', '2020-06-02 02:02:43', NULL),
(1534, 445, 791, 'According to the Westminster Shorter Catechism,\" Sin is any want of conformity unto, or transgression of, the law of God\".\r\nORIGIN:\r\nHUMAN RACE: Adam and Eve were created sinless, but to continue in the covenant blessings and avoid covenant curses, they needed to remain loyal. They were obliged to fill the earth, cultivate , rule, work an take care of Garden of Eden. But they were asked not to eat from the tree of the knowledge of good and evil.\r\nBut the serpent Eve tempted Eve to eat the forbidden fruit and she gave it to Adam and he ate it. Gen 3:1-7\r\nAs a result, god cursed Adam and Eve because of their disobedience,(Gen 3:8-24)\r\n\"The FALL\"  which refers from the serpent tempting EVE till the God\'s judgement upon Adam and eve\'s sin caused humanity to fall out of God\'s favor and blessings.', 8, '2020-05-27 17:42:49', '2020-06-02 02:03:13', NULL),
(1535, 445, 792, 'When we speak of the authorship of human sin, we have in mind the person that ultimately to blame.\r\nGod is the ultimate standard of goodness, Scripture insists that God isn\'t culpable of guilty of sin or compelling anyone to sin.\r\nJohn 1:5  says that God is light : in him there is no darkness at all.Light refers to moral purity and darkness refers to sin ,so God is completely free from sin.\r\nGod himself is the ultimate standard of good and evil. there is no ultimate moral standard outside him , that can judge him. besides this Scripture tells us that God hates sin in following passages\r\n Deuteronomy 25:16,  Psalms 5:4 &Zechariah 8:17\r\nJames 1:13 says that God cannot be tempted by sin\r\n From above references we conclude that God is free from sin,God hates sin, God is certainly powerful enough to prevent sin.', 8, '2020-05-27 17:56:48', '2020-06-02 02:03:13', NULL),
(1536, 445, 793, 'ORIGINAL SIN is the condition into which Adam\'s natural descendants are born as a result of Adam\'s fall into sin.\r\nEvery part of our human nature has been completely affected by sin :our bodies ,mind and hearts.\r\nConcepts : \r\nSin has damaged our capacity for conceptual thought and cause us to believe that false ideas are true(John 8:43-47, Ephesians 4:17-18). It is sinful to affirm false doctrines and biblical ways of thinking, but it is not sinful to misunderstand some difficult concepts (1 Tim 6:3-5)\r\nBehaviors: \r\nAdam and Eve\'s sins served as the model for all the behavioral sins that have plagued humanity and god has given the fallen humanity over to its desires(Romans 1:29-32)\r\nEmotions:\r\nSin prevents us from Loving God and or neighbors as we should. We all struggle with envy , lust pride, anger and other sinful motions (Mark 7:21-23,James 1:14,15) We cannot please God apart from His saving grace.', 8, '2020-05-27 18:09:25', '2020-06-02 02:03:13', NULL),
(1537, 445, 794, 'Spiritually dead means to dead in our sins and transgressions leading to be under God\'s condemnation because we lack spiritual vitality to please God.\r\nWe are born into this world guilty of Adam \'s sin and sentenced to death , but by the death of Christ on the cross we can escape sin\'s influence in the future. Paul says in Romans 5:10 When we were God\'s enemies , we were reconciled to him through the death of his son .\r\nRoman  8:10 says  that we have spiritual life if Christ is in us .When we come to faith in Christ, we are redeemed from sin by God\'s grace and we are spiritually alive. But by God\'s grace , we can struggle against sin\'s influence now and completely escape it in the future', 7, '2020-05-27 18:24:39', '2020-06-02 02:03:13', NULL),
(1538, 445, 795, 'God \'s purposes are not always clear to us . Our God is a loving God, but he allowed sin , death and pain into this world. the reasons for allowing is not easily comprehend by human beings, but it is obvious that God has chosen this course for us instead. Paul says in Ephesians 1:11 we were predestined according to the plan.\r\nNothing that happens is outside God\'s plan or control. So he certainly had a reason for allowing human sin. At the very least, we can affirm that our sin gives him the opportunity to express many of his attributes that would be hidden from us if we never sinned.God expresses mercy and forbearance in response to human sin.\r\nRomans 8:28 says that everything works for good. Everything God does is right and good. human sin provides an occasion for god to reveal his glory, to express his mercy and compassion through forgiveness. to express his justice and wrath through judgement.', 7, '2020-05-27 18:39:17', '2020-06-02 02:03:13', NULL),
(1539, 442, 842, 'God\'s revelation communicates in countless ways .\r\nFACTS:  Facts plays an important role in our ethical evaluations.God is our ultimate fact. Our ultimate environment. the reality of God\'s existence rules over every ethical question and obligates us to live by the standard of His Character.\r\nGoals :\r\nSpecial revelation gives us countless goals that must be considered in christian ethics Scripture teaches us various goals regarding our neighbors, family and church. It presents god\'s glory as the highest and most important goal in our life. (Romans 1:20-21)\r\nMeans:\r\nto answer any ethical question in a biblical manner , we must also find out appropriate means that God has revealed.Our actions are themselves the means we have chosen to accomplish our goals .\r\nJames 2:15-16. Scripture teaches us about ethical means by giving us examples to consider(1 Corin 10:8-11)', 8, '2020-05-28 18:15:25', '2020-06-02 02:03:43', NULL),
(1540, 442, 843, 'FACTS:\r\nRevelation communicates contents in the form of facts. These facts include everything that God reveals about  our situations.\r\nGod himself is the most basic fact that we learn through revelation. God\'s character is the ultimate norm or standard .From the situational perspective, god is our ultimate fact, our ultimate ethical environment. The reality of God\'s existence rules our every ethical question and obligates us to love by the standard of his character. Through revelation god tells us facts about himself and facts about what he requires. God is the supreme authority over all creation, His authority is absolute and his character is the perfect expression of his will. Besides communicating the facts to us , God\'s revelation also teaches us about a special set of facts that are particularly important for ethics.', 7, '2020-05-28 18:27:07', '2020-06-02 02:03:43', NULL),
(1541, 442, 844, 'Goals are the expected outcome of our endeavors.\r\nSpecial , general and existential revelation , each provides us with goals that we must adopt christian ethics.Special revelation gives us countless goals that must be considered in Christian ethics. Scripture teaches us about dealing with neighbors, relations and responsibilities in our life.\r\nSpecial revelation teaches us , it presents God\'s glory as the highest and most important \r\n(1Cor 10:31)\r\nGeneral revelation identifies many goals that are good and evil. This revelation teaches us that  the greatest goal is to glorify and thank God(Romans 1:20,21)\r\nExistential revelation helps us to discern good goals from evil goals especially through our consciences.(Phillippians 2:13)\r\nso knowing Biblical goals is important to make biblical decisions and the highest goal that we see in each revelation is God\'s glory as highest goal.', 8, '2020-05-28 18:40:06', '2020-06-02 02:03:43', NULL),
(1542, 442, 845, 'Rigor: When Christians are inclined to follow a rigorous strategy towards revelation, they are extremely concerned guard against sin ,especially as it is defined in the prohibitions listed in scripture.\r\nConsequences:\r\nThere are many negative results to this approach destroys Christian freedom by prohibiting believers that are wrong under certain conditions and good under other conditions. for eg: 1Cori 8-10 and Romans where he speaks about food that is sacrificed to idols.\r\nThis strategy also inspires despair in believers by tuning god\'s word into a heavy burden. god gave his word to his people to bless them not to oppress them. Mark 2:27\r\nCorrectives:\r\n A good corrective to rigor is to realize that modern situations are sufficiently different from biblical situations so that we cannot mimic the applications we find in scripture. We can also avoid a strategy of rigor by remembering that Scripture is always sufficiently clear to communicate God\'s will with regard to Christian ethics.', 8, '2020-05-28 18:52:40', '2020-06-02 02:03:43', NULL),
(1543, 442, 846, 'Jesus emphasized the importance of kingdom of God in sermon of the Mount in following three sections :\r\nGod is most glorified through the establishment and triumph of his kingdom in Christ\r\nBEATITUDES:Jesus\'s statements Matthew 5:3-12 are called beatitudes because they each begin with phrase \"blessed are\".In verse 3, 5 and 9 Jesus repeatedly referred to the Kingdom of heaven. Jesus taught that God will be the royal father , the loving king of his blessed children. Each of these blessings Jesus mentioned was closely related to concept of the kingdom of God and so it is essential focus of christian ethics.\r\nLORD\'S PRAYER:\r\nIt is found in Mathew 6:9-13 here also Jesus focus on kingdom of God as the goal for ethics. Our father in heaven , hallowed be your name a,d thy kingdom come all these phrases shows that Jesus set forth kingdom of God as the highest priority of christian ethics.\r\nEarthly needs:\r\nit is in Mathew 6:25-34\r\nJesus taught that we should not experience anxiety over food and clothing, but we should focus on God\'s  kingdom', 8, '2020-05-28 19:08:05', '2020-06-02 02:03:43', NULL),
(1544, 442, 847, 'The three main components of the kingdom are \r\n1. King 2. people 3. covenants\r\nKING-\r\nGod is the rules of his Kingdom.Psalms 103:19 . God \'s supreme rule as the king over all is a major theme that runs throughout the Bible. Although as the creator , God is a king over all nations over Israel in Old testament and Church in New Testament.\r\nPEOPLE\r\nThe people of God \'s kingdom is usually referring to the people that God has called to himself in contrast to the people of the world who follows the ways of evil.Revelation 5:9-10\r\nsays that God\'s kingdom now includes people from every race and  communities spread to the ends of the earth\r\nCOVENANTS;\r\nGod administrated his kingdom through covenants.His covenants expressed God\'s. goodwill towards his people. From the very beginning God\'s relationship with humanity has been governed by covenant.', 8, '2020-05-28 19:20:48', '2020-06-02 02:03:43', NULL),
(1545, 442, 848, 'Three major periods  happened in the development of kingdom of God are \r\n1 . Creation which is initial peace\r\n2. fall which means rebellion\r\n 3.Redemption which refers to final peace\r\nINITIAL PEACE:\r\nAdam and eve were obedient servants and there was peace between God and humanity.All the components of the covenant worked properly to favor humanity.\r\nREBELLION:\r\nHumanity violated one of their covenant obligation as a result they covenant curses. Humanity has continued to rebel against the great king,But mercifully god did not abandon us to rebellion and curse instead he determined to bring final peace to his kingdom\r\nFINAL PEACE:\r\nGod began to restore peace to His kingdom immediately after humanities fall into sin .\r\nHe allowed them to live, and in the midst of cursing them he presented the first offer of the gospel to them (Gen 3:15)', 8, '2020-05-28 19:36:47', '2020-06-02 02:03:43', NULL),
(1546, 442, 849, 'God\'s law is a joy and delight not a burden as it provides us with proper guidelines to live a perfect life. The proper use of the God\'s law is a great blessing to humanity. The law reveals God to us , teaching us how to please him and how to obtain his blessings.Psalms 1:2 says God\'s laws as gracious gift and Psalms 119:29 says His laws are great delight. Keeping the laws results in the covenant blessings of God\'s kingdom. Deuteronomy  28:1-4 says that laws was given for our good, for our prosperity and for our joy.\r\nGod has given us rules to follow in order to produce joy in our lives . When we obey his laws we enjoy him and we glorify him at the same time.\r\nIn my view everything God has given in His divine wisdom is perfect and I love His laws.', 7, '2020-05-28 19:50:09', '2020-06-02 02:03:43', NULL),
(1547, 457, 834, 'A second attribute of the bible that derives from divine inspiration is the authority of scripture. God has all authority therefore whenever and however he speaks all who hear him are obligated to obey him. The bible claims divine authority in two ways; \r\n1. Claim of Authority- a. Historical examples- In the days of Moses God encoded his spoken word in written word and his speech carried authority. God\'s authoritative covenant document that his people are obligated to obey. Jesus frequently appealed to Scripture to justify and explain his actions. Paul believed that God\'s authoritative word binded New testament believers.\r\n2. Explicit claims- The Bible proves its authority through explicit statements because prophecies were inspired and authorized by God, they form a moral standard. The ongoing authority of Scripture is based on God\'s authority.', 7, '2020-05-30 16:38:43', '2020-06-02 02:04:13', NULL),
(1548, 457, 835, 'Because Scripture carries God\'s authority we are morally obligated to conform all of our choices, actions, thoughts and feelings to it. Scripture proves its own authority, we should touch some implications on the idea. We might say that ethical behavior equates to keeping the word of the Lord\'\'. and keeping the word of the Lord must be done in at least two ways; we must conform to scripture\'s breadth by obeying all of its commands, and we must conform to its depth by obeying these commandments with commitment and conviction. Scripture is a great encouragement to know that learning the scriptures reminding ourselves of them, simply becoming a ethical guide. The word of God in Scripture empowers us to live for God. Constant learning and meditation on the word of God brings us into contact with power of God that will always accomplish his purposes.', 8, '2020-05-30 16:51:26', '2020-06-02 02:04:13', NULL),
(1549, 457, 836, 'Scripture helps us proper understanding of our moral standard, our goals, and our motives, or to put it another way, on normative, situational and existential concerns. Failure to reach a proper ethical judgement can be caused by failure properly to assess any of these perspectives. Either through explicit or implicit teaching, the scripture provide us with a comprehensive system of ethical norms. In this sense, the bible\'s sufficiency is unlimited when it comes to revealing the God\'s will for his glory, our salvation, faith and Christian living. General and existential revelation also contain some of these norms, but they contain no additional norms beyond those found directly or indirectly in scripture. The point is simply that bible speaks sufficiently to every area of life, so that our true duty towards God is always an application of Scriptural Norms.', 8, '2020-05-30 17:03:18', '2020-06-02 02:04:13', NULL),
(1550, 457, 837, 'God\'s word is through the uninspired preaching of his Word or the gospel. The New testament frequently confirms this idea when it says the God works through the preaching of the gospel. In Romans 1:15-16, Paul directly stated that the preached gospel carries God\'s power. Paul preached firstly the commandment given by Jesus Christ and secondly, Its God\'s will that none should perish but have everlasting life. Gospel is foolishness in the sight of men, but power of God for the saved. Even today, although people are not ready to listen and accept, still we are compelled by the Spirit of God to preach and proclaim the Good News of Salvation. And due to this many are persecuted, many become martyrs, but still the value of a saved soul is greater than all earth.', 8, '2020-05-30 17:14:45', '2020-06-02 02:04:13', NULL),
(1551, 457, 838, 'Scripture communicates in many different ways. The Bible displays full range of language that we find in human communication. If we do not understand how each type of language communicates, we are likely to misunderstand the bible. \r\nExtraordinary- Those who believes that Bible speaks in extraordinary ways often oversimplify biblical language, developing a system of interpretation that can be applied fairly equally to all of Scripture. Middle ages mistake: because the bible is inspired by God, it communicates in extraordinary ways that exceed human comprehension. Many Christians have insisted that scripture\'s extraordinary nature makes its language easy to interpret. \r\nOrdinary- The bible communicates in ordinary human language, using all the normal conventions of human communication. Clarity of scripture implies in many passages, an overly literal reading would be terribly misleading. The bible uses linguistic conventions of its authors and their original audiences. We have to learn how the authors and original audiences ordinarily used language, and what each author\'s intent was when he wrote.', 8, '2020-05-30 17:23:30', '2020-06-02 02:04:13', NULL),
(1552, 457, 839, 'The Ten Commandments have a special primacy over Scripture\'s other commandments. Historical and Theological.\r\nThe primacy of the Ten Commandments is both historical and theological. Their historical primacy depends on the fact that, to our knowledge, these laws were the first legal code that was received by Israel.\r\nBook of the Covenant: Additional laws received with the Ten Commandments. The Ten Commandments had theological or ideological primacy. God carved the ten commandments in the stone tablets. The giving of the Law was attended by thunder and lightning, smoke, clouds and heavenly trumpets. Moses identified the ten commandments as God\'s very covenant with his people. The Ten commandments were placed within the ark of the covenant. The laws listed by Jesus were from Leviticus 19:18 and summarizes the laws In short, Jesus indicated that by obeying ten commandments a person can earn eternal life. Even in the New testament the ten commandments were still spoken of in terms that reflected their theological primacy.', 8, '2020-05-30 17:31:43', '2020-06-02 02:04:13', NULL),
(1553, 457, 840, 'It is been common to categorize the various laws in the Old Testament, Bible into three major groups: moral law, ceremonial law and civil law. Moral laws are typically thought to convey God\'s ethical standards and are usually identified with the Ten Commandments. Civil Laws provide for the governing of society, especially during the period of Israel\'s theocracy. Ceremonial laws. in turn, are those which provide instruction for worshiping God. Frequently, these are most closely associated with the Old Testament sacrificial system, and tabernacle and temple administration. The existence of these categories, and the proper identification of laws, provides a mechanism by which they can avoid applying God\'s word to their lives. God\'s people are no longer to perform many of the specific behaviors that were required under the Mosaic sacrificial and temple system.', 8, '2020-05-30 17:38:33', '2020-06-02 02:04:13', NULL),
(1554, 457, 841, 'I would answer my friend by saying that the civil and ceremonial laws of the Old testament have expired in the sense that we are not to return to Old Testament patterns of life. In another sense, Old Testament civil and ceremonial laws still apply to modern Christians. Christians should still look to the civil and ceremonial laws of the Old testament, as well as to its moral laws for ethical guidance. Be it Old testament or New testament, the laws for man are needed for their social, cultural, and spiritual morality. Scripture teaches us the continuing application of every Old Testament law, and they help us to keep the good character and maintain it that we may lead a holy and God fearing life.', 8, '2020-05-30 17:48:05', '2020-06-02 02:04:13', NULL),
(1555, 444, 850, 'God\'s authority , control and presence impacts our ethical responsibilities. When God reveals His ethical judgments,they are true and never subject to scrutiny. God\'s authority in ethics is absolute, so his moral judgments , his outlook on good and evil must be accepted as true simply because he has said so. God\'s authority is always superior to creaturely authority,God\'s moral judgments are beyond legitimate questioning and it is the reason the Bible insists that ethical decisions be made in moral submission of God.\r\nPhillippians 2:12-13 Christianity has always affirmed that God is the creator, he can and does exercise sovereign control over his creation and it is the basis of for ethical responsibility.\r\nGod\'s control is moral ,he orders the creations so that the circumstances if our lives never excuse our unethical choices.\r\nOur ethical decisions must always account for God\'s presence with us as judge, both now and in the future.', 8, '2020-05-31 18:32:14', '2020-06-02 02:04:40', NULL),
(1556, 444, 851, 'The preternatural realm is the realm that is beyond the nature but not above the nature the way that God is but it is rather beside the nature as a distinct aspect of creation. It is inhabited by invisible spirits such as angels and demons.\r\nAngels and demons:\r\nGod has also populated the universe with a vast number of spiritual persons known as angel and demons. Both angles and demons are intelligent, rational beings that have wills and personalities . When God created these beings , they were all angels , pure and perfect serving God in his heavenly kingdom , but some of theses angels , willfully rebelled against God and fell from theses blessed state into condemnation.\r\nBible calls term angels to those blessed angels who remained loyal to God and refers as demons to those who are fallen and rebellious angels.\r\nAngels serve as God\'s loyal messengers and agents (2 kings 19:35, Psalms 91:11,12, Hebrew 1:14)\r\nAngels need no salvation and salvation is not available to demons.\r\nDemons harm us in many ways , by tempting us and try to lead us away from moral choices(Job 1,2)\r\nSatan and angels are in constant conflict against each other , this is called spiritual warfare(Eph 6:12)', 8, '2020-05-31 18:50:11', '2020-06-02 02:04:40', NULL),
(1557, 444, 852, 'The natural realm refers to all that is in the world with our eyes. The living beings and all other creation are its inhabitants , human beings at the centre of creation and responsibilities.\r\nCREATION\r\nIn Genesis 2: 7 we see human beings as having central importance of humanity upon the earth .\r\nIn Gen 1:28 God did not create us to be equals with the plants and animals, but to rule and govern.\r\nFALL\r\nWhen Adam and Eve fell into sin , God responded by cursing both the human race and the earth. Nature is not as it was originally designed to be, but it is corrupted by sin and often serves as God\'s instrument of discipline for us.\r\nPsalms 19:1 ans 1 Timothy 4:4-5 says that nature is still good and it is still God\' creation  ans it is still a means God uses to still minister to us and to bless us.\r\nREDEMPTION \r\nGod will ultimately refine both heaven and earth , to create a new heaven and new earth.Isaiah 65:17.66:22)', 8, '2020-05-31 19:05:20', '2020-06-02 02:04:40', NULL),
(1558, 444, 853, 'Preternatural inhabitants which are angels and demons are constantly in warfare with each other. They influence the natural realms in a great manner.\r\nNatural realms are inhabited by living beings and other things created by God as per creating accounts in Genesis 1 and 2. Humanity being the centre master work of natural realm,  since the Fall into corruption by sinning against God, the preternatural realms are always trying to interfere and influence humanity in their own respective ways. \r\nexample 1:\r\nHebrews 1:14 says that angels are ministering spirits , it means they are constantly working to ensure that we always have an opportunity to behave morally\r\nExample 2:\r\nDemons like angels are also able to interact with the natural realm , which they do in order to harm us. In New Testament the most commonly way demons attack Christians is by tempting them into idolatry. Job 1 and 2 says about  Satan the chief of demons harming  Job.\r\nExample 3 :\r\nEphesians 6 says about our warfare against demonic rulers, authorities, powers, force in the preternatural world.', 8, '2020-05-31 19:21:57', '2020-06-02 02:04:40', NULL),
(1559, 444, 854, 'All true moral goodness is rooted in God Himself. God\'s attributes are inseparable from his person : they define who he is. All God\'s essential attributes are immutable - they can never change.\r\nGoodness refers to moral purity and perfection . God is the ultimate standard of morality. There is no external standard of goodness by which he or we can be judged.\r\nHumanity was created to reflect God\'s goodness.Whatever God blesses and approve is good,and whatever God curses and condemns is evil\r\nGod blessed Adam and Eve, because they had innate attribute of goodness.\r\nGod appointed humanity to be his vassal kings on the earth and to fill , subdue and rule it for his glory.', 8, '2020-05-31 19:31:54', '2020-06-02 02:04:40', NULL),
(1560, 444, 855, 'Fall has prevented the unredeemed human beings from obtaining a proper knowledge of God\'s commands in following ways :\r\n1.  Sin hinders humanity\'s access to revelation.One of the chief ways the fall has hindered humanity is\'s access to revelation is by limiting the holy Spirit\'s work of illumination and inward leading as God cursed humanity by withholding these divine gifts.\r\n2.Sin prevents humanity\'s \'s understanding of revelation.\r\nFallen human beings still have eyes and ears to receive God\'s revelation, but hearts are hardened against God and his truth. (Ephesians 4:17, 18)\r\n3. Sin \'s impacts on humanity\'s obedience to revelation.\r\nFall has corrupted our nature and our will to the point that we rebel against God, in fact we are incapable of submitting to his word (Hosea 4:1)', 8, '2020-05-31 19:45:48', '2020-06-02 02:04:40', NULL),
(1561, 444, 856, 'God has so many attributes , it is more helpful to think of them in terms of a gemstone rather than in terms of triangle. Each of God\'s attributes is a perspective on his entire being, each of god\'s attribute is dependent on others and qualified on others.\r\nIf we consider His attributes authority, justice and goodness,His authority is good and just. It is good and just that God possesses this authority. we can always trust a God who is just and good. \r\nHis attributes  are immutable which gives us confidence that no matter what he is faithful ans His words never change.His attributes always agree because they always describe the same consistent, unified person', 8, '2020-05-31 19:56:57', '2020-06-02 02:04:40', NULL),
(1562, 444, 857, 'In Christ we have capable of true goodness again , but we struggle with sin. When God redeems , he recreates us , giving us new hearts and spirits that are righteous rather than sinful. Our redemption is not yet complete so that even with our new nature, we are still tainted by sin.  we are redeemed but still in the bondage of our corrupt body , so we struggle against sin. \r\nBut we are no longer enslaved to sin ,our wills are restored and sin\'s mastery is broken so that we are once again able to resist sin.  And the Holy Spirit indwells us in order to strengthen and motivate us against sin. So depending on Holy Spirit has helped me against sin.\r\nBut sometimes we depend on ourselves rather than Holy spirit, then we fail and fall into sin as it has happened to me many times.', 8, '2020-05-31 20:08:29', '2020-06-02 02:04:40', NULL),
(1563, 456, 766, 'Peter\'s apostolic confession as mentioned in the book of Mathew 16:15-17, wherein Jesus asked Peter  Who do do you say I am, accordingly Peter confessed that \"You are the Christ, the Son of the living God\" Jesus replied that - Blessed are you Simon, for this was not revealed to you by man, but by my Father in heaven. \r\nPeter\'s confession as mentioned in the gospels, acknowledges and recognizes that Jesus is indeed the Messiah. And then from that point on launches into the role of the suffering Messiah. Peter along with the disciples having witnessed all the miracles that Jesus did. Peter acknowledges that God has been at work through out the life of Jesus, he recognizes Jesus humanity and his divine nature as the Christ or Messiah. \r\n\r\nTransfiguration is another event wherein Jesus was revelead in His glory to His disciples, wherein Jesus appearance was transformed to a divine nature. \r\n\r\nJesus took his disciples Peter, James & John up to a mountain to pray. And while they were there, Jesus appearance changed. He was transfigured in front of His 3 disciples and also there came Moses and Elijah and they conversed with Jesus. Furthermore God\'s voice was heard from heaven, confirming that Jesus was the son of God. As Moses and Elijah appeared with Jesus, it showed that both the Mosaic Law and the Prophetic Office was fulfilled in Jesus - messianic identity.', 9, '2020-06-03 15:18:49', '2020-06-15 12:56:36', NULL),
(1564, 456, 767, 'After Jesus was baptized under John in the river Jordan, was filled by the Holy Spirit in the form of a dove. Therafter the Spirit guided Jesus into the desert where he fasted 40 days before being tempted by Satan. Jesus though he was weakened in His physical state due to the fasting period, yet He was spiritually and mentally strong as He continuously spent time in prayer with heavenly father. Despite his hunger, Jesus refused to use His divine power to satisfy His physical needs. Though Jesus had all the authority He did not demonstrate His power or authority to prove himself when He was challenged by the Devil. Since Jesus goals were well defined, He refused to compromise with the temptations of the devil and have a short cut to reach His goal by negotiating with the enemy through a sinful path. \r\n\r\nBiblical scholars point out that Jesus temptation by Satan paralleled by what Adam faced in the garden of Eden. Whereas Adam failed completely, Jesus overcame all the temptation. As the first Adam represented all of mankind, he failed and resulting in all human race becoming a slave to sin. But Jesus the second Adam overcame temptation, bringing salvation to His people.\r\n\r\nJesus entire ife was in itself was a test of temptation. Jesus had to overcome all sorts of temptation and be sinless. Also being offered as a sacrifice without sin, as the most perfect substitute for the sins of mankind. \r\n\r\nJesus temptation is His impeccability. \r\nThe word impeccability means inability to Sin. Jesus was the second persion of the trinity. And God can\'t sin, because he can\'t act in ways that are contrary to his nature. \r\n\r\nJesus overcoming the temptation with proved that He was the most perfect substitue for the sins of mankind, without sin or blemish.', 9, '2020-06-03 15:33:06', '2020-06-15 12:56:36', NULL),
(1565, 456, 768, 'Crucifixion was a form of death penalty used in the ancient Roman Empire. It\'s victims were tied to the cross, or nailed to it, as Jesus case and thereafter hung on the cross. Most of the victims died due to suffocation. Jesus crucifixion was unique because it was his responsibility to die on behalf of mankind.\r\n\r\nTwo major factors can be considered with regards to Crucifixion\r\n1. Imputation for our sins to Jesus\r\n2. Divine judgment against sin\r\n\r\nImputation:\r\nSimple meaning of imputation is assignment or reckoning. When Jesus was imputed to die on the cross, God was assigning the sins of the entire human race on Jesus, in other words Jesus became the offering or sacrifice in our place and God imputed to him all the sins and blame that was reserved for mankind. But in particular Jesus had not sinned, nor was he personaly guilty of any misconduct. But from a legal perspected, God considered Jesus as if He had personally committed every sin imputed to him.\r\n\r\nBefore our sins were imputed to him, Jesus was blameless and perfect. But once when our sins were imputed to him or recokened to his account.  God viewed him as a sinner guilty of all the sins that were assigned to him \r\n\r\nIn 2 Corinthians 5:21 says, \r\nGod made him who had no sin to be sin for us.\r\n\r\nAnd though we would think is it just or righteous for God to impute our sins to Christ ? but in God\'s perfect will, God had chosen Jesus to be a sacrifice for the sins of mankind. Only God can prepare such a salvation that is perfect and that fulfills all the requirements of the laws, and that would meet God\'s standards or requirements. \r\n\r\nJesus death was a divine judment against sin. Before God laid our guilt on him, Jesus was perfect and He couldn;t die. But once our sins were imputed to Him, His death was necessary.\r\n\r\nJesus bore the full wrath of God that was against our sins, fulfilled all the requirements, and there does not remain any more judgement for human beings, it was all assigned to Jesus.', 9, '2020-06-03 15:51:23', '2020-06-15 12:56:36', NULL),
(1566, 456, 769, 'After Jesus crucifixion, on the first day of thew week, Jesus rose from the dead and He appeared to his disciples for a period of 40 days. \r\n\r\nDeath is the greatest tragedy and enemy of human beings The worst manisfestation of sin in the world. But Jesus Christ conquered death by resurrecting from the grave through the power of the Holy Spirit. Jesus proved to all of creation that he really is God\'s Son and the heir to His kingdom. Jesus first fruits from the death, therein He has promised future resurrection to all those who believe in Him and are His faithful followers.\r\n\r\nGod\'s plan to redeem humanity and the rest of creation depended on him fulfilling all the requirements and promises of the law and to establish his kingdom on earth under the kinship of a descendant of David. But God couldn\'t do this unless Jesus had resurrected from the dead and fulfilled all of God\'s covenant promises. This is the reasons that the New Testament calls the resurrection an affirmation of Jesus role as Christ.\r\n\r\nThe next aspect to be considered is Blessings of Salvation : Jesus having accomplished resurrection, offers a wide variety of blessings. It results in our justification, which is the forgiveness of our sins. It is the regeneration of our spirits and opens the door for our eternal inheritance. The promise of a resurrection for all future believers, paves the way for the blessings of salvaiton that we have access now and also for the future.\r\n\r\nThe resurrection of Jesus from the dead is the central point of the New Testament and all the blessings that flow along with it. Firstly the resurrection teaches us who Jesus is. It\'s a vindication of him as the Messiah and the Lord and the Son of God \r\n\r\nFurthermore the most important or the main theme is that Jesus Christ is alive today. He\'s risen from the dead and is seated at the right hand of the father. Moreover through Jesus, we have access to the risen power and believers are transformed by the Holy Spirit to a new life gaining access to heavenly blessings and power through Jesus Christ.', 8, '2020-06-03 16:06:17', '2020-06-15 12:56:36', NULL),
(1567, 456, 770, 'Through Jesus Christ, I have access to the spiritual blessings - as a child of God, we are ever transformed by his resurrected power through the Holy Spirit. As a renewed, transformed believer  we are ever at the disposal for the Kingdom of God. Carrying our cross daily and following the Lord, with all our priorities set as God wants us to be, always giving importance to God\'s will in the areas of our influence in terms of family, neighbors and in our communities etc.\r\n\r\nAffirming and confessing that Jesus is the Christ, it comes under our responsibility and beavior to be every impacting the world around us through our life and sharing the benefits and privileges that God has given us as believers. Whether it be within the family among each member of the house hold, or among our neighbors or friends we come into contact with on daily basis. The communities around us wherein we are a part of. It is very important that our doctrine and lifestyles match, otherwise it is very difficult to have any sort of influence in the enviroment wherein God has placed us. \r\n\r\nIn these times of uncertainity, it is very important as a representative of God\'s kingdom to give hope to the communities or families around us. As much as possible to share the burdens together in prayer, and to develop an opportunity for fellowship to support, encourage and motivate. Even if there is a need among any of the family or individual, to find a way to support and sort out the issue to the best of God given ability.\r\n\r\nTo bear the marks of the cross and resurrection of Jesus in our life - even in the darkest moment of their life, to give them a resurrecting hope and direct them to Jesus Christ. Also in general ordinary people are confused with all the different religions and doctrines around them, not to entertain further confusion, but to present the gospel in it\'s simplicity and continuously pray for them, and let God work on their lives.', 9, '2020-06-03 16:19:51', '2020-06-15 12:56:36', NULL),
(1568, 458, 842, 'There are basic types of revelation; general revelation, which comes to us through the creation in general and existential revelation, which comes to us through persons, remember that God reveals his will to us in all three of these ways. Even though special, general, existential revelation differ in some respects, they all communicate content in the form of facts. These facts include everything that God reveals about our situation, such as events, people, objects, ideas, duties, actions- even God and his revelation. \r\nIt is possible to speak of the facts that God\'s revelation communicates in countless ways. In addition to speaking about facts in general, we will also speak of goals and means. Goals are the intended or potential outcomes of thoughts, words, and deeds. They include everything we  might think, say, or do, and any tool or method that we might use in order  to accomplish our objectives.', 8, '2020-06-03 16:46:10', '2020-06-15 22:20:58', NULL),
(1569, 458, 843, 'God is our ultimate fact, our ultimate ethical environment. In order for us to know our obligations before God, he must first reveal himself to us. God\'s character is our ultimate norm or standard. Correspondingly, from the situational, perspective, God is our ultimate fact, our ethical environment. The reality of God\'s existence rules over every ethical question and obligates us to live by the standard of his character. God is the supreme authority over all creation. His authority is absolute, and his character is the perfect expression of his will. So, when he reveals his character is the perfect expression of his will. So, when he reveals his character, that revelation is the means through which God exercises control much like human governments exercise control through their laws. And just as human beings obey civil laws because they bow to the government\'s authority, all creation must obey God\'s laws by bowing to his authority.', 8, '2020-06-03 16:55:15', '2020-06-15 22:20:58', NULL),
(1570, 458, 844, 'Goals- goal in ethics, we have in mind the expected outcomes of our endeavors. In many ways, this is no different from the way that we set goals to accomplish anything else in life. They can be things we hope to accomplish immediately, or things we plan to do in the distant future. Our goals give direction to our actions. Special, general, and existential revelation each teach us important generic facts, each type of revelation also provides us with goals that we must adopt in Christian ethics. Existential revelation also helps  us to discern good goals from evil goals, especially through our consciences. And in the case of believers, the Holy spirit is another source of existential revelation, moving within us so that we pursue good goals and shun evil ones.', 7, '2020-06-03 17:02:53', '2020-06-15 22:20:58', NULL),
(1571, 458, 845, 'The strategy of rigor results from mistaken beliefs about the Bible\'s similarity to modern world and about its clarity. This strategy gives little or no consideration to the ways that the facts, goals, and means of Scripture differ from those in the modern world. The strategies has some consequences too. Firstly, it destroys Christian freedom by prohibiting behaviors that are wrong under certain conditions, but good under other conditions. The classic example of this are Paul\'s discussions of food that had been sacrificed to idols in 1 Corinthians 8-10, and in Romans 14. \r\nSecond, a strategy of rigor also inspires despair in believers by turning God\'s word into a heavy burden. God gave his word to his people to bless them, not to oppress them. And there are many, many places in Scripture that state this idea. example is Mark 2;27 and in Romans 9;4,5. \r\nA good corrective is to realize  that modern situations are sufficiently different from biblical situations so that we cannot simply mimic the application we find in the scripture.', 8, '2020-06-03 17:19:30', '2020-06-15 22:20:58', NULL),
(1572, 458, 846, 'Jesus spoke about the kingdom of God in the sermon on the mount found in Mt 5-7. Three specific times when Jesus spoke of the kingdom of God as the goal of ethics during his sermon about earthly needs. In each of these sections, Jesus indicated that the kingdom of God must be the main priority of our lives. \r\n1. Beatitudes- Christian ethics- viewed as means of determining which human person, acts and attitudes receive God\'s blessing and which do not. So, which the beatitudes, Jesus began his Sermon by encouraging people to live ethically. Jesus set forth the blessings and ethics in terms of kingdom of God. Jesus specifically set forth the blessings of god\'s kingdom as the reward or goal that was to motivate his listeners to live ethically. \r\n2. Lord\'s Prayer- Jesus indicated that all creatures in heaven already obey God\'s will. but Jesus instructed us to pray that all creatures on earth would obey the divine king in the same way. \r\n3. Earthly needs- Jesus made it very plain that the ultimate goal of the christian life, the greatest end toward which we are to strive is the glorification of God through the triumph of his Kingdom.', 9, '2020-06-03 17:29:00', '2020-06-15 22:20:58', NULL),
(1573, 458, 847, '1. Kings- Kings were expected to protect and provide for their people, treat them with kindness, rule wisely to benefit their people. God is frequently presented as the suzerain or supreme emperor over all creation. God was king in a special way over Israel in the old testament and the church in the new testament.\r\n2. People- in old testament often Abraham and his descendants and in New testament generally the church. They populate the whole world, improve the world as Go had improved the Garden of Eden. God ruled directly over all humanity. He intended the world to be his kingdom. The people that God has called to himself; when God create the world, he set up humanity as his vassal kings. \r\n3. Covenants- God administered his kingdom through covenants. His covenants expressed God\'s goodwill toward his people , listed the people\'s obligations towards God, and stated the consequences of obedience and curses for disobedience.', 8, '2020-06-03 17:37:59', '2020-06-15 22:20:58', NULL),
(1574, 458, 848, 'Historical phases- creation; initial peace, fall- rebellion, redemption- final peace\r\n1. Initial peace- Adam and Eve were obedient servants. As a result, there was peace between God and humanity. All the components of the covenant worked properly to favor humanity. And at first, Adam and eve were blessed with close fellowship with God and continued to live in the Garden of Eden where life was easy and blissful.\r\n2. Rebellion- Humanity violated one of their covenant obligations. As a result, they received the covenant curses. Instead of turning to God in repentance and keeping our covenant obligations, we continued to rebel and to perpetuate the covenant curses. But God did not abandon us to rebellion and curse. Instead he determined to bring final peace to his kingdom and to return blessings to  his people.\r\n3. Final Peace- God began to restore peace to his kingdom immediately after humanity\'s fall into sin. Protoevangelion- God offered to send a redeemer to rescue humanity from the curse of sin. Therefore, God was working towards the goal of full redemption and success of his kingdom. But he did not restore his kingdom to the glory it had displayed during the initial peace days.', 8, '2020-06-03 17:50:08', '2020-06-15 22:20:58', NULL),
(1575, 458, 849, 'I think that God\'s laws are not burdensome. The old testament view, it was a burden because nobody can save themselves according to the law. But in the new testament, due to the sacrifice of Jesus Christ, he himself bore all the burden of our sins and set us free from its burden. In 1 John 5;3, it says that it is Love for God, to keep his commands and they are not burdensome. If someone looks at God\'s commands, in the wrong way, and says that they are heavy to bear he is merely revealing his own weakness. But if obeyed in the right way, it is easy and helps us in the proper relevant Christian Living. \r\nJesus took away our burdens in his shoulders and set us free, and hence he said in Mt 11.28 to cast all our burden to his and the yoke will be lifted. They have already been taken on the cross, we are free, we are in Christ, unburdened. This is true today and everyday.', 9, '2020-06-03 18:02:40', '2020-06-15 22:20:58', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(1576, 461, 850, 'God is the ultimate fact in our situation because he gives existent and meaning to every other fact. \r\na. Authority- God\'s right to rule derives from the fact that he is the creator and sustainer of all creation. Absolute- He has complete and total freedom on his creation. Exclusive- God\'s authority is always superior to creaturely authority. Exhaustive- He has authority on everything in every detail. \r\nb. Control- God powerfully governs everything that exists. Sovereign- He has an unlimited ability and right to control the creation. \r\nmoral- Creation is conducive to morality. He provides the means and the opportunity to avoid sin. \r\nc. Presence- 1. Covenant King- Our first parents were vassal kings whose job it was to spread God\'s kingdom throughout the earth. 2. Incarnate Lord- When Jesus was born, God became physically present and walked freely among society as one of us. 3-Ministering Spirit- When Jesus ascended into heaven he poured forth his spirit on the church.', 8, '2020-06-08 16:40:39', '2020-06-16 16:39:49', NULL),
(1577, 461, 851, 'Modern Christians, often pay little attention to angels and demons the fact is that angels and demons have significant impact on the things that happen in our lives. Inhabitants- Scripture teaches that God has also populated the universe with a vast number of spiritual persons known as angels and demons. Both angels and demons are intelligent, rational human beings that have wills and personalities. All prenatural beings were originally angels. \r\na. Angels- They serve as God\'s loyal messengers and agents. They communicate his word to human beings and interact with humanity. By observing God\'s salvation of humanity, angels learn more about Lord\'s glory and are better able to praise him.\r\nb. Demons- They are fallen rebellious angels. They are able to interact with the natural realm which they do in order to harm us.', 8, '2020-06-08 16:46:12', '2020-06-16 16:39:49', NULL),
(1578, 461, 852, 'The details of the natural world are nearly limitless.\r\n1. Creation- Human beings are of central importance upon the earth, part of nature, lords and rulers over nature. God has called human beings to govern the world- to administer it in a way that promotes life and growth, turning the world into a kingdom that is fit for him to inhabit. \r\n2. Fall- When Adam and Eve fell into sin, God cursed both the human race and the earth, subjecting them to corruption. Nature is the recipient of God\'s cursing. The earth still proclaims God\'s goodness and majesty, and God uses it to provide many good things.\r\n3. Redemption- In redemption, the effects of the fall are reversed. The natural realm becomes an instrument of redemption, a recipient of redemption.', 7, '2020-06-08 16:52:53', '2020-06-16 16:39:49', NULL),
(1579, 461, 853, 'Both angels and demons in our ethical environment have impact on our lives. Angels serve as God\'s loyal messengers and agents. They communicate his word to human beings, and they interact with humanity on God\'s behalf. Eg, in 2 Kings 19:35 we learn the angel of the Lord slew 185,000 Assyrian troops in one night to halt Sennacherib\'s invasion of Judah. another one is, Psalms 91:11-12 teaches that angels also work to prevent God\'s faithful followers from stubbing their toes. \r\nDemons are also able to interact with the natural realm which they do in order to harm us. In New testament the most common way demons attack us is by tempting them into idolatry. Another one is temptation and harming us. For eg, in Job 1-2 we find that Satan, the chief of demons was permitted to destroy Job\'s possession and health and to kill his children.', 8, '2020-06-08 17:02:56', '2020-06-16 16:39:49', NULL),
(1580, 461, 854, 'Humanity was created to reflect God\'s goodness. \r\n1. Image- God, the great king over all creation appointed human beings to be his living images. He created us with qualities that reflected his own perfections. But we were created without flaw and without sin, in conformity to the standard of his character. \r\n2. Blessing- Whatever God blesses and approves id good, and whatever God curses and condemns is evil. God blessed Adam and Eve because they had the innate attribute of goodness. \r\n3. Cultural Mandate- God appointed humanity: to be his vassal kings on earth and to fill, subdue and rule it for his glory. God indicated that humanity was not only physically capable of accomplishing this task but morally capable as well.', 8, '2020-06-08 17:09:06', '2020-06-16 16:39:49', NULL),
(1581, 461, 855, 'The Fall has prevented human beings from obtaining a proper knowledge of God\'s commands.\r\n1. Access to Revelation- The Fall limits the Holy Spirit\'s work of illumination and inward leading. Illumination: a divine gift of knowledge or understanding that is primarily cognitive. Inward leading: a divine gift of knowledge or understanding that is primarily emotive or intuitive. God reveals himself in ways that bless those who love him and that curse those who hate him.\r\n2. Understanding of Revelation- Moral understanding depends on more than mere cognition, involves the whole person. Instead of accepting true knowledge from God, we believe that lies that our sinful hearts invent. \r\n3. Obedience to Revelation- There is a sense in which knowledge and obedience are essentially the same thing. Obedience leads to Knowledge- obedience is a prerequisite for knowledge.\r\n4. Redemption- Redemption began immediately after the fall, when God extended mercy to Adam and Eve, did not immediately eradicate all the effects of the Fall.', 8, '2020-06-08 17:17:30', '2020-06-16 16:39:49', NULL),
(1582, 461, 856, 'The comfort of us Christians is in the fact that, Immutability of God is an attribute that He is unchanging in his character, will, and covenant promises. God is self existent- that he was created by nothing and has always existed forever. However, God has never once been in need of anything. God is omnipotent- there\'s absolutely nothing He is unable to do. He is Omniscient, he knows everything, is infinitely wise, consistently wise, perfectly wise. God is unchanging as said James 1.17-\"...Father of heavenly lights, who does not change like shifting shadows\".Man can be unfaithful, but God remains faithful for he cannot disown himself as said in 2 Timothy 2.13.  As with all of God\'s attributes, they are not separate, isolated traits but interconnected parts of his perfect whole being.', 9, '2020-06-08 17:26:16', '2020-06-16 16:39:49', NULL),
(1583, 461, 857, 'As human beings, we are often tempted to sin and it is a struggle to resist sin. Some of the strategies are as follows, \r\n1. Resist/ Defend it- in Heb 12.4- it says to defend and resist to the point of shedding your blood which means until the last breath of our life. \r\n2. Be Strong in the Lord and his mighty power. (Ephesians 6.10)\r\n3. Put on the whole armor of God, to stand against the schemes of devil. (Ephesians 6.11)\r\n4. Pray in the Spirit on all occasions with all kinds of prayers and requests.\r\n5. Trust in the Lord and his mighty power.\r\n6. Depend upon his abounding grace and ask of help from the Holy Spirit.\r\nSome of the unhelpful strategies can be relying on self power, wisdom and wealth, as they are of no great value.', 8, '2020-06-08 17:35:26', '2020-06-16 16:39:49', NULL),
(1584, 460, 761, 'The Scripture teaches that the Son was at the Father\'s side during creation and that the Father created the world by or through Him(John 1:1-3 and Hebrews 1:2).\r\nColossi ans 1:16 Paul says about the Son\'s involvement in the creation.He explicitly says that creation was accomplished by the Son.\r\nDuring the first three days of creation , God formed or gave shape into the world through the power of His word, HE separated light from darkness, sky fro sea, and dry land from water.He created Sun , moon ,stars, fishes,birds to fill the earth. He created humanity both to fill the earth and to rule over all creatures.\r\nThe author of Hebrews connected the idea that God the Son was active in creation,with the fact that he was the \"heir of all things\"., that means he was the king that would inherit ownership and rule over the entire creation.And we understand from New Testament that the kingdom is to be ruled by God\'s special Son ,through whom and by whom creation was accomplished.', 8, '2020-06-09 17:45:57', '2020-06-16 16:41:07', NULL),
(1585, 460, 762, 'God\'s eternal counsel regarding Christ is in two aspects:\r\nforeknowledge and purpose\r\nRegarding His foreknowledge in Isaiah 46:10 God said that from the beginning, that is , before He created the world, he knew what was still to come. And regarding his purpose he said \"My purpose will stand and I will do all that I please\".\r\nThrough God\'s foreknowledge, God knew, prior to creation, of events that would occur in the course of history.The Father, Son,And Holy Spirit are all knowing.God created the universe in order to display and increase His glory through His kingdom in Christ. WE see this purpose throughout the scriptures in Psalms 145:1-21, !timothy 1:17, Hebrew 1:1-13. God\'s eternal decree regarding his glorious kingdom as a covenant of redemption. Scripture indicates that before the creation of the world the persons of the God head entered into a solemn arrangement to secure redemption,and to apply it to fallen creation.The Son promised to become incarnate and die in order to redeem fallen humanity from the consequences of sin. And the /father promised to accept the Son\'s sacrifice in payment for the redemption of sinners.', 8, '2020-06-09 18:00:16', '2020-06-16 16:41:07', NULL),
(1586, 460, 763, 'God\'s promises are immutable.Th persons of Trinity enters into an arrangement  called \"covenant of redemption in which they promise to redeem fallen humanity. This covenant of redemption resulted in another covenant being made to secure redemption after fall into sin. It is also called COVENANT OF GRACE. in this covenant God the Father promise to fulfill his kingdom plans for creation and humanity, through the Son\'s incarnation as Jesus Christ.\r\nIT has six administrations :\r\nADAMIC ADMINISTRATIONS Or ADAMIC COVENANT:\r\nIN Genesis 3, we see that immediately after the fall with Adam as head of covenant people, redemption was first offered to humanity in Gie 3:15 as first Gospel\r\nNOAHIC COVENANT:\r\nWe see renewal of the covenant that took place with Noah in Genesis 6:9.God promised to maintain the creation in a a stable manner so that humanity may be preserved until Son\'s redeeming work was complete.\r\nABRAHAMIC COVENANT:\r\nIN Genesis 15, 17, 22 we  see that God made a covenant with Abraham that one of his descendant would be redeemer which we see to be fulfilled in Galatains 3:16\r\nMOSES COVENANT:\r\nExidus 19-24 God institued a scrificial system tahtb illustrated the sacrife the SOn would fulfill as Jesus of Nazareth\r\nDAVIDIC COVENANT:\'Psalms 89, 32 we see that redeemer would be descended from David and Th eternal kingdom would be established by him.', 8, '2020-06-09 18:20:09', '2020-06-16 16:41:07', NULL),
(1587, 460, 764, 'There are four aspects of Jesus\' redeeming work which are:\r\n1. His inauguration of the Kingdom of God:\r\nThe New Testament teaches us that Jesus, the incarnate Son Of God, inaugurated God\'s kingdom on earth. When he returns to glory , this evil age will end, new heaven and new earth will bring complete restoration. Jesus proved himself by many miracles and teachings and granted Holy Spirit as a down payment\r\n2.His obedience: His passive obedience was his submission to a life of humiliation and suffering. His life of obedience to everything the Father, Jesus perfectly kept God\'s laws, He never sinner,ad He always did what God Commanded, theses shows his active obedience. We get salvation by his merit.\r\n3. His resurrection : By raising from the dead, Jesus conquered death itself and secured the everlasting physical life of everyone that has faith in Him. 1 Cor 15:20,21\r\n4. His ascension:\r\nThe ascension is important in Jesus work of redemption as now HE rules as the Father\'s servant king over all creation ,His people or church Corinthians 15:23-25. He completes his sacrifice in the heavenly temple and to remain in the Father\'s presence mediating and interceding for his people\r\nHebrews 7:25-26', 9, '2020-06-09 18:35:46', '2020-06-16 16:41:07', NULL),
(1588, 460, 765, 'CONSUMMATION\r\n The events surrounding Jesus  future return and the final stage of our salvation are\r\ndestruction of God\'s enemies,the blessing of his people and the renewal of his creation\r\nJesus\' return:\r\nIt will be sudden as the date of Jesus\'s return is known only by Father.\r\n1. Personal and physical return:\r\nJesus will return in the same way , he ascended into heaven\r\n2. public and visible return:\r\neveryone will see Jesus\r\n3. Triumphant return :Jesus will return as a powerful conqueror.\r\nEVENTS THAT WILL HAPPEN TO ALL PEOPLE AT THE LAST JUDGEMENT:\r\n1.General resurrection: Everyone that has ever died will be resurrected. Believer\'s bodies will be free from corruption and presence of sin. Bodies of unbelievers will continue to be plagued by the effect of sin.\r\n2.Last judgement:\r\nJesus will destroy all his enemies and bless all his faithful,people. Every human being will be judged\r\n3. Renewal of creation : Jesus will purge and renew creation . All creation will be restored to God\'s original plan.', 9, '2020-06-09 18:52:24', '2020-06-16 16:41:07', NULL),
(1589, 463, 858, '1. Loyalty- loyalty is the cornerstone of the concept of love. The most basic responsibility of the people is loyalty to the king. The suzerain\'s love was expressed largely in the form of covenant loyalty to his people through his protection, justice and meeting the needs of the people. God\'s fatherhood is a metaphor, behind of which is the fact that God is our King. Jesus is our Lord and King and we render love to him through loyal obedience and loyalty to his church.\r\n2. Orientation- God and his kingdom must be our highest priorities and focus of our desires. When we orient our lives around God and his people, we pursue the agenda of his kingdom and we are motivated to live in ways that please him.\r\n3. Responsibility- Our loving allegiance to God should motivate us to seek out additional ways that we are responsible to him. When understanding that we are obligated to him in every area of our life, we are in a better position to make decisions that he approves.', 8, '2020-06-12 16:38:10', '2020-06-16 16:56:46', NULL),
(1590, 463, 859, '1. Atoning Grace- All God\'s actions are perfect expressions of his character. Scripture exhorts us to pattern our character and actions after God\'s. It teaches that we should love each other in imitation of the love that God has shown for us. The Scripture tells us to show the same kind of love for others that God showed to us in the atonement. \r\n2. Common Grace- God\'s kindness to those who will never be saved. Because we love God, we should also love the people he loves. It is easy not to have God\'s kind of love for our enemies, but we should have genuine concern for our enemies\' well being, love, pray, protect and provide for them.\r\nGod\'s love is complex. It includes both a desire for justice and hatred for evil.', 8, '2020-06-12 16:43:53', '2020-06-16 16:56:46', NULL),
(1591, 463, 860, 'My motivation to action comes from Christ and His word alone. As it says in Philippians 2.5-  Let this mind be in you which was also in Christ Jesus. Just like Christ\'s likeness and as His obedience, who took upon the form of servant, and was made in the likeness of men. Jesus Christ did the same, He obeyed God, left his heavenly abode and came down to earth for the sins of man. The same Christ\'s love is inside of us, which motivates us to go to every other villages, cities, hills and valleys, preach the good news of Gospel to every soul and reach the unreached. And because our heart is fully committed to Him and His word, we are obeying God and the outward obedience flows out.', 8, '2020-06-12 16:50:02', '2020-06-16 16:56:46', NULL),
(1592, 463, 861, 'As written in 2 Corinthians 5.17,\'\' If any man be in Christ, he is a new creature, old things are passed away, behold, all things have become new.\'\' The first when I came to this saving faith was in my teenage. In that age, even the smallest mistakes hurted my heart and would always try and keep a clean innocent conscience before  God, and would also maintain it the same way. In the course of life,the smallest mistakes are often neglected, yet Holy spirit works in our heart, and we reconcile with God in prayer and confessing our shortcomings and seek His Grace from God to lead a victorious and faithful Christian life. And always trying to keep a clean conscience with God and practice it in our daily life with others too.', 8, '2020-06-12 16:55:53', '2020-06-16 16:56:46', NULL),
(1593, 463, 862, 'The term imagination simply refers to our ability to form mental images of things that are beyond our experience. It may seem strange to think imagination as a way of acquiring ethical knowledge. But our imaginative abilities are vital to learning and thinking about God, the world and ourselves. First, a form of creativity. Second, the ways imagination enables us to think about subjects that exist in different periods of time. And third, how imagination allows us to think about things that are separated from us by physical distance. \r\n1. Creativity- Imagination is involved in everything that we make or create. It helps us to form and to recognize moral patterns and analogies.\r\n2. Time- Imagination can help us think about things that do not exist at the moment we are thinking about them. Without our ability to imagine the future, we would not be able to apply God\'s word to our lives. \r\n3. Distance- When people and things are so distant from us that they are not currently part of our experience, we have to use our imagination to think about them.', 9, '2020-06-12 17:06:41', '2020-06-16 16:56:46', NULL),
(1594, 463, 863, 'A. Reason- we evaluate the information we have received. Our intellect comes from God, and the Holy Spirit helps us use it rightly. It has an important role to play in our decision-making process. Reason is the capacity to make logical interferces and to judge logical consistency. \r\nB. Conscience- Every time sensory data is processed mentally, we are exercising reason to some degree. Scripture uses reason and it regularly calls on us to do the same. Conscience is the God given ability to discern good and evil. It can give true affirmation that our behavior is pleasing to God, rightly condemn us a guilty and encourage us to repent. \r\nC. Emotions- The solution to sin\'s corrupting influence is to rely on the power of the Holy Spirit who works within us as we strive to conform our conscience to God\'s word.', 9, '2020-06-12 17:16:01', '2020-06-16 16:56:46', NULL),
(1595, 463, 864, 'Will is the capacity for making decisions, volition and ability to make choices. Our will is affected by our fallen nature. For the Christian, the Holy Spirit enables us to make decisions that please God. Indwelling sin many persuade us to make sinful decisions. Our will maybe active or passive. It also functions in a passive, unconscious way when we respond by reflex. \r\nOur will is involved in each and everything we choose to think, say or do. It is the faculty we use to make every decision in our lives. We must will what God\'s Word commands and we must allow the Holy Spirit  working within us to influence our will in positive ways.', 9, '2020-06-12 17:20:48', '2020-06-16 16:56:46', NULL),
(1596, 463, 865, 'Our words are the commentaries on our wills, for when we speak we make, as it were a dissection of our own hearts. As it says in Proverbs 4.23-24- Keep thy heart with all diligence for out of it are the issues of life. The life and liveliness of faith is known by the good motives of the heart by the bestirring of all powers, both of the soul and body, and to do whatsoever God wills us to be doing, as soon as we once know He would have us to do it. The commitments of our own heart is greatly impacted on our works and speech. Out of the good treasure of his heart, a good man would bring forth, not harsh but kindness, gentleness, compassion filled works and out of  the evil treasure, the hypocrite  would only bring forth bitterness, and harsh surmises. Therefore, as it says in Psalms 19.14 let the words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart be acceptable in thy sight, we should pray that our life be pleasing and commitments be to God alone.', 9, '2020-06-12 17:31:16', '2020-06-16 16:56:46', NULL),
(1597, 464, 766, 'In Matthew 16:15-17 Peter says  to Jesus \"you are the Christ , the Son of the living God\".He confessed it as the spokesman for the apostles. It was an authoritative prophetic revelation from God and also infallible confirmation of the fact that JESUS really was the Christ.  \r\nPeter\'s apostolic confession confirmed that Jesus was the Christ.His affirmation of Jesus as the Christ was a direct revelation from God.\r\nTransfiguration \r\nIn this His appearance was radically transformed, revealing a portion of His divine glory. It is recorded in Mathew 17:1-8,Luke 9:28-36\r\nThe event when Jesus was revealed to His disciples in glory. Jesus took Peter , James sand John upon a mountain to pray.Moses and Elijah appeared with Jesus. God\'s voice was heard from heaven affirming that Jesus was His son. Jesus took in continuity with law and the Prophets. Jesus was the divine heir who was bringing God\'s kingdom to earth.', 8, '2020-06-13 18:15:55', '2020-06-16 16:57:36', NULL),
(1598, 464, 767, 'The temptation of Jesus temptation is recorded in Mathew 4:1-11 and Luke 4:1-13.Jesus Fasted for 40 days in the desert before being tempted by Satan. Jesus temptation by Satan paralleled the temptation of Adam and Eve. He overcame temptation to bring salvation to His people.   \r\nThree important purposes of His temptation are 1.\r\n1. Obedience-Jesus had to learn God\'s righteousness requirements and to overcome challenges and temptations.He obeyed God both by keeping the requirements of His Law and by submitting to the Father\'s plan for His life. Hebrews 5:9 says His obedience made him an acceptable sacrifice to God.\r\n2.Sympathy- Jesus grew in compassion and understanding for us, as we suffer and struggle with temptation.He felt it acutely, and then thing s that Satan offered him were desirable and His weakened condition from fasting must have amplified his longing for them. Hebrews 4:15 says that we  do not  have a high priest who is unable to sympathize with our weaknesses\r\n3. Impeccability-Jesus never sinned and He was not capable of sinning. Jesus is impeccable, His obedience and sympathy are increased.He never succumbed to temptation or had an evil thought or desire or said a sinful word. Hebrews 4:15, John 3:5', 9, '2020-06-13 18:33:25', '2020-06-16 16:57:36', NULL),
(1599, 464, 768, 'Jesus crucifixion is unique in following ways:\r\nCrucifixion was a form of the death penalty  used in the ancient Roman empire.Jesus crucifixion served as an anointing offering  for sin.\r\n1.Imputation -The act in which God assigned the guilt of sinners to the person of Jesus. Jesus offered Himself n the cross as a substitute for his people.Our sin was reckoned to his account, God viewed him as being guilty of all sins that were assigned to him.\r\nBible refers to Him as our sacrifice Romans 3:25, Ephesians 5:2\r\n and he\'s also called our ransom Matthew 20:28, Hebrews 9:15\r\n2.Judgement:\r\nHuman death is always a divine judgement against sin.Jesus \'s death was divine judgement against sin. Befor God laid our guilt on Him, Jesus couldn\'t die, But once our sin was imputed to him on the cross, his death became not only possible but necessary. Jesus remained under the power of death for three days before his resurrection,but the good news is that he has borne the full wrath of God against our sin, so that there isn\'t any divine judgement remaining to threaten us.John 5:24', 9, '2020-06-13 18:48:40', '2020-06-16 16:57:36', NULL),
(1600, 464, 769, 'Resurrection accomplished following things:\r\nGod \'s anointed Christ conquered death for all of us, when he rose from the grace through the power of the Spirit,and he ensured the future resurrection and the blessing of all his faithful followers.\r\n1.  Plan of Redemption:\r\nGod planned to redeem humanity and the rest of the creation depended on him fulfilling his covenant promises,but he could not do it if Jesus remained dead.His resurrection was an affirmation of His role as Christ. Luke 24:45,46\r\nRedemption depended on God fulfilling His covenant promise to establish his kingdom on earth.\r\nBlessing of salvation:\'\r\nBlessing we receive as part of our salvation are: \r\nJustification-which is the forgiveness of our sins Romans 4:25\r\nRegeneration of our spirits 1 Peter 1:3-5\r\neternal inheritance- it opens the door to our inheritance 1 Peter 1:3-5\r\nI produces good works and true witness and finally resurrection of believers.(2 Cor 4:10-18)', 8, '2020-06-13 19:02:51', '2020-06-16 16:57:36', NULL),
(1601, 464, 770, 'Jesus Christ is the most powerful .exciting person who has ever lived , what is more exciting is that he still lives today.He is our prophet, priest and king from his throne in heaven. And if we serve him faithfully, he assures us in his word that our blessings in the next world will be far beyond our greatest hopes. \r\nAs a minister of God , I face many challenges ,but Jesus has been my help and Christ and helped me overcome all tough circumstances.\r\nJesus is our great hope , and he will grant us the blessings of his kingdom. The vision of the future motivates me to serve God with a sense of urgency as we proclaim his gospel to the lost.\r\nThe return of Christ is the central affirmation OF Our Christian faith.\r\nAs in ministry , I face challenges from the enemy satan, Jesus governs all things and we know that the Bible assures us that because of Christ\'s rule over all,we have nothing to fear, our victory is sure. Nothing can happen to us that is beyond his control and authority. \r\nEven in our temptations since He is the Christ , HE is able to help us overcome those things.\r\nSo we affirm he is our Christ in all circumstances.', 9, '2020-06-13 19:21:52', '2020-06-16 16:57:36', NULL),
(1602, 469, 722, 'उत्तर = जब भी हम किसी पुस्तक या  किसी अन्य लेकर का अध्ययन करते हैं तो इसके लेकिन के बारे में जानना अति सहायक होता है क्योंकि जितना अधिक आम लेखक और उसके संदर्भ के बारे में जानेंगे उतना ही अधिक उसकी दृष्टिकोण तथा उसके लेखक के बारे में समझेंगे और बाइबल अध्ययन में भी यही बात बताई जाती है जितना अधिक हम बाइबल के लेखक के बारे में जानेंगे उतना ही अधिक हम उन बातों को सीखे सकेंगे जो वह हमें सिखाते हैं अच्छा जब हम मत्ती रचित समाचार को देखते हैं तो सबसे पहला प्रश्न जो हम पूछना चाहते हैं वह यहां है इस पुस्तक को किसने लिखा हम मत्ती रचित सुसमाचार के लेखक का दो चरणों में अध्ययन करेंगे पहला हम इसका पारंपरिक विचारधारा की पुष्टि करेंगे कि इस पुस्तक को प्रेरित मत्ती ने लिखा था जो यीशु की आरंभिक 12 जिलों में से एक था दूसरा हम मती के व्यक्तिगत इतिहास को देखेंगे आइए हम परंपरागत विचारधारा से आरंभ करें कि मत्ती ने इसे लिखा है|\r\n1) परंपरागत दृष्टिकोण = मैं सोचता हूं कि हम इस बात के प्रति काफी आश्वस्त हो सकते हैं कि मती अर्थात तेरी मती वास्तव में मति रचित सुसमाचार का लेखक है यदि कुछ विद्वान इस पर संदेह व्यक्त करते हैं इस एक बात हम जानते हैं कि प्राचीन कली से आई पितृत्व बहुत संदेह वादी थे बल्कि इस पर अपनी राय कम ही व्यक्त करते थे कि धोखाधड़ी से की गई कार्य को धर्म वैधानिक कार्य परमेश्वर के प्रेरणा स्रोत से लिखे गए वचन के रूप से मान्यता दैनिक से बिल्कुल इनकार करते थे दूसरी बात यह है कि मती कारज मत्ती रचित सुसमाचार के लेखक होने के विषय में कोई दूसरी परंपरा भी नहीं है केवल एक ही आधिकारिक परंपरा यह है कि मती ही ने इस पुस्तक को लिखा है तीसरी बात यदि आरंभिक कलीसिया किसी अन्य व्यक्ति का नाम ऐतिहासिक तथ्यों को छोड़कर किसी अन्य कारणों से केवल नाम के लिए या किसी प्रेरित को इस पुस्तक से जोड़ते और उन्होंने मती के नाम का चुनाव करके बड़ा ही गलत निर्णय लिया इसका  कारण यह है कि मती एक चुंगी लेने वाला था उसके व्यवसाय से यहूदी अत्यंत गुणा करते थे और मति का सुसमाचार ऐसा सुसमाचार है जो योगियों को यह बताने के लिए लिखा गया था यीशु मसीह है तो ऐसी स्थिति में क्या वे मति को इस सुसमाचार का लेखक मानते इसका कोई अर्थ दिखाई नहीं देता यदि फिर भी वह मती का नाम इस समाचार से जोड़ते हैं \r\nपरंपरा दृष्टिकोण  किमती ही ने पहले सुसमाचार को लिखा है यह कलीसिया के आरंभिक सदियों से आती है शीर्षक के साथ पाए जाने वाले इस समाचार के सभी खस्ता लिखो मैं मति और केवल मतीको लेखक के रूप में दिखाया गया है हमारे पास ऐसा कोई परिणाम नहीं है कि यह सुसमाचार कभी भी मती के नाम के बिना अलीशा में प्रसारित किया गया हो सबसे पहले हीरा पुलिस के पापिया स्नेह इस पुस्तक के लिखने का श्रीमती को दिया था पपिया का जीवनकाल पहली सदी के अंत से लेकर दूसरी सदी तक धावक अलीशा के आरंभिक समय के दृष्टिकोण का प्रतिनिधित्व करता है जिनके विषय में हमारे पास जानकारी उपलब्ध है कलीसिया के इतिहासकार केसरी  यूसीबीएस जिसने 325 ईसवी में लेखक कार्य किया ने अपनी पुस्तक  ैक्लेसियस्टिकल हिस्ट्री पुस्तक 3 से 29 खंड 16 में मति रचित सुसमाचार के लेखक के विषय में अभ्यास की गवाही को दर्शाया यहां हम देखते हैं कि पापिया स्नेह दूसरी सदी के आरंभ में इस समाचार का लेखक मति को दर्शाया यह भी ध्यान देने योग्य बात है कि यूसीबीएस ने इसलिए पापिया स्कोर ध्वस्त किया क्योंकि वह स्वयं इस बात को दर्शाना चाहता था कि मति ने इस पुस्तक को लिखा था अलीशा के एक अन्य पितृत्व क्यों शेयर एनी केस ने भी जिसने 180 ईसवी के दौरान लेखक कार्य किया मति को ही इस समाचार के लेखक के रूप में दर्शाया अग्रेस्टे रोसियस पुस्तक संख्या 3 से 1 खंड 1 में क्या लिखा है जब पतरस और पोलीस रोम में सुसमाचार प्रचार कर रहे थे और कलीसिया की स्थापना की नींव रख रहे थे तो मदीने भीम रानियों के मध्य उनके बोली में एक लिखित सुसमाचार प्रसारित किया कुछ समय पश्चात टटू लियोन का जीवनकाल 155 से 230 ईसवी के बीच था उसने भी अपनी पुस्तक अट ए  अग्रेट मार्सियन पुस्तक चार अध्याय 2 में मति के लेखक होने की पुष्टि की  तेरी तो मैं यूं ना और मदीने हमारे अंदर विश्वास जगाया ग्लूका और मंच उसने बाद में इसका नवीकरण किया जहां तक अरे नियत और टर्टुलियन का सवाल है उनके अनुसार  मति ने यह सुसमाचार लिखा उनकी इसी बात को आरंभिक अलीशा द्वारा स्वीकार किया गया मध्य द्वारा पहले सुसमाचार को लिखे जाने के लिए छत के साथ स्वीकार किया गया इस बात को महसूस करना भी महत्वपूर्ण है कि मत्ती के लेखक होने का आरंभिक दवे मस्ती के ज्यादा प्रभावशाली ना होने के कारण भी मजबूती प्राप्त करते हैं यदि कलीसिया या कोई और अपनी पसंद के किसी चेले के साथ उसे समाचार का नाम जोड़कर उसे विश्वान इयत्ता प्रदान करना चाहता था तो उन्होंने शायद किसी अन्य अधिक प्रभावशाली चेले को चुना होता परंतु मति का उल्लेख सुसमाचार में बहुत ही कम पाया जाता है ऐसा होना संभव नहीं है कि सुसमाचार के साथ उसका गलत रूप से जोड़ दिया गया हो|\r\nसबसे पहले हमें पहली सदी के प्रशांत गवाहों के महत्व को समझना है रोशन गवाहों की गवाही को बड़ा ही महत्व दिया जाता था और इन गवाहों की गवाही को हल्के में नहीं लिया जाता था वह यह होने वाली घटनाओं की बातों को पुत्र रूप में बताए जाने के समान था हम यह भी जानते हैं कि दूसरी सदी के आरंभ में प्रयास ने लिखा था किमती रचित सुसमाचार को प्रेरित मत्ती ने ही लिखा था और पापिया स्नेह अपने जीवन काल में नीचे ही पीड़ितों को व्यक्तिगत रूप से जाना होगा इस सुसमाचार के मध्य द्वारा लिखे जाने के प्रति आश्वस्त होने के का एक अंतिम कारण मैं यह कहना चाहता हूं कि यद्यपि मती का नाम मत्ती रचित सुसमाचार के लेखक में नहीं पाया जाता फिर भी सच्चाई यह है कि आरंभ से ही इसके लेखक और अधिकार के रूप में मति का सुसमाचार बिना उसके नाम के प्रसारित नहीं किया गया होगा नी संदेश आधुनिक समालोचक विद्वानों ने इस बात पर संदेह व्यक्त किया है कि पीड़ित मत्ती ने इस सुसमाचार को लिखा था ठीक वैसे ही जैसे उन्होंने बाइबल के लेखकों के बारे में अन्य अनेक परंपराओं पर संदेह व्यक्त किया है परंतु मती के इस समाचार के लेखक होने के बारे में संपूर्ण प्राचीन प्रमाण और इसके विरुद्ध किसी चुनौती के ना होने से हम इस बात पर पूरी तरह से विश्वास कर सकते हैं कि उसी ने इस पुस्तक को लिखा है हमने यहां पर इस परंपरागत दृष्टिकोण को देख लिया है|\r\n2) व्यक्तिगत इतिहास = पवित्र शास्त्र हमें मती के व्यक्तिगत इतिहास के बारे में कुछ महत्वपूर्ण बातों को बताता है उदाहरण के तौर पर यहां हमें बताता है कि वह एक यदि एक जोगी लेने वाला का हम इन दोनों का विस्तृत विश्लेषण करेंगे और इस बात से आरंभ करेंगे कि मती एक यहूदी था मत्ती की एक वंश बनी कई प्रकार से प्रकट की गई है एक बात तो यह है कि वह यीशु के 12 जिलों में से एक था और सभी चैले यहूदी थे दूसरी बात यह है कि मती के यहूदी नाम थे मस्ती भी एक यहूदी है जिसे इब्रानी पुरानी नियम से लिया गया था उसका दूसरा नाम लेवी जो हम मरकुश 2:14 और लुक्का5:28 मैं पाते हैं इजराइल के 12 गोत्र में से एक गोत्र का नाम था तथा यह दोनों नाम हमें यह बताते हैं कि मति एक यहूदी था मत्ती यहूदी वंशी वाली को प्राचीन मसीही लेखकों द्वारा इस बात से भी प्रमाणित किया जा सकता है कि उसने इब्रानी भाषा में लिखा था मत्ती के सुसमाचार को हम समझने के लिए मत्ती की अवधि परंपरा एक महत्वपूर्ण पृष्ठभूमि है क्योंकि यहां हमें विशिष्ट यहूदी महत्व को समझने के लिए सहायता करती है इस समाचार के यहूदी चरित्र का विस्तृत अध्ययन हम इस अध्ययन में बाद में करेंगे अथवा केवल स्पष्टीकरण के लिए हम एक ही उदाहरण का उल्लेख करेंगे दूसरे सु समाचारों से बढ़कर मत्ती ने इस बात पर जोर दिया कि यीशु केवल इस्राएल के लिए आया था मत्ती की यहूदी परंपरा के अतिरिक्त उसके जीवन का एक और अध्ययन देखें देने  योग्य वर्णन यहां है कि वह एक चुंगी लेने वाला था पहला सदी में फिलिप्स के आने की अवधि रोमी साम्राज्य के लिए चुंगी लिया करते थे इनमें से कुछ चुंगी लेने वाले एक स्थान से दूसरे स्थान पर ले जाकर जाने वाले समान पर चुंगी लिया करते थे वे निजी व्यवसाय थे जो चुंगी लेने के लिए शासकों को यहां अधिकार देने के लिए धन दिया करते थे वे लोगों से तय रकम से अधिक धन वसूलते थे जिससे वे अपना मुनाफा कमाते थे फल चुंगी लेने वाले लोगों के दृष्टि में लूटपाट मचाने वाले चोर ठहरते थे और इस प्रवृत्ति को उचित ठहराया जाता था इस कारण यहूदी चुंगी लेने वाले अपने देशवासियों के दृष्टि में दोहरे दोषी तैरते थे पहला व गणित कब्जा जमाने वाली रोमी ताकतों के प्रतिनिधि थे और दूसरा अपने ही लोगों को अपनी निज कमाई के लिए लूटते थे वे इतने घने समझे जाते थे के पुराने रवि ओके लेखक के अनुसार उन्हें यहूदी न्यायालय में गवाही देने के भी अनुमति नहीं थी इससे बढ़कर चुंगी लेने वालों में झूठ बोलने की अनुमति थी और इनकी न्याय संगत विरोध दरों के रूप में प्रशंसा की जाती थी\r\nअपने बारे में वर्णन करने में मत्ती बड़ा ही सच्चा था और उसने खुलेआम स्वीकार किया कि शुरू के दिनों में चुंगी लेने वाले पापियों की श्रेणी में रखे जाते थे ऐसा करके मत्ती ने अपने आपको यीशु को और अपने लिखित सुसमाचार को यहूदियों के विरोध में रख दिया उदाहरण के लिए देखी की सुने मत्ती21:31-32 मैं कैसे यहूदी अब्बू की आलोचना की अपने पाप में व्यक्तिगत इतिहास के बारे में खुलेआम बोलने की मति की इच्छा उसकी सुसमाचार के एक अन्य मतों से भी जुड़ा हो सकती है जिसका अध्ययन हम इस अध्याय में बाद में करेंगे दूसरे सुसमाचार लेखकों से बढ़कर नथी ने इस बात पर भी  अधिक जोर दिया की यीशु एक विनम्र राजा था|', 9, '2020-06-20 14:57:51', '2020-06-23 20:31:34', NULL),
(1603, 469, 723, 'उत्तर   = मत्ती रचित सुसमाचार का परिचय हमें मसीहा राजा के रूप में यीशु का परिचय देता है और यहां दो भागों में विभाजित है वंशावली व यीशु के जन्म की कहानी|\r\n1)	 वंशावली -:\r\nवंशावली मती1:1-17 मैं पाई जाती है तकनीकी रूप से पहला पद वास्तव में एक परिचय या शीर्षक है जिसमें मत्ती ने अपने मुख्य बात को बताया है अर्थात यहां की सो इजरायल का मसीहा राजा है आराम से ही मती ने इजरायल के राजा दाऊद और यहूदी लोगों की पिता अब्राहिम पर विशेष बल दिया है इस आरंभिक कथन के बाद दूसरे पद से ही वंशावली आरंभ होती है मती1:17 के अनुसार वंशावली तीन खंडों में विभाजित की गई है प्रत्येक खंड में 14 वर्ष है पहला खंड अब्राहम के साथ परमेश्वर की वाचा से आरंभ होता है जिनमें अब्राहम के साथ या वाचा बांधी गए कि उसके वंश संसार पर राज्य करेगा दूसरा खंड राजा दाऊद के साथ और दाऊद के राज्य को सर्वदा तक स्थापित  करने के द्वारा अब्राहम से ही की गई परमेश्वर की वाचा को पूरा करने की प्रतिज्ञा के साथ आरंभ होता है दूसरा करण परमेश्वर की लोगों के अपने पापों के कारण तथा वाचन तोड़ने के कारण प्रतिज्ञा की भूमि से बनवाएं में चले जाने के साथ समाप्त होता है वंशावली के तीसरे खंड में बनवाई से यीशु के जन्म का वर्णन पाया जाता है इस्राइल ने परमेश्वर की भाषा को तोड़ा और इस वाचक के सांपों के अधीन हो गए परंतु परमेश्वर फिर भी इसराइल प्रोग्राम और दाऊद से की गई वादों को पूरा करने के द्वारा आशीष देना चाहता था इजरायल के पूर्व काल के राजाओं ने इस भाषाओं का पालन नहीं किया था परंतु अब इजरायल का अंतिम राजा जो इसराइल के वासियों को निर्धारित करेगा अर्थात आ गया था इस प्रकार मत्ती ने यह प्रमाणित कर दिया कि यीशु के पास आए अपने पिता यूसुफ के द्वारा दाऊद के सिंहासन का वैज्ञानिक अधिकार था\r\nभविष्यवाणी के प्रकाशन के अनुसार मासी को दावत के वंश का होना चाहिए क्योंकि ऐसा ही भविष्यवाणी की गई थी और इसकी पृष्ठभूमि उत्पत्ति के पुस्तक में पाई जाती है जहां पर यह उदा के गोत्र के लिए भविष्यवाणी की गई थी कि उसमें राजा निकलेगा वहां भविष्यवाणी दावत पर पूरी होती है राजा बाबू जो अपने आप में इजराइल का एक महानतम राजा था उसके बाद जितने भी राजा आए उनकी तुलना राजा दाऊद के अनुकूल या प्रतिकूल से ही की जाती रही फिर हम जानते हैं कि दाऊद के साथ जो भाषा बांधी गई थी जब उन्हें नबी से दावत ने प्रमोशन के लिए मंदिर बनाने की इच्छा बताई जाए तो नेता ने वापस आकर कहां तू यह हुआ के लिए घर बनाएगा  क्या हुआ तेरे लिए घर बनाएगा यहां घर तत्पर्य उसके वंश से यहां है या दूसरा समय के साथ में पाया जाता है वह भविष्यवाणी कि यह हुआ कि उसके लिए एक घर बनाएगा उसका राज्य सर्वदा स्तर रहेगा कि उसका वंश सर्वदा दावत के सिंहासन पर राज करेगा मसीही की भविष्यवाणी की न्यू टेहरी जो कालांतर में पूरी होगी और जब अवस्थाओं ने दाऊद के वंश और उसके राज्य के विघटन की ओर इशारा किया और उस आशा की और आगे देखा कि परमेश्वर दावत के राज्य की महिमा को पुनः स्थापित करेगा तो दाऊद की वजह से ही परमेश्वर एक राजा को खड़ा करेगा इसलिए राजा अर्थात मर्सिया को दाऊद की वजह से ही आना था\r\n यीशु की वंशावली के पछता हम उसके जन्म की कहानी को पाते हैं।\r\n2) यीशु के जन्म का विवरण -:\r\n यीशु के जन्म की कहानी मती1:18-2:23 मैं पाई जाती है यहां एक साप्ताहिक भाग इसमें केवल 31 पद है जबकि लुका रचित सुसमाचार की इस अनुभव में 116 पर पाए जाते हैं इस अनुभाग में मत्ती का उद्देश्य सिमित था सभी पांचों अनुच्छेद की रचना एक महत्वपूर्ण विषय पर ध्यान देने के लिए की गई थी यीशु अर्थात मसीहा का जन्म हो चुका प्रत्येक अनुच्छेद 1 सप्ताह एक कहानी बताता है और इसे स्पष्ट करता है कि वह का ने किस प्रकार मसीहा के लिए पुराने नियम की भविष्यवाणी को पूरा करती है यीशु के जन्म का विवरण के बारे में सबसे रुचिकर बात यह सिखाते है कि उसका कोई मानवीय पिता नहीं था बल्कि परमेश्वर ही उसका पिता था पवित्र आत्मा के द्वारा मरियम गर्भवती हुई जबकि वह कुमारी ही था मसीही गीत के कुछ आलोचना को का मानना है कि इस यह यीशु की बंसवाली की कमजोरी है क्योंकि वहां शारीरिक रूप से यूसुफ की वंशिका नहीं था जिसके द्वारा उसके दाऊद की सिंहासन का उत्तराधिकारी होने का दावा किया जाता परंतु यहां तो स्वीकृत परंपरा है कि बाइबल की वंशावली जैसे एक इतिहास एक कानों में वर्णित है जो गोद लिए गए संतानों की वंशावली भी गोद लेने वाले माता-पिता की वंशावली से जुड़ी जाती है इससे बढ़कर यीशु परमेश्वर का पुत्र था यह संपूर्ण ईश्वरीय था इसका अर्थ था कि वह परमेश्वर की भाषा का शब्द रूप से पालन कर सकता था केवल मानवीय राजाओं ने ही परमिशन की भाषा का शब्द रूप से पालन नहीं किया इसलिए उन्होंने कभी भी परमेश्वर की माता की आशीष जैन की प्रतिज्ञा अब्राहम तथा दावत से की गई थी का परंपरा भरपूर आनंद नहीं उठाया था परमेश्वर ने अपने सिद्ध पुत्र को राजा होने के लिए भेजा ताकि उसकी वाक्य शुद्ध रूप से पूरी की जा सके और उसकी आशीष की प्रतिज्ञा पूरी हो सके\r\nयह स्पष्ट है कि मसीहा मनुष्य के रूप में दाऊद के वंशज से ही आता है इस संबंध में कई महत्वपूर्ण सच्चाई है परंतु इस बात का अनुभव करना भी महत्वपूर्ण है कि मसीहा परमेश्वर अर्थात ईश्वर यदि है यह ऐसा क्यों है यह ऐसा इस कारण है कि मनुष्य होने के नाते हमारी समझ से परमेश्वर के सामने यह है कि हमने उसके विरुद्ध पाप किया है उसके इसका उत्तर प्रदान करना है उसी को ही इस समस्या का समाधान प्रदान करना है पाप क्षमा की समस्या जिनके बारे में हम कभी कभी बात करते हैं परमेश्वर उसको ऐसे ही अनोखा नहीं करता यह ऐसा नहीं है जिनके बारे में वह कहे मैं देख लूंगा यहां तुम अपना सर्वश्रेष्ठ प्रदर्शन करो परमेश्वर का उत्तर परमेश्वर है परमेश्वर धर्मी है और न्याय है वह हमारे पापों को ऐसा ही अनदेखा नहीं करेगा ऐसा करना तो मानो उसका आपने आशुतोष से इनकार करना है इसलिए हमें क्षमा प्रदान करने के लिए उसी को ही प्रारंभ करना है उसकी अपनी धार्मिक मांग की परिपूर्णता के लिए उसको ही समाधान उपलब्ध कराना है वह वास्तव में स्वयं परमेश्वर को यहां करना है जब आप पुराने नियम पढ़ते हैं तो यह बार-बार अपने आपके सम्मुख आता है आप योना 2 का 2 के बारे में सोचते हैं उधार या हुआ का है यह यह वह परमेश्वर को उपलब्ध कराना है परमेश्वर को ही यहां उपलब्ध कराना है परमेश्वर ही है जो हमें पाप क्षमा करेगा इसलिए यदि मसीहा के उद्धार द्वारा उद्धार हो तो उसी को ही मनुष्य बन कर हमारा प्रतिनिधित्व करना है इसके साथ-साथ उसको प्रभु भी होना है प्रभु जो आने वाला है प्रभु जो उधार देता है प्रभु जो अपनी पवित्रता और धार्मिकता को पूरा करता है और इसलिए मसीहा को ईश्वर यह होना आवश्यक है मति ने अपने सुसमाचार के परिचय में यीशु को मसीहा राजा के रूप में प्रस्तुत किया है अर्थात दाऊद का राज्य के जिन के उन सभासदों को प्राप्त किया जिनकी प्रतिज्ञा परमिशन अब्राहम तथा इस इजराइल के लोगों से की थी इस प्रकार मति ने उस अद्भुत शुभ संदेश के लिए मंच तैयार किया जो उसकी विशेष पुस्तक का विषय है।\r\n                                                                       \r\n                                                                             ( PRAISE THE LORD )', 9, '2020-06-20 15:13:56', '2020-06-23 20:31:34', NULL),
(1604, 469, 724, 'उत्तर = 1)चिन्ह और प्रतिक्रियाएं :-\r\n              मति का कहानी खंड यीशु द्वारा दिए गए चिन्न और उन तीनों के प्रति प्रतिक्रिया हैं वह पर केंद्रित है जो मती 11 अध्याय 25 से 12 अध्याय का 50 पद में पाया जाता है इन तीनों ने दर्शाया कि राजा और उसका राज्य वर्तमान में है और इस संबंध में जो छोटी शिक्षाएं प्रचलित थी उसे सुधारा फल स्वरुप जो आलोचना पहले से ही आरंभ हो चुकी थी वहां बढ़ने और फैलने लगी चिन्नू एवं दुष्ट आंतों की संख्या पांच मुख्य भागों में विभाजित है 11 अध्याय तो पद से 19 बदमाशों ने यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा देने वाले के आश्वासन दिया कि उसके यीशु के चिन्ह या प्रमाणित करते हैं कि वही मसीहा है जिसने पुराने नियम की भविष्यवाणियों को पूरा किया है और फिर यीशु ने भीड़ का को बुलाया फिर कि वे उसके चिन्हों का प्रयोग अपने पापों से पश्चताप करके मत्ती 1:10 ; 20 पद से 30 पद में ईश्वर ने उन शहरों को संबोधित किया जहां उसने चीन दिखाए थे और उसने आज आप उचित आप ही लोगों को चेतावनी दी और उनका विश्राम देने का प्रस्ताव किया जो उसके पास आएंगे जैसे कि मति 11 का 30 पद में कहता है 12 अध्याय का एकवचन से 21 पद्मावती ने ऐसे कई वृत्तियों को आरंभ किया जो यीशु के चिन्हों के प्रति परियों की प्रतिक्रियाओं पर केंद्रित है सबसे पहले उसने बताया कि किस प्रकार विश्व में शब्द के लिए परमेश्वर के उद्देश्य के विषय में परियों से वाद-विवाद किया और एक व्यक्ति को शब्द के दिन चला कर के शब्द के ऊपर अपने अधिकार को प्रमाणित किया यशवंत सिखाएं किस शब्द का दिन चलना है और जीवन को बचाने के लिए है 12 अध्याय का पद 22 से लेकर के 37 में परसों निशुल्क पर बाल भुज की शक्ति का प्रयोग करने का आरोप लगाया हालांकि भीड़ यीशु के चार प्रमुख को देखकर अचंभित हो गई थी उसे मसीहा के रूप में स्वीकार करने की अपेक्षित था व्यवस्था के शिक्षकों ने यह माना कि वह तो दुष्ट आत्मा से ग्रह स्थित है 12 अध्याय का उन 50 पद से 50 पद में फरिश्तों ने अपने पाखंड में ईश्वर से दूसरा चीन मांगा परंतु ईश्वर ने उन्हें कहा कि योजना के चिन्ह को छोड़कर उन्हें कोई दूसरा चीज नहीं दिया जाएगा और यह चीन क्या था जिस प्रकार योना 3 दिन पछता मछली के पेट में से  निकलने के कारण निर्णय के लोगों ने मन फिर आया उसी प्रकार 3 दिन में पछताना कब्र में से यीशु का प्रभाव बहावी पूर्ण थान भी अन्य जाति के अनेक लोगों को मंत्रों की ओर प्रेरित करेगा यह दिखाने के लिए कि कोई भी जाति गोत्र भाषा के लोग जो पश्चाताप करेंगे परमेश्वर उनको स्वीकार करेगा उसने यह कहां तक कह दिया कि उसकी शारीरिक यहूदी माता और भाई भी उनके परिवार के लोग नहीं है इसके विषय में उसने मत्ती 12 अध्याय का उन 50 पद से 50 पद में यह कहा है यहां पर हम यीशु पर ईश्वर द्वारा दिखाए गए चिन्हों के मती के वर्णन को देख चुके हैं इसलिए आइए अब हम मति 13 अध्याय का एक पद से तेज 53 पद में यीशु के राज्य के दृष्टांत ओके उसके उद्देश्य की ओर मुड़े\r\n2) राज्य के दृष्टांत:-\r\n मतीन यीशु के जाने पहचाने दृष्टांत को 5 भागों में विभाजित किया है मत्ती 13:1-23 मैं बीज बोने वाले का दृष्टांत अध्याय 13 और उसका 24 पद से लेकर 30 पद में जंगली बीच का दृष्टांत 13 अध्याय का 31 पद से 43 पद में राई का दाना और खमीर 13 अध्यक्ष पद से 40 पद में छुपा हुआ धन और मोती तेरा अध्यक्ष ने ताली से 53 पद में जल का दृष्टांत यह दृष्टि परमेश्वर के राज्य के विषय में फेल फेल ही गलत धारणाओं को दूर करने के लिए कहे गए थे कुछ दृष्टांत तो जैसे तेरा अध्याय का 315 से 320 राई के दाने के 33 में खमीर के 44 में धन की ओर बहता लिस्ट 46 में मोती के दृष्टांत में ईश्वर या शिक्षा दी कि स्वर्ग का राज्य अत्यंत बहुमूल्य है इसलिए इसे किसी भी कीमत पर प्राप्त कर लेना चाहिए एक बार शायद यह महत्व लगे परंतु एक दिन यह अपनी संपूर्ण महिमा में प्रभात होगा परंतु यह सुने अत्यंत दृष्टांत भी कहे जिनमें राजा यीशु और उसके राज्य को स्वीकार करने में इजरायल के असफलता का दिखाया गया मती 13 अध्याय का एक पद सहित पद में बीज बोने वाले के दृष्टांत और उसके विवरण में विश्व ने स्पष्ट किया कि विश्वास में कई बाधाएं है और अधिकांश लोग राज्य का तिरस्कार कर देंगे इस विचार पर 24 पद से 30 पद और 36 से 43 वर्ड में जंगली बीच के दाने की दृष्टांत और 4791 जल के दृष्टांत में अधिक बल दिया गया इशू ने दिखाया कि बहुत से लोग परमेश्वर के राज्य को अपनाने से इनकार करेंगे और अंत में उनका नाश हो जाएगा यह सभी दृष्टांत यीशु के विरोधियों के लिए स्पष्ट चेतावनी थे हिंदुस्तान तो ने अविश्वास इयों को पश्चाताप करने का और एक सच्चे राजा के विश्वास योग्य अनुयाई बनने का अवसर प्रदान किया मसीहा आ गया उसने बॉस मारियो को पूरा किया है उसने अपने राज्य को स्थापित किया है फिर भी इसकी पूर्णता अभी बाकी है हम मसीही राजा जब प्रवेश करते हैं तो हमें अपनी प्राथमिकता को निरंतर रखने की आवश्यकता है यदि हमने जैसा उसका अनुकरण करना चाहिए था भाई साहब करण नहीं किया तो पछता आप करने की आवश्यकता है इस तथ्य को निश्चित करते हुए कि हम अपने जीवन को उसकी इच्छा अनुसार जीते हैं उसके नैतिकता के साथ सहमति प्रकट करते हैं जिससे राज्य संबंधित है इसलिए निरंतर पश्चताप अंगीकार करने की आवश्यकता है उसके समूह के के बहुत दुख था एक ही आज एक और एक राजा के रूप में आने की आवश्यकता है जिसका हम आदर्श मानकर अनुसरण करना चाहते हैं और उसकी सेवा ऐसे करें कि उसके उद्देश्य को अपने जीवन के द्वारा इस संसार में पूरा करें हमें मछलियों को परमेश्वर के राज्य का अनुसरण करने और उसकी इच्छा रखने के लिए प्रोत्साहित करने की आवश्यकता है पहला हम अपने व्यक्तिगत में स्वर्गीय के राज्य का अधिकार हमारे जीवन की सामर्थ है या हमारे अपने आपको परमेश्वर के हाथों में समर्पित करने के लिए प्रोत्साहित करता है|\r\nकि हम परमेश्वर पर केंद्रित जीवन जिए ताकि परमेश्वर का अधिकार जो हमारे जीवन में प्रकट होता है हमारे आत्मिक जीवन का सदैव बन जाए दूसरा हमें स्वर्ग के राज्य के उद्धार के इतिहास के दृष्टिकोण से भी देखने की आवश्यकता है जब हम यह जानते लगते हैं तो यह उसकी उधार की योजना को खोलता है पूरा करता है तब हम यहां भी देखेंगे किशोर की कि राज्य की शिक्षा पुराने और नए नियम को एक सूत्र के संबंधित है वहां हमारे छुड़ाने वाले परमेश्वर के उद्धार के महान योजना से परिचित कराता है और तब हम उसके उद्देश्यों का समझ पाते तीसरा स्वर्गराज्य बाइबल के उचित दृष्टिकोण का निर्माण करता है और हमें इस बात को समझने में सहायता करता है की सभी चीजें उसी की है उसके राज्य की पूर्णता होगी और वह इस धरती पर की सभी बुरी शक्तियों का न्याय करेगा और उसको धरती पर से मिटा डालने का क्योंकि परमेश्वर स्वयं सर्वशक्ति महाराजा होगा इसलिए अब हम केवल अपने ही नहीं जीते हमें अपने पड़ोसियों समाज और इस संसार की खुशहाली के लिए चिंता करने की आवश्यकता है हमारी कर्तव्य के रूप में समाज में प्रवेश करता है और वहां भी इन सभी बुरी बातों को बदलना है|\r\n                                                                     \r\n                                                                                 ( PRAISE THE LORD )', 8, '2020-06-20 15:29:20', '2020-06-23 20:31:34', NULL);
