(1605, 469, 725, 'उत्तर = 1)प्रचंड विरोध-:\r\n यह अध्याय यीशु के आगे बढ़ने के आधार पर तीन भागों में बठते हैं 19:1-20:16 मैं यीशु को यहूदियों में विरोध का सामना करना पड़ा  वहां उसने फ्री सी यू का और तलाक संबंधी प्रश्न का सामना किया उसने उस विरोध का भी सामना किया जो धन तथा सामर्थ्य के संबंध में गलतफहमी यों के कारण उठा सुसमाचार के प्रारंभिक अध्याय में मशीनें ईश्वर योग्य वह के मध्य दूरी यात्राओं का वर्णन किया है इस खंड में उसने यह लिखा है कि दोनों के मध्य शत्रुता विकसित हो गई थी उदाहरण के तौर पर ऋषि यों ने यीशु से ऐसे प्रश्न पूछना आरंभ किया कि यीशु को फसा सके और जैसा कि मती 19:3-9,21:16,23और 22:15-40 मै  इसके साथ-साथ ही सुने कभी-कभी यह नियमों को चुनौती दी इससे हम बत्ती 2:10-28 पद से 22 अध्यक्ष 15 पद में 2 पुत्र दृष्टांत किसानों और विवाह के भोज के दृश्य में पाते हैं परंतु झगड़ा सदैव शब्द तक ही सीमित नहीं था कभी-कभी तो यहां सीधा था तथा अधिक भयंकर होता था जैसे कीमत थी 21 अध्याय 12 :25 -16 पद में शनि मंदिर में लेनदेन करने वालों के मैच तक पलट दिए थे और उसने उन्हें मंदिर के से बाहर भगा दिया था विशेषकर मति 13:2-31 13:5-35 को हाय के शब्द सात सुरों के शब्द बहुत चुभने वाले थे निसंदेह इन अध्ययन के चरित्र केवल इस और यहूदी अब वो ही नहीं है यदि अब वह की शत्रुता उस समय और अधिक बढ़ गए गई जब भीड़ ने मती 21 अध्याय 1 पद से 11 पद में यीशु को विजय प्रवेश जैसे अवसरों पर आदर और सम्मान दिया इस पूरे खंड में यीशु ने अपने शिष्यों को इस विरोध को दृष्टिकोण में बदलने को उत्साहित किया मत्ती 19 अध्याय का 27:5-30 में यीशु ने उन्हें यह आश्वासन दिया कि एक दिन वह भी उसकी महिमा में उसके साथ बैठेंगे परंतु उसने उन्हें यहां चेतावनी भी दी कि महिमा के वे दिन दुख उठाने वाली उसकी मृत्यु के बाद ही आएंगे मत्ती 20 अध्याय का 19 पद इससे बढ़कर यीशु ने यह भी कहा कि उसके शिष्य दुख उठाने के नम्र जीवन के बाद भी उस महिमा तक पहुंचेंगे मत्ती 19 अध्याय 30 पद में यीशु ने कहा यीशु का राज्य विचित्र लगता था उसके अनुयाई दुख उठाएंगे और इजराइल का राजा स्वयं इस्राएली लोगों के द्वारा मारा जाएगा विजय से पहले अप्रिय जीत हार होगी प्रचंड विरोध का अगला खंड 20 सदस्य तरफ से 34 पद में यीशु के विशेष टीम की ओर जाने में है इस यहां स्पष्ट कर दिया था कि वह दुख सहने मरने जा रहा था उसे केवल दो चलो की माता का विरोध सहना पड़ेगा जो अपने बच्चों के लिए राज्य में अधिकार चाहती थी तब एक बड़ी भीड़ नजर उसने में यीशु का स्वागत किया जब उसने पुराने नियम की विजय प्रवेश की भविष्यवाणी को पूरा किया अगले भाग 21 1 अध्याय 12 पद 22 अध्याय का 40 पद में यीशु को विरोध का सामना करना पड़ा जब वह यरूशलेम और मंदिर में आ जा रहा था उसने लेनदेन करने वालों को बाहर निकाला उसने परमेश्वर की आने वाली न्याय के संबंध में दृष्टांत कहा यीशु और धर्मगुरुओं के मध्य कैंसर की कोचिंग इन देने मृतकों का पुनरुत्थान सबसे बड़ी आज्ञा और मसीहा किसका पुत्र है आदि विषयों पर विवाद हुआ परंतु ईश्वर ने अपने विरोधियों का इस तरह से सामना किया जैसा कि हम मत्ती 22 अध्याय का 40 पद में पढ़ते हैं स्वर्गीय के राज्य के प्रचंड विरोध पर आधारित मस्ती के वर्णन का अध्ययन करने के बाद अब हमें उन उद्देश्यों की ओर होना चाहिए जो इसके साथ पाए जाते हैं\r\n  2)भावी विजय-:\r\n यहां भागमती 23 अध्याय का 1 से 25 25 अध्याय का 40 पद में पड़ जाता है इस उपदेश में ईश्वर ने स्वर्ग के राज्य की भावी विजय का वर्णन किया यहां भागमती 23 अध्याय का एक पद से 38 पद में यीशु के विरोधियों के विरुद्ध उसके साथ हाय वचनों के साथ आरंभ होता है यह उपदेश विशेषकर परसों उनकी झूठी शिक्षा उनके द्वारा परमेश्वर के लोगों के दुरुपयोग और उनके कण पर केंद्रित है इस उद्देश्य के अंत में ईश्वर ने मती 23 अध्याय 37 पद से 38 पद में यरूशलेम की विषय में अपनी भावनाओं को इस प्रकार प्रकट किया मत्ती 23:37-38 यीशु के उपदेश के अगले भाग को हम जैतून के पहाड़ के उद्देश्य से जानते हैं और यहां मति 24 अध्याय का एकवचन से 25 से लेकर 40 पद में पाया जाता है इसे प्रिया जैतून पहाड़ के उद्देश्य से भी जाना जाता है क्योंकि इशू नया उपदेश अपने शिष्यों को जैतून के पहाड़ पर दिया था जैतून पहाड़ के उद्देश्य को हम तीन भागों में बांट सकते हैं मति 24 अध्याय का 4 पद से 28 पद में ईश्वर ने इस विभिन्न योग की उस प्रसव पीड़ा का वर्णन किया है जिसमें स्वर्ग का राज्य स्मृति पर आया परंतु यह अपनी पूर्ण महिमा और सामर्थ्य में अभी तक प्रगट नहीं हुआ है मती 24 अध्याय 29: 30 - 31 बाद में उसने राज्य की पूर्णता के विषय में बातें की और उस दिन के बारे में बताया जब मनुष्य का पुत्र बादल पर आएगा और स्वर्ग का राज्य अपनी पूर्ण महिमा और सामर्थ्य में प्रगट होगा तब मत्ती 24:29-31 मैं उसने राज्य की पूर्णता की विषय बातें की और उस दिन के बारे में बताया जब मनुष्य का पुत्र बादल पर आएगा और स्वर्ग का राज्य अपनी पूर्ण महिमा और सामर्थ्य में प्रगट होगा तब मती 24 अध्याय 32 पद से 25 अध्याय का 40 पद में उसने अपने लोगों को उत्साहित किया कि वह उस महिमा के दिन की उत्सुकता से प्रतीक्षा करें क्योंकि कोई नहीं जानता कि वह कब आएगा;\r\nयीशु ने अपने पुनरागमन के बारे में बताया तो वहां चाहता था कि हम इस बारे में आवश्यकता से अधिक ना सोचे कि वह किस समय आएगा उसने कहा कि उसके आने की घड़ी कि वह समय के विषय में कोई भी नहीं जानता यहां तक कि इस मानवीय शरीर में होते हुए उसको भी अपने पुनरागमन के समय के बारे में नहीं पता था इसलिए हमारे लिए भी उस समय को पहचानने का प्रयास करना तथा किसी विशेष समय को निर्धारित करना उसकी आज्ञा हो कि अवमानना करना है इसका तात्पर्य यह नहीं है कि हम उस दिन की प्रतीक्षा ना करें ऐसा ना कर के यहां उसके पुनरागमन के चिन्ह देकर नए नियम में मसीह के पुनरागमन की शिक्षा का उद्देश्य यह है कि वह हमें नम्र के हमें उत्साहित करें हमें आशा दे पवित्र जीवन जीने के लिए प्रेरित करें और हम मसीह के पूर्ण आगमन की प्रतीक्षा में लगे रहे और इसलिए यद्यपि हम उस समय को नहीं जानते हैं फिर भी हमें तैयार रहना चाहिए कि वह कभी भी आ सकता है ताकि हम उत्सुकता पूर्वक और आनंद के साथ उससे मिले सके हमें पूर्ण आश्वासन होना चाहिए कि वह वापस आएगा हमें इस बात का भी पूर्ण आश्वासन होना चाहिए कि वह पूना आ रहा है और जो कुछ उसने आरंभ किया है वहां उसे पूरा करेगा हमें विश्वास योग्य भी होना चाहिए हमें ऐसा नहीं होना चाहिए यह से प्रेरित ओके काम एक में जब यीशु स्वर्ग को उठा लिया गया तो उसे ज़ोर की की ओर ताक रहे थे और तब स्वर्ग दूत ने उनसे कहा तुम सुरभि की और क्या ताक रहे हो तुम्हें तो सुसमाचार लेखक जगत के छोर तक जाना है वहां वापस आएगा लेकिन हम यीशु के महान उद्देश्य को लोगों तक पहुंचाने में व्यक्त होना चाहिए हमें अन्य जातियों में इस बात की घोषणा करने के द्वारा की राजा आ गया है अपने राजा की सेवा में लगे रहना चाहिए वह पूना आ रहा है पश्चताप करके सुसमाचार पर विश्वास करो हमें उनके चेला बनाना है जो राज्य में प्रवेश करते हैं और इस ऊपर विश्वास करते हैं हम उन्हें बढ़ाने में सहायता करें ताकि वे परमेश्वर की महिमा के लिए जिए या उसकी समानता में बदले हमें अपने जीवन के हादसे में परमेश्वर की महिमा के लिए जीना है और उसके आगमन की प्रतीक्षा करते साथ रहना है और कल ईशा के साथ मिलकर यही रहना है हे प्रभु यीशु सुसमाचार के इस पांचवें मुख्य खंड में मध्य ने वर्णन किया कि यहूदी अब वह क्यों ईशु का तिरस्कार किया और उसे मार डालने की योजना बनाई परंतु ईश्वर ने स्पष्ट किया कि इस संसार की सभी योजनाएं भविष्य में राज्य की विजय को नहीं रोक सकती इतिहास इस बात को प्रमाणित करता है कि वह सही था यहूदी अगुआ ने उसकी हत्या कर दी परंतु उसका राज्य सभी युवाओं में बढ़ता चला गया और एक दिन इतिहास इसके अंतिम भाग को भी सच्चा प्रमाणित करेगा यीशु बड़ी सामर्थ्य और महिमा में आएगा ताकि वह अपने राज्य को पूर्णता में स्थापित करें और अपने विश्वास क्योंकि लोगों को राज्य की सभी आशीशों से आश्रित करें|\r\n\r\n                                                                             (PRAISE THE LORD)', 9, '2020-06-20 15:45:59', '2020-06-23 20:31:34', NULL),
(1606, 469, 726, 'उत्तर  = हमें इसलिए परवाह करनी चाहिए कि यीशु मसीह ने पुराने नियम की जो भविष्यवाणियां थी जो वह चुने थी हमारे लिए पूरा किया कलवारी क्रूज के बलिदान के द्वारा परमेश्वर की पवित्र वचन बाइबल केगलातियो   किताब में लिखा है गला4:5 इस वचन के अनुसार परमेश्वर ने हमें पुराने नियम की व्यवस्था से हमें आजाद किया क्योंकि उस व्यवस्था हमारे जीवन मेंपाप को दर्शाते थे परमेश्वर ने हमारे लिए कल वादी कुरूस परिश्रम मशीन है बलिदान हो करके उस बाप की व्यवस्था से हमें आजाद किया अर्थात हमारे लिए उस वचन उन्होंने पूरा किया अब जो हमें नया नियम दिया गया है हम नए नियम के लोग होने के वजह से इस वचन नए नियम के वचनों के अनुसार हमारा जीवन को बनाना उसके अनुसार चलना हमारे कर्तव्य है और हमारा जीवन ऐसा ही होना चाहिए प्रभु यीशु मसीह का वचन हम पढ़ते हैं पुराने नियम में प्रभु यीशु मसीह के बारे में पुराने नियम में जो भविष्यवाणी की गई थी और जो पुरानी नियम में जो व्यवस्था ही थी जो मनुष्य हमें दिया गया था उस व्यवस्था को प्रभु यीशु मसीह ने पूरा किया कलवरी क्रूज के बलिदान के द्वारा आज से 2000 साल पहले और हमारे लिए प्रभु यीशु मसीह जो है हमारे पापों को क्षमा किया क्योंकि व्यवस्था भी एक थे जो मनुष्य जाति के ऊपर में पांच को लाते थे इस व्यवस्था को पूरा करने योग्य कोई भी ना था लेकिन यीशु मसीह ने हम मानव जाति के लिए कुछ व्यवस्था को पूरा किया और उसने उस पूरा करते हुए अपने आप को समर्पित किया और कलवरी क्रश पर बलिदान हो गया इसलिए हमें इंद्र में प्रभु यीशु मसीह का अनुसरण करते हुए उस पर विश्वास करते हुए हमें दिनों दिन प्रभु यीशु मसीह के नए नियम के अनुसार हमें आगे बढ़ना है प्रभु यीशु मसीह जल्दी हमें लेने आने वाला है|\r\n\r\n                                                                           ( PRAISE THE LORD )', 7, '2020-06-20 16:01:15', '2020-06-23 20:31:34', NULL),
(1607, 465, 826, 'Ethics in general is to study on moral right and wrong, the study of good and evil.\r\nIn terms of Christian Theology, ethics is viewed as a means of determining how do we receive blessings based on human acts and attitudes.\r\n\r\nWhile studying Christian ethics we need to study on 2 important aspects\r\nGod\'s Divine Nature\r\nGod\'s Divine Actions \r\n\r\nGod\'s Divine Nature\r\nGod is not accountable to any standards outside of himself, and that everything that accords with God is good and light. \r\n\r\nScripture says in 1 John verse 5, that God is light and that there is no darkness in him.\r\n\r\nLight is considered as a metaphor of God, it is a moral evaluation and darkness is equated with Sin & Lies\r\n\r\nDivine Actions\r\nGod shows his approval for what is right by bestowing blessings. Similary God shows hatred for what is wrong and evil by withholding blessings and pouring out curses\r\n\r\nIn the old testament scriptures, God instructs the Israelites to strictly obey the commandments, on doing so - they would be blessed !!\r\nDisobedience would invite God\'s wrath, including death and destruction', 0, '2020-06-24 15:17:30', '2020-06-24 15:17:30', NULL),
(1608, 465, 827, 'Unless a work or action is performed with right motive, it is not a work that God will reward with blessings. Two important things that we need to always consider through our actions and works are \r\n1) Faith \r\n2) Love\r\n\r\nFAITH \r\nFaith plays a very important role in our life, any work done without a purified heart of faith is considered to be sinful and it does not please God. This criteria of the right motive is closely associated with good Christian Ethics.\r\n\r\nWorks of Faith can only be demonstrated by the indwelling of the Holy Spirit, and our actions and works accordingly  will culminate in rewards and blessings from God. Our faith should be consistent with growth, as it is also the means of purification within believers, motivating to produce good works.\r\n\r\nFaith without works is dead - as it says in the book of James, \r\nThe kind of faith that purifies the heart, faith that saves, faith that motivates to good works. \r\n\r\nIn the book of Hebrews it says, Without faith it is impossible to please God. \r\n\r\nUnless we try to please God and see blessings, our works and actions should be based on faith. \r\n\r\nAlso everything that is done without faith is considered to be sin, as instructed by Apostle Paul in the book of Romans.\r\n\r\nLOVE :\r\nApostle Paul says in 1st Corinthians 13 - Paul taught that our works are unproductive if it is not motivated by love. \r\n\r\nLove plays an important role in our Christian life, all our works and even spiritual gifts, for results to be evident should be motivated by love. Everything else will not receive the approval from our God.\r\n\r\nWhen Jesus spoke about the greatest commandment, it begins with Love\r\n\r\nLove the Lord your God with all your heart, and with all your soul and with all your mind.\r\n\r\nLove is an aspect of every law God requires us to obey. Love is the standard that God has set for maknkind to follow, wheter it is loving God or neighbor.', 0, '2020-06-24 15:34:51', '2020-06-24 15:34:51', NULL),
(1609, 465, 828, 'The threefold criteria for good works described in this lesson are as follows :\r\n\r\nAll our works should be based on \r\n1) Proper Motive\r\n2) Proper Standard \r\n3) Proper Goal\r\n\r\nProper Motive\r\nAll our works should have proper motive and it should be governed by two strong pillars of Faith & Love. Everything that we do, all our works if not done by faith & love will not be merited as per God\'s standards. The basic criteria for all our works to have a proper motive is Faith and Love\r\n\r\nProper Standard\r\nAll our works and actions should be of proper standard \r\nWestminster Confession of Faith says, that all our works that God commands, but unless done in a right manner according to the Word, they are sinful.\r\nAll sin violates God\'s law.\r\nIn order for our works to be of of proper standard it has to be governed by 3 aspects\r\n\r\n1) Commands of Scripture\r\nAll the commands of Scripture are designed to guide us. \r\n2) All of Scripture \r\nProper standard requires submission to the whole bible. God\'s word as a whole is a criterion for good works. \r\n3) General Revelation\r\nGod\'s revelation in creation itself is part of his word, that is commonly called as general revelation is also a standard for good works.\r\n\r\nGood works must conform to \r\nGod\'s Word - as Revealed in the Law, In all of Scriptiure and in General Revelation of Creation.', 0, '2020-06-24 15:52:37', '2020-06-24 15:52:37', NULL),
(1610, 465, 829, 'Perspectives are Ethical judgment involving the application of God\'s Word to a situation by a person. \r\nThe three different perspective to be emplyed when approaching ethics\r\n1) Situational Perspective\r\n2) Normative Perspective \r\n3) Existential Perspective\r\n\r\n1) Situational Perspective\r\nThis type of perspective focuses on the end or the result of actions. Always asking questions like, what are the best means of achieving God\'s purposes ? It also incudes appeals to moral behavior based on prior examples and other morally good characters as mentioned in the Scripture. We are to apply the scripture in our situations and follow the lead given in the word of God.\r\n\r\n2) Normative Perspective\r\nRefers to the fact that God\'s word is the norm or standard for ethics. We are doing ethics from normative perspecitve when we look at the word of God for directives as to what is to be done.\r\n\r\n3) Existential Perspecitve\r\nWhen we approach ethics by asking questions that are specific to the people involved, we are doing ethics from an existential perspective. It focuses on the self in confrontation and interaction with God.', 0, '2020-06-24 16:08:40', '2020-06-24 16:08:40', NULL),
(1611, 465, 830, 'God has the ultimate perogative to determind whether any particular action, emotions and thoughts meet or transgress his moral requirements and he has the ultimate right and power to act on his determinations. \r\n\r\nWhen we consider the scripture in the Gospel of John chapter 5, it says that \r\nMy judgement is just, for I seek not to please myself but him who sent me. \r\n\r\nGod in himself is the highest court in the universe. He will make the ultimate determination of wheterher or not we have lived morally or immorally and all his judgements will be true. No one can challenge his authority.  No one can challenge God\'s absolute authority, as it also follows absolute power. \r\n\r\nAs the absolute judge of morality, God consistently applies the absolute moral standard of his character in every judgement. His judgements are perfect, exhibiting flawless insight and wisdom.', 0, '2020-06-24 16:19:08', '2020-06-24 16:19:08', NULL),
(1612, 465, 831, 'The three categories of revelation that are part of God\'s Word are as follows :\r\n1) Special Revelation \r\nSpecial revelation is made up of Scripture, prophecy, dreams and visions\r\nThe complexity of speical revelation is that it come in various forms. It involves God communicating with people in ways that transcend the normal ways of creation. \r\nIn some cases God appears visibly, whereas in some cases speaks audibly to groups or individuals. In other cases he speaks through an angel. God also provides special revelation to write down and recorded in Scripture.  These types of special revelation are very special as they represent the extraordinary or supernatural communication between God and man. \r\n\r\n2) General Revelation :\r\nGeneral Revelation is what happens in history, in the universe, weather, plants, animals and human beings\r\nIt speaks about the way creation and history tell us true things about God and his moral requirements, But due to the fall of Adam and Eve, and the fallen world, the General Revelation does not present us with a clear picture of God\'s character. But the Bible assures us that general revelation still speaks clearly enough to teach us true things about God.\r\n\r\n3) Existential Revelation \r\nGod reveals himself in and through persons has always been recognized as a part of general revelation. \r\nIt can be further divided into External and Internal aspects\r\nExternal includes the revelation through human beings, created in the image og God. Human beings reflect God;s glory and dignity. Our image reflects God\'s character. \r\n\r\nInternal : \r\nInternal types of existential revelation involves the Holy Spirit working within human beings to reveal truth about God. Divine gifts that form part of this revelation in enabling to grow spritiually.', 0, '2020-06-24 16:39:00', '2020-06-24 16:39:00', NULL),
(1613, 465, 832, 'When God created man in his own image , God had given Adam exercising authority. When Adam named the animals he was thinking and exercising the divinely delegated authority, whenever human beings think and judge in an exercisde we are reflective God\'s character.\r\n\r\nSimilary Jesus has also taught in the Scripture - where every matter may be established by the testimony of two or three witnesses.\r\n\r\nJesus supports their exercise of the authority that he has delegated the church.\r\n\r\nInternal Existential Revelation talks about the ways that the Holy Spirit works with human beings to reveal truth about God.\r\nTheologians consider 2 important topics\r\nIllumination & Inward leading of the Holy Spirit \r\n\r\nIllumination of the Holy Spirit, is a divine gift of understanding that God gives to believers and even to unbelievers. Whe Holy Spirit illuminates a person\'s mind the ability or knowledge of that person increases and he is able to grasp information that he previously lacked. \r\n\r\nInward Leading - is one of the most common ways in which Holy Spirit works within individuals to reveal truth about God\'s character. We see inward leading displayed clearly in our individual consciences and as well in our feelings that God would provide us while taking a particular course of action. \r\n\r\nIn all these things God\'s character or standard is revealed unto us as we consistently study the scriptures.', 0, '2020-06-24 16:57:03', '2020-06-24 16:57:03', NULL),
(1614, 465, 833, '1st John 1: 7 says that \r\nBut if we walk in the light as He is in the light, we have fellowship with one another and the blood of Jesus Christ His Son cleanses us from all sin. \r\n\r\nOur commitments and submission to the calling in full obedience, enables us to have fellowship with our Lord, and also the fellowship with our co-believers. \r\n\r\nThe moment that we receive forgiveness for all our sins, as the blood of Jesus cleanses us from all our sins, automatically we become part and parcel of the divine calling and standards that God has set for us. Our Lord who is the source of light, enables us to walk in the light leaving aside all works of darkness that is equated with sin and lies. Our daily lifestyles should reflect the character, standards and values based on God\'s word. Whether in our personal lives in front of others. Our inward desire and hunger and calling should all match the calling and purpose as revealed through the scrip', 0, '2020-06-24 17:17:06', '2020-06-24 17:17:06', NULL),
(1615, 467, 589, 'The Bible relates the true story of creation in order to explain how humanity was actually designed to function within the world. Many other parts of the Bible appeal to the creation accounts to prove how the world supposed to work and what role human beings are morally obligated to play. CREATION ORDINANCES ARE MORAL REQUIREMENTS ESTABLISHED BY GOD\'S WORKS OF CREATION.God\'s works are perfect , and therefore, they are the standard for our own behavior. Sometimes creation ordinances are explicit, such as God\'s command to be fruitful and multiply in Genesis 1:28.\r\n But others are implicit such as our obligation to keep the sabbath holy.\r\nBut in the Ten Commandments ,in  Exodus 20:11, Moses clarified that God\'s pattern of working six days and resting on the seventh obligated human beings to do the same.', 9, '2020-06-24 17:44:37', '2020-06-25 21:53:53', NULL),
(1616, 467, 590, 'The book of Genesis contains two accounts of creation .One is in Genesis 1:1-2:3 and other is in Genesis 2:4-25.\r\nGENESIS 1:1-2:3\r\nGod spent six days forming and filling the universe:\r\nDay 1:God separated dark from light.\r\nDay 2: God separated the waters above from the waters below\r\nDay 3: God separated dry land and sea.\r\nDay 4: God filled the light and darkness with heavenly bodies(sun, moon ,stars)\r\nDay 5: God filled the sky and oceans with birds and sea creatures.\r\nDay 6:God filled the dry land with animals and created human beings to rule over creation\r\nFocus:\r\nhuman beings were created in God\'s image and given authority over creation \r\nSecond account:\r\nGenesis 2:4-25\r\nThis account contains more details to God\'s work on the sixth day\r\na.God formed the animals from the dust of the earth\r\nb. God made the first man from the dust of the earth and breathed life into him.\r\nc.Adam looked for a  suitable helper from among the animals\r\nd. God created Eve, the first woman from Adam\'s rib\r\nEve  was under Adam\'s authority in their marriage , but she was equal to him in the tasks God assigned to them as a  race.', 8, '2020-06-24 17:58:59', '2020-06-25 21:53:53', NULL),
(1617, 467, 591, 'Adam and Eve were created superior to the rest of God\'s earthly creatures in following ways:\r\n1.Created on the sixth day, separately from the animals ,as the culmination of creation (Gen 1:27)\r\n2. God called them \"very good\".\r\n3. Only Adam is said to have his life breathed into him by God(2:7)\r\n4. God created them in His image and appointed them to rule over creation on his behalf (Genesis 1:27-28, Psalms 8:6-8)\r\nGod created humanity to reflect his glory and his attributes in ways that other creatures couldn\'t.\r\nBecause human beings are likenesses of God.\r\na.Our existence points to his power and goodness\r\nb. no other creature carries this much honor and inherent dignity\r\nHumanity also has a superior role to administer God\'s rule over the earth (Genesis 2:20)', 8, '2020-06-24 18:08:25', '2020-06-25 21:53:53', NULL),
(1618, 467, 592, 'Some common beliefs that exist in our culture regarding human origins are  evolution theory, molecular theory , big bang theories.\r\nEvolution theories of Charles Darwin says that human beings were developed gradually from human ancestors which resembled  apes and similar creatures.\r\nBut Bible says that human beings were created the sixth day by God Almighty in His own image and likeness. The human that we see was not a gradually developed or evolved organism but we were purposefully and intentionally created by God as per His divine will.\r\nOther theory is some sort of molecular evolution , the proteins of our DNA and DNAs of other creatures were gradually developed as species and genes\r\nBut in the contrary Bible says that human beings and all other creatures were created according to their respective features and characteristics of their own  , each different in species and genes.', 8, '2020-06-24 18:19:05', '2020-06-25 21:53:53', NULL),
(1619, 467, 801, 'Adam and Eve did the works of the priests in the garden of Eden.Humanity is still responsible to God for fulfilling the moral obligations that flow from Adam\'s priestly duties  .\r\nPriestly obligations:\r\nWe fulfill it in our lives by serving God and worshiping him.  We cultivate and guard the creation . \r\n Being in full time ministry , we try our best to train others too to urn the world into a sanctuary that is fitting for God\'s purpose. We begin it with our home. We try to carry the same attitude in our local church too.\r\nIn the church ministry and our home too, in every opportunity of our lives we consider it our priority to render the sacrifices of praise and obedience to him. We try to fulfill the mission of reconciliation of others to God , by proclaiming hid goodness, salvation and forgiveness to the world.\r\nRoyal obligations:\r\nGod commanded Adam and Eve to increase the human race in order to spread its rule over the whole world. This task falls especially on God\'s faithful people in the church. So we as ministering family try our best by sharing his love to others and reaching out to others and turning the entire planet into God\'s earthly sanctuary as an extension of his heavenly kingdom .', 9, '2020-06-24 18:35:14', '2020-06-25 21:53:53', NULL),
(1620, 468, 655, 'To understand historical analysis we need to review some broad perspectives  that Holy Spirit has led the church to pursue the exegesis of Scripture in three ways :\r\nliterary analysis, historical analysis, thematic analysis\r\nHistorical analysis looks at scripture as a window to history, exploring historical events lying behind the Bible. It is especially concerned with the \"acts of God\".\r\nBiblical theology approaches the Scripture primarily with historical analysis. It looks at the Bible as a window that gives access to history. In this the focus of exegesis shifts from traditional theological themes to the historical events described in the Bible ,a very different set of priorities and concerns emerge. While sound Biblical theology is based on historical analysis of the Scriptures , we should turn to the fact that it is primarily concerned with the acts of God.', 8, '2020-06-25 18:16:47', '2020-06-25 21:53:03', NULL),
(1621, 468, 656, 'Historical analysis can take different forms  of at least two main tendencies:\r\nFACTUAL HISTORICAL ANALYSIS AND THEOLOGICAL HISTORICAL ANALYSIS\r\nThese two tendencies go hand in hand , but their main concerns are quite different\r\nA factual approach to historical analysis is concerned with questions like the date f the exodus under Moses, the historical circumstances that gave rise to Israel\'s monarchy , evidences certain battles and other crucial events. The goal of factual historical analysis is rather straight forward.\r\nTheological historical analysis-\r\nIt is  the theological significance of the acts of God reported in Scripture.\r\nChristians tend to agree with Aquinas that theology has two main concerns:\r\nOn the one hand a theological matter is anything that refers directly to God . And on the other hand a theological matter is anything that describes other subjects in relation to God.The former category is what traditional theology calls theology proper And the latter category includes matter such as doctrines of humanity, sin salvation ,ethics , church and the like', 9, '2020-06-25 18:33:49', '2020-06-25 21:53:03', NULL),
(1622, 468, 657, 'The shifts in culture that accompanied the rise of biblical theology are as follows:\r\n1. Biblical theology is in large measure a response to cultural shifts that can be traced back to the enlightenment of the 17th century\r\n2.Biblical theology is a christian response to a prominent intellectual movement in the modern period often called modern historic ism .It is the belief that history holds the key for understanding ourselves and the world around us.\r\n3. The German philosopher George Wilhelm Friedrich Hegel is best known for his proposal that every aspect of reality is caught up in logical patterns of historical progress known as dialectic.\r\n4.  This and other forms of historic ism rose to prominence in the modern period for many reasons . For instance a) archaeology\r\nb)geology\r\nc)biology\r\nd)and every academic discipline including theology.', 8, '2020-06-25 18:44:59', '2020-06-25 21:53:04', NULL),
(1623, 468, 658, 'Gabler spoke that systematic theology was not to examine or explain the Bible, but to determine what Christians should believe in the modern world through rational reflection on science and religion.As a critical theologian Gabler believed that the Christians should believe only those parts of the Bible that pass the standards of modern rational and scientific analysis.\r\nIt became increasingly difficult for critical theologians to draw from the scriptures as they formed their systematic theology. We might have expected them simply to set aside \r\nbiblical theology since they thought the Bible was riddled with misleading historical claims . And this has been the reactions of many during the modern period . But the field of Biblical theology did not die when  critical  theologians rejected biblical authority , instead they found other ways to use Scriptures for contemporary theology. Instead of teaching the Bible as true history, they began to look at the Scriptures as expressions of ancient religious sentiments presented as historical claims and they explored how these ancient religious feelings and experiences might be useful to modern Christians . So they have come to approach the Scriptures through Biblical theology', 8, '2020-06-25 19:01:09', '2020-06-25 21:53:04', NULL),
(1624, 468, 659, 'The divine goal of all world history is the extension of God\'s perfect heavenly reign to every corner of the earth.When God\'s will is done as perfectly on earth as it is in heaven, at that time the ultimate goal of history will be fulfilled. The opening chapter of the Bible describes the way God began to turn the chaotic world into his kingdom by ordering creation and placing his image in the garden of Eden but humanity rebelled and brought corruption and death in to the world.\r\nThe rest of the Old Testament reports how God Israel as his special people, God accomplished much through Israel but Israel also failed miserably.\r\nDespite these failures, God did not give upon Hid grand purpose. AS the New testament reveals God sent His eternal Son into the world and through His death God redeemed  a people for himself.Through Christ\'s resurrection and ascension , the ministry of the Holy Spirit, His glorious return, Christ is completing  the task originally given to humanity.\r\nRevelation 11:15\r\nChrist is hailed as the one who will bring God\'s  kingdom on earth.\r\nIn this approach to biblical theology. every event in biblical history is part of this grand scheme, while the Goal of biblical history is to bring God glory by establishing his worldwide kingdom in Christ', 8, '2020-06-25 19:17:04', '2020-06-25 21:53:04', NULL),
(1625, 480, 665, 'Diachronic is an approach to study a language. It is a change or development in a linguistic system over a period of time. A synchronic approach considers a language at a moment in time without taking its history into consideration. By contrast , a diachronic approach considers the development and evaluation of a language through history.', 5, '2020-06-27 01:25:29', '2020-06-29 15:23:19', NULL),
(1626, 480, 666, 'We use the term development instead of simply speaking of diachronic changes to suggest two main ideas. First,changes in Old Testament theological structures always move forward fulfilling God\'s purpose for histroy. And second, we speak of development because theological changes only occur through God\'s providential involvement in histroy. And second, we speak of development because theological changes only occur through God\'s providential involvement in history. Old Testament theological development often apprears like a road seen from distance. When we see close the road of Old testament is actually filled with steep and abrupt shifts caused by God\'s providence.', 8, '2020-06-27 01:37:00', '2020-06-29 15:23:19', NULL),
(1627, 480, 667, 'Old Testament is a book about the kingdom of God, a kingdom that God administered through covenants, which in turn were explained and applied to God\'s people in the books of the old Testament. We have entitled it as Divine Convenants becuase we will be explored how God governed his kingdome through a series of covenants that established in Old Testament history. We can clearly see how divine covenants guided the life of God\'s people in the Old Testament. It clearly shows the fundamental realtionship of God\'s kingdom , his covenants and historical developments of covenants in the Old Testament.', 8, '2020-06-27 01:48:14', '2020-06-29 15:23:19', NULL),
(1628, 480, 668, 'Typology is Christian theology. Events, persons or statements in the Old Testament are seen as types. For an example Jonah may be seen as the type of Christ in that he appreared to have emerged from the whale\'s belly and from death. In the fullest version of the theory of the typlogy, the whole purpose of the Old Testament is viewed as merely the provision of types for Christ.', 7, '2020-06-27 02:00:33', '2020-06-29 15:23:19', NULL),
(1629, 480, 669, 'The Holy Scriptures of the Old Testament have many things to say that foreshadow Jesus Christ and his redemptive work. These scriptures refer to a reality that would be fulfilled in Christ. This is discussed in several places of new Testament. Whatever it was in the Holy Scriptures that referred to Christ and his redemptive work had to be specifically pointed out and explained by Jesus.  This implies that it was not immediately evident that what was literally expressed in the Old Testament applied to Jesus in figurative way.', 8, '2020-06-27 02:15:16', '2020-06-29 15:23:19', NULL),
(1630, 474, 881, 'To explore the holy Spirit divinity we look in two directions.on the one hand we that apostle creed affirms belief in the spirit divinity.and on the way the apostle creed affirms the Divinity of the holy Spirit \r\nWhen it comes to talking about the person of the holy Spirit,one of the questions that people often ask is whether or not the church always affirmed or professed the Divinity of the holy Spirit', 5, '2020-06-28 17:24:58', '2020-06-29 15:25:13', NULL),
(1631, 474, 882, 'The biblical basis for believing in the holy Spirit can be demonstrated in many ways .but for our purposes, we will focus on the name he is called, the attributes he possesses, the work he performs and the Trinitarian formula that refer to him \r\n\r\nIs important to not in OT it is God who is reported reference to as the holy Spirit we see this 2 king 19:22 ,Is 30:11, Hosa 11, \r\nAttributes \r\n    Christian theology have traditionally spoke of God as having two distinct types of attributes.communication attributes and incommunicable attributes.one the one hand way with his creation', 7, '2020-06-28 17:36:30', '2020-06-29 15:25:13', NULL),
(1632, 474, 883, 'When we speak of the personal attributes of holy Spirit,we have in mind those questions he possesses that are unique to person things that can only be true about him if he\'s a real person and not simply an impersonal focus \r\n The holy Spirit has far too many persons attributes for us to catalog then all in this lesson , so we will simply provide four example to demonstrate his person hood to desire and to choose . clearly any being that can do thes thing cannot be a mere force or power.as one example of his will , 1 cor 12:11', 8, '2020-06-28 17:47:19', '2020-06-29 15:25:13', NULL),
(1633, 474, 884, 'As we have mentioned throughout these lessons, the relationship between the person of the Trinity have traditionally been described from two different perspective specifically, theologian have spoken of the ontological Trinity the father the son and the holy Spirit.but they emphasize different aspects of the relationship between these three divine person \r\n\r\nWhen we talk ontological Trinity, we are focusing on God\'s being and existing from this perspective the holy Spirit is equal in power and glory to the father and the Son .all three of God\'s person are infinite, eternal and unchangeable, and each has the same essential divine attributes, such as wisdom, power, holiness, justice, goodness and truth', 8, '2020-06-28 18:01:02', '2020-06-29 15:25:13', NULL),
(1634, 474, 885, 'With regard to the economic Trinity, the holy Spirit is said to be the third person because he holds the third rank, being subordinate Both to the father and to the son , the scripture indicate his subordination in a number of ways .for instance he is sent or give by the father and the son Scripture teache this in passage like Luk 11:13 John 14, and 15:25, and act 2:23 and when he comes the spirit Oby the father and the son by doing the work they sent him to do. We learn of this in places like John 16:13 .Romans 8:12 and 1 Peter 1:2\r\n\r\nOf course even when we say that the holy Spirit hold the lowest rank from the perspective of the economic Trinity, it is important to emphasize that he is still fully God , and has absolutely sovereign authority over every aspect of creation. moreover within', 8, '2020-06-28 18:11:15', '2020-06-29 15:25:13', NULL),
(1635, 479, 786, 'The office of \"image of God\" is rooted in the authority delegated to humanity. God appointed human beings to rule over his creation on his behalf .It is given in Genesis 1:27&28\r\nOne important aspect of being God\'s image is that we hold the office of delegated ruler. \r\nWe are God\'s vice reagents -his administrative deputies Or in Near Eastern times , his servants or vassal Kings.In the Near East , images of the king were placed throughout the kingdom to remind the citizens of the king\'s benevolence and greatness to encourage the people to obey the king and to show that the king was present with his people.\r\nHuman beings are physical representations that remind all creation of God\'d power , authority and goodness. And through us He manifests his rule over the world and his creatures.', 8, '2020-06-29 17:46:08', '2020-06-30 14:31:02', NULL),
(1636, 479, 787, 'In Genesis 1:26-28 we see that the first thing Scripture says about humanity is that we are the image and likeness of God. \r\nImage means a carved idol , a model , reflection or shadow\r\nLikeness means a statue , a sketch, he appearance or sound of something compared to another or having a similar form.\r\nWe are God\'s image and likenesses because we rule over the earth as God\'s servant kings and are endowed with necessary qualities and abilities to perform our duties.\r\nWe are images of God  : we rule on his behalf ,carry out his will, and reflect his glory(1 Corinthians 11:7)\r\nAs God\'s image , we are given authority over the earth. we are God\'s vice reagents or servant kings b whose task is to make sure that his will on done on earth.Our role or office of images of God elevates all humanity to the level of royalty.We hold authority only because God grants it to us', 8, '2020-06-29 17:56:23', '2020-06-30 14:31:02', NULL),
(1637, 479, 788, 'The image of God in human beings includes our capacity to think rationally and process complex emotions.Some of this rational ability was lost in our fall into sin (Ecclesiastes 9:3;\r\nJeremiah 19:9,\r\n Deuteronomy 29:2-3 Israelites could not understand the significance of miracles  \r\n,John 8:43-47:\r\n Ephesians 4:17-18 says that Gentiles live in the futility of their mind\r\nThe fall damaged our ability to think and to understand the world from God\'s perspective , but it dint destroy it completely.\r\nBut in Colossians 3:10 we read that Paul explains about the restoration of our rational abilities as an aspect of image of God being renewed in us.\r\nWhen we come to faith in Christ, God begins to restore that aspect of his image in us. As a  result , we are able to think and understand more correctly, so that our thoughts and reason become more aligned with his.', 8, '2020-06-29 18:09:57', '2020-06-30 14:31:02', NULL),
(1638, 479, 789, 'When God appointed humanity to the office of his image , he created  a variety of relationships.\r\nFirst Our obligation to reflect God\'s character:\r\nImages of God are intended to reflect his character(pure, holy, righteous) wherever they appear (1 Peter 1:15-15, Hebrews 12:14). Fallen human beings cant be holy on our own merit, but we rely on Christ\'s perfect holiness for our standing before God.By God\'s grace we are becoming clearer image s of him as we pursue holiness and righteousness\r\nSecond Our duty is to promote pure worship:\r\nMoses reminded his audience that God hadn\'t revealed himself in a physical form because he wanted to protect the purity of worship. We should also realize that God is the true God  and He isn\'t to be treated like the false gods of the nations. \r\nOur next responsibility is to build God\'s kingdom:\r\nGod commanded humanity to fill the earth instruction us to place image of himself throughout the world. (Genesis 1:28) As God\'s vice reagents we carry his rule with us wherever we go.', 9, '2020-06-29 18:22:46', '2020-06-30 14:31:02', NULL),
(1639, 479, 790, 'Our covenant relationship with God requires  his images to reflect God\'s character and to promote pure worship and its also our obligation to build his kingdom. Being God \'s people we relate to God , to other people, and to the world around us. As God\'s representatives on earth, our thoughts, behavior and emotions reflect on him. As in full time ministry, we share the gospel and His words of kingdom which results in saving them form Satan\'s s kingdom, which every unbeliever is born into.\r\nWe carry out his commandments to love , forgive , be peaceful to others as it is in His Kingdom. \r\nWe promote pure worship in our fellowship times by worshiping him in truth and Spirit. \r\n This office of image of God has made me more responsible for representing his rule.exercising his delegated authority , expressing his character and carrying out his will.', 9, '2020-06-29 18:34:37', '2020-06-30 14:31:02', NULL),
(1640, 450, 826, NULL, 0, '2020-06-30 05:51:01', '2020-06-30 05:56:21', NULL),
