(1644, 450, 830, 'In addition to being the absolute moral standard ,we wills see that God is also the absolute judge of morality ,that is he has the ultimate preoperative determine whether or not particular actions,emotions and power to act on his determinations.it is true that God delegates to human being some responsibility for making ethical judgment ,according to the scripture human govt are given limited responsibility to honer good and punish evil,but the bible also teach the human judgements are only correct and valid insofar as the mirror God\'s judgment ,God himself will judge all people by their action ,it is God\'s right to judge because he has absolute authority and his judgment are in escapable becouse he has absolute power,\r\nThere are only two option either we submit ourself to him,seeking mercy throgh christ,or we denay him suffer eternal punishment .', 0, '2020-06-30 06:52:29', '2020-06-30 06:52:29', NULL),
(1646, 450, 832, 'Existential revelation has not been common for theologians ,this a different way of catagarizing the same revelation that theologians have acepted for centuries,the suprime judge by wich all controvrsis of religion are to be detrminded ,and all decrease of counsils opinions of ancient writers doctrine of men,and privat spirit, the confes state that the suprime judge in all controversis of relegion isnthe Holy spirit and the surst guid to the holy spirit\'s judgment is scripture ,God use councils ,ancient writers , doctrin of men and private spirit to reveal his will to his people \r\nwe can call this human judgemen forms \"existential revelation\"Existential revelation divided into two main categories, external aspects of existential revelation,and the internal aspects of the existential revelation \r\nExternal :the external aspects of existential revelation include such things as human existance ,human judgement ;both indidual and coporate;and human behaviour.\r\ninternal:we might think many ways that Holy spirit work within human beings to reveal truth about God , one is illumination ,theologians traditionaly calling .secont \"inward leading\" illumination is divin gift of understanding ,', 0, '2020-06-30 07:32:23', '2020-06-30 07:32:23', NULL),
(1647, 481, 660, 'The word\"synchronic \" derives from two Greek words :the preposition sun which means \'with\' or \'together with\' and the noun chronos which means \'time\'.When the word synchronic is applied to historical events ,it describes occurrences that took place \"together in time\" or \"at the same time\".\r\nIllustration:\r\nwhen movie directors tell their stories . they convey a flow of events from beginning to end. They depict how one event leads to another and another and so on. Yet. even though the movie is one , whole unit is also broken down into smaller parts called scenes. Each scene tells a portion of the larger story . In this scene, each scene represents a synchronic moment in the movie , a period of time in the film.\r\nIn Synchronic synthesis , biblical theologians concentrate their attention on particular periods of time in the Old Testament. It\'s important to realize like scenes in a movie , synchronic approaches can focus on periods of various lengths. Sometimes biblical theologians focus on relatively brief historical moments, but other moments they concern themselves with relatively long periods of time  .', 8, '2020-06-30 18:25:23', '2020-07-01 14:17:44', NULL),
(1648, 481, 661, 'Synthesis means combining different components of something into a whole.Like when we go to a friend\'s house for dinner, we eat this and that. some people come early , some leave early. Some people , some dance and similarly all kinds of things takes place. Now when we narrate the things that happened at the dinner,we don\'t repeat everything that took place.Instead , you would synthesize or make sense out of the entire gathering.\r\nPopular denial\r\nCritical theologians argued that logic was a primary feature of the \"Greek mindset \", but was relatively foreign to the \"Hebrew mindset\".\r\nBased on a number of linguistic and cultural assessments , they argued that the Greeks focused on abstraction and logical order much like systematic theology. And by contrast, they suggested that the Hebrew mindset looked at everything in terms of historic dynamics.\r\nAffirmation :\r\nOld testament theology displays substantial concern for logical and rational thought.It doe snot employ the standards of formal western philosophical traditions :few technical terms, variety of genres, different emphases, no all-encompassing system', 9, '2020-06-30 18:42:44', '2020-07-01 14:17:44', NULL),
(1649, 481, 662, 'Two worlds of Poetry:\r\na)That world: the world they wrote about\r\nPoets of the old testament were interested in two different world that tell us about history. When writing about \"That world \" they provided objective facts about God\'s acts and words.Poetry often opened windows to the past.\r\nfor eg: Moses and Miriam sang at the red sea Exodus 15:1-21\r\nb)Their world :the world of the readers\r\nOld testament poetry often provided windows to contemporary historical information from the writers\' own time. For eg: Psalms 1\r\nTwo worlds of narrative literature \r\na)That world : the subject of their text\r\nOn one side they wrote about the world that was the subject of their text or :that world \"\r\nNarratives largely focused on the past and only rarely mentioned the present or the future. For eg:\r\nMoses wrote about Patriarchal history ij the book of genesis ,whereas he lived much later in the history\r\nb)Their world : the world in which the readers lived.\r\nOn the other side, authors of narratives also dealt with their world . They wanted their readers to think , act and feel in certain ways within their own worlds in the light of past events.', 9, '2020-06-30 18:56:50', '2020-07-01 14:17:44', NULL),
(1650, 481, 663, 'Modern evangelicals often make the mistake of expecting Old Testaments narratives to be like modern journalistic historical writings. \r\nModern historical standards: comprehensive, precise,objective.\r\nOld testament stories were only as comprehensive as suited the didactic purposes of their writers. They did not include every significant fact. They felt no compulsion to include every significant fact. They did not meet the modern criterion of comprehensiveness in good history writing.Nevertheless. their narratives are true and authoritative records of the past. \r\nOld Testament authors were only as precise as their didactic purposes required. AS long as historical records have been kept, their have always been historians who allowed their subjective opinions to skew their writing to the pointing that they actually misrepresented history.Old Testament  narratives were not designed to meet modern standards of history writing, they only present fully reliable historical information that enables us to construct syn chronic synthesis of old testament theology', 8, '2020-06-30 19:15:04', '2020-07-01 14:17:44', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(1651, 481, 664, 'Old testament authors were only as precise as their didactic purposes required. There is a vital difference between precision and truth . In every aspect of life precision is always a matter of degree. And so long as we respond with us much precision as is needed , no one accuses us of misrepresenting the facts.In many ways, the same kind of thing was true for Old testament authors. They were only as precise as they needed to be to reach their didactic goals .\r\nSeeking much more precision than this would be misguide as regarding \" God promised to uphold his covenant with David and : that a descendant of David will always rule over Israel. \r\nfor example we find that the Chronicler determined not to include the failures of Solomon because of his didactic purposes , he wanted only to concentrate on Solomon\'s successes. \r\nEvery narrative may not be exactly precise, but every narration is true as it is inspired by God.', 8, '2020-06-30 19:33:36', '2020-07-01 14:17:44', NULL),
(1652, 450, 833, 'As we know that God him self is the ultimate standard of the right and wrong ,of good and evil,by this we accept that ultimate morality is stand with God ,even if comply if he is to be consider good ,insted we insist that God is not accountable to any standerd outside himself and that everithing that accounts with his character ,while everithing is dose not evil and good ,in  1John 1:7, says that God is light  , this is a primary moral evaluation,we consider darkeness is always as sin and lies, and light is turth and purity , if we obey God we wlk in light and walk with light , if we are telling that we walk with light we must obay his word and be obligated to God ,becouse we are obligated to see God\'s natur as the standard and model of goodness and rightness ,and for the same reason we are compelled to cindmd as sin ful, evil and wrong those things that oppose his natur, by Blood of christ jesus he brigh us to light and we have an opertunity to be with light', 0, '2020-07-01 05:45:23', '2020-07-01 05:45:23', NULL),
(1653, 476, 891, 'Sin separate us from God\'s blessings, and places us under his curse .and there is no way that we can overcome this problem by ourselves.this is what we mean problem of sin\r\n\r\nMost of us are familiar with the event recorded in Genesis 3\r\nThe account of when our first parents Adam and Eve rebelled against God \r\n\r\nScripture indicate that after Adam and Eva sinned ,God judged and cursed the entire human race.\r\nThis curse affected every aspect of their being.it immediately results in the spiritual death that is spoken of throughout Scripture, as in John 5:24-25', 6, '2020-07-01 17:20:05', '2020-07-02 17:28:06', NULL),
(1654, 476, 892, '1)Father \r\n Forgiveness begin with the father because he the one that everything planned.N.T say is father send the son into the world and appointment him as the Redeemer \r\nJohn 3:16\r\nFather is the architecture of redemption.it his gracious plan and mercy \r\n\r\n2)Son\r\nThe Divine grace accomplish our forgiveness also involved the son , who is our Redeemer \r\nIn fulfillment of the father promise, the son was sent into the world, because incarnate as Jesus, the long\r\nJesus atoned for sin by dying on the cross in place of sinners.he received the Divine curse that had been warranted\r\n3) Holy spirit \r\nThe holy Spirit is the person of the Trinity who actually applie forgiveness to our lives.the father laid plans and son accomplished and atonement.but our sins are not actually forgive until the holy Spirit does his work \r\nWhen first come to faith, the holy Spirit reconcile us to God by forgiving all the sins we have committed up to the point', 7, '2020-07-01 17:38:04', '2020-07-02 17:28:06', NULL),
(1655, 476, 893, 'Scripture clear say that God does not forgive the sins of every person.som people are forgiven and some are not.\r\nFrom a human perspective the reason is that the process of forgiveness ordinary invoice an element of individual responsible general speaking, those people that fullfil these responseslity\r\n\r\nScripture say two primary condition for forgiveness. First, it speaks of faith in God as a prerequisite for forgiveness.in Scripture, faith is a multifunction concept.but in this context, when we spoke of faith in God', 8, '2020-07-01 17:47:46', '2020-07-02 17:28:06', NULL),
(1656, 476, 894, 'Before our fall into sin , our bodies and our souls were unaffected by sin .but when Adam and Eve fell in to sin .sin corrupted not only there Soul but also their bodies.and this corruption of their bodies ultimate results in their physical deaths.\r\nGenu 3:19\r\nSin affected Adam and Eve in both spiritual and physical ways. And because we are there natural descendants we bear the same cure .our souls come into the world in a state that biblical described as spiritual death.we are under God\'s judgment, and have lost all abilities to please him\r\n Our bodys corrupted by sin Roman 6:12-19', 7, '2020-07-01 18:00:05', '2020-07-02 17:28:06', NULL),
(1657, 476, 895, '1) the things believer experience during our present life on earth \r\n2) the intermediate state of our bodies that being with our physical death \r\n3) the new life of resurrection itself \r\n\r\n1) present Life \r\nSalvation our bodies begin with the individual of holy Spirit when we first come to faith.exp. Roman 8:9-\r\nRedemption of bodies Ephesians 1:13-\r\n2) intermediate state \r\n\r\nAfter the beginning of the redemption of our bodies In the present life of believers, the process continues during our physical death \r\nWhen we die our bodies are temporary separated from our souls.this stage is often called the intermediate state \r\nBut our souls are heaven, our bodies remain on earth.our bodies are still corrupted by sin , as proven by the fact that they decay .', 7, '2020-07-01 18:14:39', '2020-07-02 17:28:06', NULL),
(1658, 487, 826, 'Unlike many other ethical system our definition focus on God and his blessings rather than good or evil, wrong or right ,those things that receive Gods blessing are good and right ,by foucusing on God\'s blessing in this way we meant to say two things ,first God\'s nature is tha standard of morality ,and second god\'s action demonstrate the standard of morality .\r\nGod\'s divine nature:we must know that God himself is the ultimate standard of right and wrong ,of good and and evil .by saying this we accept that ultimate morality is in God;God is not accountable any standard outside himself and that everything that accords with his character is good and right ,while everithing not good and right ,we are obligated to see God\'s nature as the standard and model of goodness rightness .\r\nDivine action : the second we say that foucosing on God and his blessing is that God\'s action demonstrate the standard of morality ,the main thing is that God show the approve for what is right asd what is good by bestowing blessing on it, similarly he shows his angryb and haterd for what wrong and evil by with holding blessings and pouring out curs .', 0, '2020-07-02 05:46:23', '2020-07-02 05:46:23', NULL),
(1659, 487, 827, 'Unless a work is done with the right motive it is not a work that god will reward with blessings .first it must proseed from a heart that is purified by faith ,second action flow out of christian Love ,Work poceed not from a purified heart is sinful,and canot please God ,rite motive is cloesly associated thebway of defenition of chistian ethics nfocus on good person with good nature, only  believers who are indwelled by the holy spirit can do works that God reward with blessings , one reason for this is that every believers need a heart that purified by faith , \r\nLove :our works are useless if they are not motivated by love,works and even every bspiritual gifts that produse benifical result merit no reward if they are not motivated by love , God\'s revelation in scripture ,love the lord your God with all your heart , to reject Gods law is to reject him as he offers to us in covenant relationship', 0, '2020-07-02 05:58:40', '2020-07-02 05:58:40', NULL),
(1660, 487, 828, 'The practical steps that we should take when  making  ethical decision time and again, we are in a position to sketch the basic contours of the approach that will explain more fully in later lesson,to this we will touch tree matters ,1.three tendencies of different christian groups, 2.three perspective on ethical decition making ,3.the indipendance of these perspective \r\n1.Tendencies :ther are many different ways that belivers try to make ethical decision in life , but they tend fall into three amin catagories .emphazise our christian conscience by leading of the holy spirit, domes emphasize scripture,insisting tha action are good if they obeyb the scriptur,,other still emphezise thge outcome of action are good if they produce good consequence .\r\n2.Perspectives .:its about ethical judgement or decision in this way,ethics should be done from the perspective of God\'s word ,from the perspective of situation .frome the perspective of the pperson,\r\n3.Situational :when our ethical enquries turn to the problem themselves or to the consequens of action or to goal, we are doing ethics form the situationalal perspective ,this aprocjhe may be called \'teleological, becouse its fouce on the end of the result of action.', 0, '2020-07-02 06:18:49', '2020-07-02 06:18:49', NULL),
(1661, 487, 829, 'in ethics we speake about three perspective or aprach towards every judgment ,1.The situational perspective,2.normative perspective,3.Existential perspective\r\nSituational :when our ethical enquries turn to the problems them selves or to the consiquence of action or goals we are doing ethics form the situational perspective .this aproche amy called \"teleological\' becouse it focusees onthe end or the result of action \r\nNormative :The most intuitive perspective of christian is what we call the normatve perspective .normative refers the fact that god\'s word is the norm, or standard for ethics \r\nExistential:when we aproch ethic by asking questians that are specific to the peopl involved we are doing ethics form an existential perspective', 0, '2020-07-02 06:34:14', '2020-07-02 06:34:14', NULL),
(1662, 487, 830, 'In additionb to being the absolute moral standard ,we will see that God is also the absolute judge of morality .that is he has the ultimate prerogative to determine whether or not particular action ,emotions and thoughts meet his moral requirment , it is tru that God deligate human being to make some ethical jedgement ,according to bible human athorities are given limiter responsibility to judge , to honer good and punish evil,but the bible alson teach thst our human judgement are only correct and valid insofar as they miner God\'s judgment .\r\nGod himself is the highest core in the univers ,he will make the ultimate determination of whther or not we have lived moraly  immoraly , and his judgment will be utterly blinding, it is God\'s right to judge becouse he has absolute athority and his judgment are inescapable becouse he has an absolute power ,althogh God\'s creaturs are may wish to escape his authority and power they cannot', 0, '2020-07-02 06:48:39', '2020-07-02 06:48:39', NULL),
(1663, 487, 831, 'Traditionally theologians have spoken God\'s revelation primary in two part ,special revaluation and general revelation.in the catagory of special revelation they placed direct communication from God such as Scripture ,prophecy dreams and visions , the category of general revelation has include such things as history , the universe , weather ,plant animals, and human beings .\r\nhere we add existential revaluation , God\'s revelation in person , revelation that is often groped with general revaluation but winch relay deserve to be treat separately.\r\nGeneral revelation:when we speak about it we are connected with the way creation and history tells us true things about god and his moral requirment of us.general revalation ca not teach us everithing \r\nSpecial revelations :general revelation is the part of God\'s reveald standards for our lives all christian should easly recognize that special revelation is a norms that nis binding on our lives,\r\nExistential revelation :Exixtential revalation is idea of God reviels himself in through person has always been recognized by the main stream of protestand theology as part of genaral revalation, here we simply use an new way to categorize the same revelation theolagians that accepted', 0, '2020-07-02 07:07:55', '2020-07-02 07:07:55', NULL),
(1664, 487, 832, 'Existential revelation God reveals himself in and trough person,example, the suprime judge ,by wich all controversies of religion are to be determined ,all decrees of councils ,opinions of ancient writers ,doctrince of men and private spirit are to be examineed and in whose sentance we are to rest can be no other but the holy spirit speaking in the scripture\r\nGod use councils ,ancient writers doctrinces of men and private spirit to reveal his will to his people even though thieir determination must be subject to scripture,When we call these human judgement forms of \'existential revelation\'none is the simple presention of history or creation,and none is supernatural communication from God,\r\nExistential revelation divided in to two main catagories , what we might call the external aspects ,internal aspects.External aspects:of revelation includes such this human existance ,human judgement,human beings are created in the image of God  internal aspects:its tell us holy spirit works in human being to reveal the truth about God by ilumination and inward leading', 0, '2020-07-02 07:26:32', '2020-07-02 07:26:32', NULL),
(1665, 487, 833, 'First we affirm that God himself is the ultimate standard of right and wrong ,of good and evil, considering in the idea in light of john\'s teaching in 1 John 1:7 we have fellowship with God , and have fellowship with one another , and the blood of jesus purified us from all sin, this metaphore God as light is primarly a moral evaluation, Darkness is equated with sin and lies ,and light with truth and purity from sin,inlight of this pasage we are obligated to see God\'s nature as the standard and model of goodness and rightness .and for the same reason we are compelled to condemn as sinful , evil and wrong these things that oppose him, \r\nWe are obligated to obey his standared so we must walk in the light and walk with light , if we say that we have relation to God and we we cant love others we are lieing we have no relation with God, we are wlaking inthe darkness , by christ we got forgiveness becous God love us, and forgive us, same way we must love ithers and have fellowship with others , this is the acceptance of his standard.', 0, '2020-07-02 07:39:13', '2020-07-02 07:39:13', NULL),
(1666, 489, 654, 'विश्वासयोग्य लेखक :- आरंभिक कलीसिया के पास इन चारों सुसमाचारों में अटूट विश्वास के कम से कम तीन कारण थे। पहला , कलीसिया ने सुसमाचारों को प्रमाणिक रूप में ग्रहणं किया क्योंकि अपने शीर्षको में वे विश्वासयोग लेखकों के द्वारा लिखे गए थे। \r\n                 बहुत अधिक संभावना है कि सुसमाचार मूल रूप से नाम रहित थे। परंतु संभावना यह भी है कि जब वे पहली बार प्रकाशित किए गए तो उन्हें उन लोगों के द्वारा स्वीकार किया गया जो लेखकों को जानते थे या फिर शायद लेखकों को पहचानते हुए पत्रों के साथ उन्हें वितरित भी किया और आरंभिक समय से ही मसीही लेखनों ने सुसमाचारों को मत्ती मरकुस लुका और यूहन्ना के साथ जोड़ा अर्थात ऐसे चार लोग जो नए नियम में कलीसियाई अगुवो के साथ अच्छी प्रतिष्ठा में जाने जाते हैं। \r\nप्रैरितिक अनुमोदन ;- दूसरा , आरंभिक मसीही कैनन में सुसमाचारों के स्थान के प्रति भी विश्वस्त थे क्योंकि वे इस बात को जानते थे कि इन पुस्तको को प्रैरितिक अनुमोदन मिला है। \r\n                         मती और यूहन्ना प्रेरित थे, यीशु के शब्दों और कार्यों के गवाह थे। मरकुस के बारे में कहा जाता है कि उसने अपनी काफी बातों को पतरस से लिया था जिसने 1पतरस 5:13 में मरकुस के स्नेह से मेरा पुत्र के रूप में संबोधित किया है और हम लुका   1: 1 से 14 में पहले ही देख चुके हैं कि लुका ने स्पष्ट किया था कि उसने अपने कार्य को गवाह के वर्णन पर आधारित किया है।\r\nकलीसिया के गवाह :- तीसरा, सभी चारों सुसमाचार पहली सदी की कलीसिया की गवाही से समर्पित है। चारों पुस्तकें इतनी पुरानी है कि यीशु के जीवन और सेवकाई के जीवित गवाह उनके विवरणों को ठुकराने या उनकी पुष्टि करने के योग्य थे । और ऐसा हुआ भी, गवाहों ने बहुत आरंभ से ही अपनी कलीसियाओं में उन्हें स्वीकार करके उनकी पुष्टि की।\r\nएकता :- हम यहां पर तो समाचारों के साहित्यिक चरित्र को जा चुके हैं और कलीसिया में उनके स्थान को देख चुके हैं। इसलिए अब हम नए नियम के चारों से समाचारों के बीच की एकता को देखने के लिए तैयार हैं। \r\n                 हम सुसमाचारों के बीच की एकता पर दो प्रकार से ध्यान देंगे। पहला इस बात की पुष्टि करने के द्वारा कि प्रत्येक पुस्तक परमेश्वर के राज्य की सामान कहानी बताती है और दूसरा उस महत्व को जांचने के द्वारा जो वह परमेश्वर के राज्य को लानेवाले के रूप मे यीशु पर देते हैं। आइए , इस पुष्टि के साथ आरंभ करें कि नए नियम के सारे शो समाचारों के द्वारा सामान कहानी बताई गई है। \r\nसमान कहानी :- सामान्य भाव में हम कह सकते हैं कि मत्ती , मरकुस , लुका और  यूहन्ना की पुस्तकों में बताई गई कहानी सुसमाचार है। वास्तव में इसलिए उन पुस्तकों को सुसमाचार कहा जाता है। वह ऐसी पुस्तकें हैं जो सुसमाचार की कहानी बताती है, परंतु सुसमाचार की कहानी वास्तव में है क्या ? \r\n                   सुसमाचार शब्द यूनानी शब्द युऐन्गलिओन का अनुवाद है जिसका अर्थ होता है? शुभ संदेश अतः जब बाइबल यीशु के सुसमाचार के बारे में बात करती है तो यह यीशु के बारे में शुभ संदेश को दर्शाती है।विश्वासयोग्य लेखक :- आरंभिक कलीसिया के पास इन चारों सुसमाचारों में अटूट विश्वास के कम से कम तीन कारण थे। पहला , कलीसिया ने सुसमाचारों को प्रमाणिक रूप में ग्रहणं किया क्योंकि अपने शीर्षको में वे विश्वासयोग लेखकों के द्वारा लिखे गए थे। \r\n                 बहुत अधिक संभावना है कि सुसमाचार मूल रूप से नाम रहित थे। परंतु संभावना यह भी है कि जब वे पहली बार प्रकाशित किए गए तो उन्हें उन लोगों के द्वारा स्वीकार किया गया जो लेखकों को जानते थे या फिर शायद लेखकों को पहचानते हुए पत्रों के साथ उन्हें वितरित भी किया और आरंभिक समय से ही मसीही लेखनों ने सुसमाचारों को मत्ती मरकुस लुका और यूहन्ना के साथ जोड़ा अर्थात ऐसे चार लोग जो नए नियम में कलीसियाई अगुवो के साथ अच्छी प्रतिष्ठा में जाने जाते हैं। \r\nप्रैरितिक अनुमोदन ;- दूसरा , आरंभिक मसीही कैनन में सुसमाचारों के स्थान के प्रति भी विश्वस्त थे क्योंकि वे इस बात को जानते थे कि इन पुस्तको को प्रैरितिक अनुमोदन मिला है। \r\n                         मती और यूहन्ना प्रेरित थे, यीशु के शब्दों और कार्यों के गवाह थे। मरकुस के बारे में कहा जाता है कि उसने अपनी काफी बातों को पतरस से लिया था जिसने 1पतरस 5:13 में मरकुस के स्नेह से मेरा पुत्र के रूप में संबोधित किया है और हम लुका   1: 1 से 14 में पहले ही देख चुके हैं कि लुका ने स्पष्ट किया था कि उसने अपने कार्य को गवाह के वर्णन पर आधारित किया है।\r\nकलीसिया के गवाह :- तीसरा, सभी चारों सुसमाचार पहली सदी की कलीसिया की गवाही से समर्पित है। चारों पुस्तकें इतनी पुरानी है कि यीशु के जीवन और सेवकाई के जीवित गवाह उनके विवरणों को ठुकराने या उनकी पुष्टि करने के योग्य थे । और ऐसा हुआ भी, गवाहों ने बहुत आरंभ से ही अपनी कलीसियाओं में उन्हें स्वीकार करके उनकी पुष्टि की।\r\nएकता :- हम यहां पर तो समाचारों के साहित्यिक चरित्र को जा चुके हैं और कलीसिया में उनके स्थान को देख चुके हैं। इसलिए अब हम नए नियम के चारों से समाचारों के बीच की एकता को देखने के लिए तैयार हैं। \r\n                 हम सुसमाचारों के बीच की एकता पर दो प्रकार से ध्यान देंगे। पहला इस बात की पुष्टि करने के द्वारा कि प्रत्येक पुस्तक परमेश्वर के राज्य की सामान कहानी बताती है और दूसरा उस महत्व को जांचने के द्वारा जो वह परमेश्वर के राज्य को लानेवाले के रूप मे यीशु पर देते हैं। आइए , इस पुष्टि के साथ आरंभ करें कि नए नियम के सारे शो समाचारों के द्वारा सामान कहानी बताई गई है। \r\nसमान कहानी :- सामान्य भाव में हम कह सकते हैं कि मत्ती , मरकुस , लुका और  यूहन्ना की पुस्तकों में बताई गई कहानी सुसमाचार है। वास्तव में इसलिए उन पुस्तकों को सुसमाचार कहा जाता है। वह ऐसी पुस्तकें हैं जो सुसमाचार की कहानी बताती है, परंतु सुसमाचार की कहानी वास्तव में है क्या ? \r\n                   सुसमाचार शब्द यूनानी शब्द युऐन्गलिओन का अनुवाद है जिसका अर्थ होता है? शुभ संदेश अतः जब बाइबल यीशु के सुसमाचार के बारे में बात करती है तो यह यीशु के बारे में शुभ संदेश को दर्शाती है।', 9, '2020-07-03 13:43:24', '2020-07-09 03:24:41', NULL),
(1667, 489, 757, 'संयोजन :- जब हम सुसमाचार के संयोजन के बारे में बात करते हैं तो हमारे मन में यह बात है कि वह किस प्रकार से लिखे गए हैं उनके लेखक कौन थे उन्होंने इन पुस्तकों को क्यों लिखा उन्होंने यह पुस्तकें कैसे लिखी मसीहो के लिए इन जैसे प्रश्नों को खोजना महत्वपूर्ण हैं। क्योंकि अनेक व्याख्या कारों ने इन पुस्तकों के दैवीय अधिकार को कम करने के लिए संयोजन की मानवीय प्रक्रिया पर ध्यान केंद्रित किया है। परंतु शुभ संदेश यह है कि सावधानी से की हुई जांच हमें इस बात के प्रति आश्वस्त होने का हर कारण प्रदान करती है कि सुसमाचार केवल मनुष्य द्वारा लिखित कृतिया ही नहीं है। बल्कि परमेश्वर का वचन भी है। \r\nहम तो सुसमाचारों के संयोजन से संबंधित तीन विषयों को देखेंगे । \r\n1 हम भिन्न सुसमाचारिक विवरणों के बीच पाए जाने वाले सामानताओ की जांच करेंगे। \r\n२ हम संयोजन के कुछ ऐसे सिद्धांतों का सर्वेक्षण करेंगे जिनका उदय इन समानता ओं को स्पष्ट करने के लिए हुआ है । \r\n३ हम उस निश्चित के बारे में कुछ टिप्पणियां करेंगे जिसके साथ हमें इन सिद्धांतों के प्रति प्रतिबद्ध रहना चाहिए। \r\nआईये, सुसमाचारों के बीच पाई जाने वाली समानताओ पर ध्यान देने के द्वारा आरंभ करें।\r\n1 समानताएं :- चाहे ये अलग-अलग लिखे गए हो फिर भी मती, मरकुस, लुका के सुसमाचार विवरणों को एक साथ रखा जाता है और उन्हें समदर्शी सुसमाचार कहा जाता है शब्द समदर्शी का अर्थ है। एक साथ देखना और इसे इसलिए इन समाचारों पर लागू किया जाता है। उनमें अधिकांश एक समान वर्णन पाए जाते हैं। उनमें यीशु के शब्दों और कार्यों के अनेक सामान वर्णन पाए जाते हैं और जब वे यीशु के समान कथनों को बताते हैं तो वे प्राय: समान शब्दों का भी इस्तेमाल करते हैं। उदाहरण के तौर पर लकवे के रोगी को यीशु द्वारा दी गई चंगाई  मती 9:6, मरकुस 2:10-11, लुका 5:24 इस उदाहरण मे, हम देखते हैं कि प्रत्येक समदर्शी सुसमाचार में चमत्कार की सामान कहानी का सामान शब्दों में वर्णन पाया जाता है। अन्य समांतर कहानियां 3 में से कम से कम दो समदर्शी सुसमाचारों में पाई जाती है। वह है कोड़ी को चंगा करना। कफरनहूंम मैं दुष्ट आत्मा को निकालना। पतरस की सास को चंगा करना झील में आए तूफान को शांत करना आदि उदाहरण को पाते है। \r\nसमदर्शी सुसमाचारों के विपरीत , यूहन्ना के सुसमाचार का अधिकांश विवरण बिल्कुल अलग है। जहां यूहन्ना  ने भी वर्णन किया कि यीशु पानी पर चला और उसने 5000 लोगों को भोजन खिलाया वहीं उसने ऐसी घटनाओं का वर्णन भी किया जो समदर्शी सुसमाचारों में नहीं पाए जाते । उदाहरण के तौर पर यीशु के, पानी को दाखरस में बदलने , सामरी स्त्री के साथ यीशु के वार्तालाप और मित्रों में से लार्जर को जीवित करने का विवरण दिया। \r\nयद्यपि यीशु की सेवा की और जीवन की कहानियां चारों समाचारों में भिन्नता से पाई जाती है। फिर भी चारों यीशु के बपतिस्मा , अपने चेलों के साथ  अंतिम भोज , क्रूस पर यीशु की मृत्यु और मृतकों से यीशु के पुनरूत्थान की गवाही देते हैं। सुसमाचार में पाई जाने वाली समानता और असमानता ओं ने कई प्रतिद्वंदी स्पष्टीकरण को प्रेरित किया है।\r\n२ संयोजन के सिद्धांत :- समदर्शी  सुसमाचारों के बीच पाई जाने वाली अनेक समानताओं के कारण विद्वानों ने उनके संयोजन है। इतिहास के बारे में कई सिद्धांत विकसित किए हैं। यह सिद्धांत प्राय: काफी जटिल होते हैं और जब हम पहले पहल उनका अध्ययन करना आरंभ करते हैं तो वह काफी असमंजस भरे हो सकते हैं। हम सबसे लोकप्रिय सिद्धांतों को इस प्रकार से सारगर्भित कर सकते हैं। अधिकांश व्याख्या कार मानते हैं कि मरकुस का सुसमाचार सबसे पहले लिखा गया था और फिर मती  और लूका ने और उसके विवरणों का इस्तेमाल किया शायद अन्य स्रोतों के विवरणों का भी। परंतु अन्य व्याख्याकार मानते हैं कि मति पहले लिखा गया था, और मरकुस ने मती के विवरणों का प्रयोग किया और लुक्का ने मती और मरकुस दोनों के विवरणों का इस्तेमाल किया और अन्य मानते हैं कि मती और लू का ऐसे स्रोतों पर आधारित थे जो अब हमारे पास नहीं है और की मरकुस ने उन दोनों के दोनों का इस्तेमाल किया जैसे कि आप देख सकते हैं इन सिद्धांतों की सामान्य विशेषताओं की तुलना करना भी कुछ असमंजस भरा हो सकता है।\r\nइसके विपरीत यूहन्ना का संयोजन काफी सरल है। अधिकांश व्याख्या कार सहमत होते हैं कि उसने पहली सदी के लगभग अंत में लिखा था और वह कम से कम एक और शायद सारे समदर्शी विवरणों से परिचित था। कभी-कभी या सुझाव दिया जाता है कि उसने उन सारे विवरणों को नहीं दोहराया जिनके बारे में वह जानता था कि वे समदर्शी विवरण में थे और इसलिए उसने उसे अतिरिक्त जानकारी को प्रदान करने का निर्णय किया जो उन समुदायों के लिए सबसे प्रासंगिक थी जिनमें वह सेवा करता था । \r\n३ निश्चिंतता :- आरंभ से ही हमें यह पहचान लेना चाहिए कि बाइबल के लेखकों ने प्राय: मौखिक और लिखित परंपराओं का इस्तेमाल किया और इस बात ने उनकी प्रेरणा या अधिकार से समझौता नहीं किया अतः सैद्धांतिक रूप से इस बात पर विश्वास करने में कुछ गलत नहीं है कि कोई सुसमाचार लेखक पहले से उपलब्ध स्रोत पर निर्भर था जैसे कि लुका ने लुका 1:1-3 में लिखा।।\r\nऐसा प्रतीत होता है बाकी सारे सुसमाचार लेखकों के पास भी ऐसे ही स्रोतों की पहुंच थी। यद्यपि वे स्पष्ट रूप से लुका के समान इसका उल्लेख नहीं करते यदि हम अधिकांश व्याख्या कारों के साथ यह मान लें कि मरकुस ने सबसे पहले सुसमाचार लिखा तो उसके पास पहले से लिखे सुसमाचारों की पहुंच नहीं थी। परंतु उसने मौखिक परंपराओं को निश्चित रूप से इस्तेमाल किया कम से कम अपने घनिष्ठ मित्र पतरस से तो अवश्य ही किया । लुका और मति ने शायद एक नमूने के रूप में मरकुस के सुसमाचार का प्रयोग किया। इसके अतिरिक्त मती और यूहन्ना के पास यीशु के जीवन और उसकी शिक्षाओं की अपनी स्मृतियां थी और सभी चारों सुसमाचार लेखकों पर पवित्र आत्मा का नियन्त्रण था। \r\nसारांश में हम सुसमाचारों के बीच पाए जाने वाले संबंध के विषय के सिद्धांतों की सराहना कर सकते हैं परंतु हमें उनके सारे विवरणों को समझने की जरूरत महसूस नहीं करनी चाहिए और ना ही उनमें से किसी एक पर पूरी तरह निर्भर रहना चाहिए। यह सिद्धांत हमें यह बताते हैं कि प्रत्येक सुसमाचार प्रचारक के पास अनेक स्रोतों से जानकारी प्राप्त करने और यीशु के जीवन और शिक्षाओं के विश्वसनीय विवरणों की रचना करने की योग्यता थी जब हम उनके विवरणों में एक समान बातों को पाते हैं तो हमारे पास तो समाचारों के भिन्न-भिन्न दृष्टिकोण ओ पर ध्यान देने का अवसर होता है। फिर इसका कोई महत्व नहीं रहता कि कौन सा किस से पहले लिखा गया था और जब हम ऐसे विवरणों को पाते हैं जो केवल एक ही सुसमाचार में पाया जाता है तो हम उसका अध्ययन उस लेखक के उद्देश्यों के प्रकाश में कर सकते हैं।\r\nप्रमाणिकता :- कलीसिया की आरंभिक सदियों में, इस विषय में कुछ असहमतिय थी कि प्रेरितिक युग की  कौन सी पुस्तकके नए नियम से संबंधित है कुछ आरंभिक कलीसियाई अगुवो ने उन सारी पुस्तकों की पुष्टि नहीं की थी जो आज हम नए नियम में पाते हैं। अन्य लोगों ने माना था कि हमें वर्तमान की 27 पुस्तकों से अतिरिक्त पुस्तकों को भी शामिल करना चाहिए। परंतु इन विवादों में मति, मरकुस ,लुका और यूहन्ना की पुस्तकें शामिल नहीं थी। इन चारों  सुसमाचारों इनके अतिरिक्त कोई और नहीं - को सदैव परमेश्वर की विश्वासयोग्य कलीसियाओ के द्वारा विशुद्ध और अधिकारपूर्ण रूप में स्वीकार किया गया।\r\n            उदाहरण के रूप, में तीसरी सदी के कलीसियाई पूर्वज ओरिगेन, जिसका जीवनकाल 185 से 254 ईसवी तक था , ने तर्क दिया कि नए नियम में जो चार सुसमाचार आज हमारे पास है। वही प्रमाणिक है \r\nओरीगेन को कलीसिया इतिहासकार यूसेबियास, जिसका जीवनकाल 263 से 340 ईसवी तक था द्वारा उद्धृत किया गया अपनी कृति 1 ऐकलेसियार्टिकल हिस्ट्री पुस्तक 6 अध्याय 25 खंड 4 में  द्वारा ऑरिगेन के लिए कहे गए शब्द - आकाश के नीचे परमेश्वर की कलीसिया में केवल चार सुसमाचार •••• ही निर्विवाद है।', 9, '2020-07-03 13:46:08', '2020-07-09 03:24:41', NULL),
(1668, 489, 758, 'भिन्नता:- चारों सुसमाचार परमेश्वर के राज्य के आगमन के बारे में समान कहानी बताते हैं, परंतु प्रत्येक इसे अपने ही रूप में बताता है। हम दोनों के रूपों में इस भिन्नता की खोज करेंगे। \r\n1.हम सुसमाचार के विवरणों  में सामंजस्य स्थापित करने में आने वाली प्रत्यक्ष कठिनाइयों को देखेंगे। 2.हम प्रत्येक सुसमाचार के भिन्न महत्व को देखेंगे। आइए प्रत्यक्ष कठिनाइयों के साथ आरंभ करें।\r\n1.प्रत्यक्ष कठिनाइयां :- जब हम सुसमाचार को पढ़ते हैं तो तीव्र प्रभाव हम पाते हैं। वह यह है कि वे एक दूसरे के कितने समान हैं, परंतु ऐसे कई स्थान हैं जहां सुसमाचार के वर्णन भिन्न-भिन्न बातें कहते प्रतीत होते हैं निसंदेह इनमें से अधिकांश भिन्नता  इतनी सूक्ष्म है कि उन्हें गंभीरता के साथ विरोधाभास नहीं कहा जा सकता, परंतु कुछ भिन्नताएं अवश्य पाठकों को परेशान करती है। इसलिए यह महत्वपूर्ण है कि हम उन कुछ महत्वपूर्ण प्रत्यक्ष कठिनाइयों पर ध्यान दें।\r\n(A) घटनाक्रम :- सबसे अभिनेता ने घटनाक्रम से संबंधित है अर्थात उस क्रम से जिनमें घटनाओं का वर्णन बिन्नू समाचारों में किया गया है। जीवन कथा के विवरणों के रूप में प्रत्येक सुसमाचार एक जैसी आधारभूत समय रेखा का अनुसरण करता है। प्रत्येक यीशु के जन्म से आरंभ होती है और उसकी मृत्यु की ओर बढ़ती है और अंत में उसके पुलिस थान की ओर परंतु वे यीशु के जीवन की अन्य घटनाओं का वर्णन भिन्न क्रम में करते हैं। इसका कारण यह है कि सुसमाचार कभी-कभी अपनी प्रमुख अदाओं के अनुसार घटनाओं को एक साथ जोड़ते हैं जो कि पहली सदी में स्वीकार योग्य था, परंतु शायद वर्तमान की अपेक्षाओं को पूरा ना करें। सटीक रूप से घटनाक्रम का अनुसरण करने की अपेक्षा सुसमाचार कभी-कभी विषय या भौगोलिक स्थिति के अनुसार अपने बृत्तांतो को आते हैं। उदाहरण के तौर पर मरकुस ने मरकुस 6;1-6 में यीशु के अपने ही तरह नगर में निरादर पाने की कहानी बताई। पंतुलु का ने अपने विवरण में इससे पहले रखा। लुका 4:14 - 30 में , जिससे कि यह यीशु की सार्वजनिक सेवकाई की पहली कहानी बनी। लुका का सुसमाचार इस कहानी को मरकुस से अधिक प्रमुखता देता है और यह निरादर के विषय पर अधिक बल देने के लिए कहानी के लंबे संस्करण को दर्शाता है।\r\n(B) विलोपन :- दूसरे प्रकार की भिन्नता एक या अधिक सुसमाचारों में विवरणों का लोप या अनुपस्थिति है। उदाहरण के तौर पर युहना अपने सुसमाचार में प्रभु भोज के संस्कार का उल्लेख नहीं करता। इस प्रकार के लोगों को कई रूपों में समझा जा सकता है। यह शायद भिन्न लेखकों द्वारा दिए जाने वाले महत्व के फल स्वरुप हो सकते हैं या फिर यह इसके फलस्वरूप भी हो सकता है कि शायद बाद के सुसमाचार लेखकों ने उन भागों को दोहराने की जरूरत महसूस नहीं की जो पहले के सुसमाचार लेखकों की पुस्तकों में उपस्थित थे। चाहे जो भी कारण हो विलोपनो  का अर्थ सुसमाचार लेखकों के बीच असहमतिया या विरोधाभास नहीं है।\r\n                  पवित्रशास्त्र समय-समय पर इसे प्रत्यक्ष रूप से करता है। उदाहरण के तौर पर (2 इतिहास 9:29) \r\n(C) भिन्न घटनाएं :- एक तीसरे प्रकार की प्रत्यक्ष कठिनाई यीशु मसीह की सेवकाई में घटी भिन्न घटनाओं में पाई जाने वाली सामान,ताओं से आती है। कहने का अर्थ यह है कि कभी-कभी दो सुसमाचार सामान घटना को भिन्न रूपों में दर्शाते प्रतीत होते हैं। परंतु वे वास्तव में शायद दो एक जैसी परंतु भिन्न घटनाओं को दिखाते हैं। \r\n               यह याद रखना महत्वपूर्ण है कि यीशु एक भरमणशाली प्रचारक था अर्थात वह एक स्थान से दूसरे स्थान पर विचरण करता रहा। उसने कई अलग-अलग स्थानों में कई एक जैसे चमत्कार किए। कई लोगों को चंगा किया जो अंधे लंगड़े थे और नहीं संदेश सुनें। एक ही जैसे कई प्रश्नों और चुनौतियों को का बार-बार उत्तर दिया। इसके अतिरिक्त कई अवसरों पर लोगों ने सामान रूपों में यीशु को प्रत्युत्तर दिया। लुका 7:36 से 50 और मरकुस 14:3-9 में यीशु का अभिषेक करने के गुणों पर ध्यान दीजिए। लुका में इस व्यक्ति के घर में है परंतु उसमें वह शिमोन के घर में है। यह एक ही घटना के दो विरोधाभास नहीं है बल्कि विभिन्न घटनाओं के विवरण है।\r\n(D) भिन्न कथन :- चौथे प्रकार की प्रत्यक्ष  कठिनाई सामान बातों के भिन्न कथनों द्वारा उत्पन्न किया गया। असमंजस है। इसका सबसे सर्वोत्तम ज्ञात उदाहरण मती 5 :1 से 7 के यीशु के पहाड़ी संदेश लुका का 6:17 से 49 में लुका द्वारा दर्शाई गई सामान शिक्षाएं हैं। मति 5:1 में हमें बताया गया है कि यह घटना एक पहाड़ी पर घटी ।  परन्तु,लुका 6:17 हमें बताया गया है कि यह घटना एक समतल मैदान मे घटी। \r\n                  सूसमाचारों में सामंजस्य बैठाने में भिन्न तरीकों पर ध्यान देने के द्वारा हम इस बात के प्रति आश्वस्त हो सकते हैं कि यीशु के जीवन और सेवकाई उनकी संगठित गवाही सच्ची है। हां, विवरणों में भिन्नता अवश्य है। और जब हम या पाते हैं कि इस उन्हें विभिन्न अवसरों पर एक ही बात को सिखाया तो हम उसकी सेवकाई और उसके संदेश की निरंतरता को देख सकते हैं और हमारे जीवन में उसकी शिक्षाओं को लागू करने के भिन्न तरीकों को पा सकते हैं।\r\n(E) भिन्न प्रभाव :- क्योंकि प्रत्येक सुसमाचार एक भिन्न लेखक के द्वारा लिखा गया जिसने यीशु के जीवन और सेवकाई के अपने विवरण में अपने दृष्टिकोण और विषयों को डाला। इसलिए चारों सुसमाचारों में भिन्नताए पाई जाती है। यह जानने से कि चारों सुसमाचार पवित्र आत्मा के द्वारा प्रेरणा प्राप्त है। हम इस बात के प्रति आश्वस्त हैं कि हर विवरण त्रुटि रहित है और इसलिए दूसरे विवरण का विरोधाभासी नहीं है। परंतु इसका अर्थ यह नहीं है कि उनमें कोई भी भिन्नता नहीं है। पवित्र आत्मा ने मानवीय लेखकों के व्यक्तित्व रुचि हूं और सेवकाई की परिस्थितियों का इस्तेमाल उन भिन्नताओं को आकार देने के लिए किया था। यदि हम उन सारे रूपों में आशीष पाना चाहते हैं, जिनमें पवित्र आत्मा हमें आशीष  करना चाहता है तो हमें सुसमाचारों को पढ़ते समय प्रत्येक सुसमाचार के प्रस्ताव पर ध्यान देना होगा।\r\n2,(A) मत्ती में यीशु कौन है ? :- सारे सुसमाचार लेखकों में मति ऐसा है जो इस बात को बताने में अधिक रुचि रखता है कि इसराइल का वह मसीहा रूपी राजा है जिसकी भविष्यवाणी पुराने नियम में की गई थी।\r\n(B) मरकुस में यीशु कौन है? :- अपने पूरे विवरण में मरकुस ने बल दिया कि यीशु परमेश्वर का दुख उठाने वाला पुत्र था जिसने परमेश्वर के लोगों के शत्रुओं पर विजय प्राप्त की। मरकुस ने यशु के चमत्कारों के अनेक उदाहरण प्रस्तुत किए और उनके द्वारा दुष्ट की शक्तियों पर उसकी सामर्थ्य को दर्शाया।\r\n(C) लुका में यीशु कौन है? :- लुका का सुसमाचार यीशु कौन है के प्रश्न का उत्तर या घोषणा करने के द्वारा देता है कि वह संसार का करुणामय या तरस खाने वाला उद्धार करता है। इसने अमीरों और गरीबों धार्मिक अगुवो और सामाजिक रूप से पिछड़ों को एक समान रूप से परमेश्वर का उद्धार प्रदान किया। यीशु का शुभ संदेश सब लोगों के लिए था और कुछ समझे जाने वालों के लिए भी लुका ने कई रूपों में इस पर बल दिया।\r\n(D) युहन्न में यीशु कौन है? :-  युहन्न अपने सुसमाचार म यशु को परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में चित्रित किया जो उद्धार की अनन्त योजना को पूरा करता है। परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में यीशु की पहचान पर बल देते हुए युहना ने पिता के साथ परमेश्वर के आदित्य संबंध के बारे में बात की। इस व अपने पिता का संपूर्ण प्रकाशन है और वही एकमात्र है जो उन सब को अनंत जीवन प्रदान कर सकता है जो उस पर अपना भरोसा रखते हैं। उदाहरण के लिए जहां अन्य सुसमाचारों ने यीशु के जन्म और पृथ्वी पर उसकी सेवकाई के साथ अपने विवरणों को आरंभ किया, वहीं यूहन्ना ने अपने सुसमाचार का आरम्भ यह कहते हुए कहा कि परमेश्वर का पुत्र पिता के साथ सृष्टि की रचना में शामिल था और अब पिता अपने इकलौते पुत्र के माध्यम से प्रकट किया जा रहा था।', 9, '2020-07-03 13:48:20', '2020-07-09 03:24:41', NULL),
(1669, 489, 759, 'सुसमाचार लेखकों के पास उनके द्वारा लिखी घटनाओं के विवरणों तक पहुंच थी आज के समय के समान प्राचीन संसार भी विश्वासनीय इतिहासकारों से अपेक्षा रखता था कि उनके पास उनके विषय से जुड़ी अनेक बातों तक पहुंच हो यदि कोई व्यक्ति इतिहास लिखना चाहता है तो यह सबसे महत्वपूर्ण और आवश्यक है कि उसके पास सब प्रकार की पुस्तकों की भरमार हो।प्लूतार्क ने यहां पर मजबूती से यह माना कि विश्वासनीय है। इतिहासकारों की विश्वसनीय स्रोतों तक पहुंच होनी चाहिए। \r\n               प्रत्येक सुसमाचार लेखक या तो यीशु के जीवन का गवाह था या यीशु के जीवन के किसी गवाह के साथ उसका सीधा संबंध था। क्योंकि मती और यूहना यशु के चेले थे, इसलिए वे उनमे से अनेक घटनाओ के समय स्वय उपस्थित थे जिनका उन्होंने वर्णन किया है। मरकुस, पतरस का अच्छा सहकर्मी था। और उसने उससे प्रत्यश्र रुप से  काफ़ी कुछ सीखा था। लूका ने पौलुस के संग यात्रा की थी और अपने सुसमाचार के लिए विश्वसनीय गवाहिया प्राप्त की थी।२. स्पष्टवादीता :- हम  सुसमाचारों की ऐतिहासिक विश्वासनीयता को उनके कार्यों में उच्च स्तर की स्पष्टवादीता में भी देख सकते हैं। अच्छे इतिहास लेखन के लिए प्राचीन स्थलों ने इतिहासकारों से अपने इतिहास के वर्णन में निष्पक्षता या ईमानदार रहने की मांग की थी उनसे विवरणों की पूरी श्रणी का ब्यौरा देने की अपेक्षा की जाती थी। उन बातों के बारे में भी जो दिए जाने वाले संदेश के अनुकूल ना भी हो तो भी \r\n      इस भाव में यह महत्वपूर्ण है कि सुसमाचार लेखकों ने नियमित रूप से यीशु के चेलों की असफलता का वर्णन किया।और मति एवं यूहना के विषय में इसका अर्थ है उनकी अपनी व्यक्तिगत असफलताओं का वर्णन करना और यदि कुछ व्याख्याकारों का अनुमान सही है तो मरकुस 14:51-52 में गतसमने के बाग से नंगा भागने वाला युवक स्वयं मरकुस ही है। इसका अर्थ है कि  मरकुस ने भी अपनी ही कमियों का वर्णन किया और बिना किसी अपवाद के सभी सुसमाचार लेखकों ने एक रूप में यीशु के चेलों की असफलताओं को प्रकट किया और माना कि उनके छोटे कलीसीयाई आंदोलन के अगवे सिद्ध नहीं थे।\r\n             सुसमाचार लेखकों की विश्वासनीयता में हमारा विश्वास अन्य ऐतिहासिक स्रोतों के पुष्टिकरण से मजबूत होता है। रोमी और यहूदी इतिहासकारों ने सुसमाचारों के विवरणों के अनेक दावों की पुष्टि की है और आधुनिक पुरातत्व विज्ञान ने भी इस बात का प्रमाण पाया है कि उनके विवरण सत्य हैं । \r\n                        सुसमाचार विवरणों पर भरोसा करने का  कारण यह है कि जो प्रशिक्षण यीशु के चेलों ने प्राप्त किया था उसे उन्हें सिखा दिया होगा कि किस प्रकार उसके शब्दों और कार्यों को अच्छी तरह से संभाल कर रखें। \r\nयहूदी संस्कृति में शिष्यता या चेलापन जीवन का एक स्थापित मार्ग था वास्तव में चेले के लिए इब्रानी शब्द तलमीद है जिसका अर्थ है विद्यार्थी या सीखने वाला। विशेष तौर से चेला एक विशेष संत या रब्बी का विद्यार्थी होता था। इससे बढ़कर यीशु के समय कि यहूदी संस्कृति में रब्बी से सीखने का एक मुख्य कार्य कंठस्थ करना था और उसके चेलों की मुख्य जिम्मेदारी अपने शिक्षक के शब्दों और उसकी बुद्धि को सीखना थी। लुका 6:40 मे अपने चेलों से कहने का यीशु का अर्थ था कि जो भी उसका अनुसरण करते हैं उन्हें उस की शिक्षाओं और उसके कार्यों का अध्ययन करना उन्हें सिखाना और उनके अनुसार अपने जीवन को ढालना आवश्यक है। यीशु के करीब रहने वाले 12 चेलों पर यीशु की शिक्षाओं को सीखने की बड़ी जिम्मेदारी थी। वहीं अनेक लोगों ने जिन्होंने यिशु से शिक्षा प्राप्त की, उन्होंने अपनी याददाश्त में उसकी अधिकांश शिक्षा को बनाए रखा।\r\n             सुसमाचार लेखकों में मजबूत धर्म वैज्ञानिक बोध थे। जिन्होंने एक सच्चे और विश्वासनीय विवरण की आवश्यकता पर बल दिया उदाहरण के तौर पर यूहन्ना 20:310 में प्रेरित ने लिखे इस अनुच्छेद में  यूहन्ना ने स्पष्ट रूप से कह दिया कि लोग परमेश्वर के जीवन के वरदान को तभी प्राप्त कर सकते हैं। जब उन्होंने यीशु के बारे में सत्य को जान लिया हो और उसे स्वीकार कर लिया हो । उदाहरण मती 28:19-20\r\n               यीशु के शब्दों और कार्यों के विवरण को लिखने के लिए सुसमाचार के लेखकों को उन्हीं की सामर्थ पर नहीं छोड़ दिया गया था। इस प्रयास में पवित्र आत्मा ने उनकी अगुवाई की थी। \r\nपवित्रशास्त्र की प्रेरणा एक बहुत ही महत्वपूर्ण धर्म शिक्षा है। क्योंकि यह सारे पवित्रशास्त्र का एक ही लेखक बताती है अतः जब हम सुसमाचारों की ओर देखते हैं और पाते हैं कि चार अलग-अलग लेखक यीशु के चार अलग-अलग दृष्टिकोण प्रदान करते हैं तो हमें उन दृष्टिकोण  की प्रशंसा करनी चाहिए परंतु इसके साथ-साथ यह भी महसूस करना चाहिए कि पवित्रआत्मा ने उन सब को प्रेरित किया है और इसलिए वह सब अलग-अलग लक्ष्यों , धर्म विज्ञानों, श्रोताओं ,पृष्ठभूमिओ और यीशु के साथ अपने अलग-अलग लक्ष्यों के साथ आते हैं। परंतु जब मानवी लेखकों के आधार पर हम उनमें विविधता को पाते हैं। वहीं उनमें एक आदित्य एकता भी पाते हैं। पवित्रशास्त्र में आत्मा की प्रेरणा उसमें से मानवीय घटक या मानवीय कार्य को हटाती नहीं परंतु इसका अर्थ यह है कि परमेश्वर इन मानवीय प्रयासों के माध्यम से उन्हीं बातों को रखता है जिन्हें वह चाहता है । यूहना 14 : 25 - 26', 9, '2020-07-03 13:59:07', '2020-07-09 03:24:41', NULL),
(1670, 489, 760, 'चारों सुसमाचार परमेश्वर के राज्य के आगमन के बारे में समान कहानी बताते हैं, परंतु प्रत्येक इसे अपने ही रूप में बताता है। हम दोनों के रूपों में इसकी खोज करेंगे। \r\n             जब हम सुसमाचार को पढ़ते हैं तो तीव्र प्रभाव हम पाते हैं। वह यह है कि वे एक दूसरे के कितने समान हैं, परंतु ऐसे कई स्थान हैं जहां सुसमाचार के वर्णन भिन्न-भिन्न बातें कहते प्रतीत होते हैं निसंदेह इनमें से अधिकांश भिन्नता  इतनी सूक्ष्म है कि उन्हें गंभीरता के साथ विरोधाभास नहीं कहा जा सकता, परंतु कुछ भिन्नताएं अवश्य पाठकों को परेशान करती है। इसलिए यह महत्वपूर्ण है कि हम उन कुछ महत्वपूर्ण प्रत्यक्ष कठिनाइयों पर ध्यान दें।\r\n                       जीवन कथा के विवरणों के रूप में प्रत्येक सुसमाचार एक जैसी आधारभूत समय रेखा का अनुसरण करता है। प्रत्येक यीशु के जन्म से आरंभ होती है और उसकी मृत्यु की ओर बढ़ती है और अंत में उसके  की ओर परंतु वे यीशु के जीवन की अन्य घटनाओं का वर्णन भिन्न क्रम में करते हैं। इसका कारण यह है कि सुसमाचार कभी-कभी अपनी प्रमुख अदाओं के अनुसार घटनाओं को एक साथ जोड़ते हैं जो कि पहली सदी में स्वीकार योग्य था\r\n                    यह शायद भिन्न लेखकों द्वारा दिए जाने वाले महत्व के फल स्वरुप हो सकते हैं या फिर यह इसके फलस्वरूप भी हो सकता है कि शायद बाद के सुसमाचार लेखकों ने उन भागों को दोहराने की जरूरत महसूस नहीं की जो पहले के सुसमाचार लेखकों की पुस्तकों में उपस्थित थे। चाहे जो भी कारण हो विलोपनो  का अर्थ सुसमाचार लेखकों के बीच असहमतिया या विरोधाभास नहीं है।\r\n                  पवित्रशास्त्र समय-समय पर इसे प्रत्यक्ष रूप से करता है। \r\n                      यीशु के जीवन और सेवकाई के अपने विवरण में अपने दृष्टिकोण और विषयों को डाला। इसलिए चारों सुसमाचारों में भिन्नताए पाई जाती है। यह जानने से कि चारों सुसमाचार पवित्र आत्मा के द्वारा प्रेरणा प्राप्त है। हम इस बात के प्रति आश्वस्त हैं कि हर विवरण त्रुटि रहित है और इसलिए दूसरे विवरण का विरोधाभासी नहीं है। परंतु इसका अर्थ यह नहीं है कि उनमें कोई भी भिन्नता नहीं है। पवित्र आत्मा ने मानवीय लेखकों के व्यक्तित्व रुचि हूं और सेवकाई की परिस्थितियों का इस्तेमाल उन भिन्नताओं को आकार देने के लिए किया था। यदि हम उन सारे रूपों में आशीष पाना चाहते हैं, जिनमें पवित्र आत्मा हमें आशीष  करना चाहता है । \r\n                      जीवन कथा के विवरणों के रूप में प्रत्येक सुसमाचार एक जैसी आधारभूत समय रेखा का अनुसरण करता है। प्रत्येक यीशु के जन्म से आरंभ होती है और उसकी मृत्यु की ओर बढ़ती है और अंत में उसके पुलिस थान की ओर परंतु वे यीशु के जीवन की अन्य घटनाओं का वर्णन भिन्न क्रम में करते हैं। इसका कारण यह है कि सुसमाचार कभी-कभी अपनी प्रमुख अदाओं के अनुसार घटनाओं को एक साथ जोड़ते हैं जो कि पहली सदी में स्वीकार योग्य था।', 8, '2020-07-03 14:15:05', '2020-07-09 03:24:41', NULL),
(1671, 483, 791, 'Sin is any want of conformity unto, or transgression of, the law of God.\r\nHumanity fell into sin early in our existence. The first two human beings Adam an Eve were created sinless. They had no predisposition to sin  and no reason to sin.\r\nThey had every reason to continue in his blessings and to avoid his covenant curses. They were to rule over the other creatures God had created, they had to work in the garden of Eden. We see it all in Genesis 1 and 2.\r\nBut in Genesis 3:1-7 , the serpent tempted Eve to eat the forbidden fruit, and she did. Then she gave it too Adam  and he ate it too.\r\nGenesis doesn\'t claim that the tree had any power to make human beings sinful.Instead , it was Adam\'s and Eve\'s disloyalty that led to their sense of guilt and shame.  Genesis 3:8-24 . Immediately they realized they were naked and felt shame.God confronted Adam and Eve, cursed them because of their disloyalty. \r\nThis collection of events from the serpents\'s temptation through God\'s judgement- \"the fall\".', 8, '2020-07-04 17:53:57', '2020-07-09 03:25:04', NULL),
(1672, 483, 792, 'Authorship of human refers to who is ultimately to blame for it.\r\nAdam and Eve tried to blame to someone else for their sin:\r\nAdam explicitly blamed eve and implicitly blamed God who made created her(Genesis 3:12)\r\nEve blamed the serpent(Genesis 3:13)\r\nThe serpent was the ultimate author of sin because it was the first to come up with the idea to sin and the first to try to cause humanity to sin.\r\nAdam and Eve freely chose to sin and in this sense , authored human sin.\r\nGod isn\'t culpable or guilty of sin or of compelling anyone to sin (1John 1:5)\r\nGod hates sin and can\'t be tempted by sin (Deuteronomy 25:16;Psalms 5:4, Zechariah 8:17, James 1:13)\r\nGod is light; in him there is no darkness at all( 1 John 1:5)\r\n  God is free from sin , God hates sin and God is powerful enough to prevent sin.\r\nGod himself is the ultimate standard of good and evil. There is no ultimate moral standard outside him that can judge him.', 7, '2020-07-04 18:08:13', '2020-07-09 03:25:04', NULL),
(1673, 483, 793, 'The original sin refers to the consequences of humanity\'s first sin.The condition into which Adam\'s natural descendants are born as a result of Adam\'s fall into sin.\r\nCORRUPTION:\r\n1.Concepts:Sin has damaged our capacity for conceptual thought and caused us to believe that false ideas are true(Ecclesiastes 9:3,Jeremiah !7:9: Deuteronomy 29:2-4: John *:43_47: Ephesians 4:17-18)It\'s not sinful to misunderstand difficult concepts, but it is sinful to affirm false doctrine and unbiblical ways of thinking(! timothy 6:3-5)\r\n2.Behaviors: Adam and eve\'s sin served as the model for all the behavioral sins that have plagued humanity since.\r\nGod has given fallen humanity over to its sinful appetites(Romans 1:29-32)\r\n3. Emotions : Sin prevents us from loving God and our neighbors as we should, and from manifesting other righteous emotions .Every human beings struggles with coveting, lust , pride hatred , anger and other sinful emotions (Mark 7:21-22, James 1:14-15)', 8, '2020-07-04 18:22:13', '2020-07-09 03:25:04', NULL),
(1674, 483, 794, 'In Genesis 2:17, God told Adam that if he ate the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of Good and Evil, he would die.then after Adam  ate the fruit, God cursed Adam to physical death. But Adam did not die immediately when God cursed him, at least not physically.And the same thing is true of the rest of us. God permits us a physical lifespan on earth. But scripture does imply that Adam died spiritually when he was cursed and that his natural descendants are spiritually dead before they come to faith.If Christ is not in us , we are spiritually dead.\r\n We have spiritual life when we have Christ in us. Ephesians 2:1-5 says that God made us alive with Christ even when we were dead in transgressions. All fallen human beings share this spiritually dead condition until we receive spiritual life in Christ (Romans 8:10).By God\'s grace , we can struggle against sin\'s influence now and completely escape in the future.', 8, '2020-07-04 18:36:24', '2020-07-09 03:25:04', NULL),
(1675, 483, 795, 'Nothing that happens is outside God\'s plan or control. So he certainly had a reason for allowing human sin.We can affirm that our sin gives him the opportunity to express many of his attributes that would be hidden from us if we never sinned. Sometimes he expresses mercy and forbearance in him response to human sin and at other times , he express wrath.\r\nUltimately sin works through the benefit if believers , making it a useful part of his plan to bless us.Romans 8:28 \r\nEverything God does is right and good. human sin provides an occasion of God to reveal his glory, to express his mercy and compassion through forgiveness and to express his justice and wrath through judgement.  \r\nSo I would explain them , it was Adam\'s choice , he had no compulsion to disobey God, so man was fully responsible for choosing to sin and suffer pain , which resulted in physical death. God is always good that He sustained human beings and redeemed us, giving us eternal life.', 9, '2020-07-04 18:53:11', '2020-07-09 03:25:04', NULL),
(1676, 486, 665, 'The term \"diachronic \"derives from two Greek word: first, the preposition \"dia\" which often means \"through\"or \"throughout\": and second, the Greek noun Chronos which means time.\r\nDiachrony is a concern with the passage of time. In the case of the Biblical theology, the term \"diachronics\" points to the way Old Testament Theology transformed, changed,or developed throughout time.\r\nDiachronic approaches to the Bible concentrate on how theological structures progressively unfolded through time. A diachronic approach however, is much more concerned with changes that occurred in theological structures\r\nfor example it asks questions like\"How did God\'s revelation at the burning bush anticipate his work in Egypt?\"These type of issues become of central importance in diachronic approaches to this part of Old Testament.', 8, '2020-07-05 18:15:33', '2020-07-09 03:25:27', NULL),
(1677, 486, 666, 'We use term development instead of simply speaking of diachronic changes to suggest two main ideas. First, changes in Old Testament theological structures always move towards fulfilling God\'s purposes for history. And Second , we speak of developments because theological changes only occur through God\'s providential involvement in history. \r\nDivine purposes:\r\nThe Scripture affirm that everything in history, including shifts in theology, always accomplish God\'s unfailing purposes for his creation.Isaiah 46:10.God\'s goals for history exist not only as broad , long -term goals but also as particular , short term goals.God also has an all -encompassing purpose for history.God began history with great destiny in mind and every event in history will, without fail , reach his glorious end.\r\nDivine Providence:\r\nThe road of the Old Testament is actually filled with steep inclines , fast descents, and sharp turns to the left and to the right. these abrupt shifts are caused by God\'s providence, his complex involvement with His creation.God wanted these theological shifts to take place.\r\nGod offered the first generation of Exodus , the possession of the promised land , but their infidelity led to their rejection . yet none of these human changes were outside of God\'s Sovereign control.', 9, '2020-07-05 18:32:14', '2020-07-09 03:25:27', NULL),
(1678, 486, 667, 'There were six times when God established major covenants with distinctive theological emphasis.\r\nTHE COVENANTS WITH\r\n1. ADAM\r\n2. NOAH\r\n3, ABRAHAM. \r\n4. MOSES\r\n5. DAVID\r\n6. NEW COVENANT\r\nTHE SIX OLD TESTAMENT COVENANTS FALL INTO THREE CATEGORIES:\r\nTHE UNIVERSAL COVENANT: The covenants with Adam and Noah is referred as \"universal \" because they were made between God and all  of humanity.\r\nTHE NATIONAL COVENANT:\r\nGod established national covenants with his special people Israel: the covenants with Abraham , Moses and David.\r\nGod narrowed his covenantal attention primarily to just one ethnic group establishing Israel as the nation that would lead the rest of humanity in service to God. \r\nTHE NEW COVENANT:\r\nThe new covenant was designed to govern God\'s people, when God fulfilled his promise to re-establish his people after exile and to spread his kingdom through them to the ends of the earth. and for this reason we may speak of the new covenant as the covenant of fulfillment.', 9, '2020-07-05 18:45:17', '2020-07-09 03:25:27', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(1679, 486, 668, 'Biblical typology is the study of diachronic developments between the theological structures closely associated with significant persons,institutions and events in Scripture.\r\nTypology is the study of types. \r\nTHE word \"types\" derives from Greek word \"tupos\" .\r\nRomans 5:14 we see that Paul declared Adam was a pattern of the one to come, but from the larger context we know that the one to come  is Christ.So in this case, Paul observed that Adam was a type of Christ. in biblical theology,the term typology applies to any diachronic development of topics in old testament theology.\r\nEvery trace of the historical stages of a topic forms typology in this general sense of the word.\r\nOn occasions , biblical theologians will speak of the typology of the doctrine of God, or typology of worship. ans simply mean that these are the ways these themes developed in the the Bible.', 8, '2020-07-05 18:57:29', '2020-07-09 03:25:27', NULL),
(1680, 486, 669, 'We should remember two things:\r\nfirst, we are not to turn back to living as if we are in an earlier covenant age, to do that would be to reject more recent, fuller revelations from God.\r\nSecondly , God\'s people now should never forget the wisdom of what God had taught had in earlier ages.\r\nThroughout, ages the instructions given regarding worship, sacrifice and temple were different.\r\nfor example during Moses time there was a tent of meeting and during Solomon\'s time onwards there was a temple. \r\nAt new covenant Christ has been offered as a sacrifice once and for all.(Hebrews 10:100\r\n Now there is no more sacrifice to be offered and we read in Romans 12:1 that our worship is o offer our bodies as living sacrifice. In Old Testament we had to offer sacrifice , now we are living sacrifice to God\r\nRegarding Temple, we read in 1 Corinthians 2:15 that Our body is the temple of God. \r\nIn New Covenant Christ is the Passover Lamb(John 1:29), and 1 Corinthains 5:7 we read that For even Christ our Passover is sacrificed for us and as we read in 1 Corinthians 11, we break bread and drink from the cup in remembrance of the Passover Lamb.', 9, '2020-07-05 19:16:16', '2020-07-09 03:25:27', NULL),
(1681, 485, 834, 'Bible is divinely inspired, it carries God\'s autority. God has all authority and has inspired the Scriptures, hence whoever hears God are obligated to obey him. \r\n\r\nBible claims divine authority for itself in two ways\r\n\r\n1) Historical examples claiming authority \r\n2) Explicitly claims authority\r\n\r\nGod spoke directly to humanity, when we consider the fall of man in the garden of Eden. God commanded man through spoken word to stay in the Garden of Eden and cultivate the land an not to partake from the tree of good and evil. But whereas Eve disobeyed and choose rather to listen to the Serpent, thereby rejecting the authority of God.\r\n\r\nWhen we consider the New Testament, Jesus frequently appealed to Scripture as God\'s authority to explain his actions.\r\n\r\nThe apostles also showed similar demonstrations in the Scriptures as God\'s authority. \r\n\r\nBible also provides authority through Explicit Statements\r\n\r\nJesus gave his apostles authority when he said in the Bible for e.g. in the Gospel of John 13\r\nWhover accepts anyone I send accepts me, and whoever accepts me accepts the one who sent me.\r\n\r\nThe Apostles used this authority to preach the Scriptures and also in writing the epistles that we have in the New Testament.\r\n\r\nImplications : \r\nScripture carries God\'s authority.  We can consider two points in this regard.\r\n\r\nWe need to keep and obey the word of God in it\'s entirety, by obeying all of it\'s commands. \r\nWe must also conform to these commandments by convictions and commitments in fulfilling the requirements in our practical life.\r\n\r\nFully obeying God\'s word without discarding any of God\'s commandments as mentioned in the Bible. \r\n\r\nJesus instructed his disciples in the Gospel of John : If you love me you will obey my commands. \r\n\r\nJesus himself demonstrated this love by obeying and fulfilling all the commands and requirements of the heavenly Father.', 0, '2020-07-08 15:18:30', '2020-07-08 15:18:30', NULL),
(1682, 485, 835, 'God gave us scripture that we may understand the things revealed in Scripture and apply them to our lives. \r\n\r\nIn God\'s revelation Scripture is not a secret. The Scriptures fall into the division of \"Things Revealed\". As Moses in the Old Testament said they are shown to us in order that we might follow and obey them.\r\n\r\nGod has give us sufficient clarity to guide us in ethics. Bible is God\'s word we can use for studying and reading - we can come to know God\'s will for all our life. \r\n\r\nApostle Paul exhorted Timothy & said in 2nd Timothy 3:16\r\nAll Scripture is useful for teaching, rebuking, correcting and training in righeousness.\r\n\r\nBy diligently studying the Scripture and applying in our individual lives, we can come to know God\'s will and tranform to God\'s standard for morality.\r\n\r\nFurthermore Scripture is also necessary for ethical decision making specially the 3 aspects we can consider\r\n\r\n1)Scripture for Salvation\r\nScripture is necessary for people to find the way to salvation. \r\nGospel message is the means by which God delivers faith to individuals.  Human beings by and large received the gospel and come to faith and salvation through the Scriptures. \r\n\r\n\r\n2)Scripture for Faithful Living\r\nScripture is necessary for ethical living. Scripture speaks clearly and directly to humans than most of the general and existential revelation. There is more genuinity and reliability in the scriptures for us to follow. \r\n\r\n\r\n3)Implications of our need for Scripture \r\n\r\nHuman standards are not good enough to set moral standards. We need Scripture to teach us and to guide us to maintain morality and godly behavior in the society. People ignoring the scripture is like a scenario wherein peple are waiting for accidents to happen that can easily destroy their lives. Scripture reveals God;s will in sufficient details to teach us what is right.', 0, '2020-07-08 15:35:17', '2020-07-08 15:35:17', NULL),
(1683, 485, 836, 'Scripture is sufficient to say that it is able to fulfill the purpose for which it is written.  The Bible was written to teach us how to glorify God, to bring men and women into faith and to pass on instructions to believers of how they should live their life of faith and to guide them for a true Christian way of life.\r\n\r\nApostle Paul instructed Timothy that the Holy Scriptures are able to make you wise for salvation through faith in Jesus Christ. \r\nPaul meant that by studying the Bible, we can learn the things that are necessary for us to know if we are to be saved. Bible is not only powerful but it was also designed to provide every believer who trusts God and obey\'s the scrpiture speciic benefits. \r\n\r\nScripture is also intended to prepare us for every good work, and as every scripture in itself as word of God is powerful to accomplish the task or function for which it is meant. \r\n\r\nRightly understand the Scriptures we will know God\'s standards to make proper determinations about any ethical issue as long as we also have a sufficient understnding of the persons and the situation.', 0, '2020-07-08 15:46:43', '2020-07-08 15:46:43', NULL),
(1684, 485, 837, 'Paul was not ashamed of the gospel and he was ever willing to preach the gospel to those in Rome, since it is the power of God to salvation for everyone who believes. \r\n\r\nThe gospel message is the normal means by which God delivers faith to individuals. And apart from the words of Christ people do not have any access to achieve eternity.  Those who believe in the Gospel is a necessary means to salvation in all even in the most exceptional circumstances. \r\n\r\nThe disciples of Jesus learned the gospel directly from the Lord, and then delivered it not only through preaching, but also through their writings in the New Testament.\r\n\r\nThe practical outworking of this process is that human beings who receives the knowledge of the gospel and thereby comes to faith and salvation through the Scripture either by studying on their own, or through preaching based on the Bible. \r\n\r\nThe implication is that by learning, understanding and believing the gospel is an important step to attain salvation. \r\n\r\nIn the above biblical reference Apostle Paul was every willing to be used by God to preach the gospel to everyone in Rome, both to the Jews and Greeks (gentiles). Through his own experiences Paul could testify that the Gospel is the power of God to salvation for those who blieve irrespective of their individual identity in terms of their nation, creed and race.', 0, '2020-07-08 16:02:10', '2020-07-08 16:02:10', NULL),
(1685, 485, 838, 'Bible contains a full range of language. It contans statements, questions, promises, offers curses, blessings, judgements, commands, advise, request, exclamations descriptions, cries, expression, desires, love and much more everything that can be considered in terms of language. Biblical language can be very emotionally reserved or charged. Using symbolism and other figures of speech. Some are expressed in a direct manner, whereas some are unimaginative. Bible uses both sarcasm and sincere language. \r\n\r\nExtraordinary\r\nThere are those who believe that the Bible speaks in extraordinary ways, they offer solutions that ignore the different types of lanugage. Instead they oversimplify biblical language in order to develop interpretation that gives the same explanation equally to all of Scripture. \r\nMany theologians believed that because Scriptures is inspired by God, it communicates in extraordinary ways that exceed human comprehension. Their way of thinking as biblical text contained at lease some metamorphic meaning regardless of the human author\'s intentions.\r\n\r\nOrdinary \r\nBible is not obscure, in other words it does not contain any hidden meanings which needs to be discovered through mysterious means. Neither it  needs special inclidining and can be understood by special offices in the church or a special office. \r\n\r\nScripture is clear, it speaks ordinary language and communicates in normal ways\r\n\r\nThe Bible uses the linguistic conventions of its authors and their original audiences.\r\n\r\nWe have always interpret the Bible responsibly, we have to learn how they ordinarily used language and have to understand what each author\'s intent was when he wrote.', 0, '2020-07-08 16:20:46', '2020-07-08 16:20:46', NULL),
(1686, 485, 839, 'The primacy of the Ten Commandments are both historical and theological. Their historical primacy depends on the fact that these laws were the first written legal code that was received by the nation of Israel. \r\n\r\nThis law inroduced 430 years later, does not set aside the covenant previously established by God. \r\n\r\nBut as per apostle Paul this was the first time Israel as a nation possessed God\'s laws.  God gave the laws to the nation of Israel through Moses at Mount Sinai. Israel was the first nation on the earth to possess an extensive, supernaturlly revealed code of God\'s requirements.\r\n\r\nGod himself wrote the Ten Commandments on stone tablets, by doing so God demonstrated that these laws were special among his laws and they deserved special attention and notice. \r\n\r\nThe Theological primacy is indicated by the special occassion God gave them the Ten Commandments in the midst of thunder, lightning, smoke and clouds on Mount Sinai. God spoke to his servant Moses, and was allowed to be viewed by Joshua and the 70 elders of Israel \r\n\r\nMoses identified the Ten Commandments as God\'s very covenant with his people. \r\n\r\nThe Ten commandments were also placed within the Ark of the covenant. \r\n\r\nAlso Jesus also mentioned about the Ten Commandments during his discussion with a man who asked him how to inherit eternal life. Jesus indicated by obeying the Ten Commandments, a person can earn eternal life. Jesus also in this discourse gave the importance to the Ten Commandments.', 0, '2020-07-08 16:37:47', '2020-07-08 16:37:47', NULL),
(1687, 485, 840, 'The three traditional types of law are \r\n\r\nMORAL LAW\r\nMoral laws are typically thought to convey God\'s ethical standards and are usually identified with Ten Commandments\r\n\r\nCEREMONIAL LAW\r\nThe laws instructing bleivers in worshiping God. Associated with Old Testament sacrificial system, and worship at the Temple.\r\n\r\nCIVIL LAWS \r\nCivil laws provide for the governing of society.\r\n\r\nThe traditional threefold category of laws are not taught in the Bible. But they did play an important role in church history.\r\n\r\nIn the Westminster Confession of Faith statement states \r\nAll Ceremonial laws are not valid \r\n\r\nThis statement reflects the fact since the death, burial, resurrection and ascension of Christ, God\'s people are no longer to perform any of the specific ceremonial requirements in the Mosaic sacrificial system. \r\n\r\nWith regards to Civil Laws the specific requirements of civil laws do not apply as they have expired.\r\n\r\nBelievers of the present age no longer have to behave in many of the ways specified in the Old Testament with regards to ceremony and civil government as these laws have been superseded by the fuller revelation of the New Testament\r\n\r\nBut for Civil laws, there are four reasons that Christians should still look to the civil and ceremonial laws of the Old testament as well as to its moral laws, for ethical guidance only. \r\n\r\n1)God\'s Character does not change, - it is our ultimate standard for ethics, Civil and Ceremonial laws still reveal our moral standard\r\n\r\n2)Scripture teaches the continuing modern application of every law.\r\n\r\n3)Bible consistently teaches that the law is a unified whole and it all stands together\r\n\r\n4) All of Scripture is for our moral instruction. It teaches us about modern ethics. \r\n\r\nAll of Scripture is useful for teaching, rebuking, correcting and training in righteousness', 0, '2020-07-08 16:57:11', '2020-07-08 16:57:11', NULL),
(1688, 485, 841, 'Though the believers of the present age need no longer are subject to Old Testament Civil and Ceremonial laws. But it is critical to realize that in another sense the Old Testament civil and ceremonial laws still apply to modern Christians. The civil and ceremonial laws still guide us as God\'s standard today, just as the moral laws do.\r\n\r\nWe need to consider four reasons that Christians should still look to the civil and ceremonial laws\r\n\r\n1) God\'s character requires us to learn from the revelation of these laws. As God\'s character does not change and it is our ultimate standard for ethics.  Hence Old Testament\'s civil and ceremonial laws still reveal our moral standard\r\n\r\n2) Scripture itself teaches the continuing modern application even of the Old Testament laws. \r\nJesus himself instructed\r\n\r\n3) Bible consistently teaches that the law is a unified whole, that it all stands together without regard to civil, ceremonial or moal\r\n\r\n4) All of Scripture is for our moral instructions. It does not exclude any laws, hence it all has to teach us about modern ethics.', 0, '2020-07-08 17:12:31', '2020-07-08 17:12:31', NULL),
(1689, 492, 796, 'God\'s plan to redeem human beings from the corruption and consequences of our sin was made before he created the universe. This timing is mentioned in Ephesians 3:11 , which speaks of God\'s purpose.\r\n 2 Thessalonians 2;13 says that we were chosen for salvation from the beginning.\r\n2 Timothy 1:9,10  speaks of grace that was given to us \" before the beginning of time\".\r\nEphesians 1:3-4 Paul said that our redemption was determined before the creation of the world. \r\nIn Ephesians 1:11 we read \"In Him we were also chosen , having been predestined according to the plan of him who works out everything in conformity with the purpose of his will. (Ephesians 1:11)\r\nGod\'s decree of salvation is referred to by the Greek word Proorizo which is translated as Predestination.\r\nIn Romans 8:29 and Ephesians 1:5 the word Proorizo is used. It means God\'s eternal decree of salvation was foreordained or decided before the world began.', 7, '2020-07-09 17:48:07', '2020-07-15 20:25:13', NULL),
(1690, 492, 797, 'God\'s eternal plan of redemption involves the work of all the three persons of the Trinity.\r\n The Father originated the agreement because of his desire to redeem fallen human beings from the curse of the sin. Scripture says that it was the Father\'s plan to save us ..(Ephesians 3:10-11).It was the Father\'s eternal purpose to accomplish our redemption through Christ. (Ephesians 1:4, 2 Thessalonians 2:13, 1 Peter 1:20)\r\nThe Son agreed to add a perfect human nature to his perfect divine nature, so that could die on behalf of sinners. In 2 Timothy 1:9 and in John 17:4,5 Paul said that we received grace in the Son before the beginning of time. \r\nGod\'s eternal counsel decreed roles for the Father and the Son, it also determined the Holy Spirit\'s part. The Holy  Spirit agreed to enable and empower the Son\'s work and the apply salvation to those\r\nwhom the Son redeemed .\r\n2 Thessalonians 2:13 we see that Paul indicated that the Father\'s choice was made from the beginning and that plan involved the Holy Spirit\'s agreement to perform the sanctifying work of applying salvation to us .', 8, '2020-07-09 18:04:39', '2020-07-15 20:25:13', NULL),
(1691, 492, 798, 'Covenant of grace means the Covenant relationship God established with humanity after our fall into sin that provides forgiveness and redemption on the basis of God\'s mercy in Christ.\r\nbefore He created the world , God:\r\nknew humanity would fall into sin ,So HE created a plan to save us involving all three persons of the Trinity. HE also planned to redeem sinners through Christ\'s death on our behalf.\r\nThe Covenant of grace fulfills part of God\'s eternal plan for history. \r\nThe Father fulfilled his eternal decree in the covenant of grace by sending the Son and the Spirit to do their work. He appointed the Son to the office of Messiah or Christ(Acts 2:36)\r\nhe grace His powerful Spirit without limit(John 3:34)\r\nHe prepared the Son\'s perfect human nature(Hebrews 10:5)\r\nThe Son fulfilled his eternal agreement to redeem humanity by Veiling his divine glory and adding a full human nature to his full divine nature, living a perfect ,life and dying and atoning death(Philippians 2:5)\r\nThe Holy spirit fulfilled his part by enabling and empowering the Son\'s incarnation and subsequent work (Matthew 1:20),by empowering Christ\'s death on the cross, regenerating our spirits and empowering us to resist sin, giving us spiritual gifts and securing our salvation.(Ephesians :13-14)', 8, '2020-07-09 18:20:54', '2020-07-15 20:25:13', NULL),
(1692, 492, 799, 'God the Son , joined the covenant of grace as its mediator:\r\nHe intercedes for God\'s covenant people.\r\nHe reconciles us to God by taking the blame and punishment for our sins. \r\nHe preserves the integrity of the covenant and the lives of his people by suffering the covenant curses and earning the covenant blessings.\r\nThe Son began to mediate the Covenant of grace when it was first made back in the Garden of Eden, when God first offered redemption to Adam and Eve. And  he has continued to mediate ever since.\r\nNo one was ever saved or can erase sin  on the basis of his or her own merit or worthiness , since now works of obedience can erase our sin . Jesus , his life perfect faith and obedience , his death on the cross , is resurrection from the dead and his ascension to heaven and as the mediator of the covenant of grace, he fulfilled the covenant of works on our behalf and guaranteed that we would receive his blessings.\r\nJesus succeeded where Adam failed, and his righteous works benefited us because the covenant of grace does provide the mechanism for forgiveness and grace.\r\nJesus\'s role as our fully divine and fully human covenant mediator is what enabled him to atone for our sin by dying in our place.', 8, '2020-07-09 18:36:28', '2020-07-15 20:25:13', NULL),
(1693, 492, 800, 'The covenant  of grace was administered by various covenant representatives:\r\nADAM: \r\nThe covenant of Grace was instituted with Adam immediately after he fell into sin . This administration provided humanity the immediate opportunity to reconcile our relationships with God.\r\nNOAH:\r\nThe covenant confirmed with Noah after the flood explicitly incorporated all the terms of Adam\'s administration . The Noahic administration expanded the covenant blessings by adding God\'s promises never again to destroy the earth withe flood waters.(Genesis 6:18)\r\nABRAHAM:\r\nGod promised Abraham to turn Abraham\'s descendants into a mighty nation and to bless all nations through them.\r\nIn this administration, the nation of Israel was charged with expanding God\'s kingdom throughout the earth (Romans 4:13)\r\nMOSES:\r\nwith Mosaic administration God confirmed his promises to Abraham , provided structure for the nation of Israel , gave Israel the first codified version of Law a,d redirected Israel to build his kingdom throughout the world.(Exodus 19-24)\r\nDAVID:(2 Samuel 7, Psalms 89)\r\nIN this administration God confirmed the mosaic administration and revealed the greatest covenant blessings would be fulfilled under the kingship of David  and his dynastic heirs.\r\nJESUS\r\nThis covenant is referred to as new covenant. in the new covenant , god established a permanent, unbreakable covenant in which his people would receive all his covenant blessings.(Jeremiah 31:31)', 8, '2020-07-09 18:54:16', '2020-07-15 20:25:13', NULL),
(1694, 493, 670, 'The two fold concept of revelation has characterized biblical theology of the New Testament.The New Testament reports many revelatory acts of God such as Christ\'s earthly ministry and the ministry of the Holy Spirit in the first century church.It also foretells the acts of God that will take place in this future, such as the glorious return of Christ.But on the other hand , the New Testament also reports word revelations associated with the act of God:God the Father spoke, Christ also spoke  and at times , angels and humans , by the Spirit of God , revealed God\'s word as well. \r\nNew Testament narratives report both the actions and words of Jesus, the apostles and other Christians in the New Testament:because God reveals himself through their actions and their word. \r\nBible theologians  have pointed out that the New Testament contains all three kinds of word revelations as well. The Gospels reports how God spoke through the words  of Jesus to reflect on Jesus earlier actions and Jesus\' teachings explained his simultaneous actions and he predicted future actions.\r\nSame was done by the authors of epistles , Acts and Revelation. Throughout the New Testament God revealed himself through the intersections between his creations and his word.', 8, '2020-07-10 18:13:29', '2020-07-15 20:24:42', NULL),
(1695, 493, 671, 'One major contrast between old testament and new testament biblical theology is the ways Biblical theologians have handled dichronic developments.\r\nAS the New Testament moved forward, theological structures under went dichronic changes.\r\nOld Testament covers a very long period of 1600 years whereas the entire New Testament represents only around 100 years of history.\r\nOld Testament presents a great variety of circumstances in its  history which includes, Patriarchs, judges, early monarchy, latter kings and leaders , exile and restoration.By comparison , the circumstances of God\'s people were fairly consistent during the New Testament history like no extreme changes took place, consistently marginalized, no tremendous wealth or poverty, no large group travel and no  wide scale disobedience and obedience.\r\nThe New Testament deals with only single covenant whereas the old Testament deals with five covenants which were quite different from each other.', 8, '2020-07-10 18:28:53', '2020-07-15 20:24:42', NULL),
(1696, 493, 672, 'Toe understand how New Testament biblical theologians have understood the last days, we need to become familiar with Old Testament eschatology.Eschatology developed alongside the major covenant administrations of the Old Testament , beginning with Adam through Noah, Abraham, Moses and David.\r\n1. ADAM:\r\nGod revealed two crucial elements of eschatology, first being the fact that humanity was created in God\' s image. Genesis 3:15 says that seed of women and seed of serpent are the two groups of people competing for control of the world.\r\n2. NOAH\r\nIn Genesis 8:22 the covenant secured the stability of nature as humanity pursued God\'s plan for the world.\r\n3. ABRAHAM\r\nIN Genesis 12:1-3. God singled out Abraham to be the one through whim he would carry out his promise given through Adam and Eve \r\n4. MOSES\r\nMoses\' covenant focused on the law o God as the guide for Israel\'s special service in spreading\r\nhis kingdom. One key feature of Moses\' eschatology is the way he described this time of Israel\'s repentance and restoration to the land in Deuteronomy 4:30\r\n5 DAVID:\r\nGod\'s covenant with David focused on specially on the establishment of David\'s family as Israel\'s permanent dynasty.', 8, '2020-07-10 18:46:00', '2020-07-15 20:24:42', NULL),
(1697, 493, 673, 'Jesus\' three phase eschatology was so prominent in then hearts of early Christians that we find it either explicitly or implicitly in every page of the New Testament. Eschatology was especially important for the New Testament because Jesus\' teaching about the last days represent one of the most decisive way in which Christians had broken with first century Judaism .Jewish religious leaders and the general Jewish population raged against Christianity precisely because of the Christian outlook on the Messianic last days. Christians believed that the Messiah had already come , but in the way that was unexpected . He had suffered and died at the hands of Jews and gentiles. He has been resurrected and had ascended into heaven where he ruled over all and he would return one day to judge all of humanity including unbelievers within Israel.  Such a  Messianic scenario was utterly contrary to what most Jews believed in that days. And for theses reasons, New Testament authors were deeply preoccupied with Jesus\' three phase eschatology and this preoccupation reflected in everything hey wrote.', 8, '2020-07-10 18:59:16', '2020-07-15 20:24:42', NULL),
(1698, 493, 674, 'IN Matthew 13-25, we have studied that Jesus explained that the Kingdom of God would come in three phases.It would began  with his first coming in a small way , grow for an indefinite period of time and reach its fulfillment only when he returned in glory. So having understood that his kingdom is growing now and we all are laborers in His Kingdom, we work hard and sincerely.\r\n We try to teach, preach, proclaim the message of his Kingdom to all around us. We try to bring about the experience of kingdom in our families and churches. \r\nWe are to live for Christ in the light of what he has already accomplished in his first coming, we are to live for Christ in the power of his Spirit within us now and we are to live for Christ in the hope of his glorious return.\r\nWe are getting ready for the visible appearance of His Kingdom.\r\nwe try to bear fruits and characteristics which appeal to His kingdom.As we read in Romans 14:17\r\nFor the kingdom of God is not a matter of eating and drinking but of righteousness, peace and joy in the Holy Spirit. so applying the concept of Kingdom of god to all aspects of life helps us to be accountable and responsible throughout our life.', 8, '2020-07-10 19:15:45', '2020-07-15 20:24:42', NULL),
(1699, 490, 834, 'Authority is a bible attribute that derives from divine inspiration is the authority of scripture,becouse Bible divinely inspired ,its carry\'s Gods authority    ,bible claims divine athority for itself in at least two ways , first its provides historical examples for its authority ,second its explicitly clams authority \r\nwhen we talk about spoken word of God and the written word of God that we have alrady seen ,we can see maany ways bible gives the authority of God word that aplay to  the bible  it self ,In history God spek to people dirctly and his speach carried athority ,for example in the account of creation and fall ,Gen 2-3,God commented man to cultivate the  garden of Eaden , and also we can find in  later in the days of moses God encoded his spoken word in writtern form,insted of simply telling moses to ten comandment,\r\nThe new testament is also confirm the authority of scripture through its example ,as in john 17:12 wher he prayed these words, That scriptur would be fulfiled , the apostels demonstrated thier bilife in the bible\'s authority', 0, '2020-07-13 05:18:43', '2020-07-13 05:18:43', NULL),
(1700, 490, 835, 'When God inspired the authorized the writers of scriptur he had a particular goal in  in mind ,specificaly he wanted to give the people clear revalation conserning his will and his charecter in order that they would be better able to confirm them-self to him,  \r\nclarity of scripture :when we say tht scriptur is clear we do not mean that everithing in bible is easy to understand and everithibng in bible is stayed plainly and directly ,insted we understand bible is not obsecure ,it is not filled with  hidden meanings that can only be discoverd throgh mystiruos meanings,or special spiritul gifts,\r\nNature:  srcipter speak so plainly about the gospel that every mental comptent person should be able to figour out that salvation comes through repentance and faith in Christ,also scripture are particularly clear about the gospel of salvation in christ  the confession of faith also makes some observation about all of scriptur .', 0, '2020-07-13 05:33:06', '2020-07-13 05:33:06', NULL),
(1701, 490, 836, 'some mistaken ideal about scripture is that scripture is silent in certain matters ,christian frequntly teach that some issues of life are moraly \"indifferent \" becouse scripture dose not provide us with sufficient information to know God\'s will on these matter, the typical position has been that indifferent things are niether right or nor wrong in and of theme self , Everithing God made are good, nothing to be rejected ,it is recived by thangs giving , to find out nGods will we learned in first chapter we define \'good\'as being that wich recive Gods blessing and evil as that dose not recive the blessings ,by this aspects of human being as thire lives are good or evil,if he bless its good and his will, if he dont bless its not his will ,', 0, '2020-07-13 05:46:25', '2020-07-13 05:46:25', NULL),
(1702, 490, 837, 'Romans 1:15-16,i am so eager to preach the gospel ........becouse it is the power of God for the salvation of everione who belives .the gospel paul had in his mind he was not just set a truth about what jesus had done nor was ijn the power of God represented by the statement of the gospel he did not meant that the gospelmis about God who he has power ,rather paul meant thtat act of preaching the gospal is powerful ,becouse God uses prechers to bring people to faith , \r\nthe people who are foolish they dont understand the power of the gospel, gospel it self has power to bring people to christ , in our day today life we are also comple to preach gospel becouse by the prachig people will come to christ, God will use preachers to bring people to christ ,foolish people do not understand the power of the word .', 0, '2020-07-13 05:56:53', '2020-07-13 05:56:53', NULL),
(1703, 490, 838, 'Anyone who read much of the bile should recognize that script scriptur is notn uniform,its contains history ,poetry ,wisdom,prophecy , correspondence  and all sort of other writings ,also we find even further variety , after all each author wrote in his own way ,and his writings it self varied throghout his work, some time he gave command some time he explained ,some time recall personal experience and this variety is not accidental, \r\nLanguage:in the first place the bible displays the full range of language ,that we find in all human communication ,its contains staements , questions ,promises, offers, curs ,  blessings ,threats,judjments,quotations,summations,commands,advice,requext, exlamations,cries of desper, expressikon of desire ,and admiration and love,much more biblical languge can be emotionaly reserved or emotionaly charged ,some of it quit imaginative, using symbolism and other figursof speach,\r\nthose who belive bible uses the extra ordianry language that bible speak ignore the differant typoe of lanugae in bibe insted oversimplyfy the biblical languge in order to devolop system intrepratation \r\nordinary :we spoke of the clarity of scriptur by wich we maent that bible is not obsecure ,it is not filled with hidden meanings,', 0, '2020-07-13 06:15:51', '2020-07-13 06:15:51', NULL),
(1704, 490, 839, 'The ten commandments are listed in exodus 20,various theological tradition enumerate the commandments differently ,\r\nThe nprimacy of ten comandments is both historical and theological ,their historical primacy depend on the fact that ,to our knowledge ,these laws were the first written legal code that was recived by the nation of israewl, paul called special attention,Paul referred  to the giving of the ten commandments  as the \"introduction\" of the law ,indicating that this was the first time israel has possed the Gpod\' s law in this form,israel recivefd ten commandments trough moses ,who himself recived it direct from God \r\nIn addition to having a temporal primacy the ten comandment also had theological or ideological primacy , in exodus 24:12 ,God tell to mose come up to mountain and stay here and i will give you the tables of stone ,with the law,\r\nGod himself wrote the commandment on stone tablets , the theological primacy of ten commandment is alos indicate by special occation  on wich israel recived them,the giving of law was attended by thunder and lighting ,somke cloude ,and heveanly trumpet .', 0, '2020-07-13 06:31:32', '2020-07-13 06:31:32', NULL),
(1705, 490, 840, 'Categorize the various laws in the old testament bible into three major gorps :moral law,ceremonial law, and civil law, moral laws always typicaly thoght to convay God\'s ethical standerds and are usualy identified with the ten commandments ,civil law provide for the governing of socity ,espcialy during the period of israel\'s theocracy .Ceremonial laws in turn are those wich provide instructions of worshiping God , frequently these are most closely associated with the old testament sacrifical system,and tabernacle and temle administration .   \r\nmany theologiance agree on the validity of the traditional category of the Old testament law they often disagree on how to apply these atagory to study of ethics , some have said that whole catagry of law dont aplay in morden christian,the proper identification of law provieds a mechanism by wich they can avoid aplaying God\'s word to thier livies ,all cermonial laws are now abrogated under the new testament .', 0, '2020-07-13 06:47:45', '2020-07-13 06:47:45', NULL),
(1706, 490, 841, 'Since the death , burial , Resurrection and ascension of Christ ,God\'s people are no longer to perform many of the specific behavior  that were required under the mosaic sacrificial and temple system,  we are no longer to maintain the temple or to restrict women and genital to access to God\'s holy presence or sacrifice animal for our sin, but we can allow the general equity ,or basic moral priciples of civil laws continue to apply , the basic idea here is that specific requirment of civil laws no longer applay,they have expierd,\r\nit is true that belivers no longer have to behave in many of the ways specified in the old testament ,espscily when law has pertain to old testament semony and civil goverment ,the civil and cermonial laws of the old testament realy have expierd ,in the sence that we are not to return old testament patters of life, \r\nit is dificult to realize that in another sense the old testament civil and cermonial laws still maplay to mordern Christianity,the civil and cermonial laws still guid us to God\'s standard todya ,just as the moreal laws do.', 0, '2020-07-13 07:03:57', '2020-07-13 07:03:57', NULL),
(1707, 494, 842, 'There are three basic typs of revelation, special revelation such as the Bible, General revealation which comes to us through the creation in general and existential revelation which comes to us through persons. \r\n\r\nBut based on these for us to make ethical decisions we have to consider three important aspects they are \r\nFACTS\r\nGOALS\r\nMEANS\r\n\r\nFacts :\r\nThrough revelation God speaks to us facts about himself and what he requires. Undrestand that God is the supreme authority over all creation, his aauthority is absolute and his character is perfect. God\'s revelation also teaches us about special set of facts that are particularly important for ethics.\r\n\r\nGoals :\r\nGoals in ethics are the targeted outcome that we have in mind. It is similar to the set of goals that we keep in mind, that we set to accomplish. Revelation provides us with goals that we ust adopt in Christian ethics.\r\n\r\nScripture teaches us about goals for doing good to our neighbors, raising children, striving for unity of the church. But the most important revelation is it presents God\'s glory as our primary and most important goal in life.\r\n\r\nMeans :\r\nAny ethical question in biblical manner requires - to find the appropriate means to achieve as revealed by God. Setting goals, assessing facts etc are things that influence our action. But our actions themselves are the means we have chosen to accomplish our goals. Godly means are equally important to achieve our goals and to understand the facts about God.', 8, '2020-07-20 15:18:07', '2020-07-21 04:09:09', NULL),
(1708, 494, 843, 'Facts are very important for us to know more about God in order to make ethical decisions. \r\nGod\'s character should be our ultimate norm or standard, and obligates us to live by the standard of his character. \r\nThrough revelation, God tells us facts about himself and facts about what he requires. Without the knowledge about the facts, we would still obey God, but without much knowledge.\r\n\r\nGod is the supreme authority over all of creation. His authority is absolute, His character perfect. Whenever we receive a revelation about his character, it is a means by which God exercises control over humans, similary to governments exercising control over it\'s citizens through their laws. \r\n\r\nGod not only communicates facts to us, but God\'s revelation also teaches us about special set of facts that are particulary important for ethics ; the proper goals of Christian behavior and decision making.', 8, '2020-07-20 15:25:17', '2020-07-21 04:09:09', NULL),
(1709, 494, 844, 'Goals in ethics are the expected outcomes of our endeavors that we have in our mind. Goals are similar to that which we set in our mind to accomplish. Goals can be small or large. They can be immediate goals or that which we plan in the distant future. But in every case our goals give direction to our action.\r\n\r\nScripture teaches us about goals of doing good to our neighbors, raising children in Christ, striving for the unity of church. But the most important goals is God\'s glory.\r\n\r\nGod glory in revelation reveals that we must be loyal to God and that we should praise him and glorify God in everything that we do. Scripture teaches us to set God\'s glory as our highest goal.\r\n\r\nExistential revelation helps us to discern good goals from evil goals, especially through our consciences. Holy Spirit is another source of existential revelation, moving within us so that we pursue good goals and shun evil ones.\r\n\r\nGod uses all three forms of revelation, special, general and existential in order to teach us the goals that God approves.', 8, '2020-07-20 15:32:05', '2020-07-21 04:09:09', NULL),
(1710, 494, 845, 'Christians inclined to follow a rigorous strategy towards revelation, resulting in tending to err on the side of overly restricting behavior rather than on the side of permitting it.\r\n\r\nRigor often views the situation in Bible as being similar to our own and applies the Scripture directly to our lives without consideration or scope to think about how it differs from the modern world, in terms of facts and goals. \r\n\r\nChristians endorsing a rigorous strategy, mistakenly believe that when the Bible\'s facts, goals and means appear to be vague, the proper response is to apply Scripture in restrictive ways. By doing so we often end up forbidding some things that God permits and other things that God actually commands.\r\n\r\nDangers :\r\nIt destroys Christian Freedom by prohibiting behavior that are wrong under certain conditions. But good under other conditions. As matters of conscience are not clear, a strategy of rigor would tend to prohibit certain actions resulting in missing Godly blessings.\r\n\r\nA strategy of rigor also inspires despair in believers by turning God\'s world into a heavy burden. \r\n\r\nAvoid falling into this strategy :\r\nRealize that modern situations are sufficiently different from biblical situations, we cannot just apply or copy the applications to the present modern era, without giving it further considerations.\r\n\r\nWe can avoid a strategy of rigor by remembering that Scripture is sufficiently clear to communicate God\'s will with regard to ethics.', 9, '2020-07-20 15:47:11', '2020-07-21 04:09:09', NULL),
(1711, 494, 846, 'Jesus spoke about the Kingdom of God in the Sermon on the Mount found in the Gospel of Mathew Chapter 5\r\n\r\nThe Sermon on the mount is well known, Jesus began by encouraging people to live ethically in terms of the Kingdom of God.\r\n\r\nLets consider the three different sections wherein Jesus emphasized the importance of the Kingdom of God\r\n\r\n1) Mathew 5:3 - the blessing was \"theirs is the kingdom of heaven\" Though Mathew here used the phrase the \"Kingdom of Heaven\" biblical scholars have agreed that this term is is the same as Kingdom of God. \r\n\r\n2) Mathew 5:5 - the blessing was \"they will inherit the earth\" this was also a kingdom blessing, and it referred to the new earth that God will create when his kingdom will come in it\'s fullness.\r\n\r\n3) Mathew 5:9 - the blessing was \"they shall be called the sons of God\" Even this statement of blessedness refers to the kingship and kingdom of God. In the times of old biblical times, human kings were called \"father\" by their subjects. Same is true about the scriptures. God is our heavenly father. \r\n\r\nEach of the blessings Jesus mentioned was connected to the concept of the kingdom of God.', 8, '2020-07-20 15:56:24', '2020-07-21 04:09:09', NULL),
(1712, 494, 847, 'The Three main components of the Kingdom of God are \r\n\r\nKING (role of the King) \r\nPEOPLE (Citizens of the Kingdom) \r\nCOVENANTS (that govern the relationship between king and his people)\r\n\r\nKing :\r\nThe concept of King is unfamiliar to the modern people but in oden times Kings were expected to fulfill their responsibilities to the citizens of the country. They were to protect and provide for them and to treat them with kindness. In return King will charge them taxes and raise armies and regulate the many aspects of life.\r\nGood Kings ruled wisely to benefit the people. \r\n\r\nIn the Bible God is presented as the Supreme King or emperor over all creation.\r\nAll the earthly kings are his vassals or servan kings. \r\nThough David and thereafter his son Solomon sat on the throne of the Lord in Jerusalem. The throne still belongd to God so that the human kings were just representatives or vassals of God.\r\n\r\nPeople :\r\nThe people here refers to those whom God has called to himself in contrast to the people of the world. \r\n\r\nOld testament refers to Abraham and his descendants. In the New Testament, it refers to the Church, since christians of all races have been adopted into the family of Abraham in Christ.\r\n\r\nUnder the kingship of Jesus the focus of God\'s kingdom became ecclesiastical it was centered on the church. God\'s kingdom includes people from every race and continues to spread to the ends of the earth.\r\n\r\nCovenants :\r\nGod administered his kingdom through covenants. God\'s expressed good will towards his people through covenants, wherein clearly the parameters were mentioned regarding the consequences for obedience & disobedience and it was binding covenant for both parties.\r\n\r\nThere are 6 major covenants between God and his people, beginning with Adam to that of Noah, Abraham, Moses, David and finlly the Final Covenant in Christ Jesus.', 9, '2020-07-20 16:09:36', '2020-07-21 04:09:09', NULL),
(1713, 494, 848, 'Traditionally Bible has summarized the kingdom of God through three historical phases :\r\n\r\nInitial Phase (Creation)\r\nRebellion (Humanity\'s fall into sin)\r\nFinal Peace (Redemption)\r\n\r\n1) Initial Phase : \r\nUnder creation story, humanity lived in perfect harmony with God. Human life was full of joy and gladness, of thanksgiving and singing. in the garden there was great peace.\r\nThere was no enemy to threaten them, no war, no violence, no sickness, no drought or flood or fire to destroy them etc.\r\nGod cared tenderly for Adam and Eve, and even met them and walked with them in the cool of the garden.\r\n\r\n2) Rebellion \r\nAs we study Genesis 3, we are aware of humanity\'s initial rebellion against God through disobedience & the fall of man. Serpent tempted Eve to eat the forbidden tree and shared the fruit with Adam. By sinnning humanity violated one of the covenant obligation.\r\n\r\nGod threw Adam & Eve out of the Garden and forced them to live in a world wherein it was the cursed ground followed by pain in childbirth and along with sickness and famine with wild animals and threats of war. They stil lhad to fulfill the covenant obligations but they were experiencing the negative considequences due to sin. \r\n\r\nHumanity has continued to rebel against God throughout history. God has punished humans with covenant curses. \r\n\r\n3) Final Peace\r\nGod began to restore peace to his kindom immediately after humanity\'s fall into sin. God did not wipe out humanity completely when they sinned, but he allowed them to live. God introduced the first steps, promise of salvation through Genesis 3:15. Throughout history God was working toward the goal of full redemption and success of his kingdom.\r\n\r\nAt the appearance of Christ, the restoration of final peace took a huge leap and reached the final stages of fulfillment. Jesus came to earth as a vassal king in order to establish a faithful kingd om earth. His work still continues and he will come again in glory and restore the kingdom, bring the whole world under final peace.', 9, '2020-07-20 16:28:57', '2020-07-21 04:09:09', NULL),
(1714, 494, 849, 'God\'s laws are a delight and it adds joy to our life. As humans when we obey the laws laid down by God, in return we receive blessings that God has itended for obedient citizens of his kingdom.\r\n\r\nLaw\'s reveals God to us, teaching us how to please him and how to obtain his blessings. Laws were given for our good and for our prosperity and for our joy.\r\n\r\nDavid summarized in Psalms 19\r\n\r\nThe law of the Lord is perfect, reviving the sould. The precepts of the Lord are right giving joy to the heart\r\n\r\nGod has given us rules to follow in order to produce joy in our lives. And those rules are his law. So when we obey God\'s law, we enjoy him and we glory him at the same time. We enjoy him because he blesses our obedience and because it pleases us to bring pleasure to the God we love. And our godly joy brings glory to God by fulfilling his purpose. In all of these ways, the role of the Law shows us that enjoying God is an important part of God\'s goal for humanity.\r\n\r\nIn our present modern age, our enjoyment of God is often hindered by our suffering. But we also need to understand that God\'s plan for us is through suffering, it further enhances our faith and improves our understanding of God\'s grace and knowledge about him. \r\n\r\nA close analysis of the Scripture teaches us that God uses suffering as a tool that proves our faith and brings us to spiritual maturit and that ultimately results in our joy.\r\n\r\nManytimes we do not understand the full purpose and plan in our sufferings. But if you further study the scriptures and draw closer to God, we will experience more the grace of God in our sufferings and challenges of life. Also our experiences of joy will bring great glory to our divine King. \r\n\r\nOur view of the laws and the scriptures need to be focussed on drawing nearer to our creator.  To increase our trust factor in God and to understand that we are the clay in the hands of our master builder.', 9, '2020-07-20 16:46:58', '2020-07-21 04:09:09', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(1715, 496, 655, 'Biblical theology is the theological reflection drawn from the historical analysis of acts of God reported in Scripture.Historical analysis is especially concerned with \"acts of God\".\r\nThe holy Spirit has led the church to pursue the exegesis of Scripture in three main ways : literary analysis, historical analysis and thematic analysis. Historical analysis looks at Scripture as a window to history, exploring historical events lying behind the Bible.\r\nBiblical theology approaches the Scriptures primarily with historical analysis. It looks at the bible as a window that gives access to the history. When the focus shifts from theological themes to the historical events described in the Bible, a very different set of priorities and concerns emerge .', 8, '2020-07-24 17:43:02', '2020-07-25 06:02:14', NULL),
(1716, 496, 656, 'Biblical theological reflection is based on the historical analysis of the acts of God in Scripture. historical analysis take two different forms: factual historical analysis and theological historical analysis. These two tendencies go hand in hand , but their concerns are quite different.\r\nFactual approach are concerned with  the events are reported in scripture fit within the large environment ancient Near East. A factual approach to historical analysis is concerned with questions like the date of the exodus under Moses etc.\r\nThe goal of factual historical analysis is straight forward.It is to establish a reliable account of the facts of history along with the data we gather from extra biblical resources.\r\nChristians agree with Aquinas that theology has two main concerns .A theological matter is anything that refers directly to God.  And on the other hand theological matter is anything that describes other subjects in relation to God. Biblical theology opens the way for enhancing and enlarging our understanding of all of these theological subjects like the human race, sin, salvation etc', 9, '2020-07-24 17:59:51', '2020-07-25 06:02:14', NULL),
(1717, 496, 657, 'There are many cultural changes that set the stage for biblical theology .Biblical theology is in large measure a response to cultural shifts that can be traced back to the Enlightenment of the 17th century.\r\nSimply put biblical theology is a Christian response to a prominent intellectual movement in the modern period, often called modern historic ism.\r\nOne of the most well known Enlightenment figures who expressed this cultural shift was the German philosopher George Wilhelm Friedrich Hegel, known for his proposal that every aspect of reality is caught up in logical patterns of historical progress known as the dialectic. \r\nThe study of geology, biology, and similar shifts toward modern historicism took place in the nearly academic discipline including theology.\r\nEverything in life was thought to be understand most thoroughly when it was assessed in terms of the flow of history.', 7, '2020-07-24 18:14:49', '2020-07-25 06:02:14', NULL),
(1718, 496, 658, 'As per Gabler Christians should believe in the modern world through rational reflection on science and religion. Gabler believed that the findings f the biblical theology might be of some interest from time to time ,but modern Christians should believe only the parts of the bible that pass the standards of the modern rational and scientific analysis. From the perspective, the crossing of the Red Sea was nothing more than that a strong wind blowing through a marsh.\r\nWe might have expected them simply to set aside biblical theology since they thought that the Bible was riddled with misleading historical claims. \r\nBut the field of Biblical theology did not die when critical theologians rejected biblical authority. Instead they found other ways to use scriptures for contemporary theology. Instead of treating the Bible as true history, they began to look at scriptures as expressions of ancient religious sentiments presented as historical claims, and they explored how these ancient religious feelings and experiences might be useful to modern Christians .', 7, '2020-07-24 18:30:48', '2020-07-25 06:02:14', NULL),
(1719, 496, 659, 'The divine goal of all world history is the extension of God\'s perfect heavenly reign to every corner of the earth . When God\'s will is done as perfectly on earth as it is in heaven, every creature will bow before God and honor him as the divine king., the supreme creator of all. \r\nThe opening chapters of the Bible describes the way God began to turn the chaotic world into his kingdom by ordering creation and placing his image in the garden of Eden and by commanding humanity to extend to the ends of the earth.\r\nThe rest of the Old Testament reports how God chose Israel as his special people and commissioned them to the lead the rest of humanity in spreading the kingdom of God to the ends of the earth, but Israel also failed terribly.\r\nDespite these failures, God did not give up on his grand purpose. As the NEW Testament reveals , God sent his eternal son in to the world. through his death, resurrection and ascension, the ministry of the holy Spirit through his body and his glorious return, Christ is completing the task originally given to humanity. \r\nIn this approach to biblical theology, every event in biblical history is part of this grand scheme.\r\nThe vast variety of divine actions , great and small will bring ultimate glory to God through the establishment of his kingdom in the new heavens and new earth, thus completing the goal,of biblical history to bring God glory.', 9, '2020-07-24 18:45:05', '2020-07-25 06:02:14', NULL),
(1720, 497, 776, 'The majority of the interpreters reject Pauline authorship.\r\nthere are three reasons for this :\r\n1.Identifying the author of Hebrews is not as simple as it is with many other testament books because the author never identified himself other nook is anonymous. and it was Paul\'s practice to name himself in his epistles. As Per 2 Thessalonians 2:2 it is clear that Paul was deeply concerned that forgeries had spread under his name , so it seems that he would have failed to identify himself had he written Hebrews\r\n2.The book of Hebrews emphasizes subjects that are not mentioned in Paul\'s other letters. The themes like Melchizedek, Old Testament tabernacle,Christ as High priest distinguish the book of Hebrews from books that we know were written by Paul.\r\n3.The strongest reason for doubting is the way the writer of Hebrews distance himself from the first generation of Jesus\' followers. Hebrews 2:3', 7, '2020-07-25 18:20:33', '2020-08-04 22:36:10', NULL),
(1721, 497, 777, 'The five characteristics of Hebrews\' original audience are :\r\n1. Jewish:\r\nA good portion of the original audience was Jewish, we can see it in Hebrews 1:1 .The author referred to the Old Testament Israeiltes as \"our forefathers\".The traditional title attatcahed to this book has been \"Pros Hebraious\"by Tertullian AD 155.\r\n2. Hellenistic\r\nIt is also likely that the large part of the audience was hellenistic. the content of Hebrews indicates that the audience was familiar with the theological teachings that were common among Jews living outside  of Palestine than among more traditional Jewish circles within Palestine.\r\n3.Immature\r\nThird,the original audience was immature. Hebrews 5:12 says that the audience had been long enough for the author to say \" by this time you ought to be teachers, but he furthers noted that they needed to be taught the elementary truths of God\'d word all over again.\r\n4. Persecuted:\r\nthen we  see another original audience to be the persecuted ones. In AD 49 Roman emperor Claudius and in AD 64 Nero persecuted Christians. In Hebrews 10:32-35, we read about how author praised his audience about their strength when they were persecuted in those earlier days.\r\nHebrews 12:3-4 author states to audience about their future troubles.\r\n5. Near apostasy.\r\n At The last audience of Hebrews who faced persecution were near apostasy.Hebrews 10:26-27 we read that rather they were discouraged by sufferings , they were in danger of turning away from Christ entirely.', 8, '2020-07-25 18:39:18', '2020-08-04 22:36:10', NULL),
(1722, 497, 778, 'MAny literary devices that were associated with persuasive oratory or urgent debate in the first century. \r\n1. One rhetorical device called synkrisis in Greek  is a detailed comparison between two or more things designed to convince audience to affirm the speakers\'s point of view. we see it in Hebrews 7:11-28. the author gave his audience a compelling , eight point comparison between Melchizedek and Christ.\r\n2. Another rhetorical device in the book of Hebrew is known as \"exampla\".These are list of example or illustrations that follow one after the other to build a persuasive argument for a particular point of view. In Hebrews  11 the author listed many names.\r\n3. Another rhetorical devise used by the author is known by the Hebrew expression called qol wahomer. This is well known from both Greco-Roman and rabbinical traditions and maybe translated \"light to heavy\" or \"less to great\" or \"simple to complex\". we read it in Hebrews 10:28,29', 8, '2020-07-25 18:51:47', '2020-08-04 22:36:10', NULL),
(1723, 497, 779, 'We read in Hebrews 5:12, the original audience of Hebrews was immature. We too are immature in certain areas of our life. We too need to  have doctrinal progress in spiritual life. I need to learn to forgive more in regarding with different people that we deal with in our ministry. I need to meditate more on the word , much deeply to understand the truths of the Bible so as to teach the people of my church . I need to grow in greater ways in understanding His word , so as to teach with more authority and clarification . \r\nDoing the course of Master of Divinity is one of the reason to grow in doctrinal progress in my spiritual life.\r\nI need more doctrinal progress to understand between certain gifts of the Holy Spirit like interpretation of tongues or different types of prophets. To discern the sound or false doctrines also I need to have more progress. certain doctrines which have evolved these last days have to be comprehended better by me.', 8, '2020-07-25 19:09:40', '2020-08-04 22:36:10', NULL),
(1724, 497, 780, 'False doctrines and False teachings have been a threat and a challenge to the Church from the days of its origin. the most influential false doctrine now a days is\r\n1. prosperity theology-According to it God is there available to make us rich. \r\n2. Grace doctrine: in this a person can continue to sin . knowingly as God is gracious and loving, He will forever forgive.\r\n3. No-hell doctrine: as per this teaching, god is a loving God and He cannot put anyone in hell\r\n4. Jerusalem- Holy mother Temple: as per false teaching Jerusalem is the mother and God is the Father\r\nStrategy : \r\nwe have used following strategies against these and a number of other teachings that has been widely spread in Christians in India\r\n1. we should be well versed in the Bible. The truth shall make us free. Only the Word is our base and foundation of our teachings.\r\n2. we always measure every teaching and current human revelations in the form of dreams or direct from god as they say, as per the plumb line of Word of God. if these revelations contradict the Word , we are not to follow them\r\n3. we equip and make disciples in Word of God all the members of the church in the basic doctrines of the Bible that was followed by Apostles and we read in bible.', 8, '2020-07-25 19:22:54', '2020-08-04 22:36:10', NULL),
(1725, 500, 727, 'उत्तर = हम मर्कुस के सुसमाचार को लिखने के अवसर के दो आयामों  का अध्ययन करेंगे पहले हम और कुछ दूसरा लिखने की तिथियां समय पर विचार करेंगे और फिर हम और कुछ द्वारा लिखने के उद्देश्य का अध्ययन करेंगे आइए हम पहले मरकुस द्वारा सुसमाचार को लिखने की तिथि को देखें।\r\n1)तिथि \r\n अमर कुछ कि सुसमाचार के लेखक तिथि का निर्धारण व निश्चिता के साथ नहीं किया जा सकता परंतु विशाल रूप से प्रमाण पहली सदी के मध्य में साठ के दशक के अंत के समय की ओर संकेत करते प्रतीत होते हैं।\r\nआइरेनियस और मरकुस का एन्टी मार्सीयनाइट प्रोलोन जैसे प्राचीन गवा दावा करते हैं कि मरकुस ने अपने सुसमाचार को पतरस  की मृत्यु के बाद लिखा था इसकी अत्यधिक संभावना है कि ईवी 64 मैं रूम में लगी आग के बाथरूम में सम्राट नीरू द्वारा कलीसिया पर किए गए अत्याचारों के दौरान पत्र सहित हो गया था पापिया स्काई ए आया यहां हो सकता है कि मर्कुस ने अपने कार्य की शुरुआत तक कि जब पतरस जीवित था परंतु वह इस संभावना से इनकार नहीं करता कि मर कुछ द्वारा कार्य को समाप्त करने से पहले पतरस मर चुका था अच्छा यह स्वीकार करना उपयुक्त प्रतीत होता है कि मर्कुस द्वारा अपने सुसमाचार को पूरा करने की सबसे आरंभिक तिथि ईस्वी 64 में पतरस की मृत्यु के आसपास रही होगी मर्कुस द्वारा लिखने की सबसे अंतिम तिथि को निर्धारित करना कठिन है जैसे कि पिछले 1 अध्याय में हमने देखा बहुत से विद्वानों का मानना है कि मर को सबसे पहले लिखित सुसमाचार था और पति एक लुका दोनों ने अपने सुसमाचार को लिखते समय संदर्भ के रूप में मरकुस का प्रयोग किया था चौकी इन तीनों में से कोई भी सुसमाचार इस  ईसवी 70 में हुए यरूशलेम और उसके मंदिर के विनाश का खंडन नहीं करता इसलिए बहुत से विद्वानों का यह निष्कर्ष है कि मत्ती मरकुस और लुका तीनों उस समय से पहले लिखे गए थे और यदि मती और लुका ने अपनी रचनाओं को पूरा करने से पहले मर उसका उपयोग किया है तो यह कहना सुरक्षित है कि मर्कुस इसमें 70 से भी पहले लिखा गया था निश्चित रूप से इ वी 69 तक जो मती और लुका को अपनी स्वयं की रचनाओं को पूरा करने से पहले मर्कुस की सुसमाचार से परिचित होने के लिए अधिक समय उपलब्ध कराएगा मरकुज की सुसमाचार की तिथि को ध्यान में रखते हुए आइए हम उसके लिखने के उद्देश्या पर विचार करे।\r\n2)मरकुस का सुसमाचार लिखने का उद्देश्य  \r\nएक अर्थ में मर्कुस और अन्य सारे सुसमाचार का एक ही उद्देश्य था यीशु के जीवन और शिक्षिकाओं के सच्चे ऐतिहासिक अभिलेख को सुरक्षित रखना है ईसवी 50  के बाद से यीशु के जीवन मृत्यु और पुनरुत्थान के गवाहों और प्रेरित ओके मृत्यु हो जाती जा रही थी इसलिए उनकी गवाही को सुरक्षित रखने की आवश्यकता पड़ती जा रही थी जैसे यूसीबीएस और अन्य आरंभिक कलीसायी लेखकों ने बताया मरकुस का आशिक उद्देश्य यहां यीशु की सेवा के पत्र के अभिलेख को सुरक्षित रखना था परंतु इस अभिलेख को सुरक्षित रखना है मरकुस का एकमात्र उद्देश्य नहीं था प्रत्येक सुसमाचार लेकर कि समान मरकुस किया केवल या नहीं चाहता था कि उसके पाठक यीशु के बारे में जाने वह यह भी चाहता था कि वे यीशु के जीवन से बातों को सीखे जिन्हें वे अपने स्वयं के जीवन में लागू कर सके परंतु उनके जीवन कैसे थे जिन वर्षों के दौरान संभवत मरकुस लिख रहा था उस समय रूम की कलीसिया रोमी सम्राट नियमों के अधीन अत्याचार सहे रही थी नीरो ने इस 64 में 68 तक राज्य किया वहां इसवी 64 में रूम में आग लगने का दोष मशीनों पर लगाने और उन्हें भयानक तरीके से दंड देने के लिए मुख्यता है नीरू के शासन के अधीन रूम निकली सपा और अत्याचार किया आरंभ में रूम का गठन एकत्रित रूप में किया गया था बाद में यूसीएस कैसेट की हत्या के बाद अस्तित्व में सेना की कामना संभालकर रामनगर पर अधिकार लिया और सीनेट की को भाग कर दिया अटरू में गणराज्य रोम साम्राज्य बन गया और अस्तित्व उसका पहला सम्राट बन गया यहीं से रूम में क्रूरता से के ऐतिहासिक जांच होती यह है यथार्थ मशीनों पर अत्याचार के मामले में नीरो सबसे बुरा नहीं था अन्य सम्राटों ने मुसीबत पर और भी घातक हमले किए और ऐतिहासिक अभिलेखों के अनुसार बहुत से मछलियों को उस पर किलो से ठोकर मारा गया या जीवित जला दिया गया आरंभिक अलीशा में बहुत से सही थे जिन्होंने अपनी मृत्यु के द्वारा परमेश्वर की करुणा और धार्मिकता की गवाही दी इस अवधि के दौरान रूम और उसके आसपास बस्तियों के लिए जीवन कई प्रकाश से कठिन था और जैसा हम देखेंगे मर उसने उनकी परिस्थितियों में सेवा के लिए अपना सुसमाचार को तैयार किया मरकुस के लिखने के उद्देश्य का वर्णन करने के बहुत से तरीके परंतु इस अध्ययन में हम इस बात पर ध्यान केंद्रित करेंगे कि मर उसने अपनी सुसमाचार को रोकने का से पीड़ित मरीजों को बल देने के लिए लिखा मर्कुस की सुसमाचार ने यह स्पष्ट किया कि वह मशीनों ने जिस कठिनाई और परिस्थितियों का सामना किया यीशु पहले ही उनका सामना कर चुका था उसे रोमी न्यायालय में अन्य पूर्व तरीके से दोषी ठहराया गया उसे रूमी सैनिकों द्वारा पीटा गया और उसे एक रोमी क्रूर पर लटकाया गया परंतु अपने कष्टों के बीच में यीशु की विजय रहा और मर्कुस अपने पाठकों को भरोसा दिलाना चाहता था कि यदि वे विश्वास योग्यता शिशु के पीछे चलते हैं तो वह भी विजई होंगे हां उन्हें कष्ट सहना होगा परंतु उनका कष्ट उनकी महिमा का मार्ग होगा जैसे ईश्वर ने कहा था।\r\n                                                                           \r\n                                                                             PRAISE THE LORD', 9, '2020-07-26 04:16:53', '2020-08-04 22:35:45', NULL),
(1726, 500, 728, 'उत्तर =  सुने मरकुस 1:1 मैं सुसमाचार की शुरुआत कैसे होती है:\r\n परमेश्वर के पुत्र यीशु मसीह के सुसमाचार का आरंभ\r\n जब मैं पूछने यीशु को मसीह के रूप में संबोधित किया तो उसने एवरी शब्द मसीहा की यूनानी अनुवाद का प्रयोग किया इसी प्रकार परमेश्वर का पुत्र शब्द एक और संकेत था कि शिव परमेश्वर का मसीहा है । पुराने नियम और तत्कालीन यहूदी धर्म विज्ञान में मसीहा कोच राजा दाऊद पवन से होना का जो सही सिंहासन को इस्राएल को वापस लौट आएगा और देश को प्रगति पर परमेश्वर के राज्य की ओर लाएगा इस सुबह की घोषणा के बाद मरकुस 1:2-11 मैं यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा दाता के द्वारा यीशु के बपतिस्मा का साहित्य अभिलेख दिया गया है यीशु के 32 माह के अंत में पवित्र आत्मा यीशु पर उतरा और स्वर्गीय से पिता परमेश्वर की आवाज यहां घोषणा करते हुए सुनाई दी कि यीशु उसका प्रिय पुत्र था इस प्रकार आत्मा और पिता दोनों ने यहां प्रमाणित किया कि यीशु वास्तव में बहुत प्रतिनिधित्व मसीहा था यहां सोचना बहुत ही रुचिकर है कि यीशु के समय कि यहूदी मसीहा के आगमन के संबंध में क्या सोचते थे और वास्तव में उनके बीच में बहुत सारे विविध प्रकार के विचार थे मृत सागर चर्म पत्र में से हमारे पास कुछ अभिलेख है जो यहां सिखाते हैं कि कुछ लोगों का यह विश्वास था कि दो मसीही आएंगे कि आज की मशीन और राजकीय मसीहा परंतु मुख्यधारा की अपेक्षित आयाती की मसीहा दाऊद का पुत्र होगा और वह राजनीतिक शांति स्थापित करेगा और रोमियो को खदेड़ देगा मेरे विचार से धार्मिक केंद्र का यह मानना था कि यदि इजराइल व्यवस्था का पालन करें तो राज्य आ जाएगा विश्व को इस संबंध में वास्तव में एक ख़तरा मानते थे क्योंकि इस व्यवस्था को मानने की अपेक्षा उसे तोड़ने को बढ़ावा देता था लगता था कम से कम उसकी दृष्टि में उसके पास वहां राजनीतिक दल नहीं था जिनकी उन्होंने पपीता की थी और फिर व्यवस्था के संबंध में भी उसने वह नहीं किया जिनकी उन्हें अपेक्षित थी और इसलिए मेरे विचार में वे उनके कारण दुविधा में थे वास्तव में मेरे विचार में अनंत वह यीशु को बरस व्यवस्था विवरण 13 के अर्थ में एक ऐसे व्यक्ति के रूप में देखते थे जो चीन चमत्कार और अचर कर्म तो करता था परंतु एक झूठा बहुत दुखता था और उसे मार डालना जाना चाहिए था परंतु यीशु उस प्रकार का मसीहा नहीं था जैसी बहुत से लोगों ने अपने पिता की थी सामान्यता पहली सदी के यहूदियों का सोचना था कि मसीहा इसराइल में आएगा और शासन को अपने हाथ में लेगा परंतु मरकुस1:12-13 मैं हम देखते हैं कि यीशु के 32 माह के तुरंत बाद पवित्र आत्मा ने उसे शैतान द्वारा परीक्षित के लिए मरुभूमि में भेज दिया अंत में वहां विजय हुआ पंच परमेश्वर योजना के अनुसार विजय का उसका मार्ग कठिन से भरा लंबा रास्ता था।\r\n\r\n              \r\n                                                                          {PRAISE THE LORD}', 8, '2020-07-26 04:32:57', '2020-08-04 22:35:45', NULL),
(1727, 500, 729, 'उत्तर = मसीहा के कष्ट का मरकुस का बिल 13 मुख्य भागों में विभाजित है अपने कष्ट और मृत्यु के लिए यीशु द्वारा चेलों को तैयार करना यरूशलेम में यहूदी अब वह के साथ उसका टकराव जिसने उसके कष्ट और मृत्यु को उकसाया और अनंत उसका कष्ट और मृत्यु हम इन सब को देखेंगे आइए हम मर्कुस 8:31- 10:52 मे  दी गई उसकी तैयारी से शुरू करते हैं।\r\n1 तैयारी :-\r\n यीशु द्वारा चेलों को तैयार करने का वर्णन करने वाले लेखक को तीन भागों में विभाजित किया जा सकता है जिनमें से प्रत्येक की शुरुआत यीशु द्वारा अपने कस्टम रितु और पुनरुत्थान की भविष्यवाणी के साथ होती है मर्कुस8:31-9:29 मैं पहला भाग राज्य के प्रभु के रूप में यीशु पर केंद्रित है मर उसने परमेश्वर कहते जो समय राज्य को पृथ्वी पर लाने के लिए यीशु की अनपेक्षित रणनीति अर्थात यीशु के कस्टम रितु और पुनरुत्थान की जानकारी देने के साथ शुरू किया जिससे मर्कुस ने8:31-9:1 मैं समझाया इस पूरे भाग में अपने शिष्य के दौरान यीशु ने अपने स्वयं के कष्ट के बारे में बात की और चोरों को चेतावनी दी कि जब वे उसकी सुसमाचार की सेवकों को जारी रखते हैं तो उन्हें भी कष्ट सहना पड़ेगा इसके बाद मरकुस9:2-13 मैं मरकुस ने उस घटना की जानकारी देने के द्वारा यीशु के आदित्य अधिकार की ओर ध्यान खींचा जिसे सामान्य रूपांतर के नाम से जाना जाता है इस घटना में यीशु की महिमा अदृश्य रूप में पत्र याकूब और योहन्ना पर प्रकट की गई मूसा ऑरेलिया भी यहां संकेत देते हुए यीशु के साथ प्रगट हुए कि सोने पुराने नियम की व्यवस्था और मोक्ष देवताओं की सूचनाओं की सूचनाओं की पुष्टि की और उन्हें जान जारी रखा है परंतु परमेश्वर ने चलो कोमोसा ऑरेलिया से भी बढ़कर यीशु का आदर करने और उसकी बात मानने की आज्ञा दी इस घटना ने चेलों को यहां से याद दिलाते और प्रशांत देते हुए तैयार किया कि उन्हें दूसरे सब लोगों से बढ़कर यीशु के प्रति विश्वास योग्य रहना है और यीशु के प्रति विश्वास योग्यता परमेश्वर और पुराने नियम में उसके प्रकाश के दिन प्रति विश्वास योग्यता का शुद्ध रूप है।\r\nअन्तत्: मरकुस 9:14-29 मैं मरकुस ने दुष्ट आत्माओं को नियंत्रित  करने की यीशु की योग्यता को प्रकट करने के द्वारा उसकी आदित्य सामर्थ पर ध्यान केंद्रित किया यीशु के चेले कठिन दुष्ट आत्मा को नहीं निकाल पाए और इशू ने सिखाया कि ऐसी दुष्ट आत्मा को केवल प्रार्थना के द्वारा ही निकाला जा सकता है परंतु स्वयं ईश्वर ने एक छोटी सी आज्ञा के द्वारा दुष्ट आत्मा को निकाल दिया इस प्रकार उसने सब के ऊपर अपनी श्रेष्ठता का प्रदर्शन किया और अपने चेलों को भरोसा दिलाया कि उसके पास अपनी इच्छा पूरी करने की असीम सामर्थ है उसके मारे जाने पर अनुभव किए जाने वाले संधि और डा के बावजूद उसकी सामर्थ्य से उन्हें उसके प्रति अपने विश्वास में दृढ़ रहने की प्रेरणा मिलनी चाहिए थी।\r\n2)सामना :- \r\n टकराव का मर्कुस का बिल एक दो भागों में विभाजित है पहला 11:1-12:44 मैं विरोध की घटना और दूसरा13:1-37 मैं जैतून का व्याख्यान अपनी सुसमाचार कि इस पूरे भाग में मत पूछ ने बताया कि किस प्रकार विश्व नहीं होगी अब वो को आशा है कि मर उसके सुसमाचार के पहले भागों में यीशु का यह यह वह में विवाद नहीं हुआ था उसका विरोध मुख्यता तब हुआ जब लोगों ने उसकी करुणा की शिव कई पर आपत्ति जताई थी परंतु इस भाग में मरकुस ने बताया कि ईश्वर ने सक्रियता से विरोध का प्रयास किया था कि वह अपनी क्रश मृत्यु की ओर बढ़ सके\r\n पहला मरकुस 11:1-11 मैं यीशु की यरूशलेम में विजय प्रवेश ने सार्वजनिक रूप से यहां घोषित किया कि वहां मसीहा और इसराइल का अवैध राजा है।\r\nफिर मरकुस 11:12-14,20,25 मैं सूखे हुए अंजीर के पेड़ के समान इसराइल को दोषी ठहराने और पद15-19 मैं मंदिर के शुद्धिकरण ने प्रसारित रूप से यह होगी अबू के नैतिक दृष्टिकोण पर हमला किया और लोगों पर उसकी अधिकार एवं प्रभाव को नीचा दिखाया।\r\n यीशु ने मरकुस11:27-12:12 मैं महायज्ञ व्यवस्थापक को और पूर्णिया से वाद-विवाद किया उसके अधिकार को दी गई उनकी चुनौती को जीतने के बाद उसने दाख की बारी के किसानों का दृष्टांत बताया जिसने यहूदी नेतृत्व पर परमेश्वर के विरुद्ध हत्या का आरोप लगाया इस समय वे उसे गिरफ्तार करने के लिए तैयार थे परंतु भीड़ के डर से वे पीछे हट गए।\r\nफिर मरकुस 12:13-17 मैं इशू नेहरू में कारों के इस मामले में परियों और हर उद्देश्य में वाद विवाद किया और उनका खंडन किया।\r\n इसके बाद मरकुस 12:18-27 मैं यीशु ने साबित किया कि पुनरुत्थान के बारे में पवित्र शास्त्र की  सत्यता को परियों ने गलत समझा था।\r\n और अंत में मरकुस 12:28-44 मैं उसने व्यवस्थापक को पर हमला किया यद्यपि यीशु ने माना कि उनमें से कुछ लोग के व्यवस्थापक था जो को जानते थे परंतु उसने बल दिया कि वे मुख्य लोग और सांसारिक महत्वता द्वारा नियंत्रित थे।\r\n किसी ना किसी तरह ही सुने प्रभावशाली यहूदियों को प्रत्येक समूह को व्यवस्थापक को परियों है रख दियो और यह सदुपयोग का सार्वजनिक रूप से सामना किया उसने प्रत्येक समूह को उससे घृणा करने और उसे मार डालने की खोज में रहने का एक कारण दिया था कि वह उन्हें पुरानी मृत्यु के लिए उकसा सके।\r\n यीशु द्वारा यदि आंखों के सामने का दूसरा मुख्य भाग ईश्वर उसके चेलों के बीच का मुख्य ध्यान है इसे सामान्य ताजे तो में ध्यान कहा जाता है क्योंकि या जैतून के पहाड़ पर दिया गया था विशाल रूप से यहां मरकुस 13:1-37 तक है इस भाग में ईश्वर ने अपने चेलों को भविष्य में आने वाली घटनाएं की चेतावनी दी ताकि उन पर अचानक ना पड़े उसने उन्हें बताएं कि उनके बारे में गवाही देने के कारण ने घसीट कर शासकों के सामने ले जाया जाएगा उन्हें पीटा जाएगा उसने गणना की जाएगी उनके परिवार बिखर जाएंगे वे प्राकृतिक आपदाओं और बड़े क्लबों को सहेंगे वास्तव में उसने यहां स्पष्ट किया कि सत्ता और कष्ट उसके द्वारा दूसरे आगमन तक मसीही कल ईशा की  विशेषता बने रहेंगे।\r\n3)अनुभव :-\r\n यीशु के कष्ट और मृत्यु का यथार्थ अनुभव परिचित घटनाओं से भरा है यह उदा दूसरा धोखा पत्र के इनकार की घोषणा गत समय में यीशु के साथ जागते रहने और प्रार्थना करने में चेलों की असफलता यीशु की गिरफ्तारी दो मुकदमे और पतरस का इनकार और अनंत यीशु का क्रूस पर चढ़ाया जाना है जाना यह काले डरावने अध्याय है इनका मिजाज पूर्व भाषी है वह असफलता से भरे हैं सऊदी अब वो की असफलता यहूदी और रूम इन इकाइयों प्राणियों की असफलता और चेलों की असफलता अत्याचार की शिकार रोमिक अलीशा को लिखते समय मर्कुस ने स्पष्ट किया कि यरूशलेम में मसीही अर्थ की प्रसव पीड़ा इतनी ही वृद्धि जितनी रूम में।\r\n यीशु द्वारा कष्ट और मृत्यु के अनुभव के मर्कुस के अभिलेख को चार मुख्य भागों में बांटा जा सकता है जिन की शुरुआत मरकुस14:1-11 मैं दफनाए जाने के लिए उसकी अभिषेक से होती है। इस बात में मर कुछ नहीं कुछ अत्यधिक महत्वपूर्ण विवरणों की जानकारी दी है पहला उसने कहा कि महायज्ञ को रिवर्स का पक्षों को गिरफ्तार करने और मारने की अवसर की खोज में थे दूसरा एक स्त्री ने अत्यधिक महंगे इससे यीशु का अभिषेक किया और उसने यह कह कर जवाब दिया कि उसने उसे दफनाए जाने के लिए यह किया है।\r\n इस प्रकार यीशु ने संकेत किया कि वह निकट भविष्य में मार डाला जाएगा तीसरा यह उदास कृतियों यीशु को महज एक और उसका पको को हाथ पकड़ा मारने का षड्यंत्र रचने लगा इसे हम यीशु के कष्ट और मृत्यु की कहानी में एक मोड़ के रूप में देख सकते हैं। उसकी मृत्यु आप एक धुंधली धमकी नहीं रह गई थी बल्कि कठिन भविष्य में होने वाले यथार्था बन गई थी।\r\n फिर मरकुस 14:12-42 मैं मर्कुस ने अपने चेलों के साथ ही सूखे अनंत घटनाओं के बारे में जानकारी दी।\r\n मर्कुस की कहानी के इस भाग की शुरुआत मरकुस14:12-13 मैं यीशु और उसके चेले द्वारा अंतिम भोज की तैयारी करने और खाने सा खाने के साथ होती है इस भोज के दौरान ही सुने प्रभु भोज के मसीही संस्कार की शुरुआत की थी उसने इस समय का उपयोग अपना कष्ट और मृत्यु के दौरान चालू की सहायता के लिए उन्हें कुछ अंतिम निर्देश देने के लिए भी किया उदाहरण के लिए उसने चेतावनी दी कि वे सब बिखर जाएंगे और उसने पत्र के इंकार की भोंसड़ी की। अंतिम भोज की बात मागणी के बगीचे में गया जैसा हम मरकुस 14:32-42 मैं देखते हैं इस अनुच्छेद के अनुसार ईश्वर से अधिक परेशान और व्याकुलता और दुख के मारे उसका प्राण निकलने पर था स्पष्ट की अपनी क्रश की मृत्यु की प्रतीक्षा में यीशु बहुत कष्ट है रहा था यीशु के कष्ट और मृत्यु के अनुभव के मरकुस के विवरण का तीसरा भाग  मरकुस 14:43-15:15 मैं यीशु की गिरफ्तारी और मुकदमों का है। इस बात की शुरुआत मरकुस15:1-15 मैं हमरो मिराज पाली पिलाती उसके सामने उसके मुकदमे के बारे में पढ़ते हैं इन अपमानजनक अनुभव के अंत में यीशु को कोड़े मारे जाते हैं और फिर उसे क्रूस पर चढ़ाए जाने के लिए रोमी सैनिकों को सौंप दिया जाता है यीशु के कष्ट और उसकी मृत्यु के अनुभव के मर्कुस विवरण के चौथे भाग में मरकुस15:16-47 मैं उसे पुरुष पर चढ़ाए जाने के बारे में बताया गया है।\r\n इसकी शुरुआत यीशु के को पीटे जाने अपमानित करने और एक अपराधी के समान क्रूस पर चढ़ाए जाने के लिए सैनिकों को सौंपने से होती है मानवीय दृष्टिकोण से यह कष्ट सहने के के बाहर था इस तथ्य नहीं घटनाओं को मरकुस के मूल पाठक को रोमियो से दृढ़ता से जोड़ा गया होगा कि ईश्वर ने रोगियों के हाथों इस दुर्व्यवहार को सहन किया था उन्होंने अपने और अपने प्रभु के कष्टों के बीच समानता ओं को शीघ्र ही देख लिया होगा और इसमें उन्हें अपनी स्वयं की घटनाएं के बीच स्थिर रहने की प्रेरणा मिली होगी।\r\n\r\n                                                                                {PRAISE THE LORD}', 9, '2020-07-26 04:49:02', '2020-08-04 22:35:45', NULL),
(1728, 500, 730, 'उत्तर = हम अपने वर्तमान परिस्थितियों में जो सेव काय करते हैं उसमें परमेश्वर हमें दर्शन देता है या फिर जिस फिल्ड में भी हम सेवर काय करते हैं उस फील्ड में मैं यदि परमेश्वर भेजा है तो जरूर परमेश्वर हमें एक नई मार्गदर्शन देगा वह हमें एक दर्शन के रूप में देगा और जब हम परमेश्वर से प्रार्थना करते हैं इस फील्ड में जा कर के तो परमेश्वर जब हमें दर्शन देता है या फिर हमें किसी भी प्रकार से वचन या किसी भी तरीके से बात करता है और उसके में मार्गदर्शन और उसके दिखाए हुए रास्ते के अनुसार जो दर्शन में में दिखाया जाता है फॉलो करते हैं तो जरूर प्रमोशन में इस्तेमाल करते हैं जिससे हमारी सेवक है कि भी बढ़ोतरी होती हैं और इस प्रकार से हमारी शेव काय के परिस्थितियों में हम परमेश्वर के दर्शन को हम जो हैं दर्शा सकते हैं। जब कोई भी एक सेवक परमेश्वर की सेवा कार्य करने के लिए निकलता है उससे पहले परमेश्वर होने दर्शन या फिर किसी भी तरीके से परमेश्वर उनसे बातचीत करता है और अपने सेवक आई के लिए उन्हें बुलाता है अपने पीछे कुछ लोग परमेश्वर की बुलेट को जल्दी समझ लेते कुछ लोग परमेश्वर के प्लाट को बहुत देरी से समझते हैं। और इसी प्रकार से कुछ लोग परमेश्वर की सेवक आए और परमेश्वर की दिखाए हुए रास्ते और दिखाई भी फील्ड में जब सकते हैं वहां पर सेवर काय करते हैं प्रार्थना करते हैं उस फील्ड के लिए उस प्लेफील्ड की बढ़ोतरी और वहां के लोगों के लिए वहां की एरिया के लिए प्रार्थना करते हैं उस समय में परमेश्वर ने एक दर्शन देता है या फिर वहां के बातें और वहां की चीजें परिस्थितियों के बारे में परमेश्वर अगुवाई करता है और जैसे-जैसे परमेश्वर अगवाई करता है उसी प्रकार से कार्य करने करने के द्वारा भी हम परमेश्वर की अगुवाई को दर्शा सकते हैं|   \r\n                                            \r\n                                                                                 {PRAISE THE LORD}', 8, '2020-07-26 05:06:44', '2020-08-04 22:35:45', NULL),
(1729, 500, 731, 'प्रभु यीशु मसीह योहन्न रचित सुसमाचार उसका  उसका 14 अध्याय में कहा मैं स्वर्गीय जाता हूं और जगह तैयार करता हूं और यदि जगह तैयार करूं तो तुम्हें लेने के लिए जल्दी ही आने वाला हूं प्रभु यीशु मसीह पृथ्वी पर जल्दी ही हमें लेने आने वाला है हमें लेने आने के बाद में प्रभु यीशु मसीह हमारा न्याय करेगा स्वर्ग पर उसके बाद में प्रभु प्रभु यीशु मसीह इस पृथ्वी पर जो है शैतान से युद्ध करेगा शैतान को हराकर के इस पृथ्वी पर अपना राज्य को स्थापित करेगा प्रभु यीशु मसीह का आगमन अभी तक नहीं हुआ है लेकिन हमें  मसीह जल्दी ही हमें लेने आने वाला है। प्रभु यीशु मसीह ने कहा कि मैं स्वर्ग पर जगह तैयार करूंगा और तुम्हें लेने आने आऊंगा अभी  जगह तैयार कर रहा है और अभी तक नहीं आया इसका मतलब का कोई जगह तैयार कर रहा है और जब कर कार्य पूरा होगा हमे लेने जल्दी ही आने वाला है प्रभु यीशु मसीह का आगमन निकट है इस पृथ्वी पर आज भी अनुग्रह का समय है जो प्रभु इस समय पर विश्वास करता है प्रभु उस पर अनुग्रह करता है जो अपने पापों को मान लेता है उसके पापों को क्षमा करता है और एक दिन प्रभु यीशु मसीह हमें बादल पर लेने आएगा उस दिन अनुग्रह का समय खत्म होगा परमेश्वर के पवित्र आत्मा उठा लिए जाएंगे और जब परमेश्वर की बहुत आत्मा उठा लिए जाएंगे तो इस पृथ्वी पर परमेश्वर के लोग  नहीं होंगे परंतु परमेश्वर की लोग प्रभु यीशु मसीह के साथ में स्वर्ग में होंगे। उसके बाद ही प्रभु यीशु मसीह इस पृथ्वी पर अपना राज्य को करने अर्थात अपना राज्य स्थापित करने इस पृथ्वी पर आएगा और जो है हम इस नानी की किताब में जो पढ़ते हैं दूसरी की आत्मा और दुष्ट और विनाश का पुत्र को प्रभु यीशु मसीह  आएगा और उन्हें हरा करके हमेशा के लिए उन्हें नर्क में डालकर की स्मृति पर राज करेगा प्रभु यीशु मसीह का राज स्थिति पर जल्दी से जल्दी आने वाला है। यीशु मसीह के अभी तक इस पृथ्वी पर राज्य नहीं हो देख रहे हैं ,उसके प्रत्युत्तर इस प्रकार दे सकते हैं।\r\n\r\n                                                                         {PRAISE THE LORD}', 8, '2020-07-26 05:22:46', '2020-08-04 22:35:45', NULL),
(1730, 503, 660, 'The word \"synchronic\" is derived from two Greek words: the preposition \"sun\" which means \"with\" or \"together\" and the noun chronos means \"time\". In relation to the historical events , it describes occurrences that took place \"together in time\" or \"at the same time\".\r\nThe term synchronic is used to indicate how biblical theologians often explore sets of events in Old Testament history that happened at the same time.\r\nIllustration:\r\nIn a movie, the directors tell their stories in a flow from beginning to the end. They depict how one event leads to another and so on. The movies is on , whole unit is broken down into smaller parts called scenes. every scene tells a portion of the larger story. Each story represents a synchronic moment in the movie, period of time in the film. \r\nSimilarly . The sychronic study of the Old Testament takes the same approach. The Biblical theologians concentrate their attention on particular periods of the time in the Old Testament  as if they were scenes in a movie rather on the flow of its entire story.Sometimes biblical theologians focus on relatively brief historical moments, but other times they concern themselves with relatively long periods', 8, '2020-07-28 17:47:30', '2020-08-04 22:35:09', NULL),
(1731, 503, 661, 'Synthesis means combining different components of something into a whole. Synchronic synthesis describes the way different components of a particular periods of history fit together in a coherent, logical structure.\r\nMany critical scholars distinguished biblical theology from systematic theology by pointing out the role of logic in each.Critical theologians believed that logic was a primary feature of the\"greek mindset\", but was relatively foreign to the \"hebrew\" mindset. \r\nAffirmation\r\nStudies have largely discredited the contrasts between Greek and Hebrew mindsets. Old Testament theology displays substantial concern fro logic and rational thought. Old Testament theology does not employ the standards of formal western philosophical traditions:\r\nFew technical terms \r\nvariety of genres\r\ndifferent emphases\r\n no all en-compassing system\r\nIn Romans 5:12-14 Paul treated the time from Adam\'s fall to the giving of the law as one synchronic unit. Paul\'s main concern was to prove how the far-reaching effects of Adam\'s sin far reaching effects of Christ\'s obedience', 8, '2020-07-28 18:01:56', '2020-08-04 22:35:09', NULL),
(1732, 503, 662, 'Poets of the old Testament were interested in two different worlds that tell us about history:\r\n1. THAT WORLD: THE WORLD THEY WROTE ABOUT\r\nWhen writing about that world, they provided objective facts about God\'s acts and word.\r\nin first place, Poetry often opened windows to the past as we see in Exodus 15  :1-21. where we see the song that Miriam and Moses sang.\r\nIn second place,Old testament often provided windows to contemporary historical information about  their own time as in Psalms 1.\r\nIn third place Old Testament writers turned their readers attention towards the future as in Isaiah 40:1-11\r\n2. THEIR WORLD:WORLD OF THEIR READERS\r\nThe old testament writers design their texts to influence their original readers in particular ways :Exodus 15, Psalms 1 and Isaiah 40\r\nNARRATIVES:\r\nTrue stories about historical peoples, place and events that reveal many details about history through:\r\n words ,speeches , characters , place and connections,\r\nTWO WORLDS:\r\nTHAT WORLD: THE SUBJECT OF THEIR TEXT\r\nNarratives largely focus on the past, and only rarely mention the present or the future.\r\nMoses wrote about creation etc\r\n\r\nTHEIR WORLD: the world in which the readers lived\r\nThey wanted their readers to think, act and feel in certain ways within their worlds in light of past events.', 8, '2020-07-28 18:20:16', '2020-08-04 22:35:09', NULL),
(1733, 503, 663, 'It is important while discerning historical information not to expect them to be like modern journalistic historical writing. Historians must seek to be as exacting as their counter parts in science s like chemistry and biology. True historical records will include every significant fact about a situation to give a balance account. They will avoid all subjective evaluations that will prejudice readers.\r\n\r\nOld testament narratives wrote in ways that were determined largely by their didactic purposed and not by our modern sensibilities. These narratives were only as comprehensive as suited the didactic purposes of their writers. they dint not include every significant fact. For example in Solomon\'s life 2 Chronicles 1-9 , they emitted every negative dimension of Solomon\'s reign.\r\nThey were only as precise as their didactic purposes required. They did not meet the modern criterion of good history writing', 8, '2020-07-28 18:33:28', '2020-08-04 22:35:09', NULL),
(1734, 503, 664, 'Old Testament writers were only as precise as their didactic purposes required . There is vital difference between precision and truth. In every aspect of life, precision is always a matter of degree and so long as we respond with as much precision as is needed , no one accuses us of misrepresenting facts. This was true with the Old Testament authors .they were only as precise as they needed to be reach their didactic goals.\r\n1 Kings 9:5 and 2 Chronicles 7:18, we can read God spoke to David and God covenanted with David respectively. so we can see here that Old Testament narratives were not designed to repeat words and thoughts if god or anyone else with absolute precision. What they wrote was historically true. They did not misrepresent what God said.\r\nNumbers of people, measurements and geographical references often do not modern significant standards. But this lack of modern precision does not mean the accounts are untrue.\r\nIn summary we can say with confidence that old testament narratives were not designed to meet modern standards of history writing, but they represent fully reliable historical information that will enables us to construct synchronic synthesis Testament theology .', 8, '2020-07-28 18:50:53', '2020-08-04 22:35:09', NULL),
(1735, 505, 781, 'The author of the Hebrews quotes to the Old Testament nearly 100 times . There are mainly five way that the author of Hebrews repeatedly quotations from Old Testament\r\n1. FACTUAL BACKGROUNDS:\r\nIn first place he drew attention to factual backgrounds. Hebrews 7:2 He refers to the name Melchizedek from Genesis 14:17 and then he compared with Jesus.\r\n2. THEOLOGICAL OUT LOOKS\r\nThe author focused on theological beliefs affirmed by the scriptures like beliefs about God himself and other matters in close relation to God.\r\nauthor quoted angels as serving spirits in Hebrews 1:7, the author cited God\'s oath to Abraham \r\n3.MORAL OBLIGATIONS:\r\nThe author pointed out that God placed certain moral requirements on his people in Old Testaments .In Hebrews 12:5,6 showed that Proverbs 3:11,12 urged Israel not be discouraged when God disciplined them.\r\n4. ESCHATOLOGICAL PREDICTIONS:\r\nIn old Testament in many passages authors made predictions about last days or latter days as in Deuteronomy 32:43 or Jeremiah 31:31-34\r\n5. DYNASTIC IDEALS:\r\nHe had referred to a number of dynastic ideals established for David\'s lineage in the Psalms.\r\nThe author of Hebrews insisted that Jesus is the supreme , perfect fulfillment of the ideals for David\'s royal house.', 7, '2020-07-31 18:17:09', '2020-08-04 22:34:20', NULL),
(1736, 505, 782, 'The book of Hebrews deal t with angelic revelation in Hebrews 1:1-2:18.\r\nin the first century Jewish community exalted angels as powerful , glorious creatures who brought divine revelations to inferior human beings.They gave excessive honor to the angels. These exaggerated honor for angels raised a serious challenge to those who followed Christ. \r\nAs Jesus was flesh and blood a human being. The author responded to this challenge in five steps:\r\n1. In Hebrews 1:1-4 he wrote that his audience  should follow Jesus Christ because Jesus is the God\'s supreme source of divine revelation an that the revelation that the brought was superior to any revelation given through angels.\r\n2. In Hebrews 1:5-14 the author of Hebrews explained that Jesus is greater than angels because he alone is God\'s messianic Son.He noted that angels are nothing more than the spirits sent to serve those who inherit salvation in Christ.\r\n3.The author exhorted in Hebrews 2:1-4 His audience to pay careful attention to the great message of salvation first announced by Jesus .He reminded violating messages from  angels received great punishment then how could anyone escaping he message from Jesus the Son Of God Himself.\r\n4. Hebrews 2:5-9 supports belief in the supremacy of Christ by explaining that Jesus is now ruler over the angels. this final glory is give to a human beings is anticipated in Christ\'s current reign in heaven as God\'s royal high priest.\r\n5. Hebrews 2:10-18, here the author demonstrated that Jesus is Abraham\'s descendant an Jesus will share his glory with Abraham\'s descendants , not with angels.', 8, '2020-07-31 18:35:17', '2020-08-04 22:34:20', NULL),
(1737, 505, 783, 'The fourth major division in Hebrews 8:1-11:40 focuses on the new covenant.\r\nJesus mediates the new covenant as the royal high priest in heaven.\r\nLet us discuss how the new covenant is superior to the old\r\n1. The old Testament failed because of Israel\'s sins by the contrast , the new covenant of Jeremiah 31 cannot fail as Hebrews 8:6 tells us it is found on better promises\r\n2.Hebrews 9:1-28 the author elaborated on the fact that Jesus heavenly royal priest hood is superior to the Levitical priesthood.\r\n3. Moses covenant was initiated with death and blood , the new covenant was initiated with death and blood with Christ\'s blood in the sanctuary of god;s heavenly place,\r\n4.In Hebrews 10: 1-18 the new covenant Jesus high priesthood brought final forgiveness of sin\r\nLevitical,sacrifices could not bring final forgiveness of sin ,Jeremiah\'s  prediction of a new covenant promised that God would forgive that sin of his people forever. Jesus accomplished that, so there is no longer nay need for animal sacrifice.', 7, '2020-07-31 18:50:16', '2020-08-04 22:34:20', NULL),
(1738, 505, 784, 'The author refers to the Old Testament nearly 100 times. to understand better way the things written in New Testament we need to have a basic knowledge of the things given in Old Testament. When we start from Genesis, we come to know a creator God and then as we go on reading to the next books in old Testament we come to know how God choose some people out of the nations to follow him. \r\nWhen we understand about commandments, sacrifices, laws, feasts then only we understand why and how Jesus died on the cross as an eternal sacrifice for our sins.\r\nWhen we read about certain characters in Bible in Old Testament , they inspire us greatly to be faithful and they also remind us of God\'s faithfulness and forgiveness. \r\nThe covenants that God made from Adam to Davidic covenant reminds us of God fulfilling His covenant to each one with faithfulness.\r\nThe Old Testament gives us an outlook about the history of humanity  and God\'s walk with His people.\r\nThe Books of Psalms is of great encouragement to any common man and broken people.\r\nThe book of Proverbs teaches us to wise and careful and tells us the importance of His words.\r\nThe prophetical books opens the window to the things that is to happen in latter days and has happened in old days.\r\nMany more to say about the inspiration that we get from Old Testament, it  always proclaims about a God who never failed to fulfill His faithfulness to His people, even when they go astray.', 8, '2020-07-31 19:05:46', '2020-08-04 22:34:20', NULL),
(1739, 505, 785, 'The book of Hebrews offers great treasure to followers of Christ. Its theological outlook penetrate deeply into all that Christ has done for us. The book of Hebrews call us to turn gospel scripture as our authority and to receive Christ as  the fulfillment of all  that God has promised. \r\nJesus Christ has died for our sins . He has overcome sin for us. While Levitical sacrifices could not bring final forgiveness of sins , Jeremiahs\' prediction of a new covenant promised  that would forgive the sins of his people forever . Jesus accomplished that . so there is no longer any need for animal sacrifice.\r\nwhen we see youths or non believers struggling with their past or present sins we encourage them to trust and believe son Jesus Christ as He is sufficient to forgive sins and make them a new creation.\r\nWe try to initiate faith on Jesus Christ.\r\nHebrews 9:11 this emphasized that those who have faith in Christ have been freed from sin through his perfect priestly atonement and now have opened access to the throne of grace in heaven.\r\nSo this shows and proves that when Christ has overcome sin for us Christ is sufficient for us , for any of us , regardless of how weak and strong we are, His atonement has made us free from sin and His grace is sufficient for us to lead a godly life as we have been gifted with His righteousness. Hebrews 9:26', 8, '2020-07-31 19:24:39', '2020-08-04 22:34:20', NULL),
(1740, 507, 866, 'The creed was a collective work that gradually developed over several centuries. Rules of Faith: summaries of beliefs and practices: To preserve the teachings of the church and train its people (especially leaders) Often these rules varied from from congregation to congregation. Generally speaking, they included affirmations of important doctrines as well as teachings and traditions. \r\nCreeds were the summaries of doctrinal portions of church\'s rules of faith. These were recited in liturgical settings. One ancient creed that rose to prominence was from the church in Rome, often called the Roman Creed, which was similar to the Apostolic Creed. the Apostolic creed eventually came into widespread use, especially in Western churches. In the early centuries, its precise wording varied from church to church. But in the eighth century the wording was generally standardized into the form that we recognize and use today.', 6, '2020-08-01 15:37:57', '2020-08-04 22:33:46', NULL),
(1741, 507, 867, 'The bible is our only inspired infallible rule of faith and practice. Creeds, are fallible teaching tools that summarize our understanding of Scripture. And the apostles\' creed was created to help Christians learn and remain true to the teachings of the bible. The purpose of the apostles creed is as follows;\r\n1. Scripture- Scripture in all its parts was word of Christ, and that it was the source of all true doctrine. Basis of doctrine, Sola scriptura- this is the perspective that scripture is the only infallible rule of faith, and final arbiter in any theological controversy.\r\n2. Traditional teaching- The early church depended on the traditional teachings of the church to summarize and protect the teachings of scripture. Christian leaders created summaries so that all Christians would know and affirm the basic content of faith. \r\n3. Apostolic Creed- the apostles\' creed was largely used to confirm that new Christians believed the fundamental teachings of the Bible.  The goal was to ensure that the churches did not stray from the original meaning of scripture.', 8, '2020-08-01 15:46:53', '2020-08-04 22:33:46', NULL),
(1742, 507, 868, 'The creed is based on the belief that there is only one God and that this God exists in three persons. The trinity is one of the most important beliefs of Christianity. One essence- only one God. By the term person, we mean a distinct, self aware personality. And by the term essence, we are referring to God\'s fundamental nature or the substance of which he consists. \r\nThree persons: The Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit- distinct from one another. \r\nFather- Almighty, Maker of heaven and earth. The creed\'d description of Father doesn\'t distinguish Christianity from other religions that express belief in a sovereign creator.\r\nSon- The creed mentions Jesus\' incarnation, his coming to earth as human baby, and living a genuinely human life. And it speaks of his suffering, death, burial, resurrection and ascension into heaven.\r\nHoly Spirit- The creed associates the Holy Spirit with the church, and with our experience of salvation both now and in the future. The creed says enough about God and his persons to distinguish those who affirm the historic Christian faith from those who do not.', 7, '2020-08-01 15:56:21', '2020-08-04 22:33:46', NULL),
(1743, 507, 869, '1. Participation- The creed emphasizes the importance of participating in the church. The bible teaches Christians to form an actual physical community and it insists that this community is extremely important to every believer. It is not to be limited to spiritual fellowship, although it is true that Christians have spiritual communion with each other through Christ and his Spirit. Rather, our community is to be like a family or neighborhood. It is to consist of people who interact with each other face to face. \r\n2. Preservation- The creed affirms the fact that Christ appointed his church in part to protect and proclaim the gospel and other truths. According to Jude, part of church\'s job is to contend for faith, to protect the truths and beliefs that have been entrusted to it against those who promote false teachings and practices. We have to keep trying to preserve doctrine in the church.', 7, '2020-08-01 16:05:25', '2020-08-04 22:33:46', NULL),
(1744, 507, 870, 'The Apostle\'s Creed is foundational to theology because it introduces us to the teachings of apostles recorded in scripture. \r\n1. Standard- The apostles\' creed functions as a doctrinal standard because it presents several of the biggest most important ideas of Christianity. These ideas are taught so clearly in Scripture that they should be recognized and embraced by everyone. Using the creed as a standard helps us remain faithful to scripture when convincing false teachers present us with bad theology. So, it helps to have a short list of essential beliefs that can anchor us to the teachings of Scripture and the apostles\' creed provides such an anchor. \r\n2. Logical Basis- Logically basic ideas are the sources of other ideas. The creed provides the big doctrines so we can: see the relationship between the different beliefs in our theological systems. Doctrines that are more remote from Scripture in ways that harmonize with our fundamental beliefs helps us remain faithful to scripture.', 8, '2020-08-01 16:14:40', '2020-08-04 22:33:46', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(1745, 508, 665, 'The english word \"diachronic \"derives from the two Greek Words :first the preposition dia which often means \"through\" or \"throughout\" and the second , the Greek Nouns Chronos which means \"time\". Diachrony  is a concern with the passage of time. \r\nIn the case of biblical theology, the term \"diachronic \"points to the ways the Old Testament  theology transformed , changed or developed through the time.\r\nDiachronic approches to the Bible concentrate on how theological structures progressively unfoldes through the time. It says about God\'s revelations took place or developed as history moved forward.\r\nLooking at the Old Testament diachronically is like concentrating on the storyline of a movie as it moves from scene to scene.\r\nIt\'s to focus on the ways a film progressively unfolds its drama from beginning to the end.', 7, '2020-08-01 17:43:36', '2020-08-04 22:33:16', NULL),
(1746, 508, 666, 'We use the tem \"development \"instead of simply speaking of diachronic changes to suggest two main ideas. First the changes in Old Testament theological structures always move toward fulfilling God\'s purposes for history and second , we speak of development because theological changes only occur through God\'s providential involvement in history.\r\n1.Divine purposes-\r\nIsaiah 46:10 reflects a common outlook throughout God\'s unfailing purposes for his creation. When we go through the Scriptures , they affirm that everything in history including shifts in theology, always accomplish God\'s unfailing purposes for his creation.\r\nGod;s goals for history exist not inky as broad, long term goals , but also short term goals. God has an all-encompassing kingdom purpose for history.From the beginning, his design has been to glorify himself by extending his heavenly kingdom to the entire earth through the work of his image and this unites all of God\'s purposes\r\n2. Divine providence:\r\nWhen we look at Old testament , we see that the road is actually filled with steep inclines, fast descents and sharp turns to the left an the right.These abrupt shifts are caused by God\'s providence, his complex involvement with his creation. The only explanation that we can hold with certainity is that God simply wanted these theological shifts to take place.', 8, '2020-08-01 18:02:43', '2020-08-04 22:33:16', NULL),
(1747, 508, 667, 'The six Old Testaments covenants fall into three main categories. First . the universal covenants with Adam and Noah.\r\nSecond, the national covenants with Abraham, Moses and David.\r\nand third , the New Covenant predicted by Old Testaments.\r\n1. UNIVERSAL COVENANT\r\nWe speak of the covenants with Adam and Noah as universal  because they were made between God and all of humanity.  the relationship between Adam and God emphasized that all human beings have a basic responsibility of loyal service to their creator.\r\n2. NATIONAL COVENANT:\r\nGod narrowed his covenantal attention primarily just one ethnic group, establishing Israel as the nation that would lead the rest of humanity in service to God. God\'s special benevolence toward Abraham and his descendants , God made a second covenant with Israel through Moses when he brought them to  Mount Sinai\r\n3.NEW COVENANT\r\nThe prophets of Israel faced the time when Israel would go into exile, they spoke of a covenant , when God would make a final covenant with his people. The New Covenant was designed to govern God\'s people when God fulfilled his promise to re-establish his people after exile and to spread his kingdom. and the new testament explains the work of Christ , the Holy Spirit and ministry through the apostles', 8, '2020-08-01 18:21:27', '2020-08-04 22:33:16', NULL),
(1748, 508, 668, 'Biblical Typology is the study of diachronic developments between the theological structures closely associated with significant persons , institutions and events in scripture.\r\nin simple language , we might say that typology is the study of the types. The word \"type\" derives from the Greek word tupos.\r\nBiblical theology applies the term typology to any diachronic development of topics in Old Testament theology. On occasions , biblical theologians will speak of the typology of the doctrine of God, or the typology of worship, and simply mean that these are then ways developed in the Bible.\r\nFor example Jesus spoke of   a typological connection between Moses\' bronze serpent and himself.\r\n1. Typology functions as a figure of speech For example Romans 5:14 the apostle Paul declared that Adam was a pattern or type\r\n2. A second feature of biblical theology is that compared elements are quite varied. In Peter 3:21 Peter compared the event of Noah\'s flood with baptism\r\n3. In the third place , typologies in the Bible always compare the theological structures that are closely associated with their elements.\r\n4.A fourth characteristic of typologies in Scripture is that they always reflect diachronic developments', 8, '2020-08-01 18:39:08', '2020-08-04 22:33:16', NULL),
(1749, 508, 669, 'We do apply the Scriptures concerning aspects of Old Testament worship as sacrifice , temple,and Passover meal but in a different way. Romans 12:1 says we are to offer  or bodies or ourselves as a \r\n living pleasing sacrifice to God. Jesus offered himself as a sacrifice on the cross forever, for us. Now we believe on him but at the same way we are living sacrifice to him. \r\nPaul says in Romans 12:1 that we should present our bodies  as a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable to God which is our reasonable service. \r\nWe offer praises, songs , making melodies unto him. 1 Corinthians 3:16 says we are the temple of God. Now we are His temple and the Spirit of God dwells in us. We have to keep our heart and mind holy for him to dwell in us. \r\nJesus Christ is the Passover Lamb , He has been sacrificed once and for all. And when we partake in His blood and body during Holy communion. 1 Corinthians 5:7', 8, '2020-08-01 18:54:15', '2020-08-04 22:33:16', NULL),
(1750, 510, 871, 'God as he is presented in scripture by looking at two subjects. The \'\'singularity\'\' of God, the fact that he is the only God that exists. And the \'\'simplicity\'\' of God, noting that he really is only one God, despite the fact that he has three persons. \r\n1. Polytheism- Belief in the the existence of multiple Gods. In polytheism, no one God can claim to be the only supernatural being who exercises control over the universe. One reason for this was so common that polytheism was often required by law.\r\n2. Monotheism- Belief in only one God. Scripture asserts that there is only one God- 1 Kings 8.60- The Lord is God...there is no other. Psalms 86.10- You alone are God. \r\n3. Christianity- The creed does not explicitly say that there is only one God. It is organized around a Trinitarian Formula. It indicates that the God of Christianity is the only one who deserves to be called \"God.\"', 8, '2020-08-04 15:40:53', '2020-08-04 22:32:44', NULL),
(1751, 510, 872, 'God has three persons, but only one essence. The term \"person\" refers to distinct, self aware personality and that the term \"essence\" refers to God\'s fundamental nature, or the substance of which he consists God\'s essence is not a composite of different substances; but a unified whole consisting of only one substance. God has a simple unified essence, they were denying that the Father, Son and Holy Spirit were three separate Gods that somehow joined together in the trinity. And instead, they were affirming that these three persons had always existed together as only one God. We believe in only one God- one divine being- who exists in three persons.', 6, '2020-08-04 15:50:14', '2020-08-04 22:32:44', NULL),
(1752, 510, 873, 'The word ontological means being related to being. It is considering how the three persons of the Trinity are integrated with one another, and how they share a single essence. From the perspective of ontology, all three of God\'s persons are infinite, eternal and unchangeable. And each has the same essential divine attributes, such as wisdom, power, holiness, justice, goodness and truth. \r\nThe word \'\'economic\'\' means \'\'relating to household management.\'\' When we consider how God\'s persons interact with each other, how they relate to one another as individual persons. \r\nFrom both the ontological and economic perspective the Father is said to be the first person, generated by the Father, and the Holy Spirit is said to proceed from the Father. Besides being the first person of the ontological Trinity, the Father is also called the first person of the economic Trinity. \r\nThe Son is generated by the Father (externally generated) and Holy Spirit proceed from the Father (externally proceeds) in the ontological trinity.\r\nIn economic trinity, authority is over the Son and the over the Holy Spirit.', 7, '2020-08-04 16:00:34', '2020-08-04 22:32:44', NULL),
(1753, 510, 874, 'Fatherhood- Scriptures that talk about God\'s fatherhood come from the Old Testament, prior to the time that God clearly revealed his truine nature. The word \"Father\" refers and foremost to the entire Trinity, and not just to the person of the Father. \r\n1. Creator- Scripture refers to God as father of everything he has created. For instance, in passages like Deut 32.6, Isa 43.6-7, God\'s general fatherhood over creation motivates him to show great patience with our fallen world and with sinful humanity in particular.\r\n\r\n2. King- God was called father because he was the great king that ruled over all the kings of the world, and because he ruled directly over his chosen nation Israel. Jesus instructed his disciples to pray to \"Our Father in Heaven.\"\r\n\r\n3. Family Head- In the old testament, God is portrayed as family head of nation Israel. Everyone is familiar with concept of family head. Well, Scripture often describes God\'s relationship to his people in the same terms. This description also continues in New Testament.', 7, '2020-08-04 16:09:45', '2020-08-04 22:32:44', NULL),
(1754, 510, 875, '1. Absolute- The father has complete freedom to do whatever he wants with his creation. Scripture often compares his absolute authority to a potter\'s authority over his clay. We find this description in places like Isa 29.16, Isa 45.9 etc. God is the creator of all, has the freedom and right to do whatever he wants with what he creates. \r\n2. Exclusive- Besides having absolute authority the Father also has exclusive authority over everything he created. The Father\'s authority as creator is exclusive in sense that no creature possess absolute authority. Absolute authority belongs only to the creator and God is the only creator. The authority ultimately resided in the Father,and was his exclusive prerogative. \r\n3. Exhaustive- God\'s authority is exhaustive, we mean that it extends over everything he has created, in every detail. And there is at least important implications of the fact. First, everyone is under God\'s authority. There is no person or other creation the obligation to obey God. Second, Everything is under God\'s authority. His authority extends to every detail of what he has created. Everything in creation either functions as God wants it to, and therefore good or rebels against him, is therefore evil.', 8, '2020-08-04 16:22:08', '2020-08-04 22:32:44', NULL),
(1755, 506, 850, 'God\'s authority :\r\nGod\'s authority in ethics is absolute. His moral judgements, his outlook on good and evil. God alone holds ultimate authority, and is always superior to all other authority.  God\'s authority is exhaustive, it extends to everything he has created in detail. All humans are accountable to God irrespective of their culture or religion. Everything in creation functions as God wants it to and is therefore good. Everything else against is considered to be evil.\r\n\r\nGod\'s Control :\r\nChristianity has always affirmed that God is the creator and he exercises sovereign control over his creation. This has been the basis for ethical responsibility. We are to live morally and reverently becaus God is working in our lives, causing to will and to act according to his plan. God orders creation, our circumstances are never an excuse to our unethical choices. \r\n\r\nGod\'s Presence :\r\nGod is omnipresent, hence us judges us on the basis of what he sees. Our ethical decisions must always account for God\'s presence with us as a royal judge to be always considered as we make ethical decisions.\r\nJesus earthly presence also provides us with the supreme pattern of righteousness for all human life. \r\nHoly spirit bestows gifts for our spiritual growth & obligates us to identify and use the gifts that God has given us.', 0, '2020-08-05 15:20:46', '2020-08-05 15:20:46', NULL),
(1756, 506, 851, 'Preternatural realm is inhabited by invisible spirits such as angels and demons. Angels and demons have a significant impact that happens in real life. Preternatural world is an important consideration when it comes to making ethical decisions.\r\n\r\nAs we study the scripture, it teaches us that God has also populated the universe with a vast number of spiritual persons known as angles and demons. They both are considered to be rational beings that have wills and personalities.\r\n\r\nWhen God created angles, they were pure and perfect serving God in heaven. But some of the angels rebelled against God and were removed from their blessed estate to being condemned. \r\n\r\nAngles serve as God\'s loyal messengers and agents. They communicate God\'s word to human beings, and they interact with humanity on God\'s behalf, Angelse are also known as ministering spirits sent to serve those who will inherit salvation. \r\n\r\nDemons are also able to interact with the natural realm, but they do in order to harm us.  Demons constantly tempt us trying to lead us away from moral choices\r\n\r\nInteractions / Spiritual Warfare :\r\n\r\nEver since Satan and his demons rebelled against God, they have been locked in spiritual battle against God\'s holy angels. \r\n\r\nAs Apostle Paul teaches us in the book of Ephesians, our enemies include the demonic rulers, authorities, powers and forces in the preternatural world. It also allows and influences us in ethical ways, as angels help us find ways to obey god, whereas demons tempt us to sin.\r\n\r\nThough Jesus has already crippled demon\'s ability to overtake us through his death and resurrection. but still demons persist in skirmishes against us, as a result we always need to be vigilant and ready for battle, relying on the armor of God and his grace to take a stand against evil forces.', 0, '2020-08-05 15:38:17', '2020-08-05 15:38:17', NULL),
(1757, 506, 852, 'Natural World includes\r\n1) Creation - original condition\r\n2) Fall - of humanity into sin\r\n3) Redemption - of humanity from sin\r\n\r\nCreation : \r\nWhen we study the book of Genesis, Moses described the creation of the entire natural realm in a way that emphasized the central importance of huanity over the earth.\r\nHuman beings are a part of nature\r\nGod created us from the dust of the ground\r\nWe have an ethical obligation to protect nature\r\nHuman beings are lords or rules over nature, to have dominion over all of God\'s creation, to rule, administer, to govern - to promote life and growth and turning this world into a kingdom that is fit to inhabit.\r\n\r\nFall : \r\nAfter the sin of Adam & Eve, God cursed both the human race, the earth and subjected it to corruption. Causing the earth to oppose the lordship of humanity.\r\nIt became difficult for humans to work and produce food.\r\nNature too is a recipient and instrument in God\'s curses\r\nNature is not as it was originally designed it often complicated our ethical decisions since it is corrupted by sin.\r\n\r\nRedemption :\r\nRedemption reversed the curses on the natural realm. Natural realm became an instrument of redemption\r\nGod purges corruption of the natural world through redemption of humanity.\r\nGod uses things in the natural realm as tools in the redemptive process\r\nEvents in the natural world testify to God\'s greatness\r\nGod will refine both heaven and earth to create a new heaven and a new earth\r\nThe corruption of natural world will last until humanity\'s redemption is completed at Christ\'s return.', 0, '2020-08-05 15:56:41', '2020-08-05 15:56:41', NULL),
(1758, 506, 853, 'Preternatural realm :\r\nIt is based beyond nature\r\nDistinct aspect of creation\r\nInhabited by invisible spirits such as angels and demons\r\nAngels & demons have a significant impact on the things that happen in the natural world.\r\nAngels and demons are intelligent rational beings that have wills and personalities\r\nAngels are those who remained loyal to God\r\nDemons are the rebel angels\r\nAngels serve as God\'s loyal messengers and agents, they communicate his world to humans they interact with huanity on God\'s behalf. \r\nDemons are just the opposite of Angels, they have many bad implications on human lives.\r\n\r\nNatural Realms : \r\nRealm is based on creation and nature\r\nNatural aspect of creation\r\nInhabited by human beings which form part of creation and natural world\r\nHuman beings are called to govern the natural world to administer, turning the world into a kindom to fit to inhabit.\r\nHuman beings are lords or rulers over nature, to govern, to administer\r\nDue to the fall into Sin, human beings were disloyal to God\'s command and and had to suffer corruption.\r\nNatural world is not completely corrupted by the Fall\r\nThough nature is corrupted by sin, it is still good, it is God\'s reation and God uses to minister to us and to bless us\r\nRedemption from God, reverses the instrument of cursing and and the recipient of cursing.\r\n\r\nSatan and his demons rebelled against God and they have been in battle against God\'s holy angels. \r\nThere is always a battle going on between the spiritual forces and the demonic forces.\r\nApostle Paul teaches us through the book of Ephesians 6:12 that our warfare is against the enemies demonic rulers, authorities, powers and fores in the preternatural world.', 0, '2020-08-05 16:12:14', '2020-08-05 16:12:14', NULL),
(1759, 506, 854, 'Goodness of humanity will focus on three details of humanity\'s creation :\r\n\r\n1) Humanity was created in the image of God\r\n2) God\'s blessing on humanity\r\n3) Cultural mandate that God assigned to the human race\r\n\r\nHumanity :\r\nIn the image an likeness of God, we need to consider the attributes like reason, spirituality, moral nature, immortality and our original righteousness. Humans share these attributes in common with God.\r\nGod appointed huan beings to be his living images, so whenever we see a human being it reminds us of God.\r\nWhen we wrongfully disrespect human beings, we dishonor the Lord whose image we are\r\n\r\nBlessing : \r\nAfter the creation of mankind, God blessed humanity \r\nGood is not only in terms of God\'s character, but also in terms of what he blesses and approves. \r\nWhen God blessed humanity during creation time, he indicated that humanity was morally good\r\nGod\'s blessings were just not an affirmation of their behavior but of their being blessed.\r\n\r\nCultural Mandate :\r\nGod\'s cultural mandate to humanity were - be fruitful and increase in number, fill the earth and subdue it. Have dominion over the fish of the sea, birds of the air and over every livng creature that moves on the ground\r\nHumans were God\'s representatives as vassal kings to fill, subdue and rule over.\r\nGod indicated that humanity was physically and morally capable of accomplishing the task of God in this world.\r\nGod created us morally pure in our being, possessing the attribute of goodness and being free from the corruption of sin.\r\nGoodness was rooted in our very being.', 0, '2020-08-05 16:31:23', '2020-08-05 16:31:23', NULL),
(1760, 506, 855, 'Fall has actually damaged our ability to obtain moral knowledge, Unbelievers can read the bible and understand its commands but cannot gain access to the true knowledge and revelation that God has to offer. \r\n\r\nFall has indered mankind from the following 3 aspects, namely\r\n\r\n1)Access to Revelation :\r\nFall has hindered humanity\'s access to revelation by limiting the Holy Spirit\'s work of illumination and inward leading. Illumination and inward leading is a divine gift \r\nIn some sense God provides a easure of both illumination and inward leading to all fallen human beings.\r\nHoly Spirit does not provide the same measure of illumination and inward leading to unbelievers that he provides to believers\r\n\r\n2) Understanding of Revelation \r\nHuman beings have the cognitive ability to understand the basic teachings of God\'s revelation. But moral understanding depends on more than mere cognition, it involves the whole person\r\nEthical judgements  are based on many non cognitive factos that influence our ethical evaluations, such as our emotions, consciences, intuitions, desires, fears, weakness, failures etc\r\nFallen human beings have eys and ears to receive God\'s revelation but their hearts are hardened, and they are unable to grasp the full understanding or the revelation.\r\nDue to the fall human hearts were hardened, that hinders them from fully understanding God\'s revelation\r\n\r\n3) Obedience to Revelation\r\nKnowledge and obedience are essentially the same things, fall hinders our knowledge of God and we are unable to obey\r\nFirst we receive and understand God\'s revelation and then we obediently apply it to our lives, whereas due to the fall they lack both understanding and obedience. \r\nIn the Scripture, obedience is a prerequisite to knowlege', 0, '2020-08-05 16:50:09', '2020-08-05 16:50:09', NULL),
(1761, 506, 856, 'The Scripture makes it clear that God has authority, the right to rule over all of creation and it derives from the fact that \r\nGod is the creator, sustainer of all creation\r\nAll of creation was brought to life by God and depends on him for continued existence\r\nGod\'s authority has three basic attributes\r\n\r\nABSOLUTE :\r\nGod has absolute,, complete, total freedom over his creation.\r\nScripture illustrates God\'s absolute authority by comparing it with the authority as potter has over the clay\r\nGod is the creator and has all the freedom and right to do whatever he wants with what he creates\r\nThe absolute power applies to all of creation\r\nGod has the freedom and the right to act upon, as he sees fit to require of it. \r\nWhen God reveals his ethical judgements they are true and never subject to scrutiny\r\n\r\nEXCLUSIVE\r\nGod has exclusive authority over everything he has created his absolute or complete authority belogs only to the creator, and God alone holds this authority. All other authorities are delegated by God, and is subject to God\'s authority. All smaller or lesser authorities can be overruled by te greater authority of God.\r\n\r\nEXHAUSTIVE \r\nGod has exhaustive authority over the universe. This authority extends over everything he has created in detail.\r\nEven though most humans rebel against God and refuse to submit to his commands, his moral judgements aply to them as well. All human beings irrespective of our culture or religion, we are all accountable to God\r\n\r\nGod\'s sovereign control is completely compatible with human responsibility. \r\nGod\'s attributes are immutable, they do not change, they existed before the universe was formed and is still active & present and also will continue for the future. As God can never change his character or attributes, they are constant. The attributes do not conflict as they have been well defined in the entire personality and character of God. \r\n\r\nAs humans we are still learning about God\'s several attributes and characters by studying his word. God\'s word is also immutable and stands perfect for us to learn more about God.', 0, '2020-08-05 17:07:28', '2020-08-05 17:07:28', NULL),
(1762, 512, 871, 'Basic idea of God as he is presented in Scripture by looking at two subjects.  on the one hand we will explore what the theoretical afte call...\r\nMany passage in Scripture assert God\'s singularity by explicitly stating that there is only one God.listen to just a few examples.in 1 king 8:60 \r\nPs.86:10\r\n2 King 19:19\r\nRom 3:30\r\nJames 2:19\r\nThere are one dive being.\r\nThe word God can mean many things. Many religious refer to their deities as God\'s and the Bible itself sometime use the word God to refer to things like demon, ideals', 7, '2020-08-06 16:39:17', '2020-12-14 21:46:25', NULL),
(1763, 512, 872, 'The theologian use terms like simple and simplicity in a rather technical way we are not saying that God is simple in the sense that he is easy to understand. instead.we mean that his Essen is not a composite of different substance but a unified whole consisting \r\nWe all illustrate this idea of simplicity by comparing pure water to mud . on the one hand.water many be viewed as a simple substance.it is composed entirely of water, and nothing else.but if we add dirt to our pure water, it turns into mud \r\nBut why is this important? Why does Christianity emphasize that God is simple and not composed of different substance? To answer this question.lest look on more at the doctrine of  Trinity', 7, '2020-08-06 16:54:32', '2020-12-14 21:46:25', NULL),
(1764, 512, 873, 'The father s associate with the son and Holy spirit many by described in a number of ways but in the history of theology, two participate perspective on the Trinity have come to foreground \r\nSpecially it has been common to speak ontological Trinity and the economic Trinity.both these approaches speak of the same Trinity the father,the son and the holy Spirit but they emphasize different aspects of the relationship between the three persons of the Godhead \r\n\r\nOne the hand t has been common to speak of the ontological Trinity when we are focusing on God\'s being the word ontological mea rebate to begin or ease, we are \r\nThe both are economic Trinity perspective the father is said to be the first person the father is called the first person of the ontological Trinity because the son is said to be generated by the father and', 7, '2020-08-06 17:14:35', '2020-12-14 21:46:25', NULL),
(1765, 512, 874, 'The fatherhood of God has many aspects that we could discuss.but we will focus on three of Scripture more prominent idea. first we will consider the father role as creator second we will look at fatherhood in terms of his position as King over his creation and people.\r\n1) Creator \r\nIn the broadest sense, Scripture sometime refers to God as being the father of everything he has created for instance, we find this in passage like deut 32:6\r\n\r\n2) king \r\nIn the ancient near East it was common for people to refer to human kings as their father, and for kg to refer to the people as a children\'s \r\nAs well for example the Israelites refere to David\'s as their father because he had been there King.of course some of the Israelites referred were directed \r\n\r\n3) family head \r\nEveryone is familiar with the concept of a family head.usually it is a parent, grandparent , or other relatives who leads and makes decisions for the family or household', 7, '2020-08-06 17:30:49', '2020-12-14 21:46:25', NULL),
(1766, 511, 670, 'God  disclosed himself during the Old Testament in two main ways: through act revelations and word revelations. This two fold concept of revelation has characterized biblical theology of the New Testament as well. \r\nThe New Testament reports many revelatory acts of God, such as earthly ministry, and the ministry of the Holy Spirit in the first century church. It foretells acts of God that will take place in the future, such as the glorious return of Christ . The New Testament also reports word revelations associated with the acts of God: God the Father spoke : Christ also spoke , angels, human and animals too spoke by the Spirit of Gog revealed God\'s words as well.\r\nNew Testament narratives report both the actions and words of Jesus. the epistles and other Christians is the new testament as God reveals himself through actions and their words.\r\nNew Testament contains all three kinds of word revelation as well.\r\nThe Gospel report how God spoke through the words pf Jesus to reflect on Jesus earlier actions.\r\nwe see that Jesus\' teachings explain his simultaneous actions as well as times when Jesus predicted future actions. similarly authors and characters in the books of acts and Revelations , New Testament epistles , throughout the New testament God revealed himself through the intersections between his actions and his words.', 8, '2020-08-06 17:48:57', '2020-08-07 04:19:55', NULL),
(1767, 511, 671, 'In the following ways the New testament  biblical theologians have differed from Old testament theologians ;\r\nBy the comparison  with old testament  the new testament covers a very short period of history.OLD testament covers a history of 1600 years form Abraham  whereas new testament deals with only 100 years.\r\n 2.\r\nthe most situations in the new testament are very similar to each other. by contrast the old testament presents  a great variety of circumstances in its history . the circumstances  of God \'s people were fairly consistent during New testament history. throughout the period of hsitroy of new testamnet, early Christians did not face the kinds of extreme changes that took place with God;s peopeli in the Old Testament. in the testament Christians were consistently margiaslized and persecuted. They dint experiences  periods of tremendous health a nd terrible pverty.\r\nthey dint travel from en masse from one lace to another. nor dod they experience periods of wide sclae obedience and disobedience.\r\nin the third palce , jnlike the old testamnet , the new testamnet only deals iwth one divine covenant. in the old testamnet there are several covants with epocahal sifts.', 8, '2020-08-06 18:08:51', '2020-08-07 04:19:55', NULL),
(1768, 511, 672, 'the background of Old Testament help us understand diachronic developments in New Testament eschatology.\r\nAt the beginning, God revealed two crucial element of first that humanity was created in God;s image, but with Adam and Eve\'s sin , and the curse that fell upon them. Genesis 3:15 reveals that there will be two groups . but God promised that victory will ultimately be with seed of woman.\r\nNoah: this covenant secured the stability of nature as humanity pursued God\'s plan for the world.\r\nAbraham : God singled out Abraham to be the the one through whom he would carry out his promises given to Adam and Noah\r\nMoses : his covenant focused on the law of God as the guide for Israel\'s special service in spreading his kingdom\r\nDavid \'s descendants and Jerusalem with its temple played a central role in Israel\'s understanding of the end times. the prophets declared that in the restoration, a great son of David would become the focus of a new order.\r\nThe old testament ends with this sad postponement of the eschatological age.It developed diachronically. It began in the days of Adam ,refined in the days of Noah.', 7, '2020-08-06 18:26:30', '2020-08-07 04:19:55', NULL),
(1769, 511, 673, 'Jesus and the new testament  explain that his fulfillment of Old Testament expectations would take place in three phases: the inauguration , continuation and consummation of the kingdom.\r\nbecause of this the new testament writes often drew attention  to different ways in which Jesus fulfills Old Testament hopes.for example Jesus began to fulfill Adam\'s call to rule first in his earthly ministry .\r\nJesus fulfilled Noah\'s rescue of humanity for service to God in his earthy ministry as he called men and women to repent and ordered his disciples to baptize them.\r\nThese examples provide a framework from within which we can grasp many specific ways New Testament authors focused on Christ as the fulfillment of Old Testament hopes.\r\nEschatology was specially important for the New Testament because Jesus teaching about last days represented one of most decisive ways in which Christians had broken with first century Judaism .\r\nJewish religious leaders and the general population raged against Christianity precisely because of the christian outlook on the Messianic last days. Christians believed that Messiah had already come, but in a way that was unexpected . He had suffered and died in the gentiles and Jews. he had been resurrected and ha ascended to heaven where he ruled over all. he would return one day to judge all of humanity, including unbelievers with Israel,. such a messianic scenario was utterly contrary to what Jews believed in that day .', 7, '2020-08-06 18:46:04', '2020-08-07 04:19:55', NULL),
(1770, 511, 674, 'We are all labourers in the kingdom of God.  Christ inaugurated the kingdom of God and has planted us in His kingdom .Now we are to live for Christ in the light of what he has already accomplished in his first coming, and we are to live for Christ in the power of his Spirit within us now and how we are to live for Christ in the hope of his glorious return.\r\n2 Corinthians 5:20 says we are the ambassadors of Christ , we are to represent the kingdom and the characteristics of the king to the people we come  in contact. \r\nNow as we know we are in the kingdom of God, it is our duty to extend His kingdom and to bring many into his kingdom to be partakers of the same joy that we have.\r\nThis also leads us to serve our king , God Almighty with joy as we serve a just and loving king , but it also makes us more responsible, accountable and loyal.\r\n2 Peter 2:9 says we are holy people, royal priesthood  called out to do his works with faithfulness.\r\nThe truth that we are in His Kingdom and applying the concept of God\'s kingdom to our family , church and ministry makes us more dedicated, sincere and the same time joyful and cheerful, that we serve a  Wonderful God', 7, '2020-08-06 19:02:47', '2020-08-07 04:19:55', NULL),
(1771, 515, 876, 'The first thing we should note about the language son of God is that Scripture often user it to talk about being that are not divine in any way.for example. the angel are referred to as sons of God in passage like job 1:6 and 3:1 \r\n The Israeli also call God\'s son  2 Samuel 7\r\n And also all Christian know... many passage mentioned that Mathew 5:9, Rom 8:14\r\n\r\nJesus sonship is especially clear in the Gospel of John..1:1- \r\nAnd also John 8:18- \r\n\r\nWe also many other passage also see that hebw 1:1-\r\nThis is emphasis on Jesus as the Divine and eternal son of God is reflected in the doctrine of the Trinity, which states that..\r\nAs the son of God, Christ is equal in power and and glory to the father and the holy Spirit..all three of God\'s person.. including the son..are infinite..', 7, '2020-08-08 06:21:01', '2020-08-10 13:47:06', NULL),
(1772, 515, 877, 'Roman 10:9,13 ..vers 13 is everyone who called Jesus will be saved.but in this verse from Joel in the Hebrew old testament the name of the Lord was Yahweh.the proper name of Lord  and God of the old testament \r\nOther n t passage also say Jesus is Lord \r\nThis is not say that every time people in new Testament called Jesus Lord\'s they recognize his Divinity, sometimes they simply intended to show him human respect \r\nThe Divinity of Christ has all kinds of implications for the Christian life.for instance.it means that we should acknowledge and worship Jesus as God in our prayers and songs.it means that we should pray to him', 7, '2020-08-08 06:31:04', '2020-08-10 13:47:06', NULL),
(1773, 515, 878, 'In the last couple century many theologian have readily accepted that Jesus was human . But they have questions his Divinity.but in the early century of the church \r\n\r\n1)Experience -\r\nServeral of Jesus experience prove that he was truly human because only human being have such experience listen \r\nJesus was conceived by the holy Spirit \r\nAnd born of the virgin Mary \r\nHe suffered under Pontius Pilate \r\nWas crucified into hell \r\n\r\n2) Generation \r\nHe was conceived by holy Spirit..not a human being \r\nHis father also human \r\nJesus also in marry womb like all human beings ways \r\n3)Body \r\nJesus suffering Crucifixion, death and burial demonstrate that he was a real man with a physical human body..one that could be beaten one that could bleed one that could be abused by soldiers one that could collapse under exhausted one that could be killed \r\n\r\n4) soul \r\nScripture say human body house an a soul it speaks of our Soul by many different rmteran \r\n\r\n5) resurrection \r\nThe resurrection proves that Jesus Christ was a real human being because it reaffirm that his full glorified human existence include the reunion of his real human body with his real human soul.', 8, '2020-08-08 06:48:28', '2020-08-10 13:47:06', NULL),
(1774, 515, 879, 'In modern Christianity many believer are unaware that the word Christ is actually the title of Jesus office rather than part this personal name in this regard the word Christ \r\n\r\nOt background \r\nChrist Greek mean christos which I\'m turn is translate ot Hebrews mashiacha meaning anointed one \r\nMost important use in anointed one inn Ps 89 \r\n132:19\r\nThe new Testament speak of Jesus as the Christ in over 500 place..so it almost goes without saying that from a Christian point of view.he is the great Messiah that the old testament anticipate but to remove all doubt.. there are two passage in John gospel Jesus is called Messiah and John say Messiah mean same thing Christ', 8, '2020-08-08 07:00:33', '2020-08-10 13:47:06', NULL),
(1775, 515, 880, 'When we talk about the Divinity of Christ or even properly the deity of Christ..the fact that he is fully God ..we are talking about the central claim of the new Testament concerning who Christ is . What we are told is that Jesus is fully God and fully man .the moment we back off either of those, we no longer have Jesus.the only way we can explore Jesus in terms of his deity is exactly as the Bible declared him . We are told that he is the son of the living God this is the most fundamental facts preaching by the early church.and what we have for instance', 7, '2020-08-08 07:09:41', '2020-08-10 13:47:06', NULL),
(1776, 513, 876, 'Christians have always intended words like Christ, Son of God, and Lord to indicate Jesus\' divinity. Son of God is often used for beings that are not divine like Angels(Job 1.6), nation of Israel (ex. 4.22), adam, believers etc. Jesus is God\'s son in a unique way. Jesus as the divine and eternal Son of God is reflected in the doctrine of the Trinity.\r\nOntological Perspective- It focuses on God\'s being and existence. As the Son of God, Christ is equal in power and glory to the Father and the Holy Spirit. All three of God\'s persons are infinite, eternal and unchangeable and each has the same essential divine attributes such as wisdom, power, holiness, justice, goodness and truth.\r\nEconomic perspective- it describes how they interact with each other. All have different responsibilities, different level of authority and assigned roles. For Example, Christ has always been subordinate to Father\'s authority. Within the economy of Trinity, the Son has authority over the Holy Spirit as in John 15.26', 8, '2020-08-08 15:40:28', '2020-08-10 13:47:46', NULL),
(1777, 513, 877, 'When the Jewish scholars translated the Old testament they used the term kurios to translate the sacred name of God: Yahweh. The use of the word kurios in the New Testament often implies the Jesus is divine. The divinity of Christ has all kinds of implications for the Christian life. It means we should acknowledge and worship Jesus as God in our prayers and songs, we should pray to him, just as we do to the Father and the spirit. It means that we can take great comfort in the security of salvation, knowing that God himself has redeemed us from sins. These practical concerns in the Christian life rest on the belief that Jesus is divine.', 7, '2020-08-08 15:46:28', '2020-08-10 13:47:46', NULL),
(1778, 513, 878, '1. Experiences- Several of Jesus experience prove that he was truly human because only human beings have such experiences; These experiences confirm four aspects: his generation, his body, his soul, and his resurrection.\r\n1. Generation which included his conception and birth. First, he was conceived by the Holy Spirit rather than by a human father. Jesus was born in Mary\'s womb that did not violate his mother\'s virginity. \r\n2. Body- The creed attributes experiences to Jesus that would only have been possible if he was truly a physical human being. Jesus was a real man with a physical human body. A genuine human being had to suffer physical divine judgement to atone for sins of humanity.\r\n3. Soul- Human beings consist of a mortal body that houses an immortal soul. While Jesus\' body would be placed in the grave his spirit or soul would be in the hands of God the Father. \r\n4. Resurrection- The resurrection proves that Jesus was a real human being because it included the reunion of his real human body with his real human soul.', 8, '2020-08-08 15:55:59', '2020-08-10 13:47:46', NULL),
(1779, 513, 879, 'The word Christ is actually the title of Jesus\'office, similar to words like \'\'king\'\' or \'\'judge.\'\' \r\n1. Old Testament Background- The word \"Christ\" is a translation of the Greek christos, which in turn is a translation of the Old Testament Hebrew word mashiach or \'messiah\', meaning anointed one, which in the Old testament applied to the descendants of David that served as Kings over Israel and Judah. \r\n2. Fulfillment in Jesus- Jesus is the great messiah that Old testament anticipated. Messiah had to be human: in the case of the covenant with David, God obligated himself to send a human messiah to save his people. And that Messiah was Jesus. \r\nA second reason is that only a human son of David could be an atoning sacrifice. A third reason Messiah had to be human was that he had to be the second Adam. \r\nThrough his righteous life, atoning death, empowered resurrection and heavenly enthronement, Jesus succeeded where Adam and the rest of us failed. He became humanity\'s second Adam.', 8, '2020-08-08 16:08:48', '2020-08-10 13:47:46', NULL),
(1780, 513, 880, 'Jesus possesses all the attributes and traits that are essential to being human. Jesus differs from other human beings in some important way, \r\n1) by being a perfect human being. Jesus was not at all flawed, whereas we human beings have sinned. He was Perfect in all ways. He was born without sin and led a perfectly sinless life.  \r\n2) Jesus is one person with two distinct natures, which is divine nature and a human nature.  Every human being has only one human nature, but Jesus had  both God and man, being both fully human and fully divine at the same time, which is also known as the \"hypostatic union.\"\r\nJesus emptied himself not by losing his divine nature but by taking on an additional nature- a human nature that did not replace but merely veiled his divine glory. \r\nJesus gave out implications for the way we live , we have an effective human mediator between us and God. He has constituted a new human race. We can approach the throne of Grace with confidence.', 8, '2020-08-08 16:21:31', '2020-08-10 13:47:46', NULL),
(1781, 517, 881, '1. Structure- The Apostles\' creed affirms the divinity of the Holy Spirit. Apostles\' creed does not explicitly state the Holy Spirit is divine. But it implicitly affirms the Spirit\'s divinity in two ways. First, the Trinitarian structure equates the Holy Spirit with the Father and the Son in important ways.\"was conceived by the Holy Spirit\". \r\n\r\n2. Jesus\' Conception does not explicitly declare the Spirit\'s divinity but strongly implies that the Holy Spirit is fully divine alludes to Luke 1.35(\"the power of the Most High, by alluding to this verse as an example of the Holy Spirit\'s work, the Apostles\' creed affirms the Spirit\'s full divinity. This conclusion is confirmed by Hebrews 10.5-7, creating Jesus\'human body was specifically the work of God. In light of verses like these it is safe to say that when the Apostles\' Creed attributes Jesus\' conception to the Holy Spirit, it intends to affirm the Spirit\'s divinity.', 7, '2020-08-11 15:38:37', '2020-08-14 04:02:30', NULL),
(1782, 517, 882, 'We value the creed as summary of scripture not as a replacement for Scripture. \r\n 1. Names- The name that implies his divinity in the most implicit way is the name holy spirit. The names that lie between implicit and very explicit on the continuum are: Spirit of the Lord, Spirit of the God, Spirit of living God, Spirit of Jesus, Spirit of Christ. Acts 5.3-4 explicitly refers to the Holy Spirit by the name of \"God\"\r\n2. Attributes- A. Communicable- THe Bible demonstrates the divinity of Holy Spirit by ascribing divine attributes to him. Attributes which can be communicates in some way with God\'s creatures. another communicable attribute is love. and many places we teach that our love derives from God\'s attribute of love.\r\n3. Work- The Holy spirit\'s works demonstrate his divinity. it performs many works that are appropriate to God alone. Holy Spirit inspired the writing of Scripture- access to the FAther, regenerates our spirits, applies salvation, power behind the miracles', 7, '2020-08-11 15:56:30', '2020-08-14 04:02:30', NULL),
(1783, 517, 883, 'Personhood- The Holy Spirit is a true person and not simply a divine force or power. The creed\'s affirmation of the Holy Spirit as a member of the Trinity is an implied affirmation of his personhood.\r\nA. Attributes- Qualities the Holy Spirit possesses that are unique to persons:\r\nHoly Spirit has a will. This is the faculty he uses to plan, to desire, and to choose. in 1 corinthians 12.11- One and the same Spirit works all these things, distributing to each one individually just as He wills.\r\nHoly Spirit also has the attribute of intelligence, through which he possesses knowledge and the ability to teach others Corinthians 12.8\r\nHoly Spirit also has emotions, internal feelings and affections that he expresses in response to other persons and events his emotions prove that he is a person and not simply a power.His emotions like love, joy and grief proves he is a person and not simply a power.\r\nThe spirit possesses what we might call the attribute of agency. Eg- Testimony, fellowship and he speak and commands.', 7, '2020-08-11 16:05:59', '2020-08-14 04:02:30', NULL),
(1784, 517, 884, 'The Holy Spirit is identified as the Spirit of God\'s son is Galatians 4.6, and as the Spirit of the Father in Matthew 10. 20. And he has several other names that highlight the relational connections between the members of the Trinity. The distinction between the Spirit and the other persons of the Trinity is not always entirely clear. \r\nDistinctions between the Spirit and the other persons of the Trinity: distinctions between the Spirit and the other persons of the Trinity is to look at passages in Scripture that show them interacting with one another in ways that emphasize their differences. There are many passages that show these distinctions, but two passages will suffice to show that the Spirit is distinct from the Son and from the Father. As consider Jesus\' words in John 16. 7; I tell you the truth, it is for good that I am going away. Unless I go away, the counselor will not come to you, but if I go, I will send him to you. \r\nalso in John 16. 7 the spirit would not begin until the Son had completely his earthlyd into heaven. This makes it clear that Spirit is distinct from the Son.\r\nHoly Spirit intercedes on our behalf with the Father, he demonstrated that they are distinct persons- one interceding and other hearing the interceding.', 7, '2020-08-11 16:18:07', '2020-08-14 04:02:30', NULL),
(1785, 517, 885, 'There are two perspectives: \r\nOntological Trinity- We are focusing on God\'s being and existence. From this perspective, the Holy Spirit is equal in power and glory to the Father and the Son. All three of God\'s persons are infinite, eternal and unchangeable. and each has the same essential divine attributes such as wisdom, power, holiness, justice, goodness and truth. \r\nEconomic Trinity- we are considering how God\'s persons interact with each other. From this perspective, each person of the GodHead has different responsibilities, different authority and a different assigned role. The Spirit\'s authority is subject to higher authority of the Father and the Son. and the Spirit\'s role is largely to carry out their instructions and to bring them glory. The Holy Spirit is called the third person of the Trinity.', 7, '2020-08-11 16:24:44', '2020-08-14 04:02:30', NULL);
