(1786, 519, 732, 'उत्तर =  हम लुका के मूल पाठकों का अध्ययन दो प्रकार से करेंगे। पहला हम थियुफिलुस  के लिए पुस्तक के प्रत्यक्ष समर्पण को देखेंगे और दूसरा हम इंस संभावना पर भी विचार करेंगे कि पुस्तके विशाल पाठक समूह के लिए भी लिखी गई थी आइए हम लुक्का के\r\n पहले पाठक के रूप में थियुफिलुस के साथ आरम्भ करते है ।\r\n थियुफिलुस:-\r\n\r\n सदियों से इस पर अत्यधिक वाद विवाद होता आया है कि थियुफिलुस  कौन था और लुक्का1ः1-4 मैं यहां किसे बताता है और  प्रेरितो के काम 1ः1-2 मैं भी उसका वर्णन है थियुफिलुस  शब्द का अर्थ परमेश्वर का प्रेमी है और इस कारण बहुत से लोग ने यहां सोचा कि संभवत थियुफिलुस  किसी व्यक्ति का नाम नहीं था परंतु वहां लुक्का के सुसमाचार के पाठकों का प्रतिनिधित्व करता है जो अपनी कक्षा में परमेश्वर के प्रेमी होने निस्संदेह एक और बड़ी संभावना या की थियुफिलुस  एक व्यक्ति था अधिकांश विद्वान इस बुरे विचार को मानते हैं क्योंकि लुका उसे श्रीमान क्रिस्टीना कहकर संबोधित करता है और बाद में लिखा उसी शब्द क्रिकेटर का प्रयोग रोमी अधिकारियों के फ्लेक्स और अग्रिप्पा से को संबोधित करने के लिए करता है अच्छा स्पष्ट लुका के मन में यह एक तकनीकी अभिव्यक्त है जो एक उच्च पद वाले व्यक्ति को और विशेष रूमी सरकार के उच्च अधिकारी की ओर संकेत करती है इसके अतिरिक्त लुक्का1ः1-4 एक समर्पण प्रतीत होता है यहां परिचयात्मक समर्पण ओं की शैली के शब्दों के अनुरूप है और ऐतिहासिक रचनाओं को प्रिय इस प्रकार की भाषा का प्रयोग करते हुए किसी संरक्षण के प्रति समर्पित किया जाता था एक ऐसे व्यक्ति के प्रति जो वास्तव में उस संरचना का मूल चुका था था और इसलिए वह वास्तव में समर्पण कथनों के अनुरूप है और इस कारण यहां लगभग निश्चित है कि थियुफिलुस  एक व्यक्ति था ।\r\n लुक्का के प्रस्तावना यहां संकेत देती है कि थियोफिलस उसका संरक्षण था उसी ने उसे पुस्तक लिखने के लिए अधिकृत किया था और उसकी आर्थिक सहायता की थी लुका 1 अध्याय का 3 पद मलूका ने अपनी कृति में श्रीमान यूपी लूसिया क्रेडिट थियोफिलस कोष को संबोधित किया क्रिकेट सबवे कुछ आधार कार्ड शब्द था वास्तव में पूरे नए नियम में इसका प्रयोग केवल दो और लोगों के फ्लेक्स और फेसबुक के लिए किया गया है।\r\n वास्तव में पूरे नए नियम में इसका प्रयोग केवल दो और लोगों के फिलिप्स और पेस्ट उसके लिए किया गया यदि थियुफिलुस  एक उच्च पद वाला रोमी अधिकारी नहीं थी था तो भी वहां निश्चित रूप से प्रतिष्ठा और महत्त्व वाला व्यक्ति था परंतु लुक्का और थियोफिलोस के बीच का संबध केवल संक्षण से ही कहीं अधिक जटिल था एक अर्थ में  थियोफिलस लुका का शिष्य भी था लुका 1 अध्याय का 3 पद से चार में हम इन वचनों को पढ़ते है ।\r\nथियुफिलुस  पहले ही यीशु के बारे में जानता था परंतु लुक्का ने यीशु के जीवन में बारे में इस पूर्ण और अधिक व्यक्तित्व भी ले को इसलिए लिखा की थी फिर उसको उन बातों का निश्चित हो जाए जो उसे सिखाई गई थी लुक्का द्वारा अपने पहले पाठक के रूप में थियोफिलोस का उल्लेख उनके बारे में देखने के बाद विशाल पाठकों के लिए रुका की रचना को देखना भी सहायक है।\r\n\r\nविशाल पाठक:-\r\n\r\n यह सोचने के  बहुत से कारण है कि लुका के ने केवल थियोफिलोस की अपेक्षा बड़ी संख्या में दूसरे पाठकों के लिए लिखी आरंभिक मशीनों में और अन्य रचनाओं को आपस में बांटने की प्रवृत्ति थी एक उदाहरण के रूप में देखे कि पॉल उसने कुलुसियो 4ः16 मैं क्या लिखा है आरंभिक मशीनों में अपनी पुस्तकों को आपस में बांटने की प्रवृत्ति थी जो यह अनुमान उपयुक्त प्रतीत होता है कि थियोफिलोस भी पूर्व लुक्का की पुस्तक को दूसरों के साथ बांटने के लिए उत्सुक रहा होगा इसके अतिरिक्त सुसमाचार की उच्च साहित्य शैली इस बात को लगभग सुनिश्चित बनाती है कि लुका ने उसे विशाल पाठकों को ध्यान में रखते हुए लिखा था सहेली केवल एक व्यक्ति के लिए ही की गई निजी टिप्पणी के रूप में नहीं लुक्का एक अध्याय 13 पद में लुका जिस वृत्त ऐतिहासिक खोज के बारे में बताता है उसका संकेत भी अधिक विस्तृत पाठकों की ओर है और इसके अतिरिक्त सुसमाचार और पीड़ितों के काम की पुस्तक का बड़ा आकार यहां सुझाव देता है कि लुका ने बड़ी संख्या में पाठकों को ध्यान में रखते हुए एक प्रमुख रचना को लिखा था परंतु में पाठक कौन थे सर्वाधिक संभावना यह प्रतीत होती है कि लुका ने मुख्य गैर यहूदी बस्तियों के लिए लिखा था उदाहरण के लिए यूनानी कि उससे लूजर यहूदी जैसी थी और परमेश्वर के राज्य की सुसमाचार की सर्व भौमिक प्रस्तुति ने इस पर बल दिया कि उद्धार सारी जातियों के लिए थानिसंद्र लुका का सुसमाचार यहूदियों के लिए मूल्यवान रहा होगा परंतु मसीह के सुसमाचार के समान इसके उनके लिए नहीं लिखा गया था एक सामान्य अर्थ में परमेश्वर सदैव यहां जाता है कि संपूर्ण इतिहास में उसके सब लोग संपूर्ण बाइबल को पढ़े और समझे परंतु यहां पहचानना महत्वपूर्ण है कि आज पवित्र आत्मा ने लेखकों को उनकी पुस्तकों को लिखने के लिए प्रेरित किया तब उसने उनके निजी व्यक्तित्व और रूचि योग के द्वारा कार्य किया इस प्राथमिक अर्थ मलूका ने अपनी पुस्तक को प्रत्यक्ष रूप में थी और उस और पहली सदी के दूसरे गैर यहूदी बस्तियों की आवश्यकताओं के लिए लिखी आधुनिक पाठकों से सुन रहे हैं जिससे लोगों ने उसके लिए लिखा था परंतु इस सुसमाचार को पढ़ते समय यदि हम लुक्का और उसके मूल पाठकों को ध्यान में रखते हुए रखते हैं तो हम उसके द्वारा लिखी गई बातों को बेहतर रूप से समझने और उसे हमारे स्वयं के जीवन में लागू करने के लिए तैयार हो सकते हैं।', 9, '2020-08-15 11:47:15', '2020-08-22 11:57:40', NULL),
(1787, 519, 733, 'उत्तर =  यीशु की शुरुआतो का लूका का अभिलेख यीशु के जन्म से कुछ पहले आरंभ होता है और उसकी सर्वजनिक सेवकाई से पहले के  उसके संपूर्ण जीवन तक विस्तृत है।\r\n इन अध्ययनों में लुक्का का मुख्य उद्देश्य यह दिखाना था कि यीशु परमेश्वर का पुत्र और दाऊद का पुत्र भी है और इस प्रकार वहां पूर्वतः देवी और पूर्व तथा मानवीय है।\r\n इसके अतिरिक्त दाऊद के पुत्र के रूप में यीशु मसीहा  यीशु मसीह भी था जो परमेश्वर के राज्य को पृथ्वी पर लाकर संसार को उध्दार देने वाला था इस पूरी कहानी में रुका नहीं यहां दिखाने के लिए नियमित रूप से पुराने नियम में परमेश्वर की प्रतिज्ञा का उल्लेख किया है कि परमेश्वर यीशु के द्वारा उन प्रतिज्ञा को पूरा कर रहा था। और इसलिए परमेश्वर के प्रति विश्वास योग्य बने रहने और उसके राज्य की आशीशों को पाने का एकमात्र मार्ग यीशु को राजा और उद्धार करता के रूप में स्वीकार करना था इन अध्ययनों को चार मुख्य भागों में विभाजित किया जा सकता है यह ना बपतिस्मा देने वाले और यीशु के जन्म की घोषणा है और उनके जन्म और बचपन योहन्ना द्वारा यीशु की पहचान और यीशु के परमेश्वर के पुत्र होने के बारे में तीन मूर्तियां आइए हम लुका 1ः5-56 मैं जन्म की घोषणाओं से आरंभ करते हैं\r\n\r\n जन्म की घोषणाए:-\r\n\r\n यह महत्वपूर्ण है कि लुका ने अपने सुसमाचार की शुरुआत गबिरिएल  स्वर्गदूध के प्रकटीकरण के साथ की सैकड़ों वर्ष पूर्व दानियल अध्ययन 9 में बताया गया था कि गाब्रीएल  ने घोषणा की कि दंड की अवधि समाप्त होने वाली थी लुका 1ः5-25 मैं गाब्रीएल  नए यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा देने वाले के जन्म की भविष्यवाणी की  गाब्रिएल  यहूदियों में जकरिया याजक के सामने प्रकट हुआ और उसे बताया कि उसकी  बांझ पत्नी एलिशेबा आश्चर्यजनक रूप से एक बच्चे को जन्म देगी उन्हें उसका नाम यूहन्ना रखना था वह जन्म से ही पवित्र आत्मा से भरा होगा और परमेश्वर के उद्धार का मार्ग तैयार करने के लिए महान बहुत दुखता एरिया की आत्मा में सेवा करेगा पहले जकरिया ने गाब्रिएल  के संदेश पर संदेह किया इसलिए अपने पुत्र के जन्म के समय तक वह बोल नहीं सका।\r\n लुक्का ने यमुना की जन्म की घोषणा को लुका 1ः26-38 मैं गाब्रीएल  कि उससे भी बड़ी घोषणा से जुड़ा गाब्रिएल  ने मरियम से कहा कि परमेश्वर आश्चर्यजनक रूप से उसकी कोख में एक पुत्र उत्पन्न करेगा और स्वयं परमेश्वर ही उस बालक का पिता होगा परमेश्वर के पुत्र का नाम यीशु अर्थात उद्धार करता रखना था इसके अतिरिक्त वहां अपने पुरखे दाऊद के सिंहासन का उत्तराधिकारी होगा अर्थात वह दाऊद का वंशज मसीही होगा जो परमेश्वर के अनंत राज्य के उद्धार को पृथ्वी पर लाएगा। मरियम और एलिशेबा चचेरी बहन थी इसलिए मरियम यह दिया में अंसिबल के पास यह बताने के लिए गई कि उसकी कोख में पर विश्व का पुत्र है इसके बारे में हम लुका 1ः39-56 मैं पढ़ते हैं जब मरियम ने इंलिशिबा को नमस्कार किया तो बच्चा अपनी मां के गर्भ में आनंद सूचना और तुरंत ही इल्ली शिबा आत्मा  से भर गई ताकि वह अपने बच्चे की प्रतिक्रिया के महत्व को समझ सके एलीशिबा ने मरियम के पुत्र को अपना प्रभु कहते हुए मरियम को धन्य कहा और जब अब मैं मरियम ने अपने बच्चे के द्वारा अब आने वाले उद्धार पर अत्यधिक आनंद को अभिव्यत करते हुवे लुका 1ः46-55 मैं अपना विख्यात स्तुति गीत गाया जिसे प्रियः द मैग्रीफिकेट कहा जाता हैं ।\r\n\r\n जन्म और बचपन:-\r\n\r\n यूहन्ना के जन्म और बचपन के बारे में लुका के अभिषेक लुका 1ः57-80 मैं पाया जा सकता है योना का जन्म बुजुर्ग माता पिता के यहां हुआ था और जब आठवें दिन वे खतने के लिए उसे मंदिर में लेकर आए तो उसके पिता की आवाज लौट आए उस समय जकरिया पवित्र आत्मा से भर कर भविष्यवाणी करने लगा जिससे कि उसका पुत्र दाऊद के वंश मसीह का मार्ग तैयार करेगा लुका 1ः69-76 पुराने नियम में परमेश्वर ने अब्राहम दाऊद के साथ उधार की भाषा के वायदे किए थे और जकरिया ने बहुत स्वामी की कि परमेश्वर उन वादों को पूरा करने वाला है और उसका पुत्र योहन्ना मार्ग तैयार करने वाला बहुत दुखता होगा।\r\nफिर लुका 2ः1-52 मलूका ने यीशु के जन्म और बचपन के बारे में बताया इस अभिलेख और यह अन्ना के जन्म के बारे में उसके पिछले अभिलेख में कई समानताएं हैं परंतु यीशु के जन्म और बचपन के बारे में लुक्का का अभिलेख कहीं अधिक बड़ा और विस्तृत है उसकी शुरुआत दाऊद के नगर यहूदा के बदले में यीशु के जन्म के साथ होती है जिसके बारे में लुका 2ः1-20 मैं बताया गया है।\r\n यीशु का जन्म अत्यधिक विनम्रता में हुआ था उसका जन्म एक गौशाला में हुआ और उसे एक चरणीय में रखा गया परंतु आसपास के चरवाहों को उसके जन्म की सूचना देने वाली स्वर्ग जूतों की घोषणा सही थी सुने स्वर्ग दूतों ने लुका 2ः10-11 मैं चरवाहों से क्या कहाः\r\n स्वर्ग दूत ने यहां से समाचार सुनाया की मसीहा रूपी राजा परमेश्वर के लोगों को परमेश्वर के दंड से बचाएगा फिर इस वर्ग दूध के साथ स्वर्ग दूतों की एक बड़ी सेना दिखाई दी जो यीशु के जन्म के लिए परमेश्वर की स्तुति कर रही थी लुक्का ने यह स्पष्ट किया कि निर्धारण था में जन्म के बावजूद मरियम का पुत्र वास्तव में परमेश्वर का चुनाव हुआ मसीहा और राजा था।फिर लुका 2ः21-40 मैं लोगों ने यीशु को यरूशलेम मंदिर में लाए जाने और खतने का वर्णन किया मंदिर में श्रीमान के साथ-साथ पवित्र आत्मा बहुत दुखता यूहन्ना ने पवित्र आत्मा से भर कर घोषणा की कि यीशु ही वहां मसीहा था जो संसार में उधार लाने वाला था लुका 2ः30-32 मैं श्रीमान द्वारा परमेश्वर की स्तुति को सुनें।यह यशायाह 49ः6 के पूर्णता थी जहां परमेश्वर ने यह वचन कहे थे सिमोन के द्वारा परमेश्वर के प्रकट किए कि यीशु वहां मसीहा था जो इजरायल के लिए उधार और महिमा लाने वाला था और इससे बढ़कर वा परमेश्वर के राज्य के सुसमाचार को गैर यहूदी राष्ट्र तक भी फैल आएगा ताकि वह भी उद्धार पाएंगे लुका 2ः41-52 मैं मंदिर में यीशु की संक्षिप्त कहानी के साथ लुक्का की यीशु के पुत्र होने के विषय की और वापस लौटता है जहां यीशु 12 वर्ष का था तो वहां फसा के पर्व के लिए अपने माता पिता के साथ यरूशलेम गया परंतु वापस लौटते समय वह अपने माता-पिता से बिछड़ गया उसके माता-पिता ने कई दिनों के बाद उसे मंदिर के आंगन में शास्त्रियों से बातें करते हुए पाया यीशु के ज्ञान और समझ से मंदिर में हर कोई चकित रह गया जब मरियम ने यीशु का सामना किया तो उसके उत्तर ने यहां प्रकट किया कि वहां कितना विशेषता सुने लुक्का 2ः49 मैं यीशु ने मरियम से क्या कहा मंदिर उसके पिता का घर था क्योंकि यीशु परमेश्वर का पुत्र था यूहन्ना और यीशु के जन्म और बचपन के बाद लोका ने लूका 3ः1-20 मैं यह न द्वारा यीशु की पहचान की जानकारी दी।\r\n\r\n  युहन्ना द्वारा यीशु की पहचानः-\r\n\r\n\r\n इस विवरण में यूहन्ना ने औपचारिक रूप से यीशु की मसीहा के रूप में पहचान करने के द्वारा परमेश्वर के उद्धार का मार्ग तैयार किया या ना नदी के क्षेत्र में अपनी प्रचार किससे उठाएं में युवाओं ने परमेश्वर के राज्य के आगमन की घोषणा की लोगों को अपने पापों से मनाने का उद्देश्य उपदेश दिया और मन फिर आने वालों को बपतिस्मा दिया परंतु जब यीशु बपतिस्मा लेने के लिए उसके पास आया तो न19 मसीहा के रूप में उसकी पहचान की और साफ शब्दों में शब्दों में घोषणा की कि वह मसीहा की जूती का बांध खोलने के योग्य भी नहीं है यूहन्ना ने कहा कि यीशु की पवित्र आत्मा से बपतिस्मा देगा जैसा यशायाह 44ः3 और येहजकेल 39ः29 जैसे पुराने नियम के परीक्षणों में बताया गया है और इसका अर्थ यह था कि इतिहास का अंतिम युग वह समय आ चुका था जब परमेश्वर का उद्धार पूर्व होगा।\r\n\r\n\r\n परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में पुष्टिः-\r\n\r\n\r\n लोका ने यीशु के परमेश्वर के पुत्र होने के बारे में तीन अलग-अलग पुश्टियां उपलब्ध कराई है जिसकी शुरुआत लुका 3ः21-22 मैं देवियां पुष्टि से होती है लुका 3ः22 मैं यीशु की बपतिस्मा के इस विवरण में को सुनेः यीशु की 32 माह के समय आत्मा के दृश्य प्रकटीकरण और स्वर्ग में वाड़ी के द्वारा स्वयं परमेश्वर के सार्वजनिक रूप से यहां पुष्टि की कि यीशु उसका पुत्र है।\r\nफिर लुका ने लुका 3ः23-38 मैं वंशावली के द्वारा यह पुष्टि की कि यीशु परमेश्वर का पुत्र है मती के समान लुका ने दाऊद और अब्राहम के धर्मी वंश के द्वारा यीशु की वंशावली को बताया परंतु मत्ती ने अलग-अलग दुकाने अपने विवरण में आदम तक मानवता की सारी धर्मी वंशावली को शामिल किया इस महा वंशावली के महत्व को समझने के लिए लुका 3ः38 मैं इसकी समाप्ति को देखेंलुका ने आदम को परमेश्वर का पुत्र कहां इन अध्ययनों में वही नाम यीशु को दिया गया है इस प्रकार लुका ने उसकी ओर संकेत किया जिस जिस से नए नियम के अन्य भागों में स्पष्टता से दिखाया गया है परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में यीशु परमेश्वर के पहले पुत्र आदम के उद्देश्य को पूरा करना था यह जैसे एक कुर्तियों 15 अध्याय का 45 पद में प्रेरित पौलुस ने कहा है  यीशु अंतिम आदम था आदमपुर थी पर परमेश्वर का सेवक राजा था जिससे परमेश्वर की इच्छा को पूरा करना था परंतु वह बुरी तरह से असफल हो गया यीशु परमेश्वर का महान पुत्र है जो वहां सफल हुआ जहां आदम हार गया था और उसके द्वारा पृथ्वी की प्रत्येक जाति तक उद्धार आया परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में यीशु की अंतिम पुष्टि लुक्का4ः1-13 मैं स्वयं इस द्वारा की गई है यह मरुभूमि में परीक्षा का अभिलेख है लू का 4 अध्याय का एक पद में लुका के वचन के अनुसार पवित्र आत्मा ने यीशु को भरा और उसे यरूशलेम में ले गया जहां शैतानी उसकी परीक्षा की शैतानी यीशु को पत्थर को रोटी बनाने शैतान से देशों पर अधिकार पाने और स्वयं को मंदिर के कंगूरे पर से नीचे गिराने के लिए लाल ललचाया इन दो परीक्षाओं की शुरुआत से ताने इन उपहासपूर्ण शब्दों से कि यदि तू परमेश्वर का पुत्र है जवाब  में  यीशु ने तीनों परीक्षाओं को जनता से अस्वीकार किया और पुराने नियम के उन परिचय दो का उल्लेख किया जो यह बताते हैं कि परमेश्वर एक विश्वास योग्य पुत्र को क्या करना चाहिए इसके बाद यीशु की वंशावली आती है जो परमेश्वर के रूप में आदम के साथ समाप्त होती है इसलिए यीशु की परीक्षा के लोगों के विवरण को उस उत्पत्ति अध्याय 3 में आदम की परीक्षा की तुलना में देखना चाहिए उस कहानी में श्वेता ने अदन की वाटिका में आदम की परीक्षा की और जब आदम ने पांच किया तो परमेश्वर ने सारी सृष्टि को शराब दिया और सारी मानवता को मरुभूमि में निकाल दिया इसके विपरीत मरुभूमि में यीशु ने परीक्षा का सामना किया और इससे यहां पुष्टि हुई कि वह परमेश्वर का विश्वास योग्य पुत्र था जो परमेश्वर के विश्वास क्योंकि लोगों को वापस स्वर्ग में लाएगा |', 9, '2020-08-15 12:03:30', '2020-08-22 11:57:40', NULL),
(1788, 519, 734, 'उत्तर   सुसमाचार के इस भाग में लुका ने यहां साबित करने के लिए यीशु की आर्चरी जनक सामर्थ्य और सुसमाचार प्रचार के बहुत से उदाहरणों की जानकारी दी कि यीशु ही आत्मा द्वारा अभिषेक तू धार करता था जिसका वायदा  पुराने नियम के द्वारा किया गया था।\r\n गलील मैं यीशु की सेवा कार्य का वर्णन करने वाले लुक्का के विवरण को पांच भागों में विभाजित किया जा सकता है पहला नसरत में यीशु का प्रचार दूसरा उसके उपदेश और अचारयकर्म तीसरा यीशु यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा देने वाले की भूमिकाओं में अंतर और पांचवें यीशु द्वारा बारह पेरितों को सेवकाई के लिए तैयार करना हम लुका 4ः14-30 मैं नासरत में यीशु के पहले प्रचार से आरंभ करके इनमें से प्रत्येक भाग को देखेंगे\r\n\r\n नासरत में प्रचार:-\r\n\r\n तीनों समदर्शी सुसमाचार यीशु की गलीली सेवाकाल के दौरान उसकी आश्चर्यजनक सामर्थ्य और सुसमाचार प्रचार पर बल देते हैं। परंतु लुक्का की प्रस्तुति दूसरों से भिन्न है क्योंकि उसने यीशु किससे इकाई के इस चरण का परिचय अपने गृहनगर नसरत में प्रभु के पहले प्रचार के साथ दिया है तू का ने बताया कि शब्द के दिन यीशु आराधना नहीं में था और उसे यशायाह की पुस्तक दी गई उसने यशायाह 61ः1-2 पड़ा और फिर एक चैंकाने वाली घोषणा की सुने लुका 4ः18-21  मैं यीशु ने क्या पढ़ा और कहाः जब उसने कहा आज ही वहां ले तुम्हारे सामने पूरा हुआ है तब यीशु यह कह रहा था कि पुराने नियम में जो बताया गया है और जिसकी अपेक्षा रखी गई है वहां अब पूरा हो रहा है और जुबली का पूरा विचार यही था कि आप की गणना के आधार पर 49 या 50 वर्ष  मैं पुराने नियम के इजरायल में लोगों को ऋण रोग से मुक्त कर दिया जाता था उनकी पैतृक संपत्ति वापस लौटा दी जाती थी उनके  गोत्रो को मूसा और यह उसी के दिनों में दी गई उनकी भूमि उन्हें वापस लौटा दी जाती थी यदि हम निर्गमन को छुटकारे के लिए पुराने नियम की एक बड़ी और महत्वपूर्ण घटना मानते हैं तो हमें यहां भी समझने की आवश्यकता है कि जुबली वर्ष पुनर्स्थापना के लिए परमेश्वर का महत्वपूर्ण प्रबंध था। क्योंकि जब तक हम इस पापी संसार में रहते हैं तब तक छुटकारा हमारे हमें बचाएगा परंतु पुनर्स्थापना परमेश्वर की छुटकारे का भाग है और इसलिए यीशु इस जुबली के चिन्हों को दिखाना आरंभ करना है वह लोगों को शैतानी दमन से मुक्त करता है उन्हें सामाजिक कल अन्य सामाजिक भेदभाव से मुक्त करता है और उन्हें उनके सृष्टिकर्ता और उस उनके पिता से मिलवाता है।\r\n यसायाह नो भविष्यवाणी की थी कि परमेश्वर के राज्य के आगमन से परमेश्वर के सारे विश्वास है कि लोगों को उद्धार मिलेगा और यीशु ने घोषणा की कि वह दिन आ चुका है या कथन यीशु की संपूर्ण सेव करके व्याख्या के लिए लूका के मूलभूत आदर्श को अभिशप्त करता है यीशु ही वह मसीहा उद्धार करता था जिन की भविष्यवाणी पुराने नियम में की गई थी और जो अपने लोगों को उध्दार देने के द्वारा परमेश्वर के राज्य को पृथ्वी पर प्रकट करेगा  नसरत में यीशु के प्रचार की जानकारी देने के बाद लुक्का ने लूका 4ः31-7ः17 मैं यीशु के सामर्थ्य उपदेश और चमत्कारों के कई उदाहरणों की जानकारी दी है।\r\n\r\n उपदेश और चमत्कार:-\r\n\r\n इस बात में लुका ने  दिखाया कि इस वास्तव में मसीहा था क्योंकि वह यशायाह 61ः1-2 की भविष्यवाणी को पूरा कर रहा था यीशु ने लूका 4ः31-36 मैं एक दुष्ट आत्मा से छुटकारा दिया4ः38-42 मैं उसने दूसरे बहुत से लोगों को चंगा किया और लुका 5ः1-11 मैं उसने अपने चेलों पतरस याकूब और यह युहन्ना को बुलाया।\r\n और बात के वचनों में भी हम इसी प्रारूप को पाते हैं जहां 5ः12-15 मैं थोड़ी और 5ः17-26 मैं लकवा की चंगाई के बाद 5ः27-32 मे  चेले लेवि या मत्ती को बुलाया जाता है  यही प्ररूप अगले वचनों में भी दोहराया गया है परंतु चंगाई की बजाय लुक्का ने यीशु के उपदेश को बताया है लुका 5ः33-39 मैं यीशु ने सिखाया कि उसकी शारीरिक उपस्थिति में उपवास की समाप्ति और आनंद होना चाहिए 6ः1-11 मैं इशू ने सिखाया की शब्त चंगा यू और प्राणों को बचाने के लिए है और 6ः12-16 मैं उसने अपने चेलों में से 12 को अपने विशेष प्रेरित बनने के लिए चुना जिन्हें इजरायल के लिए एक नए क्रम की स्थापना का कार्य सौंपा गया इन चमत्कारों और उपदेशों के द्वारा ईश्वर ने यहां दिखाएं कि वह वास्तव में यशा यहां द्वारा भविष्यवाणी किया हुआ मसीहा था क्योंकि वहां वास्तव में चंगाई और दमन से मुक्ति के रूप में प्रभु की कृपा को लाया था फिर लुक्का एक लंबे प्रचार के बारे में बताता है जिसे लोका ने 6 अध्याय का 17 पद से 49 में किया इस प्रचार को प्रिय यीशु का मैदानी उपदेश कहां जाता है और इनमें मती पांच और 7 अध्याय के पहाड़ी उपदेश के साथ बहुत सी समानताएं हैं।\r\n मैदानी उपदेश में ईश्वर ने उसी महान उल्टा पर बल दिया जिसकी यशायाह ने घोषणा की थी कंगाल धन्य होंगे भूखे तृप्त किए जाएंगे जो विलाप करते हैं वह हसेंगे और परमेश्वर असहयोग को को आशीष देगा परंतु शुभ संदेश एक और कदम आगे गया यीशु ने आशीष पाने वालों को अपने पीछे लाने और परमेश्वर के राज्य के मानकों एवं मूल्यों के अनुसार जीने के लिए बुलाया जो प्रिय सांसारिक मानकों से बहुत अलग होते हैं उदाहरण के लिए उसने उन्हें अन्य नदियों और यहां तक कि शत्रुओं से भी प्रेम रखने के लिए बुलाया जबकि सांसारिक मूल्य इसके विपरीत है जो हमें  अजनबी यों से सावधान रहने और शत्रुओं से गिरना करने के लिए कहते हैं तथा राज्य का संदेश केवल आशीष का ही नहीं परंतु नैतिक जिम्मेदारी का भी है मैदानी उपदेश के बाद लुका ने इसके कुछ और प्रमाणों के साथ इस भाग को समाप्त किया कि यीशु यशायाह की भविष्यवाणी को पूरा कर रहा था लुक्का 7 अध्याय का एक पद से 10 पद में यीशु ने एक सूबेदार के दास को चंगा किया और 7 अध्याय का 11 से 16 पद में उसने नाइन नगर की एक विधवा के मृत पुत्र को जीवित दिया दलील में यीशु की सेव काई में लुक्का आग अगले अभिलेख लुक्का 7 अध्याय का 18 पद से 50 पद में कहानियां का एक समूह है जो यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा देने वाले के बारे में है।\r\n\r\n यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा देने वाला:-\r\n\r\n यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा देने वाले की गिरफ्तारी के बाद उसने अपने कुछ चेलों को यीशु के पास यह पूछने के लिए भेजा कि क्या वहां वास्तव में मसीहा था और उसने जो किया था उसे स्मरण दिन आने के द्वारा उन्हें उत्तर दिया यीशु के चमत्कारों और प्रचार ने स्पष्ट यशायाह 61ः1-2 की भविष्यवाणियों को पूरा किया और उन्होंने यह साबित किया कि इस वास्तव में मसीहा था सुनील लुक्का 7 अध्याय का 22 में ईश्वर ने योजना के दूतों को क्या उत्तर दिया फिर इस नया इस पर पुष्टि की कि यूहन्ना  बहुत दुखता ओं में से सबसे महान था परंतु योना भी परमेश्वर के राज्य में सबसे छोटा व्यक्ति के बराबर नहीं था और लुक्का ने 7 अध्याय का 47 से 50 पद में यहां समझाते हुए इस बिंदु को विराम दिया कि ईश्वर ने वास्तव में अपने पैर धोने वाली अनैतिक स्त्री का पाप क्षमा कर दिया यूहन्ना परमेश्वर   क्षमा पाने के लिए लोगों को मन फिर आओ का बपतिस्मा दिया था परंतु यीशु पापियों को क्षमा करने बीमारों को चंगा करने और कंगारुओं को सुसमाचार सुनाने के द्वारा परमेश्वर के राज्य को लोगों के वर्तमान अनुभव में लाया योजना से संबंधित कहानियों के बाद लुक्का 8ः00 का एक से एक पद से 56 पद में काने यीशु के उपदेश और चमत्कारों के बारे में और अधिक जानकारी दी|\r\n\r\n उपदेश और चमत्कार:-\r\n\r\n अतिरिक्त उपदेशों और चमत्कारों में यीशु ने राज्य के शुभ संदेश पर ध्यान केंद्रित किया लुक्का 8 अध्याय का एक पद से 15 पद में बीज बोने वाले कब्रिस्तान और लू का 8 अध्याय का 16 पद से 18 पद में दिवस के दृष्टांत विश्वास और आज्ञा पालन में राज्य के संदेश का प्रयोग कर देने के महत्व का वर्णन किया और इन्हीं विषयों को उसने लू का 8 अध्याय का 19 पद से 21 पद में दोहराया जब उसने कहा कि उससे के सच्चे पारिवारिक सदस्य वह है जो परमेश्वर के वचन को सुनते हैं और मानते हैं फिर लुका 8 अध्याय का 22556 पर मलूका ने कई चमत्कारों की जानकारी दी जिन्होंने इशू द्वारा लाया गया उद्धार की पुष्टि और उसका प्रदर्शन किया इसने तूफान को शांत किया दुष्ट आत्मा को निकाला एक बीमार स्त्री को चंगा किया और एक मृत लड़की को जीवित किया अंशु का 9 अध्याय का एक पद से 50 बदमाशों द्वारा सेव काय के लिए 12 पेरितों को तैयार करने की जानकारी देने के साथ लुक्का गलील में यीशु की सेव कोकेके अपने विवरण को समाप्त करताहै \r\nबाहर प्रेरितो की तैयारी:-\r\n पहले लुका 9 अध्याय का एक से 9 पद में यीशु ने अपने 12 पृष्ठों को बीमारों को चंगा करने और सुसमाचार का प्रचार करने के लिए भेजा यह वही लोग थे जिन्होंने उसने लोकांचे में अलग किया था फिर उसने 9 अध्याय का 10 से 17 पद में 5000 लोगों को तृप्त करने के द्वारा अपनी सामर्थ्य का प्रदर्शन किया और अपने प्रेरकों को उसकी सामर्थ्य उसके प्रबंध पर भरोसा रखना  सिखाया और यह तैयारी लुक्का 9 अध्याय का 18 पद से 27 पद में पूरी हुई जहां प्रेरित हों ने यह अंगीकार किया कि इस वही चिर प्रतिक्षित मसीहा है लुका ने यीशु द्वारा अपने प्रेरकों को सेव काय के लिए विशेष स्वर्गारोहण के बाद की सेव काय के लिए निरंतर तैयार करने से संबंधित कई कहानियां के द्वारा इस भाग को समाप्त किया लू का 9 अध्याय का 28 पद से 36 पर्द  में पत्र याकूब और यूहन्ना के सामने यीशु का रूपांतर हुआ जहां यीशु के प्रति उनके समर्पण की पुष्टि  करने के लिए स्वर्ग से पिता की वाणी सुनाई दे फिर 9 अध्याय का 37 पद से 45 यीशु ने एक बहुत ही कठिन दुष्ट आत्मा को निकाला और 9 अध्याय का 46 पद से 50 पद में राज्य में महानता के बारे में सिखाया इन सारे विवरणों में इसने अपने चेलों को उसके अधिकार को पहचानने उसकी शामत पर भरोसा रखने और उसके नाम में नम्रता सो के रूप में सेवा करने के लिए तैयार किया था कि वे पृथ्वी पर उसके राज्य के प्रभावशाली  बना सके ।', 9, '2020-08-15 12:20:36', '2020-08-22 11:57:40', NULL),
(1789, 519, 735, 'उत्तर =  पापियों और कंगाल हो जैसे सामाजिक रुप से अलग-थलग किए गए समूह पर लुका द्वारा दिए गए  बल के प्रति हमें  इस प्रकार प्रत्युत्तर  देना चाहिए - प्रभु यीशु मसीह धर्मों के लिए नहीं लेकिन पापियों के लिए इस संसार में आए पापियों के पाप के उद्धार के लिए प्रभु यीशु मसीह 39 कोडे  करके कलवरी क्रूस पर बलिदान हो  लोका ने अपनी किताब में इस प्रकार से भी लिखा है प्रभु यीशु मसीह धन वालों के लिए नहीं परंतु निर्बल के लिए इस संसार पर आए प्रभु यीशु मसीह का वचन हमें सिखाते हैं जो अपने आप को छोटा बनाएगा वह बड़ा किया जाएगा अर्थात सचमुच जो इस संसार में रहने के समय जिस भी व्यक्ति प्रभु ईसा मसीह को नम्र और दीनता के साथ में यीशु मसीह को ग्रहण करता है स्वीकार करता है उन्हें प्रभु यीशु मसीह अपना राज्य उसको उसको देगा हम अपने आपको नंबर और दिन बनाते हैं तो प्रभु यीशु मसीह हमारे लिए इस संसार में आया क्योंकि हम अभी ही थे जन्म से हम पाप में जीवन व्यतीत करते थे और प्रभु यीशु मसीह धार्मिकता में अर्थात परमेश्वर का वचन में लिखा है सारे जो है व्यवस्था के अध्ययनों को मॉल में ले कर के हमारे लिए उन्हें पूरा किया और आज दिया नम्रता से ईश्वर से प्रार्थना करते हैं हमारे उद्धार प्रभु यीशु मसीह जरूर हमें देगा इसी प्रकार से हम लुक्का द्वारा दिए गए बल के प्रति हमें इस प्रकार से प्रत्युत्तर  दे सकते हैं एक डॉक्टर चंगू के लिए नहीं परंतु बीमारियों के लिए उपयोगी होता है उसी प्रकार से प्रभु यीशु मसीह भी धर्मों के लिए नहीं परंतु पापियों के लिए स्वर्गीय की महिमा को छोड़कर इस पृथ्वी पर आया प्रभु यीशु मसीह कलवरी क्रूस पर धर्म युग के लिए नहीं परंतु पापियों के लिए बलिदान हुआ जब तक हमें संसार में है तब तक हम प्रभु यीशु मसीह के सामने अपने आप को छोटा बनकर के नंबर बनकर के दिन बंन करके उसके उपस्थित में हर एक समय में उसे स्मरण करें लुक्का भी हमें इसी प्रकार से अपने सुसमाचार में सिखाता है तथा अपने आपको हम छोटा और नम्र बने प्रभु यीशु मसीह ने एक दृष्टांत दिया स्वर्ग का राज छोटे बच्चों के समान है बच्चों को मेरे पास में आने दो क्योंकि यह बच्चे अपने आप पर नंबर होते हैं निष्कलंक होते हैं अपने मन में कोई कपट नहीं रखते हैं इसीलिए यीशु मसीह ने बच्चों का उदाहरण दिया और हमें भी अपने आप को बच्चों के समान नंबर और देवता के साथ में छोटे बनकर के प्रभु यीशु मसीह का स्मरण करें प्रभु यीशु मसीह के सामने अपने आप को जो है ना और दिन तक साथ में प्रभु यीशु मसीह के सामने अपने जीवन को समर्पित करें ऐसा करने से प्रभु समस्या में प्रेम करेगा इस प्रकार से लुका द्वारा दिए गए बल के प्रति हम उसका प्रत्युत्तर कर दे सकता ।', 9, '2020-08-15 12:35:45', '2020-08-22 11:57:40', NULL),
(1790, 519, 736, 'उत्तर = यहां जान करके हमें इसलिए महत्वपूर्ण है कि यीशु स्वर्गीय की महिमा को छोड़कर के सारे मनुष्य जाति के पापों के लिए इस संसार पर आए सारे मानव जाति पाप की दुनिया में जीवन जीते थे पाप में जीते थे जन्म से पापी ही जीते थे और वह उनका भाग नर्क था यह सब देख कर के प्रभु यीशु को तरस आया पिता परमेश्वर को सारे मानव जाति के लिए ऊपर में दया आया और उसने सारे मानव जाति के जाति से प्रेम किया अनंत काल का प्रेम किया यीशु मसीह ने उस प्रेम के खातिर प्रभु यीशु मसीह आज से 2000 वर्ष पहले इस संसार पर आया और हमारे पापों के लिए सारे मनुष्य जाति जो प्रभु यीशु मसीह पर विश्वास करता है उनके पापों को उसने कलवरी क्रूस पर उठा करके अपने आप को बलिदान हुआ प्रभु यीशु मसीह मर कर के मृत्यु के ऊपर में जयपाकर के तीसरे दिन जी उठा और 40 दिन तक के चेलों को प्रगट होता रहा उसके बाद प्रभु यीशु मसीह जी भी स्वर्ग पर उठा लिया गयाहै  प्रभु यीशु मसीह पिता के दाहिने और विराजमान है आज भी पिता के दाने और जीवित है वह प्रभु यीशु मसीह हमारे लिए निरंतर पिता से बीच हवाई करता है जो प्रभु यीशु मसीह पर विश्वास करता है उससे नंबर और दीनता से प्रार्थना करता है उसके पापों को प्रभु यीशु मसीह क्षमा करता है और उनके लिए नर्क नहीं परंतु उनके लिए स्वर्ग का राज्य प्रभु यीशु मसीह देने वाले हैं प्रभु यीशु मसीह जल्दी ही इस पृथ्वी पर आने वाले हैं अपने पुत्र लोगों को लेने के लिए हमें इस बात की बहुत ही खुशी होती है कि प्रभु यीशु मसीह ने हमारे पापों के लिए अपने ऊपर में उस पात को मिटा लिया और उसमें आपको ऐसा मिटा दिया कि वह पाप हमारे जीवन में कभी भी नहीं आ सकता है और अब प्रभु यीशु मसीह हमें दर में ठहरा दिया है प्रभु समस्या में धर्मी ठहराया है तो आ मेशवर्क कर आज भी समस्या में देने वाला है और अब हमारा नरक नहीं है परंतु स्वर्ग है इस बात की खुशी हमारे जीवन में होती है प्रभु यीशु मसीह स्तुति पर अपना राज्य को जल्दी ही स्थापित करने वाला है हम सभी को प्रभु यीशु मसीह पर इन दिनों विश्वास करना चाहिए प्रभु यीशु मसीह पर विश्वास करना और अपने आपको नंबर बनाना ही हमारे लिए महत्वपूर्ण है प्रभु यीशु मसीह अपने लोगों को पाप से इस प्रकार से बचाने के लिए इस पृथ्वी पर आया यही हमारे लिए खुशी की बात है। हर व्यक्ति को यह बातें जानना अवश्य है कि प्रभु यीशु मसीह हमारे पापों के खातिर कलवरी क्रूस पर मारा गया हमारे पापों के खातिर प्रभु यीशु मसीह इस संसार पर अपने आप को बलिदान हुआ प्रभु यीशु मसीह का स्वर्ग की महिमा को छोड़कर की इस पृथ्वी पर आने का भी यही कारण था कि अपने लोगों को पाप की गंदगी से बचा करके उन्हें स्वर्ग राज्य में खड़ा कर सके और उन्हें स्वर्ग राज्य का अधिकार दे सके हम सभी को प्रभु यीशु मसीह पर इंदिरा में विश्वास बनाए रखें अपने पवित्र लोगों को प्रभु यीशु मसीह जल्दी लेने आने वाला है।', 9, '2020-08-15 12:51:01', '2020-08-22 11:57:40', NULL),
(1791, 520, 886, 'The concept of the church in the New Testament finds it roots in the Old Testament. The NT speaks many times of the church using the word ekklesia. But this term comes from the Greek translation of Old Testament, Septuagint. Ekklesia and its Hebrew counterpart is frequently used to identify the gathered nation of Israel. In the New Testament, ekklesia became a technical term referring to the church while being used to the assembly of Old Testament Israel. For example, in Acts 7.38- the Greek word translated assembly is ekklesia, which is commonly translated to \'\'church.\'\' This means that the assembly of Israel was Old Testament equivalent to our New Testament Church.\r\nWe can see that the Old Testament church has been improved and built into the New Testament church. They are different in some important ways and they represent different stages of growth, but are still the same church.', 9, '2020-08-16 15:39:34', '2020-08-22 11:58:31', NULL),
(1792, 520, 887, 'In the original context of Jesus ministry, the only church that existed was Jewish synagogues scattered throughout the region and the temple of Jerusalem. They were the Old Testament forms of Israel\'s assemblies, but Jesus still called them, \'\'the church.\'\' Firstly, the New Testament presents Jesus as the fulfillment of God\'s promises to Israel. As we see in Romans 8.1-4 and Galatians 3.16-29, Jesus is shown as the faithful Israelite who keeps God\'s covenant and inherits all the blessing, God promised to Abraham and Moses. \r\nSecondly, Jesus is the founder of  the New Testament church, who brought the restoration and renewal that changed the failing Old Testament into the New Testament church. He is called the head of the church in Ephesians 5.23 and Colossians 1.18. He is also called the husband of the church in Ephesians 5.22-23. \r\nThus Jesus built his church in these ways that relied and advanced the Old Testament church.', 8, '2020-08-16 15:48:38', '2020-08-22 11:58:31', NULL),
(1793, 520, 888, 'Jesus ordained the New Testament church as the restoration and development of Old Testament Israel, one important implication is that there is fundamental continuity between the Israel in the Old Testament and the present Christian church in the New Testament. Practically, we should expect the community of God\'s people in the New Testament to reflect its Old Testament. \r\nPurpose- to turn the world into God\'s earthly kingdom. Redemption of humanity and creation has always been the purpose of God\'s church in both the testaments. \r\nBelievers and Unbelievers- both assemblies include believers and unbelievers. The continuity between Old Testament church and New Testament in the present time is that both assemblies of God\'s people include believers and unbelievers.\r\nObligations- Both the testaments, people of God were given the responsibility to love God, spread His Kingdom throughout the world,and bring him glory. Greatest commandment is Heartfelt love for God as in 1 John 5.3.', 8, '2020-08-16 15:57:29', '2020-08-22 11:58:31', NULL),
(1794, 520, 889, 'The word \'\'catholic\'\' means universal; or including all Christians in all congregations. word Catholic coming from the Latin word Catholicus derives from Greek preposition  .Kata and the adjective holos means whole or \'\'complete.\'\' It is a description of the unity that exists between all churches that faithfully follow Christ. The Apostolic Creed speaks of the catholicity of the church, it does not have in mind an organization of all Christian congregations. Rather, it tells about the unity of the Holy Spirit that exists all legitimate Christian Churches. In history, it meant to extend the name \'\'church\'\' to every Christian congregation. At this time, these churches began to use the word \'\'catholic\'\' in new exclusive sense. By insisting that their own churches were catholic or universal, each meant to identify itself as the only valid church, and to condemn rival churches.', 8, '2020-08-16 16:10:32', '2020-08-22 11:58:31', NULL),
(1795, 520, 890, 'The visible church is said to be as one worldwide fellowship of all people in covenant with God under headship of Christ. There is no single denomination whose government extends over all Christian congregation. Rather the unity of the visible church is based on the fact that each church is in covenant with same God, and under the covenant headship of the same Christ. The three traditional marks of the church are as follows,\r\nPreaching of the word. God has given the Bible to the whole visible church and he gave the Holy Spirit to help us understand it. Scripture exhorts the whole church to read, understand, and to teach God\'s word as we see in Matthew 28.20, 1 Timothy 4.17 etc.\r\nSecond mark is the right administration of the sacraments of baptism and the Lord\'s Supper. These sacraments belong to the visible church not just to one denomination.\r\nthird mark is the formal church discipline such as excommunication. No christian enjoys formal church discipline. And this had led churches to avoid the use of formal discipline.', 9, '2020-08-16 16:18:42', '2020-08-22 11:58:31', NULL),
(1796, 518, 858, 'Love is central to Bible\'s teaching, we are exhorted to love the Lord and also to love each other. \r\n\r\nLoyalty is the cornerstone of the concept of love. \r\nIn the Old Testament period, God is our king and he rules over us, Suzerain love was expressed largely in the form of covenant loyalty to his people. We are bound in covenant with God. The most important way we can show our love form him is through our earnest covenant loyalty\r\nIn the New Testament - Jesus is our Lord and King, and we are to render love to him through loyal obedience.\r\nWe cannot place other loyalties ahead of our loyalty to him. \r\nLoyalty is a positive virtue, motivating us to serve our Lord and King\r\n\r\nOrientation:\r\nOur lives must be comprehensively oriented around God. God and his kingdom should be our highest priorities, our focus and our desires should revolve around God. Scripture teaches us to be fully committed to God and his people.\r\nThe prime example for proper orientation is the life of Jesus. \r\nJesus life revolved around God and the people he came to save. This orientation motivated him to obey God perfectly in all things.\r\n\r\nResponsibility\r\nOur loving submission to God should motivate us to seek out additional ways that we are responsible to him.\r\nSeeking our reponsibilities before God, provides us unlimited allegiance to God.\r\nUnderstanding that we are obligated to God in every area of our life, we are in a better position to make decision that God approves.', 0, '2020-08-19 15:16:04', '2020-08-19 15:16:04', NULL),
(1797, 518, 859, 'The actions of God in atoning grace and common grace can be explained as follows :\r\n\r\nATONING GRACE \r\nGod always acts according to his character, all his actions are perfect expressions of his character. Scripture exhorts us to pattern both our character and our actions after God.\r\n\r\nJesus taught that we are to imitate God\'s forgiveness. We are to forgive those who sin against us because God has forgiven us.\r\n\r\nAs sinners we were offensive to God. We hated God and were his enemies. We deserved punishment no mercy. But God loved us and gave his only begotten son as sacrifice for our sins. And following his example we should be willing to suffer on behaf of others.\r\n\r\nWe are asked to show the same kind of love towards others that God showed in the atonment, by giving up our comforts and supporting others sharing our wealth and possessions, and even our lives to protect, care for our brothers and sisters. To love the people around us wholeheartedly\r\n\r\nCOMMON GRACE\r\nCommon grace refers to God\'s kindness to those who will never be saved. \r\nJesus referred to God\'s common grace as an expression of his love to all humanity and it is true and genuine, it provides us a model we are to imitate.\r\n\r\nJesus taught that God\'s perfection includes his love for evil people, even for those who will never come to faith in Christ.\r\nGod expresses his love in many ways, sch as through sunshine, rain etc. God is kind to all people, providing stability and productivity for them in nature and allowing them to thrive in this life', 0, '2020-08-19 15:32:48', '2020-08-19 15:32:48', NULL),
(1798, 521, 891, 'The problem of sin is that it separates us from God\'s blessings and places under His curse. It condemns us. Apart from Christ, there is no other way to save ourselves from its presence or its consequences. Bible uses words like lawlessness, rebellion, transgression, offense, evil, and missing the mark to describe things that are sinful. It is violation of God\'s law. Omitting or neglecting the Law, is called the sin of omission and the transgression of law is doing what scripture forbids. This is the sin of commission. \r\nSin originated from the rebellion against God, when Adam and Eve disobeyed and violated God\'s law and willingly chose to sin. Love for God is manifested in obedience to his law. \r\nAnd because of this, the consequences was that God judged and cursed the entire human race resulting in Spiritual death, corruption, and physical death. Sin earned humanity eternal suffering under God\'s judgement in hell.', 9, '2020-08-19 15:39:08', '2020-08-22 11:59:12', NULL),
(1799, 521, 892, 'God was not willing to let the entire human race remain under the curse of sin. So He sent us the redeemer, Jesus Christ to solve the problem of sin. \r\n\r\n1. Father- The Father sent the Son into the world and appointed him as the redeemer. He is the great architect of redemption. \r\n2. Son- Son was sent to the world becoming incarnate as Jesus, the long awaited Messiah, in order to atone for human sin. Jesus atoned for sin by dying on the cross in place of sinners. He received the divine curse that had been warranted by our sin. \r\n3. Holy Spirit- It reconciles us to God for forgiving all the sins we have committed. He gives us new spiritual life by regenerating our spirits, implications of the saving grace, continuity to forgiveness to us and maintains our faith, and leads us to daily repentance. \r\n\r\nWe have been given the right to make petition to all three divine persons, give thanks to all three persons of God and take great confidence n our salvation, knowing that all three persons of the Trinity love us and work to ensure our redemption.', 8, '2020-08-19 15:48:48', '2020-08-22 11:59:12', NULL),
(1800, 518, 860, 'Motive can be the purpose for which we take an action. Motives are essentially the same as goals. \r\nMotive serve as causes, and our actions are the affects they produce. The list of motives include, our character traits, desires, feelings, commitments etc.\r\n\r\nBible makes it clear that if we are truly ethical, we must be rooted in God honoring motives. \r\n\r\nDavid taught Solomon that obedience to God must flow from the depths of our inner person, and it involes wholehearted devotion and willing mind, as God hates hypocrisy.\r\n\r\nGod is not interested only in the outward obedience. He requires every heart and motive behind the thoughts to be truly committed to him, genuine obedience from our deepest thougts and desires. \r\n\r\nGod requires wholehearted obedience, that flows from the heart with good motives.\r\n\r\nBible condemns lip service, or evil motives calling it hypocrisy.\r\n\r\nThe virtue of Christian love should motivate us to act in loving ways. Similarly people who are joyful in the Spirit should be motivated by their joy. Peaceful peple motivated by the peace within them.\r\n\r\nThe greatest example we can look at would be the life of Jesus Christ, which provides us a lasting impact with genuine values both inward and outward and motivates us to do our best in glorfying God both externally and internally.', 0, '2020-08-19 15:50:09', '2020-08-19 15:50:09', NULL),
(1801, 521, 893, 'The process of forgiveness involves an element of individual responsibility.\r\n1. Conditions- Faith in God- God\'s divine sovereignty, loyal submission to him, and trust that he will show us mercy for sake of our redeemer Jesus Christ should be acknowledged. Those who fear the Lord receive his forgiveness. Genuine sorrow over sin and true regret over violating God\'s law shows the brokenness of heart. \r\n2. Means- Sometimes Christians fail to distinguish between means of grace and basis of grace. The basis of grace is the merit of Christ. The tool is prayer and means of grace is faith. Prayer is an ordinary means for appealing to God for grace and forgiveness. We can receive forgiveness by asking for it with a broken heart. Prayer of intercession acts as extra ordinary means of forgiveness. Sacraments, which refer to Lord\'s supper and baptism, become means to ask for forgiveness.', 8, '2020-08-19 16:03:14', '2020-08-22 11:59:12', NULL),
(1802, 518, 861, 'Yes I do remember when I came first to faith. It was a complete transformation and change in one\'s life. The submission and surrender as well as the motivation to serve the Lord and this priority, all other factors revolved around this priority pleasing God and serving Him in faith \r\n\r\nFaith is the means of initial salvation, it is a tool that God uses to apply salvation to sinful individuals. There is nothing in our faith that deserves or earns salvation. On the contrary Christ freely gives us salvation through faith.\r\nIt is God\'s gracious act by which he forgives our sins. And it changes our status forever.\r\nGod uses saving faith to justify us, and this indeed motivates us to repent of our sin and trust in Christ for our salvation.\r\nThe good works that follows are the first evidences of our salvation since they can only be motivated by a genuine saving faith.\r\n\r\nOngoing commitment, consists of studying the word of God and continuing trust in Christ to save us fro our sin. Active faith plays a very important role in motivating our life to good works. \r\nSaving faith involves our hearts. creating within us an inward desire to think, speak and act in ways that pleases God\r\nSpending more time in the Word, meditating on God\'s promises with continual repentance on daily basis with genuine faith and commitment - helps us to grow spiritually in faith in our salvation journey, motivating us to grow form the point from where we began. This growth is visible both internally and externally.\r\n\r\nTrue faith characterizes us to good works, through out our lives and with the guidance of the Holy Spirit - the equation changes completely, because it is God who works in our life to do his good will.', 0, '2020-08-19 16:05:37', '2020-08-19 16:05:37', NULL),
(1803, 521, 894, 'God created human beings to consist of physical bodies and non physical souls, as according to Hebrews 4.12 and 1 Thessalonians 5.23. Before our fall into the sin, our bodies and our souls were unaffected by sin and its corrupting powers. But when Adam and Eve fell into sin, sin corrupted not only their souls, but also their bodies. And this corruption of their bodies ultimately resulted in their physical death. \r\nWhen Adam and Eve sinned against God, he cursed them both with that they would be mortal. They would die and return to dust. Since all human beings descend from Adam and Eve, we all are born with similar corruption. \r\nSin affected Adam and Eve in both spiritual and physical ways. Our souls come into the world in a state that Bible describes as spiritual death. We are all under God\'s judgement and have lost all ability to please him. This corruption results in physical hardship, sickness and eventually death, as said in Romans 6.12-19 and 7.4-25. Sin therefore, corrupts all that we are- our entire being, body and soul.', 9, '2020-08-19 16:16:05', '2020-08-22 11:59:12', NULL),
(1804, 521, 895, 'The three stages of redemption is as follows,\r\n1. Present Life;- Salvation of our bodies begins with the indwelling of the Holy Spirit. Bible teaches that salvation of our bodies begins when we come to faith, with the indwelling of Holy Spirit. and our bodies continue to benefit through it, by the process of sanctification. Sanctification of our bodies is similar to the sanctification of our souls.\r\n2. Intermediate State- During this state, our souls dwell with Christ in heaven while our bodies remain on earth. When we die, our bodies are temporarily separated from our souls. Our bodies are still corrupted by sin, as proven by the fact that they can decay. But the sin that corrupts them can no longer influence us to commit sin.\r\n3. New Life- Our bodies will receive new, perfect life when they are restored to life in the general resurrection. In the resurrection, the consequences of sin will finally and forever be completely put away from us.', 8, '2020-08-19 16:24:26', '2020-08-22 11:59:12', NULL),
(1805, 518, 862, 'Imagination refers to our ability to form mental images of things beyond our experience. Imaginative abilities are vital to learning and thinking about God the world and ourselves\r\n\r\nTo study further we need to consider three factors that affect imagination\r\n\r\nCREATIVITY\r\nImagination is a form of creativity, it involves in everything we make or create. We use imagination on our day to day lives and in many creative ways.\r\nImagination is involved in everything we make or create. Scientists use thier imaginations to come up with theories and ways of testing them. \r\n\r\nFor instance in the old testament we read about Nathan the prophet confronting King David using an imaginary situation, and he asks David to draw a conclusion on that situation.\r\n\r\nTIME\r\nTime is another important factor, since we have to consider that Jesus Christ is no longer on earth teaching his disciples, we have to consider the period in which all these events happened in history. We have to draw out our imaginations accordingly. Bible requires us to pursue goals for the future in glorification of God through the triumph of his kingdom. But since these events are yet to happen, we have to figure out the best means to use to reach this goal and this cannot happen unless we imagine the future. \r\n\r\nDISTANCE\r\nMost of the historical places mentioned in the Bible are places which we have never seen for ourselves, but we need to imagine those places and study the scriptures with regards to the context and place. When people and things are so far rom beyond our range of senses, we cannot have it as part of experience, but instead we need to use our imaginations to think about the place they lived in and the situation around them. We have to strongly rely on the Holy Spirit to evaluation our imagination according to God\'s word and then to harmonize it with our abilities to understand and study the Scripture further.', 0, '2020-08-19 16:24:43', '2020-08-19 16:24:43', NULL),
(1806, 518, 863, 'Assessing knowledge is an important step in the process of making ethical decisions, it can be divided into three categories\r\nReason\r\nConscience\r\nEmotions \r\n\r\nREASON :\r\nReason is defined as the capcity to make logical inferences. \r\nAs a Christian, right reasoning is the ability to think in orderly ways and to make judgements in accordance with biblical pattern\r\nReasoning enables us to make sense of the situation, both by helping us understand the facts and to compare these facts with the word of God. All the knowledge that we acquire through sensory experience requires a measure of reasoning. \r\nJesus taught us that since God feeds the birds, which have little value, how much more will he feed his people who have more value.\r\nScripture uses reasons all the time and it calls us to do the same. It constantly present logical, moral arguments.\r\n\r\nCONSCIENCE \r\nIt is God given ability to discern both good and evil. It is also referred to as the sense of conviction that our thoughts, words and deeds are either pleasing or offensive to God.\r\nConscience enables us to assess the knowledge we have acquired and to judge it against the standard of God\'s word. It approves us when we believe we are acting in accord with God\'s word and it condemns us when we believe we are violating God\'s word.\r\n\r\nEMOTIONS\r\nEmotions are inner feelings, they are affective in our ethincal sensitivity.\r\nEmotions are God given human abilities that enable us to assess our knowledge in many diferent ways. Our emotions are the initial interpretation of the facts.\r\nOur emotions can be very useful tools for determining how God\'s word applies to our lives\r\nFeeling of compassion can result in helping those in need\r\nAnger can persuade us to follow pursuing justice\r\nExperiences of Joy can enable us to affirm God\'s goodnees even in difficult times\r\nFeeling of guilt can alert us to times we have fallen into sin\r\n\r\nE', 0, '2020-08-19 16:44:46', '2020-08-19 16:44:46', NULL),
(1807, 518, 864, 'Will is the capacity for making decisions, it is our ability to make choices. \r\nWhen we consider our will, it is to view our entire decision making process from the perspective of the choices that we make, especially from the perspective of the final outcome.\r\n\r\nFor Christians this eans that while Holy Spirit enables us to make decisions that please God, there is always the possiblity that indwelling sin will persuade us to make sinful decisions. \r\n\r\nOur will may be neither active nor passive. We make decisions in a passive unconscious manner wuch as by force or habit. But at other times the ethical questions we face require reflection and conscious decisions.\r\n\r\nThere are many other ethical issues that we handle in a passive manner such as those that we deal with habitually or we respond to in a reflective manner.\r\n\r\nIf we really need to please our Lord, we must submit our will to him at every turn. We must will that God\'s word commands and we must allow the Holy Spirit working within us to influence our will.\r\n\r\nApostle Paul says in the book of Philippians\r\nIt is God who works in you to will and to according to his good purpose\r\n\r\nGod has given faculties that play important role in choosing good. If we overlook any of them we run the risk of not being able to make truly moral decisions.', 0, '2020-08-19 16:53:45', '2020-08-19 16:53:45', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(1808, 518, 865, 'Jesus here refers to the fact that motives of the heart does matter. God requires every heart and every motive behind the thoughts to be truly committed to him. He requires genuine obedience that flows from our deepest thoughts and desires. \r\n\r\nHerein Jesus refers as to who is a good man, who has his heart with the right motives, it is referred to as good treasure stored in his heart. And that treasure when it is traded or brought out makes the person itself good in the sight of God, his entire personality is changed due to the fact that the treasure stored in his heart is good. The radiance of God that flows out through his life, reflects his lifestyle and behavior and that does play a major role in impactive the lives of all those who come in contact with him and he is referred to as \"Good Man\" useful for God and man.\r\n\r\nBut whereas exactly the opposte - the Evil man is definied by his source of motive in the heart - wherein is stored evil motives, same fact here also but the treasure stored is evil.  His life and personality has a negative impact on the society. Life itself becomes a tragedy as the motives of the heart does matter in the sight of God and Man. His entire personality revolves around the evil that emanates from his heart. \r\n\r\nJesus made it very clear that a persons actions or words are known by what is stored in his heart.  Out of the abundance of his heart, his mouth speaks, and that defines his lifestyle in general.\r\n\r\nFrom this perspective Jesus wants all of us to surrender our lives and hearts to the will of God, and to draw closer to him in genuine good works with godly motives. \r\n\r\nMy heart and works are in sync with the Word of God and under the guidance of the Holy Spirit. \r\nAs long as we are in the flesh, there is bound to be corruption, but God is gracious and helps in correcting our desires and motives under the guidance of the Word and Holy Spirit. \r\n\r\nNo man is perfect, but everyone needs to strive and work out your own salvation and grow spiritually as Christ the Head.', 0, '2020-08-19 17:11:52', '2020-08-19 17:11:52', NULL),
(1809, 522, 761, 'During  the creation week the rolls as per the scripture John 1.1-3 and Hebrews 1.2 God the Father created the the world by or through him {Jesus} and scripture teach us that son was fathers side during the creation and the Father created the world through him.\r\n\r\nIt was Christ the word the logos of God who was the creative agents through whom God made the world, not only son created the world he bought everything into being God spoke it was verbal action, the word which was spoken we come to understand that this word is Jesus Christ.\r\nwithin six dAYS GOD FORMED and shaped the world through the power of His word.\r\ng\r\nGod ordered and filled the universe in ways that pleased him.first three days of creation\r\nformed the world\r\nseparated light from the darkness\r\nSEPARATED SKY FROM WATEDCREATED VEGETATIONS\r\n\r\nsecond three days\r\ncreated the sun moon and stars\r\nassigned the sun to rule day and moon to rule in the night\r\ncreated the fish and other creatures of the sea\r\ncreated the birds to inhabit all the animals that is on the earth', 9, '2020-08-21 17:49:48', '2020-08-22 11:56:33', NULL),
(1810, 522, 762, 'God s eternal counsel regarding Christ is God\'s plan for the universe\r\n which were set before his work before the creation\r\nforeknowledge and purpose are to aspects of his eternal counsel. GODs knowledge prior to the creation of events that world occurs in the course of history and God created the universe in order to display and increase his glory through his kingdom in Christ\r\nthe bible says Ish 46.10 I make known to end from the beginning, from ancient times, what is still to come. I say my purpose will stand and I will do all that I please.', 7, '2020-08-21 17:58:59', '2020-08-22 11:56:33', NULL),
(1811, 522, 763, 'God\'s promises are immutable, they can never change and he will never break them, whatever God promises he will continually fulfill.\r\npromises between the fATHER and son being rooted for sons role in redemption\r\n\r\nTherefore Trinity entered into an arrangement that they promised to redeem fallen humanity.\r\nthrough the covenant grace God, the father promised to fulfill his kingdom plan for creation and humanity through the son. particularly sons incarnation as Jesus Christ of Nazareth. and son promised to be incarnate as he being descended from God\'s chosen line of Davidic kings.', 7, '2020-08-21 18:09:46', '2020-08-22 11:56:33', NULL),
(1812, 522, 764, 'Through obedience Jesus\' role as a redeemer included success.\r\n\r\nThere are four aspects of Jesus redeeming work that is His inauguration of the kingdom of God, His obedience to the father his resurrection, and his ascension.\r\n\r\nPassive obedience Jesus submission to a life of humiliation, suffering, and crucifixion.\r\nJesus was our substitute \r\nJesus sacrifices on the cross freed us from God just condemnation\r\nactive obedience, Jesus life of obedience to everything the father commanded\r\nJesus perfectly kept gods law', 7, '2020-08-21 18:20:21', '2020-08-22 11:56:33', NULL),
(1813, 522, 765, 'At least three crucial events will take place when Jesus returns. The general Theresurrection the last judgment and renewal of the creation.\r\nas per Jesus\' words, john 5.28 29 at the christ return everyone that has died will be resurrected both the wicked and the righteous will be blessed.\r\nTransform our lowly bodies so that there will be like his glorious bodies Phil 3.20\r\nlast judgement Jesus will exercise his authority and power as king destroying the enemies and blessing all his faithful people.\r\nrenewal of creation also will take place.', 7, '2020-08-21 18:33:22', '2020-08-22 11:56:33', NULL),
(1814, 523, 722, 'लेखक :- जब भी हम किसी पुस्तक या पत्री या किसी अन्य लेखन का चयन करते हैं तो इसके लेखक के बारे में जानना अति आवश्यक होता है क्योंकि जितना अधिक हम लेखक और उसके संदर्भ के बारे में जानेंगे। हम उतना ही अधिक उसके दृष्टिकोण तथा उसके लेखन के बारे में समझेंगे और बाइबल अध्ययन में भी यही बात पाई जाती है। जितना अधिक हम बाइबल के लेखकों के बारे में जानेंगे। उतना ही अधिक हम उन बातों को सीख सकेंगे। जो भी हमें सिखाते हैं। अतः जब मत्ती रचित सुसमाचार को देखते हैं तो सबसे पहला प्रश्न जो हम पूछना चाहते हैं, वह यह है इस पुस्तक को किसने लिखा है। हम मत्ती रचित सुसमाचार के लेखक का दो चरणों में अध्ययन करेंगे।\r\n1.हम इस पारंपरिक विचारधारा की पुष्टि करेंगे कि इस पुस्तक को प्रेरित मत्ती ने लिखा था जो यीशु के आरंभिक 12 चेलों में से एक था। \r\n2. हम मत्ती के व्यक्तिगत इतिहास को देखेंगे। आइए हम पर अवगत विचारधारा से आरंभ करें कि मत्ती ने इसे लिखा है।\r\n1.परंपरागत दृष्टिकोण।:- मैं सोचता हूं कि हम इस बात के प्रति काफी आश्वस्त हो सकते हैं की मती,  अर्थात पेरित मति वास्तव में मत्ती रचित सुसमाचार का लेखक है। यद्यपि कुछ विद्वान इस पर संदेह व्यक्त करते हैं। एक बात हम जानते हैं कि प्राचीनकाल कलीसियाई पैतुक  बहुत संदेह  वादी थे बल्कि इस पर अपनी राय कम ही व्यक्त करते थे कि धोखाधड़ी से किए गए कार्य को धर्म वैधानिक कार्य परमेश्वर के प्रेरणा स्रोत से लिखे गए वचन के रूप में मान्यता देने से बिल्कुल इनकार करते थे। दूसरी बात यह है कि मती का मत्ती रचित सुसमाचार के लेखक होने के विषय में कोई दूसरी परंपरा भी नहीं है। केवल एक ही आधिकारिक परंपरा यह है कि मति ही ने इस पुस्तक को लिखा है। तीसरी बात यदि आरंभिक कलीसिया किसी अन्य व्यक्ति का नाम , ऐतिहासिक तथ्यों को छोड़कर किसी अन्य कारणों से केवल नाम के लिए या किसी प्रेरित को इस पुस्तक से जोड़ते तो उन्होंने मती के नाम का चुनाव करके बड़ा ही गलत निर्णय लिया। इसका कारण यह है कि मत्ती एक चुंगी लेने वाला था। उसके व्यवसाय से यहूदी अत्यंत नफरत करते थे और मति का सुसमाचार ऐसा सुसमाचार है जो यहूदियों को यह बताने के लिए लिखा गया था कि  यीशु ही मसीह है तो ऐसी स्थिति में क्या वे मती को इस सुसमाचार का लेखक मानते इसका कोई अर्थ दिखाई नहीं देता। यदि फिर भी व्यक्ति का नाम सुसमाचार से जोड़ते हैं तो इसका अर्थ यह है कि उनके पास कोई ना कोई ठोस प्रमाण तो होगा ही जो यह प्रमाणित करें कि मत्ती ही ने इस सुसमाचार को लिखा था।\r\nपरंपरागत दृष्टिकोण कि मती ही ने पहले सुसमाचार को लिखा है या कलीसिया की आरंभिक सदियों से आता है। शीर्षक के साथ पाए जाने वाले इस सुसमाचार के सभी हस्त लेखों में मती और केवल मत्ती को लेखक के रूप में दिखाया गया है। हमारे पास ऐसा कोई प्रमाण नहीं है कि यह सुसमाचार कभी भी  मती के नाम के बिना कलीसिया में प्रसारित किया गया हो। सबसे पहले यह हियरापोलिस के पापियास ने इस पुस्तक के लेखक का श्रेय मति को दिया था। पापियास का जीवनकाल पहली सदी के अंत से लेकर दूसरी सदी तक था। वह कलीसिया के आरंभिक सालों के दृष्टिकोण का प्रतिनिधित्व करता है। जिन के विषय में हमारे पास जानकारी उपलब्ध है। कलीसिया के इतिहासकार केसरिया के यूसेबियस  जिसने 325 ईसवी में लेखन कार्य किया ने अपनी पुस्तक ऐकलेसिआ आरटीकल हिस्ट्री पुस्तक 3,39 खंड 16 में मत्ती रचित सुसमाचार के लेखक के विषय में पापियास की गवाही को दर्शाया।', 8, '2020-08-23 13:36:33', '2020-09-08 00:32:24', NULL),
(1815, 523, 723, 'Ans. :-  परिचय -  मसीह राजा :-  मत्ती रचित सुसमाचार का परिचय हमें मसीहा राजा के रूप में यीशु का परिचय देता है और यह दो भागों में विभाजित है : (1)वंशावली व (2) यीशु के जन्म की कहानी। \r\n1. वंशावली :- वंशावली मती 1:1- 17 में पाई जाती है तकनीकी रूप से पहला पद वास्तव में एक परिचय या शीर्षक है जिसमें मत्ती ने अपनी मुख्य बात को बताया है अर्थात यह कि यीशु इसराइल का मसीहा राजा है। मति 1:1 में ऐसा लिखा है: इब्राहिम की संतान दाऊद की संतान यीशु मसीह की वंशावली (मति 1:1 ) आरंभ से ही ने इस्राइल के राजा दाऊद और यहूदी लोगों के पिता अब्राहम पर विशेष बल दिया है। \r\n         इस आरंभिक कथन के बाद दूसरे पक्ष से ही वंशवाली आरंभ होती है । मति 1:17 के अनुसार वंशावली तीन खंडों में विभाजित की गई है। प्रत्येक खंड में 14 वंश है पहला खंड अब्राहम के साथ परमेश्वर की वाचा से आरंभ होता है। जिसमें अब्राहम के साथ यह वाचा बांधी गई कि उसके वंश संसार पर राज्य करेंगे । दूसरा खंड राजा दाऊद के साथ और दाऊद के राज्य को सर्वदा तक स्थापित करने के द्वारा अब्राहम से की गई परमेश्वर की वाचा को पूरा करने की प्रतिज्ञा के साथ आरंभ होता है । दूसरा खंड परमेश्वर के लोगों के अपने पाप के कारण तथा वाचा तोड़ने के कारण प्रतिज्ञा की भूमि से बंधुवाई में चले जाने के साथ समाप्त होता है । \r\n         वंशावली के तीसरे खंड में बंधुवाई से यीशु के जन्म का वर्णन पाया जाता है। इस्राइल ने परमेश्वर की वाचा को तोड़ा और इस वाचा के स्रापो  के अधीन हो गए । परंतु परमेश्वर फिर भी इस्राएल को अब्राहम और दाऊद से की गई वाचाओ को पूरा करने के द्वारा आशीष देना चाहता था । इसराइल के पूर्व काल के राजाओं ने इन वचनों का पालन नहीं किया था । परंतु अब इसराइल का अंतिम राजा जो  इस्राएल के भविष्य को निर्धारित करेगा , अंततः आ गया था। \r\n                   यीशु के पूर्वजों की सूची मती 1:16 में समाप्त होती है, जहां हम इस प्रकार पढ़ते हैं : \r\n     और याकुब से युसुफ  उत्पन्न हुआ ,जो मरियम का पति था जिस से यीशु जो मसीह कहलाता है ,उत्पन्न हुआ । (मती 1:16) \r\n   इस प्रकार मत्ती ने यह प्रमाणित कर दिया कि यीशु के पास अपने पिता यूसुफ के द्वारा दाऊद के सिहासन का वैधानिक अधिकार था।\r\n       भविस्यवाणी के प्रकाशन के अनुसार मसीह को दाऊद के वंश का होना चाहिए क्योंकि ऐसी ही भविष्यवाणी की गई थी। और इसकी पृष्ठभूमि उत्पत्ति के पुस्तक में पाई जाती है । जहां पर यहूदा के गलील  के लिए भविष्यवाणी की गई थी कि उसमें से राजा निकलेगा वहां भविष्यवाणी दाऊद पर पूरी होती है।राजा दाऊद जो अपने आप में इस्राएल का एक महानतम राजा था। उसके बाद जितने भी राजा आए उनकी तुलना राजा दाऊद के अनुकूल या प्रतिकूल से ही की जाती रही है । फिर हम जानते हैं कि दाऊद के साथ तो आजा बांधी गई थी जब नातान नबी से दाऊद ने परमेश्वर के लिए मंदिर बनाने की इच्छा जताई  तो नातान ने वापस आकर कहा तू यहोवा के लिए घर नहीं बनाएगा , \"यहोवा तेरे लिए घर बनाएगा\" यहां घर का तात्पर्य उसके वंश से है। यहां 2 शामुऐल 7 में पाया जाता है और भविष्यवाणी कि यहोवा उसके लिए एक घर बनाएगा उसका राज्य सर्वदा स्थिर रहेगा , कि यहोवा उसका वंश सर्वदा दाऊद के सिहासन पर राज करेगा , मसीह की भविष्यवाणी की  नीव ठहरी जो कालांतर में पूरी हुई । और जब भविषवक्ताओं ने दाऊद के वंश और उसके राज्य के विघटन की ओर इशारा किया और इस आशा की ओर आगे देखा कि परमेश्वर दाऊद के राज्य की महिमा को पुनर्स्थापित करेगा , तो दाउद के वंश से ही परमेश्वर एक राजा को खड़ा करेगा । इसलिए राजा, अर्थात मसीहा को दाऊद के वंश से ही आना था । \r\n2. यीशु के जन्म का विवरण :-   यीशु के जन्म की कहानी मती 1:18-2:23 में पाई जाती है । यह एक संक्षिप्त भाग है, इसमें केवल 31 पद है जबकि लुका रचित सुसमाचार के इस अनुभाग में 116 पद पाए जाते हैं । इस इस अनुभाग में मती का उद्देश्य सीमित था सभी पांचों अनुच्छेदों की रचना एक महत्वपूर्ण विषय पर ध्यान देने के लिए की गई थी । अर्थात मसीहा का जन्म हो चुका है प्रत्येक अनुच्छेद एक संक्षिप्त कहानी बताता है, और फिर इसे स्पष्ट करता है कि वह कहानी किस प्रकार मसीहा के लिए पुराने नियम की भविष्यवाणी को पूरा करती है । \r\n               यीशु के जन्म के विवरण के बारे में सबसे रुचिकर बात हम यह सीखते हैं कि उसका कोई मानवीय पिता नहीं था । बल्कि ,परमेश्वर उसका पिता था । पवित्रआत्मा के द्वारा मरियम गर्भवती हुई जबकि वह कुमारी ही थी । \r\nमसीहयत के कुछ आलोचकों का मानना है कि यह यीशु की वंशावली की कमजोरी है , क्योंकि वह शारीरिक रूप से यूसुफ के वंश का नहीं था, जिसके द्वारा उसने दाऊद के सिहासन का उत्तराधिकारी होने का दावा किया था । परंतु यह तो स्वीकृत परंपरा है कि बाइबल की वंशावली जैसे 1 इतिहास 1 से 9 में वर्णित है ,गोद लिए गए संतानों की वंशावली भी गोद लेने वाले माता-पिता की वंशावली से जोड़ी जाती है।       इससे बढ़कर, यीशु परमेश्वर का पुत्र था, वह संपूर्णत: ईशवरिय था । इसका अर्थ था कि वह परमेश्वर की वाचा का शुद्ध रुप से पालन कर सकता था । केवल मानवी राजाओं ने ही परमेश्वर की वाचा का शुद्ध रुप से पालन नहीं किया । इसलिए उन्होंने कभी भी परमेश्वर की वाचा कि आशीष जिसकी प्रतिज्ञा अब्राहम तथा दाऊद से की गई थी का भरपूर आनंद नहीं उठाया । अत: परमेश्वर ने अपने सिद पुत्र को राजा होने के लिए भेजा ताकि उसकी वाचा शुद्ध रूप से पूरी की जा सके और उसकी आशीष की प्रतिज्ञाएँ पूरी हो सके । \r\n                  यह स्पष्ट है कि मसीहा मनुष्य के रूप में दाऊद के वंश से ही आता है । इस संबंध में कई महत्वपूर्ण सच्चाई है । इस बात का अनुभव करना भी महत्वपूर्ण है कि मसीहा परमेश्वर अर्थात ईश्वरीय भी है। ऐसा क्यों है ?ऐसा इस कारण से है कि मनुष्य होने के नाते हमारी समस्या परमेश्वर के सामने यह है कि हमने उसके विरुद्ध पाप किया है । उसे इसका उत्तर प्रदान करना है । उसी को ही इस समस्या का समाधान प्रदान करना है । पाप क्षमा की समस्या जिसके बारे में हम कभी कभी बात करते हैं परमेश्वर उसको ऐसे ही अनदेखा नहीं करता है । यह ऐसा नहीं है जिसके बारे में वह कहे \"मैं देख लूंगा\" या \"तुम अपना सर्वश्रेष्ठ प्रदर्शन करो ।\" परमेश्वर पवित्र परमेश्वर है । परमेश्वर धर्मी और न्यायी है । वह हमारे पापों को ऐसे ही अनदेखा नहीं करेगा । ऐसा करना तो मानो उसका अपने अस्तित्व से इनकार करना है इसलिए हमें क्षमा प्रदान करने के लिए उसी को ही प्रारंभ करना है । उसकी अपनी धार्मिक मांग की परिपूर्णता के लिए उसको ही समाधान उपलब्ध कराना है । स्वयं परमेश्वर को यह करना है । जब आप पुराना नियम पढ़ते हैं तो यह बार-बार आपके सम्मुख आता है आप योना 2:2 के बारे में सोचते हैं ,\"उद्धार यहोवा का है।\" यह परमेश्वर को उपलब्ध कराना है । परमेश्वर को ही यह साधन उपलब्ध कराना है।परमेश्वर ही है जो हमें क्षमा प्रदान करेगा । इसलिए यदि मसीहा के द्वारा उद्धार है तो उसी को ही मनुष्य बन कर हमारा प्रतिनिधित्व करना है । इसके साथ-साथ उसको प्रभु भी होना है। प्रभु जो आने वाला है । प्रभु जो  उद्धार देता है । प्रभु जो अपनी पवित्रता और धार्मिकता को पूरा करता है। और इसलिए मसीहा को ईश्वरीय होना आवश्यक है। \r\n                       मती ने अपने सुसमाचार के परिचय में यीशु को मसीहा राजा के रूप में प्रस्तुत किया है। अर्थात दाऊद का राजकीय  पुत्र जिसने उन सब आशीषों को प्राप्त किया जिसकी प्रतिज्ञा परमेश्वर ने अब्राहम तथा इसराइल के लोगों से की थी । इस प्रकार मत्ते ने उस अद्भुत शुभ संदेश के लिए मंच तैयार किया जो उसकी शेष पुस्तक का विषय है ।आमीन।', 9, '2020-08-23 13:38:59', '2020-09-08 00:32:24', NULL),
(1816, 523, 724, 'Ans.  चिन्ह और दृष्टांत :- मती के सुसमाचार का तीसरा प्रमुख खंड चिन्हों और दृष्टांतों के द्वारा राजा और उसके राज्य के प्रदर्शन को जारी रखता है, जो मती 11: 2-13 :53 में पाया जाता है । \r\nचिन्ह और प्रतिक्रियाएं :-- मती का कहानी खंड, यीशु द्वारा दिखाए गए चिन्हों और उन चिन्हों के प्रति प्रतिक्रियाओं पर केंद्रित है जो मती 11 :2--12:50 में पाया जाता है इन चिन्हों ने दर्शाया कि राजा और उसका राज्य वर्तमान में है और इस संबंध में जो झूठी शिक्षा प्रचलित थी, उसे सुधारा फल स्वरुप ,जो आलोचना पहले से ही आरंभ हो चुकी थी ,वह बढ़ने और फैलने लगी। \r\n                चिन्हों एवं दृष्टांतों की श्रंखला पांच मुख्य भागों में विभाजित है मति 11:2-19 में यीशु ने यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा देने वाले को आश्वासन दिया कि यीशु के चिन्ह यह प्रमाणित करते हैं कि वही मसीहा है जिसने पुराने नियम की भविष्यवाणियों को पूरा किया है, और फिर यीशु ने भीड़ को बुलाया कि वह उसके चिन्हों का प्रत्युत्तर अपने अपने पापों से पश्चाताप करके दे। मती 11:20--30 में यीशु ने उन शहरों को संबोधित किया जहां उसने चिन्ह दिखाए थे और उसने  अपश्चातापी सभी लोगों को चेतावनी दी और उनको विश्राम देने का प्रस्ताव दिया जो उसके पास आएंगे जैसे कि वह मत्ती 11:30 में कहता है : क्योंकि मेरा जुआ सहज और मेरा बोझ हल्का है ।\r\n               मत्ती 12:1--21 में मती नें ऐसे कई वृतांतो को आरंभ किया जो यीशु के चिन्हों के प्रति फरीसीयो की प्रतिक्रियाओं पर केंद्रित थे। सबसे पहले, उसने बताया कि किस प्रकार यीशु ने  सब्त के लिए परमेश्वर के उद्देश्य के विषय पर फरीसीयो से वाद-विवाद किया और एक व्यक्ति को सब्त के दिन चंगा कर के सब्त के ऊपर अपने अधिकार को प्रमाणित किया। यीशु ने सिखाया कि सब्त का दिन चंगाई और जीवन को बचाने के लिए है। \r\n             मती 12:22 -37 में फरीसीयो ने यीशु पर बालजबूल की शक्ति का प्रयोग करने का आरोप लगाया, हालांकि  भीड़ यीशु के आश्चर्यकर्मों को देखकर अचंभित हो गई थी । उसे मसीहा के रूप में स्वीकार करने की अपेक्षा व्यवस्था के शिक्षकों ने यह माना कि वह तो दुष्टआत्मा से ग्रसित है ।           \r\n                 मती 12:49 से 50 में फरीसीयो ने अपने पाखंड में यीशु से दूसरा चिन्ह  मांगा, परन्तु यीशु ने उन्हे कहा कि योना के चिन्ह को छोड़कर उन्हें कोई दूसरा चिन्ह नहीं दिया जाएगा । और यह चिन्ह क्या था ? जिस प्रकार योना तीन दिन पश्चात मछली के पेट से निकलने के कारण निनवे के लोगों ने मन फिराया, उसी प्रकार तीन दिन पश्चात कब्र में से यीशु का भावी पुण्य स्थान भी अन्यजाति के अनेक लोगों को मनफिराव  की ओर प्रेरित करेगा। \r\n       यह दिखाने के लिए कि कोई भी जाती,  कुल, भाषा के लोग ,जो पश्चाताप करेंगे ,परमेश्वर उनको स्वीकार करेगा, उसने यहां तक कह दिया कि उसकी शारीरिक यहूदी माता और भाई भी उसके परिवार के लोग नहीं हैं । इसके विषय में उसने मत्ती 12 : 49-50 में यह कहा : देखो, मेरी माता और मेरे भाई यह हैं। क्योंकि जो कोई मेरे स्वर्गीय पिता की इच्छा पर चलें, वही मेरा भाई और बहन और माता है । \r\n            यहां पर हम यीशु द्वारा दिखाए गए चिन्हों के मती के वर्णन को देख चुके हैं ,इसलिए आइए अब हम मत्ती 13:1-53 में यीशु के राज्य के दृष्टांतों के उसके उपदेशो की ओर मुड़े । \r\nराज्य के दृष्टांत :-- मती ने यीशु के जाने - पहचाने दृष्टांतों को पांच भागों में विभाजित किया है । \r\n(१)  मति 13:1-23 में बीज बोने वाले का दृष्टांत। \r\n(2) मती 13:24-30 में जंगली बीज का दृष्टांत । \r\n(3) मती 13:31-43 में राई का दाना और खमीर। \r\n(4)  मती 13:44-46 में छुपा हुआ धन और मोती। \r\n(5)  मती 13:47-53 में जाल का दृष्टांत । ये दृष्टांत परमेश्वर के राज्य के विषय में फैली गलत धारणाओं को दूर करने के लिए कह गए थे। \r\n        कुछ दृष्टांतों, जैसे कि 13: 31 से 32 में राई के दाने के, 33 में खमीर के, 44 में धन के और 45 - 46 में मोती के दृष्टांत में यीशु ने यह शिक्षा दी कि स्वर्ग का राज्य अत्यंत बहुमूल्य है इसलिए इसे किसी भी कीमत पर प्राप्त कर लेना चाहिए । एक बार शायद यह महत्वहीन लगे परन्तु एक दिन वह (यीशु) अपनी संपूर्ण महिमा में प्रकट होगा । \r\nपरन्तु यीशु ने अन्य दृष्टांत भी कहे जिनमें राजा यीशु और उसके राज्य को स्वीकार करने में इसराइल की असफलता को दिखाया गया है । मत्ती 13:1-23 में बीज बोने वाले के दृष्टांत और उसके विवरण में यीशु ने स्पष्ट किया कि विश्वास में कई बाधाएं हैं और अधिकांश लोग राज्य का तिरस्कार कर देंगे । \r\n          इस विचार पर 24 से 30 और 36 से 43 में जंगली बीज के दाने के दृष्टांत और 47 -51 में जाल के दृष्टांत में और अधिक बल दिया गया है । यीशु ने सिखाया कि बहुत से लोग परमेश्वर के राज्य को अपनाने से इनकार करेंगे और अंत में उनका नाश हो जाएगा । ये सभी दृष्टांत यीशु के विरोधियों के लिए स्पष्ट चेतावनी थे, इन दृष्टांतों ने तो अविशवासियो को पश्चाताप करने का और एक सच्चे राजा के विश्वासयोग्य अनुयायी बनने का अवसर प्रदान किया। \r\n           मसीहा आ गया है। उसने भविष्यवाणियों को पूरा किया है उसने अपने राज्य को स्थापित किया है। फिर भी इसकी पूर्णता अभी बाकी है। हम मसीही जब उस राज्य में प्रवेश करते हैं तो हमें अपनी प्राथमिकता को निरंतर रखने की आवश्यकता है। यदि हमने जैसा उसका अनुकरण करना चाहिए था वैसा अनुकरण नहीं किया तो पश्चाताप करने की आवश्यकता है, इस तथ्य को निश्चित करते हुए कि हम अपने जीवन को उसकी इच्छा अनुसार जीते हैं उसकी नैतिकता के साथ सहमति प्रकट करते हैं जिससे राज्य संबंधित है इसलिए निरंतर पश्चाताप,अंगीकार करने की आवश्यकता है उसके सम्मुख एक भविष्यवक्ता एक याजक और एक राजा के रूप आने की आवश्यकता है, जिसका हम आदर्श मानकर अनुकरण करना चाहते हैं और उसकी सेवा ऐसे करें कि उसके उद्देश्य को अपने जीवन के द्वारा इस संसार में पूरा करें । \r\n‌     हमें मसीहीयो को परमेश्वर के राज्य का अनुकरण करने और उसकी इच्छा पूरी करने के लिए प्रोत्साहित करने की आवश्यकता है। पहला, अपने व्यक्तिगत में स्वर्ग के राज्य का अधिकार हमारे जीवन की सामर्थ है। यह हमें अपने आपको परमेश्वर के हाथों में समर्पित करने के लिए प्रोत्साहित करता है कि हम परमेश्वर पर केंद्रित जीवन जीए ताकि परमेश्वर का अधिकार जो हमारे जीवन में प्रकट होता है हमारे आत्मिक जीवन का ध्येय बन जाए । दूसरा, हमें स्वर्ग के राज्य को उद्वार के इतिहास  के दृष्टिकोण से भी देखने की आवश्यकता है। जब हम यह जानने लगते हैं तो यह उसके उद्वार की योजना को खोलता और पूरा करता है। तब हम यह भी देखेंगे कि स्वर्ग के राज्य की शिक्षा पुराने और नए नियम को एक सूत्र में बांधती है। वह हमें हमारे छुड़ाने वाले परमेश्वर के उद्वार की महान योजना से परिचित कराता है और तब हम उसके गहन उद्देश्य को समझ पाते हैं। तीसरा, स्वर्ग का राज्य बाइबल के उचित दृष्टिकोण का निर्माण करता है और हमें इस बात को समझने में सहायता करता है कि सभी चीजें उसी की है । उसके राज्य की पूर्णता होगी और वह इस धरती पर की सभी बुरी शक्तियों का न्याय करेगा और उनको धरती पर मिटा डालेगा क्योंकि परमेश्वर स्वयं सर्वाधिकार राजा होगा। इसलिए अब हम केवल अपने लिए ही नहीं जीते हैं हमें अपने पड़ोसियों, समाज और इस संसार की खुशहाली के लिए चिंता करने की आवश्यकता है। हमारे चारों ओर की घटनाओं, चाहे वे पास हो या दूर, की खबर रखने की आवश्यकता है। हमें हमारे कर्तव्य के रूप में समाज में प्रवेश करना है और वहां सभी बुरी बातों को बदलना है। आमीन', 9, '2020-08-23 13:42:42', '2020-09-08 00:32:24', NULL),
(1817, 523, 725, 'Ans : यीशु ने इस प्रश्न का उत्तर निर्देश उदाहरण और दृष्टांत को मिलाकर चार मुख्य खंडों में दिया पहला मस्ती 18:2-4 में यीशु ने अपने चेलों को छोटे बच्चों के सामान नम्र जीवन जीने के लिए प्रेरित किया उसके विरोधियों के विरोध के मध्य यीशु ने अपने शिष्यों को सिखाया कि उन्हें स्वर्ग के राज्य में परमेश्वर की संतानों के सामान कैसा जीवन जीना चाहिए। उसे मालूम था कि राज्य की भावी पूर्णता का समय अभी नहीं आया था । और वह जानता था कि शत्रु और पाप के विरुद्ध संघर्ष परमेश्वर के बच्चों के जीवन का हिस्सा होगा। और 5:14 पदों में उसने सिखाया कि जिस प्रकार स्वर्गीय पिता को अपनी खोई हुई पेड़ की चिंता रहती है ठीक उसी प्रकार वे भी कमजोरों की चिंता किया करें । मती 18:10,14 में यीशु के कथनो को सुनें : देखो तुम इन छोटो में से किसी को तुच्छ न  जानना ऐसे ही तुम्हारे पिता की जो स्वर्ग में है यह इछा नहीं, कि इन फोटो में से एक भी नाश हो । \r\nयीशु ने मती 18:15-20में इस विचारधारा को विकसित किया जहां पर उस ने मांग की कि उसके अनुयायी तब भी एक दूसरे के साथ परमेश्वर के सदस्यों के रूप में व्यवहार करें जब पाप उनके पारिवारिक संबंध में परेशानी उत्पन्न करें उसने मति 18:21-35 में कहा कि जैसे उनके स्वर्गीय पिता ने उन्हें क्षमा किया है वैसे वे भी पाप करने वाले भाई को क्षमा करें । परमेश्वर की महिमा हमारे दिनों में भी बढ़ रही है क्योंकि परमेश्वर निरंतर सामर्थ के कार्य कर रहा है और पृथ्वी पर अपने राज्य को बढ़ा रहा है परंतु जैसे यीशु के दिनों में होता था वैसे ही उसके राज्य का विरोध भी बढ़ता जा रहा है परमेश्वर का धन्यवाद हो कि वह हमें बहुत से वरदान देकर हमारी कठिनाइयों और परीक्षाओं में हमारी सहायता करता है इन वरदानों में धीरज और शांति है और इसके साथ परमेश्वर की उपस्थिति भी इनमें सबसे महत्वपूर्ण वरदान तो परमेश्वर के साथ पिता के रूप में हमारा संबंध है परमेश्वर हमारा ध्यान रखता है और हमारी सुरक्षा करता है वह हमारी कमजोरीयो में हमें समझाता और अपनी सहानुभूति प्रकट करता है और वहां मनुष्यों का ऐसा परिवार प्रदान करता है जो हमारी सेवा करते हैं और वह हमें प्रेम करते हैं अर्थात कलीसिया जो परमेश्वर के परिवार में हमारे भाई बहन हैं। \r\nवर्तमान विरोध तथा भविष्य में विजय :-- मती के सुसमाचार के पांचवे मुख्य खंड का शीर्षक स्वर्ग के राज्य का वर्तमान विरोध तथा इसकी भावी विजय है यह वर्णन मती 19 :1-22:46 में पाया जाता है और दर्शाता है कि यीशु ने अपने जीवन के इस समय में बड़े-बड़े विरोधो का सामना कैसे किया। \r\nप्रचंड विरोध :-- ये अध्याय यीशु के आगे बढ़ने के आधार पर तीन भागों में बढ़ते हैं । 19:1-20:16 मैं यीशु को यहोदिया में विरोध का सामना करना पड़ा वहां उसने फरीसीयों का और तलाक संबंधी प्रश्न का सामना किया । उसने उस विरोध का भी सामना किया जो धन तथा सामर्थ के संबंध में गलतफहमीयो के कारण उठा । \r\n       सुसमाचार के प्रारंभिक अध्याय में मती  ने यीशु और यहूदी अगुवो के मध्य दूरी या तनाव का वर्णन किया है । इस खंड में उसने यह लिखा है कि दोनों के मध्य अब शत्रुता विकसित हो गई थी । उदाहरण के तौर पर फरीसियो ने  यीशु से ऐसे प्रश्न पूछना आरंभ किया कि यीशु को फसा सके जैसे की मती 19:3-9, 21:16,23 और 22:15-40 मे। एक उदाहरण के तौर पर मती 22:15 मे मती के वर्णन को सुनिए : तब फरीसियो ने जाकर आपस में विचार किया कि उसको किस प्रकार बातों में फंसाए । \r\n      इसके साथ-साथ यीशु ने भी कभी-कभी यहूदी अगुवो को चुनौती दी इसे हम मत्ती 21:28-22:15 में दो पुत्रों और दुष्ट किसानों और विवाह भोज के दृष्टांत में पाते हैं । परंतु झगड़ा सदैव शब्दों तक ही सीमित नहीं था। कभी-कभी तो यह सीधा तथा अधिक भयंकर होता था जैसा कि मत्ती 21:12-16 में यीशु ने मंदिर में लेनदेन करने वालों के मेज तक पलट दिए थे और उसने उन्हें मंदिर से बाहर भगा दिया था। विशेषकर मती 23:13-35 में हाय के उसके सात श्रापों के शब्द बहुत चुभने वाले थे। सुनिए मत्ती में यीशु ने उन्हें कैसे डांटा : हे  कपटी शास्त्रियों और फरीसियो तुम पर हाय तुम एक जन को अपने मत में लाने के लिए सारे जल और थल में फिरते हो और जब वह मत में आ जाता है तो उसे अपने से दुगुना नरकीय बना देते हो । \r\n         निसंदेह इन अध्यायों के चरित्र केवल यीशु और यहूदी अगुवे ही नहीं है । यहूदी अगुवो की शत्रुता उस समय और अधिक बढ़ गई जब भीड़ ने मती 21:1-11 में यीशु को विजय प्रवेश जैसे अवसरों पर आदर और सम्मान दिया । इस पूरे खंड में यीशु ने अपने शिष्यों को इस विरोध को दृष्टिकोण में बदलने को उत्साहित किया मती 19:27-30 में यीशु ने उन्हें आश्वासन दिया कि एक दिन वह भी उसकी महिमा में उसके साथ बैठेंगे उसने उन्हें यह चेतावनी भी दी कि महिमा के वे दिन दुःख उठाने वाली उसकी मृत्यु के बाद ही आएंगे। (20:17-19) इससे बढ़कर यीशु ने यह भी कहा कि उसके शिष्य दुःख उठाने के जीवन के बाद ही उस महिमा तक पहुंचेंगे। यीशु ने कहा :परंतु बहुतेरे जो पहले हैं पिछले होंगे और जो पिछले हैं पहले होंगे तब उसने मत्ती में कहा इसी रीती से जो पिछले हैं वह पहले होंगे और जो पहले हैं वे पिछले होंगे फिर उसने इसको मती 20:26-28 में यह कहते हुए इसे दोहराया जो कोई तुम्हें बड़ा होना चाहे वह तुम्हारा सेवक बने और जो तुम में प्रधान होना चाहे वह तुम्हारा दास बने जैसे कि मनुष्य का पुत्र इसलिए नहीं आया कि उसकी सेवा टहल की जाए परंतु इसलिए आया कि आप सेवा टहल करें और बहुतों की चुनौती के लिए अपने प्राण दे । यीशु का राज्य विचित्र लगता था उसके अनुयाई दुख उठाएंगे और इस्राएल का राजा स्वयं इस्राइली लोगों के द्वारा मारा जाएगा विजय से पहले अप्रत्याशित हार होगी। प्रचंड विरोध का अगला खंड 20:17-34 में यीशु के यरूशलेम की ओर जाने में है इसलिए स्पष्ट कर दिया था कि वह वहां दुख सहने और मरने जा रहा था उसे केवल 2 चेलों की माता का विरोध सहना पड़ा जो अपने बच्चों के लिए राज्य में अधिकार चाहती थी। तब एक बड़ी भीड़ ने एक दूसरे में यीशु का स्वागत किया जब उसने पुराने नियम की विजय प्रवेश की भविष्यवाणी को पूरा किया अगले भाग 21:12-22:46 में यीशु को विरोध का सामना करना पड़ा जब वह यरुशलेम और मंदिर में आ जा रहा था उसने लेन देन करने वालों को बाहर निकाला उसने परमेश्वर के आने वाले न्याय के संबंध में दृष्टांत कहा इस और धर्मगुरुओं के मध्य केसर को चुंगी देने, मृतकों का पुनरूत्थान, सबसे बड़ी आज्ञा और मसीहा किसका पुत्र है आदि विषयों पर विवाद हुआ। परंतु यीशु ने अपने विरोधियों को इस तरह से सामना किया जैसा कि हम मत्ती 22:46 में पढ़ते हैं उसके उत्तर में कोई भी एक बात ना कह सका परंतु उस दिन से किसी को फिर उससे कुछ पूछने का हियाव ना हुआ। स्वर्ग के राज्य के प्रचंड विरोध पर आधारित मती के वर्णन का अध्ययन करने के बाद अब हमें उन उद्देश्यों की ओर मुड़ना चाहिए जो उसके साथ पाए जाते हैं।', 9, '2020-08-23 13:47:38', '2020-09-08 00:32:24', NULL),
(1818, 523, 726, 'Ans :-- हमें इस बात की परवाह इसलिए करनी चाहिए क्योंकि पुराने नियम ने यीशु की मसीहा रूपी भविस्यवानी का जिक्र  है जो हमारे लिए बहुत महत्वपूर्ण है। जिसे मत्ती का सुसमाचार पुराने नियम की भविस्यवानी को लेकर प्रगट करता है।\r\n     पुराने नियम की धरोहर :--  मत्ती का सुसमाचार वास्तव इस बात का बहुत ही रोमांचक विवरण है कि यह कितना महत्वपूर्ण है कि पुराने नियम ने यीशु मसीह के आगमन की अपेक्षा की थी। यीशु प्रकट होता है और वह देहधारी इसराइल है । वह मिश्र जाता है वह मरुस्थल में लेकर जाया जाता है जहां उसकी परीक्षा होती है वह पहाड़ों पर चला जाता है और पुनः लोगों को व्यवस्था की शिक्षा देता है नए मूसा या देहधारी इसराइल की यह सारी तस्वीरें पुराने नियम में अपने स्रोत और प्रतिक्रिया में पाते है क्योंकि जब इसराइल बुलाया गया, जब इस्राएल परमेश्वर के द्वारा चुना गया, उसका चुनाव केवल आनंद लेने का सौभाग्य ही नहीं था । यह बुलाहट जिम्मेदारी निभाने के लिए थी, उन्हें राष्ट्रों के लिए आशीष बनना था। परंतु इसराइल के लंबे और पाप से भरे इतिहास होने के कारण वह ना तो कभी अपने लिए आशीष बन पाया और ना ही कभी उन राष्ट्रों के लिए जिनके लिए उन्हें बुलाया गया था । अतः यहां यीशु परमेश्वर के पुत्र और देहधारी इस्राएल के रूप में है, जो प्रकट होता है और वह उस कार्य को करता है जो इस्रायल ना तो कभी अपने लिए कर सका और ना ही राष्ट्रों के लिए और मैं सोचता हूं कि यह हमें इस बात को और भी गहराई से बताता है कि पुराना नियम किस प्रकार यीशु की अपेक्षा कर रहा था, बल्कि इससे कि हम उसे किसी पद में इधर-उधर ढूंढे । यही इसराइल का संपूर्ण इतिहास है। यही इसराइल का चुनाव है। यही इस्राएल की असफलता है जिसने यीशु के आने की अपेक्षा की थी और मत्ती इसी को लेता है और पहले पांच या छ: अध्याय में इसका वर्णन करता है।\r\n               सबसे बढ़कर, बाइबल की कहानी उस परमेश्वर के विषय में है जिसने अपने आपको अपने लोगों के साथ प्रेम के ना टूटने वाले बंधन से बांध दिया। यह उसकी विश्वासयोग्यता की कहानी है जिसमें उसने आशीष की अपनी प्रतिज्ञा को लोगों के साथ बनाए रखा। इसलिए मत्ती ने अपने पीढ़ी के लोगों को बताया कि वह कभी भी पुरानी प्रतिज्ञाओं पर भरोसा कर सकते हैं और इस पर विश्वास कर सकते हैं कि परमेश्वर अभी भी उनके दिनों में यीशु के व्यक्तित्व में कार्य कर रहा है। इसलिए मत्ती बड़े साहस के साथ मसीहा राजा, यीशु मसीह के दावों और सेवकाई  का समर्थन करने के लिए पुराने नियम पर निरंतर आश्रित रहा । \r\n               हम संक्षिप्त रूप से  उन पांच रूपों का सर्वेक्षण करेंगे जिसमें मत्ती यीशु के राज्य और सुसमाचार की पुराने नियम की धरोहर को दर्शाता है: मत्ती के पुराने नियम के उल्लेख और संकेत, स्वर्ग के राज्य पर उसका बल, मसीहा राजा के रूप में उसका विवरण, अविश्वासी यहूदी अगुवो के साथ यीशु का संघर्ष, और यीशु की दीनता और नम्रता। आइए हम मत्ती के पुराने नियमों के उल्लेख के साथ आरंभ करें। \r\n1 :-- उल्लेख और संकेत :--  मत्ती ने दूसरे सुसमाचार लेखकों की अपेक्षा सबसे अधिक पुराने नियम का उल्लेख किया है। मत्ती ने कितनी बार पुराने नियम से उल्लेख किया है इस बात पर विद्वानों के मध्य विवाद है  परंतु  निश्चित रूप से हम कह सकते हैं कि कम से कम 40 बार उसने पुराने नियम से उल्लेख किया है और कई और भी संकेत उसने अपने लेख में दिए हैं।               एक वाक्यांश जो मती ने जानबूझकर बहुधा प्रयोग किया, वह यह है, \"जो कहा गया था वह पूरा हो।\" मत्ती ने इस वाक्यांश का प्रयोग पुराने नियम और यीशु के जीवन की घटनाओं के मध्य स्पष्ट संबंध स्थापित करने के लिए किया। उदाहरण के लिए, मत्ती ने 8:17 में क्या लिखा : ताकि जो वचन यशायाह भविष्यवक्ता के द्वारा कहा गया था वह पूरा हो, कि उस ने आप हमारी दुर्बलताओं को ले लिया और हमारी बीमारियों को उठा लिया।', 8, '2020-08-23 14:05:07', '2020-09-08 00:32:24', NULL),
(1819, 525, 675, 'The word derives from Greek words related to the verb hermeneuo, which means \'\'interpret\'\' or \'\'explain.\'\' Hermeneutics refers to the interpretation or explanation of some kind of message or communication. \r\nFreiedrich Schleiermarcher [1768-1834] is the father of modern hermeneutics. In 1819 he spoke of the need for \'\'general hermeneutics\'\',a unified theory for understanding all literature. \r\nBiblical hermeneutics is the study of interpreting the meaning and significance of Scripture. Informal approaches to the Bible are of great value, and these lessons will build on what most of us already understand. But we\'ll also move beyond informal hermeneutics and explore the kinds of issues that move to the foreground in academic, scholarly interpretation of the Bible.', 8, '2020-08-27 15:37:36', '2020-09-08 00:32:53', NULL),
(1820, 525, 676, 'The biblical roots of scientific hermeneutics make it a legitimate exercise. People living in biblical times weren\'t modern scientist. But this doesn\'t mean that they were unintelligent or irrational. On the contrary, their sophisticated architectural accomplishments, extensive maritime travel, innovative agricultural programs, and countless other cultural achievements demonstrate that people in biblical days dealt with facts and thought rationally about the world, much like modern scientists do.\r\nFor this reason, Biblical authors interpreted other scriptures with an orientation toward factual and logical analysis [Romans 4.3-5]. As this one example illustrates, time and again biblical authors presented this kind of careful interpretation of scripture. And their approach to Scripture indicates that scientific biblical hermeneutics is firmly rooted in the Scriptures themselves.', 8, '2020-08-27 15:45:57', '2020-09-08 00:32:53', NULL),
(1821, 525, 677, 'Devotional hermeneutics is the Christian tradition of emphasizing our need to draw near to God as we interpret the scriptures. Devotional hermeneutics focuses primarily on the divine authorship of scripture. Christians have acknowledged that the human words of scripture are also word of God. As 2 Timothy 3.16 tells us, the scriptures were inspired by God, or more literally were \'\'God-breathed.\'\' This fact makes biblical hermeneutics distinct from other facets of general hermeneutics because we must interpret the scriptures devotionally, as the living God himself. The biblical authors approached the scriptures devotionally. Followers of Christ are to read the scriptures as the word of God, in the presence of God, in ways that bring about extraordinary even supernatural experiences of God.', 8, '2020-08-27 15:52:58', '2020-09-08 00:32:53', NULL),
(1822, 525, 678, 'There are two important aspects of organic inspiration that helps us orient ourselves to task of interpretation ; first, the fact that the Holy Spirit was the divine source of scripture, and second the fact that he worked through human means to produce scripture. \r\n1] Divine Source- The Holy Spirit has intimate knowledge of the Bible\'s meaning and of the way it communicates that meaning. One of the most important implications of the divine origin of scripture is the Bible\'s unquestionable veracity. \r\n     a] Critical Interpreter - Reject the divine divine inspiration of scripture and elevate their understanding over the spirit\'s authority\r\n     b] Submissive interpreter- affirm the divine inspiration of scripture, expecting and assuming it to be true and harmonious even when they can\'t demonstrate or prove its truthfulness.\r\n2] Human Means- God had the scripture composed by means if human authors. The Scriptures were written by different people, and they reflect the diversity of that human authorship.', 8, '2020-08-27 16:01:50', '2020-09-08 00:32:53', NULL),
(1823, 525, 679, 'Illumination\r\nThe Holy Spirit grants us knowledge of His word. And this knowledge isn\'t purely cognitive.  It also imparts our imagination, intuition, emotion, will, motivation, desire, moral conscience- any part of us that contributes to our understanding of scripture can be illumined by the our understanding of scripture can be illumined by the Spirit. Human beings are so deeply affected by sin that we can\'t understand the things of God on our own. We desperately need God himself- the Holy Spirit- to illumine us. Without the work of the Spirit, we have no hope of grasping the thoughts of God as we should. This is why the Spirit\'s personal illumination is so important to our interpretation of the Scriptures.', 8, '2020-08-27 16:07:48', '2020-09-08 00:32:53', NULL),
(1824, 525, 680, 'By being an exegete of scripture, it gives me a bigger picture and larger story. Once we look it that way, that\'s when it gets interesting. We see shards of truth in the details but nothing can compare to the full mosaic of the Word as we see the progression of scripture. \r\nExegetical study reveals what God is saying rather than what we want Him to say. It gives us the perspective of what God is telling and helps us follow it accordingly. \r\nWe grasp scripture and apply it appropriately. When they think about theology, envision, demanding degrees, multisyllabic mysteries, and complicated theories. \r\nWe understand different genres and styles that God reveals through His Word. The brilliance and  clarity of God\'s story comes alive with dynamism and surprising depth.', 8, '2020-08-27 16:24:53', '2020-09-08 00:32:53', NULL),
(1825, 526, 771, 'Critical interpreters have suggested at least three alternatives. some interpreters have looked for an unknown James in the early church. They say that the person who letter was indeed James , but he wasn\'t the son of Jesus. The simplicity of the author\'s identification at the beginning of the letter indicates that he was well known.\r\nAnother theory that critical interpreters states is that of pseudonymity. it refers to the practice of assigning written books to someone other than the actual author. first they say  that there is no mention of the author\'s relation to Jesus. they say that it\'s unthinkable that a brother of Jesus would write to the churches and not reveal this familial bond when he identified himself. \r\nSecond , some critical scholars assume pseudonymity because the book gives evidence that the author was hellenistic  or Greek, James was from Palestine. \r\nA third argument for pseudonymity points to inconsistencies with the theological portrait of James in the books of Acts and Galatians.\r\n we affirm the traditional outlook that Jesus\' brother James wrote this epistle ,as the writer didn\'t give any credentials beyond saying that he was a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ. And based on this authority, he gave command after command. This open greeting makes a strong sense for Jesus\' brother James because of his status in the early church.\r\nIn the second place , the testimony of the early church confirms this outlook on te authorship of the book. The first epistle of Clement, written aorund A.D 96 and the shepherd of Hermas, written around A. D 140, both refer to or quote from James commentary on the epistle to the Romans.', 9, '2020-08-27 17:53:11', '2020-09-08 00:33:21', NULL),
(1826, 526, 772, 'In James 1:1 James identified his readers as \" the twelve tribes scattered among the nations \".\r\nThis seems to be  a reference to Jews who lived outside of Israel and in 2:1. James addresses his audience as Believers in our glorious Lord Jesus Christ (James 2:1).\r\n Taken together, these verses indicate that James\' original audience was made up primarily of Jewish Christians who lived outside of Palestine.\r\nOn several occasions in his book, James addressed his audience affectionately as \"brothers\".\r\nJames even being in Jerusalem, know his audience well enough to speak to them in  such a way as we read in Acts 8:1-4, in the wave of persecution following Stephen\'s martyrdom , members of the Jerusalem church were scattered throughout Judea and Samaria. So may be James being the leader of the Jerusalem church was writing to the scattered members of the twelve tribes.\r\nThe vocabulary James used also supports the idea that his original leaders were Jewish followers of Jesus. As in James 2:2 James chose the word Synagogue in Hebrew language original script.', 8, '2020-08-27 18:05:58', '2020-09-08 00:33:21', NULL),
(1827, 526, 773, 'Location\r\nBoth the New Testament and early church fathers suggest that James lived his life of ministry in Jerusalem. And he remained in Jerusalem until he was martyred in A. D 62, so there is no reason to think that he wrote the epistle from any other location.\r\nDate\r\nActs 12:17 indicates that James became a significant leader of the Jerusalem church by the time of Peter;s release from prison. According to Acts 12:19-23, Peter was released in the year Herod Agrippa I died in A.D 44. So this letter was not written much before this date. \r\nSecond possible date for the epistle is A. D 62, the year of James martyrdom.\r\nPurpose:\r\nJames 1:2-4 says that  \"considers it pure joy whenever you face trials and James called them to have pure joy in their trials. A we have read that, James audience was scattered abroad , far from their homes , so it wasn\'t easy for them to find joy in their trials far from their homes. This appears to have led some of them to abandon their loyalty to Christ. Instead they were pursuing what James called friendship with the world.  (James 4:4). So he commanded and exerted his authority as a leader of the church.', 8, '2020-08-27 18:23:19', '2020-09-08 00:33:21', NULL),
(1828, 526, 774, 'Old Testament wisdom writings include Job and Ecclesiastes ,as well as the book of Proverbs and number of so- called wisdom Psalms and prophetic wisdom sayings. James used the example of Job , the main character in the boo of Job to promote perseverance. Beyond this James touched on topics such as speech, the treatment of widows and orphans , poverty and favoritism. This topics reflects numerous parallels with  the content of the book of Proverbs .\r\nThe letter of James also reflects the content of influential wisdom books outside of scripture like the wisdom of Sirach, also known simply as Sirach and the wisdom of Solomon , these were well known in James  days and there are striking parallels to both n his letter \r\nSirach 1 :26 and James 1:5\r\n\r\nBecause of Jesus close ties to wisdom literature , then structure of the epistles is quite different.\r\nthe book of James deals with a variety of important themes and it often spends only a few verses on one theme, before moving n go another . \r\noccasionally, it returns to one or more of its themes later in the letter, but not with any consistency. \r\nSome commentators have even concluded that there is no structure to James, they have suggested that its only a collection of wisdom sayings with no real order or flow of thought.', 8, '2020-08-27 18:37:51', '2020-09-08 00:33:21', NULL),
(1829, 526, 775, 'James 1:2 says to consider it pure joy , in midst of trails . and James 1:5 says that pursuit of wisdom makes it possible.The greek word for pure joy \" pasan charan\" may be translated as\" complete, unmigitated joy\".\r\nin James 1:3-4 he taught that perseverance through trials make it possible for believers to be mature and complete. In other words, they grow into the fullness of all that God intend for them. But in reality , its often difficult for even the most sincere believers see how this is true in the midst of suffering. this is why the very next verse James told his readers to pursue wisdom from God.\r\nJames 1:5 says that Those who want yo have pure joy as they suffer trails must ask God for insight . They need wisdom to help them understand how their trails lead to their betterment and if we ask for this kind of wisdom from God, he will give it to us .\r\nin James 1:18 , we spread that , when we receive the wisdom to understand how God works through trials, we can be joyful .Wisdom strengthens our confidence that God has ordained for us the blessing of eternal salvation', 9, '2020-08-27 18:50:48', '2020-09-08 00:33:21', NULL),
(1830, 528, 737, 'उत्तर =  नए नियम की सभी बड़ी पुस्तकों में जटिल उद्देश्य पाए जाते हैं और योहन्ना का सुसमाचार भी कोई अपवाद नहीं है जिस प्रकाश यीशु ने अपनी सेवाएं के दौरान अनेक विषयों को संबोधित किया वैसे ही ईशु किस सेव काहे के यूहन्ना के वर्णन भी कई विषयों को संबोधित करते हैं परंतु फिर भी इन उद्देश्यों का एकीकृत रूप में वर्णन करना संभव है वास्तव में स्वयं यूहन्ना ने हमारे लिए इसके उद्देश्य का सार प्रस्तुत किया है विशेष रूप से उसने कहा कि वह इस साधारण की पुष्टि करना चाहता था कि यीशु मसीह भी है और परमेश्वर का पुत्र भी सुनिए उसने यूहन्ना 20:30-31 मैं क्या लिखा आमतौर पर यूहन्ना ने इसलिए लिखा कि उसके श्रोता यहां विश्वास कर ले कि यीशु मसीह है और परमेश्वर का पुत्र है ताकि वे उस लाभ को प्राप्त करें जो इस समाचार के संदेश पर विश्वास करने से प्राप्त होता है।\r\n सुसमाचार के लिखे जाने के उद्देश्य के विषय में यूहन्ना काफी स्पष्ट है योहन्ना 20 अध्याय का 31 पद में कहता है कि यह बातें इसमें लिखी गई है कि हम जान सके कि यीशु मसीह है और परमेश्वर का पुत्र है ताकि उस पर विश्वास करने से हमें उसमें अनंत जीवन मिले आपको यह उद्देश्य व्दिपीया है जो यहां बताया गया है सबसे पहले यहां उसने सुसमाचार की सुसमाचार प्रचार करने की प्रकृति से संबंधित है स्पष्ट रूप से उसने इसलिए यहां लिखा कि उसके पाठक किसी ना किसी समय जब प्रभु उन्हें पास बुलाए तो वह उसमें अपने विश्वास को क्रियान्वित करें दूसरा यहां चरित्र में विश्वास हंसती है वहां अपने पाठकों को इससे भी आश्वस्त करना चाहता था कि यीशु वास्तव में मनुष्य की देह धारण किया हुआ परमेश्वर है।\r\n यह कह रहा है मैं यह सुसमाचार इसलिए लिख रहा हूं कि तुम यीशु की पहचान को जान लो कि तू परमेश्वर का पुत्र है और वहां स्पष्ट कहता है कि परमेश्वर का पुत्र कौन है वह जो शब्द है जो पिता के साथ था और मनुष्य बना की यीशु प्रतिज्ञा क्या हुआ मसीहा है और यह कोई सहमति जानकारी नहीं है जिससे हम स्वीकार करते हैं परंतु यह कहता है मैं चाहता हूं कि तुम इस पर विश्वास के साथ निर्बलता रखो ताकि तुम्हें वह जीवन मिले जो पिता उसके द्वारा सेट में दे रहा है।\r\n इस पूरे सुसमाचार में यूहन्ना के उद्देश्य का यह मुख्य ध्यान मसीहा और परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में यीशु पर विश्वास करने को बढ़ावा देना था यह दो बिंदु थे जिन पर यहूदी मसीही ओ को अरब नाले के साथ अपने संघर्ष में सहारे की आवश्यकता थी वेरी सुपर मसीह परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में विश्वास करने लगे थे और यदि उन्हें उद्धार की आशीशों को प्राप्त करना था तो उन्हें अपनी इस विश्व विश्वास में निरंतर आगे बढ़ना था।\r\n निसंदेह एक ऐसा भाव भी है जिनमें योहन्ना का सुसमाचार सब विश्वास यों के लिए है उदाहरण के तौर पर यहन्ना 13-17 मैं यूहन्ना ने इस बात पर बल देने के द्वारा सब विश्वास यों के विश्वास को बढ़ाने का प्रयास किया  कि यद्यपि यीशु इस पृथ्वी पर नहीं है फिर भी वहां पवित्र आत्मा के द्वारा अपने लोगों के जीवन में उपस्थित वास्तविकता है यूहन्ना की समस्त शिक्षा सभी विश वासियों के जीवनों को मजबूत करने के लिए थी।\r\n विद्वानों ने कहा है कि अन्ना का सुसमाचार वहां तालाब है जिसे सच्चे पार करते हैं और हाथी तैरते हैं इसका मूल संदेश स्पष्ट और सीधा है यीशु मसीह अर्थात परमेश्वर का पुत्र है परंतु इस मूल संदेश के विवरण व्याख्या कारों को निरंतर चुनौती प्रदान करते हैं जो वर्षों से इसका अध्ययन कर रहे हैं।\r\n पहले मसीही जिन्होंने इस सुसमाचार को पढ़ा होगा वे उसके द्वारा बहुत उत्साहित हुए होंगे उसने उन्हें अपने विरोधियों के साथ संगत के बीच मसीही विश्वास में बने रहना सिखाया होगा और इसने उन्हें उस मसीही के प्रति अपने प्रेम और सम्मान में भी प्रेरित किया होगा जो उनके बहुतायत के जीवन का एकमात्र स्रोत है और यूहन्ना का सुसमाचार वैसा ही उत्साह और प्रेरणा आज के मसीही ओ को भी प्रदान करता है। \r\n\r\n                                                                         PRAISE THE LORD', 9, '2020-08-28 03:46:34', '2020-09-08 00:33:58', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(1831, 528, 738, 'उत्तर =  यूहन्ना ने अपने उद्देश्य आत्मकथा यूहन्ना20:30-31 मैं अनेक महत्वपूर्ण विषयों की सूची दी है जहां हम इन वचनों को पढ़ते हैं।\r\n यीशु ने और भी बहुत से चीन और चेलों के सामने दिखाएं जो इस पुस्तक में लिखे नहीं गए परंतु यह इसलिए लिखे गए हैं कि तुम विश्वास करो कि इशू ही परमेश्वर का पुत्र मसीह है और विश्वास करके उसके नाम से जीवन पाओ।\r\n हमारे अध्याय के इस भाग में हम आपस में गहराइयों से जुड़े उन चार विषयों को देखेंगे जिन्हें योजना के उद्देश्य आत्मक कथन से लिया गया है जी विश्वास करने का कार्य मसीही के रूप में यीशु के पहचान उसके साथ-साथ परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में उसकी पहचान और उसके जीवन की राशि से जो वहां लाता है आइए विश्वास करने परियोजना द्वारा दिए गए महत्वपूर्ण के साथ शुरू करें\r\n\r\n विश्वास करने का विषय महत्वपूर्ण :-\r\n\r\n यूहन्ना ने यूनानी शब्द पिटयुओ  अर्थात विश्वास करना का 106 बार प्रयोग किया अन्य तीन  समाचारों ने मिलकर 34 बार इसका प्रयोग किया है यूहन्ना के सुसमाचार का केवल तीसरा हिस्सा महत्व देने में यह अंतर दर्शाता है कि यह ना की कहानी में विश्वास का विचार कितना महत्वपूर्ण है।\r\n यूहन्ना के सुसमाचार में विश्वास करने का विचार उन अन्य विचारों से निकटता से जुड़ा है जो इन शब्दों के द्वारा प्रकट किए गए हैं जैसे स्वीकार करना आना और जाना था यीशु में विश्वास करने का अर्थ है उसने स्वीकार करना उसके पास आना और परस्पर अनुभव करने के भाव में उसे जानना।\r\n इस प्रकार का विश्वास करना स्वीकार करना जानना और यीशु के पास आना प्रिय मसीही पर भरोसा करने और उसका अनुसरण करने के व्यक्तिगत निर्णय के समय के साथ आरंभ होता है वही कार्य जिसे आज के मसीही प्रिया हृदय परिवर्तन कहते हैं जब हृदय परिवर्तन सच्चा होता है यानी भिन्न रूपों में हमें परमेश्वर के कार्य में शामिल होने और उसकी आशीशों को प्राप्त करने में प्रेरित करता है उस अपने सुसमाचार के इस भाग में यूहन्ना ने हृदय परिवर्तन का उल्लेख परमेश्वर की संतान बन्ना अनंत जीवन प्राप्त करना जैसे वाक्यों के रूप में किया है यह होना  1 अध्याय 12 पद में विश्वास करने की योजना के वर्णन को सुनें।\r\n और यूहन्ना3:36 मैं हम ऐसी ही अभिषेक तो को पाते हैं जहां हम यह शब्द पढ़ते हैं: \r\n ऐसे अनुच्छेदों में विश्वास करना यीशु पर व्यक्तिगत निर्भरता और समर्पण का सच्चा और हृदय से निकाला कार्य है जो हमें उसके साथ जोड़ता है यहां इतिहास में हमें परमेश्वर के कार्य का भाग बनाता है और यह अपनी संपूर्णता में तभी पहुंचेगा जब यीशु अपनी पूरी महिमा में प्रगट होगा।\r\n अब यह अनुभव करना महत्वपूर्ण है कि यूहन्ना ने विश्वास करना का शब्द प्रयोगशाला एक ही रूप में नहीं किया कुछ अनुच्छेदों में यूनानी विश्वास करना शब्द का प्रयोग सत्ता ही विश्वास को दिखाने के लिए किया है जिसे धर्म विज्ञानी प्रिय अस्थाई या पाखंडी विश्वास कहते हैं उदाहरण के तौर पर यूहन्ना 2 अध्याय का 23 और 24 पद में यूनान के वर्णन को सुनें:\r\n यीशु ने अपने आप को इन लोगों के भरोसे पर नहीं छोड़ा क्योंकि उनका विश्वास केवल सता ही था यह वह सच्चा विश्वास नहीं था जिसे धर्म विज्ञानी प्रिया उधार देने वाला विश्वास कहते हैं।\r\n अधिकांश हम संदर्भ के अनुसार कह सकते हैं कि युवाओं ने विश्वास करना का प्रयोग तब किया जब उसके मन में सच्चा उधार देने वाला विश्वास था अर्थात उद्धार करता और परमेश्वर के रूप में यीशु पर सच्चा विश्वास यूहन्ना के लिए यीशु हमारे विश्वास का लक्ष्य संपूर्ण महत्व रखता है यहां हमारे विश्वास की शक्ति नहीं है जो हमें उद्धार देती है परंतु उसकी शामत जिस पर हम विश्वास करते हैं।\r\n हम यहां पर यीशु पर विश्वास करने के विषय को देख चुके हैं इसलिए आइए अब हम उस महत्वपूर्ण बात की ओर मुड़े जिन पर यह ना चाहता है कि हम यीशु के विषय में विश्वास करें वह मसीह है पुराने नियम का मसीहा है परमेश्वर द्वारा अपने लोगों इस्राएल से की गई प्राचीन प्रतिज्ञा ओं की पूर्णता।\r\n\r\n                                                                PRAISE THE LORD', 9, '2020-08-28 03:56:38', '2020-09-08 00:33:58', NULL),
(1832, 528, 739, 'उत्तर =  यीशु को मसीही कहने के द्वारा यूहन्ना ने स्पष्ट रूप से उसे इस्राएल के राजा के रूप में दर्शाया पहली सदी में मसीही या मसीहा शब्द इसराइल के राजा का सामर्थ्य बन गया था मसीह यही था परंतु इस तथ्य के बहुत से अर्थ थे कि इस्राएल का राजा था और इस यूहन्ना कईयो पर ध्यान आकर्षित किया है।\r\n उदाहरण के तौर पर बल दिया कि पुरानी नियम के इस्राएल और यहूदा के राजाओं के समान यीशु ने उन लोगों को प्रस्तुत किया जिन पर उसने शासन किया यीशु वह सब बन गया जो इसराइल बनने में असफल हो गया था और इसलिए उसने वहां सारी आशीष से प्राप्त की जो इसराइल पहले पाने में असफल हो गया था। इसराइल के राजा के रूप में यीशु ने हर रूप में इस्राएल का प्रतिनिधित्व किया और उनका स्थापना एवं उनके लिए परमेश्वर की आशीशों का माध्यम दोनों बन गया।\r\nयूहन्ना 15:1-8 मैं यूहन्ना ने यह कहते हुए यीशु के विषय में इस सत्य को प्रकट किया कि इस सच्चीदा करता है और कि उसके अनुयाई उसकी डालियां है सुनिए (15:5-8)\r\n संपूर्ण पुराने नियम में इस्राएल को परमेश्वर की दक्षता के रूप में चिन्हित किया गया है हम इस चिन्ह को भजन 80 में यिर्मयाह अध्याय 2 यहेजकेल अध्याय 17 और होशे अध्याय 10  मैं पाते हैं इससे बढ़कर दाऊद के राज्य के परिवारों भविष्य के महान मसीहा को भी उस डाली के रूप में प्रस्तुत किया गया था जिसमें परमेश्वर के सारे लोग निकलेंगे हम इसे यशायाह 11:1 जैसी जगहों में पाते हैं अतः इस पृष्ठभूमि में जब यीशु ने सच्चीदा करता होने और परमेश्वर को प्रस्तुत करने एवं उससे महिमा देने के एकमात्र मार्ग होने का दावा किया तो उसके चेले शायद समझ गए होंगे कि इसराइल का वह सच्चा राजा था जिसने अपने लोगों का प्रतिनिधित्व किया और उन्हें प्रस्तुत किया।\r\n परंतु इस विचार के क्या अर्थ है कि राजा होने के रूप में यीशु सच्चा या वास्तविक इस्राएल है एक तो यह कि वह सब बन रहा था जो इसराइल को बनाने के लिए बुलाया गया था इसराइल वह सब बनने और करने में असफल हो गया था जो परमेश्वर ने उसे बनने और करने के लिए बुलाया था परंतु जहां इसराइल पाप के कारण असफल हो गया था वह यीशु की पूरी तरह से सफल रहा था उसने इसराइल के नेतृत्व को पूरा कर दिया था अपने व्यक्तिगत में यीशु ने पुराने नियम के सदियों के इतिहास को पूरा किया और परमेश्वर की महिमा मई उपस्थिति को के वैसे ही पूरा किया जैसे केवल वहां कर सकता था और इस कारण इसराइल के सच्चे लोगों की पहचान इसराइल राष्ट्र की सदस्यता से नहीं होती इसलिए अपेक्षित था वह ऐसे लोग हैं जो सच्चीदा तथा में डालिया है अर्थात मसीह में विश्वासी है जो विश्वास के साथ उससे जुड़े हुए हैं।\r\n मसीह के रूप में यीशु की प्रतिनिधि की भूमिका के बारे में हमारी चर्चा 29 तरीकों पर केंद्रित होगी जिनमें यीशु ने पुराने नियम की मसीह की अपेक्षित था वह को पूरा किया और जो यूहन्ना के सुसमाचार में बहुत महत्वपूर्ण पहला यीशु ने मंदिर को पूरा किया दूसरा उसने इसराइल के पर्व द्वारा रखी गई अपेक्षाओं को पूरा किया और तीसरा उसने परमेश्वर की व्यवस्था को पूरा किया हम इन सारे विचारों को देखेंगे आइए इस से शुरू करें कि यीशु ने किस प्रकार मंदिर को पूरा किया।\r\n\r\n मंदिर :-\r\n\r\n पवित्र शास्त्र में मंदिर के महत्वपूर्ण होने का कारण यह था कि यह वह स्थान जहां परमेश्वर ने अपने लोगों के साथ एक विशेष रूप में से उपस्थित होने की प्रतिज्ञा की थी निस्संदेह हम जानते हैं कि परमेश्वर व्यवस्था भी है वह हर समय में हर जगह है परंतु जब हम उसकी विशेष उपस्थिति के बारे में बात करते हैं तो हमारे मन में उसकी उपस्थिति का प्रकटीकरण होता है अर्थात ऐसे समय जब परमेश्वर ने किन्हीं विशेष स्थानों में अपनी उपस्थिति को दर्शाया और प्रिया रूपों में जो दिखाई देने में महिमा माई हो।\r\n अपने लोगों के बीच परमेश्वर की विशेष उपस्थिति का विषय बाइबल के इतिहास में कई चरणों में पूरा होता है आरंभ में अदन की वाटिका पृथ्वी पर एक पवित्र स्थान थी जहां परमेश्वर की विशेष उपस्थिति रहती थी वहां पृथ्वी पर उसका सिंहासन का समझा जाता था जहां से मनुष्य जाति को पूरी पृथ्वी को पुत्र करना था अर्थात पूरे संसार को परमेश्वर के पुत्र राज्य में बदलना था।\r\n बाद में  जब परमेश्वर ने इस्राएल को राज्य की आया जब पद दिया तो उसने पहले अपनी विशेष उपस्थिति को पहले तंबू के समान साथ जोड़ा फिर बाद में मंदिर के साथ तंबू और मंदिर की सजा सजा और बनावट अदन की वाटिका के सदृश्य थी और तंबू एक मंदिर ने वाटिका के सामने कार्यों को पूरा किया पवित्र शास्त्र यह दर्शाते हुए इस संबंध की पुष्टि करता है की तंबू और मंदिर प्रति पर परमेश्वर के राज्य के सिंहासन थे अर्थात् ऐसे स्थान जहां उसने अपने लोगों के बीच महिमा माई रूप में वास किए या बात 1 इतिहास 28:2 भजन 11:4 और यशायाह 6:1 जैसे स्थानों में स्पष्ट रूप में पाई जाती है यह पृथ्वी के सबसे पवित्र स्नान थे यह ऐसे स्थान थे जहां परमेश्वर की आशीष से उसके लोगों द्वारा प्राप्त की जा सकती थी और अदन की वाटिका के सामने वह उसके राज्य के केंद्र थे जहां वे से उसके लोगों को उसके राज्य के रूप में पृथ्वी को पत्र बनाना था और यह ना कि सुसमाचार के अनुसार यीशु के महत्व को समझने का एक जीवित तरीका यह देखना है कि वह परमेश्वर के तंबू और मंदिर के पुराने नियम के विषय को पूरा करना है सुनिए यूहन्ना यूहन्ना एक अध्याय 14 पद में क्या लिखा।\r\n जब यह 9 सुख के हमारे बीच में डेरा करने के विषय में कहां तो हमने यूनानी  क्रियास्केनू  का प्रयोग किया जोस्केने नामक संज्ञा से जुड़ी है जिसका अर्थ है मंडप यह तंबू वास्तव में इसी संज्ञा का प्रयोग सेप्टुआजिट पुराने नियम के अनुवाद में परमेश्वर के पुत्र तंबू के लिए किया गया है इस क्रिया का प्रयोग करने और इससे परमेश्वर की उपस्थिति की महिमा से जोड़ने के द्वारा यूहन्ना ने इसे स्पष्ट कर दिया कि ईश्वर परमेश्वर की उसी विशेष उपस्थिति तक हमारी पहुंच स्थापित कर रहा था जो पहले तंबू में उपलब्ध थी। और यह होना नहीं होना 2 अध्याय का 19 और 21 पद में उसी बात को दर्शाए जहां हम इस विवरण को पढ़ते हैं।\r\n यह यूहन्ना ने स्पष्ट कर दिया कि शिव मंदिर की पूर्ण बता था यूहन्ना ने यह भी स्पष्ट किया कि देहि तौर पर यीशु के प्रति पर उपस्थित नहीं होने के बाद भी उसके अनुयाई परमेश्वर की विशेष उपस्थिति का आनंद लेंगे इसलिए यह ना चार अध्याय कई किस पद में यीशु ने सामरी स्त्री को बताया कि वह दिन शीघ्र आ रहा है जब परमेश्वर की आराधना में ना तो यरूशलेम के मंदिर और ना ही सांवरिया के पवित्र स्नान का कोई विशेष महत्व रह जाएगा जैसा कि सोने यूहन्ना 4 अध्याय का 23 से 24 पद में कहा सावरी स्त्री से कह गए यीशु के शब्द आधुनिक अलीशा के लिए बड़े उत्साह वर्धक होने चाहिए क्योंकि हम वैसे ही समय में रह रहे हैं जिसके बारे में यीशु बात कर रहा था हमारे समय में यीशु पृथ्वी पर दैहिक रूप से उपस्थित नहीं है इब्रानियो 8:3-9:11-12 के अनुसार वहां स्वर्ग में परमेश्वर के तंबू में दैहिक रूप से वास करता है परंतु आत्मिक रूप से वहां हमारे साथ उपस्थित है विशेषकर जब हम एक अलीशा के रूप में एकत्रित होते हैं हम इस बात को मत्ती 18:20 और 1 पतरस 2:4-9 जैसे स्थानों में देते हैं और क्योंकि यीशु हमारे साथ उपस्थित है इसलिए अब हम पृथ्वी पर परमेश्वर की विशेष उपस्थिति के पुत्र मंदिर है परंतु मसीह में मंदिर के यहां अद्भुत पूर्णता भी जाती रहेगी जब यीशु अपनी महिमा में पुनः आएगा  प्रकाशितवाक्य 21:1-5 जैसे अनुच्छेद  सिखाते हैं जब यीशु का पुनरागमन होगा तो वहां संपूर्ण सृष्टि को परमेश्वर के निवास स्थान में बदल देगा उस समय मसीह और पिता सदैव हमारे साथ वास करेंगे और सारी पृथ्वी परमेश्वर की महिमा से भर जाएगी।\r\n यूहन्ना के सुसमाचार में यीशु द्वारा पुराने नियम की मसीही संबंधित अपेक्षाओं को पूरा किए जाने के दूसरा रूप इसराइल के पर्व के महत्व को पूरा करना था।\r\n\r\n पर्व :-\r\n\r\n जैसे कि हमने पहले उल्लेख किया यूहन्ना के सुसमाचार को उसके पर्व इर्द-गिर्द देखा जा सकता है जिसमें यीशु शामिल हुआ था इन पर्वों में फंसा झोपड़ियों और समर्पण के कई पर्व थे परमेश्वर कि इस्राएल को राज्य के याजक पद प्रदान करने और तंबू एवं मंदिर में उसकी विशेष उपस्थिति की आशीष शो का आनंद लेने के लिए इन पर्वों को स्थापित किया था और अपने सुसमाचार में यूहन्ना ने इसे स्पष्ट किया कि ईश्वर ने इन पर्वों के महत्व को पूरा किया।\r\n आस्था का पर्व इसराइल के तीन मुख्य वर्षिक पर्व में से एक था यहां मिश्र से इस्राएल के कुछ का पर्व था साप्ताहिक में यीशु ने इस पर्व को पूरा किया क्योंकि वह हंसा के मिलने के उस सामान था जिसे फसा के दिन मारा गया और खाया गया और जिसका लहू मिश्र से इस्राएल के छुटकारे का प्रतीक था सभी चारों समाचारों निशु को फसा के सच्चे में मनी के रूप में पहचाना परंतु केवल यह अन्ना ने ही यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा दाता इन शब्दों को दर्शाते हुए योजना 1 अध्याय का 29 पद में इस बात को प्रकट किया देखो यहां परमेश्वर का मेमना है जो जगत के पापों को उठा ले जाता है यह 19 अध्याय के तहत इस पद में यूहन्ना ने यह भी बताया कि जब यीशु की मृत्यु हुई तो सैनिकों ने उसकी टांगें नहीं तोड़ी जिससे निर्गमन 12:46 की बात पूरी हुई फसा के भोज के लिए चुने हुए मैंने की हड्डियां तोड़ी नहीं जानी चाहिए इन अन्य कई रूपों में यूहन्ना ने दर्शाया कि सुने हंसा के प्रत्येक और अर्थात को पूरा किया।\r\n यह ना 7 अध्याय का 2 पद और 37 पर में यूहन्ना ने इस्राएल के तीन अन्य वार्षिक पर्वों में भी यीशु के शामिल होने का वर्णन किया झोपड़ियों का पर्व इस पर्व की सबसे महत्वपूर्ण स्मरण उस बात को याद करके पानी उड़ेल ना थी जिस प्रकार परमेश्वर ने मरुभूमि में इस्राएल को पानी प्रदान किया था और जिस प्रकार परमिशन हर साल इसराइल की फसलों के लिए वारिस प्रदान की थी और इस बात की प्रतीक्षा में भी कि परमेश्वर किस प्रकार अंत के दिनों में अपने लोगों पर आशीष के सोते वह आएगा और यूहन्ना ने इस समारोह और यूहन्ना के बीच यहां दिखाते हुए गहरा संबंध दिखाया कि उन सारी आशीशों का माध्यम बनेगा जो परमेश्वर इतिहास के अंत में उडेलेगा।\r\n विशेष रूप से यूहन्ना ने बताया कि झोपड़ियों के पर्व के अंतिम दिन यीशु परमेश्वर की आशीष को देने की अपनी सामर्थ्य की घोषणा की सुनी सुनी योहन्ना साथ देकर सेट इस पद में भीड़ से क्या कहा यो हनी बताएं कि परमेश्वर की आशीशों का जीवन काजल यीशु से बहेगा भूत का कि आशीष वर्तमान की आशीष और भविष्य की आस ए सब उसके द्वारा आती है इस प्रकार यीशु परमेश्वर के अंसारी हादसों के पूर्ण होता है जो झोपड़ियों के पर्व में चुन्नी थी अंत में यह अन्ना 10 अध्याय का 22 से 29 पद में यीशु से समर्पण का पर्व यहां हनुक्काहमनाया  समर्पण कपड़ों पुराने नियम में स्थापित इसराइल के पर्व का कोई महत्वपूर्ण पर्व नहीं था परंतु पहली सदी के सरल के जीवन के लिए यह महत्वपूर्ण था क्योंकि यहां 165 ईसवी में यूनानी से सको पहल की विजय का पर्व था और इसके साथ  वेदी और मंदिर के पुनर्निर्माण का भी जो इस विजय के बात हुआ यूहन्ना 10 अध्याय का 30 पद में जब यीशु समर्पण का पर्व माना माना रहा था तो उसने यह आरंभिक घोषणा की यदि समझ गए थे कि वह परमेश्वर होने का दावा कर रहा था अतः उन्होंने उस पर पथराव करने का प्रयास किया फिर भी उसने स्वयं को यह दर्शाते हुए अपना बचाव किया।\r\n\r\n व्यवस्था :-\r\n\r\n व्यवस्था पी मसीही प्रिया परमेश्वर की व्यवस्था के विषय में नकारात्मक रूप से सोचते हैं वहां जो हमें दोषी ठहरा टी है परंतु हमें यहां भी याद रखना है कि व्यवस्था सच्चे विश वासियों को परमेश्वर की आंसुओं की और अगुवाई करने के लिए दी गई थी पुराने नियम में परमेश्वर की व्यवस्था को अपने लोगों के लिए एक विशेष उपहार के रूप में चयनित किया गया था भजन 119 और अन्य कई अनुच्छेद इसे इसराइल के लिए परमेश्वर की आशीशों का मार्गदर्शन मानते हैं और नए नियम में याकूब परमेश्वर की व्यवस्था को याकूब एक का 25 पद में वहां सिद्ध व्यवस्था कहता है जो  स्वतंत्रता देती है और पॉलिसी से 1 कुरि 9:21 मैं मशीन व्यवस्था कहता है और इशू होना 10 अध्याय का 35 पद में यह कहते हुए व्यवस्था क्या महत्त्व मूल्यों की पुष्टि करता है यहां यीशु ने शिकायत की व्यवस्था समेत पूरा पुराना नियम अपने लोगों के लिए परमेश्वर का अंत और स्थाई वचन है फिर भी यूहन्ना ने स्पष्ट किया कि व्यवस्था अपने आप में अंत नहीं थी एक महत्वपूर्ण वहां में इस स्नेह सदैव अपने से  पर यीशु की ओर संकेत किया यूहन्ना 5 अध्याय का 40 पद से 47 पद में यीशु ने अविश्वास यहूदियों से कहा यूहन्ना ने अपने पूरे सुसमाचार में इस बात पर जोर दिया पुराने नियम की व्यवस्था निशु की ओर आगे संकेत किया था अच्छा यीशु को ठुकराने का अर्थ है उस व्यवस्था को ठुकरा ना जिससे उसकी भविष्यवाणी की थी यह न द्वारा इस बात पर बल देने का एक तरीका यीशु को वेद सारे शिर्सत चरित्र और कार्य प्रदान करना था जो यहूदी धर्म में व्यवस्था को दिए गए उदाहरण के तौर पर यहूदी धर्म ने कहा था कि तुम्हें एक भूखे शत्रु को तो रहा व्यवस्था की रोटी का भोजन देनी चाहिए यहूदी धर्म का दावा था कि तोहरा के शब्द जगत के लिए जीवन है और यह ना चार अध्याय के 11 पद में इस जीवन का जल देने वाला है यह भी धर्म ने यह भी कहा कि व्यवस्था की ज्योति हर मनुष्य को प्रकाशित करने के लिए दी गई है और यह एक अध्ययन ओपन कहता है कि यीशु वहां सच्ची ज्योति है जो हर एक मनुष्य को प्रकाशित करती है यह योहन्ना के सुसमाचार के कुछ उदाहरण है जो दिखाते हैं कि यीशु परमेश्वर की व्यवस्था कब प्रकृति करण था इशू और उसकी स्थिति उन सबके लिए आज भी जीवन और ज्योति के स्रोत है जो उसका अनुसरण करते हैं यह ना चाहता था कि उसके पाठक समझ ले कि यीशु के लिए मसीही होने का अर्थ किया था वह चाहता था कि वह इस बात की समझ में भी विश्वास प्राप्त करें कि ईश्वर ने अपनी कलीसिया को त्यागा  है  बल्कि वहां हमारे साथ सदैव उपस्थित है वह चाहता है कि वह  यीशु पर भरोसा रखें ताकि वे उसके द्वारा परमेश्वर की आशीशों को प्राप्त करें और वह चाहता था कि वह परमेश्वर के वचन के प्रति आज्ञाकारी रहे ताकि वे उसके या जी को के राज्य के रूप में प्रभु की महिमा करें|\r\n\r\n                                                                                PRAISE THE LORD', 10, '2020-08-28 04:12:03', '2020-09-08 00:33:58', NULL),
(1833, 528, 740, 'उत्तर = परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में  यीशु की पहचान मसीहा के रूप में उसकी पहचान की समांतर है क्योंकि वह दोनों इस बात को दर्शाते हैं कि वह पृथ्वी पर परमेश्वर के राज्य का राजा है। परंतु इन सारे शब्दों पर अलग-अलग चर्चा करना महत्वपूर्ण है क्योंकि उन सबका अलग-अलग अर्थ है।\r\n यूहन्ना के सुसमाचार में परमेश्वर का पुत्र नामक शब्द समूह देवीय मसीहा रूपी राजा को दर्शाता है एक और यह देवी पुत्र के भाव में दिखाता है जो स्वर्ग से पृथ्वी पराया जैसा कि योहन्ना10:22-40 मैं दूसरी और यह इसराइल के राजा मसीहा का सामर्थ्य हो सकता है अर्थात दाऊद का मानवीय वंशजों इसराइल का न्याय सिंहासन राजा था जैसा कि हम यूहन्ना 1:27 - 11:27 मे देखते हैं।\r\n यूहन्ना के सुसमाचार में यीशु के परमेश्वर के पुत्र होने के अर्थ को अच्छी तरह से समझ लेना हमें यह देखने में सहायता करता है कि यूहन्ना ने इस बड़े रहस्य पर कैसा बल दिया कि यीशु पूर्ण रूप से देवीय है और पूर्ण रूप से मानवीय है।\r\n\r\nदैवीय :-\r\n\r\n युहन्ना दोबारा पुत्र के देवी होने के दर्शाने का एक रूप पुत्र यीशु और पिता परमेश्वर के बीच संबंध को दिखाना था ऐसे कई अनुच्छेद है जो दर्शाते हैं कि यहां संबंध उस संबंध से गुणात्मक रूप से अलग है जो पिता का अपनी मानवी संतान अर्थात विश वासियों के साथ यूहन्ना10:30-33 मैं यीशु और यहूदियों के बीच इस वार्तालाप को सुनें यहूदी सही रूप से समझ गए थे कि परमेश्वर पिता के साथ एक होने के यीशु के दावे अर्थात यह दावा करना था कि यीशु वास्तव में परमेश्वर था।\r\n इससे बढ़कर योहन्ना 14 अध्याय का 9 पद के अनुसार यीशु परमेश्वर का वह आदित्य पुत्र है जिसने पिता को इस प्रकार प्रकट किया जो कोई कभी नहीं कर सकता 1:18  पुत्र शब्द का प्रयोग नहीं करता फिर भी विचार बिल्कुल वही है यीशु अपने लोगों के सामने पिता को शुद्ध रूप से प्रकट करता है वास्तव में यह ना 14 अध्याय का 9 पद में यीशु के अनुसार यीशु को देखना पिता को देखना है।\r\n और प्रकाशन की विषयों से परे यीशु के पास जीवन और मृत्यु एवं अंतिम न्याय पर पूरा देवी अधिकार है जैसा कि हम यूहन्ना 5:21-22 मे पढते हैं \r\n यूहन्ना ने इस बात को स्पष्ट किया कि यीशु देह में परमेश्वर था वह स्वयं परमेश्वर था और उसके पास प्रति पर परमेश्वर के कार्य को पूरा करने का अमित अधिकार था।\r\n यूहन्ना द्वारा पुत्र की दिव्यता को प्रकट करने का अन्य माध्यम में हूं के रूप में यीशु का स्वयं का वर्णन है निर्गमन 3:14 मैं परमेश्वर ने मैं जो हूं सो हूं कहते हुए मूसा के सामने अपने वचा ईनाम को प्रकट किया यह उस दिव्या नाम का आधार था जिसे हिंदी में प्रिया केवल प्रभु के नाम में प्रस्तुत किया जाता है परमेश्वर के नाम को इतना पवित्र माना जाता था कि शो के समय के यहूदी उसका नाम तक नहीं लेते थे परंतु यीशु ने उसे स्वयं पर लागू किया।\r\nयूहन्ना 8:12-59 मैं यीशु और यहूदी अब वह काजोल अनसीन अमन सामना  हुआ विवाद यीशु के पुत्र होने के दावे पर और उसके विरोधियों के अब्राहम के पुत्र होने के दावे पर था पद 44 में यीशु ने उन्हें बताया कि उस उनका सही पिता शैतान है इसके जवाब में उन्होंने यह पूछते भी उसे चुनौती दी कि क्या अब्राहम हमसे बड़ा है तभी सुने योहन्ना 8 अध्याय 58 पद में इन शब्दों के साथ विवाद में का सामना किया।\r\n यीशु ने यह नहीं कहा मैं था जो ज्यादातर स्वभाविक होता है यदि उसे यह कहना होता कि वह अब हमसे आयु में बड़ा है उसने कहा मैं हूं जिसके द्वारा उसने दावा किया कि वह न केवल अब राम से बड़ा और महान बल्कि इसराइल का अनंत परमेश्वर भी है।\r\n यीशु की दिव्यांगता पर विचार करने के बाद यह ना कि इस बात पर चर्चा करें कि परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में यीशु पूर्ण रूप से मानवीय भी था।\r\n\r\n मानवीय :-\r\n\r\n दाऊद के समय से परमेश्वर का पुत्र शब्द समूह का प्रयोग उस्मान वीर आजा के लिए किया जाता था जो इसराइल के राजा के रूप में दाऊद के सिंहासन पर बैठना था हम इसे भजन 2:1 शमूएल 7:14 जैसे स्थानों पर देख सकते हैं योहन्ना 7 अध्याय 42 पद भी दिखाता है कि यहूदियों की अपेक्षा थी कि मसीह दाऊद के वंश से आएगा और योहन्ना 1 अध्याय का उन 50 पद में परमेश्वर का पुत्र शब्द समूह का प्रयोग इस्राएल के राजा के समानार्थी के रूप में किया जाता है।\r\n यूहन्ना के कई अन्य अनुच्छेद भी यीशु को यहूदियों के राजा के रूप में दर्शाते हैं जैसे 12:13-15,18:33-40 और 19:1-21 सारांश में दाऊद यूहन्ना यीशु को परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में दर्शा ना तो उसका आंशिक अर्थ था यीशु दाऊद का सिद्ध मान्य व्यवस्था जो इसराइल पर सदा सर्वदा राज्य करेगा।\r\n यूहन्ना का सुसमाचार बल देता है कि परमेश्वर के पुत्र के रूप में यीशु में संपूर्ण देवी राज्य तो और संपूर्ण मानवी राजत्व पाया जाता है वह प्रत्येक आशा जो पुराना नियम ब्राह्मण पर परमेश्वर के राज्य में रखता है और वह प्रत्येक आशा जो पुराने नियम ने दाऊद के वंश के मसीहा के राजा के लिए स्थापित किया है वह सब यीशु के राज्यों में पूरी होती है।\r\n\r\n                                                                          PRAISE THE LORD', 9, '2020-08-28 04:27:07', '2020-09-08 00:33:58', NULL),
(1834, 528, 741, 'प्रभु यीशु मसीह आज से 2000 साल पहले स्वर्गीय की महिमा को छोड़कर के सारे मानव जाति के उद्धार के लिए इस संसार पर आए 39 कोड़े खाए मारे गए कलवरी क्रॉस पर गाड़े गए और तीसरे दिन मृत्यु के ऊपर में जी उठा गलातियो 4:4-6 मैं प्रभु यीशु मसीह व्यवस्था के आधीन में व्यवस्था को मोर ले कर के प्रभु यीशु मसीह ने हमारे लिए वचन को पूरा किया व्यवस्था को पूरा किया पुराने नियम के सारे व्यवस्था को प्रभु यीशु मसीह ने हम सभी मानव जाति के लिए पूरा किया पुराने नियम में लिखा है कि जो व्यवस्था को मनुष्य कर नहीं सका और जो कार्य को कर नहीं सका प्रभु यीशु मसीह ने उसे पूरा किया सो प्रभु यीशु मसीह ने हमारे लिए सारे व्यवस्था को पूरा किया और नए नियम हमारे जीवन में दे दिया लेकिन फिर भी परमेश्वर का पुत्र वचन नए-नए में लिखा है कि प्रभु यीशु मसीह यदि हमारे पापों के लिए करवरी क्रूस पर बलिदान हुआ तो क्या हम पाप करे कदापि हम पाप ना करें परंतु और भी परमेश्वर के पुत्र बचन को अपने जीवन पर लागू करते हुए नए नियम के अनुसार हमारे जीवन को पवित्र जाएं और निष्कलंक और निर्दोष होकर के इस जीवन में जीना हमारे लिए जरूरी है यूहन्ना भी हमें इसी प्रकार से सिखाते हैं कि प्रभु यीशु मसीह हमारे लिए कलवरी क्रूज पर बलिदान हुआ हमारे पापों के लिए बलिदान हुआ तो हम बात ना करें परंतु प्रभु यीशु मसीह पर विश्वास करके हम उसके पीछे चलने वाले बन पाए यीशु ने हमारे लिए व्यवस्था को पूरा कर दिया फिर भी हमें उस वचन के अनुसार नए नियम के वचन के अनुसार हमें अपने जीवन में निष्कलंक और पत्रिकाएं और परमेश्वर की भाई रखते हुए हमें इन दिनों में आगे बढ़ना जरूरी है क्योंकि स्वर्गीय के आसन के सामने प्रभु यीशु मसीह के सामने सारे मसीह का इसी व्यवस्था के द्वारा न्याय किया जाएगा यदि हम व्यवस्था के आधीन जीते हैं तो व्यवस्था के अनुसार हमारा न्याय किया जाएगा हमें प्रतिफल भी दिया जाएगा।\r\nइन दिनों हमें प्रभु यीशु मसीह पर सारे विश्वास के साथ में उसके पीछे चलना चाहिए हमें परमेश्वर की व्यवस्था को उत्तर नजर से और पुत्र दिल से स्वीकार करना है और उस वचन के अनुसार अपने जीवन को बनाना है क्योंकि इस वचन के अनुसार ही स्वर्ग के सिंहासन पर एक दिन हम सभी मानव जाति का न्याय किया जाएगा अगर हम परमेश्वर के पवित्र वचन कौन निर्दोष और निष्कलंक रीति से पवित्र मन से स्वीकार करते हैं तो स्वर्ग सिंहासन के सामने भी हम निर्दोष और परमेश्वर की नजरों में पवित्र ठहराए जाएंगे।\r\n                                                                            PRAISE THE LORD', 8, '2020-08-28 04:42:12', '2020-09-08 00:33:58', NULL),
(1835, 527, 826, 'Our definition focuses on God and his blessing rather than on terms like god or evil, or right or wrong. those things that receive God\'s blessings are right and those things that do not receive his blessing are wrong and evil.\r\nBy focusing on God and his blessing in this ways , we mean that God\'s nature is the standard of morality. and secondly God\' s actions demonstrate the standard of morality.\r\nGod himself is the ultimate standard of right and wrong., of good and evil.\r\nwe are obligated to see god\'s nature as the standard and model of rightness and goodness.\r\nthe second thing we mean to say that by focusing on God and his blessing is that God\'s actions demonstrate the standard of morality.\r\nGod shows his approval for what is right and good is by bestowing blessings. similarly he shows his hatred for what id wrong and evil  y withholding blessings and pouring out curses.\r\nLeviticus 26:3 God threatens curses to those who disobeys his commandments. We see many times in Bible communicates right or wrong by recording God\'s reactions rather than explicitly labeling things right or wrong', 8, '2020-08-28 17:52:13', '2020-09-08 00:34:30', NULL),
(1836, 527, 827, 'Unless a work is done with the right motive , it is not a work that God will reward with blessings. First it must proceed from a heart that is purified by faith . Second it must flow out of Christian love.\r\nFaith- Only believers whoa re ind welled by the holy spirit can do works that rewards with the blessings. Only believers have hearts that are purified by faith. Saving faith that remains and grows  within believers. It is the means of purification through which believers  receive new and good natures. And it properly motivates believers to do good works. James 2:14-20\r\nThe kind of faith that purifies the heart, kind of faith that saves  is the kind pf faith that motivates good works. This is the faith possessed by believers and only believers\r\nLove-\r\n1 Corinthians 13 we read that our works are useless if they are not motivated by love. Works and even spiritual gifts that produce beneficial results merit no reward if they are not motivated by love.\r\nThings that do no merit reward are not good in God\'s eyes.Love is an aspect of every law God requires us to obey, so that we do not act in love , no work we do can conform to his standard. And what makes God\'s standard even harder to meet is that our love must be for both God and neighbor.', 9, '2020-08-28 18:04:47', '2020-09-08 00:34:30', NULL),
(1837, 527, 828, 'The threefold criteria  to good works are :\r\nObedience to God\'s command must be done with the proper motive , second it must be dine according to the proper standard and third it must be dine with the proper goal in mind  to glorify God.\r\nProper Motive:\r\nUnless a work is done with the right motive, it is not a work that god will reward with blessings. First kit must proceed from a heart that is purified by faith. Second actions must flow out of Christian love.\r\nProper Standard :\r\nBesides pointing that good works must flow from the right motives, the Westminister Confession of faith also states that good works must conform to the right standard In order for works to be good, they must be done according to the standard of the word of God , i.e God\'s revelation in the form of commands of Scripture, all of scripture and third general revelation, creation itself.\r\nProper Goal:\r\nAll good works must have the right end or goal.\r\nEven in our immediate gals like caring for our families , obeying our parents, our core we want to glorify God, by living in a way that please him.', 8, '2020-08-28 18:17:28', '2020-09-08 00:34:30', NULL),
(1838, 527, 829, 'Ethical judgement involves the application God\'s word to a situation by a person.s \r\nThere are three perspectives or approaches or toward every ethical judgement.\r\nSITUATIONAL\r\nThis approach may be called \"teleological \" because it focuses on the end or the result of actions . It involves noting the relations of means to ends in God\'s economy, asking questions what are the best means of achieving God\'s purposes?Romans 6:2-4\r\nNORMATIVE\r\nNormative refers to the fact that God\'d word is the norm or standard fro ethics or this way applies when we look to when Bible to tell us what to do.\r\nThe apostle John also adopted this perspective when appealed to God\'s commandments as the basis for believe or behavior in John 3:23\r\nEXISTENTIAL\r\nThis perspective views ethics through the lens of the individual person\'s experience. It focus on the self in confrontation and interaction with God.In  John 3:21 and Galatians 5:16 he explained that believers can perform good deeds by obeying the inward leading of the Holy Spirit', 8, '2020-08-28 18:30:17', '2020-09-08 00:34:30', NULL),
(1839, 527, 830, 'God is the absolute judge of Morality. That is , he has the ultimate prerogative to determine whether or not particular actions, emotions and thoughts meet or transgress his moral requirements. Jesus himself made it clear that on the last day , God himself will judge all people by their actions, an thereby he will either confirm or condemn all, the judgement that human beings have ever made.\r\nGod himself is the highest court in the universe. He will make the ultimate determination of whether or not we have lived morally or immorally and his judgement will be utterly binding. All authority an all power belong to him , so that there is no way to avert his judgments. Job 40:2-14\r\nIt\'s God\'s right to judge because he has absolute authority and his judgments are inescapable because he has absolute power.\r\nAs the absolute judge of morality god consistently appeals the absolute moral standard of his character in every judgments  He makes.His judgments are perfect, exhibiting flawless insight and wisdom , unfailing fairness and impeccable morality.', 8, '2020-08-28 18:41:58', '2020-09-08 00:34:30', NULL),
(1840, 527, 831, 'They are three categories of God\'s revelation:\r\nGeneral Revelation:\r\nBible assures us that general revelation still speaks clearly enough to teach us true things about God, it reveals the perfect standard of God\'s character serves as one of God\'s revelation norms.some general revelation is known by so few  people that it appears to be very similar to special revelation.\r\nGeneral revelation a is a standard or norm for belief about God that is binding on all people., every one who acts contrarily to what God has revealed is guilty of sin.Romans 1:32\r\nSpecial Revelation:\r\nThis type of revelation is complex , coming to us in a  way number of forms. Most of theses forms rely on the spoken or written word , but all of them involve God communicating with people in ways that transcend the normal working of creation. Scripture is the most relevant form of special revelation for us today.\r\nExistential Revelation:\r\nIt is the idea that God reveals himself in and through persons has always been recognized by the  mainstream of Protestant theology as apart of general revelation. God uses human existence and judgments, and human behavior as an external type of existential behavior.Romans 2:14-15, according to Paul God also communicates truth to unbelievers through illumination. Bey', 8, '2020-08-28 19:01:57', '2020-09-08 00:34:30', NULL),
(1841, 527, 832, 'The external aspects of existential revelation includes such things as human existence, human judgement, both individual and corporate and human behavior. human existence as a form of revelation because human beings are created in the image of God. We are replica or reflection of God. Human beings are the image that reflects God;s glory and dignity.\r\nIndividual and corporate human judgement is a form of existential revelation ,is closely relate to the fact that we are in  God\'s image.It is fair to say that when human beings think and judge in an exercise of divinely delegated authority, we are reflecting God\'s character.\r\nBesides human exercise and judgment, God also uses human behavior as an external type of existential revelation.\r\nThe Holy Spirit works within the human beings to reveal truth about God  in the form of illumination and inward leading of the Holy Spirit.\r\nPhiliippians 2:13 This too form is a form of revelation because it communicates impressions and intuitions about God\'s character to us..Because it reveals God\'s character, it is a binding standard that we must obey and to which we must conform.', 8, '2020-08-28 19:19:07', '2020-09-08 00:34:30', NULL),
(1842, 527, 833, 'Because God\'s behavior is also perfectly good and moral, it is also a binding moral standard. So it is the obligation of every person to obey God by conforming to the standard of his actions. 1 John 1:7 John teaches that  we must all walk in the light  as he is in the light, John indicated that all believers are obligated to imitate God, Second John  said that our obligation to obey  God\'s standard is related to our forgiveness  in Christ. Only if we are imitating God does the blood of Christ cleanse from sin, We cannot have Jesus as Savior without also being obligated to obey him as Lord.\r\nJesus died for our sins, but we have no license to sin pr live as we please. in truth, even believers must live by the standard of God\'s character./', 7, '2020-08-28 19:28:46', '2020-09-08 00:34:30', NULL),
(1843, 524, 766, 'Peter\'s apostolic confession confirmed that Jesus was the Christ. Peters affirmations of Jesus. as christ was a direct revelation from God\r\n\r\nPeters\'s. confession is recorded in three gospels Mathew 16.15to17, Mark 8.27 to 30, and Luke 9.18to20.\r\nThrough the nature of the miracles and through the teaching and so peter get it and recognized that Jesus is indeed the messiah.\r\nIt was an authoritative prophetic revelation from God as such it was an infallible confirmation of the fact that Jesus really was the Christ.\r\n\r\nEven when Jesus was revealed to his disciples in glory Jesus took Peter James and John up on a mountain to pray. Moses and Elijah appeared with Jesus.. Jesus was the Davidic heir who was bringing gods kingdom to earth\r\n\r\nThe event is recorded in mt 17.1-8 Mark 9.2-8 and luke 9.28-36 it is also reffered in 2 peter 1.16-18.\r\n\r\nChange of his appearance at the voice of God heard from heaven that Jesus is His Son and the elijha was the appearance of Moses and Elijah was fulfilling the expectations set by the greatest leaders of Israel past.\r\n\r\nThe identity in these ways through amazing transfiguration.', 8, '2020-08-31 05:50:35', '2020-09-08 00:34:55', NULL),
(1844, 524, 767, 'Jesus fasted for forty days in the desert before being tempted by satan - Jesus temptation by Satan paralleled the temptation of Adam and Eve.\r\n\r\nThe purpose of his temptation there are three important faceted of Jesus temptations \r\nfirst obedience as Heb 5.8 and 9\r\nJesus learned obedience from what he suffered and once made perfect he became the source of eternal salvation for all who obey him.\r\n\r\nJesus had to learn God\'s righteousness requirement and to overcome challenges and temptations.\r\n\r\nAnd the second idea is that gave him sympathy for his people. Jesus grew in compassion and understanding for us as we suffer as struggle with temptations.\r\n\r\nwe do not. have a high priest who is unable to sympathize with our weakness, but we have one who has been tempted in every way just as we are yet was without sin Heb 4.15.\r\n\r\nAnd the third idea we will mention in relation to Jesus\' temptation is his impeccability.\r\nInability to sin Jesus never sinned Jesus was not capable of sinning because he is impeccable his obedience and sympathy are increased.\r\n\r\nsince he learned perfectly from the experience and now responds to us in a way that is perfectly suited for our needs.', 8, '2020-08-31 06:24:07', '2020-09-08 00:34:55', NULL),
(1845, 524, 768, 'A form of the death penalty use in the ancient roman empire Jesus crucifixion served as an atoning offering for sin.\r\nas the Christ, it was his responsibility to dies on behalf of his people as we read in Heb 9.11 to 28.\r\nThere are far too many doctrines associated with the crucification. we will bring two main ways one the imputation of our sin to Jesus and the fact that he died as a result it of divine judgement against sin.   By imputed our sin to Jesus God counted Jesus as if he had personally committed every sin imputed to him.\r\n\r\nJesus. act in which God assigned the guilt of sinners to the persons of Jesus \r\nJesus offered Himself on the cross as a substitute for his people our sacrifices Romans 3,25 Eph 5,2\r\n\r\nas per the patterns of the ot sin offering jesus offered on the cross as substitute for His people. \r\nHuman death is always a divine judgment agant sin. before god laid our guilt on him once our sin was imputed to him on hthe cross his death', 8, '2020-08-31 06:43:43', '2020-09-08 00:34:55', NULL),
(1846, 524, 769, 'There is two major accomplishment happened through Jesus resurrection.\r\none plan of redemption and the second blessing of salvation.\r\nredemption depended on god fulfilling his covenant promises to establish his kingdom on earth.\r\nGod\'s anointed Christ conquered death for all of us. when he rose from the grave through the power of the spirit he proved to all creation that he really is gods favoured son and the heir of his kingdom and even more wonderful is that he ensured that future resurrection and blessings of all his faithful followers.\r\nThe resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead is the central point of the new testament out of it falls many blessings. The resurrection teaches us he Jesus is like messiah the Lord, the son of God.\r\nThe key things that Jesus is alive today and since someone, who can know and meet now and risen power is available to us.\r\n\r\nGods pledge to renew his creation. it is the resurrection which gives us that clue and the confidence Romans 8\r\n\r\nGods pledge that death is not the end and very hopeful. a resurrected body being in Christ Jesus\r\n\r\nJesus resurrection was a critical step that enables god to fulfil his covenant promises.', 8, '2020-08-31 07:00:57', '2020-09-08 00:34:55', NULL),
(1847, 524, 770, 'We can affirm and confess that Jesus is the Christ in our present circumstances and areas of influences like sharing the kingdom\'s purpose of Jesus\' incarnation to this world for redemption purposes.\r\n\r\nAlso resurrected Jesus\' blessings can bring glory and hope to the people who lost due to their sin and the guilt of sin committed by Adam and Eve.\r\n\r\nJesus who establishes the peace to every human who approaches. Victory through life offered by Jesus in his gospel messages is very essential to the circumstances of the present world. \r\n\r\nsending Holy spirit to and all prophetic words mighty way influence people to come out from the corrupted surrounding and deeds.', 8, '2020-08-31 07:15:41', '2020-09-08 00:34:55', NULL),
(1848, 529, 681, 'Investigating the original meaning of a biblical passage involves exploring the text as if it were still within the historical circumstances of its writer and first audience. This kind of exploration requires a lot of research, careful thinking and imagination. In other words, it requires a lot of human effort because biblical documents no longer exist in their original settings. Bible is organically inspired by God. The Holy Spirit chose to communicate his word through the personalities, experiences, emotion and patterns of thought of human biblical writers. And there are several places in the Bible where the importance of the human writers is mentioned explicitly. \r\nThe Holy Spirit chose to communicate his word through human writers. Focusing on the human writer helps us understand many features of Scripture. Human writer helps us understand many features of scripture. Scripture demonstrates how important it is for us to focus not just on God as the ultimate author of Scripture, but also on the human writers he inspired. And that means that we have to learn as much as we can about the situations, personalities, experiences, skills and intentions of these writers.', 8, '2020-08-31 15:38:54', '2020-09-08 00:35:24', NULL),
(1849, 529, 682, 'The Holy Spirit inspired human authors to write scripture. The doctrine of organic inspiration extends only to the original texts of scripture, only those documents have the full authority of God himself. The changes that have taken place in these texts as they have been copied over the centuries are not inspire by God, and neither are the translations of those texts. Responses to objections made about copies and translations of Scripture. \r\nThe original documents of the Old Testament didn\'t exist in Jesus\' day. Jesus and his apostles believed that the scriptures that had were trustworthy. Many decades of scholarly research devoted to studying and comparing ancient copies of scripture are available today. The doctrine of accommodation implies that everything in scripture- including things like its words, grammar and literary style- rose out of the cultural and linguistic conventions of its day. Literary devices and conventions demonstrate the importance of accommodations in the original documents of Scripture, and encourage us to focus on similar issues in our investigation of original meaning.', 8, '2020-08-31 15:47:38', '2020-09-08 00:35:24', NULL),
(1850, 529, 683, 'Manuscript simply means an original document or piece of writing. It is interactive way to read and study the various passages within the Bible. It is a privilege for our age to have access to the manuscripts that contain the original words of Scripture as it brings out the original words and meanings of the conversations. It is an engaging, challenging and fun way to learn and understand the Bible. I feel that with the manuscript study, it draws strength, encouragement and truth from His written word. Since, these manuscripts are easily accessible the chances of false teachings and wrong interpretations are considerably reduced.A bible student would find it easy through manuscripts to learn, to teach, to preach and propagate the Word of God more confidently. And more importantly, the truth is brought to the people of God.', 8, '2020-08-31 16:03:14', '2020-09-08 00:35:24', NULL),
(1851, 529, 684, 'When we interpret the Bible, we are the subjects, and the object of our study is the Bible. Three major approaches towards the object and subjects of knowledge are, \r\nFirst, some people tend toward an approach we call objectivism. Objectivists believe that under the right circumstances, it\'s possible to arrive at impartial or objective knowledge. \r\nSecond, other people tend toward an approach called subjectivism. Subjectivists believe that our knowledge is always influenced by our personal biases, making impartial objectivity impossible. \r\nAnd third, some people have found a middle ground that we might call dialogism. This approach emphasizes the constant \'\'dialog\'\' or interplay between objective reality and our subjective perspectives. All three of these approaches have been used in biblical interpretation.', 8, '2020-08-31 16:09:30', '2020-09-08 00:35:24', NULL),
(1852, 529, 685, 'Scientific Rationalism; Objectivism can be identified with the most prominent current in the stream of modern philosophy- the current we\'ll call scientific rationalism. Rene Descartes, who lived from 1596 to 1650, is often called the father of modern rationalism because he promoted reason as the supreme judge of truth. Francis Bacon [1561- 1626], the father of modern science, applied rational, logical thinking to the study of the physical world.\r\nStructuralism; Structuralists tried to use rational and scientific objectivity to obtain an exhaustive understanding of everything they studied. The concepts of rationality and science have changed in a variety of ways. But the fundamental assumption of objectivism has remained the same, specifically; by following rational scientific analysis, we can arrive at objective knowledge. In the twentieth century, modern objectivism was taken to the extreme by broad philosophical outlook known as structuralism. Structuralists tried to use rational and scientific objectivity to obtain an exhaustive understanding of everything they studied- including sociology, art, language and literature.', 8, '2020-08-31 16:17:58', '2020-09-08 00:35:24', NULL),
(1853, 529, 686, '1. Authority dialog and objective- Objective and subjective approaches to meaning oppose each other in some fundamentals ways, but they have something very important in common. In the extremes, both models ultimately make the authority of interpreters equal to or even greater than the authority of the Bible itself. Objectivism tends to over estimate how reliable to our rational and scientifically objective views are. Subjectivism tends to overestimate how reliable our personal intuitions and opinions are. But in both cases the result is the same; I acknowledge that objective truth can be found in text of scripture. The authority- dialog model helps us avoid thinking that we can be utterly objective when we approach the scriptures. \r\n2. Authority- Dialog and Subjective- The authority dialog model resembles objective models in some ways, it also has similarities with subjective models. It acknowledges that we all come to the Scriptures with perspectives and beliefs that influence the way we interpret biblical passages. Moreover, it agrees with scripture and subjectivism that the personal, subjective input we bring to interpretation is valuable. If we don\'t submit our subjectivity to the authority of scripture, our interpretations of the Bible will be severely hindered. Investigating the bible is a lifelong process in which Scripture  changes us and causes to grow and mature in our Christian faith.', 9, '2020-08-31 16:31:01', '2020-09-08 00:35:24', NULL),
(1854, 530, 834, 'The Scripture is God\'s voice , his living, active word to every generation. God has all authority , therefore, whenever and however he speaks , all who hear him are obligated to obey him. The Bible claims divine authority for itself in at least two ways ways.\r\nFirst it provides historical examples f its authority.\r\nGenesis 2- 3 in the account of creation and fall in Genesis, God commanded man to cultivate the Garden of Eden and not to eat the forbidden fruit, following Even listening to Serpent\'s spoken word , then Adam listening to Eve\'s spoken word and thereby rejecting God\'s word .God enforced his spoken word \'s authority by punishing Adam and Eve, all creations with them\r\nExodus 24:4-8 we see that God\'s spoken word is the basis for his written word and the written word is God\'s authoritative covenant document that his people are obligated to obey.\r\n And second it explicitly claims authority \r\nThe New testament  also confirms the authority of Scripture through its examples.John 17:12\r\nJesus speaks of his eleven loyal disciples and the one who betrayed him, indicating that both his protection of the eleven and his losing of one were in accordance with the Scripture.\r\nRomans 12:19 says that Paul\'s argument here assumes that the Old Testament carries authority when it assigns vengeance to God. \r\nIMPLICATIONS\r\n1. God\'s people must keep the breadth of biblical instructions. \r\n2. God\'s word has authority over us not just in the full breadth of its teaching but also in the depth of obedience.\r\n3. Scripture indicates that the moral requirements God places on us are based in his love for us and we should fulfill in in His love', 8, '2020-09-01 17:51:45', '2020-09-12 03:14:38', NULL),
(1855, 530, 835, 'Scripture is also necessary for our ethical living. The biblical model for making ethical decisions may be summed up as Ethical judgement involves application of God;s word to a situation by a person.\r\n\'We must act on a proper understanding of our moral standard , our goals and our motives or to put it another way , on normative, situational and existential concerns.\'while understanding the power of scripture, it empowers us to live for God,. Constant learning and meditation on the word of God brings us into contact with the power of God that will always accomplish his purposes.\r\nIn relation with the authority of Scripture, both the Old Testament and New Testament , the Bible connects obedience with love  for God. the basis of duty is the fact that God has called us in love and authority to be his willing servants.\r\nWe see that according to the Bible, we cannot do the right thing unless we have the right motive . When we embrace the Scripture deeply from the heart we can rightly submit to the authority of God .', 8, '2020-09-01 18:08:45', '2020-09-12 03:14:38', NULL),
(1856, 530, 836, 'When God inspired and authorized the writers of Scripture, he had a particular goal in mind. he wanted to give his people clear revelation concerning his will and his character.\r\nScripture speaks so plainly about the gospel that every mentally competent person should be able to figure out that everybody does figure that salvation comes through repentance and faith in Christ.\r\nGod has revealed his will to us sufficiently clear to guide us in ethics. He has given us the Bible so that through due use of the ordinary means through reading and studying , we can come to know God\'swill for all the ares of our life. 2 Timothy 3:16\r\nAll scripture is a clear enough to be useful if we apply ourselves to study it diligently.\r\nIf we apply ourselves sufficiently, we can all come to know God \'s will well enough to conform ourselves to his standard for morality.', 8, '2020-09-01 18:21:12', '2020-09-12 03:14:38', NULL),
(1857, 530, 837, 'Romans 1:15-16 says the I am so eager to preach the gospel . because it is the power of God for the salvation of everyone who believes. We see that the power of God\'s word is through the uninspired preaching of His word or the Gospel. The New Testament frequently confirms this idea when it says that God works through the preaching of the gospel even when the preachers are not infallibly inspired.\r\nPaul indicates here that the preached gospel carries God\'s power.\r\nThe gospel Paul had in mind here was not just a set of truths about what Jesus had done, nor was it the power of God  represented by the statements of the gospel   .\r\n. Paul says that the preaching of Gospel is powerful, because God uses preaching to bring to faith.\r\nIts a message us to people may count the gospel message as foolish because they do not believe that its statements are true, or it may seem to them like a fanatic late or a even a lie. \r\nIt is for this reason that the gospel seems like foolishness to unbelievers. But to people who believe the message, the preaching of the gospel is the power of God because it is the means by which God brings them to  saving knowledge of the truth. so we should also preach it to all around us', 9, '2020-09-01 18:36:09', '2020-09-12 03:14:38', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(1858, 530, 838, 'The bible displays the full range of language that we find in all human communication. It contains statements, questions,promises, offers, curses, blessings, threats, judgments, quotations, summations, commands, descriptions, cries of despair, love and much more.\r\nThe Bible includes both sarcasm and sincere language.\r\nEXTRAORDINARY:\r\nIn the middle ages, many theologians believed that because the Bible is inspired by God, it communicates in extraordinary ways that exceed human comprehension . Many Christians also believe that Scripture;s language is extraordinary , which makes its language easy to interpret\r\nORDINARY:\r\nMATTHEW 6:11\r\nThese statements are imperatives but when we say these words , we are not ordinarily issuing commands. Amos 5:5  we see that Amos spoke sarcastically, meaning just the opposite of what he said.He didn\'t want them to sin in these places , but to stop sinning in them.\r\nThis means that if we are to interpret the Bible responsibly, we have to learn how they ordinarily used language and we have to under stand what each author\'s intent was when he wrote.', 9, '2020-09-01 18:53:47', '2020-09-12 03:14:38', NULL),
(1859, 530, 839, 'The Ten Commandments are listed in Exodus 20 and in Deuteronomy 5. The primacy of the Ten commandments is both historical and theological. Their historical primacy depends on the fact that , to our knowledge , these was were the first written legal code that was received by the nation Of Israel. \r\nPaul referred to the giving of the Ten Commandments as the introduction of the Law.\r\nin this way, Israel,became the first nation to possess an extensive, supernaturally revealed code of God\'s holy requirements.\r\nDeuteronomy 9:10. God himself wrote the ten commandments, which confirms that these were special among his laws and deserved special attention and notice.\r\nThe Theological primacy of then ten commandments  also indicated by the special occasion on which Israel received them. The giving of the laws was attended by thunder and lightening, smoke, clouds and heavenly trumpets.\r\nIt is also emphasized in Deuteronomy 4:13 where Moses identified the Ten commandments as God\'s very covenant with his people.Exodus 4:20 says that the Ten commandments were also placed within the ark of the covenant, God\'s footstool.', 8, '2020-09-01 19:07:14', '2020-09-12 03:14:38', NULL),
(1860, 530, 840, 'The old testament bible into three main types :\r\nMoral Law, ceremonial law and civil law \r\nMoral laws are typically thought to convey God\'s ethical standards and are usually identified with the ten commandments.\r\nCivil laws provide for the governing of society, especially during the Israel\'s theocracy.\r\nCeremonial laws are those which provide instruction for worshiping God.\r\nSince death , burial, resurrection and ascension of Christ , God\'s people are no longer  to perform many of the specific behavior that were required under the Mosaic sacrificial an temple system.. We are no longer  to maintain the temple or to restrict human and Gentiles from access to God\'s holy presence or to sacrifice animals for our sin,. Christ fulfilled the ceremonial  aspects of the law. We are to follow them by trusting Christ as our sacrifice and by worshiping him by spirit and truth.\r\nChrist fulfills the civil aspect of the law, but we live rightly under respective earthly governments and also directly honoring Christ as a king and by keeping his commandments.\r\nChrist fulfills the moral aspects of the law, we must also conform ourselves to Christ;s image and example seeking to live as morally as He did.', 9, '2020-09-01 19:24:21', '2020-09-12 03:14:38', NULL),
(1861, 530, 841, 'All of God\'s laws remains our standard for morality and we are obligated to apply all of God\'s law to our modern situation. The ceremonial principles of the law are still binding, and we are to follow them by trusting Christ as our sacrifice and by worshiping in Spirit and truth. \r\nAs per following civil laws and the church, which is his nation on the earth, bound to obey these aspects not only  by living rightly under respective earthly governments, which are under Christ\'s greater Lordship, but also by directly honoring Christ as king .\r\nWe are no longer to maintain the temple, or to restrict women and gentiles from access to God\'s holy presence or to sacrifice animals for our sins.', 8, '2020-09-01 19:34:14', '2020-09-12 03:14:38', NULL),
(1862, 531, 687, 'The famous theologian Thomas Aquinas, who lived from around 1225 to 1275, championed a much more responsible approach to Quadriga. Unlike many of his predecessors and contemporaries, he insisted that the literal sense is the singular meaning of Scripture. He also taught that nothing necessary to faith was communicated as spiritual meaning without being taught elsewhere in scripture in the literal sense. Not all scholars would agree that Aquinas always followed these principles as he interpreted the scriptures, but nevertheless he insisted the principle that every sense of a passage of scripture must be tied to its literal meanings. The meaning of scripture is multifaceted. Each passage\'s meanings has many smaller parts of aspects that contribute to the singular unified meaning we\'ve called its literal sense. But the most responsible approach to the richness of scriptures is to ensure that everything we say about a biblical passage is tied to its grammar set within the historical context of the ancient world.', 8, '2020-09-04 15:39:25', '2020-09-08 00:35:46', NULL),
(1863, 531, 688, 'Biblical Elaborations are places where one part of scripture directly or indirectly comments on an aspect of the meaning of another passage in scripture, these elaborations always accord with and confirm original meaning.\r\n1] The first biblical elaboration of this passage is primarily a repetition of these exact words in Deuteronomy 5, where Moses reminded the nation of Israel of the content of Ten Commandments. In Deuteronomy 5.17, scripture again says, You shall not murder. This repetition confirmed the commandment and reminded God\'s people of the term of his covenant. \r\n2] The second type of elaboration is clarification, and we find clarification of commandment against murder in Numbers 35. In that chapter, Moses distinguished between murder and accidental manslaughter.\r\n3] The third type of biblical elaboration was expansion, in which scripture provides additional information about the passage or topic it references. We find an expansion of commandment against murder in Matthew 5, where Jesus criticized the rabbis of his day for wrongly limiting the commandment\'s scope', 8, '2020-09-04 15:50:29', '2020-09-08 00:35:46', NULL),
(1864, 531, 689, 'Interpretation is simply trying to understand what the text says, in short, hermeneutics. Interpretation that does not somehow relate what is being displayed or described to something within the personality or experience of the visitor will be sterile. The aim of interpretation is not instruction, but provocation. It should stimulate people into form of action. Thus we should also prevent it from being misapplying in our sphere of influence too. We should first ask for the guidance of the Holy Spirit to help us think correctly, lest we distort the scriptures. The goal should be understanding the Author\'s Intended meaning and must follow principles derived from God\'s Word. It shouldn\'t be of what we\'re meaning it to be, thus preventing from misapplication.', 8, '2020-09-04 16:07:00', '2020-09-08 00:35:46', NULL),
(1865, 531, 690, 'The writer, the document, and the audience are interdependent guides to meaning. If we fail to account for their interdependence, it\'s very easy to fall into error. We need guidance from all of these sources so that our readings of Scripture aren\'t skewed by an imbalanced emphasis on just one or two. The three interpretive fallacies are \r\nIntentional fallacy- If we overemphasize the author, we often fall into an intentional fallacy. An intentional fallacy relies too heavily on what we think we know about a writer and his intentions, and de-emphasizes the things we learn about document and audience. \r\nGraphic fallacy- over emphasizes the document itself to the relative exclusion of contextual considerations like writer and audience. \r\nAffective fallacy- Overemphasizes the audience and focuses too heavily on how scripture affects the audience.', 8, '2020-09-04 16:14:41', '2020-09-08 00:35:46', NULL),
(1866, 531, 691, 'Normally a summary will come from a particular vantage point or emphasize a particular concept that appears in the passage. Since every passage has a complex meaning, summaries help us by narrowing our study, allowing us to focus on just a portion of what the passage has to say. Multiple legitimate summaries bring us closer and closer to the passage\'s full meaning. One student summarizes how characters developed in the story. One summarizes cultural values of the day. Another summarizes the events in chronological order. All of these responses are legitimate summaries of the presentation\'s meaning. But not the full meaning of the entire thing. So multiple summaries help us focus on individual aspects of meaning and allows us learn the whole picture. And taken together, it brings us closer and closer to the passage\'s full meaning.', 8, '2020-09-04 16:22:03', '2020-09-08 00:35:46', NULL),
(1867, 533, 826, 'Unlike many other ethical system our definition focus on God and his blessing rather than on terms like good and evil,or right or wrong ,those this that recive Gods blessings are right ,where bas those things that do not reiceve Gods blessings are wrong and evil ,By focoucing on God and his blessing in these way we meant to say two things First God\'s nature is the standared of the morality ,second God,s action demonstrate the standard of the morality .\r\n  God him self is the ultimate standared of the right snd wrong ,of good and evil,insaying this we deny that ultimate morality is standard of out side God ,The second things we meant to say that by focusing on God and his blessing is God\'s action demonstrate the standard of the morality ,one of the chefe way God shows his aprovel is bestowing blessin g on it ,similarly he shows his haterd for what is wrong and evil by with holding blessings and pouring out curses .', 0, '2020-09-07 06:15:40', '2020-09-07 06:15:40', NULL),
(1868, 533, 827, 'Unless a work is done with right motive ,it is not a work that God will reward with blessing ,first it must proceed with a heart that purified by faith Second action must flow by christian love ,work prosed from a heart purified by faith canot please God ,this critierion of the right motive closely associated with the way our deffenition of christian ethics focuses on good person with good nature,only believers who are indwell by holy spirit  can do work that God rewards with blessing .unless our attempt to seek God\'s blessing are founded on faith ,we canot please God and therefor canot be rewarded by God  ,Second love , consider that in  corinthiance 13 Paul says our work are usless unless they are motivated by by Love ,work and even spiritual gifts that produce benificial results merit no reward if thery are not produced by Love.', 0, '2020-09-07 06:30:56', '2020-09-07 06:30:56', NULL),
(1869, 533, 828, 'To describe three fold criteria for good work our approach will touch on three matters  ,First Three tendencies of different christian group  ,Second Three perspective of ethical decision making , third the inter dependence of these perspective .\r\n  Tendencies :there are many different ways that believers  try to make ethical choice in life ,but they tend to fall in main tree categories , some emphasis our christian consciousness and the leading of the holy spirit , other emphasis scripture , and other emphasis the out come of the action ,\r\n  Perspective :ethical judgments involves the application of Gods word to a situation a person ,we mentioned Gods word because the divine revelation is the stranded or norm  by we must mesur all judjment,\r\n  Independence:in the first place consider what is involved inthe situational perspective ,the situation involves all the relevent facts of the ethical questians we are considering .', 0, '2020-09-07 06:49:20', '2020-09-07 06:49:20', NULL),
(1870, 533, 829, 'Three different perspective or approach towards every ethical judgement , The situational perspective , The normative perspective ,and the existential perspective ,\r\nSituational : when our ethical inquiries turn to the problem themselves or to the consequences of  action or the goals ,we are doing ethics from the situational perspective , this approche may called \'teleological\' because this focus on the ed or the result of the action, approaching ethics from the situational perspective involves the nothing the relation of means to end in the relation of God  \r\n      Normative :perhaps the most intutive perspective of  christian is what we called is normative perspective ,normative reffers the facts that God\'s word is the norm,or standard for ethics ,we are doing normative perspective ethics when we look to the bible what tyells us to do .\r\n      Existential :when we aproch ethics bya sking questions that are specific to the people involves wenare doing ethics from existential perspective', 0, '2020-09-07 07:06:20', '2020-09-07 07:06:20', NULL),
(1871, 533, 830, 'In addition to being the absolute moral standard we wills ee that the God is also the absolute judge of the morality ,that is he has the ultimate prerogative to determine whether or not particular action ,emotions and thoughts,meet or transgress his moral requirement,and he has the ultimate power to act on his determination .it is true that God deligates some power to human being some responsibility to making ethical decision, for incest according to scripture  legetimate human government are given  to honer good and punish evil.but also bible teaches us that human judgement are only correct and valid insofar they mirror to God\'s judgment .  its God\'s right to judge because he has absolute authority and his judgement are in inescapable becouse he has absolute power ,In the final analysis ther are only two options ,either we submit ourselves to him as our judge seeking mercy through Christ ,or we defy him and suffer eternal punishment   .', 0, '2020-09-07 07:21:32', '2020-09-07 07:21:32', NULL),
(1872, 533, 831, 'To understanding of christian ethics we must come to grip with the fact that God reveled him self in three ways  ,traditional theologian have spoken of god\'s revelation primerly in two categories, special revelation and general revelation   ,inn the category of special revelation they have placed direct communication form God such as scripture ,prophasy dreams and visions ,the catogory of genaral revelation are include such things as history ,universe ,weather ,plants animals and human beings ,this traditional aproch will helf full in some ways  ,its tends to keep our attention from some important demonition of God\'s revelation .so we will aslo speak existential revelation,God\'s evelation in person,revelation that is often grouped with genaral revelation but wich realy deserves to be treated seperatly .', 0, '2020-09-07 07:34:24', '2020-09-07 07:34:24', NULL),
(1873, 533, 832, 'Existential revelation the idea that God reveal him self in and through the person has always been recognized by the main stream of protestant theology as the part of general revelation here nwe are not intruding a new kind of revelation,but simply a different way of categorizing the same theologian has accepted\r\nin the first place existential revalation divided in to two category, external aspect of existential revaleation and internal aspect of existential relavation   \r\nExternal aspects  of existentian revelation include such as humans judgement both individual and corporate ,as a form of revelation human created of image of God .human being are the images that reflects god\'s glory and dignity \r\nInternal :there also internal type of existantial revelation ,we might think of the many ways tha holy spirit work  within human beings to reveal the work of God', 0, '2020-09-07 07:50:07', '2020-09-07 07:50:07', NULL),
(1874, 533, 833, 'If we walk in the light ,as he him self is the light ,we have fellowship with one another ,and the blood of Jesus his son purify us from all sin , john :7, This metaphore God as light is primeryly a moral evaluation , darkness is equated with sin and lie,light with purifes from sin ,it is the pictur of God as perfectly free from the sin in his very nature, here john tells us to be in light walk with light thatr we amy ave fellowship with holy /God ,holiness is his standers , sinless is his standard , the same way we have fellowhiop with one another , becose when we do this we do the same same things what god teach and show us , by this we god will purify us through the blood of Christ Jesus , being in light , telling truth is the standard of God , God want we do that , if some one walk inthe light means we walk in god , the our stnadersd should chane , out ethic will cahge , our prsperctives will change  .', 0, '2020-09-07 08:02:22', '2020-09-07 08:02:22', NULL),
(1875, 534, 692, 'God is immutable, meaning that he doesn\'t change. Since God is immutable. The biblical concept of divine immutability doesn\'t imply that God is inactive. But the God of Scripture is constantly interacting with his creation is real and meaningful ways. \r\n\r\n1. Eternal Counsel- Christian traditions understand God\'s eternal plan differently, everything God has done, is doing, and will do is part of a unified plan. God knows everything, and he is using that knowledge to direct history towards the ends for which he created it God\'s eternal counsel, or ultimate plan for history, is immutable and directs history toward the ends for which he created it.\r\n\r\n2. Character - God reveals different aspects of his character more prominently at some times than others. Sometimes he displays his mercy, sometimes his wrath. Sometimes he reveals his omniscience and other times he hides it. But the full range of his attributes- his eternal nature- always stays the same. God\'s character, his essence, persons and attributes, never change.\r\n\r\n3. Covenant Promises- Every revelation of God in scripture assumes that God will keep his covenant and his covenant promises. The original audiences were supposed to understand every passage of scripture in this light, and modern audiences should do the same. Where God hasn\'t made a promise, his words are best understood as threats of curse and offers of blessing.', 9, '2020-09-07 15:40:45', '2020-09-08 00:36:13', NULL),
(1876, 534, 693, 'There are at least three ways in which modern people are very similar to the people who first received the scriptures. First, all human beings, no matter when or where they live, are sinful images of God. Second, we suffer religious divisions. and third, humanity still includes the same classes of people. \r\n1. Sinful Images- God created humanity in his image, but we have fallen into sin. All recipients of scripture, whether ancient or modern, share the same sinful nature.\r\n2. Religious Divisions- Both the original and modern audiences of scripture suffer religious divisions. Readers of scripture fall into one of three religious groups; Unbelievers- who refuse to submit to God. False believers- people who make superficial commitments to God. Believers- who make faithful commitments to God. \r\n3. Classes- the same classes of people exist for both the original and modern audiences. Many portions of scripture are directed toward particular classes. The connections we share with the classes of people that exist in every age can help guide our application of Scripture.', 8, '2020-09-07 15:47:51', '2020-09-08 00:36:13', NULL),
(1877, 534, 694, 'The developments between original and modern audiences should influence our application. We need to account for the epochal developments of redemptive history when we apply the Bible to modern life. \r\nThe Bible\'s perspective on world history in three stages; \r\nCreation- the progressive nature of God\'s rule over creation has resulted in periodic developments that create discontinuity between the various epochs mentioned in scripture. When God first made the world. But theologians also commonly identify epochs according to God\'s various covenants throughout the Bible, especially those associated with Adam, Noah, Abraham, Moses and David in the Old Testament, and with Jesus in the New Testament. \r\nFall- when humanity first committed sin and was cursed by God. \r\nRedemption- the period following the fall, in which God redeems us from our sin. Soon after Adam and Eve fell into sin, God began a long slow process of redemption. And throughout the millennia, he had mercifully built his kingdom of redemption within and alongside the cursed creation.', 8, '2020-09-07 15:56:01', '2020-09-08 00:36:13', NULL),
(1878, 534, 695, 'Significant theological changes are the basis for identifying epochal divisions. Each epoch is period of time characterized by substantial and long lasting transitions in Old Testament theology. Time doesn\'t pass in sharply segmented periods. So, transitions between epochs generally took place gradually. And the epochs themselves often overlapped. The Old Testament reports many theological changes that took place throughout history. Theological changes occurred every time God altered his expectations regarding the concepts, behaviors and emotions of his people. And when the changes were significant enough, they became the basis for identifying epochal divisions. In similar way, theologians obviously tend to use theological criteria to delineate the epochs. But they still don\'t always agree on the divisions because theology within the Old Testament developed in different ways at different times. In a similar way, some parts of Old Testament theology advanced slowly, others proceeded at a medium pace, and others changed rapidly. And many of these parts did their growing at different times.', 9, '2020-09-07 16:04:53', '2020-09-08 00:36:13', NULL),
(1879, 534, 696, 'The divisions of the Old Testament make it clear that God wanted his people to apply theological themes in different ways at different times. And just as Old Testament believers weren\'t supposed to serve God as if they lived in earlier periods of history, New Testament believers should never apply the scriptures as if they live in earlier periods of history. Once God commanded a new way for sacrifice in worship, he expected his people never to return to the old ways. Christ\'s sacrifice has superseded every earlier form of sacrifice [Hebrews 8.13]\r\nAs people living under the new covenant, we follow Jesus the great son of David, as he leads his people into war against the forces of evil. Another striking example is the theme of leadership in battle. Imagine that you live in the period of David\'s dynastic covenant. You know that God has ordained the kings of Israel to lead his people into war against evil. The kings receive direction from God, and in turn direct the ways that you participate in war. \r\nGod has always expected his people to serve him in ways that were appropriate to the covenant age in which they lived. So, understanding how Old Testament history divided into major covenant epoch is essential for applying the scriptures in our day.', 9, '2020-09-07 16:14:58', '2020-09-08 00:36:13', NULL),
(1880, 532, 842, 'Special , general and existential revelation differ in some respects , .the three types of situational content of God\'s revelation is Facts, Means and Goals\r\nFacts:\r\nthese facts include everything that include everything that reveals about our situation, such as events ,people  , objects, ideas , duties and actions-even god and his revelation.God is our ultimate fact , our ultimate ethical environment. the reality of God\'s existence rules over every ethical decision and obligates us to live by the standard of his character.\r\nGoals\r\nGoals are intended or potential outcomes of thoughts, words and deeds.They are the ends for which we do things or for which we ought to do things. Our ultimate goal must be to do it all for the glory of God. God\' s glory in creation reveals that we must be loyal to God and that we must praise Him that we must glorify him in all that we do . It teaches us to set God\'s glory as our highest goal.\r\n\r\nMeans :are the ways of reaching our goals. They include everything we might think, say or do and any tool pr method that we might use in order to accomplish our objectives. One of the main ways Scripture teaches us about ethical means is by giving us examples to consider . On the one hand , we find ,many negative examples of people who  did not perform so admirably. But on the other hand we also find many positive examples of people who properly understood God\'s norms .', 8, '2020-09-07 17:50:50', '2020-09-08 00:37:00', NULL),
(1881, 532, 843, 'Facts include everything that God reveals about situation , such as events, people ,objects, ideas, duties, actions -even God and his revelation.\r\nGod is our ultimate fact , our ultimate ethical environment. The reality of God\'s existence rules over every ethical questions and obligate us to live by his standard of his character.\r\n Through revelation ,God tells us facts about himself and facts about what he requires.\r\nGod is the supreme authority over all creation. his authority is absolute and his character is the perfect expression of his will. So when he reveals his character, that revelation is the means through which God exercises control much like human governments exercise control through their laws. Just as human being s obey civil laws , all creation must obey God\'s laws by bowing to his authority.', 8, '2020-09-07 18:00:53', '2020-09-08 00:37:00', NULL),
(1882, 532, 844, 'Goals are the intended or potential outcomes of thoughts, words and deeds.they are the ends for which we do things or for which ought to do things. Our goals can be small or large. They give direction to our actions. \r\nSpecial revelation gives us countless goals that must be considered in Christian ethics. on of he main goals special revelation teaches us . it presents God\'s glory as the highest and most important .\r\n1 Corinthians  10:31\r\nGeneral revelation also identifies many goals that are good and evil. It also teaches us that the greatest goal is to glorify and thank God. Romans 1:20,21\r\nExistential revelation also helps us to discern good goal from evil goals ,especially through our consciences.Holy Spirit is another source of existential revelation moving within us so that we pursue good goals and shun evil goal. Philippians 2:13\r\nSo it is important to understand Biblical goals revealed in all three revelations if we want to make biblical decisions.', 8, '2020-09-07 18:12:02', '2020-09-08 00:37:00', NULL),
(1883, 532, 845, 'When Christians are inclined to follow a rigorous strategy toward revelation, they are extremely concerned to guard against sin, especially as it is defined in the prohibitions listed in scripture. As a result , we tend to err on the side of overly restriction behavior than on the side of permitting it.\r\nChristian who endorse a rigorous strategy mistakenly believe that when the Bible\'s facts a, goals and means appear to be vague, the proper response is to apply scripture in restrictive ways.\r\nConsequences:\r\nIt destroys Christian freedom by prohibiting behaviors that are wrong under certain conditions.\r\nThe bible teaches us that Christians have certain freedom of conscience.\r\nSecond a strategy of rigor also inspires despair in believers by turning god\'s word into a burden.\r\nSo in order to avoid falling into this strategy we must realize that modern situations are sufficiently different from biblical situations so that we cannot exactly  do it as it is.\r\nWe can also avoid the strategy of rigor by remembering that Scripture is always sufficiently clear to communicate God\'s will with regard to Christian ethics.', 9, '2020-09-07 18:28:07', '2020-09-08 00:37:00', NULL),
(1884, 532, 846, 'From Genesis to revelation, Scripture reveals that god is the king over all creation. The ultimate goal of history is to display God\'s kingship and his kingdom.\r\nThree specific times , Jesus spoke of the kingdom of God as the goal of ethics during the Sermon on the Mount. \r\nBeatitudes:\r\nA Beatitude is a statement about blessedness. Matthew 5:3-12\r\nIn Mathew 5:3, the blessing was theirs is the kingdom of heaven\r\nin verse -5, they will inherit the earth, this was also a kingdom blessing because it referred to the new earth that god will create when his kingdom comes in all its fullness.\r\nIn verse 9, the blessing was they will be called sons of god, this refers to the kingship and kingdom of God.\r\nLORD\'S PRAYER(MATHEW 6:19)\r\nOurs father in heaven , remind us of the royal father , the divine king enthroned in heaven, the great father of this empire.\r\nHallowed be your name, that all creatures would bow to God because of his unsurpassed kingly authority.\r\nyour kingdom come, Jesus exhorted his disciples to pray for the fulfillment of God\'s kingdom on earth\r\nEARTHLY NEEDS:\r\nMATHEW 6:31-33\r\nOF all the goals we have in life, our first or primary concern should be the glorification of God through the triumph pf his kingdom on earth.', 9, '2020-09-07 18:44:20', '2020-09-08 00:37:00', NULL),
(1885, 532, 847, 'There are three main components of the Kingdom of God. They are \r\n1. King-\r\nGod is the ruler of this kingdom, but since we haven\'t lived under a king , its difficult to understand the authority of a human king.\r\nIn the ancient world of the Bible, people were very familiar with kings and kingdoms. They were to protect  and provide for them , and to treat them with kindness. Good kings ruled wisely to benefit their people.God\'s supreme rule as the king over all is a major theme that runs throughout the Bible.\r\n\r\n2. People-\r\nThe bible speaks about the people of God\'s kingdom , it is referring to the people that God has called him to himself in contrast  to the people pf the world who follow the ways of evil.\r\n\'In the Old testament it was about Abraham and his descendants.\r\nIn New Testament, it is about the Church, since Christians of all races have been adopted in to family of Abraham\'s family in Christ\r\n3. Covenants-\r\nThroughout the Bible . God administered his Kingdom through covenants.\r\nIt expressed God\'s good will towards his people, blessings for obedience and curses for disobedience,.\r\nThese covenants are Adamic, Noahic, Abrahamic, Mosaic, Davidic and New Covenant.\r\nBiblical covenants indicates the facts of our situation that God is our kings and that we are his kingdom servants', 9, '2020-09-07 19:00:33', '2020-09-08 00:37:00', NULL),
(1886, 532, 848, 'THERE ARE THREE PHASES IN HISTORICAL ORDER:\r\nINITIAL PEACE:\r\n when  God created the world, humanity ,lived in  perfect harmony with God. Adam and eve were obedient servants. human life was full of peace a, joy and gladness of thanksgiving and singing\r\nWorld in which child bearing were relatively easy and full of joy.\r\nNo enemy threatened war. no animals threatened violence. no sickness threatened health\r\nContinuity with Rebellion\r\nGenesis 3 records that serpent tempted eve to,eat from the forbidden of the knowledge of good and evil.in response to their rebellion, god through Adam and eve out of the garden and forced them to live in a world , where the ground was hard to work , where childbirth was painful , were sickness and famine and wild animals and war threatened them and their children.\r\nFinal peace:\r\nGod began to restore peace to his kingdom immediately after humanity\'s fall into sin.\r\nin Genesis 3 we see that God did not immediately strike Adam and Eve dead, when they sinned, instead he allowed them to live. An in the midst of cursing them, he presented then first offer of the gospel to them(Genesis 3:15)\r\nThroughout the history of the world, after the fall, god was working toward the goal, of the full redemption and success of his kingdom.', 9, '2020-09-07 19:15:45', '2020-09-08 00:37:00', NULL),
(1887, 532, 849, 'God\'s law  is a joy and delight to us. God is a loving king. He sis good  and gracious and benevolent to us, And he wants us to love him . his ideal kingdom is not one in which we cower in fear of him and obey so that we can avoid punishment. \r\nGod\'s law is the revealed standard by which he governs his kingdom, and we are obligated to live by it.\r\nAnd when we live according to the law, we receive the blessings. One role of the was is to instruct us to live in way that lead to blessing and enjoyment.\r\nWhen we use the law wrongly, it is a curse, we can not try to earn salvation by good works but \r\n only through Christ\r\nThe Bible speaks proper use of God\'s law a s great blessing to humanity.\r\nScripture speaks of God\'s law as a delight Psalm 1:2 ,Deuteronomy 28:1-14 says law was given for our good prosperity, and for our joy.', 8, '2020-09-07 19:25:54', '2020-09-08 00:37:00', NULL),
(1888, 470, 655, 'Historical analysis is the study of Biblical literature, method of criticism of the Hebrew Bible ( Old Testament) and the New Testament that emphasizes the interpretation of biblical documents in the light of their contemporary environment.', 5, '2020-09-11 00:03:34', '2020-09-11 03:38:51', NULL),
(1889, 470, 656, 'Traditionally, faith and reason have each been considered to be sources of justification of religious belief. As both can purportedly serve this same epistemic function, it has been a matter of much interest to philosophers and theologians how the two are related and thus how the rational agent should treat claims derived from either source.  Some have held that there can be no conflict between the two - that reason properly employed and faith properly understood will never produce contradictory or competing claims. Others have maintained that faith and reason can be genuine contention over certain propositions or methodologies.', 7, '2020-09-11 00:10:29', '2020-09-11 03:38:51', NULL),
(1890, 470, 657, 'Biblical theology is in large measure a response to a cultural shift that be traced back to the 17th century. This is not to say that the concerns of biblical theology were entirely new, or belong only to the modern period. Christians have always explored the acts of God reported in Scripture. But in the modern period, significant cultural shifts took place that led theologians to emphasize interests as never before. \r\n\r\nBiblical theology is a Christian response to prominent intellectual movement in the modern period, often called modern historicism. In very general terms, modern historicism is the belief that history holds the key to understanding ourselves and the world around us. In this view, an adequate understanding of anything can only be gained by considering the place it occupies in history.', 7, '2020-09-11 00:20:46', '2020-09-11 03:38:51', NULL),
(1891, 470, 658, 'There are two common approaches to using scripture in modern Christianity. The task of interpreting scripture becomes a matter of discovering where in our theological system a particular passage fits. The usage of scriptures is for our won purpose. The bible may be viewed as authoritative, but it provides either confirmation of our preconceived ideas or divine advice for felt needs.\r\n\r\nA theological reading or learning brings a map for a journey. The map may not give all the answers about a particular context but our reading sends us on a journey in which God in Scripture encounters us again and again. Reading scriptures is not about solving puzzles but discerning a mystery. Through scriptures, we encounter no less than the mysterious triune God himself.', 7, '2020-09-11 00:31:14', '2020-09-11 03:38:51', NULL),
(1892, 470, 659, 'Interest in the history of biblical interpretation is currently rising among students of the Bible. The rich history of its interpretation and that the history of biblical interpretation is marked to a great extent by the rich variety of distinct purposes of which biblical writings have been employed over the centuries. \r\n\r\nA veritable revolution in the biblical scholarship began toward the end of the renaissance among a group of Christian biblical scholars in Europe. On the model of leading classicists began to learn Hebrew and Greek and to consider the Bible from a similarly philological perspective.', 7, '2020-09-11 00:45:13', '2020-09-11 03:38:51', NULL),
(1893, 535, 850, 'God\'s authority is absolute in the sense that God has complete and total freedom over what he has created.\r\nGod\'s absolute is comparing it with the authority that a potter has over his clay.\r\nJeremiah 18:1-10\r\nAbsolute authority belongs only to the creator, and God is the only creator.\r\nGod\'s moral judgments are beyond legitimate questioning, so Bible insists that our ethical decisions be made in ultimate submission to God.\r\nGod has created everything for a purpose and everything in creation functions as God wants to it to be \r\nControl-Christianity has seen God \'s sovereign control as the basis for ethical responsibility. Philippians 2:12-13.Christianity has always affirmed that because God is the creator, he can and does exercise sovereign control over his creation.\r\nPresence-\r\nEven  after fall of mankind, God did not leave his creation, he rained present with the human face as our covenant king.It means that he is here to enforce his judgments over all the earth and its inhabitants.\r\nHebrews 4:13 \r\nOur ethical decisions must always account for God\'s presence with us as Judge both now and in the future', 8, '2020-09-14 17:46:20', '2020-09-17 15:56:33', NULL),
(1894, 535, 851, 'Preternatural realm is that realm which is beyond the nature.It is not above nature, in the way that God is, but is rather beside nature as a distinct aspect of creation. this is the realm inhabited by invisible spirits such as angels and demons.\r\nGod has populated the universe with a vast number of spiritual persons known as angel and demons. \r\nBoth angels and demons are intelligent, rational being, that have wills and personalities,When God created those beings, they were all angels,pure and perfect, serving God in His heavenly kingdom/.\r\nbut some of these angels willfully rebelled against God and fell from this blessed state into condemnation\r\nAngels remained loyal to God  whereas demons rebelled against God.\r\nEver since satan and the rest of the demons, rebelled against God , they have been locked in a battle against God\'s holy angels. Because this conflict is fought between good and evil spirits namely and angels, it is also called spiritual warfare Ephesians 6:12', 7, '2020-09-14 17:56:41', '2020-09-17 15:56:33', NULL),
(1895, 535, 852, 'Natural realm is the world God created in Genesis 1, the world in which we live and operate. It is the  side of the  creation that is most familiar to human beings.\r\n\r\nCREATION\r\nAccording go Genesis 2:7, God created us from the dust of the ground and because we are part of nature, we have an ethical obligation to protect it. Genesis 1:28, from the very beginning God has called human being s to govern the world.\r\nFALL-\r\nWhen Adam and Eve fell into sin, God responded by cursing both the human race and the earth, subjecting them to corruption.As a result of this curse, the natural world is effected by sin in many \r\nways. Nature is both corrupted by sin and is often hostile towards us\r\nREDEMPTION-\r\nWhen humanity fell into sin, the natural realm became both instrument cursing and recipient of cursing. but in redemption both of these effects are reversed. the natural realm becomes an instrument of redemption, as god works within the natural realm to accomplish redemption for human beings', 8, '2020-09-14 18:07:31', '2020-09-17 15:56:33', NULL),
(1896, 535, 853, 'Preternatural and natural realms both are created by God\r\nPreternatural realm is beyond nature, inhabited by invisible spirits such as angels and demons\r\nNatural realm is the visible world or creation, which we read in Genesis 1,2 , which we humans are familiar with.\r\nAngels serve as God\'s loyal messengers and agents  . They communicate his word to human beings and they interact with humanity on God\'s behalf.2 kings 19:35, angel of the Lord slew 185,000 Assyrians and .Psalms 91:11-12\r\nDemons are able to interact with natural realm , which they do in order to harm us.\r\nIn New Testament, demons attack Christians by temping them into idolatry\r\nJob 1-2 we find that Satan the chief of demons were permitted to destroy, his possessions and health, and to kill his family.\r\nDaniel\'s prayers reply were blocked by the demons and relieved by angels.\r\nEphesians 6:12, spiritual warfare is a struggle between the force of the good and the force of evil.\r\nMore ever it influence us in ethical ways, as angels help us find way to obey God and demons tempt us to sin', 8, '2020-09-14 18:22:17', '2020-09-17 15:56:33', NULL),
(1897, 535, 854, 'God is perfectly free from sin and in every aspect of his being. Goodness is one of God\'s essential attributes. All true moral goodness is rooted in the being of God., we are ready to consider the fact that god created humanity to be good that is he created us to reflect his personal goodness\r\nHumanity\'s role as God\'s representatives and offspring that forms the basis for many of the conclusions we draw about our goodness. We were created without flaw and without sin, in conformity to the standard of his character, in this way, God established humanity with our own attribute of goodness rooted in our very beginning.\r\nGenesis 1:28 when God blessed humanity in the creation account, he indicated that humanity was morally good and He blessed them because they had and innate attribute of goodness.\r\nGenesis 1:28, records God\'s cultural mandate to humanity.\r\nIn keeping with humanity\'s role as a God\'s image, god appointed humanity to be his vassal kings on the earth, to fill subdue and rule it for his glory.', 8, '2020-09-14 18:36:47', '2020-09-17 15:56:33', NULL),
(1898, 535, 855, 'Fall corrupted our nature.Fall caused our will to become enslaved to sin so that we lost our ability to choose and to do morally good things. Fall affected our knowledge so that we became incapable pf fully recognizing moral goodness. \r\nAdam\'s one sin resulted in the fall of human beings into sin and the corresponding curse on humanity corrupted the nature of each one of us leading to death and sin.Romans 8:5-8\r\nSin hinders humans\'s access to revelation , then sin prevents human\'s understanding of revelation  and sin\'s impact on humanity\'s obedience to revelation\r\nFall has hindered humanity\'s access to revelation by limiting the holy spirit\'s work of illumination and inward leading\r\nThe corruption of human nature in the fall resulted in the hardening of our hearts and this hardening keep us from properly understanding  God\'s revelation.\r\nFall has corrupted our nature, and our will to the pint that we rebel against God. We are incapable pf submitting to his word.', 8, '2020-09-14 18:49:40', '2020-09-17 15:56:33', NULL),
(1899, 535, 856, 'All of  God\'s essential attributes  are immutable, meaning that they can never change.God cannot be loving one day and unloving another day. he cannot be all powerful and  all knowing at certain times , but limited in his knowledge and power at other times.\r\nPsalms 102:25-27. James 1:17 \r\nDespite all the shifts and changes that take place in creation, we can rest assured that God does n not change , who he is. Today God is the same person with the same essential attributes that he was before he created the world. he will remain the same person forever .\r\nso we find comfort in an never changing God, because His nature, words ,promises all, can be always trusted . We are always safe with a God of this nature and character.\r\nHis love, mercies, faithfulness, goodness, kindness, all of these attributes are always in favour of us.\r\nso it gives us great hope, assurance and peace to be joyful in Him.', 8, '2020-09-14 18:59:46', '2020-09-17 15:56:33', NULL),
(1900, 535, 857, 'W e are fallen and indwelt by sin, in capable of reflecting god\'s goodness, but the good news is that when the Holy Spirit applies redemption to us , He indwells us and gives us new nature so that we are able to live in ways that God approves and blesses\r\nSubmitting to Holy Spirit \'s guidance in our lives helps us to resist sin.\r\nObeying the word of God and looking unto Jesus , the author and finisher of our faith, let us try to run with perseverance.\r\nTrusting of self and relying too much on our efforts may lead us to failures. \r\nWe should pray to God for an obeying heart . Holy Spirit guards our hearts and our minds, destroying sin\'s ability to deceive  us and empowering us to understand revelation (Colossians 1:9)\r\nSo in our strategy, we should include prayer, obedience to the knowledge of God and listening to the illumination of the Holy Spirit', 8, '2020-09-14 19:11:48', '2020-09-17 15:56:33', NULL),
(1901, 542, 660, 'Synchronic approach is the final form of the text is examined in the terms of language and literature. The synchronic approach has evolved from modern linguistic and literature criticism. Tools of structural linguistic are used. Following the are the 3 synchronic approaches: Discourse Analysis, Narrative Criticism and ideological criticism.\r\n\r\nFor example: Matthew 15:21-28 - A Canaanite woman came to Jesus and crying out \"Lord, son of David, have mercy on me! My daughter is suffering terribly from demon-possession\" ... after a few scriptures ... Jesus answered, \"Woman , you have great faith! Your', 7, '2020-09-21 12:15:36', '2020-09-23 14:38:31', NULL),
(1902, 542, 661, 'Synchronic synthesis of the Old Testament touches on three main issues: a basic orientation about what synchronic synthesis is: the ways Old Testament passages convey the historic information used in synchronic synthesis; and the synthetic theological structures of the Old Testament historic Information.', 4, '2020-09-21 12:22:12', '2020-09-23 14:38:31', NULL),
(1903, 542, 662, 'Poetic literature that evokes a concentrated imaginative awareness of experience or a specific emotional response through language chosen and arranged for its meaning, sound, and rhythm. \r\n\r\nLiterature in its broadest terms is any written work. Literature can be classified according to major forms such as the novel, short  story or drama, and works are often categorized according to historical periods or their adherence to certain aesthetic or expectations.', 2, '2020-09-21 12:28:11', '2020-09-23 14:38:31', NULL),
(1904, 542, 663, 'Literary Journalism is a reflection on the historic roots, concepts, practices, and processes. Its wealth is precisely its diversity. The result of the study point to three possible improvements. The first one is to reinforce the connection of communication with other fields of knowledge, such as Sociology, Anthropology, and Psychology. It needs to form efficient networks of researchers, and academic community.', 2, '2020-09-21 12:33:55', '2020-09-23 14:38:31', NULL),
(1905, 542, 664, NULL, 0, '2020-09-21 12:34:02', '2020-09-21 12:34:02', NULL),
(1906, 538, 858, 'Love motivates us to do good works first of all in allegiance, second of action and third of affection\r\nAllegiance is divided into three parts:\r\nLoyalty:\r\nit is the corner stone of the concept of love. It was common  for the covenant relationship between a suzerain and his vassal state to be describe in terms of love.\r\nThe suzerain\'s love was expressed largely in the form of loyalty to his people. He gave them protection, preserved justice for them. Jesus is our Lord and King and we are to render love to him through loyal obedience\r\nOrientation:\r\nOur lives must be oriented around God and His kingdom, which is our highest priorities , the focus of our desires and the center of our world view. The commitments to God and His people should be our primary orientation in life. They should be the most fundamentals commitments of our inward dispositions. \r\nResponsibility:\r\nLove is an orientation of obedience and service to God. It should dispose us to keep all of God\'s commandments. When we properly seek our responsibilities before God, understanding that we are obligated to Him in every area of our life.\r\nIt should motivate us to discover all our responsibilities towards our great king and His people, so that we can fulfill our duty in the best possible way.', 8, '2020-09-21 17:52:13', '2020-09-23 15:04:18', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(1907, 538, 859, 'Atoning grace:\r\nGod\'s character is our ultimate ethical standard. Matthew 18:23-35 Jesus taught  that we are to imitate God\'s forgiveness, We are to forgive those who sin against us, because God ahs forgiven us for sinning against Him.\r\nwe should love each other in imitation of the love that God has shown for us. The greatest example for this is Christ, who  died for our sins, 1John 4:9-11 .\'God asks us to imitate his grace by placing the value of making sacrifices for our children, similar value on his children too.\r\nGod \'s gracious example obligates  us to protect and care for our brothers and sisters in Christ.\r\nIt teaches us to love them whole heartedly so that we are motivated to sacrifice, to suffer and to even to die for them.\r\nCommon grace:\r\nIt refers to God\'s kindness to those who will never be saved.\r\nFor those who will ultimately receive salvation, God\'s grace always works to ward our redemption.\r\nBut go also extends non-redemptive kindness or common grace, to those who will never receive salvation. On the sermon on the mount Jesus referred to God\'s common grace as an expression of his love for all humanity.\r\nSimilar way, we should preserve justice for all people even if they hate us. We Christians are make to make sure that our desires for justice and or hatred for evil are part and parcel with our love for all humanity.', 8, '2020-09-21 18:08:30', '2020-09-23 15:04:18', NULL),
(1908, 538, 860, 'Colossians 3:17 Whatever you do , whether in word or deed , do it all in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God the Father through him.\r\nIt is the Love of God  and the sacrifice Jesus made on Cross and the exemplary life  that he lived that motivates me to do all things in love.\r\nOur thankfulness for the gift of His son motivates us to Love our Lord and to express His love through good works done in His name and for His glory.\r\nOur gratefulness to God motivates me to obey Him and help those he loves.\r\nWe can never repay God for the gift of Christ, so what we do is not a repayment to him., but we do it in loving response of those who appreciate what God has done. \r\nSo mine outward obedience flow from a heart truly committed To God and His word.', 7, '2020-09-21 18:17:10', '2020-09-23 15:04:18', NULL),
(1909, 538, 861, 'I do remember when I came first to saving faith. Earlier we had selfish motives , revenge taking attitudes, we used to do everything for name and fame. But when we come to Christ, God changes our hearts. Our hearts are cleansed by the Word of God as we meditate on it daily. His word changes our lives as we follow it. The indwelling of the Holy Spirit guides us to take right paths of our lives. Then by following the example of Christ ,we learn to forgive and love unconditionally.\r\nOur motive changes  us as we grow in Christ.\r\nWe start doing everything out of His love and out of obedience to His word.\r\nWe can never repay God for the gift of Christ, so all that we do to Him and his people are a loving response to appreciate what God has done. \r\nWe have received the greatest gift imaginable.  So we give ourselves whole heartedly to our covenant Lord.', 7, '2020-09-21 18:30:04', '2020-09-23 15:04:18', NULL),
(1910, 538, 862, 'Imagination simply refers to our ability to form mental images of things that are beyond our experience. sometimes it is thought to be an illegitimate way yo pursue knowledge , as if it necessarily entails falsehood or deceit.\r\nBible has many positive uses for imagination.\r\nImaginative skills or abilities are vital to learning and thinking about God, the world and ourselves.\r\nWe have to use our other faculties to make sure that the conclusions of our imaginations agree with god\'s word. but we can still have a good degree of confidence in our imagination , when we use it carefully and rightly, because the Holy Spirit grace us this faculty as a reliable tool for assessing knowledge.\r\nTo understand the time of Jesus ministry, his cross, rising from the dead, to understand and apply Jesus ministry to our ethical decisions, we have to use our ability to imagine the best.\r\nWhen people and things are so distant from us, that they are beyond the range of our senses, they are not currently part of our experience, we have to use our imagination to think about them.\r\nSo imaginative skills are useful to think about God, the world and us', 8, '2020-09-21 18:46:37', '2020-09-23 15:04:18', NULL),
(1911, 538, 863, 'There are three particular existential faculties that aid us in our tasks of assessing knowledge.\r\n1. Reason \r\nit can be defined as the capacity to make logical inferences and to judge logical consistency.\r\nit enables us to make sense of our situations , both by helping is understand the facts and by enabling us to compare this fact to the norms revealed in God\'s word.\r\nIt permits us to compare different facts to each other more extensively to determine , their logical relations. It helps us to relate statements of facts to statements of duty.\r\nScripture uses reason all the time and it regularly calls on us to do the same.\r\n2.Conscience:\r\n2 Corinthians 1:12\r\nit is defined as the ability to discern good and evil.\r\nIt is the sense of conviction that our thoughts , words, deeds are either pleasing or offensive to God.\r\nwhen we have sinned, our conscience can rightly condemn us as guilty and encourage us to repent.\r\nconscience means lev which literally means heart.\r\nconscience enables us to assess the knowledge we have acquired and to judge it against the standard of God\'s word.\r\nIt approves us when we believe we are acting in accord with God\'s word and it condemns us when we believe when we are violating God\'s word.\r\n3.\r\nEmotions:\r\nthey are inner feelings, they are the effective aspects of our ethical sensitivity.\r\nthey are God given human  abilities, that enable us to assess our knowledge in many different ways.\r\nour emotions are often the initial interpretation of the facts.\r\nour emotions can be very useful tools for determining how  God\'s word applies o our modern lives.', 8, '2020-09-21 19:03:41', '2020-09-23 15:04:18', NULL),
(1912, 538, 864, 'Our will is our capacity for making decisions.\r\nit is our volition, our ability to make choices. so each time we make a choice or decisions we are using our will.\r\nMaking the right decision is often hard because our will is affected by our fallen nature.\r\nFor the Christian, this ,means that while the Holy spirit enables us to make decisions that please God. there is always the possibility that indwelling sin will persuade us to make sinful decisions.\r\nOur will may be either active or passive.\r\nEither actively or passively , our will is involved in  each and everything we chose to think, say or do.\r\nSo of our decisions are to please our Lord, we must submit our will to him at every turn.\r\nWe must will what God\'s word commands  and we must allow the holy Spirit working within us to influence our will in positive ways. Philippians 2:13', 7, '2020-09-21 19:12:37', '2020-09-23 15:04:18', NULL),
(1913, 538, 865, 'Our heart is the center of our  entire being. It is the depth of our inner person and the seat of our motives. Heart is the seat of moral knowledge and moral will.\r\nMy commitment to God is above all others. this governs the fundamental direction of my entire life and all my other commitments .\r\nI am fully committed to fulltime ministry with my family.  As we read in Luke 6:45, we act according to the heartfelt loyalty to God. so even when troubles and trials  come, in our lives especially when we serve His people,  we do it all as we serve God and not merely people. \r\n We forgive them and guide them as Christ would do. \r\nWe submit to the Holy Spirit as he works within us to conform all our commitments to God\'s character, both through our understanding of his word and through the input of our other faculties.', 7, '2020-09-21 19:24:23', '2020-09-23 15:04:18', NULL),
(1914, 540, 681, 'There is a sound theological basis for three aspects of original meaning in our investigation of scripter first theological basis for giving attention to the writer, second consider the original audience ,third the function of the document itself , \r\nWriter :as we bible is originally inspire by God   the holy spirit chose communicate his word through the personalities ,experience ,emotional patterns of though human writers ,focusing on human writer shelp us to understand many features of scripter\r\nAudience : Do you ever heard  throughout the biblical history God gsve his word  to his people in ways that suited their historical circumstances ?God desighned his revalation to be understood by its firat audience. He adapted the word and ideas of scripture to the culture ,technology social structurs and even religious experience  \r\nDocument: its all about the original passage of the bible, if you wanyt to know anything about god , and the orginal meaning of the scripture we have to look at the passage it self \r\n ,', 8, '2020-09-22 17:45:45', '2020-09-23 15:05:45', NULL),
(1915, 540, 682, 'The doctrine of organic inspiration teaches that the holy spirit inspired human authors to write scripture ,but it dose not say that every copy made of that document will be perfect ,or that every transilation made from that document will be perfect ,scripture it self says in Jer.8:8 that copies of biblical document can be contain mistakes , we have all seen that different translation of the bible document can very greatly . because the doctrine of organic inspiration extended only to the orginal text of scripture , only those document have the fully athority of god him self ,\r\nThe doctrine of accommodation implies that everithing nin scripture including things like its word ,grammar and literary style rose out of the culture and linguistic convention of its day .if we pay carefully attention to the way scripture reflect these convention will be more likely to interpret it correctly .', 7, '2020-09-22 17:58:43', '2020-09-23 15:05:45', NULL),
(1916, 540, 683, 'Its should be obviouse that we want to know the original meaning of the of the biblical pasasge we have to look ate the passage it self ,modern translation are not infallible but thay represent one of the most important teaching ministries of the church  and as long as we are careful note to depend too much on a particulare word or a phrase that may be different in a one translation or another  ,we can learn a lot from the transialtion we use ,but we must do all we can to grasp the orginal mening of biblical passage ,orginal languages of scripture :Hebrew and aramic in the old testament ,Greek in new testamament ,we should also become familiar as much as possible with orginal language to understand the real word and meaning of thye scripture ,', 7, '2020-09-22 18:13:12', '2020-09-23 15:05:45', NULL),
(1917, 540, 684, 'There are three major approaches  towards the object and subject of the knowledge,  if we began to ask a question about the meaning of passage we find in bible ,it will help to begun by making a basic distinction between object of knowledge and subject of knowledge , object of knowledge are that the things thaat we try to understand , and these object can be either abstract ,like ideas ,or concrete ,like people or place , For exzmple biologiest studies object like animal and plants ,,By contrast subject of knowledge are the people that do studieng ,in the field of biology ,biologist themself are the subject , \r\n     so when we intrepret the Bible we are the subject,    becouse we are the one doing the interpretation ,and the objuct of our study is the Boble ,becouse thagt is we are trying to interpret ,\r\nnow it is easy to see that human understanding of every sort involves both objects and subjects of knowldege , and the third one is Dialogism :this aproache emphasize the constand diologe or intrplay between objective and subjective perspective .', 8, '2020-09-22 18:30:53', '2020-09-23 15:05:45', NULL),
(1918, 540, 685, 'The modern subjectivism gained prominence partly in response to the objectivism of the seventeen and eighteenth century ,philosophers like David hume, argue that reason and scientific study cant lead us to objective knowledge about the word , hume and others believed that our emotion ,desire ,and mantel categories always influence our thinking ,making imprtial objectivity imposible , \r\n The germen philosopher Immanuel Kant made tremendous contributions to subjective thoughts , he argue tha we cant know objective  reality as it realy is ,After hume and kant subjective approach to meaning continued to develop in the nineteenth century through movement like romanticism .in our day subjuctivesm has becomer wide spred ,especly in the interpretation of art and literature ,subjective interpret argue that sice we cant discover the objective understanding of the world around us, subjuctive talk about how the music ,painting, books and like viewed by different culture  ,different ethics groupe , different economic classes , these arethe philosephical and the cultural suppoirt for the subjectivism .', 8, '2020-09-22 18:46:43', '2020-09-23 15:05:45', NULL),
(1919, 540, 686, 'Objective and subjective to meaning oppose each other in some fundamental ways , but they have something very important in common in the extremes both models ultimately make the authority interpreters equel even greater than  the athority of bible itself , Objectivism tend to overestimate how reliable our rtional and scintificaly objective views are ,subjectivism tend to overestimate how reliable our personal intuition and opinion are , but in both case the result is same ,\r\nAuthority dialog and objective : its says truth can be found in the text of scripture , the bibe is \r\nGod\'s word and revelations to us, and everything is says is objectivly is true and meaning full ,and methodes of interpretation can help us understand this revelation as long as the mothod complay with biblical standard .\r\nAuthority dialog and subjective : it acknowledge that   we all come to the scripture with gthe perspective and belife that influence the way we intrepret biblical passage ,more over it agree with scripture and subjectivism ,that the personal subjective input we bring to interpretation is valuable .', 8, '2020-09-22 19:02:06', '2020-09-23 15:05:45', NULL),
(1920, 543, 806, 'The literature of the ancient Near East is very important to our purposes first because other premeval accounts were widely available to Moses, and second, because Moses actually interacted with other premeval accounts.\r\n1. Availability- Many Nations in the near east had already written many myths and epics about premeval history. Moses was educated in the royal courts of Egypt. His writings indicate that he knew the literature of the ancient world. Moses wrote his own divinely- inspired and true account of the premeval period, he was quite aware of other literary traditions in the ancient Near East. \r\n2. Interaction- Moses wrote his history of the early times to counter falsehood with truth. His writings purposefully resembled other ancient Near Eastern writings to communicate God\'s truth in ways that Israel could understand. The Atrahasis Epic follows a basic threefold structure. Comparing Genesis with Atrahasis strongly supports the idea that Moses\' formed his record with an intentional overarching structure.', 8, '2020-09-25 15:39:08', '2020-09-29 00:56:14', NULL),
(1921, 543, 807, 'Did God create the world in six ordinary days? Were the \"days\" of Genesis 1 great ages or epochs? Or is Genesis 1 a somewhat poetic, non-historical celebration of God\'s creative activity? All of these positions are acceptable within evangelical circles. Although my own view is that Genesis 1 teaches that God made the world as we know it today in six ordinary days, not all Bible-believing Christians hold to this view. This passage has three major steps, namely, a beginning, a middle, and an ending. \r\nMoses\' creation account begins with 1:1-2. We may summarize the content of these verses as the \"dark chaotic world.\" Chapter 1:3-31 form a middle section of the material which contains the so-called \"six days of creation\" or what we will cay the \"six days of ordering\" creation. Finally, 2:1-3 is the Sabbath Day, or as we will call it, the \"ideal world.\"', 8, '2020-09-25 15:46:29', '2020-09-29 00:56:14', NULL),
(1922, 543, 808, 'The first portion of Genesis 1, we see a very important dramatic tension between the chaos covering the earth and the spirit of God. The opening of 1:1-2 sets the stage by giving a title in verse 1, and by describing the initial condition of the world in verse 2. The world is \"formless and empty.\" Scholars believe that it meant that the world was uninhabitable, hostile toward human life, much like a desert or wilderness is inhospitable to human life. We see that an uninhabitable, dark, primordial, chaotic deep covered the entire earth. The second element in the dramatic tension also appears in 1:2. Moses wrote that \"Spirit of God was hovering over the waters.\" The Hebrew term used here is merachefet which means to \"fly above\" or to \"encircle above.\" So we see a very dramatic picture right at the beginning of this passage. On one side we see chaos on the earth; on the other side we see the spirit of God hovering above the chaos. In effect, God was ready to move into action to remedy the chaos which covered the earth.', 8, '2020-09-25 15:54:15', '2020-09-29 00:56:14', NULL),
(1923, 543, 809, 'Moses wrote to influence Israel to conform themselves to God\'s will. Other premeval accounts shared this same purpose. The cultures around Israel wrote their premeval accounts to justify their current religious and social programs. Their myths called the people to conform to creation ordinances of the Gods, the structures they had set for the universe. Moses focused on the ways Yahweh had created and ordered the world. Moses\' policies and goals for Israel were true to God\'s design for the universe. Israel was moving toward God\'s ideal by going to Canaan. When God entered Sabbath rest, the tension between the chaos and God\'s hovering Spirit had been resolved. God had subdued the darkness, ruled over the chaotic deep, and delighted in his ideally ordered world. The creation story comes to an end with this delightfully peaceful vision of the universe in perfect harmony.', 8, '2020-09-25 16:00:22', '2020-09-29 00:56:14', NULL),
(1924, 543, 810, 'John 1:4-5 \"In him was life, and that life was the light of men. The light shines in the darkness, but the darkness has not understood it.\" John continued to draw upon the themes of Genesis 1, especially the theme of the light which God brought to the dark chaotic world on the first day. John pointed to the incarnation of Christ as the light shining into the darkness of the world caused by sin. Followers of Christ find in Genesis 1 a portrait, an anticipation, of what God did in the first coming of Christ, the inauguration of the kingdom. Christ\'s appearance on earth was the beginning of God\'s final re-ordering of the world. We are right to place our faith in him and in him alone.', 7, '2020-09-25 16:05:43', '2020-09-29 00:56:14', NULL),
(1925, 541, 687, 'The theologian Thomas Aquinas insisted that the literal sense of scripture foundational to all its other sense ,he insisted that every legitimate spiritual interpretation was rooted in the literal sense of passage . He also taught that nothing nessesery to faith was communicated as aspiritual meaning without meaning taught elswhere in scripture in the literal sense ,he insted in principle that evry sense of passage of scripture must be tied to its literal meaning ,\r\n       althogh Aquinas effort to ancher spiritual meanings in th e literal meaning of the bible may seems like common sense to most of us ,spiritual interpretation that were disconnected from the literal meaning of passage had been used to support many doctine of the midival church , church athorities asserted that thay had special God given insight into spiritual meanings that had no connection to the literal meaning of the bibel .', 8, '2020-09-26 05:44:36', '2020-09-29 00:55:36', NULL),
(1926, 541, 688, 'Because of all Scripture is inspired an infallible, these elaborations always accored with and confirm orginal meaning , some time elaborations is stated as a repetition of a fact of the orginal meaning ,at other time biblical elaboration amay be stated as a clarification of things that weren\'t enterally apparent or well understood, there are three types of biblical elaborations often used in the scripture \r\n YOU SHALL NOT MURDER Exodus 20:13 \r\n  The First biblical elaboration   of this passage  well mention primarily a repitaion of these exact word , the repetaion confirmed the commandmend and the reminded God\'s people of the terms of his covenant when a elaboration nis stated in the form of a repetation ,its never merly repeat what was said before , the context of the elaboration always adds somthing tonits meaning \r\n    The second type of elaboration is Clarification , the clarification provide information that was crucial to understanding  \r\n  The third type of biblical elaboration is  expansion , in wich scripture provide aditional information about the passage or topic its reffernace .', 8, '2020-09-26 06:01:02', '2020-09-29 00:55:36', NULL),
(1927, 541, 689, 'The scripture has multiple meaning has gained wide acceptance in the contemporary world too,but mosstly for difference reason, scripture came from God was pure , but there are any misinterpretation came , same verese some can interpret as prosperity , some can interpret as promise , scripture actuly didn\'t teach about the material world, matter by ots very nature , but  many of teachings are al about materiel world , whene the scripture reffers to a physical thinngs that took place in history they actually pointed to heavenly , spiritual truth , that could be discern by allegory , , i need to explore the spiritual sense in number of different ways , so that i can interpret scripture and make them relevant ,', 6, '2020-09-26 06:18:04', '2020-09-29 00:55:36', NULL),
(1928, 541, 690, 'There are three interceptive fallacies , in oreder for us to interpret the bible we need to understand thet each of the guides informed by people,\r\n  Firstly  if we over emphazise the author we often fall into an intentional fallacy ,   \r\n   there are many way to commit to intentional fallacy in biblical interpretation for instance we might make unwarranted assumption about an author intention, \r\nA second type of mistake we acn make is overemphasizing the document , this kind of erreon often called a graphic fallacy , this is afallacy or mistake becouse the some document can be very different dthink depending on who wrote it and whom it was written, \r\n A third type of  interpretive mistake can we make is overemphasizing the audience, , this is often called effective fallacy, because eit focus too heavy on how scripture effect its audience', 7, '2020-09-26 06:36:14', '2020-09-29 00:55:36', NULL),
(1929, 541, 691, 'One of the most useful way to discover meaning in scripture is to make multiple summaries of a passage  ,or a description of a passage , normally a summary will come from a particular vantage points or emphasize a particular concept that appears in the passage  , sice every passage jas coplex meaning , summerisis help us by narrowing our studies , allowing us to focus on just potion or a passage has to say , some summarize we find describing character  developed through the story , another summaries chronical orded, some decribe criticizing cultural value , some will find the beautiful language in the same text, , there can be many legitimate summaries bring us closer and closer to the passage full meamning, these summarize can help us better understand aspect of its meaning . and taken together multiple legitimate summarizes bring us to closer and closer to the passage\'s full meaning .', 8, '2020-09-26 06:51:18', '2020-09-29 00:55:36', NULL),
(1930, 545, 692, 'The scripture are clear that there is only one God to whom all audience of scripture owe their loyality and obedience, and the traditional Christian theologians teaches  ,God is immutable ,meaning that he dose not change ,since God is immutable and loyalty and obedience to hime are universal obligation , the biblical concept of divine immutability dosen\'t imply that God is inactive , in biblical terms an inactive god is a worthless idol , but the God of scripture is constantly interacting with his creation in real and meaningful ways , \r\ntraditional christian theology has rightly insisted that there are three critical aspects of God\'s  immutability , First God\'s eternal counsel :means God knows everything and he is using that knowledge to  direct history towards the end of wich he created it, \r\nSecond: his character: God reveals different aspects of his character more prominently , God\'s immutable charecter heps us see there will always be significant connection between the original meaning  and morden meaning of scripture \r\nthird his covenant promises :when God promise ,his word is immutable ,otherwise he is free to change his mind .', 8, '2020-09-27 17:18:07', '2020-09-29 00:55:06', NULL),
(1931, 545, 693, 'There are at least three ways in which modern people are very similar to the people who first received the scripture  ,First , all humane beings ,no matter when or where they live are sinful image of God , second , we suffer religious divisions , and third ,humanity still include the same classes of  people  \r\nSinful image :When God created the humanity , he created us in his image , amonge other things ,this means that all human beings are rational , linguistic , and religious vice-regent of God ,at the same time all human beaing have fallen in to the sin , humanity today no longer use our rational ,linguistic moral and religious capacities to glorify God the we should ,there is no one who dose not sin, \r\nReligious Divisions : from the time the first scriptures were inspired , it has always been the case that reders of scripture have fallen in to the one of three religious grope , unbelievers, false believers and believers.\r\nClasses : human beinvg can be classified in may different ways , we might be classified acording to particular traits or attributes we have , some people are old, other are young ,some are male and some other are female , some are rich and others are poor, some ar epowerful others are weak ,also we can be clasified according to what we have done, alos opure job.', 8, '2020-09-27 17:34:33', '2020-09-29 00:55:06', NULL),
(1932, 545, 694, 'Christians have frequently summarized the bibles perspective on world history in three stage ,Creation :when God first made the world , Fall: when humanity first committed sin  and was cursed by God ,and Redemption :the period following the fall in wich God redeems us from our sin, many theologians have recognized that the progressive nature of God\'s rule over creation has resulted in periodic developments that create discontinuity between the various epoch mentioned in the scripture , but theologians also commonly identify epochs according to God\'s various covenant throughout the bible, \r\nIn many ways biblical history is a growing  tree  , every trees grow from a seed , in similar way redemption has grown and developed throughout biblical history ,  , and we have to account for these devolopment as we apply the bible to our lives .', 7, '2020-09-27 17:47:42', '2020-09-29 00:55:06', NULL),
(1933, 545, 695, 'Theologians have found different ways to divide the history records in the old testament .for one thing time doesn\'t pass in sharply segmented period , so transition between epochs generally took place gradually and the epoch them selves often overlapped, and the another things division theologians draw depend on the criteria they use  ,theologians obviously tend to use theological criteria delineate the epoch, but they still don\'t always agree the division because theology within the old testament developed in different way at different times , some part of old testament theology advanced slowly , others proceeded at a medium pace, and others changed rapidly ,  and may of this part did thire growing at different times, this way theologians have divided old testament history in a variety of ways ,', 6, '2020-09-27 18:00:08', '2020-09-29 00:55:06', NULL),
(1934, 545, 696, 'The divisions of the Old testament into ages makes it clear that God wanted his people to understand and apply theological themes in different ways at different times , and just as old testament believers werent supposed to serve God as if they lived in earlier periods of history , new testament believers should never apply the scripture as if they live earlier period of history , the reason is if imagin that we are an Israelites living shortly after Solomon built God\'s temple in Jerusalem, you know you are living in David\'s convent age  you know that in earlier mosaic epoch Israel scarifies at Moses temple , Once God commanded a new way for sacrifece in worship , he expected his people never to return to the old ways, so you will not sacrifice at moses tabernacle, becouse it s againest the will of God as you lives in Davids cavanet era , \r\nin the same way we think about the modern application of the Old testament , we have to remember we live in epoch of the new covenant', 7, '2020-09-27 18:15:13', '2020-09-29 00:55:06', NULL),
(1935, 547, 675, 'Hermeneutics is a common word in theological and biblical studies ,but we don\'t use it often in our daily lives ,many of us will notice that word hermeneutics  derives from the famly of Greek terms that includes the name \"Hermes \" the mythological messenger of the gods, the word it self derives from the falmy of Greek word related to the verb hermeneuo , which means \"interpret \"or explain, so broadly speaking when we refers to hermeneutics we have in mind the interpretation or explanation of some kind of message or communication .\r\n  by the end of the twenty century leading scholers saw the need of general hermeneutics because the prosses of the interpretation had become an important fact of many field of study , the biblical hermeneutics is the study of interpreting the meaning and significance of scripture , if you have ever reade the scripture then you \'ve involved your self in biblical hermeneutics ,at least informally .its helful to make distinction and a comparison between general and biblical hermenuetics .', 8, '2020-09-28 08:46:01', '2020-09-29 00:54:36', NULL),
(1936, 547, 676, 'People living in biblical times weren\'t modern scientists .but this doesn\'t meant that they were unintelligent or irrational , on the contrary their sophisticated  architectural , accomplishment , extensive maritime travel , and many other cultural achievement demonstrate that people in bilical days dealt with fact and thought rationally about the world , much like modern scientist do, it shouldn\'t surprise us that biblical authors themselves often interpreted other scripture with an orientation towards factul and logical analysis ,Romance 4:3-5, paul quoted from Genesis 15:6, wher God credited righteousness to Abraham when he believed in God\'s promises ,but see how methodically Paul deal with this passage ,    paul carefully analized the mening of the word \'credited \' may be transilated , by his knowledge in greek he argued that \"wages are not credited \" as a gift but as an obligation ,  but then he noticed that anyone who trust God his faith doesn\'t work .', 8, '2020-09-28 09:03:55', '2020-09-29 00:54:36', NULL),
(1937, 547, 677, 'Devotional hermeneutics focuses primaily on the divine authorship of the scripture , christian have always acknowledged that the human word of scripture are also the word of God , the scripture were inspierd by God , or more literally were \"god-breathed \"Even though biblical authors often examined the more or less scientific way  , it is just as important to see that thay also aproched the scripture devotionally , timne and again they indicated that followers of christ are to read the scripture asnthe word of God, in the presence of God , in ways it brings extra ordinary even supernatural experiens of God ,having seen the biblical roots of devotional hermeneutics  we should mention a few historical examples to illustrate the way followers of Christ have combined scientific and devotional aproaces to interpretation, \r\n  Devotional intrepretation of the bible  was particularly in the Patristic period of church history , and also throughout  the medievel period ,nearly every leading interpreters of scripture practiced some from the devin reading, By the time of reformation the church of Rom used the ptractis of this,', 8, '2020-09-28 09:20:39', '2020-09-29 00:54:36', NULL),
(1938, 547, 678, 'Two important aspects of organic inspiration ,help us to orient ourseves to task of interpretation \'\r\nFirst ,the fact that Holy spirit was the divine source of Scripture ;and Second , ,the fact that worked through human means to produce scripture ,\r\nDivine source: as the one who inspired all the scripture , Holy spirit has intimate knowledge of the bible\'s meaning and of the way it communicate that meaning , so preparing to interpret the scripture involves dealing personally with the holy spirit as thier ultimate author ,\r\nHuman means : sometime Christian act as if they would prefer that God had given us thye bible directly , but that\'s not the correct way , instead God had the scriptures composed by means of human authors , he revealed him self through the gift and abilities of different human beings , without a doubt , the holy spirit could have eliminated any influence or presents of human writers in scripture .', 7, '2020-09-28 09:33:30', '2020-09-29 00:54:36', NULL),
(1939, 547, 679, 'In the context of biblical hermeneutics , illumination may be defined as: The Holy spirit\'s work of conveying proper understanding of the scripture to a human being , we can distinguish two works, one is the work of inspiration where the holy spirit come to the  original human authors of scripture and empowers them so that what thay write is the word of God, \r\nIllumination is where the Holy spirit stand with us , he indwells Christian believers and open our mind to understand and receive what he has inspired in the bible, Throughout the illumination holy spirit grand us knowledege of his word , this knowldege impacts our imaginations , intuition , emotion, will, motive, desire moral conscience , the illimination of the holy spirit is a subject that seldom beend addressed at the length  ,', 7, '2020-09-28 09:45:53', '2020-09-29 00:54:36', NULL),
(1940, 547, 680, 'There are many things we might say about exegete , when we interpret the scripture especlly we might look at the things like , historical context , literary forms ,use of grammar and vocabulary ,theological settings and many other things, every involvement we have with exegesis of scripture prepare us for the further interpretation of the bible, the knowledge  , skill and attitudes we develop from one encounter with the bible, influence us to the next time we go to scripture , for instance every time we study thye vocabulary and grammar , we increase our ability to handle these aspect of scripture more responsibly , being an exegate os scripture i learned to study scripture in systematical way  and in close to real meaning of the text, its help me to interpret bible in may different context ,', 7, '2020-09-28 10:01:00', '2020-09-29 00:54:36', NULL),
(1941, 546, 811, '1. The Garden- The first dramatic step in 2:4-17, where we read that God put Adam in the Garden of Eden. The whole garden was Adam\'s splendid place to dwell and to work. Adam was given a great privilege by God\'s grace. He was to keep the garden on God\'s behalf. \r\n2. Condition Enhanced- The second step of our narrative consists of 2:18-25, which we will designate humanity\'s \"condition enhanced\" In this material God added even greater blessing to Adam\'s life. God formed a woman and bought her to Adam. In this way, God greatly enhanced the wonderful creation that he had made already Eve ready.\r\n3. Condition Cursed- In 3:1-21- the material begins with the introduction of new character and topic- the tempting serpent. Eve falls prey to the serpent\'s temptation so they eat the forbidden fruit and fall under divine curses. \r\n4. Out of Garden- God speaks about problem of tree of life in 3:22-24. God drove Adam from the garden and placed the cherubim and a flaming sword to guard the entrance to Eden. Human no longer have access to Eden apart from Direct intervention by God.', 8, '2020-09-29 15:39:12', '2020-10-07 16:14:42', NULL),
(1942, 546, 812, 'Moses revealed the central concerns of his narrative. To explore the symmetries of this narrative- \r\n1. Beginning and Ending- Gen 2:4-17 and 3:22-24 contrast at least three ways- \r\nLocation- 2:4-17- It begins with God placing Adam within the paradise Garden. Adam lived and worked in a place full of divine blessings and ends with God expelling Adam and Eve from the garden.  Trees- Emphasis on tree of knowledge and tree of life. It was knowledge to Good and Evil and Tree of Life is eternal life. God banished Adam and denied access to the tree. This shows the once free access to humanity and all the blessings, that had been lost until God decreed. \r\nHumanity\'s commission- God commissioned Adam to blessed work in garden with no pain or difficulty. But when banished, Condemned them to difficult toil. \r\n2. Middle Portions- The three contrasting symmetries are Divine relationship, 2:18-25- Disharmony replaced the initial harmony between God and humanity- 3:1-21\r\nHuman Relationships 2:18-25- Perfect bliss and in 3:1-21 Strife between Man and woman\r\nRelationship with evil- 2:18-25- Evil is absent, 3:1-21- Long term struggle with evil. \r\nMoses wrote about Adam and Eve in ways that connected directly with Israel\'s experience.', 9, '2020-09-29 15:49:23', '2020-10-07 16:14:42', NULL),
(1943, 546, 813, 'If the Israelites would be faithful to God they would have the opportunity to receive long life and happiness in the land of Canaan. Just as Adam and Eve had lost access to Tree of Life, in Moses\' day, God was offering Israel a partial taste of the blessing of the life found there. This experience of life was not full measure of the eternal life that we know when Christ returns. Yet, it would have been a partial foretaste of what was to come in Christ. Moses offered Israel the opportunity to enjoy blessing of long life in Promise Land. By drawing connections between Eden and Canaan, Moses taught his Israelites readers about their own lives as well. They learned how wonderful the Promise land could be for them.', 7, '2020-09-29 15:53:50', '2020-10-07 16:14:42', NULL),
(1944, 546, 814, 'In the inauguration of the Kingdom Christ retraced and reversed what Adam and Eve had done in the Garden of Eden, In his earthly ministry, Christ fulfilled God\'s commands where Adam and Eve failed. \r\n1. Paul- Romans 5.14 and Romans 5:18-19- Paul said Adam was a type of one to come. The rest of Romans 5 makes it clear that \'\'the one to come\'\' was Christ. Adam\'s one trespass resulted in condemnation for all people but Christ\'s one act of righteousness resulted in Justification for all mankind. \r\n2. Matthew- In Mat 4:1- Just like God tested Israel to see if she would be obedient, Christ was tested in wilderness too. The length of time is also parallel as Israel was for 40 years and Jesus was for 40 days. Also, Hunger was an important feature of Christ\'s temptation and testing of Israel was over food and water in the wilderness. Jesus quoted Deut 8.3. In Mat 4.7- he quoted Deut 6.16. Matthew drew attention to the way Christ retraced and reversed Adam\'s sin in his account of Christ\'s temptations in Matthew 4.1-11.', 8, '2020-09-29 16:04:35', '2020-10-07 16:14:42', NULL),
(1945, 546, 815, 'In the Modern world, we can see that people are away from God, and have become selfish, proud, ungrateful, arrogant. It robs us of the joy Christ has given us in our life as  we are kept in a place that God approves of, and sin robs us of that joy. It destroys the peace that is characterized by the inner calm and contentment God gives us. It also creates problems and strife between inter human relationships. Sin hinders our fellowship with God. Living a sinful means trying to live a life in the energy of Christian Life in the energy of flesh. We become unfearful to what is uncovered when Christ judges our work. \r\nin short, when we sin, we lose our Christian sharpness and move far away from God.', 8, '2020-09-29 16:15:59', '2020-10-07 16:14:42', NULL),
(1946, 548, 776, 'The majority of the interpreters believe that Paul was not the author of the book of the Hebrews. there are many reasons for it:\r\n1. This book is anonymous  and it was Paul\'s practice to name himself in his epistles. in 2thessalonians 2:2, we read that Paul was deeply was concerned to with forgeries, so it seems unlikely that he would have failed to identify himself had he written Hebrews.\r\n2. the book of Hebrews emphasizes subjects that don\'t receive much attention in Paul\'s letters.\r\n3. The third and the strongest reason for doubting Pauline authorship is the way the writer of Hebrews distanced himself from the first generation of Jesus\' followers .Hebrews 2:3 and Galatians 1:11, 12 and 1Corinthains 11:23 says differently .', 8, '2020-09-30 17:40:10', '2020-10-07 16:15:07', NULL),
(1947, 548, 777, 'Five important characteristics of Hebrews\' original audience :\r\n1. Jewish- the reason to think that at least a good portion of the original audience was Jewish. Hebrews 1:1 the traditional title attached to this book has been \"Pros hebraious\" which means \"for the Hebrews\"\r\n2. Hellenistic- its also likely that the audience was in large part Hellenistic. Hebrews 13:24 has been used to support this point of view because it mentions \" those from Italy\"\r\n3. Immature:\r\nthird the original audience of Hebrews was immature:\r\nHebrews 5:12 the audience had been long enough for the author for to say : by this time you had to be teachers\"\r\n4. Persecuted: the original audience of Hebrews was persecuted. There were two well known time for persecutions for Christians . Hebrews 10:32-35\r\n1: AD 49. BY CLAUDIUS\r\n2:AD 64 BY NERO\r\n5.  Near apostasy:\r\n\'the audience of the Hebrews faced persecution, at least some of them were near apostasy.\r\nthey were in danger of turning away from Christ entirely\r\nHebrews 10:26-27', 8, '2020-09-30 17:52:28', '2020-10-07 16:15:07', NULL),
(1948, 548, 778, 'Frequency \r\nthe frequency of the author\'s exhortations helps us understand the urgency of this message\r\nRhetorical style:\r\nthe book of Hebrew has often been characterized as highly rhetorical.\r\nOne rhetorical device called synkrisis in Greek is a detailed comparison between two or more things designed to convince audiences to affirm the speaker\'s point of view.\r\nAnother rhetorical device in the book of Hebrew is known as exempla .\r\nexempla are illustrations and examples\r\nA third rhetorical device used by the author of  Hebrews is expression qol wahomer\r\nit contains for example light to heavy, less to great simple to complex.\r\nHebrews 10:28-29', 8, '2020-09-30 18:02:22', '2020-10-07 16:15:07', NULL),
(1949, 548, 779, 'According to Hebrews 5:12, the original audience was immature. immature attitude includes lack of faith in several area of our life. when we are in troubles or things don\'t go as we planned , we may get impatient.\r\nseveral trials one after another can really test our faith. and can make us act immaturely even leading to denial of our faith. sometimes we are dependent on others pushing us regularly and behave immaturely. \r\nSometimes we behave immaturely in our behavior and attitude to the response to others deeds to us. \r\nWe may be slow to forgive them and even wait for their downfall. these all are immature behaviors from our side. \r\nWe may doubt God for all small trials and lack faith in Him when our prayers are not answered as we wished. so these are some areas I do need to overcome and become mature and perfect in Christ.', 8, '2020-09-30 18:10:22', '2020-10-07 16:15:07', NULL),
(1950, 548, 780, 'False doctrines and false teaching have been there from the beginning of the Church. Jesus already taught that in the end times it will be difficult to find real and genuine love for God.\r\nPaul and Peter talked about false prophets and false doctrines which will lead us away from the Love of  God.\r\nJude talked about false people who will come in disguise to drift the children of God from faith.\r\nNow currently in India, many false doctrines and teachings are encountered by us\r\n1. saying that Jesus has already come again and new Jerusalem is His wife,.\r\n2. another one which says Jesus is not God\r\n3. Mormonism is widely spread here.\r\nThe only strategy we follow is to learn from the word of God as ,much as possible and teach the believers of Christ deeply and truly from the word of God as . if they are aware of the truth , no one can drift them away from the truth of the Bible.', 8, '2020-09-30 18:18:32', '2020-10-07 16:15:07', NULL),
(1951, 549, 866, 'It was believed that Apostles\' creed was written and that each apostle contributed one of the creed\'s twelve distinct theological statements. but there is no evidence that it eventually took place.\r\nthe writing s of the early church fathers indicates that written rules of faith summarized the beliefs and practices of the churches that produced them.\r\nRules of faith like theses were intended to preserve the teachings of the church and were used to train its people.\r\nIn the first and second centuries , it is believed that each church had its own creed.\r\nOne ancient creed that rose to prominence in this manner was the creed from the church in Rome, often called the Roman creed.\r\nthis sis so similar to Apostles\' creed.\r\nBut regardless of its precise origins, Apostle\'s creed eventually came into widespread use, especially in western churches. in the early centuries, its precise wordings varied somewhat from church to church. but in the eighth century the wording was generally standardized into the form that we recognize and use today.', 8, '2020-10-01 17:43:44', '2020-10-07 16:15:36', NULL),
(1952, 549, 867, 'Apostles\' creed  was created to help Christian learn and remain true to the teachings of the Bible.\r\nFirst , Scripture as the original repository of true doctrine.\r\nBasil appealed to scripture as the highest authority to settle the matter.\r\nthe early church relied strongly in scripture as the base for all its doctrine.\r\nSecond the churches traditional teaches as affirmations of scripture.\r\nChrist the first link. the apostles as they had direct contact with Christ, so their teachings as the second link and the Scripture as the third link. Fourth link as the traditional teachings of the church\r\nThird the apostle creed was intended to summarize the churches traditional understandings of the scripture .Origen and other early church fathers wrote down the church\'s rule of faith to make sure that Christian through out the world would  be able to compare their doctrines to the traditional ones.', 8, '2020-10-01 17:55:46', '2020-10-07 16:15:36', NULL),
(1953, 549, 868, 'Apostles\' creed is divided into three main parts. the first section speaks of belief of God the Father, the second is about belief in Jesus Christ, His Son our Lord. And the third section belief in the holy Spirit and lists his active ministries. This formula is Trinitarian\r\nthat is it is based on the the belief  that there is only One God, that this God exists in three persons, namely the person of the father, the son and the Holy Spirit\r\nThe trinity is commonly stated this way\r\nGod has three persons , but only one essence.\r\nNature:\r\nwe use the term essence to refer to that thing that each of theses three persons share eternally in common with the others , to the stuff or being that belongs as much as to the Father as it does to the son and to the Holy spirit\r\nGod exists in three persons , we are defending the biblical truth that the Father, the Son and the holy spirit are  distinct from one another. they are sperate individual , who converse with another, interact and engage in relationships with one another.\r\nPerson:\r\nwith regard to the Father, the creed ascribes to him the attribute of being almighty and mentions that He is the maker of heaven and earth.\r\nthe creed mentions that Jesus; incarnation , his coming to earth as a human baby, genuine human life, sufferings. death, burial and resurrections and ascension.\r\nthe creed says that Holy Spirit cause the virgin Mary to become pregnant with Jesus.\r\nit also associates the Holy Spirit with Church, with our experience of salvation , both now and future.', 9, '2020-10-01 18:12:06', '2020-10-07 16:15:36', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(1954, 549, 869, 'When creed says the \"I believe in the Holy Church:, it emphasizes the importance of participation in the church.\r\nParitcipate:\r\nAs per Hebrews 10:25, Church is important and necessary for Christians as it is a place for worship, teaching and fellowship. Bible teaches Christians to form an actual physical community and it insists that this community is extremely important to every believer. it is not to be limited to spiritual fellowship, though it is true that Christian have spiritual communion with each other, our community is to be like a family or neighborhood.\r\nPreserve:\r\nJude verses 3-4 says that part of church\'s job is to contend for the faith, to protect the truths and beliefs.\r\nChurch is still trying to protect the doctrines. we have to keep trying to preserve the doctrines in the church, if we abstain from this call, we are denying a central article of the historic Christian faith, I believe in the church.', 8, '2020-10-01 18:23:45', '2020-10-07 16:15:36', NULL),
(1955, 549, 870, 'The foundation is the  base on which the rest is the building is  created.\r\nit is the anchor and provides strength and stability to the building. Ephesians 2:19-21.\r\nChristian theology must be founded on true doctrines and principles if it is to honor God and be useful to his people.\r\njust as Jesus is the cornerstone of the church, his teachings are the cornerstone of theology.\r\nApostles\' creed is foundational to theology because it introduces as to the teachings of the apostles recorded in scripture.\r\nFoundational nature of the apostles\' creed can be divided in two parts: \r\nit provides a standard against which other doctrines can be judged .\r\nit functions as doctrinal standard because it presents several of the biggest, most important ideas of Christianity.\r\nit serves as the logical basis on which other true doctrines are built.\r\nIt helps us see the relationship between the various different belief s in our theological systems and it helps us think about doctrines that are more remote from scripture in ways that harmonize these less central ideas with our fundamental beliefs.', 8, '2020-10-01 18:37:35', '2020-10-07 16:15:36', NULL),
(1956, 550, 816, 'Moses completed the scenario of threat and hope of deliverance. The destruction of violent, sinful humanity through the flood would actually result in a deliverance for future generations. From our explorations of the literary structures of Genesis 4:1-6-8, we see that these chapters in Genesis focus on two major issues: first, they focus on threat of violence from those who rebelled against God in the days of Cain and his descendants; second, they focus on the threat of sinful people in the days of the sons of God and the Nephilim. In both cases, Moses indicated that God would bring deliverance through the one special son of Seth, the man named Noah.', 8, '2020-10-02 16:10:29', '2020-10-07 16:16:02', NULL),
(1957, 550, 817, 'The violence of early human history closely resembled the violence Israel had endured. \r\nEarly violence and hope- Moses wanted his readers to associate: Cain and his family with the Egyptians. Righteous Abel, Seth and the Sethites with Israel as the people of God. Occupations and Sacrifices God rejected Cain\'s sacrifice but was pleased with Abel\'s sacrifice. Moses first approached Pharaoh to ask for the release of Israel because he w\r\nanted to offer sacrifices to Yahweh. \r\na. Sinful Cain, Genesis 4:1-16\r\nMoses focused on five concerns that allowed the Israelites to connect this passage to their own day; Moses mentioned the occupations of Cain and Abel to create these associations.', 8, '2020-10-02 16:23:01', '2020-10-07 16:16:02', NULL),
(1958, 550, 818, 'The unfaithful spies reported that the land of Canaan was a terribly violent and threatening place, and that among the inhabitants of Canaan were Nephilim, vicious warriors who stuck fear into their hearts. Unfortunately, this report led the first generation following Moses to turn away from God\'s call to conquest. \r\nThis light we can understand how Moses drew another strong connection between this portion of his primeval history and the experience of Israel. He wanted his Israelite readers to associate the primeval Nephilim of Genesis 6 with the terrifying Nephilim warriors of Canaan. In this way, the violence and hope of deliverance in Genesis 6:1-8 spoke directly to the threat of violence in the conquest of Canaan.', 8, '2020-10-02 16:28:12', '2020-10-07 16:16:02', NULL),
(1959, 550, 819, 'Abel is a character I would like myself to be like. He managed to learn about what sacrifices to make to God, and how to worship. Abel gave the most valuable, sellable worthwhile and  delicious parts to God, and this pleased Him. On the contrary, Cain didn\'t put much thought to what he gave, he picked something random and brought it to the altar. He brought the leftovers, whereas his brother brought the finest. Just like that, we should view our work as an offering to the Lord and to live in the spirit and attitude of Abel. To bring our skills and talents to the altar with a willingness to use them to the fullest for the glory of God. Moses was hoping that we learn from the mistakes and let Cain be a example of what the worship to God should not be, and Like Abel, how it should be.', 8, '2020-10-02 16:38:22', '2020-10-07 16:16:02', NULL),
(1960, 550, 820, 'In the primeval history, inspite of many drawbacks and wrongdoings of humanity, God never abandoned them.  He was always the loving Father and helped them throughout their journey. From creating humanity is His own image, God provided everything for man to live and to have dominion over.  God had a relationship of family with humanity. He was the Father and we are His children. Because of the mankind\'s rejection, this relationship has become broken and fractured. But He never leaves us. Just like in the primeval history, Adam and Eve disobeyed God, but he still cared for them. He promised that a Savior would come and destroy Satan\'s power over them. God kept his promise by sending his Son Jesus. By dying for our sins, Jesus destroyed Satan\'s powers over us.  God always brings us back to His amazing grace and love, He brings us back to His eternal family.', 8, '2020-10-02 16:51:00', '2020-10-07 16:16:02', NULL),
(1961, 551, 781, 'The book of Hebrews quotes or refers to the Old Testament nearly 100 times.\r\nthere are five main ways that the author of Hebrews repeatedly treated quotations from the Old Testament.\r\nFirst place he drew to Factual backgrounds like in Hebrews 7:2 Melchizedek from Genesis 14:18\r\nSecond place the author noted abiding theological outlooks- beliefs about god himself and other matters in close relation to God.\r\nthe author in Hebrews 1:5 referenced 2 Samuel 7:14, here God declared that every king in David\'s dynasty would be called God\'s son from David\'s time forward.\r\nhebrews 1:7 the author quoted Psalm 104:4 where angels are described as spiritual beings.\r\nHebrews 2:6,8 He cited Psalms 8:4-6. He argued that God had ordained human beings to be lower than angels only until the end when mankind not angels will rule with Christ over all of creation.\r\nHebrews 6:13,14 the author cited God\'s oath to Abraham from Genesis 22:17. Here God established that his promise to Abraham was permanent, extending even to New Testament times.\r\nHebrews 12:29 describing God as a consuming fire in Christ.', 8, '2020-10-05 17:50:51', '2020-10-07 16:23:48', NULL),
(1962, 551, 782, 'The outlooks of the local Jewish community were rooted in biblical passages, but they give excessive honor to angels. so this exaggerated honor for angels raised a serious challenge to those who followed Christ.\r\nthe author of Hebrews challenged it in five steps,:\r\n1. in Hebrews 1:1-4 wrote that his audience should follow Jesus because Jesus is God\'s supreme source of divine revelation, that Jesus brought revelation that was far superiors to any revelation given through angels\r\n2. in Hebrews 1:5-14 the author explained that Jesus is greater than angels because he is God\'s messianic Son.\r\n3. in 2:1-4 the author exhorted his audience to pay careful attention to the great message of salvation first announced by Jesus.\r\n4.Hebrews 2:5-9 says that belief in the supremacy of Christ by explaining that Jesus is now ruler over the angels.\r\n5. Hebrews 2:10-18 the author demonstrated that Jesus is Abraham\'s descendant and Jesus wills share his glory  with Abraham\'s descendants, not with angels.', 8, '2020-10-05 18:02:05', '2020-10-07 16:23:48', NULL),
(1963, 551, 783, 'The author of the Hebrews further explained the supremacy of Christ as God\'s ordained royal high priest by discussing how the new covenant is superior to the  old. \r\nThe new covenant derives from Jeremiah 31:31, called covenant of peace in Isaiah 54:10 and Ezekiel 34 and 37\r\nJesus mediates the new covenant as the royal high priest in heaven.\r\nHebrews 9:1-28, the author says that Jesus heavenly royal priesthood is superior to the Levitical priesthood. \r\nJesus died as ransom to set his people from judgement.\r\nHebrews 9:26 says Jesus did away with sin once for all because his blood is not sprinkled in a man made sanctuary. he entered heaven by the sacrifice of himself, just as God promised in Jeremiah 31:34', 8, '2020-10-05 18:13:50', '2020-10-07 16:23:48', NULL),
(1964, 551, 784, 'Old Testament quotes refers to 100 times in the  book of the Hebrews.  its the Old Testament that gives us first picture of the God , how the universe came into being.  what happened to his creation and what ways did God make way t save human kind. What promises God made and how was it being  fulfilled in New Testament ,in Christ Jesus.  \r\nThe promises made by God and its fulfillment definitely gives an inspiration about the faithfulness of God.\r\n Old Testament gives us the factual backgrounds of all things in New testament.\r\n It makes us clear about the theological outlooks.\r\n  the moral obligations were to remain as standards for God\'s people in New Testament times.\r\nOld Testament eschatological predictions to show that God\'s final judgements and blessings are fulfilled with in Christ.', 8, '2020-10-05 18:31:23', '2020-10-07 16:23:48', NULL),
(1965, 551, 785, 'one  of the purpose of the Hebrews is to emphasize that Jesus Christ has overcome sin for us.\r\nChrist  obeyed God and went through sufferings in silence.\r\nHebrews 2:1 says to pay more careful attention and fix thoughts on Jesus.\r\nHebrews 5:8 says though he was a son , he learned obedience by the things he suffered.\r\nHebrews 12:2 says that looking unto Jesus we should run our race who is the author and finisher of our salvation.\r\nJesus died as a ransom to set his people free from judgement and the fiath on him alone is sufficient in every area of our life.\r\nso looking unto Jesus every day and trusting on Him, as he is able to help us when we are weak as he ahs also undergone the same sufferings .\r\nJesus is the good high priest to intercede for us and give us strength to overcome.\r\n. this we can teach and share to all around us in our ministry', 8, '2020-10-05 18:50:38', '2020-10-07 16:23:48', NULL),
(1966, 555, 821, 'Flood of Deliverance- These chapters form a symmetrical five-step drama. \r\n1. Initial Covenant- The first step of this narrative also tells us that God spoke to Noah and revealed why he planned to destroy the human race. God planned to start over again by delivering Noah and his family. \r\n2. Enduring Covenant- God entered into a second covenant with Noah at the end of the flood narrative. God decided to give humanity the opportunity of a new order in the world. Noah was the mediator and God promised a covenant that flood won\'t destroy the earth and setting his bow was a sure sign.\r\n3. Escape from Water- It appears in 7:1-16. Noah prepared the ark and brought animals of every kind into it. Noah, his family and the animals he had gathered were safely sealed in the ark. \r\n4. Exit to dry land- A dramatic counterpoint to the second step. After a waiting period, dry lands appeared God commanded Noah to leave the ark, just as he had previously ordered him to enter it. \r\n5. Divine Remembrance- The center or turning point of the narrative. God did not forget the covenant he made with Noah. he remembered the passengers of the ark, and moved on their behalf against raging flood.\r\n Moses\' chief concern was to show that through Noah God brought humanity into a world of tremendous blessings.', 9, '2020-10-06 15:41:21', '2020-10-11 01:22:21', NULL),
(1967, 555, 822, '1. Sons of Noah- Genesis 9.20-29 sets forth distinctions among the sons. Genesis 10:1-32 describes the distribution of Noah\'s sons and their descendants: \r\nJaphethites- North, Northeast, and northwest of Canaan, Hamites- Northern Africa\r\nCanaan, son of Ham- land of Canaan, Israel\'s Promised Land, Shemites- Arabian Peninsula\r\n2. Defeat of Babel- The story of the tower of Babel divides into five symmetrical dramatic steps.\r\na. Humanity Unified first steps of verses 1 &2 begins with vast majority of humanity together. \r\nb. Humanity\'s Plan- Second step of verses 3&4 reports a plan which the people had. They intended to build a city with great tower reaching heaven so that they will be famous for all time. \r\nc. Divine Investigation- in verse 5, where God investigated the city and its tower. Once God saw the city and the proud plans of its inhabitants, he determined to bring an end to the city of Babel. \r\nd. Divine Plan- Fourth step is verses 6 and 7 balances the human plan by reporting God\'s counterplan. God called his heavenly army to attack the city by confusing the language of the people and thereby to stop the construction of the city and its tower. \r\ne. Humanity Dispersed- in verses 8&9 where we learn that God dispersed humanity over the earth as he confused human language. Humanity move from being together with one language to being scattered and having many languages.', 9, '2020-10-06 15:52:14', '2020-10-11 01:22:21', NULL),
(1968, 555, 823, '1. Connections- Moses established connections between the flood and his own day by pointing to connections between himself and Noah.\r\na. Violence- The work of both Noah and of Moses was to deliver from violence. In Genesis 6:13 Noah\'s flood came because there was violence in earth. In Exodus 1-2, Egyptians inflicted much violence on People of Israel.\r\nb. Ark- Both Moses and Noah had been delivered from watery deaths by means of an ark, or tevah.\r\nc. Covenants- Noah entered into covenant with God on behalf of entire human race. Moses led the people of Israel into a special covenant with Yahweh. \r\nd. Water Judgement- God delivered Noah and his family by taking them safely through flood that destroyed the wicked of earth, Moses brought Israel out of Egypt by passing through the waters of Red Sea, which destroyed the army of Egyptian oppressors. \r\ne. Wind- God sent wind to drive back the waters in both the days of Noah and the days of Moses.', 8, '2020-10-06 16:02:44', '2020-10-11 01:22:21', NULL),
(1969, 555, 824, 'In the inauguration of the kingdom, Christ accomplished a great salvation on the behalf of his people in ways that corresponded to the themes Moses emphasized in Genesis 6:9-11:9 these connections in at least two ways: the covenant which Christ mediated and the victory he accomplished. \r\n\r\n1. Covenant- Christ delivered his people from God\'s judgement by means of the new covenant. He came to earth when God\'s people were under divine judgement. Noah played a special role as the mediator of a covenant, and Moses drew upon this fact as he explained his own ministry to Israel. In similar fashion in the inauguration of the kingdom, Jesus delivered those who trusted him from judgement by mediating the new covenant through his blood which he shed on the cross. \r\n\r\n2. Victory- The new order of the world required Israel to move forward into conquest of Canaan and he assured them of a great victory. Jesus was victorious over the spiritual forces of darkness in his death and resurrection.', 8, '2020-10-06 16:09:01', '2020-10-11 01:22:21', NULL),
(1970, 555, 825, 'In the inauguration of the kingdom, Christ accomplished a great salvation on the behalf of his people in ways that corresponded to the themes Moses emphasized in Genesis 6:9-11:9 these connections in at two ways: the covenant which Christ mediated and the victory he accomplished.\r\nContinuation- The time between the first and second comings of Christ relate to Genesis 6:9-11:9 where the Baptism and Spiritual Warfare is seen. Peter drew a direct relationship between the water of Noah\'s flood and Christian life by focusing on baptism. He said that water in Noah\'s day symbolized like Moses\' passing through Red Sea. And the spiritual warfare, as water of Noah\'s flood delivered humanity into a holy war. Similarly, every believer is in war with evil. \r\nConsummation- New Testament writers described the return of Christ in glory as the final cataclysm and the final battle. When Christ returns, there will be cataclysm. Peter argued in 2 Pet. 3:3-7 that just as the primeval world had come to an end through the flood, the present heavens and earth would come to end at return of Christ in judgement. \r\nFinal Battle will be in the return of Christ in which Christ himself appears and destroys all of his enemies. The divine purpose will be fully realized when Christ returns in glory and people of God in Christ will enjoy  eternal peace and victory in new heaven and new earth.', 9, '2020-10-06 16:22:55', '2020-10-11 01:22:21', NULL),
(1971, 554, 871, 'Christianity is a monotheistic religion because we insist that there is one and only one divine being.\r\nMany scriptures assert God\'s singularity by explicitly stating that there is only one God. \r\n1 kings 8:60 states THE LORD IS GOD.. THERE IS NONE OTHER.\r\nPsalms 86:10 says you alone are God.\r\nRomans 3:30 says there is only one God.\r\nall these verses prove that there is only one divine being.\r\nthis was true in the days of the old Testament. It was true in the days of New Testament.\r\nit was true in the days of the early church.\r\nthere are many religions that worship multiple gods, demons, creation.\r\nBut Bible insists that only the Christian God is truly divine, only the Christian world will judge the world and also to save us.', 8, '2020-10-06 17:41:51', '2020-10-11 01:21:54', NULL),
(1972, 554, 872, 'Simplicity of God  refers to to his essence that we have in mind, his fundamental nature, the substance that makes up his being. Simplicity is the unity of his nature or essence.\r\nGod has three persons, but only one essence. His essence is not a composite of different substances but a unified whole consisting of only one substance. comparing it as mud and water, mud sis a complex substances, whereas God\'s essence is like absolutely pure water, it is composed of only one substances.\r\nChristianity emphasizes that God is simple and not composes of different substances.\r\nAs strongly as the Bible insists that God has three persons-the Father, the son and the Holy Spirit - it also insists that there is only one God .God has a simple and unified essence, it means that the Father, son and holy Spirit are not separate, but it means that these are persons who had existed together as only one God.', 8, '2020-10-06 17:55:25', '2020-10-11 01:21:54', NULL),
(1973, 554, 873, 'Two particular perspectives on the trinity have come into the foreground. they are \r\n1. ONTOLOGICAL TRINITY-\r\nWhen we speak of it, we are focusing on God\'s being. the word ontological means relating to being.\r\nwe are looking at the trinity in terms of his essence or being. we are considering how the three persons of the trinity are integrated with one another, how they share a single essence.\r\n2. ECONOMIC TRINITY\r\nWhen we speak of the economic Trinity. when we consider how God\'s presence interact with each other , how they relate to one another as individual persons. the word economic means relating to household management, so  when we speak of the economic aspects of the Trinity. we are describing how the Father, the son and the holy spirit relate to one another as distinct individual personalities.\r\nFrom both ontological and economic perspectives , the Father is said to be the first person.', 8, '2020-10-06 18:08:41', '2020-10-11 01:21:54', NULL),
(1974, 554, 874, 'The Fatherhood of God has many aspects , main three of Scriptures more prominent ideas.\r\nCREATOR:\r\nScripture sometimes refers to god as being the father of everything he ahs created \r\nDeuteronomy 32:6. Paul insisted that God of the Bible was the real Creator and also affirmed that to create something is to become its father.\r\nKING:\r\nEarlier kings were referred as the father of the people, kings referred to their people as their children,\r\nDavid was referred by Israelites as their father because he had been their king.\r\nGod was called Father , because he was the great king that ruled over all the kings of the world and because he ruled directly over his chosen nation Israel.\r\nIsaiah 63:15.16\r\nJesus prayed in Our Father in heaven and thy kingdom come .\r\nFAMILY:\r\nat time sin old testament, we see that God is the head of the family of human race.\r\nGen 5:1-3 Adam is described as God\'s son\r\nGod is also portrayed as the family head of the nation Israel.\r\n\r\nit also continues in new testament.\r\nMathew 7:9-11, Luke 11;11-13. in genealogy we read Adam as the son of God.\r\nGod disciplines us , loves us , cares for us as does a Father to his children.', 8, '2020-10-06 18:25:03', '2020-10-11 01:21:54', NULL),
(1975, 554, 875, 'ABSOLUTE:\r\nthe Father\'s authority is absolute in the sense that he has complete freedom to do whatever he wants with his creation. His absolute authority is compared to a potters\' authority over his clay. Jeremiah 18:1.God is the creator of all .\r\nEXCLUSIVE: Father  also has exclusive authority over everything he ahs created. it is in the sense that no creature possess absolute authority. Authority belongs only to the creator and God is the only creator.\r\nEXHAUSTIVE:\r\nWhen we say that God\'s authority is exhaustive, we mean that it extends over everything he ahs created, in every detail. everyone is under God\'s authority there is no person or other created things that is free from  the obligation to obey God.\r\nEverything is under God\'s authority. because God has created all things, no aspect of creation is morally neutral. He has created everything for a purpose and assigned it a moral character.', 8, '2020-10-06 18:36:50', '2020-10-11 01:21:54', NULL),
(1976, 560, 826, 'Unlike many other ethical system our definition focuses on God and his blessing , rather than the terms likes good or evil , right or wrong, Those things that receive God\'s blessings are good and right , whereas those things that do not receive his blessings are wrong and evil, by focusing on God and his blessing this  way we mean to say two things , First God\'s nature is the standard of morality , and second God\'s action demonstrate the standard of morality .\r\nGod\'s Devine nature :we affirmed that God him self is the ultimate standard of right and wrong ,of good and evil, in saying that we deny that ultimate morality  is a standard outside of God, we insist that God is not to any standard outside himself and that everything accords with his character is good and right ,while everything that dose not is evil and wrong, \r\nDivine action:the second things we meant to say by focusing on God\'s blessing is tha God\'s actions demonstrate the standard of morality , one of the chief way  God shows his aprovel for what is right and good is by bestowing blessings . similer he shows his haterd for what wrong and evil by withhold blessings and pouring out curses .', 7, '2020-10-11 15:45:31', '2020-10-16 21:30:16', NULL),
(1977, 560, 827, 'Unless a work is done with right motive , it is not a work that God will reward with blessings . first we must proceed from a heart that purufied by faith , second action must flow out of Christian love, confection of the faith \"works that proceed not by a heart that purified by faith , sinfull and cannot please God , this criterion of  right motive is closely associated with the way our defenition of christian ethics focused on good person with good nature , we believed that who are indwelled by the Holly spirit  can do work that good rewards with blessing , this is that only belivers have heart that purifed by faith .the kind of faith purified the heart purification through believers receive new and good nature ,also work action must flow out of saving faith if God is to be pleased with them as good work, in addition to necesity of saving faith,the scripture also stresses the theme of proper motive when its focused so much Christian Love .', 6, '2020-10-11 15:58:45', '2020-10-16 21:30:16', NULL),
(1978, 560, 828, 'Here we will examine the practical steps that we should take when making ethical decision time and again, to  introduce our approach we will discus on three matters , First, three tendencies of different Christian groups, second ,three perspective on ethical decision making, and third ,the independence of   these perspectives ,\r\nTendencies : there are many different way that believers try to make ethical choices in life , but they tend to fail into three main categories ,some emphasize our Christian conscience and leading of the holy spirit, insisting the action are good if they accord with this internal indicater, others emhazise scripture ,insisting that action are good if they obey the dictation of the scripture, still others emphasize the out come of action, \r\nPerspective :by this we will speak the ethical judgement od decision inthis way, Ethical judgment involves the application of God\'s word ton a person by situation, the bterm situation reminds us of problem, the goal and the consequence of the solution we are to consider , a person to stress the importance of a person nature .\r\nInterdepend : we involved in the situational perspectives ,the situational entails all the relevent facts of wthical questian we are considering, including the person involved in matter and God\'s word wich is standard by wich the matter is to be evaluated .', 8, '2020-10-11 16:15:34', '2020-10-16 21:30:16', NULL),
(1979, 560, 829, 'Ethical judgements involves the application of God\'s word to a situation by a person, We will speak three perspective of approaches toward every ethical judgments :these three are , Situational perspective , the normative perspective , and the existential perspective , \r\n    Situational Perspective : when our ethical enquiries turn to the problem themselves , or to the consequence of action, or to goal we are doing ethics from the situational perspective , this approach maybe called \"teleological\" because its focuses on the end or the result of the action, approaching ethics from the situational perspective involves nothing the relations of means to end in God;s economy ,\r\n  Normative perspective :   the most intuitive perspective for is what we call the normative perspective , normative reffers the facts that God\'s word is the  norm, or standard for ethics, we are doing ethics from normative perspective when we look to the bible to tell nus what to do .\r\n   Existential perspective : this approach ethics by  asking quiestian that are specific to the people involved , we are doing ethics from an existentional perspective , we mean tha this perspective views ethics through the lens of the individual persons experience .', 7, '2020-10-11 16:32:59', '2020-10-16 21:30:16', NULL),
(1980, 560, 830, 'God is also the absolute judge of morality , that is he has the ultimate prerogative to determine whether or not particular action , emotion, and thoughts meet or transgress his moral requirement .and he has the ultimate right and power to act on his determination, \r\n  it is true that God delegates to human beings some responsibility for making ethical judjment , for instance according to the scripture legitimate human government are given limited responsibility too honor  good and punish evil , bible also teach that aour human judgement are olny correct valid insofar as they mirror God\'s judgments , God himself will judge all people thier actions , and thereby he will either confirm or condemn all the judjments that human beings are ever made ,at taht time he will curse those whose works are evil , ahe will bless those whose works are good.', 8, '2020-10-11 16:44:34', '2020-10-16 21:30:16', NULL),
(1981, 560, 831, 'There are three categories of revelation that are the part of God word , we will look first at the normative aspects of God\'s word found IN general, revelation, second at the norm of the special revelation and third at existential revelations \r\nGeneral revelation  :when we speak of genaral revelation we are concern with the way creation ad the history tells us the true things about God ,and his moral requirements of us, general revelation cannot teach us everything , for example , the way of the salvation through Jesus Christ , are taught only trough the special revelation, there are two important features of genaral revalation applies to Christian ethics n :its complexity and its its importance \r\nSpecial revelations: special revelation is a norm that is binding in our lives ,just we did with genaral revelation we will fouse on special revelations complexity and important to christian ethics,special revelation coming us to in number of forms , most of this forms rely on the spoken or writen word ,but involves God communicating with people inways that trancend normal workings of creation ,\r\n     Existential Revelation : it has not been commen for theologians,E xistential revelation the idea that God reveals him sefe in and trough person has always recognize by the mainstream of protastent theology a part of genaral rvelation .', 8, '2020-10-11 17:03:16', '2020-10-16 21:30:16', NULL),
(1982, 560, 832, 'Existential revelation teach us God reveals himself trough person has always been recognized by the main stream part of the general revelation, the supreme judge by which all controversies of religion are to be determined and all decrees of councils , opinions ,of enceinte writers doctrines of men  and private spirit ,are to be examined and in whose sentence we are to rest , can be no other but the Holy spirit speaking in scripture , , the confection state is that the supreme judge in all controversies of religious is the holy spirit , applying to the scripture as the ultimate reveled standard by wich all others are judged , the confession dose not simply  brush aside these others as the usless or invalide , God use councils, enceinte writers ,privat spirit to reviel his will to his people , even thogh thire determination subject to scripture , we can call this human judgement forms of \"existential revelation\" none is a simple presentation of the history or creation and none direct supernatural communication from God .', 8, '2020-10-11 17:18:12', '2020-10-16 21:30:16', NULL),
(1983, 560, 833, 'We affirm that God him self is the ultimate standard of everithing, means right and wrong, good and evil and all, 1John 1:7 teachs us that we have fellowship with one another , and the blood of jesus his son purifies us from all sin, it the picture of God is perfectly free from sin in every nature in this pasage we  can see that we are obligated to see God\'s nature as the standard and the model of goodness and rightness , goodness is his standard, so being kind to others as this passsage teaching, we are following God\'s nature,', 6, '2020-10-11 17:27:56', '2020-10-16 21:30:16', NULL),
(1984, 561, 834, 'Bible claims divine authority ,this is the atributes of the bible, that derives from divine inspiration is the authority of scripture ,because the bible is divinely inspired ,it carries God\'s authorities  ,in one sense scripture is Gods\' voice ,his living active word to every generation,, God has all authority ;there for when ever and how ever he speak all who hear him obligated to obey , , it is still vauable to see how bible speak about its own authority , as well as to look at some moral ,  implication of this authority ,\r\n  the biblical clams divine authority for itself in atleast  two ways, first its provide historical exzample of its authority and second ,it explicitly clams authority .when we remember the close connection between the spoken word of God and written word of God  that we have alrady seen in this lession we can see in many ways bible gives exaple of authority bof God\'s word that applay to the bibel it self \r\nImplication :scripture carries God\'s authority   we are morally obligated to confirm all our choise , action , thoguht ,and feelings to it,', 0, '2020-10-12 15:46:50', '2020-10-12 15:46:50', NULL),
(1985, 561, 835, 'When w easy scripture is clear we do not mean that everithing in the bible is easy to understand or that everithing in the bible stated plainly and directly , insted we mean that the bible is not obscure , it is not filled with hidden meaning that can olyy be dicoverd through mystirious mean , or special spiritual gifting or by those who hold special offices in the church , \r\nAll the scripture are not alike plain in them self , nor alike clear unto all, yet those things which are necessary to be known , believed ,and observed for salvation , are so clearly propounded , and opend in some place of scripture or other ,\r\nscripture speak so plainly about the gospel that every mentally comptent person should be able to figure out that salvation comes through repentance ,', 0, '2020-10-12 16:00:18', '2020-10-12 16:00:18', NULL),
(1986, 561, 836, 'We will speak about popular but mistaken idea that scripture is silent on certain matter perhaps one of the most commen ways that well meaning christian underestimate the sufficiency of scripture . christian frequently teach that some issues of life are morally \'inddiferent\' becouse scripture dose not provide us with sufficient information to know God\'s will on these matters, but Scripture teaches us that God bless some good choice more than he blesse other good choice ,and scripture some time praise one good option over another good option , 1 cor. 7:38 , it should be noted that scholars are not agreed as to the praise circumstances paul adressed here ,\r\n  we will  recall that in our first lession we defined \"good \" nas being that wich receives God\'s blessing and \"evil\" as that which dose not receive his blessing , by this deffenition aspects of human beings and thiere lives are either good or evil;nothing and no one is indiffernat or neutral,', 0, '2020-10-12 16:16:09', '2020-10-12 16:16:09', NULL),
(1987, 561, 837, 'We can see the power of God\'s word through the uninspired preaching of his word or the gospel , Romance 1:15-16 , paul directly stated that the preaching gospel carries God\'s power , the new testament frequently confirms this idea when its says that God works through the preaching of the gospel, Gospel is about about the God who he has power ,\r\nmessage of the cross is foolishness\' to those who are perishing , some people ashamed to preach the gospel because the dont know the power of the gospel, Paul compelled to preach gospel becose he knew the power of the gospel, he realized that this is the only one way to get salvation for all, so it was his responsibility to preach , \r\n we also apply this in our lives today, because Gospel have its power to save thuis world, if we dont preach ,people will perish without salvation, once we realized the poer of gospel we have to share it with others .', 0, '2020-10-12 16:28:50', '2020-10-12 16:28:50', NULL),
(1988, 561, 838, 'Anyone who has read much of the bible should recognize that scripture is not uniform ,it contains histories, poetry, wisdom ,prophecy ,correspondence and all sorts of other writings ,bible displays full range of verity of language that we find in all human communication , it contains statement ,questions, promises , offers ,curse ,exclamations, descriptions , commands, advice   , request ,blessings, threats, judgments, desiers, cries, joy, admiration and Love, and much much more , biblicalm language can be emotionally reserved or emotionally charged , \r\nthe bible includes both sarcasm and sincere language ,this tremendous veriety of lanuage present us with a number of challenges when we read the bible , but it is safe to say that there are solutions to understand these lanugaes , they are fallen in two gropes, Extraordinary and ordinary uses of language , \r\nExtraordinary : those who believe this they over simplify biblical language in order to develop a system of interpretation that can be applied fairly to all scripture    \r\nOrdinary :they belive bible is not obscure , that it is not filled with hidden meanings that can only be discoverd by mysterious means , or through special spiritual giftting .', 0, '2020-10-12 16:46:57', '2020-10-12 16:46:57', NULL),
(1989, 561, 839, 'The primacy of ten commandment is both historical and theological , their historical primacy depends on the fact that ,to our knowledge ,these laws were the first written legal code that was received by the nation of israel, Paul reffers to the giving of the Ten commandments as the the introduction of law , indicating that this was the first time israel had possesed God\'s law in this form, now the ten commandment were not only the law given to israel  as they camped at the foot of mount sinai, together with ten commanments book of the covenant also given, \r\nin addition to having  a temporal primacy the ten commandment also had theological or ideological primacy , God himself wrote the Ten commandment on stone tablets . Deut:9:10 confirms that God him self carved the Ten commandment in the stone tablet ,\r\nThe theological primacy of Ten commandment is also indicated by the special occasion  on wich Israel recieved them , the giving of the laws was attended by thunder and lighting, smoke, clouds and heavenly trumpets , during tyhjis time God allowed himself to be viewed not only by Moses , but also by Josua, aron, and seventy elders of Israel.', 0, '2020-10-12 17:03:37', '2020-10-12 17:03:37', NULL),
(1990, 561, 840, 'In most protestant branches of the church it has been commen to categorize the various laws in the old testament bible in to three major groups , Moral law, ceremonial law, and civil law ,  \r\nMoral laws are typicaly thought to convey God\'s ethical standard and are usualy identified with the Ten commandments , Civil law provide for the governing of society , especially during the period of Israel\'s theocracy , Ceremonial law  in turn are those winch provide instruction for worshiping God ,frequently these are the most closely associated with the old testament sacrificial system, and Tabernacle and Temple administration, \r\nmany theologians agree on the validity  of the traditional  categories of old testament law, they often disagree on how to apply these category to study of ethics,   some have said that all acatogories of law dont apply to modern Christan , in thier understanding  the existence of these catogory and the proper identification of law provied a mechanism by wich they can avoid applying God\'s word to thier lives .other theologians have said that all the indidual laws still apply but only with regard to some of thier aspects .still other have argued that the traditional catogories simply help us to see how each aspect of each law should appllied in life of every christian .', 0, '2020-10-12 17:21:22', '2020-10-12 17:21:22', NULL),
(1991, 561, 841, 'according to theologians opinion civil law is provided for the governing of society , especly during the period of Israel theocracy aswell as the law of ceremonial provide for the instruction to worship god , especially in the sacrificial system in the Tabernacle , these all system for a period of time , and for a particular people ,it was not  for the modern Christian, but still we can apply the system and the message god given through these laws, in our modern system we can follow the indidual aspects of the civil and ceremonial laws, We believe that since the death , bujriel and the ressurection and ascention of christ , God people are nologer to perform many of the specific behaviors that were requierd under Mosaic sacrifical and temple system , but still we can find many motral and ethical facts in the given laws, we can apply this in our life, only the messages  not the system .', 0, '2020-10-12 17:34:47', '2020-10-12 17:34:47', NULL),
(1992, 557, 842, 'There are three basic types of the situational content of revelation we will take closure look at the content of revelation by looking briefly at each of the situational elements , first revelation interims of the fact its present to us, second the goal revelations obligates us to pursue , and the third the means revelation teaches us to use as we pursue the goals , Facts :it would be impossible to list every fact that special , general, and existential communicate to us , in order toi illustare the important role that dfdacts play in our ethical evaluations , the most basic fact we learn through revelation, from the situational perspective God is our ultimate fact , our ultimate ethical environment, \r\nGoals :goals in ethics , we have in mind the expected outcome of our endeavors .in many ways this is not different from the way set goal to accomplish anything els in life ,\r\nMeans:answer any ethical question in a biblically manner  we must not only know thye fact and goals, God has reveled , but we must also find the apropriate means that God has reveled ,', 8, '2020-10-13 15:45:41', '2020-10-16 21:31:04', NULL),
(1993, 557, 843, 'It would be impossible to list every facts that are special, genaral, when we studied the normative perspective ,God\'s character is our ultimate norm or standard , corresponding from the situational factys God is our ultimate facts, the reality of God existence rules over every ethical questions , and obligates us to live by the standard of His character ,in order for us to know our obligation befor God , he must reveal himself to us, and this is were revelation comes in, through revelation god tells us fact about him self, and fact about what he require, \r\nGod is the suprime authority over all creation , his authority is absolute , and his charecter is the perfect expression of his will , so when we reveal his charecter the revelation is the means through wich God exercise control much like human goverments exercise through thier law,', 7, '2020-10-13 15:57:57', '2020-10-16 21:31:04', NULL),
(1994, 557, 844, 'When we speak of Goal in ethics we have in mind the expected outcomes of our endeavors . in many ways this is non different from the way that we set goal to accomlish anything else in life , in most cace goal are rather complex ,if the action are to be truly good , ultimate goal must be to do it all for the glory of God , biblical goal always glorify and thank God, we must glorify him in all tyhat we do , in short its teaches us to nset God\'s golry as our highest goal, understanding biblical goals also helps us to descern the goal from evil and good, biblical goal is always understand by the revelation , special revelation gives us the countless goals that must be consider in christian ethics .', 7, '2020-10-13 16:08:58', '2020-10-16 21:31:04', NULL),
(1995, 557, 845, 'Strategy of rigorous will proceed in the same manner as our discussion of laxity , we will present a general description of rigor as a strategy , second example for consequens of rigor , \r\nWhen christians are includes to follow a rigorous strategy towards revelation they are extremely concerned  to guard against sin, especially bas it is defined in the prohibitions listed in scripture ,as a risult they tend to err on side of overly restricting behaviour rfather than on the side of permitting it, the strategy of rigor also commonly results from mistaken belief about the bible\'s similarity to modern  world and about its clarity , \r\nThere are many negative result of this rigorous approach , its destroys christian freedom by prohibiting behaviors that are wrong under certain conditions , but good under other conditions .\r\n  as we have seen a strategy of rigor generally depends  on one of two illusion ,on the one hand , it can result from the mistaken beliefe situational fetuires ,', 8, '2020-10-13 16:25:10', '2020-10-16 21:31:04', NULL),
(1996, 557, 846, 'Jesus emphasized the importance of the kingdom of God in three different times in the sermon of the mount ,first , we will look nate the discussion of the kingdom of God in the beatitude at the beginning of the sermon , second consider the lords prayer, third teaching about earthly needs, jesus indicated that the kindom of god muat be the main priority of our lives \r\n  Mathew 5:3-12 jesus teaches us a beatitude is a nstatement about blessing, teaching on blessedness are important of ethics , theology viwed as a meaning of determining wich bhuman person , acts and attituds receive God\'s blessing and wich do not, whatever God bless is good and right , so the beatitudes ,jesus began his sermon by encoraging people to live ethically ,\r\n  in lord\'s prayer : found in Mathew 6:9-13 focuses on the kingdom of God as the goal for ethics, \r\nEarthly needs :nMathew 6:25-34 ,  everyone has earthly needs , such as food and clothing , but jesus taught that we should not experience anxiety over these issues , insted we should focus on God\'s kingdom .', 8, '2020-10-13 16:42:00', '2020-10-16 21:31:04', NULL),
(1997, 557, 847, 'There are many ways to describe the kingdom of God , but we will speak of main three components of the kingdom, first the role of the king, second the people or citizen and third the covenants that govern the relationship between king and his people , \r\n King:  in ancient world of bible people were very familiar with kings and kingdom, in those days kings were  expected to fullfill thier responsibility to citizen of their countries , they were to protect and provide for them , and treat them with kindness , kings also have the legal authority to to tax, to traise army, and regulate many aspect of life, \r\n in bible God is frequently  presented as the suzerain or supreme emperor over all creation, \r\n   People: since God is the emperor over all creation ,there is a sense in wich is reign has always been over every living person , but when bible speak about the people of kingdom it is usually reffering to the people that God has called to himself in contrast to the people of the world who follow the ways of evil .\r\nRelation between :in ancient world kings often administrated their great empiers by imposing covenant or treaties upon vassal nation and their kings, these covanat typically mention the kings and stated the consequence of obedience or disobedience to these obligation .', 8, '2020-10-13 16:59:28', '2020-10-16 21:31:04', NULL),
(1998, 557, 848, 'It has been a longstanding tradition to summarize the bible story in terms of three historical phase :creation , fall and redemption , \r\nInitial peace: in the beginning when God created the world  humanity lived in  the perfect harmony with God , Adam and Eve were obedient servants, and as result there was peace between God and humanity , during this period God appointed human beings to serve as his vassal kings, as result Adam and Eve blessed with close fellowship with God and continued to live in the garden of Eden wher life was blissful and easy , during this time of peace in the garden of Eden , human life was full of joy and gladness , of thanksgiving and singing , in this initial period rest of the world was undeveloped\r\nRebellion : as we all know that the story of humanity\'s   initial rebellion against God .Gens 3, records that serpent tempted Eve to eat from the forbidden tree of knowledge of good and evel, they eat , by sinning in this way humanity violated one of their covenant obligations. God throw\'s them out of the garden, force them to live inthe world where the ground was hard to work , humanitybhas continued to rebel againist God , God has continued to punish and curs them, but mercifully God did not abandon us,\r\nFinal peace: God began to restore peace  to his kingdom immediately after humanity fall in to sin, God did not  immediately strike Adam and  Eve dead b when they suinned, but he allowed them to live.', 8, '2020-10-13 17:17:12', '2020-10-16 21:31:04', NULL),
(1999, 557, 849, NULL, 0, '2020-10-13 17:19:31', '2020-10-13 17:19:31', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(2000, 556, 876, 'Jesus\' unique sonship is clear in the gospel of John. John 1:1-18 we see that the Jesus is the eternal word of God. it means that he is both God himself and the only begotten of the Father John 8:18-23 we see Jesus as the Father\'s son , he had come from above, that he had not originated in this world. John 10:3- says that he and the Father are one. \r\nJohn 5:18 Jesus was even calling God his own Father, making himself equal with God.\r\nwhen Bible says that Jesus is the son Of God , it means that he is both unique and divine.\r\nHebrews 1:1-3 says that son of God, Jesus created the universe and  is the exact representation of the Father\'s being , Jesus is identified as God\'s son in a special way that indicates his eternal divine nature.\r\nAs the son of God, Christ is equal in power and glory to the Father and the Holy Spirit. \r\nSo the New Testament teaches us that the Jesus is the son of God, one of the three persons in the Trinity.', 8, '2020-10-13 17:44:10', '2020-10-16 21:31:40', NULL),
(2001, 556, 877, 'When the New Testament calls Jesus Lord, it is translating from Greek Word kurios. Kurios means ruler or master, or English word Sir.\r\nNew testament  also used the word kurios as a name for God as in Mathew 11:25, Acts 2:39.\r\nRomans 10:9,13 Everyone who calls on the name of the Lord shall be saved .\r\nJoel 2:32 when compared Paul says that Jesus is Lord, he means that Jesus is Yahweh, the Lord and the God of Old Testament.\r\nJesus is the Lord from Isaiah 40 Jesus is the Lord, whose path John has prepared .\r\nHebrews 1:10 where the Lord Jesus is the God that Psalms 102: 24.25 who created the world. \r\nIn the Apostles creed  we are affirming the biblical teachings that Jesus Christ is God, and that as God he is a full member of the trinity with the same divine attributes as the Father and the Holy Spirit.', 8, '2020-10-13 17:55:33', '2020-10-16 21:31:40', NULL),
(2002, 556, 878, 'Jesus\' experiences prove that he was truly human. these affirm at least four aspects of Jesus\' humanity\r\n His Generation:\r\nFirst , he was conceived by the holy spirit rather than human father. Jesus began in the same way that all human being after Adam and eve had begun as tiny baby in his mother\'s womb.\r\nLuke 2:5-6\r\nMary herself recognized that to conceive a child in this way would require a miracle.\r\nJesus could not have been truly human because he did not have a human father, but the very first human did nit have fathers either, or mothers.\r\nHis body:\r\nMathew 27. Luke 23 says that Jesus suffered under Pontius Pilate in a variety of ways. Jesus\' sufferings, crucifixion, death and burial shows that he was a real man with physical human body.\r\nHis Soul;\r\nHebrews 4:12 speaks of our soul by many different terms , but the most common are soul and spirit.\r\nthe words \" soul and Spirit both refers the same underlying reality that man consists of only two main parts : body and soul.\r\nFather into your hands i command my spirit. Luke 23:46\r\nwhen Jesus died on the cross , he indicated that while his body would be placed into the grave , his human spirit or soul would be in the hands of God the Father.\r\n\r\nResurrection : this proves that Jesus was real human being. the resurrections of his body  occurred when his human soul was introduced into his perfect human body\r\n1 Corinthians 15:20-23', 9, '2020-10-13 18:11:49', '2020-10-16 21:31:40', NULL),
(2003, 556, 879, 'Christ comes from Greek word \"Christos\", which in turn is the translation of the Old Testament Hebrew word Mashiach or messiah meaning :anointed one\"  \r\nthe rem anointed one in the old testament applies to the descendants of David that serves as kings over Israel and Judah.\r\nPsalms 89:38\r\nMany old testament prophets talked about the Messiah or Christ as a descendant of David who could return the exiles to the promised land , bring God\'s greatest blessings to the restored nation.\r\nJeremiah 23:5, 6\r\nThe New Testament speaks of Jesus as the Christ in over 500 places. John 1:41 and john 4:25-26 John explains that Messiah means the same thing as Christ.\r\nJesus conversation with the woman at the well John 4:25-26, Jesus admitted to being the Messiah prophesied by the Old Testament.', 8, '2020-10-13 18:22:29', '2020-10-16 21:31:40', NULL),
(2004, 556, 880, 'Jesus has a human nature means that he possesses all the attributes and traits that are essential to being human- thins like a physical human body and a rational human soul. Jesus is fully human in every respect: he has a body and soul, he was subject to sickness, injury and  death, he had normal physical limitations.\r\nJesus is a perfect human being, whereas the rest of us are flawed.\r\nbut Jesus is different ,He was born without sin and lived a perfect , sinless life.\r\nJesus had a true and complete human nature, as the commission of sin and even the ability to sin are not essential to bein human.\r\nAdam and eve lived this way, before the fall.\r\nso it is possible to have a human being that does not sin, sinfulness is not an essential attribute of humanity. that is why we say that Jesus human nature includes all the attributes and traits that are essential to being human.\r\n what makes Jesus different is the fact that , he is the only person that possess two natures : a human nature and a divine nature.\r\nJesus is both god and man, being both fully human and fully divine at the same time.\r\nthe term we used to describe the existence of both a human and divine nature in the person of Christ is hypostatic union.', 8, '2020-10-13 18:36:39', '2020-10-16 21:31:40', NULL),
(2005, 563, 633, 'The word eschatology comes from two Greek words: eschatos meaning \"last\" or \"final\"; and logos in this case meaning \"study\". So, \"eschatology\" is \"the study of last things\" or \"the doctrine of last things\". Broadly understood, eschatology covers the entire period of the last days that began with Jesus\' life and ministry, and that will be completed when he returns.\r\nOld Testament Expectation: God\'s kingdom was expected to unfold in three phases: the initial creation of the universe and its creatures; a long period of redemption necessitated by humanity\'s fall into sin; and finally, the everlasting eschaton- the ultimate state of the universe, after redemption is complete, when God\'s heavenly kingdom fills the earth.', 7, '2020-10-14 15:36:17', '2020-10-16 21:32:06', NULL),
(2006, 563, 634, 'Creation\r\nGod\'s work of creation is detailed in Genesis chapters 1 & 2. God intended humanity to be his \"vassals\" or servant kings to rule over creation on behalf of God, the great \"suzerain\" or emperor. \r\nCultural Mandate: God\'s command to reproduce and create human culture throughout the world (Genesis 1:27-28). That means not only reproducing to create enough people to fill the world, but also creating human culture throughout the world. Humanity\'s directive to \"work\" and \"take care\" of the garden (Genesis 2:15) uses language that also describes the priests\' work in the tabernacle (Numbers 3:8).\r\nHuman beings are God\'s royal and priestly images that serve and honor him by ruling over creation on his behalf.  Our job is to extend his rule until it fills the world, and to cultivate the whole earth until everything resembles the Garden of Eden.', 8, '2020-10-14 15:43:52', '2020-10-16 21:32:06', NULL),
(2007, 558, 850, 'From cover to cover scripture make it clear that God has authority ,the right to rule over all creation .this right to rule derives from the fact that the God is the creator and sustainer of all creation , there is no remnant of creation that God dose not bring into existence or that dose not depend on him for its continue existence ,we need to understand God\'s control over creation in different way , becose the scripture are very clear about certain aspects of God\'s control, \r\nin order to preserve human ethical responsibility open theism teaches that God has either limited his sovereignty voluntarily   ,christian theology always thaught that God\'s sovereign control is completely compatible with human responsibility  .\r\nAlso God has present with humanity as our covenant king ever since he created Adam and Eve , God has always been invisibly omnipresent, but also appeared in many visible manifestation , in our ethical responsibility we know that his presents and controll are there always .', 7, '2020-10-14 15:47:14', '2020-10-16 21:32:35', NULL),
(2008, 563, 635, 'Redemption \r\nAll Christian should know the story of humanity\'s fall into sin recorded in Genesis 3. God put Adam and Eve in the garden to work it and to take care of it. But Satan spoke through the serpent in the garden. He tricked Eve into eating the fruit from the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil, which God had forbidden. Then Eve gave the fruit to Adam and he ate it, too. Because of this sin, God cursed all humanity, and the great hope of his eschatological kingdom appeared to be lost. But God mercifully introduced a plan of redemption that would rescue individuals through personal salvation, and would restore the hope of his great messianic kingdom on earth. Proto-Euangelion (\'\'first gospel\")- the plan of redemption first introduced after the Fall (Genesis 3:15). God promised to redeem humanity from the curse of sin. He continued to affirm this expectation through redemptive acts associated with his covenants.', 8, '2020-10-14 15:50:54', '2020-10-16 21:32:06', NULL),
(2009, 558, 851, 'Human experiences typically limited to the natural world  , we constantly interact with other other people as well as with our physical environment , and we normaly try to explain most of the world and events around us as natural phenomena, so we really much emphasis on the preternatural world .but the fact is that the angel and demons have significant impact on the things that happen in our lives, \r\nInhabitance :scripture teaches us that God has populated the univers with a vast number of spiritual person known as Angels and demons, both angels and demons are intelligent ,rational beings that have will and personalities ,when God created these being thay wer all angels ,pure and perfect , serving God in his heavenly kingdom\r\nAngels serve as God\'s loyal messengers and agents , they communicate his word to human beings, and they interact with humanity on God\'s behalf    , some time these are dramatic event , God\'s angels are continuely working to ensure that we always have an opportunity to behave morally .', 7, '2020-10-14 16:02:14', '2020-10-16 21:32:35', NULL),
(2010, 563, 636, '1. Adam- After Adam sinned, God offered him salvation through the proto-euangelion (Genesis 3:15). Expectation- God\'s worldwide kingdom would come to pass, but its growth would be characterized by strife between the children of the serpent and the children of Eve. From the beginning, human race has been divided between those who serve God\'s purposes and those who rebel against God.\r\n2. Noah- God made a covenant through Noah never to flood the earth again and to establish the stability of nature (Gen 8:21-9:17).\r\nExpectation- The growth of God\'s kingdom would proceed without further global catastrophes. \r\n3. Abraham- God called Abraham and his descendants to serve him in a special way. They were the special nation through whom God would extend redemption to rest of humanity.\r\nExpectation- God\'s earthly kingdom would include members from all nations on earth. \r\n4. Moses- God confirmed that the Mosaic covenant incorporated and continued the early covenants. God promised if they repented of their sin and sought him with all their heart and soul, he would restore them to his in \"later days\"\r\nExpectations- In future age, God would fulfill all of his covenant promises of blessings for his people and judgement against his enemies.\r\n5. David- God promised to establish the house of David as permanent dynasty ruling God\'s earthly kingdom. \r\nExpectation- God\'s kingdom is a real place, populated by real people who will live in perfect harmony with God forever.', 9, '2020-10-14 16:02:16', '2020-10-16 21:32:06', NULL),
(2011, 563, 637, 'Theological Developments, two great ages of Jewish eschatology: \"this age\" (olam hazeh)- characterized by sin, exile, suffering, and death; began at the Fall and corresponds to the age of redemption. And \"the age to come\" (olam haba)- future eschaton when God\'s kingdom would fill the earth; characterized by forgiveness, righteousness, peace and eternal life. Most first century Jewish sects agreed that the Messiah would lead an army of angels and faithful men to victory over Israel\'s enemies. Many of God\'s people that the prophecies in Daniel chapters 2&7 indicated that their oppression was about to end. Jesus and New Testament writers also taught the Messiah would end \"this age\" of sin and death and usher in \"the age to come\" with all its blessing (Mark 10:29-30). Jesus indicated that he was the Messiah that was expected to bring transition from this age to the age to come (Mark 10:29; Matthew 12:32). Paul associated the triumph of the age to come with Christ, the Messiah (Eph 1:20-21, 1 Cor 2:6-8, 1 Tim 6:17-19). Jesus and his apostles and prophets agreed with most other Jews in their day about the basic structure of the eschaton.', 9, '2020-10-14 16:14:00', '2020-10-16 21:32:06', NULL),
(2012, 558, 852, 'The details of natural world are nearly limitless, so we will focus on our attention on the natural world as a whole ,In Genesis 1, moses describe the creeation of the natural realm  in way that emphasized the central importance of humanity upon the earth  ,we can see the human beings are the part of the nature ,God created us from the dust of the ground , and because we are part of the nature we have an ethical obligation to protect it ,God called human being toi govern the world, to administrate in  the way that promotes life and growth , tuning the world into kingdom that is fit for him to inhabit, \r\nFall: now we have looked at the original state of the natural realm at creation , now we will look at the humanity\'s fall in to sin, and particular to the impact on the natural world .when Adam and eve commited sin, god responded by cursing both the human race and the earth , subjecting them to curreption, these cause the earth to oppose the lordship of humanity in many ways , it become difficult to numan beings to work the land to make it produce food, as the result of this curs natural world is affected by sin in many ways, \r\nRedemption:when humanity fell into sin tha natural realm become both an instrument of cursing and recipient of cursing, but the redemption both of thede effects are reversed  .', 8, '2020-10-14 16:17:22', '2020-10-16 21:32:35', NULL),
(2013, 558, 853, 'There are two Realms what we see in the bible , preternatural realm, and natural realm, natural realm :this is the world that God created for the human beings in Gensis 1, the world which we live and operate , and without a doubt it is the side of creation that is most familiar to human being , and another is preternatural realm, that realm that beyond nature , it is not above , nature in the way that God is , but is nrayher beside nature as a distinct aspects of creation, this is the realm inhabited by visible spirt such as angels and demons, \r\nin the natural realm we huamn being constantly inrtact with each other , people as well as with our phycial body, but in preternatural world angels and demons done not have any physicals endowment, but still angels working as Gods mesengers as we inthe natural world ,', 8, '2020-10-14 16:32:27', '2020-10-16 21:32:35', NULL),
(2014, 558, 854, 'In Genesis 1:27-28, goodness of humanity will focus on three details of humanity cvreation mentioned in the verses we just read , Humamnity was created as the image of God, the visible presentation of God that depicted his goodness , when theologians talk about humanity as the image of God they often speak about attributes like reason, spiritually , moral nature , immortality , and our original righteousness , its true that some degree human beings share these attributes in common with God, \r\nBlessings: creation of the humanity as the image of God is confirmed by athe fact that God pronounced a blessings on humanity , ,in Genesis 1:28 records an important event took palce when humanity was created , we defined \"good\" not only in terms of chatrecter , but also in terms of what he blesse and approves .\r\nCultural mandate: in keeping with humanity\'s role as God\'s image ,God appointed humanity to his vassal king on the earth , to fill subdue and rule it for his glory, as we created original created human beings were able to build a holy, righteous kingdom fit for God\'s habitation .', 8, '2020-10-14 16:48:40', '2020-10-16 21:32:35', NULL),
(2015, 558, 855, 'It may seems odd to some of us to speak of the fall as damaging our ability to obtain moral knowledge ,after all unbelievers can pic up a bible and understand its commands, scripture itself affirm that unbelievers know many true things about God , but when we look more closly at the scripture we see that while fallen and unredeemed human beings posses some true knowledge the fall has prevented them from obtaing a proper knowledge of God\'s command, \r\n  sin hinders huamnity bto access to god\'s revelation, and understanding the God\'s revelation, and sin\'s has made an impact on humanity to obedient God\'s revelation, fall has hindred humanity acces to revelation, by limiting the ho,y spirit\'s work of illumination and inward leading, humanity\'s fall into sin profoundly reduse our ability to make sense of God\'s revelation, even though fallen human beings still have acces to much of God\'s revelation, we lack many  of the skill needed to comperhend it,', 8, '2020-10-14 17:01:35', '2020-10-16 21:32:35', NULL),
(2016, 558, 856, 'There are countless things that scripture says about God\'s being , God\'s attributes are inseparable from his person, they define who he is , this is the one reason ,that  the writers of scripture commonly describe and even named God according to his attributes, for example he is called \"Father of compassion \"  and \"God of all comfort\" by identifing  God\'s attributes in these ways , the writers of scripture were teaching us about God as person, they were describing his fundamental character,\r\n as we consider God\'s being it is imposible to remember that all of God\'s essential attribuites are immutable , meanig that they never change , for instance , God cannot be holy one day and unholy next day,', 6, '2020-10-14 17:14:01', '2020-10-16 21:32:49', NULL),
(2017, 558, 857, NULL, 0, '2020-10-14 17:14:43', '2020-10-14 17:14:43', NULL),
(2018, 559, 858, 'our discussion of allegiance will divide into three parts , First Loyalty we owe to God and to others , second the Life orientation and third important of discovering our responsibility , these are some of the main ways that the  bible speak abut allegiance .so thay will give us a good foundation for understanding allegiance as whole ,\r\nLoyalty :Loyalty is the cornerstone of the concept of the love , old testament consistently protryes God as the covenant king over his people , he is supreme emperor , and his people are vassal or servant kingdom, the most basic responsibility of the people is loyalty to the king , \r\nOrientation :the allegiant we owe to God touches every area of our lives ,there is no aspect of life take place otside the kingdom or beyond his sovereign rule ,for this reason our lives must be comprehensively oriented around him, God and his kingdom must be our highest priority ,the focus of our desire ,and the center of our world view ,we must be inwardly disposed to work for the benefits of God and his people in everything that we think ,say and do.\r\nResponsibility :Love is an orientation of the obedience and service to God, it should dispose us to keep all of God\'s commandment . our loving allegians to God should motivate us to seek out additional ways that we are responsibility to him,', 8, '2020-10-15 15:47:15', '2020-10-16 21:33:30', NULL),
(2019, 559, 859, 'God\'s action will divide into two parts , specifically God\'s action serves as model for our own behavior , we will look at the God\'s action of atoning grace , also at his action of common grace ,\r\nAtoning grace :God\'s character is our ultimate ethical standard .and because God always act according to his character , all his action are perfect expression of his  character .this is why scripture commenly exhorts us to patteern both our character and our actio0n after God\'s especially with regards to his rescue redemption of those he love, \r\nas a sinner we were offensive to God , we ahted him, we were set againest him , we deserved punishment , not mercy , but God was willing to sacrifice his son, \r\ncommon grace :common grace is a technical term in theology that refers to God\'s kingdom to thoise who will never be saved , for those of us who will ultimately receive salvation  God\'s grace always work towards our redemption, but God also extended non -redemptive kindness or \"common grace\" to those who will never recive salvation, \r\nTo be sure ,Gopd\'s general love for humanity is not nearly as great as his love for believers , neverthless it is true and genuin an it provbide a model that we are to imitate .', 8, '2020-10-15 16:03:15', '2020-10-16 21:33:30', NULL),
(2020, 559, 860, 'Scripture speaks of human heart in many differnt ways , but we will discuss description of the heart as the depth of our inner person and seat of our motive ,there is a great deal overlap between the biblical concept of heart , mind thought ,spirit and soul, God requierd hois people to love him with thier hearts , God\'s law was to be written in their heart , so that tahy would obey him their heart , God required whole hearted obedience-obedience that flows from our heart , \r\n  having seen good motives are necessary because good works must be done from the heart , we must have good motive when we make ethical decision   ,', 6, '2020-10-15 16:13:43', '2020-10-16 21:33:30', NULL),
(2021, 559, 861, 'Scripture says so much about faith ,it would be impossible for us to mention every way faith service as a motive  , there is much more that could be said about saving faith , scripture talk abut saving faith in two main ways ,one is faith as the means of initial salvation , other is same saving faith as ongoing commitment through out our Christian life ,  \r\n i do remember when i came to saving faith , it was in a revival meeting, message was al about the important of salvation, value of the life, and how to cme to salvation, this change me to saving faith, i started to believe in Christ, \r\nComing to faith this totally effect my motives and behavior, i came to know that only faith cant save me, i have to change my behavior , motives, i had to leave many worldy  motives , desires , i had change my behavior to Christ like ,  if you dont have a good behavior and motive  you ncant have a saving faith, this change me  to having a fait in christ wich vcan save my life .', 6, '2020-10-15 16:26:25', '2020-10-16 21:33:30', NULL),
(2022, 559, 862, 'The term imagination simply refers to our ability to form mental image of thigs that are beyond our experience , it many seen strange , to think of imagination as away acquiring ethical knowledge . but as we see our imaginative abilities are vital, to learn and thinking about God , the world and our selves , a typical way to think about imagination as creativity is to consider the steps artist take when drawing picture , imagination is involved in everithing we make or create , we use our imagination every day  for simple acts or creativity , 1 samuel 12:1-7 under the inspiration of the holy spirit Nathan created an imaginary ethical situation, an imaginary leagal case ,as this biblical example illustrate , imagination enables us to form and to recognize moral patterns and analogies , we have to use our other faculties to make sure that the conclution of our imagination agree with God\'s word . but we can still have a good degree of confidence in our imagination when we use carefuly and rightly ,because the holy spirit gives us this facully as a reliable tool for assessing ethical knowledge .', 8, '2020-10-15 16:42:58', '2020-10-16 21:33:30', NULL),
(2023, 559, 863, 'Christian go extremes when thay think about the role of reason in ethics , on the one side some theological traditions give reason more attention to any of other existential faculties , these theologians some time speak abut \"primacy of the intellect\" as if our reason were to be trusted above all  other abelites and capacities , but we must always remember that to user reason rightly ,in making ethnical decision  reason is the one of the main think in assessing knowledge, \r\n  an other side we will consider our conscience  as our God given ability to discern good and evil  , it is the sense of conviction that our thoughts,words and deeds are either pleasing God or offensive to God ,in case we have sinned , our conscience have rightly condemn us as guilty and encorage us to repent ,the same way emotions are also included in assessing knowledge , emations are our inner feeling , they are the efcteive aspect of our ethical sensitivity , Emotions are God given human ability that enable us to assess our knowledge in many different ways .', 8, '2020-10-15 17:00:18', '2020-10-16 21:33:30', NULL),
(2024, 559, 864, 'Our will is our capacity for making decision , its our volition , our ability to make choices , so each time we make a choice or a decision , we are using our will, like all our existential faculties ,our will is perspective on our whole person, so nwe will not make the mistake of thinking that it is in tention with our other capacities and abilities , rather to speak of our will is to view our entier decision making process from the perspective of the choice we make , \r\nmaking the right decision is often hard because will is affected by our fallen nature , there always possibility that indwelling sin will persuade us to make sinful decision , now it is imporant to understand and recognize that our will may be either active or passive, this is to say some time we make decision is a passive , unconscious manner, such as by force of habit , but other time the ethical question we face require active reflection   and conscience decision .', 8, '2020-10-15 17:13:00', '2020-10-16 21:33:30', NULL),
(2025, 559, 865, 'Commitment are important in ethics because there ia a sense in which they govern all our choices . to be more specific , we chose according to the commitments that we feel most greatly at the moment that we choose , when our righteous commitments are the strongest we act according to our hertfelt loyality to God and judges our behavior to be good , but when we give our sinful commitments ,god judge our behavior to be evil as jesud said in Luke 6:45, the good man brings good things out of the good stored up in his heart , and evil man bring evil things out of the evil stored up in his heart , \r\n our commitments as the things are stored up in our hearts.we express our commitment to God in good works, i suggest and speach to sumbit our heart to the holy spirit as he work within us to confirm all our commitments to God\'s character , Bothe thoughts and understanding of this word, with our understanding of our commitments and loyality in mind we do things, will bring good outcome .', 8, '2020-10-15 17:27:04', '2020-10-16 21:33:30', NULL),
(2026, 567, 638, 'Eschatology as \"the study of last things\" or \"the doctrine of last things.\" We also said that eschatology covers the entire period of the last days, which began with Jesus\' life and ministry and will be completed when he returns. Individual eschatology- the study of how individual human beings experience the events of the last days.\r\n\r\nPresent State- During the last days, or eschaton: believers (\"the regenerate\")- experience both hardships of  \"this age\" (e.g sin, death)and blessings of the \"age to come\" (e.g forgiveness, salvation) unbelievers (\"the unregenerate\")- experience mostly the hardships of \"this age.\" \r\n\r\nRegenerate means recreated or reborn; It is the spiritually living of a person. \r\nUnregenerate is what is not recreated or reborn; it means that they are spiritually dead. Fallen human beings are born spiritually dead and remain in this state unless they are renewed or \"regenerated\" by the Holy Spirit.', 8, '2020-10-16 15:39:59', '2020-10-16 21:33:57', NULL),
(2027, 567, 639, 'Moral inability- no capacity to please God or merit his blessing. Augustine\'s states of moral ability: posse non peccare- the ability not to sin (Adam and Eve\'s moral state before the fall) \r\nnon posse non peccare- the inability not to sin (Adam and Eve\'s moral after the Fall)\r\nAfter the Fall, all of Adam and Eve\'s naturally generated descendants lost the moral ability to avoid sin . The unregenerate live under sin\'s control and remain in the state of spiritual death until God saves them. The unregenerate are morally incapable of doing works that God considers to be good (Luke 6:43-45; Romans 8:6-8).', 8, '2020-10-16 15:45:39', '2020-10-16 21:33:57', NULL),
(2028, 567, 640, '1. Spiritual Life- The regenerate are those who have been born again (or regenerated) through the work of the Holy Spirit. The Bible teaches that to become regenerate, our souls must pass from death into life: \"spiritual resurrection\"- John 5:24; Ephesians 2:4-5; Colossians 2:13. \"rebirth\"- John 3:3-6;\r\n2. Moral ability- the capacity to please God and merit his blessings. Our moral ability does not enable us to earn salvation, but it does empower us to obey God\'s will. Augustine\'s state of moral ability: posse non peccare- the ability not to sin, non posse non peccare- the ability not to sin. \r\nEven though we continue to struggle with sin, we also do good works because of the Spirit\'s influence.\r\n3. Reconciliation to God- Through Christ\'s death, we\'ve been brought into his household as heirs of his covenant promises (Romans 5:10). Because we\'re united to Christ: we share Jesus\' status as God\'s favored Son. God credits Christ\'s perfections and righteousness to our account. No punishment remains for us- only blessings. Union with Christ is a fulfillment of God\'s eschatological promises.', 8, '2020-10-16 15:56:11', '2020-10-16 21:33:57', NULL),
(2029, 567, 641, 'Terms used for \"hell\" in Scripture: \r\nSheol- home of unregenerate souls (Psalm 9:17)\r\nAbaddon- \"destruction\" (Job 26:6, Proverbs 15:11)\r\nBowr- \"pit\"; a place of punishment (Isaiah 14:15-19)\r\nHades- place of punishment (Luke 10:15)\r\nabussos- \"abyss\" prison for demons (Luke 8:31)\r\nplace for human souls, including Jesus\' righteous soul (Romans 10:7)\r\nGehenna- universally identifies a place of fiery punishment, torment and destruction. It\'s mentioned in many passages, including Matthew 5:22. Gehenna is often described as bodily suffering, which associates it with the final state, rather than with the intermediate state. Suggesting that it\'s where unregenerate souls go during the intermediate state. Jesus described a rich man who died and was immediately tormented in Hades.', 8, '2020-10-16 16:02:52', '2020-10-16 21:33:57', NULL),
(2030, 567, 642, 'Regenerate souls continue to exist just like unregenerate souls do. But their experience is far different. Whereas unregenerate souls suffer a foretaste of their final punishment, regenerate soul enjoy a foretaste of their final blessings. \r\n1. Lord\'s presence- When the regenerate die, their souls are immediately taken into God\'s presence in heaven (Luke 23:43, Revelation 6:9). Regenerate souls are taken into Lord\'s presence regardless of whether or not their bodies rest in physical graves. Jesus, Paul and others believed they would enjoy each other\'s presence in heaven immediately upon their deaths. \r\n2. Fellowship- During the intermediate state, regenerate souls fellowship with other regenerate souls in heaven: Martyrs in heaven know and fellowship with each other and together appeal to God to hasten the final judgement. Hebrews speaks of a heavenly assembly that includes every regenerate person who has experienced physical death (Hebrews 11:40). \r\n3. Perfect Holiness- During the intermediate state, regenerate souls reach perfect holiness. Human holiness- moral purity and acceptability in God\'s presence. Augustine\'s states of moral ability: Scripture suggests that we lose the ability to sin when we enter the intermediate state (Hebrews 12:23). \"The souls of believers are at their death made perfect in holiness, and do immediately pass into glory\"', 9, '2020-10-16 16:13:20', '2020-10-16 21:33:57', NULL),
(2031, 566, 742, 'उत्तर = क्योंकि अब हमने प्रेरित के काम और लुका के सुसमाचार की एक ही लेखक होने के बारे में कुछ प्रमाणों  को देख लिया है इसलिए हम अब आरंभ की कलीसिया के द्वारा दिए गए प्रमाण की ओर ध्यान करने के लिए तैयार है दूसरी से  लेकर चौथी शताब्दी ईस्वी तक आरंभ की कल ईशा ने लुका के बारे में गवाही दी है जो कि पौलुस उसके साथ सहयात्री था कि वही दोनों प्रेरित के काम और लुका के सुसमाचार का लेखक था हम संक्षेप में 2 तरीकों से इस प्रमाण की जांच करेंगे। सबसे पहले हम बाइबल के बारे में और इसके प्रारंभिक लिखित पाण्डुलिपियों  को देखेंगे और दूसरा हम यह देखेंगे कि हरम कि कल ईशा के अगुआ ने लूटा के द्वारा लेखन किए जाने के बारे में क्या कहा आइए हम कुछ प्राचीन पाडुलिपियों के प्रमाण के साथ आरंभ करते हैं।\r\n\r\n1)पाण्डुलिपिया :-\r\n\r\nएक सबसे पुरानी पांडुलिपि जिसे प पपाइरस 72 कहा जाता है 1952 ईस्वी में खोजी गई थी। यहां पपाइरस पर लिखा था और इसमें हमारे नए नियम के सबसे आरंभ की प्राचीन पांडुलिपि के प्रमाण सम्मिलित किए गए हैं शायद इसवी सन 175 और 200 के बीच के समय में नकल कर लिखी गई की गई थी और इसमें लुक्का के सुसमाचार और यह यूहन्ना के सुसमाचार के बड़े  बड़े हिस्से में शामिल है 200 समाचारों के पठन सामग्री के बीच में उनके विषय वस्तु के दो विवरणों को लिखा गया है लुका के सुसमाचार के समापन के बाद पांडुलिपि में यह शब्द आया है इवागेलियोन काटा ल्योकाॅन या लुका के अनुसार सुसमाचार और इन शब्दों के तुरंत बाद यह वाक्य आता है इवागेलियोन काटा योआनाॅन या यूहन्ना  के अनुसार सुसमाचार यह टिप्पणियां संकेत देती है कि जो सामग्री लुका के अनुसार सुसमाचार वाले शब्द के पहले आती है उसकी पहचान लुका के सुसमाचार के रूप में की गई है पांडुलिपि का यहां प्रमाण इस बात को दर्शाता है कि बहुत शुरुआत से ही यह विश्वास किया जाता था कि लोका ने तीसरे सुसमाचार को लिखा और स्तर के विस्तार के द्वारा साथ में यह भी दर्शाता है कि प्रेरितो के काम का लेखक भी लुका है।\r\n दूसरा 170 से 180 ईसवी के आसपास मारटोरियन  के टुकड़े पाए जाते हैं जो कि नए नियम की पुस्तकों के बारे में सूची देने वाले सबसे प्राचीन जानकारी वाले दस्तावेज है जिन्हें आरंभ की कलीसिया ने मानक माना है लुका के सुसमाचार के लिए लुका के लेखक होने की पुष्टि करने के बाद यह स्पष्ट रूप से संकेत करता है कि वही प्रेरित के काम कभी लेखक है इसकी पंक्तियों 34 से लेकर 36 में हम इन शब्दों को पढ़ते हैं कि:\r\n इसके अलावा सभी प्रेरितो के कार्यों को एक ही पुस्तक में लिखा गया लोका ने उस अलग-अलग घटनाओं को संकलित किया जो उसकी उपस्थिति में घटित हुए थे।\r\n यह वाक्य संकेत करता है कि दूसरी शताब्दी में यहां व्यापक तौर पर विश्वास किया जाता था कि लुका ही प्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक का लेखक था और उसने कम से कम कुछ घटनाओं को स्वयं देखा जो इसमें वर्णित है तीसरा तथाकथित ऐटाए मारसिओनाईट की प्रस्तावना जो कि तीसरी सुसमाचार का परिचय है जिसे 160 से लेकर 180 ईसवी सन के आसपास लिखा गया वह लुका और प्रेरितो के काम की पुस्तक के लेखक के बारे में इस तरह से वर्णन करता है:\r\n लुक्का पवित्र आत्मा के द्वारा प्रेरित होकर इस पूरे सुसमाचार को संकलित करता है और इसके बाद में यही लुका पीड़ितों के काम नामक पुस्तक को लिखता हैं ।\r\n इस आरंभिक पांडुलिपि के अलावा हमारे पास आरंभ कि कल ईशा के अंगों की गवाही भी है जो यह संकेत करती है कि लुका तीसरे सुसमाचार और प्रेरितो के काम की पुस्तक का लेखक है।\r\n\r\n 2)आरंभिक कलिसीयाई अगुवे :-\r\n\r\n कलीसियाई धर्मचार्य इरेनियुस जो 130 से लेकर 202 ई.सन्  के आसपास जीवित रहे यहां विश्वास करते थे किंतु का ही तीसरे सुसमाचार का लेखक था उन्होंने अपने साहित्य कार्य अगेस्ट हैरेसीज पुस्तक 3 अध्याय 1 खंड 1 मेरी यह लिखा है:\r\n लुक्का ने भी जॉब पोल उसका सहकर्मी था एक पुस्तक में उसके द्वारा प्रचार किए हुए सुसमाचार को लिखा।\r\n यहां पर इरेनियुस  का संकेत  प्रेरितो के काम की पुस्तक के लिए है जो कि उस सुसमाचार को अभी लिखित करती है जिसका प्रचार पौलुस ने किया था उसके शब्द महत्वपूर्ण है क्योंकि अच्छा ऐतिहासिक यह संकेत देता है कि इरेनियुस  को प्रोत्साहन रूप में लुका को  प्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक के लेखक होने का ज्ञान था। अलेक्जेंड्रिया के क्लेमेट जो कि 150 से लेकर 215 इसवी सन के आसपास रहे उन्होंने भी  दिखाया की दुकानें ही प्रेरितो के काम की पुस्तक को लिखा उन्होंने अपनी स्टोमाॅटा या  विभिन्न मामले नामक अपनी पांचवी पुस्तक के 12वें अध्याय में इन शब्दों को लिखा है:\r\n  प्रेरितो के काम की पुस्तक मलूका ने पुलिस के संबंध में ऐसे कहा है एथेन के लोगों में देखता हूं कि तुम हर बात में देवताओं के बड़े मानन वाले हो।\r\nऔर टरटुलियन जो कि 155 से लेकर 230  इसवी सन तक रहे उन्होंने अपने साहित्य कार्य अगेस्ट मारसियोन पुस्तक 4 के अध्ययन 2  मैं इन शब्दों को लिखा:\r\n इसलिए प्रेरितो मैं से यूहन्ना और मति सबसे पहले हमें विश्वास को स्थापित किया लुका और मर्कुस इसके बाद में ली नवीनीकृत करते है ।\r\n यहां टर्टुलियन विशेषकर लुका को ही तीसरे सुसमाचार को ही लेखक मानते हैं अंत में प्रसिद्ध कलीसायी इतिहासकार ईशु बियूष ने 323 इस मिशन के आसपास अपने लेखक कलीसिया इतिहास की पुस्तक एक अध्याय 5 के खंड 3 में उल्लेख किया है कि लुक्का ही प्रेरितो  के काम की पुस्तक का लेखक है वहां उसने क्या लिखा है इसे सुनिए:\r\n लुका ने प्रेरितो के काम में जनगणना के बारे में उल्लेख किया है।\r\n इस प्रकार की सकारात्मक स्वीकारोक्तियो के साथ ही यह आश्चर्यजनक है कि आरंभ की कलीसिया के साहित्य में ऐसा एक संकेत नहीं मिलता है कि लुका के अलावा किसी और ने लूटा के सुसमाचार और प्रेरितो के काम की पुस्तक को लिखा विद्यापीठ उसे  कभी भी एक  प्रेरितो के रूप में मनोनीत नहीं किया गया परंतु इस तरह के चुनावों के कारण हमारे पास विश्वास करने का कारण है कि आरंभ की कलीसिया ने लूटा को ही इनका लेखक होने के लिए आस्वीकृत नहीं किया परंतु इसके बजाय जो कुछ उसे सच के रूप में प्राप्त हुआ था सिर्फ उसे ही आगे पारित कर दिया कि लुका ने इन दोनों पुस्तकों को लिखा।', 8, '2020-10-17 03:12:24', '2020-10-27 18:25:27', NULL),
(2032, 566, 743, 'उत्तर =  अभी तक हमने यहां देखा कि प्ररितो  के काम और तीसरे सुसमाचार का एक ही लेखक होने की पुष्टि करने के अच्छे कारण है और आरंभ की कलीसिया ने इसके बारे में सहमति दी है कि वह अकेला लेखक लुका ही था अब आइए यहां देखकर कि हम स्वयं लूका  के बारे में नए नियम के अन्य भागों में किस तरह की सूचनाओं को प्राप्त कर सकते हैं।\r\n हम दो तरीकों से इस प्रमाण की जांच करेंगे सबसे पहले हम अपने गुमनाम लेखक के बारे में नए नियम से प्राप्त कुछ सुराग ऊपर ध्यान देंगे और दूसरा हम स्वयं लुका के बारे में दी गई सूचनाओं के साथ इन सुरागो की तुलना करेंगे आइए सबसे पहले हम अपने लेखक के बारे में दिए गए सुरागो को देखते है।\r\n\r\n लेखक के बारे में सुराग :-\r\n\r\n जैसा कि हम पहले कह चुके हैं कि प्ररितो  के काम की पुस्तक के लेखक ने नाम से स्वयं की कोई पहचान नहीं कराई है ऐसा अभ्यास होता है कि उसे अपने सहमत का थियुफिलुस  के कारण नाम देने की कोई आवश्यकता महसूस नहीं हुई लुका 1:3 मैं वह सिर्फ ऐसा कहता है कि मुझे भी यहां उचित मालूम हुआ और प्रेरितो  के काम की पुस्तक 1:1 मैं उसने ऐसे कहा कि अपनी पहली पुस्तक में मैंने लिखा लेकर कि यहां मानता था कि उसका सहमत यहां जानता है कि वहां कौन था और जब कि इस बात ने थियुफिलुस  के लिए तो कोई समय उत्पन्न नहीं की परंतु आधुनिक पाठकों के लिए इस बात ने बहुत सारे प्रश्नों को उत्पन्न कर दिया इसके साथ ही कई ऐसी बातें हैं जो कि नया नियम हमारे लेखक के बारे में हमें बताता है सबसे पहले वह प्रेरितो नहीं था वास्तव में शायद वह यीशु के स्वर्ग रोहन के होने के बाद विश्वास में आया था लुका के सुसमाचार 1:1-2 मैं दिए गए इन विवरणों को सुनें:\r\n जब लेखक ने यहां कहा कि शो के जीवन की घटनाएं हम तक पहुंची तो उसका संकेत यहां है कि वहां यीशु के जीवन का प्रथम दृश्य नहीं था।\r\n दूसरा प्रेरितो  के काम की पुस्तक और लुक्का के सुसमाचार में यूनानी भाषा की लेखन शैली यहां संकेत देती है कि लेखन अच्छी तरह से शिक्षित था नए नियम की अनेक पुस्तकें यूनानी भाषा में सामान्यतः यहां लिखी गई है यहां तक कि वह अपनी कृत यूनानी भाषा की शैली में लिखी गई है परंतु प्रेरितओ के काम की पुस्तक और लुक्का के सुसमाचार की भाषा में प्रयोग में अधिक परिष्कृत शैली को दिखाता है।\r\n तीसरा प्रेरित के काम के पुस्तक का अंतिम आधा हिस्सा इंगित करता है कि लेखक पौलुस का करीबी सहायक था प्रेरित ओके काम के आरंभिक अध्ययनों में कहानी निरंतर तृतीय पुरुषवाचक के रूप में है। परन्तु प्रेरितो  के काम अध्याय 16 से शुरू होकर कहानी अक्सर प्रथम पुरुष वाचक के दृष्टिकोण का प्रयोग करती है जिनमें हम और हमें जैसे शब्दों का प्रयोग किया गया है हम इस तरह की भाषा को प्रेरितो के काम 16:10-17,20:5-15,21:1-18 और 27:1-28:16 मैं पाते हैं यह अनुच्छेद संकेत देते हैं कि लेखक ने पौलुस की बाद की मिशनरी यात्रा वह में पौलुश के साथ यात्रा की और पुलिस के साथ केसरिया से रोम की यात्रा में गया ।\r\n अब जबकि हमारे पास हमारे लेखक के बारे में कुछ सुराग है तो अब हम यहां देखने की उपस्थिति में है कि यह तथ्य लुका के बारे में जो कुछ हम जानते हैं उनसे  कितनी अच्छी तरह से मिलते जुलते हैं।\r\n\r\nलुका :-  आइए हम उन बातों को एक बार पुनः देखें कि जिन्हें हम लुक्का और प्रेरितो  के काम के लेखक के बारे में जानते हैं वहां प्रेरित नहीं था ऐसा अभ्यास होता है कि वहां अच्छी तरह शिक्षित था और वह पॉल उसके साथ उसकी यात्रा में सहकर्मी तालुका के बारे में जो कुछ हम जानते हैं उसके साथ यह तथ्य कैसे जोड़ बनाते हैं? ठीक है सबसे पहले लुका एक प्रेरित नहीं था प्रेरितो नेक अलीशा के लिए न्यू की भूमिका को अदा करते हुए मसीह के  विवरण विशेष अधिकार का प्रयोग करते हुए एक अलीशा की स्थापना की और गलती एवं परेशानी से इसकी हस्तक की ओर प्रेरित के काम 1:21-22 के अनुसार प्रेरितो को संयोग यीशु द्वारा ही प्रशिक्षित किया जा लेकिन दुकाने यीशु के साथ कभी भी व्यक्तिगत तौर पर मुलाकात नहीं की थी और ना ही कभी उस अधिकार पर दावा किया जो कि प्रेरितो  से संबंधित था।  इसकी बजाय वह तो पॉल उसकी मिशनरी यात्राओं में सहायता  करने वाला एक सदस्य था वह एक प्रेरित का सेवक था यहां जैसा कि पॉल उसने प्ले मोहन की आयत 24 में उसका विवरण दिया है कि वहां एक प्रेरित का सहकर्मी था। दूसरा यहां भी संभावना है कि लुक्का अच्छी तरह से शिक्षित था हम इसका अनुमान कुलुसियो 4:14 2तिमुथियुस 4:11 प्ले मोड आयत 24 में उल्लेख करता है कि लुका उसके साथ यात्रा करता था।\r\nहम प्रेरितो   के काम के लेखक कविता को इस तरह सारांश में बता सकते हैं कि विस्तृत यात्रा में ऐतिहासिक यह इंगित करते हैं प्रेरितो  के काम की पुस्तक का लेखक लुक्का ही है लुक्का के सुसमाचार और  प्रेरितो के काम की पुस्तक का लेखक एक ही है आरंभिक कलिसीया  समक्ष निरंतर लुका को ही इसके लेखक होने का हकदार मानते हैं और बाइबिल का विवरण इसी विचार से सहमत है इन प्रमाणों के आधार पर मे हमारे पास वह सभी अच्छे कारण है कि हम यहां विश्वास करें कि लुका ही दोनों अर्थात तीसरे सुसमाचार और प्रेरित के काम की पुस्तक का लेखक था और हमें सदैव यहां स्मरण रखना चाहिए कि लुका के जिस विषय का उसने विवरण दिया उसके लिए उसके पास उत्कृष्ट पहुंच और निकटता थी।', 8, '2020-10-17 03:23:38', '2020-10-27 18:25:27', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(2033, 566, 744, 'उत्तर = प्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक की तिथि और वास्तविक सूरतगढ़ पर ध्यान देने के बाद हम किसी बात को संबोधित करने के लिए तैयार है जो कि लुका के कार्य का सामान्य सामाजिक संदर्भ है ऐसा संसार जिनमें प्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक को लिखा गया था जिनका अधिक हम लुका के दिनों की सामाजिक शक्तियों के बारे में समझेंगे उतने ही बेहतर तरीके से हम इस पुस्तक की कई विशेषताओं को समझने के लिए सुसज्जित हो जाएंगे।\r\n हम पहली शताब्दी की कलीसिया के जीवन के दो केंद्रीय गुणों को देखने के द्वारा प्रेरितो के काम की पुस्तक के सामाजिक संदर्भ की खोजबीन करेंगे पहला शो मी सम राज्य का शासन और शक्ति और दूसरा कलीसिया और यहूदियों के बीच का न्याय संबंध आइए सबसे पहले रोम साम्राज्य को देखें।\r\n\r\n रोमी साम्राज्य :-\r\n\r\n जब तक लुका प्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक में लिखा उस समय तक रोमी साम्राज्य ने पूरे भूमध्य संसार पर विजय प्राप्त कर इसे अपने नियंत्रण में कर लिया था और इसने अपने साम्राज्य के पहुंच को वर्तमान के ब्रिटेन उत्तरी अमेरिका और एशिया के कुछ भागों तक फैला दिया था आरंभ की कली से के दिनों में साम्राज्य अभी भी विस्तार कर रहा था तथा अधिक से अधिक लोगों और को अपने साम्राज्य में जोड़ रहा था जैसे जैसे उसने ऐसा किया रोमी सम्राट जिन्हें समाज के सभी पहलुओं को अपने विशिष्ट रूम में मूल्य लक्ष्य और विश्वास के साथ गहराई से प्रभावित किया।\r\n इसमें कोई शक नहीं कि जीते हुए प्रदेशों के ऊपर रोम साम्राज्य की सबसे बड़े प्रभाव राजनीतिक और आर्थिक पैरों में साम्राज्य की प्रमुख राजनीतिक दिलचस्पी ओं में से एक थी के स्थानीय अधिकारियों के ऊपर शक्तिशाली नियंत्रित करने के द्वारा साम्राज्य के भीतर शांति और मिस वासियों की सूची निश्चित करें जीते गए रास्तों को कुछ सीमा तक स्थानीय स्वतंत्रता प्रदान की जाती थी परंतु उनके स्थानीय अधिकारियों को अक्सर बदल दिया जाता था और वह सदैव रूमी साम्राज्य के पदक्रम के अधीन रहते थे उदाहरण के  लिए प्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक केसरिया के  रोमांस राज्यपालों अर्थात फेलिक्स और फेसतुस का उल्लेख करती है जिन्होंने यहूदी की सारे देश पर केसरिया से शासन किया कर लेने के कार्य को देखने के अलावा वे रूमी साम्राज्य के अपने हिस्से में शांति और व्यवस्था बनाए रखने के लिए भी जिम्मेदार थे साम्राज्य ने जीते गए देशों के लोगों में रोमन नागरिकों को छोड़ने के माध्यम से संस्कृति और राजनीतिक प्रभाव का भी प्रयोग किया।\r\n अक्सर शो मी सम राज्य ने जीते हुए प्रदेशों को सेवा मित्र हो रहे सैन्य बल को रहने के लिए देता था इस रीति के द्वारा पूरे साम्राज्य भर में विश्वास योग्य रूप में नागरिकों के पहले स्थापित हो गए और उन्होंने दोनों अर्थात सरकारी एवं सामाजिक ढांचे में रोमी मूल्यों और प्रतिबंधों को बढ़ावा दिया यही कारण है कि प्ररितो के काम  की पुस्तक समय-समय पर रूम के लोगों का उल्लेख करती है जिसे हम पर पहनते कोस्ट के दिन के आरंभ में ही प्रेरितो के काम 2:10-11 मैं पढ़ते हैं कि वहां पर रूमी में आए हुए लोग थे दोनों यहूदी और यहूदी धर्म में धर्म आधारित और फिर प्रेरितो के काम  10  अध्याय में कुरनेलियुस परमेश्वर का डर रखने वाले एक रूमी सूबेदार ने प्रेरित के काम  मैं सुसमाचार को फैलाने में महत्वपूर्ण भूमिका अदा की है इसके अलावा स्थानीय संस्कृति रूम के लोक निर्माण में जैसे कि सैकड़ों विस्तृत इमारते और सार्वजनिक बैठकों के स्थानों से प्रभावित थे रोमन साम्राज्य का यह पहलू बताता है कि किस तरह से पौलुस और अन्य लोगों ने अपनी मिशनरी प्रयास में इतनी स्वयं था और सुरक्षित रूप से यात्रा की प्रेरितो  ने भी जैसे जैसे एक स्थान से दूसरे स्थान को गए इन सार्वजनिक स्थानों का प्रयोग सुसमाचार के प्रचार के लिए किए आरंभ की कली से के लिए साहित्य में साम्राज्य की सबसे महत्वपूर्ण विशेषता जीते गए लोगों के धर्मों के ऊपर उनका प्रभाव था लुका के लेखक समय में एक व्यक्ति पूरे रोम साम्राज्य के केंद्र में खड़ा था वहां था केसरिया साम्राज्य के सर को ना केवल उसके लोगों और के ऊपर देवता के रूप में देखा जाता था बल्कि वहां लोगों के लिए छोटे या बचाने वाले के रूप में भी देखा जाता था रोमी प्रचार के अनुसार केसर उनके लोगों को अराकताऔ और अंधकार में से छुटकारा देता था और रोमी साम्राज्य के विस्तार को उसके उद्धार के विस्तार के रूप में प्रस्तुत किया जाता था यह नहीं लोगों को स्थानीय राजाओं के अत्याचार से मुक्त करना और लोगों को रूम के उदार शासन के अधीन लाना ज्यादातर स्थानों में जीते गए लोगों को उनकी अपनी धार्मिक प्रस्ताव का पालन करते रहने की अनुमति जाती थी परंतु उन्हें केसर और पारंपरिक रोमी देवताओं की श्रेष्ठता को स्वीकार करना अनिवार्य था अब कई तरह से पहली शताब्दी में ज्यादातर यहूदी और मसीही विश्वासी रोम के सबसे सम्मानित नागरिक थे परंतु विश्वास योगी यहूदियों और मसीही विश्वासी यों के घरों में धर्म की सर्वोच्चता को स्वीकार करने से इनकार कर दिया था रोम साम्राज्य ने यहूदी धर्म को लिजियो लिक्टिका या कानूनी धर्म के रूप में नामित किया था और जहां तक संभव हो उसने मसीह विश्वास को सहन किया चाहे भले ही उसने दोनों समूह के लोगों का दमन किया सरकार लोग लोक निर्माण और धर्म के ऊपर अपने नियंत्रण के माध्यम से रूम ने अपने प्रभाव का हर जगह जहां तक संभव था प्रयास करने का प्रयास किया।\r\n अब क्योंकि हमने प्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक को सामाजिक संदर्भों को रोमी साम्राज्य के प्रभाव के प्रकाश में देख लिया है इसलिए आपको सामाजिक स्थिति के एक महत्वपूर्ण आयाम की जांच करने के लिए तैयार है जिनमें लुका ने इसे लिखा आ विश्वासी यहूदी और आरंभिक मसीही विश्वासी यों में बीच का संबंध है।\r\n\r\nयहूदी और कलिसीया :-\r\n\r\n हम यहूदी और आरंभ की कली से के बीच के संबंध को पहले उनके बीच में घनिष्ठ संबंध पर ध्यान देकर और दूसरा उनके बुनियादी मतभेद की खोजबीन के द्वारा विचार करेंगे आइए इन दो समूह के बीच आपसी संबंधों के साथ आरंभ करते हैं।\r\n आरंभ की कलीसिया यहूदी लोगों के साथ एक ही विरासत को साझा करती थी जैसा कि स्वभाविक ही है आधुनिक संसार में अक्सर हमें स्वयं को स्मरण दिलाना होता है कि यीशु यहूदी थे सभी प्रेरित यहूदी थे। पुलिस और जो उसके साथ यात्रा करते थे उन्होंने सभा घरों में यहूदियों के साथ शिवम की पहचान पूर्वजों को हमारे पिता कहकर और हम इस वासियों को उनकी सम्मान कहकर की इसके अतिरिक्त आरंभ की कलीसिया और यहूदी समाज बड़े पैमाने पर एक ही पवित्र शास्त्र के प्रति प्रसिद्ध थे प्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक में मसीही विश्वासी लोक निरंतर पहुंच शास्त्री की दुहाई देते थे जब भी वे यहूदी संदर्भ के में सुसमाचार का प्रचार करते थे।\r\nप्रेरितो के काम 17:1-3 मैं बताता है कि पौलुस किस तरह पहुंचकर शास्त्र में हवाला देता है जब वहां यहूदियों को मसीह का प्रचार कर रहा था वहां पर लुक्का के शब्दों को सुनें\r\nइसके अलावा मसीही अट और यहूदी धर्म के बीच घनिष्ठ संबंध के परिणाम स्वरुप यहूदी अधिकारियों और आरंभिक अलीशा के बीच महत्वपूर्ण आपसी बातचीत पैदा होती है।\r\nप्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक के अनुसार मसीह के अनुरूप समाचार प्रचार में आरंभिक अलीशा के साहस न यहूदी अधिकारियों के साथ संघर्ष की स्थिति को पैदा किया परंतु जितना अधिक संभव हो सका आरंभ की मसीही विश्वासी यों ने यहूदी अब वह को स्वीकार किया और उनका विरोध केवल उसी समय किया जब वे उन्हें परमेश्वर के आदेशों की अवज्ञा करने के लिए आदेश देते थे।\r\n यहूदी लोग को और आरंभ कि कल ईशा के बीच घनिष्ठ संबंध होने के बावजूद वे फिर भी बुनियादी मतभेदों के कारण वे अलग पहुंचने जाते थे सबसे पहले और सबसे मौलिक मसीही विश्वासी औरत विश्वासी यहूदी यीशु के व्यक्तित्व और उनके कार्यों पर ऐसा मत थे कल शाम घोषणा कर दी थी कि यीशु ही मसीह थे जिन्होंने मृत्यु पर विजय प्राप्त की थी और सारी सृष्टि को वहां पुनः बहाल कर रहा है जिन की शुरुआत उसने मृतकों में से अपने जी उठने के साथ की है परंतु अविश्वास यह उद्योग के लिए यहां मानना असंभव था कि अपराधी के रूप में क्रूस पर चढ़ाया गया व्यक्ति प्रतिज्ञा  क्या हुआ मसीह है इस मतभेद ने मसीह विश्वासी और आदिवासियों में दरार को उत्पन्न कर दिया जो कि आज के दिन तक निरंतर बनी हुई है\r\nदूसरा जबकि आरंभ कि कल ईशा और यहूदी अगले इब्रानी बाइबल के अधिकार पर सहमति थे लेकिन वह विशेष रूप से यीशु के संबंध में इब्रानी पवित्र शास्त्रों की सही व्याख्या पर कठोरता के साथ सहमत थे अरुण की कलीसिया विश्वास करती थी कि अब रानीपत्र शास्त्र में आने वाली मासी के लिए की गई आशा यीशु में पूरी होती है परंतु आ विश्वासी यहूदी लोगों ने इस समझ को स्वीकार करने से इनकार किया यहूदी धर्म के भीतर ही कई संप्रदाय थे जो कई तरह के विचारों को मानते थे परंतु उनमें से अधिकांश ने यहां स्वीकार करना असंभव पाया कि यीशु पुराने नियम के मसीहा की आशाओं को पूरा करता है।\r\n तीसरे स्थान पर पहली शताब्दी के आरंभिक कलीसिया और यहूदी लोग इस बात पर मतभेद रखते थे कि अन्य जातियों के प्रति उनका दृष्टिकोण कैसा हो अधिकांश बातों के लिए चौकस रेल यहूदी लोग अन्य जातियों के साथ संगति नहीं रखते थे परंतु दूसरी ओर कई खतना रहित अन्य जातियों के लोग यहूदी धर्म के नैतिक शिक्षा और मान्यताओं की और इतना ज्यादा आकर्षित है कि वे स्थानीय होती सभाओं में स्वयं को सलंग रखते और परमेश्वर से डरने वाले के रूप में जाने जाते थे परमेश्वर का डर रखने वालों को दूसरे अन्य जातियों से ज्यादा सम्मान प्राप्त था लेकिन वे यहूदी समुदाय के संपूर्ण सदस्य नहीं थे अन्य जाति के व्यक्ति यहूदी धर्म में धर्म आमंत्रित हुए थे लेकिन इनमें दीक्षा संस्कार में से जाना शामिल था जिनमें बपतिस्मा और खतना और यहूदी परंपराओं का पालन करना नियमित था।\r\n जबकि आरंभिक अलीशा के बीच वासियों ने अन्य जातियों के प्रति अपना व्यवहार इसी समय के साथ आरंभ किया था परंतु वह धीरे-धीरे समझे कि वे अन्य जाति लोग जो मसीह के पीछे चल रहे हैं उन्हें कल ईशा में संपूर्ण सदस्यता का दर्जा प्रदान किया जाना चाहिए पवित्र आत्मा से नए प्रकाशन के द्वारा आरंभिक अलीशा ने यह निर्धारित किया कि मसीह में विश्वास से व्यक्ति करना और बपतिस्मा लेना ही मसीही अलीशा में पूर्व सदस्यता के लिए पर्याप्त था इसलिए प्रेरितो  ने दोनों यहूदियों एवं अन्य जातियों के लिए मसीह की सार्वभौमिक प्रभुता के सुसमाचार को प्रचार करने की अपनी नीति बनाई और जैसे-जैसे कलीसिया बड़ी उन्होंने दोनों प्रकार के लोगों के वरदान ओ एवं सेवाएं को ग्रहण किया वे समझ गए कि परमेश्वर अन्य जातियों के राज्य की आशा को पूरी करने के लिए प्रयोग कर रहा है जो कि उसने पुराने नियम में अपने लोगों को दिया था इसमें कोई आश्चर्य नहीं कि यह बता विश्वासी यहूदियों और आरंभ के मसीह विश वासियों के बीच कई तरह के संघर्ष को ले आया।', 9, '2020-10-17 03:33:47', '2020-10-27 18:25:27', NULL),
(2034, 566, 745, 'उत्तर =  परमेश्वर के राज्य के ऊपर हमारे विचार विमर्श तीन भागों में विभाजित होगा सबसे पहले हम मसीहा वाले यहूदी धर्म विज्ञान पर ध्यान देंगे जो की पहली शताब्दी में प्रचलित था दूसरा हम यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा देने वाले के धर्म विज्ञान पर ध्यान देंगे और तीसरा हम हस्तक्षेप में इंडस्ट्री कोणों का मसीही विश्वासी की मसीहा वाले धर्म विज्ञान से तुलना करेंगे जिसे लोका ने समर्थन दिया है आइए यहूदी धर्म विज्ञान के दृष्टिकोण से आरंभ करें।\r\n\r\n यहूदी धर्मविज्ञान:- \r\n\r\n पांचवी शताब्दी ईसा पूर्व मैं पुराने नियम की अंतिम पुस्तकों के लिए लिखे जाने के बाद इसराइल आत्मिक अंधकार के युग में प्रवेश करता है कई  वर्षों से इसराइल योग की एक बड़ी संख्या प्रतिज्ञा किए हुए देश से बाहर जीवन यापन कर रहे थे और जो देश में बचे हुए रह गए थे उन्होंने अन्य जातियों के शासकों से बहुत ज्यादा अत्याचार सहा ।\r\n सबसे पहले बबूल के हाथों फिर माझी और पारसी फिर यूनानी और अब अंत में रोमियो से दुखों के लंबे इतिहास के परिणाम स्वरुप यह आशा कि परमेश्वर इसराइल में एक छुटकारा देने वाला मसीहा भेजेगा यहूदी धर्म विज्ञान में एक सबसे ज्यादा प्रबल होती विचारधारा बन गई थी।\r\n यह जिओ की मशीन के बारे में आशा ने कई अलग-अलग दिशाओं को ले लिया उदाहरण के लिए ज्योति अर्थात उग्र पंथी वाले विश्वास करते थे कि परमेश्वर इसराइल लोगों से चाहता है कि रोमी अधिकारियों के विरुद्ध विद्रोह को बढ़ाने के द्वारा वे मसीह के आगमन के दिन में प्रवेश को तेज कर सकते थे विभिन्न रहस्य योगदान टर्न विचारधारा वाले समूह या विश्वास करते थे कि परमेश्वर अलौकिक तरीके से उनके शत्रुओं को नाश करने के लिए हस्तक्षेप करेगा और अपने लोगों को विजेताओं के रूप में स्थापित करेगा वह इस्राएल में व्यवस्था के प्रति खट्टर लोगों थे जैसे की लोकप्रिय ऋषि और दूसरी लोग जो यहां विश्वास करते थे कि परमेश्वर तब तक हस्तक्षेप नहीं करेगा जब तक इसराइल व्यवस्था के प्रति पूर्ण आज्ञाकारी नहीं बन जाता प्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक में विभिन्न स्थानों पर लुकाया उल्लेख करता है कि कई यहूदियों ने मसीहा वाले राज्य की इस मसीही विश्वासी यों की विचारधारा को मानने से इंकार कर दिया था यद्यपि मसीहा के लिए योगियों में कई तरह की आशाएं थी दुकाने यह देखा कि यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा देने वाले की सेव काय के द्वारा यहूदी धर्म विज्ञान में एक महत्वपूर्ण परिवर्तन आया है।\r\n\r\n यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा देने वाला :-\r\n\r\n लुक्का का सुसमाचार और प्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक दोनों यहां एगीत करते हैं कि यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा देने वाले ने सच्चे पछता के लिए बुला हड्डी और शुभ संदेश की घोषणा की कि मसीह परमेश्वर के राज्य को इस पृथ्वी पर लाने वाला था और इसमें भी बढ़कर यूहन्ना नेहा सही मायनों में यीशु की पहचान मसीहा के रूप में की। लूका 3:16-17 यहां पर यूहन्ना ठीक ही मसीहा के बारे में घोषणा करता है कि मसीहा पवित्र आत्मा की महान आशीशों और शुद्धता को लाएगा जिनमें न्याय भी शामिल थे परंतु वह इस गलत धारणा में था कि मसीहा इस कार्य को अभी एक दम से ही करेगा।\r\n यह ना पहले से नहीं देखा सका की मसीहा संसार में उद्धार और न्याय को कोई चरणों में लाएगा बाद में यूहन्ना इस तथ्य को लेकर पशोपेश मैं था कि यीशु ने अभी तक कुछ भी एक ऐसा कार्य नहीं किया जिसके बारे में यहूदी धर्म स्त्रियों ने आशा की थी कि मसीहा ऐसा करेगा यह ना इतना ज्यादा परेशान हो गया था कि उसके यीशु से यह पूछने के लिए दूतों को भेजा कि क्या वह वास्तव में मसीहा था कि नहीं  लुका 7:23-20\r\n यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा देने वाले की दिए अपने उत्तर में यीशु  ने यशायाह  की पुस्तक में मसीहा से संबंधित कई भविष्यवाणियों का हवाला दिया उसने ऐसा ही होना को आश्वस्त करने के लिए किया कि वह पुराने नियम की मशीन वाली भविष्यवाणियों की विभिन्न आशाओं को पूरा करने की प्रक्रिया में लगा हुआ था यद्यपि उसने अभी तक उन्हें पूरा नहीं किया था। यीशु ने यूहन्ना को उत्साहित भी किया कि जिस तरह से मसीहा का कार्य प्रगट हो रहा वहां उसमें अपने विश्वास में किसी भी तरह से ना गिरे।\r\n हस्तक्षेप में इशू ने मसीहा वाला मिशन जैसी आशा की गई थी उससे बहुत ज्यादा बिनता योगियों की मसीहा वाली आशय मसीहा के शासन के अधीन एक अति शीघ्र सांसारिक राजनीतिक राज्य की स्थापना की और देख रही थी उस राज्य के समान जिसमें शताब्दियों पहले शूटआउट ने शासन किया था परंतु ईश्वर ने अपने सांसारिक सेवकों के दौरान इस तरह के राज्य की स्थापना करने की कोई कोशिश नहीं की यहूदियों के मसीहा वाले इस धर्म में विज्ञान की समझ के साथ और यूहन्ना बपतिस्मा देने वाले के दृष्टिकोण को अपने ध्यान में रखते हुए हम अब मसीहा और परमेश्वर के राज्य के आरंभिक मसीहा धर्म विज्ञान को देखने के लिए तैयार है।\r\n\r\n मसीही धर्मविज्ञान:-\r\n\r\n लुका के साहित्य में जैसा कि बाकी के नए नियम में है मसीही विश्वास का मसीहा वाला धर्म विज्ञान मसीह यीशु समाचार या शुभ संदेश से निकटता के साथ संबंधित है हम नए नियम के सुसमाचार के संदेशों को इस तरह से सारांशित कर सकते हैं :\r\n सुसमाचार यह घोषणा है कि यीशु जो मसीहा है उसके व्यक्तित्व और कार्य के द्वारा परमेश्वर का राज्य इस पृथ्वी पर आया है और यहां अपने बड़े समापन की ओर बढ़ रहा है जैसे जैसे परमेश्वर उन लोगों को मुक्ति प्रदान कर रहा है जो यीशु को मसीहा के रूप में मान रहे हैं और उस पर भरोसा रख रहे हैं।\r\n आप ध्यान देंगे कि सुसमाचार का संदेश दो आवश्यक विचारों को स्पर्श करता है एक और तो हम वह पाते हैं जिसे हम मसीही सुसमाचार का विषय पर एक पहलू कह सकते हैं और परमेश्वर का राज्य इस पृथ्वी में यीशु के कार्य और व्यक्तित्व के द्वारा आता है लोका ने विश्वास किया कि मसीहा के रूप में यीशु ने पति परमेश्वर के राज्य का अंतिम चरण आरंभ कर दिया है और यहां की एक दिन वहां जो कुछ उसने आरंभ किया है उसे पूरा करने के लिए वापस आएगा।\r\n और दूसरी और नए नियम की सुसमाचार संदेशों में बहुत ज्यादा व्यक्तिक पर एक पहलू भी है इस ने घोषणा की है कि जैसे-जैसे परमेश्वर उन लोगों को उधार दे रहा है जो यीशु को मसीहा के रूप में मार रहे हैं और विश्वास कर रहे हैं परमेश्वर के राज्य का अंतिम चरण इसके महान समापन की ओर बढ़ता चला जा रहा है जैसे-जैसे सुसमाचार उन लोगों के हृदय को स्पर्श करता है जो विश्वास करते हैं और उनको उस उद्धार में ले आता है जिसे यीशु ने पूरा किया है तो परमेश्वर के राज्य का शासन इस संसार में आगे बढ़ता है।\r\nप्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक मेलों का सुसमाचार के इन दोनों पहलुओं की ओर ध्यान आकर्षित करता है विषय पर एक पहलू की ओर मसीहा में उतार वाले परमेश्वर के महान कार्य की वास्तविकता ओं पर उसने जोर दिया उसने कल ईशा के प्रचारक घोषणा को लिखा कि यीशु अपने लोगों के पापों के लिए मरा कि उसको मृतकों में से जलाया गया है कि वह पिता  परमेश्वर के दाहिने हाथ विराजमान होकर राज्य करता है और यह कि वहां महिमा के साथ पुनः वापस आएगा।\r\n ध्यान देकर पत्र इसकी सुसमाचार की घोषणा में मसीहा के जीवन मृत्यु और पुनरुत्थान के विषय पर तथा सम्मिलित है।\r\n परंतु लुक्का सुसमाचार के ज्यादा व्यक्ति पर एक विषय की ओर भी ध्यान आकर्षित करता है कई अवसरों पर लोगों द्वारा मसीह की सच्चाई को व्यक्तिगत तौर पर स्वीकार करने की महत्वपूर्ण का के ऊपर उसने जोर दिया ताकि यह उसके जीवन को बदल पाए प्रेरितो के काम 2:37-38 मसीही सुसमाचार उन लोगों के हृदय को छेदता है  जो उसे सुनते हैं या ना केवल उन तथ्यों को महज अस्वीकार करता है परंतु उद्धार करता का हरदेव को छूने वाला जीवन परिवर्तन करने वादा मिलन है जैसा कि हमने कहा था पहली शताब्दी का यहूदी धर्म विज्ञान यहां विश्वास करता था कि मसीहा एक राजनीतिक राज्य को एकदम से स्थापित कर देगा परंतु यीशु और उसके प्रेरितो  नहीं यहां सिखाएं की मसीहा का राज्य कल ईशा के फैलाव और लोगों के व्यक्तिगत परिवर्तन के द्वारा धीरे-धीरे बढ़ता है।\r\n यहां एक कारण है कि लुक्का ने सुसमाचार की घोषणा के द्वारा आविस वासियों को मन फिर आपके ऊपर इतना राज्य ध्यान केंद्रित किया है वहां जानता था कि यही वहां माध्यम है जिसके द्वारा परमेश्वर का मसीहा वाला राज्य पूरे संसार भर में फैला आएगा।', 9, '2020-10-17 03:45:02', '2020-10-27 18:25:27', NULL),
(2035, 566, 746, 'उत्तर = पुराने नियम का संसार के इतिहास के प्रति साधारण मसीही लोगों विश्वासी होने के नाते आधुनिक संसार के प्रति हमारी सोच को समस्या जरूर ही प्रदान करता है क्योंकि जिस तरह से हम नए नियम में पढ़ते हैं बाइबिल में परमेश्वर के पवित्र आत्मा और प्रभु यीशु मसीह का क्रूस ई करण बलिदान और परमेश्वर की भिन्न-भिन्न बातों और परमेश्वर केविन उत्पत्ति और भिन्न-भिन्न तरीकों से हम परमेश्वर के वचनों को और परमेश्वर के गुण बातों को हम नए नियम में सीखते हैं वह सारी बातें हमें पुराने नियम में भी सीखने को मिलता है क्योंकि प्रभु यीशु मसीह का आगमन और उसकी उल्लेख और उसकी भविष्यवाणी हमें पुराने नियम में मिलती है जितना परमेश्वर नए नियम में विराजमान है उतना ही परमेश्वर पुराने नियम में भी विराजमान था थे पुराने नियम में परमेश्वर के महान बातों को और महान शब्दों को हम परमेश्वर के भक्तों के द्वारा हम सीखते हैं परमेश्वर के बड़े-बड़े भक्तों के द्वारा जो है पुराने नियम में परमेश्वर उनसे बातचीत करते थे उसी प्रकार से आज भी नए नियम में परमेश्वर हमसे भिन्न भिन्न परमेश्वर के दांतो के द्वारा तथा पवित्र आत्मा की द्वारा जो हर एक विश्वासी जो प्रभु यीशु मसीह पर विश्वास करता है उसे दिया गया है और उन्हें ही पवित्र आत्मा की द्वारा उन्हें उन्हें समझ प्रदान करता है सो हमें जो है पुराने नियम के द्वारा परमेश्वर हमें और नए नियम के द्वारा परमेश्वर हमें जो है इन दिनों में समझ प्रदान करता है हर मशीन व्यक्ति को नया नियम के बातों को सीखना जरूरी है और पुराने नियम के बातों को भी जो है नजरअंदाज नहीं करना है परंतु उससे भी सीखना हमारे लिए महत्वपूर्ण है क्योंकि पुराने नियम में भी प्रभु परमेश्वर जो है विराजमान था हमें पुराने नियम में सारे शब्दों को झांकना और मैं सीखना समझना जरूरी है क्योंकि पुराने नियम में परमेश्वर की कई बातें लिखी हुए हैं प्रभु यीशु मसीह के शब्द पुराने नियम लिखे हुए हैं यदि हम पुराने नियम को नहीं सीखेंगे तो हम परमेश्वर के सारे बातों को नहीं सीख पाएंगे और यदि हम नहीं सीख पाएंगे तो परमेश्वर की जो है बातों से हम अनजान रहेंगे जब परमेश्वर की बातों से हम अंजार रहेंगे तो हम हमेशा को ना समझने के कारण में हम आप कर बैठेंगे इसीलिए इन सारे पाप और बुराई से बचने के लिए हर मसीह व्यक्ति को पुराने नियम और नया नियम को सीखना और समझना जरूरी है अगर ऐसा करेंगे तो परमेश्वर हर एक विश्वासी को इसकी द्वारा एक नया समझ प्रदान करें करेगा।', 8, '2020-10-17 03:55:39', '2020-10-27 18:25:27', NULL),
(2036, 568, 643, 'Jesus will descend from heaven as the victorious, conquering King over all creation. \r\n1. Personal - Jesus is coming back in person to finish his work. After Jesus\' resurrection, he explained that he was going to send the Holy Spirit to empower the church for ministry (Acts 1:4-5). After Jesus\' ascension, two angels appeared and told the apostles that Jesus would personally return in the future.\r\n2. Physical- Jesus didn\'t  give up his humanity when he ascended into heaven; he has both a divine nature and human nature. Jesus has to return in his human nature in order to complete his work as the prophet like Moses. The New Testament consistently teaches that when Jesus returns, he\'ll appear in his glorified physical human body.\r\n3. Visible- When Jesus returns in his glorified human body, we\'ll be able to see him. The New Testament explicitly states that Jesus will be seen when he returns (1 John 3:2, Revelation 1:7) and it will be an earth shattering event.\r\n4. Triumphant - Jesus\' first coming did not appear triumphant: born to a poor, humble family, with no political or military power and then condemned and executed as a criminal. He\'ll come with blazing fire and angelic armies and will be crowned with many crowns, and carrying an iron scepter to rule the nations. Everyone will bow before His power and authority (Philippians 2:9-11) .', 8, '2020-10-19 15:41:59', '2020-10-21 18:30:32', NULL),
(2037, 568, 644, 'The timing of Christ\'s return is divine mystery. Scripture mentions several circumstances that are precursors to Jesus\' return. These circumstances create legitimate expectations for how the future may unfold, and they warn and encourage us as we prepare for Christ\' arrival.\r\n1. Demonic Opposition- A particularly terrible period of demonic opposition will precede Jesus\' return (\'\'the Great Tribulation\"). In the Great Tribulation, demons will empower false prophets to perform misleading signs and wonders (Revelation 16:13-14)\r\n2. Human Opposition- Many human beings will cooperate with the demonic opposition to God. For instance: two beasts with power to control societies and governments (Revelation 13).  \"the false prophet\" (Revelation 16:13, 19:20) \"the man of lawlessness\"(2 Thessalonians 2:1-10) False prophets and false Christs (Matthew 24:24) many antichrists (1 John 2:18).\r\n3. Worldwide Evangelism- The kingdom will successfully present its gospel message to the nations (Matthew 24:14). Jesus associated the Great Commission with the entire continuation of the kingdom until the end of the age. When Jesus returns, the church will include members from every tribe, language, people and nation (Revelation 7:9).', 9, '2020-10-19 15:52:58', '2020-10-21 18:30:32', NULL),
(2038, 568, 645, 'Evangelical interpretive strategies exhibit four main tendencies with regard to the \"signs of the times\". \r\nPreterism- the precursors to Christ\'s return appeared in our past and will not be repeated in the future.\r\nFuturism- the precursors to Christ\'s return haven\'t appeared yet, but will appear in the future. \r\nHistoricism- the precursors to Christ\'s return are associated with actual people and events throughout history.\r\nIdealism- the precursors to Christ\'s return are related to abstract concepts and general principles.\r\nThese interpretive strategies all can be used as tools to help us understand various aspects of Scripture. Each of these interpretive strategies has strengths and weaknesses, and evangelicals use all of these strategies to varying degrees.', 9, '2020-10-19 16:05:08', '2020-10-21 18:30:32', NULL),
(2039, 568, 646, 'Millennium is a period of one thousand years. The eschatological period of Christ\'s reign mentioned in Revelation 20:2-7. Evangelicals often disagree over where to place the millennium in the eschatological timeline. \r\nA. Historic Premillennialism- Premillennialism is a belief that Jesus will return before the millennium begins. Historic is this view has been held throughout church history. Basic views are: the church will go through the great tribulation just prior to Jesus\' return. When Jesus arrives, he\'ll gather all living believers, bind Satan\'s influence and begin his earthly reign. Historic Premillennialists differ on whether the millennium will be literal one thousand years or a long unspecified length of time. Believers that remain alive when Jesus returns will be gathered to him in the air, and will immediately return to earth with Jesus as part of his victorious military parade and will live on earth during Christ\'s millennial reign. \r\nB. during millennium- Believers and unbelievers alike will enjoy earthly blessings, peace and prosperity. Unbelievers that have died won\'t be resurrected until end of millennium, but those living will still be on earth. The final judgement will come, and God\'s eternal reign over the new heavens and new earth will be fully realized.', 9, '2020-10-19 16:16:31', '2020-10-21 18:30:32', NULL),
(2040, 568, 647, 'Post Millennialism is a belief that Jesus will return after the millennium ends. \r\nBasic Views- During the millennium, Jesus is physically in heaven while he reigns spiritually on earth. The millennium is an age of success for the gospel that prepares the earth for Christ\'s return. \r\nSome postmillennialists believe the millennium stretches from Jesus\' ascension to his return: others think it will be the last thousand years before he comes back. It will produce greater and greater success for the gospel and the church throughout the world.  Christ will successfully defeat his enemies before he returns. The millennium will be a time of increasing victory for Kingdom of God. Satan\'s rebellion will occur at the end of the millennium, and he will be defeated when Christ returns. The rapture will include resurrected and still living believers. Believers will meet the Lord in the air and immediately return with him as part of his victorious military parade. Jesus will render his final judgements on both believers and unbelievers and will usher in the new heavens and new earth, and the final state will begin.', 8, '2020-10-19 16:25:00', '2020-10-21 18:30:32', NULL),
(2041, 564, 881, 'Luke 1:35 says that Mary conceived Jesu Christ by Holy Spirit.\r\nij this verse the holy Spirit is equated to the power of the most high. \r\nThrough out the Old Testament it is God who is repeatedly referred to as the Holy One, we see this in 2 Kings 19:22, Isaiah 30:11-15 an there are other passages that seem to refer to God Himself by the name \"Holy Spirit\"  as in Isaiah 63:10-11.\r\n\r\nNAMES\r\nThe names that include the \" spirit of the Lord\", the spirit  Of God and the Spirit of the living god also the Spirit of Jesus , Spirit of Christ, the Spirit of Jesus Christ, the Spirit of your Father, the Spirit pf His son and the Spirit pf him who raised Jesus from the dead ,all these names suggest that the holy Spirit is divine by indicating that God is united to the holy Spirit in the same way that a human being is united to his own spirit.\r\nATTRIBUTES\r\nGod possesses incommunicable attributes which belong to him only , we can prove that the Holy Spirit is god by showing that he possesses one or more of theses attributes.\r\nSpirit perfectly knows the mind of god Ephesians 1:17. 1Cor 2:10\r\nWORK\r\nA THIRD evidence for the divinity of Holy spirit is by the type of work He does.\r\nHe creates new life, regenerates our Spirit. our access to salvation.\r\nFORMULAS\r\nThe last way is through the Trinitarian formulas that include his name along side the Father and the son.\r\nMathew 28:19, Romans 15:30\r\nBaptism should be taken in the name of the Trinity and the benediction 2Cor 13:14 also includes the name of Trinity', 9, '2020-10-19 17:49:03', '2020-10-21 18:29:41', NULL),
(2042, 564, 882, 'The biblical basis for believing n the divinity of the Holy Spirit can be demonstrated in many ways:\r\nNames:\r\nthe Spirit of the Lord , the  Spirit of God, the Spirit of the living God, Spirit of Jesus etc. all these names suggest that Holy Spirit is divine by indicating that God is united to the holy Spirit in the same way that a human being is united to his own spirit. 1corinthian 2:11\r\nattributes:\r\nGod possesses incommunicable attributes, which can only belong to him, we can prove that the Holy Spirit by showing that he possesses one or more of these attributes.\r\nHoly Spirit\'s omniscience can be seen when we read in scripture that the Spirit knows the mind of God. Ephesians 1:17\r\nHoly spirit is also proven to be omnipotent.\r\nWork:\r\nthird evidence is the type of work He does.\r\nHoly Spirit performs many works that exhibit divine power and attributes. He creates new life when he regenerates our spirits, he is our access to the father, Ephesians 2:18\r\nHoly Spirit inspired the writing pf Scripture, on in recognizing that the word of the holy spirit is the word of God, we acknowledge that the Holy spirit is God Himself.\r\nFormulas\r\nMathew 28:19 \r\nThe divinity of the holy Spirit is affirmed when we see in the Trinitarian Formulas, seeing Holy spirit alongside Father and the Son\r\nwe see it in Jesus teaching about baptism and also in benediction.', 9, '2020-10-19 18:07:10', '2020-10-21 18:29:41', NULL),
(2043, 564, 883, 'The Holy spirit is the person that has a distinct self awareness and divine personal attributes.\r\nthe holy Spirit is a real and distinct person within the God head.\r\n1. The Holy Spirit has a will. this is the faculty he uses to plan, to desire and to choose. He wants certain people to have certain gifts and other to have other gifts, only persons do. therefore the holy Spirit must be a person\r\n1Cor 12:11\r\n2.the holy spirit also has the attribute of intelligence. through which he possesses knowledge and the ability to teach others. He expresses his intelligence in many ways like searching and knowing the mind of God. Romans 8:27. Impersonal forces do not think, know ,teach. so the attribute of intelligence proves that the Spirit is a person.\r\n3. the holy spirit  also has emotions, internal feelings and affections that he expresses in response to other persons and events. Romans 15:13\r\nEmotions prove that  He is a person and not a simply a power.\r\n4. He has a will,  the ability to intern things and act on its own accord. this enables him to perform many actions that can only be done by persons. Holy Spirit offers testimony in John 15:16\r\n5. the Fact that the holy Spirit prays for believers is another proof of his personhood .\r\nImpersonal powers and forces do not pray and intercede , groaning in sincerity.\r\nOnly persons can do these things.\r\nso its proved that Holy Spirit is a person.', 8, '2020-10-19 18:24:09', '2020-10-21 18:29:41', NULL),
(2044, 564, 884, 'The Holy Spirit is identified as the Spirit of God\'s son in Galatians 4:6, and Spirit of the Father in Mathew 10:20.\r\nIt makes perfect sense to think of the Holy spirit as the Spirit of the father and of the son, and at the same time to insist that he is an entirely distinct person from them.\r\nJohn 16:17 says that Jesus says that Holy Spirit would not come unless the Son went away. Here Jesus clearly distinguished from the Spirit by saying that one goes before the other comes,\'\r\neach one had an appointed role and the role of the spirit would not begin until the son had completed his earthly work and ascended into heaven, this makes it clear that the spirit is distinct from the son.\r\nIn a similar way the Spirit also does things that distinguish him from the father.\r\nIn his role as counselor, the Holy Spirit is our defense attorney.\r\nwhen Holy Spirit intercedes with our Father, he demonstrated that they are distinct persons- one interceding and other hearing the intercession.', 8, '2020-10-19 18:35:46', '2020-10-21 18:29:41', NULL),
(2045, 564, 885, 'In Ontological Trinity, we are focusing on God\'s being and existence.\r\nthe Holy spirit is equal in power and glory to the father and the son.\r\nAll three of God\'s persons are infinite, eternal and unchangeable.\r\nEach person of the god head has different responsibilities , different authority, different assigned role. the Spirit\'s authority is subject to the higher authority of then father and the son.\r\nAnd the Spirit\'s role is largely to carry out their instruction and to bring them glory.\r\nHe is the third person of the ontological trinity, because he is breathed out by the father , whos is the first person  and by the son who is the second person.\r\nHoly Spirit is said to be the third person because he holds the third rank, being subordinate both to the father and to the son.\r\nThe Holy Spirit holds the lowest rank from the perspective of the economic trinity, but it is important to emphasize that he is still fully god and has absolutely sovereign authority over every aspect of creation. within trinity , there is a sense of mutual difference, since what one person does they all do . so the holy spirit\'s subordination to the Father and the son does not mean that he is some how inherently inferior to them- he is not.\r\nHe is fully equal to them in their essential divinity.', 9, '2020-10-19 18:50:45', '2020-10-21 18:29:41', NULL),
(2046, 565, 717, 'Missions originated in the heart of God. it is not something we decide to do, but God.\r\nGod reveals his purpose to us so that we may have a creative part in his mission.\r\ngod has limited what he will do. That limit is the possibility of what we can do through us\r\nGod sums up our awesome responsibility and the faith he puts in us in three basic purposes of his mission and ours.\r\n1. To bring glory to God\r\nGod\'s eternal plan is for his people to be the praise of his glory.(ephesians1:6)\r\nGlory of God is the ultimate goal of god\'s missions\r\n2. to share the good news with the alienated\r\nChristian mission or god\'s mission includes recreating man spiritually. God restores man\'s identity and his purpose for being\r\n The mystery of God\'s mission is clear that the gentiles should be fellow-heirs of the same bidy and partakers of his promise.(Ephesians 3:6)\r\n3. to display the wisdom of God to evil powers\r\nRedeemed man is the primary exhibit of God\'s grace.\r\nin the purpose of Christian mission , God intends for man to bring glory to him, to share the good news with the alienated , and to display God\'s wisdom to evil powers', 8, '2020-10-20 17:49:03', '2020-10-21 17:21:07', NULL),
(2047, 565, 718, 'God intends for his people to be a disciplined people, holy priests, and suffering servants to the world.\r\nits the mission of God\'s people to be \r\n1. A disciplined people: the purpose of discipline is to make one holy and separate does not mean lack of love and contact with others. God choose Abraham . his  descendants became a pilgrim people.\r\nGod had the right and obligation to discipline  Israel. this disciple involved nurture for motivation, training for obedience and punishment for correction.\r\nbut Israel often refused god and discipline.\r\nbut god the most holy and separate one is the most concerned for all people.\r\n\r\n2. A nation of priests\r\nOld testament priests represented god to man and secondly God to man.\r\nBut Israel misunderstood and misinterpreted and rejected it,\r\n3. servant people:\r\nthe Lord of Heaven and earth serves us  and expects us to be a servant people. we are to love like god and minister to all people like God.\r\nThe four servant passages in Isaiah clearly expresses the servant role of Israel and ultimately of Christ.\r\nThere is no way a people can become a holy nation of servant priests without suffering.\r\nGod\'s people must be willing to suffer if they are to be links to bring men to God.\r\nSo this is the mission of God\'s people to take his message of love and restoration with a servant hood attitude.', 8, '2020-10-20 18:07:50', '2020-10-21 17:21:07', NULL),
(2048, 565, 719, 'God fullfilled the purpose by becoming the disciplined Son in the incarnation the suffering servant and High Priest in the Crucifixion and the kingdom of heaven and earth in the resurrection.\r\nThe incarnation:\r\nwhen God spoke at the beginning of time, the world was created , it cost God nothing to speak the world into existence , but it cost him His Son to create the new humanity.\r\nThe incarnation is the good news that the kingdom of heaven has come in Christ.\r\nGod emptied himself as Christ\r\nJesus became a servant, he served man n the most menial ways, so that man might catch the vision of serving.\r\nThe Crucifixion:\r\nthe self emptying of Christ climaxed with Gethsemane and Golgotha.\r\nJesus the lamb was slain before the foundation of the world. Rev 13:8\r\nJesus \' will always submissive to the Father\'s overcame both the physical reality and Satanic demonic presence when he uttered \"not my will but thine be done\"\r\nJesus fulfilled the priestly role  by his intercessory prayers and by his death.\r\nJesus satisfied the father , subdued the Satan and reconciled man to God.\r\nForgiveness was available to those who believe in Christ as Savior on the basis of his sacrifice.\r\n\r\nThe resurrection:\r\nJesus emerged from the grave and a new  age  broke on the world.in his death and resurrection, Jesus spoiled the principalities and powers. Jesus grace the great commission on the basis of his resurrection.\r\nThe resurrection shouts that the victory is won over sin , death and satan', 8, '2020-10-20 18:27:19', '2020-10-21 17:21:07', NULL),
(2049, 565, 720, 'The mission of Christ could not be accomplished without the mission of the holy Spirit.\r\n1. the inspirer of the missions:\r\nthe Holy Spirit came to make God\'s people into the body of Christ.\r\nthrough the Spirit , God enables man to become  all he wants him to be. \r\nthe Holy Spirit performs varied ministries within the body of Christ, he regenerates, sanctifies, teaches, guides, comforts, illuminates and intercedes.\r\nthe most important ministry in relation to his mission is the filling of Christians for service.\r\nTh holy Spirit is the executor and administrator of the Great commission.\r\n2. The empowerer of the church\r\nThe filling of the holy Spirit gives us the boldness , wisdom, and the ability to witness.\r\nthe power we receive from the Holy Spirit is life changing and world changing because it is living and spiritual power.\r\nGod\'s mission demands God\'s power. Romans 8:16-17\r\nThe filling of the Spirit energizes and empowers different gifts in different persons, but in every case the result brings glory to Christ and attracts others to him.\r\n3. The guide in missions:\r\nAs executor of Christ\'s will, The Holy Spirit determines the course of missions.\r\nThe Holy Spirit usually guides his people nearby before sending them on a distant mission.\r\nThe Holy Spirit works throughout the world to prepare men\'s hearts for the gospel, but his primary work among God\' people is to send them forth with the gospel message . the Spirit works through God\'s people to accomplish his mission.', 9, '2020-10-20 18:46:10', '2020-10-21 17:21:07', NULL),
(2050, 565, 721, 'the Co- mission of the Church\r\nGod has chosen , sanctified and commissioned Church to be a blessing to the world. it is the body of Christ that fulfills his ministry in the world.\r\nWe are priests of God: the Calvary principle\r\nFormerly we were Christ less, homeless, promise less, hopeless and Godless(Ephesians 2:12)\r\nChrist redeemed us by his own Sacrifice and gave us even greater promises than Israel received (2 Peter 1:3-4)\r\nas the royal priesthood , we receive both the promises and the responsibilities of the new covenant.\r\nas royalty, we live in the blessedness of the kingdom as priests, we function as kingdom representatives.\r\n2.Servants of God: the incarnation principle:\r\nthe church as the body of Christ, is incarnate in the world to become the suffering  servant. it is not called out if the world but called to go into the world and love like Christ, forgive like Christ and give itself to the world like Christ.\r\n3.Sons of the King: the resurrection principle\r\nAs God\' s children we have an intimate relationship and and inherited interest in the kingdom. Jesus shared his heart with the children of the kingdom to involve them in establishing it. \r\nas children of the king we announce that the kingdom has come. With joy we tell the good news that our Father owns everything.', 9, '2020-10-20 19:04:33', '2020-10-21 17:21:07', NULL),
(2051, 562, 771, 'Critical scholars have offered three arguments with regards to the authorship of the Epistle of James\r\n\r\n1) They say that there is no mention of the author\'s relation to Jesus in the entire Epistle. They suggest that it\'s not possible that a brother of Jesus would write to the churches and not reveal his identity or relationship details when he identified himself\r\n\r\n2) Some other critical scholars assume psedonymity, as the book gives insights into the Greek culture, whereas James was from Palestine. Some of the Greek phrases or terminology used in the book of James is more advanced.\r\n\r\n3) The thrird view is that some of the views expressed in the epistle of James does not tally or match with  theological outlooks in the New Testament books. \r\n\r\nBut when we study or analyze the epistle traditionally, these arguments against the book\'s authoriship are weak and substantial to prove otherwise.\r\n\r\nThe arguments in fact are more compelling to prove that James has written this epistle. Also because of this, most evangelical scholars rightly affirm that James the brother of Jesus was the author of the letter that bears his name.', 8, '2020-10-21 15:16:31', '2020-10-21 17:21:34', NULL),
(2052, 562, 772, 'As the Epistle of James 1: verse 1 begins by addressing the epistle to \r\n1) The Twelve tribes scattered among the nations\r\n2) James 2:1 - addresses to Believers in our glorious Lord Jesus Christ\r\n\r\nWhen we consider the above 2 verses, it indicates that James original audience was primarily made up of Jewish Christians who lived outside of Jerusalem or Palestine.\r\n\r\nAfter persecution of the church began after Stephen\'s death the church were scattered throughtout Judea and Samaria. James was the leader of Jerusalem Church and was writing this epistle to the scattered members of the twelve tribes.\r\n\r\nThought the language and vocabulory supports the idea that it was addressed to the Jewish followers of Jesus. \r\n\r\nBut also there were many Gentile God fearing converts to Judais who attended synagogues, Gentile believers were regarded as Abraham\'s offspiring. Hence the epistle also covered gentile believers.', 8, '2020-10-21 15:22:47', '2020-10-21 17:21:34', NULL),
(2053, 562, 773, 'James the brother of Jesus Christ wrote this epistle addressed to the Jewish believers :\r\n\r\nPLACE :\r\nJames lived all his life in Jerusalem, until he was martyred, hence he wrote this epistle from Jerusalem\r\n\r\nWHEN : \r\nThis Epistle was written in AD 44, as leader of the early church in Jerusalem, \r\n\r\nFurthermore there is another probability that the latest possible date of composition is AD 62, the year of James martyrdom.\r\n\r\nBut since the epistle talks about the word synagogue, it seems to indicate an early stage in the development of Christian movement. \r\n\r\nWHY ? PURPOSE ?\r\nJames 1:2-4 addresses his readers\r\nThe early Jewish converts were facing trials of many kinds, James was encouraging them and motivating them, saying that the testing of your faith produces perseverance. And let perseverance finish its work that you may be mature and complete, not lacking anything\r\n\r\nJames audience were facing trials of many kinds, James was calling them to have pur joy in their trials. Trials produce persevrance. Those who persevere will become mature and complete not lacking anything. Facing trials, ask God for wisdom and it will be given to you\r\n\r\nJames called his audience to pursue wisdom from God so that they would have joy in their trials. Wisdom from God was the key to receiving joy as they endured their many trials.', 8, '2020-10-21 15:39:28', '2020-10-21 17:21:34', NULL),
(2054, 569, 648, 'General resurrection: called \"general\" because it includes all human beings that have ever lived. Called \"resurrection\" because the souls of the dead will be reunited with their reconstituted bodies. The general resurrection can be considered either one of the final events of the intermediate state or one of the first events of the final state which ends all temporary punishments of unregenerate souls\r\nEarly Controversies- Pharisees believed that there would be a general resurrection of the righteous and the wicked. Sadducees denied that there would be a general resurrection of the dead. \r\nThe controversy is rooted in their understanding of scripture- Pharisees accepted the Old Testament as scripture where general resurrection is clearly taught (Isaiah 26:19, Daniel 12:2) and Sadducees accepted only the five books written by Moses. Jesus, Paul and the early church took the side of the Pharisees and strongly refuted the Sadducees (Mark 12:18-27). Paul said they rejected the truth and destroyed faith. Paul\'s opponents in Corinth found resurrection repulsive (1 Corinthians 15:12-34). \r\nIn defending the resurrection of the regenerate, Paul removed any objection to the general resurrection.', 8, '2020-10-21 15:39:56', '2020-10-21 17:22:04', NULL),
(2055, 569, 649, 'Divine Authority is God\'s legal and moral right to carry out his will that it\'s perfectly within his rights to do it, and that he commits no wrong if he does it. God\'s divine authority in the general resurrection will divide into two parts: his authority over hell, and his authority over heaven.\r\n1. Hell- When unregenerate souls suffer in hell during the intermediate state, they suffer because God is punishing them. And when they\'re drawn out of hell in order to face judgement, it\'s because God has summoned them into his court. God rules over hell and has complete over Satan, the demons, and the unregenerate souls he imprisons there (2 Peter 2:4,9).\r\n2. Heaven- Heaven is God\'s throne room, where his authority and glory are manifested more openly than anywhere else (Isaiah 66:1, Matthew 5:34). The descriptions of God ruling from his throne in heaven appear to be literal (1 kings 22:19, 2 Chronicles 18:18).', 8, '2020-10-21 15:46:36', '2020-10-21 17:22:04', NULL),
(2056, 562, 774, 'The Epistle of James focuses a great deal of attention on wisdom as the way to find joy in trimes of trial. Many interpreters have considered it to be a book of wisdom.\r\n\r\nPreceding the Epistle of James, there were alread wisdom writings in the Old Testament, including the books of Job, Ecclesiastes and Proverbs. James indebtedness to the Old Testament literature is evident when he takes the example of Job to proote perseverance. \r\n\r\nJames touched on many topics, such as speech, the treatment of widows, orphans, poverty and favoritism. These topics reflect numerous parallels with the content of the book of Proverbs.\r\n\r\nMuch of Jesus instruction recorded in the gospel is characteristic of wisdom teaching in Israel, biblical scholars have noticed a number of similarities between the writing of James and instructions from Jesus\r\n\r\nJames book resembles wisdom literature in form and content. It focuses on important themes, by spending few verses on a particular topic and thereafter moving on to another. \r\n\r\nThe most important point which is unique to James in terms of wisdom is that he links his wisdom very closely with the teachings of Jesus. \r\n\r\nJames uses a wide range of practical illustrations to explain his point to the readers, referring to ships being guided by little rudders and farers that are patiently waiting, about merchants that are travelling. \r\n\r\nBut the content of James is really carrying forward the way in which Jesus presents the kindom and the way the presence of the kingdom changes your life.\r\n\r\nAs part of the New Testament, James is an epistle written to the Church to gain practical wisdom.', 9, '2020-10-21 15:51:25', '2020-10-21 17:21:34', NULL),
(2057, 569, 650, '1. Natural World- God uses eschatological events to alter how the natural world works in order to prepare it for his presence. God\'s curse on mankind included a curse on the earth itself (Genesis 3:17-18). Paul taught that the earth will be rescued through the resurrection of redeemed humanity (Romans 8:19-23). Just as creation was corrupted through God\'s curse on humanity it will be purged of corruption through humanity\'s redemption. \r\n2. Hell- the souls of regenerate will be removed from hell and returned to their bodies on earth so they can face God\'s judgement. The demons may be released either to fight in the rebellion or be summoned to judgement with the unregenerate. \r\n3. Heaven- Regenerate souls will return to earth in order to appear before God\'s judgement throne. We don\'t have bodies in heaven, so we aren\'t complete human beings there. Jesus\' throne will be on earth, not in heaven and it\'s much better to remain in his presence. The new heaven and new earth will be even more wonderful.', 9, '2020-10-21 15:54:19', '2020-10-21 17:22:04', NULL),
(2058, 569, 651, '1. Fallen Angels- Both 2 peter 2:4 and Jude 6, report that the demons used to be angels that held authority from God.  But they rebelled against him, and abandoned their heavenly homes and their authority. As a result, they\'re now chained in gloomy dungeons awaiting Christ\'s judgement. \r\n2. Unregenerate- Scripture teach that when the resurrected human race appears before Christ\'s judgement throne. At the final judgement, the Lord will separate the unregenerate from the regenerate and will condemn the unregenerate (Romans 2:5-8; Rev 11:18, 20:11-15). \r\n3. Regenerate- After Jesus separates the unregenerate from the regenerate, he\'ll also render judgement on the regenerate. We see this in many places, including Romans 2:7, Revelation 11:18, and again in Matthew 25, where Jesus compared the ungenerate to goats and the regenerate to sheep Matthew 25:33-34)', 8, '2020-10-21 16:01:16', '2020-10-21 17:22:04', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(2059, 562, 775, 'James audience were the Jewish believers, Christians who had been driven out of Jerusalems and were scattered around, away from their homes. They were facing different kinds of trials that discouraged them. And for this reason James first words about the importance of wisdom began with a call to joy.\r\n\r\nJames 1:2 says\r\nConsider it pure joy, whenever you face trials of many kinds\r\n\r\nJames is encouraging his readers and appealing to them to consider trials pure joy, complete and unmitigated joy.\r\n\r\nJames taught that perseverance through trials makes it possible for believers to be mature and complete. In other words, when God\'s people endure hardships, they grow into the fullness of all that God intends for them. \r\n\r\nJames 1:5 \r\nIf any of you lacks wisdom, let him ask God who gives generously\r\n\r\nJames suggested that those who want to have pure joy as they suffer trials must ask God for  insight and wisdom to help them understand how their trials will lead them to a better understanding that God intends us to have. We need to have wisdom to understand how God works through the trials and we can be hence joyful. Wisdom strengthens our confidence and our trust in god increases preparing us for eternal salvation.', 8, '2020-10-21 16:09:45', '2020-10-21 17:21:34', NULL),
(2060, 569, 652, 'God will consider every piece of evidence in order to ensure that perfect justice is upheld (Eccl 12:14; Matt 12:36 says that, Men will have to give account..for every careless word they have spoken; 1 Cor 4:5 says that He will bring to light what is hidden in darkness and will expose the motives of men\'s hearts; Psa 62:12; Prov 24:12; Matt 16:27) \r\nWe\'ll be jugded according to our own situations: \r\nHowever, not everyone will be held to the same level of accountability. \r\nThose who have sinned with more knowledge of God\'s requirements will be judged more harshly (Luke 10:13-14). Those of us who are bound to God in covenant are more greatly obligated to obey him (Psalm 50:4-6). Teachers within the church will be judged more strictly (James 3:1). Those that have never heard the gospel will still be judged and condemned although their guilt will be less (Acts 20:26,27).', 9, '2020-10-21 16:12:07', '2020-10-21 17:22:04', NULL),
(2061, 571, 660, 'In regards to methodology in terms of language study in general and of lexical semantics in particular. there are two foci of study; diachronic study and synchronic study. This is true of any language, ancient or modern, whether related to the New Testament or Old Testament or to neither. In other words, this is not an issue unique to biblical studies. \r\nIn other words, the Diachronic study is what traces the historical development of a language from its earliest known form or usage up to the particular instance under consideration. To illustrate with lexical semantics, it is possible to trace the historical origin and development of a particular work.', 8, '2020-10-23 02:11:10', '2020-10-27 17:02:02', NULL),
(2062, 571, 661, 'The concept of Synthesis is not difficult to grasp. We use it often in daily life. Basically, it simply means combining different components of something into a whole. In many respects, this is what we do when we look at the scriptures with the synchronic synthesis in mind. We describe the ways different components of theology revealed in a particular period of history fit together in a coherent, logical structure. To grasp how synchronic synthesis involves assessing the logical structure of Old Testament theology at a particular time, we\'ll touch on two issues. First, we\'ll look at a popular denial of the Old Testament\'s logical character, and second, we\'ll offer an affirmation of its logical coherence.', 8, '2020-10-23 02:18:53', '2020-10-27 17:02:02', NULL),
(2063, 571, 662, 'poetry is a form of literary art that uses aesthetic and rhythmic qualities of language to evoke meanings in addition to prosaic ostensible meaning. Poetry has traditionally been distinguished from prose by its being set in verse. The prose is cast in a sentence, poetry in lines the syntax of proses is dedicated by meaning, whereas that of poetry is held across meter or the visual aspects of the poem,.\r\n\r\nThe defining feature of a narrative poem is its plot. Narrative poems feature an entire story, told by one narrator from beginning to end. Narrative poetry is one of the major categories of poetry but is distinguished from lyric poetry by its focus on plot over emotions. In practice, there is a crossover between these two types of poetry; poets often incorporate lyric elements into their narrative poems and vice versa.', 8, '2020-10-23 02:31:52', '2020-10-27 17:02:02', NULL),
(2064, 571, 663, 'A synchronic study of the Old Testament concentrates their attention on particular periods of time in the Old Testament. Unlike the modern journalistic historical writing,  biblical theologians exercise temporal flexibility when they divide Old Testament history into synchronic units. Sometimes they focus on relatively short, time frames, and other times they focus on longer periods of history.\r\n\r\nFor instance, in the relatively short story of Abraham\'s sacrifice of Issac in Genesis chapter 22, many things happen. But biblical theologians ask, \" What theological outlooks characterized this part of Abraham\'s life\" \r\n\r\nBiblical theologians also deal with a larger period of time, like Abraham\'s life in Genesis chapter 11 through chapter 25 a time that spanned around 175 years.', 8, '2020-10-23 02:46:04', '2020-10-27 17:02:02', NULL),
(2065, 571, 664, 'To get to the plain meaning of the text, We tend to think that our understanding is the same things as the Holy Spirit\'s or Human author\'s intent. The bible that most of us ready is already an interpretation from the language that is originally was penned in. This is another reason for the close examination of Scriptures and good exegetical study. \r\n\r\nThe word of God is given to people throughout history. Because God chose to speak to us in this way every book of the Bible has historical particularity. This means that every document is conditioned by the language, time, and culture in which it was originally written, as well as the oral history it had before it was written. \r\n\r\nThe important aspect of the Bible is the variety of ways in which God chose to speak to us: a narrative history, genealogies, chronicles, laws of all kinds, the poetry of all kinds, proverbs, prophetic oracles, riddles, drama, parables, letters, sermons, and apocalypse.', 8, '2020-10-23 03:00:29', '2020-10-27 17:02:02', NULL),
(2066, 578, 747, 'उत्तर =  जब लोग अच्छी खासी लंबाई और जटिलता के साहित्य को लिखते हैं तो सामान्यता उनके कई इरादे और उद्देश होते हैं और यही बात लूका के लिए भी सत्य थी जब वह लुका को सुसमाचार और प्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक के अपने दो संस्करणों को लिखता है वहां आशा करता है कि उसका लेखक कार्य थियुफिलुस  और कलीसिया के जीवनों को कई विभिन्न तरीकों से प्रभावित करेगा इसलिए हमें उसके उद्देश्यों को कम करके नहीं समझने के लिए सावधान रहना चाहिए परंतु फिर भी लुका ने स्पष्ट कहा है कि लेखक कार्य के लिए उसके पास एक उद्देश्य था।\r\n जैसा कि हम देखेंगे कि लोगों ने स्पष्टता से कहा कि जब वह इसके लिए लिखता है तो उसके पास दोहरा उद्देश्य था एक और तो लुका यहां घोषित करता है कि उसका ऐतिहासिक उद्देश्य था पहली शताब्दी की कलीसिया की एक सच्ची और विश्वास योग्य ऐतिहासिक कहानी को लिखने की इच्छा और दूसरी और वह यह घोषणा करता है कि उसके कुछ विशेष धर्म में वैज्ञानिक इरादे थे सुसमाचार के संदेश की सत्यता और महत्वपूर्ण था को प्रमाणित और बताने की इच्छा एक सच्चे ऐतिहासिक विवरण को लिखने की इसके इरादे से आरंभ करते हुए हम लुका के दोहरे उद्देश्यों के दोहरे पहलुओं को देखेंगे ।\r\n\r\n ऐतिहासिक विवरण:-\r\n\r\n\r\nलुका 1:1-3 मैं अपने सुसमाचार की प्रस्तावना में लोगों ने यहां एक गीत किया है वह आरंभ की कलीसिया का इतिहास लिखने के बारे में बहुत ज्यादा उत्सुक था वहां पर उसके शब्दों को सुनें किस अनुच्छेद में सच्ची इतिहास को लेकर लुक्का की चिंता कई तरीकों से स्पष्ट है उसका यह कहना है कि उन बातों का जो हमारे बीच में बीती है का  अर्थ यह है कि वह ऐतिहासिक घटनाएं जो घटित हो चुकी है लुक्का यहां भी उल्लेख करता है कि उसके इनके बारे में प्रदर्शित हो अर्थात चंद दिनों से विचार-विमर्श किया है और सावधानी से जांच करके इनके विवरणों का वर्णन किया है साथ ही उसने क्रम अनुसार विवरण लिखने में भी सावधानी बरतनी है ताकि जिस सत्य की वह सूचना दे रहा है वास्तव में स्पष्ट और सटीकता से बताई जा सके।\r\n संक्षेप में लुक्का का सुसमाचार और प्रेरित ओके काम की पुस्तक के अपने दो संस्करणों में रुका एक सच्चे ऐतिहासिक विवरण को देना चाहता था सुसमाचार में यीशु के जीवन के साथ आरंभ करते हुए पहली शताब्दी की कलीसिया में प्रेरितो के काम  की पुस्तक में जारी रहते हुए लुका सच्चे ऐतिहासिक को लिखने के बारे में चिंतित था क्योंकि वहां संपूर्ण बाइबिल में दोहराए गए एक मौलिक सिद्धांत को समझता था परमेश्वर स्वयं को वास्तविक विवरण के द्वारा स्थान और समय में प्रकट करता है वह अपने उद्धार और न्याय को लाने के बारे में इतिहास के माध्यम से काम करता है।\r\n दुर्भाग्य से हाल ही की शताब्दी में कई आलोचनात्मक विद्वानों ने यह तर्क दिया है कि मुक्ति और न्याय की असाधारण वास्तविकता इतिहास से बिल्कुल अलग है सामान्य उन्होंने आश्चर्य पूर्व कहां है कि परमेश्वर ने आलू की कार्य इतिहास में यह ने वास्तविक स्थान और समय में प्रगट नहीं होते हैं।\r\n इसकी बजाय वे यहां विश्वास करते हैं कि वास्तविक इतिहास केवल स्वभाविक है ना कि अलौकिक परिणाम स्वरुप जब आलोचनात्मक धर्म शास्त्री पवित्र शास्त्र में परमेश्वर के कार्य के बारे में पढ़ते हैं तो वे अक्सर इन घटनाओं को तथ्य हीन धार्मिक भावनाओं की अभिव्यक्ति के रूप में देखते हैं एक तरह से धार्मिक कपोकथ।\r\n परंतु लुकयम स्पष्ट करता है कि वह कोई धार्मिक कपोल कथा को लिखने की कोशिश नहीं कर रहा था उसका इरादा वास्तविक इतिहास का वर्णन करना था तथ्य तो यह है कि उसने इस तरह से लिखा जिससे कि उसने दावे को सत्यापित किया खंडन करना आसान बनाता है एक उदाहरण के रूप में लुका ने अपने लेखन कार्य को प्रसिद्ध ऐतिहासिक संदर्भों की सीमाओं के भीतर ही लिखा प्ररितो के काम की पुस्तक में उदाहरण के लिए हम इन पुरुषों के नामों को पाते हैं जैसे कि गम लीएल 5:34 मे गल्लियो 18:12 मे फेलिक्स 23:26 मैं और फेसतुस 24:27 मैं यह सभी  प्राचीन यहूदी और रोम के संसार में जाने पहचाने लोग थे इन पुरुषों और अन्य ऐतिहासिक बारीकियों का उल्लेख करके रुका अपने पाठकों के लिए स्वयं रूप में अपने शोध की जांच करने को आसान बनाता है वे अन्य लोगों के साथ बातें करते थे जिन्हें इन लोगों और घटनाओं का ज्ञान था जिनका उन्होंने वर्णन किया और कुछ मामलों में वह इन्हीं विषयों पर दूसरों के लेखन को पढ़ सकते थे यदि लुक्का का विवरण तथ्य सामान्य था नहीं होता तो शंख वादियों को इसका खंडन करना आसान हो गया होता विशेष रुप से 19 वीं सदी के अंत के बाद से कई विद्वानों ने बाइबिल के अलावा दूसरे लेखन और अन्य पुरातत्विक वर्णों के साथ तुलना करके प्रेरितो के काम की पुस्तक की ऐतिहासिक सच्चाई की जांच की है इन अध्ययनों से कई ने कई तरीकों से यहां संकेत दिया जिनमें लुक्का एक जवानियां इतिहासकार था  लेकिन समय हमें केवल 1 जोड़ी विशिष्ट उदाहरण का उल्लेख करने की अनुमति देगा।\r\nपहला प्रेरितो के काम 28:7 बिल्लू का विशेष ऐतिहासिक शब्द वाली के ज्ञान को प्रदर्शित करता है वहां  उसने माल्टा दीप के प्रधान को दीप के सबसे पहले व्यक्ति के रूप में संबोधित किया है इस असामान्य शब्द वाली ने सदियों से कई अनुभवों को पहेलियों में डाला हुआ है लेकिन हम ही पुराना तरीका अनुसंधान ने यहां प्रगट किया है कि यह वास्तव में उस समय के प्रधान का अधिकार पद था।\r\nदुसरा प्रेरितो के काम 27:21-26 मलूका ने जहाज में प्रकट किए गए पॉल उसके विवरा व्यवहारों को उन तरीकों से वर्णन किया है जिनको की ऐतिहासिक अनुसंधान द्वारा प्रमाणित किया गया है वहां पर लुक्का लिखता है कि पॉल उसने बड़े तूफान के दौरान जहाज के पूरे नाविक दल को जो उसे रूम ले जा रहे थे प्रोत्साहित किया और सुझाव दिया अतीत में कई आलोचनात्मक विद्वानों ने बहस की है कि एक कैदी के रूप में पॉल उसके लिए इस तरह से खुले तौर पर बात करना असंभव रहा होगा इस कारण उन्होंने यहां सार निकाला कि लुक्का ने प्रेरित के  एक काल्पनिक वीर उत्पन्न किया था परंतु हाल के अनुसंधान सोदिया दिखाते हैं कि पहली सदी में समुद्री कानून जब जहाज गंभीर खतरे में होता था तो किसी को भी बात करने और चालक दल को सलाह देने की अनुमति देता था यह उदाहरण लुक्का की देहात की तथ्यों के प्रति निष्ठा को दिखाते हैं और वास्तविक इतिहास घटनाओं को लिखने का उसका इरादा हमें यह स्मरण दिलाता है कि परमेश्वर का सत्य सत्य जीवन की असली वास्तविक से अलग नहीं है इसलिए बजाए बाइबिल पर आधारित विश्वास में उधार वास्तविक इतिहास मैं और उस के माध्यम से आता है इसलिए हीरो का एक सच्चे ऐतिहासिक वरुण को लिखने के लिए इतना चिंतित था|\r\n\r\n: सुसमाचार का संदेश :-\r\n\r\n लुक्का के ऐतिहासिक उद्देश्य को अपने मन में रखते हुए हमें लुक्का की राधे के दूसरे पहलू का उल्लेख करना चाहिए प्रेरितो के काम की पुस्तक में सुसमाचार के संदेश की वास्तविक सामर्थ को संचारित करने का धर्म वैज्ञानिक उद्देश्य लुका 1:3-4 जैसा कि हम यहां पर देखते हुए लोका ने प्रेरित के काम  का इतिहास थियुफिलुस  और अन्यों ने शिक्षा पाई थी उसकी पुष्टि करने के लिए लिखा इसका अर्थ यह है कि प्रेरित ओके काम की पुस्तक सही अर्थों में धर्म शिक्षा की प्रश्नोत्तरी वाली पुस्तक या उपदेश आत्मक इतिहास के रूप में चिन्हित की जा सकती है लुका चहाता था कि थियुफिलुस  और उसके अन्य पाठक गण एक विशेष तरह के दृष्टिकोण और विशेष तरह की धर्म वैज्ञानिक प्रसिद्ध शब्दों के ऐतिहासिक घटनाओं पर कुछ निश्चित धर्म ज्ञानिक दृष्टिकोण को जिनका कि उसने प्रेरितो के काम की पुस्तक में विवरण दिया है उसको अपनाएं।\r\n जैसा कि हमने पहले के पाठक में देखा लुका इस संसार और संपूर्ण इतिहास को मसीह के प्रभुत्व और राज्य की नजरों से देखता था उसने पुराने नियम की आशाओं और प्रतिज्ञा हो कोई इशू और उसकी शिक्षा के द्वारा पूरा होते हुए देखा और वह चाहता था कि थियुफिलुस  भी आराम की कलीसिया की घटनाओं के उसके लेख को इन्हीं नजरों से देखे की कैसे मशीनें परमेश्वर की आत्मा के द्वारा मसीह में परमेश्वर के राज्य को विस्थापित किया और उसे निरंतर बनाया था जा रहा है इसलिए जब हम आज प्रेरित हों के काम के पुस्तक को पढ़ते हैं तो हमें सदैव ध्यान में रहना रखना है कि लुका केवल सच्चे तथ्यों का ही विरोध नहीं दे रहा था ताकि हम सिर्फ यह जाने की बहुत पहले कौन सी घटना घटी थी इसकी वजह वहां हमारा ध्यान 19 शिक्षकों की ओर भी आकर्षित कर रहा था जो कि कल ईशा के लिए मूलभूत थी अर्थात पवित्र आत्मा के मध्य समिति के शपथ काम करने के लिए विश्वास ने गवा|', 9, '2020-10-23 03:41:31', '2020-10-27 17:02:36', NULL),
(2067, 578, 748, 'उत्तर =  यरूशलेम प्राचीन इजरायल की राजधानी थी जो कि पुराने नियम में परमेश्वर का विशेष राष्ट्र था यरूशलेम लुक्का की कहानी का प्रारंभिक बिंदु था क्योंकि संपूर्ण पुराने नियम में परमेश्वर के राज्य में और साथ में यीशु की सेवकाई में  भी इसने पूर्व प्रमुख भूमिका को आधा किया था इसके अलावा लुक्का ने यरूशलेम की घटनाओं को प्रेरित ओके काम की पुस्तक में कई स्थानों पर लिखा जो कि नियमित रूप से दिखाई दिखता है कि प्ररितो के काम के द्वारा सुसमाचार को नए देशों में फैलाने का कार्य अभी इसी विशेष शहर में निहित है ।\r\n यरूशलेम में सुसमाचार के द्वारा राज्य के विकास की कहानी को लोका ने चार मुख्य समूह में लिखा है सबसे पहले प्रेरित ओके काम अध्याय 1और 2  मैं पवित्र आत्मा के  जाना और उड़ेला जाना दूसरा प्रेरितों के काम अध्ययन 3-4 मैं मंदिर में दिया गया पत्र उसका संदेश और उसके बाद आने वाला सताओ तीसरा प्रेरितों के काम अध्ययन 5 मैं अन्नया और सपेरा की कहानी और उसके बाद आने वाला सताओ और चौथा प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 6:18:4 मैं सेवको  चुनाव और इसके बाद आने वाला सताव।\r\n उदाहरण के द्वारा स्त्री के विकास कई जानी पहचानी घटनाओं में प्रगट होता है जो की यरूशलेम में घटित हुई जैसे कि।\r\n●प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 1 मे प्ररितो का अधिकृत किया जाना\r\n●प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 2  मैं पवित्र आत्मा का पहनते कोस्ट के दिन उड़ेला जाना\r\n●प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 3,4 और 5  मैं यरूशलेम में अचरी कर्म का अनुभव विशेषकर पतरस के द्वारा\r\n इसी समय मसीही समुदाय में हम कई तरह के तनाव को देखते हैं जिन पर  सम्मिलित है ।\r\n\r\n●प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 1 मैं वहां प्रश्न कि कौन 12वां प्रेरित बनेगा\r\n●प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 5  मैं अनन्या और सपेरा के द्वारा दान दिए गए पैसों के लिए बोला गया झूठ और\r\n●प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 6  मैं यूनानी भी दुआओं की अपेक्षिता\r\n\r\n इसके आगे लुका के लेखक में यार उसने में सुसमाचार के लिए दी गई गवाही के साथ ब्रह्म विकास और विरोध का प्ररूप दिखता है उदाहरण के लिए।\r\n\r\n●प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 2 मे पेन्तेकुस्त के दिन  लगभग 3000 लोग कलिसीया में जोड़े गए\r\n●प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 4 मे कलिसीया की सदस्यता  लगभग 5000 तक बढ गई जब यूहन्ना और पतरस को बन्दी गृह मे डाल दिया गया और \r\n●प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 6 मे कई यहूदी याजक कलिसीया में जुड गए ।\r\n\r\n परंतु फिर भी जैसा कि हमने पहले ही सुझाव दिया था यहां ब्रह्मा विश्वास का अक्सर आ विश्वास ही संसार की ओर से आए सताओ के साथ-साथ आया जैसे कि:\r\n●प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 5  मैं पतरस और यूहन्ना का पकड़ा जाना और पीटा जाना\r\n●प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 7 मैं इस्तिफ़ानुस का सहीद होना\r\n●प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 8 मैं यरूशलेम में सताओ के कारण कलीसिया बिखरना\r\n\r\n अतिरिक्त  तनाव और अब ब्रह्म विरोध के कारण  नई कलीसिया के मां तो उत्साहित होने की हम अपेक्षित आ कर सकते हैं परंतु पवित्र आत्मा की सामर्थ्य के अभियंता में वास्तविकता इसके बिल्कुल विपरीत थी सुसमाचार की गवाही बड़ी निर्बाध गति के साथ आगे बढ़ती रही अंतत बिना किसी रूकावट के इस का विकास होता रहा।', 8, '2020-10-23 03:52:49', '2020-10-27 17:02:36', NULL),
(2068, 578, 749, 'उत्तर =  प्ररितो के काम की पुस्तक  का दूसरा मुख्य खंड प्रेरितों के काम 8:5-9:31 मैं यहूदियों और सांमरिया मेक अलीशा की सुसमाचार ये गवाही के ऊपर केंद्रित होता है यहूदियों और सामरिया कहवा टी पुराने नियम के सॉइल को दी गई प्रतिज्ञा की हुई भूमि के दक्षिणी और उत्तरी के लगभग बराबर था यीशु ने स्वयं इन हंस तो मैं अपने स्वर्ग रोहन से पहले सेवक आई की थी यहूदी और सांमरिया पर लुक्का के ध्यान केंद्रित को कहानियों के दो मुख्य समूह में बांटा जा सकता है प्रेरितों के काम 8:5-40 मे फिलिप्पुस की सेवक आई और प्रेरितों के काम 9:1-31 मैं पौलुस का मन परिवर्तन।\r\n यह कहानियां कल विकाश के आंतरिक विकास की ओर हमारा ध्यान आकर्षित करती है उदाहरण के लिए प्रेरितों के काम अध्याय 8 में अतिरिक्त विकास निरंतर जारी रहा जैसे जैसे नए विश्वासी लगातार पवित्र आत्मा से बढ़ते चले गए और  प्रेरितों के काम अध्ययनों में राहुल को उसके मत परिवर्तन के बाद एक प्रेरित बन गया ।\r\n फिर भी इन घटनाओं के साथ-साथ कलिसीया के भीतर तनाव भी बनने लगा  उदाहरण के लिए प्रेरितों के काम अध्ययन 8 मैं प्रश्नों को उठाया गया क्योंकि कुछ विश वासियों ने अभी तक पहुंचा आत्मा को प्राप्त नहीं किया था। प्ररितो के काम 8 मैं शिमोन जादूगर ने प्रेरित  से पवित्र आत्मा की शक्ति को खरीदने की कोशिश की \r\n दूसरी तरफ ब्रह्मा विश्वास और विरोध का नमूना भी निरंतर चलता रहा उदाहरण के लिए दिया और सांमरिया में इन घटनाओं जैसे कि कई नए लोग फिलिपु के सुसमाचारीय सेवकाई  के द्वारा और प्रेरितो के काम अध्यय 9 में  उसके मन परिवर्तन के द्वारा कलिसीया  निरंतर गुणात्मक तौर पर विकास करती चली  गई ।\r\n परंतु फिर भी यहां विकास अविश वासियों के विरोध के बगैर घटित नहीं हुआ उदाहरण के लिए शाउल ने प्रेरित के काम 9 मैं अपने मन परिवर्तन से पहले विश वासियों को सताया और प्रेरितों के काम अध्ययन 9 मैं ही कुछ यहूदियों ने शाउल का उसके मन परिवर्तन के बाद कत्ल करने की कोशिश की एक बार फिर से आंतरिक तनाव और ब्रह्म विरोध अंत में कलिसीया को रोकने में विफल रहा ।\r\n इसकी बजाय पवित्र आत्मा ने कलीसिया में परिपक्व और गुणात्मक विकास को लाने के लिए इनकी चुनौतियों का उपयोग किया।', 8, '2020-10-23 04:03:15', '2020-10-27 17:02:36', NULL),
(2069, 578, 750, 'उत्तर = प्ररितो के काम  का तीसरा मुख्य खंड यह बताता है कि  कैसे सुसमाचार प्रतिज्ञा कि वे देश की सीमाओं के बाहर पृथ्वी के छोर तक फैल गया जैसा कि उस समय इसे जाना जाता था जैसा कि हमने उल्लेख किया है 9:32-12:25 मे फीनीके कुप्रस  और अंत किया में सुसमाचार के फैलने से आरंभ करते हुए हम इस खंड को ज्यादा बारीकी से देखेंगे।\r\n\r\n\r\nफीनीके कुप्रस और अन्ताकिया :-\r\n\r\n\r\n यह खंड सुसमाचार प्रचार कार्य हो दिया और सांमरिया  से आगे की ओर पहले विशेष प्रसार के बारे में बताता है जब यहां फीनीके कुप्रस  और सीरिया में अंतर क्या की अन्य जातियों के आस पास वाले क्षेत्र में फैल गया है प्रेरितों के काम  इस खंड में हम पतरस की सेवर कायको प्ररितो के काम 9:32-43 मे लुद्दा और याफा में 10:1-11:12 मैं पतरस की सेव काई केसरिया में अन्य जाति कुंरनेलीस उसके यह 11:19-30 मैं सीरिया के अंत क्या में सुसमाचार के विस्तार और 12:1-25 मैं पतरस का आश्चर्यजनक तरीके से यरूशलेम के बंदी गिरा से छुटकारे के बारे में पढ़ते हैं।\r\n इसमें कोई आश्चर्य की बात नहीं है कि यहां पर भी अंत किया विकास और तनाव का नमूना नियमित रूप से कार्य कर रहा है दुकाने अंत किया विकास के कई उदाहरणों को लिखा है उदाहरण के लिए प्रेरितों के काम अध्ययन 10 अनु जाति कलीसिया में लगाए गए प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 12 मेक अलीशा पतरस के आश्चर्यजनक तरीके से छुटकारे को लेकर उत्साहित हो गई थी।\r\n और इसमें कोई संदेह नहीं है कि वहां पर संबंधित तनाव भी थे उदाहरण के लिए प्रेरितों के काम अध्ययन 11 मैं कई यहूदी विश्वास यानी जातियों को कल ईशा की संगति में पूरी तरह से लेने में झिझक के और इसी अध्याय 11 में बहुतों ने पुराने नियम के भोजन संबंधित विभागों के प्रतिबंधों में ढील दिए जाने के कारण विरोध प्रकट किया ।\r\n इस खंड में भी लोग का भ्रम विश्वास और विरोध के नमूने पर जोर देता है उदाहरण के लिए उसने प्ररितो के काम अध्ययन 10 में कुरनेलुयस और कई अन्य जातियों की मन परिवर्तन और प्रेरितों के काम अध्ययन 11 मे बरनबास  की सफल सुसमाचार यह सेवर काय के माध्यम से बाहरी विकास के लिए लिखा है।\r\n परंतु यहां विकास भी बिना विरोध के नहीं हुआ था इस तनाव में प्रेरित के काम अध्ययन 12 मे  याकूब की मृत्यु और इसी अध्याय 12 में पतरस को बंद ग्राम में डाला जाना सम्मिलित है।\r\n\r\n\r\nकुप्रस फ्रूगिया और गलातिया:-\r\n\r\n\r\nप्ररितो के काम 13:1-15:35 मेलु का चौथे मुख्य खंड की ओर मुड़ता है कुप्रस फ्रूगिया और गलतियां में सुसमाचार का प्रचार होना इस खंड में सुसमाचार यरूशलेम यह दिया सांवरिया से और आगे की ओर बढ़ता हुआ एशिया माइनर के पूर्व हिस्सों में फैल गया  प्रेरितों के काम  की पुस्तक का यह अखंड दो मुख्य विश्व में विभाजित होता है 13:1-14:28 मैं पॉलिश की पहली मिशनरी यात्रा है और प्रेरितों के काम 15:1-35 मैं यरूशलेम की महासभा।\r\n अपनी रणनीति को जारी रखते हुए लोका ने अंत क्या विकास और तनाव को नमूने में इस खंड में भी दिखाया है उसमें अंतरिक विकास की और कुछ ऐसी बातों के द्वारा संकेत किया है जैसे कि प्ररितो के काम 14  मैं पोलिस गलतियों की कलियों को मजबूत करना और प्रेरित ओके काम अध्ययन 15 मैं प्यार उस लेन की महासभा का निर्माण जिसमें मसीह के लिए मन फिर आओ के समय अन्य जातियों के खतने की मांग को नहीं करता था।\r\n लोका ने इस खंड में अंतरिक तनाव का भी उल्लेख किया है विशेष पर जब वह अन्य जाति से आए हुए लोगों से संबंधित व्यवहारिक परेशानियों के बारे में लिखना प्रेरित ओके काम अध्याय 15 में यहूदियों और अन्य जातियों विश वासियों के बीच खतने और यहूदी परंपरा अनुसार भोजन संबंधित कठोर नियमों को लेकर तनाव उत्पन्न हो गया था।\r\n\r\n\r\nएशिया मकिदुनिया और अखाया :-\r\n\r\n\r\nप्ररितो के काम का पाॅचवाॅ प्रमुख 15:36-21:16 तक चलता है जहां पर सुसमाचार की गवाही कोरोमंत ओएशिया मकदुनिया और आख्या तक फैलाया गया प्रेरित ओके काम का यहां खंड पौलुस की\r\nदुसरी और तीसरी मिशनरी यात्राओं के ऊपर ध्यान केंद्रित करता है इस समय के दौरान पौलुस  पूर्व एशिया माइनर से होता हुआ यात्रा करता है जैसे कि उसने पहले किया था परंतु फिर वह ऐसे के पक्ष में एशिया माइनर के प्रांत की ओर बढ़ता है और एशियन सागर को पार करता हुआ मक्की दुनिया और वर्तमान समय के यूनान में आख्या के कई शहरों में आता है।\r\nपौलुस की दुसरी\r\n: मिशनरी यात्रा का प्रेरितों के काम 15:36-18:22 मैं वर्णन है और तीसरी मिशनरी यात्रा का 18:23-21:16 मे । उस नमूने से जिससे कि अब तक अच्छी तरह परिचित हो जाना चाहिए यह अध्याय अंतरिक विकास और तनाव के बीच के संबंध पर प्रकाश डालते हैं हम यहां पर आंतरिक विकास के कई उदाहरणों को पाते जैसा कि प्ररितो के काम 18 मैं अक्किला और प्रिसक्किला के द्वारा अपुल्लोस  को दी गई शिक्षा और प्रेरितों के काम 19 मैं पौलुस का इफिसुस  के यहूदी सभा घर में दी गई शिक्षा और तरसुस  की पाठशाला में दिए गए उपदेश।\r\n और निस्संदेह इसी आंतरिक विकास के साथ ज्यादा तनाव था उदाहरण के लिए पौलुस स्वर्ण वास नेवर उसके ऊपर बहस और प्रेरित ओके काम 15 में उससे अलग हो गए और प्रेरित ओके काम बीच में पोलूशन एक अलीशा को उसका ही अब वह से स्वयं को सुरक्षित रखने के लिए चेतावनी दी जिनके बारे में उद्देश्य थे।\r\n\r\nरोम :- \r\n\r\n अंत में लुक्का की कथा का अंतिम बड़ा खंड प्ररितो के काम 21:17-28:31 मेरो में सुसमाचार की गवाही पर केंद्रित है यहां खंड पौलुस की यात्रा को यरूशलेम से आरंभ करता हुआ और तब उसके बाद उसकी गिरफ्तारी करवा कारावास और रूम को भेजने जाने पर ध्यान केंद्रित करता है यह सामग्रियों मोटे तौर पर चार बड़े वर्गों में विभाजित है प्रेरितों के काम 21:17-23:11 मैं पौलुस की यरूशलेम में अंतिम गवाही 23:12-26:32 मैं पॉलिश का कारावास 27:1-28:14 मैं रूम के लिए उसकी कठिन यात्रा और अन्तत: 28:15-31 मैं रोम में उसकी गवाही।\r\n जैसा कि हम अपेक्षा करते आए हैं यह अध्ययन तरिक विकास योजनाओं के परिचय सामने को अपने में सम्मिलित करते हैं हम आंतरिक विकास के कई परमाणु को देखते हैं जिनमें ऐसी बातें सम्मिलित है जैसे कि प्रेरित ओके काम 21 में वह आनंद जिसको यहूदी विश वासियों ने यरूशलेम में अनुभव किया जब उन्होंने या सुना \r\n कि बहुत सारे अन्य जाति विश्वास में आ रहे हैं और प्रेरित ओके काम 22 में पॉलिश और अन्यों की दुख उठाने और यहां तक कि सुसमाचार के लिए मरने के लिए भी स्वच्छ है परंतु हम यहां भी देखते हैं कि इस आंतरिक विकास के साथ तनाव भी ज्यादा था जैसा कि प्रेरित ओके काम अध्याय 21 में एक बस अफवाह की पॉलिसी आदिवासियों को यहां शिक्षा दे रहा था कि वह अपनी परंपराओं को त्याग दें और इसी अध्याय 21 में इसके परिणाम स्वरूप व तनाव जिसे उसकी परिस्थितियों ने यह  की कलीसिया में उत्पन्न कर दिया हम ब्रह्मा विश्वास और विरोध के नमूने को पाते हैं लोका ने लिखा है कि कल ईशा ने इस अवधि के दौरान बाहरी विकास के उल्लेखनीय प्रगति के उदाहरण के लिए प्रेरित ओके काम 23,24,25,26,28 मे पौलुस  कई उच्च पद वाले अधिकारियों को समाचार बताने में सफल रहा था और प्रेरित ओके काम 28 में उसने रोम में बिना किसी रूकावट के सुसमाचार प्रचार का कार्य किया परंतु उल्लू का यह भी संकेत देता है कि इस विकास के साथ घोर विरोध भी आया जिनमें पौलुस का बंदी बनाया जाना और प्रेरित हो कि  24 में रोमी\r\n सरकार द्वारा 4 साल के लिए जेल में डाला जाना तथा प्रेरित ओके काम 28 में रूम की जेल में डाला जाना शामिल है।\r\n प्रेमी तो की काम की पुस्तक प्रत्येक मुख्य खंड यहां प्रमाणित करता है कि सुसमाचार की विश्वास क्योंकि गवाह सफल नहीं हुए पुत्र आत्मा निशु समाचार पूरी यरूशलेम से लेकर रोमी साम्राज्य की राजधानी तक ले जाने के लिए कल ईशा को सशक्त किया अंत किया एवं बाहरी परेशानियों के बावजूद जिन्हें कलिसीया सहन किया था रुक  सकने वाला सुसमाचार कलीसिया में आत्मिक परिपक्वता और संख्यात्मक विस्तार को लेकर आया जिसने परमेश्वर के राज्य को पृथ्वी की छोर तक ला दिया।', 9, '2020-10-23 04:13:41', '2020-10-27 17:02:36', NULL),
(2070, 578, 751, 'उत्तर = प्रेरितों के काम  की   की पुस्तक में पहली शताब्दी में जो परमेश्वर के दास लोगों ने प्रभु यीशु मसीह का सेवक आई किया उनके शव का इमेज रुकावटें और उनकी सेवक आई में जो परिस्थितियां और परेशानियां उन्होंने उठाया उन सारे बातों का वर्णन प्रेरितों के काम मे है  तो आज भी वह परिस्थितियां हमारी कल शाम में पाए जाते हैं आज के युग में भी कई परमेश्वर के दास लोग परमेश्वर की सेवा कार्य करने के लिए जब निकलते हैं तो इन सारे परिस्थितियों का सामना उन्हें करना पड़ता है परमेश्वर की सेवक आई करना आसान नहीं है परंतु परमेश्वर के नाम के लिए यीशु के नाम के लिए परिस्थिति दुख मुसीबत भोग विलास और इन सब चीजों को सामना करते हुए परमेश्वर के राज्य के लिए आगे बढ़ना है यही यीशु मसीह का से उठाई है यह सारी बातें हमें प्ररितो के काम  की पुस्तक की परिस्थितियां हमें सिखाती है और उसके साथ में हमारी परिस्थितियां सदस्य भी है इन दिनों में एक अलीशा और कल ईशा के लोगों को इन बातों पर ध्यान देना चाहिए कि जिस तरह प्रेरितों के काम  की पुस्तक में प्रेरितों  लोग प्रभु यीशु मसीह के लिए अपनी जान को भी जोखिम में डालते हुए उन्होंने बहुत सारे कष्ट उठाकर के प्रभु यीशु मसीह के सुसमाचार के लिए पीछे ना हट ले परंतु उसकी सुसमाचार को बड़े किया और हिम्मत के साथ में बढ़ते चले गए और उन्होंने उन लोग जो है सारे देश में फैलाते रहे इसी तरह से आज भी इन बातों को ध्यान में रखते हुए आशिक अलीशा को भी प्रभु यीशु मसीह के लिए दुख उठा करके उसकी सुसमाचार को खिलाना चाहिए इस प्रकार से हमें प्ररितो के काम  काम की पुस्तक को लागू करना चाहिए हमारे जीवन में शो इन दिनों में एक अलीशा का जिम्मेदारी है कि यीशु मसीह के राज्य को और यीशु मसीह के सुसमाचार को और भी जितना चाहे उतना फैलाना हमारा कर्तव्य है और कल ईशा का जिम्मेदारी भी है इन जिम्मेदारी को हमें विश्वास योग्यता से निभाना हमारे लिए जरूरी है|जिस तरह से पिछली शताब्दी में पहले शताब्दी में परमेश्वर के दास लोग परिस्थितियों में भी गांव के साथ में उस परिस्थितियों में पीछे ना हट थी वह परमेश्वर के राज्य को लेकर के आगे ही बढ़ता गया हमें उनके जीवन को सीकर के इन दिनों में हमें परमेश्वर के राज्य को लेकर आगे बढ़ना हमारा कर्तव्य है और जिम्मेदारी भी है लुका  लुका परमेश्वर के दास यह सारी बातें हमें इन दिनों में आज सिखाता है कि पहले शताब्दी में जिस तरह से लोगों ने प्रभु यीशु मसीह के सुसमाचार को बढ़ाया प्रभु यीशु के राज्य को बढ़ाया वैसे ही आज भी हमें उसके राज्य को बढ़ाना है|', 8, '2020-10-23 04:25:05', '2020-10-27 17:02:36', NULL),
(2071, 572, 866, 'It was once believed and taught that the Apostles \'creed was written in the first century by the twelve apostles themselves , it was even said that each apostles contributed one of the creed\'s twelve distinct theological statement .how ever there is virtually no evidence that this took place ,or even that any apostles were directly involved in the writing of the creed ,\r\nthe writing of the Christian there are many lists of essential doctrine that resemble the apostles creed .on the one hand there are rules of faith that catalog and explain fundamental beliefs in some details ,the writing of the early church fathers indicate that written rules of faith summarized the belief and practice of the churches produce them ,on the other hand some ancient doctrinal list are in the form of creeds.these were short lists that summarized the doctrinal portion\'s of the church rule\'s of faith especialy its most critical beliefs,these were often recited in liturgical setting , in the first and second century it may have been case that each local congregation had its own creed ,or way of summerizing essential biblical truth .', 8, '2020-10-24 01:16:13', '2020-10-27 18:24:57', NULL),
(2072, 572, 867, 'Now its reasonable to wonder why the church felt it was necessary to preserve its , the early church believed that the whole Bible was Christ\'s word ,given to believers by apostles ,in this regard they affirmed the concept that theologians often call sola scripture alone ,this is then perspective that the scripture is the only infallable truth of faith ,and the final arbiter in any theological contraversary , \r\n   according to Dr.pau;l chung  the apostles\'creed was especially valuable , even necessary in early church history because the canon of scripture was not formally listed untill around AD397, so , it was the authoritative faith of the church ,it was summurized in the apostls\' creed , but at the time we had bible ,so why should we continue to have creed ? because we cant require people to understand the whole bible befor we accept them as Christian . the apostles creed still summarize the essential teaching of the bible in simple way .and for this reason it must continue to be used even now.', 8, '2020-10-24 01:31:32', '2020-10-27 18:24:57', NULL),
(2073, 572, 868, 'Apostles\' creed is divided in to three major parts , each of which began with the statement \" i believe\" The first section speak of belief in God the Father , the second section about belief in Christ , our lord ,and the third section summarizes belief in the holy spirit ,and lits his active ministers , \r\nthe division of the creed according to the persons of God ,has been universally recognized by the church , this formula is Trinitarian , that is it based on the belief that there is only one God , and that this God exist in tree person, namely the persons of the father ,the son, and the Holy spirit ,\r\nThe apostles creed dose not specifically mentioned the word Trinity , or spell out its details, not every christian understand the full meaning of the worr Trinity , so we should pause to explain it, the trinity commonly stated this way \r\n  God has three person but only one essence .\r\nwith regard to father creed ascribe to him the attribute of being almighty , God has far more attributes that his infinite power and sovereignty  ,and in some important sence the creed description of the father dose\'t even distinguish christianity from other religian that might also express belief in sovergian ,creed much morensay about son, Jesus christ ,', 8, '2020-10-24 01:51:14', '2020-10-27 18:24:57', NULL),
(2074, 572, 869, 'We will focus on just two aspects of the church that were central to the article of faith in the apostels creed , one is participation , in the church and other we will consider preservation by the church , \r\nParticipation :when the creed says \" i believe in the holy spirit .........church\" it ephasize the important of participate in the church, even in the first century some profesing believers wanted to avoid the gatherd church as a place for worship, teaschinf and fellowship , but scripture teaches that the church is important and necessary  for christain , creed was used particulary inthe church and it was affirmed by those who came to baptism they came to be joined its numbers ,to be include in its gatherings , this is the model that creed puts forth for us to follow ,\r\nPreservation: from the earliest days the regular reaction , confection, amd memorization of the creed and confessions in the church served a very , very important role, espscally in sociteties  like the first century world and beyond in early christanity  were like literacy rates were very very low, the church is not infallable , apostles creed not encoraging us to believe whatever our local church teach ,mrather its simply affirming that the fact that Christ apointed his church in part to protect and to proclaim the gosplel and other truth .', 8, '2020-10-24 02:08:45', '2020-10-27 18:24:57', NULL),
(2075, 572, 870, 'Most are familiar with the idea that large building need solid foundation ,in similer way christian theology must be founded on true doctrines and principles if it is to honor God and be useful to his people ,just as Jesus is the corner stone of the church, his teachings are the cornerstone of the theology , and just as the apostles and prophets become the churh foundation by inruducing christ to the world the Apostles creed is faoundational to theology becaus us to the teaching of the apostles recorded in scripture,', 6, '2020-10-24 02:16:14', '2020-10-27 18:24:57', NULL),
(2076, 573, 871, 'We chritian believe that there is only one God our belife in God is really fundamentel to our our belife about everything else, God is at the center and everything else is as its because of its relation ,we will consider the basic idea of God as he is presented in scripture by looking at two subjects , often theologians call the singularity of God , the fact that he is the only God that exist , nothing that he is the only one God ,despite the fact that he has three person .we believe thatv the God of the bible isnthye one because many passage in the scripture assert God\'s singularity by explicity stating that three is only one God ,in Psalms 86:10 david sang to the l;ord , You alone are God , there is only one devine being , it was the true in old testament days , it was true in the new testament days , centuries of the church that still true today , \r\napostles creed dose not explicitly says that there is only one God , but on the hand the creed denies non-christian monothesm through other things that is says plenty about God , we belive there is only one God because scripture teach about only one true God.', 7, '2020-10-26 01:23:33', '2020-10-27 18:25:51', NULL),
(2077, 573, 872, 'you will recall that when we defined the doctrine of the Trinity in a prior lesson , we stand its this way :God has three person but only one essence ,we also said the term \'person\' refers to distinct , self -aware personality , and that the term \"essence \" refers to God\'s fundamental nature ,or the substance of which he consist , when we speak about simplicity , it is his essence that we have in mind , \r\n now , theologians use term like \'simple\' and \'simplicity \'in a rather technical ways ,we are not saying thyat God is simple in the sense thyat he is easy to understand ,insted we mean that his essence is not a composite of different substances but a unfied whole consisting of only one substance ,the doctin of trinity states that :God has three person but only one essence ,central of the doctrine of the trinity is the distinction between person and essence , God is one with respect to essence and three with respect to person, in fact we might say that with God , there is one \"what \" are three \"whos\".', 7, '2020-10-26 01:37:43', '2020-10-27 18:25:51', NULL),
(2078, 573, 873, 'The father\'s association with the son and the holy spirit may be described in a number of ways .but in the history of theology two particular perspectives on the trinity have came to the foreground , specifically it has been common to speak in terms of the Ontological Trinity and the Economic Trinity , both these approaches speak of the same trinity , the father , the son and the holy spirit , but they emphasize the different aspects of the relationship between three person of the God head , \r\n It has been common to speak of the ontological trinity when we are focusing on God\'s being , the word ontological means relating to being , so when we speak the ontological trinity we are looking at the trinity in terms of being or essence , we are considering how the three person of the trinity are integrated with one another , and how they share a single essence , \r\nfrom the perspective of ontology all three of God\'s person are infinite ,eternal and unchangeable ,and each has the same essence such as wisdom, power ,holiness, justice, goodness and true .\r\n  We normally says that we are speking of economic trinity when we consider how God\'s person interact with each other ,how thay relate to one another as individual prson, The word \'economic\' means relating to house hold management ,so when we speak of economic trinity we are discribing how the father son and the holy spirit relate to one another as distinct individual personalities .', 7, '2020-10-26 01:54:41', '2020-10-27 18:25:51', NULL),
(2079, 573, 874, 'The father of God has many aspect that we discus , but we will focus on three of scripture\'s more prominent ideas, Father\'s role as creator ,fatherhood interms of position as king over his creation, and people , and the family head over his people , \r\nCreator: scripture some times refers to God as being the father of everything he has created ,the bible was written in human language ,our human relationship to God as creator is often expressed in terms in terms of the relationship between a father and his children in the context , God\'s fatherhood represent our orgin and his authority ,\r\nKing : in the ancient near east , it was common for people to refer to human Kings as their fathers and for kings to refer to their people as their children , this language is often reflected nin the scripture as well, kings were portraying themselves as paternalistic , that is they were caring for their people , taking care of their needs , protecting them and those kinds of things ,the same way same time God revealed him self to Israel , he used the common way of kings as father ,\r\nFamily head :everyone is familiar with the concept of a family head ,usually it is a parent ,grandparent ,or other relative who leads and make decision for the family , scripture often describe relationship to his people in these way ,God as the head of the family of the human race .', 7, '2020-10-26 02:13:47', '2020-10-27 18:25:51', NULL),
(2080, 573, 875, 'God has ultimate matchless power over his creation ,There are many ways we might to say about the Fathers as the creator , his authority is absolute ,exclusive and exhastive.\r\nAbsolute : the father authority is absolute in the sense that he has the complite freedom to do whatever he wants with his creation , scripture often compare to his authority to a porter\'s authority over clay ,we find this description in place like isaiah 45:9,Jer18:1-10, Rom 9:18-24, \r\nExclusive :father has exclusive authority over everithing he has created , the father autnhority as creator is exclusive in sense that no creature possesses absolute authority , absolute authority only belongs to creator ,\r\nExhaustive : in adition to having absolute and exclusive authority , the father also has exhaustive authority  over the univers , when we say God\'s authority is exhaustive , we maen that it extends over everithing he has created ,in every detail,  everyone is under authority , there is no one or other created things that is free from the obligation to obey God .', 7, '2020-10-26 02:31:29', '2020-10-27 18:25:51', NULL),
(2081, 579, 927, 'The word \"trinity\" simply means \"tri-unity\"- three in one. So, the doctrine of the trinity can be defined in this way: God is three divine persons in one divine essence. When we talk about trinity- we means that there\'s only one God, not three. God reveals who God is in terms of Father, Son and Holy Spirit- the three persons- not three people but the three persons of the one God. So, we have the Father who sends the Son, the Son who, After His death and resurrection, goes to the Father and they send the Spirit. And so we come up with terms like \"essence\"- God\'s essence is one; his person is three. The Bible talks about God as Father, and so we talk about this person of Father. It talks about God as son. It talks about about God as Holy Spirit too. When we say that God is one divine essence, we\'re affirming that he is the one uncreated creator. According to Romans 1:25 there is one uncreated creator, and all other things in the universe are a part of God\'s created order. The doctrine of the Trinity is concerned with persons of the Trinity within the one divine essence, or Godhead.', 8, '2020-10-26 15:40:46', '2020-10-27 18:26:46', NULL),
(2082, 579, 928, 'When we speak of three divine persons, we\'re referring to the distinct persons of the Father, Son, and Holy Spirit. We can define the word \"person\" as \"a distinct, self- aware personality existing in relationship with other persons.\" God\'s personhood is what we should define ours. One thing that we can pretty substantially rule out is the modern concept of person as a distinct ego, an individual self  consciousness attached to separated body and a particular personal name that no others share. The Father isn\'t just conscious of the Father as a self, but is conscious of himself in relation to the Son and in relation to the Spirit, and so too, the Son is conscious of himself as the one begotten eternally by the Father speaking and so forth.', 8, '2020-10-26 15:53:49', '2020-10-27 18:26:46', NULL),
(2083, 579, 929, 'Tritheism violates the biblical doctrine of divine simplicity- that God is indivisibly one- but the doctrine of God\'s threeness does not. This can be difficult to grasp until we recognize that although God is three divine persons, he is only one divine essence. And his essence cannot be divided into parts. He is indivisibly one. God\'s simplicity is a very interesting notion because, on one hand, the Bible says that God is inconceivable. That is, a man cannot analyze him and sort him out. And on the other hand, theology contains the concept of God\'s \"simplicity.\" God has revealed himself as Trinity, but these three persons are one- they have one essence. That is, he cannot be broken down into what we\'d call \"parts.\" And God is one. So, in this sense, he is simple.', 8, '2020-10-26 16:02:55', '2020-10-27 18:26:46', NULL),
(2084, 579, 930, 'When we look back to the Old Testament, we see hints there of the existence of Christ and of the Holy Spirit. So, while some challenges have been raised to the eternity of the Son, of which Colossians is perhaps the classic text. We see there in Colossians 1:15-17..we see there Paul explaining how Jesus Christ is God\'s image. He speaks of Jesus here as the first born over all creation, as the first created being. So, Paul is establishing for them, \"we have one God and one Lord,\" and that Lord, Jesus. He is expecting the Corinthians to worship God the Father and God the Son, and that\'s how we can be confident that Jesus is part of creation as it happened, that Jesus is God, has always been God and that Paul, one of the earliest Christian authors, establishes the fact.', 8, '2020-10-26 16:13:24', '2020-10-27 18:26:46', NULL),
(2085, 579, 931, 'The scriptures are clear that Jesus Christ, the second person of the Trinity, is uncreated and eternal, just like God the Father. He is equal to the Father in power and glory, sharing equally in all the attributes of the Godhead. And the same thing is true of the Holy spirit as well. In fact, every Trinitarian formula found in Scripture mentions the Holy Spirit as an  equal member of the Trinity, together with the Father and the Son. The Trinitarian formulas of the New Testament help us to understand that the Holy Spirit is fully divine and fully personal. For example, In the Great commission Jesus commands us to baptize people in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit. And in Paul\'s benediction at the end of 2 Corinthians 13: \"The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, the love of God, and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit..\" again there\'s a blessing in the name of the triune God, grace extended through the sacrifice of the Son, motivated by the love of God and applied to us by the Holy Spirit.  So, we see the Spirit is fully divine, equal with the Father and the Son, and fully personal, no less than the Father and the Son.', 8, '2020-10-26 16:22:53', '2020-10-27 18:26:29', NULL),
(2086, 574, 876, 'The first things we should note about the language \"son of God\" is that scripture often uses it to talk about beimng that are not divine in any way , some tines its used for angels , the nation of Israel also called as the son\'s of God , Adam the first human being is also called son\'s of God , and sone pasasges of te bible reffers the all christian faithful believers as sons of God ,but if the little son of God dose not in and of itself mean that Jesus is divine , \r\nwhen we look at how the new testament talk about jesus , it become clear that he is God\'s son in unique way , in fact one of the most emphatic things that we find in the new testament is that Jesus is the unique son of God , thgat he shares in the very essence of who God is,jesus unique sonship is especially clear in the gospel of John, in John 5:18, jesus spoke of himself as son of God , he meant that he was equl with God the father ,christian have rightly understood that when bible say that Jesus is the son of God, it means that he is both unique and divine .throughout the new testament the son is subordinate to father\'s authority ,there is no conflict between  them ,', 8, '2020-10-27 01:14:18', '2020-10-27 18:27:12', NULL),
(2087, 574, 877, 'When the new testament calls Jesus Lord , it is translating the greek word kurios ,kurios was arather common word meaning ruler or master ,some times its used for human authority , at the same time , the new testament also used the word kurios as name for God, in Matt:11:25, as many other passages , \r\nThe key to Christian use of the word kurios is the old testament , the old testament scripture were written in the Hebrew , yet a couple centuries before Jesus was born, Hebrew text was translated into Greek, when Jewish scholars translated the old testament they used Greek term kurios 6700 times to translate sacred name by which God revealed him self to his people , one of the most amazing passage  in the new testament is where is talk about \"every knee will bow and every tongue will confess that Jesus Christ is the lord ,here Paul deliberately talking about the old testament passage and saying that instead of Jesus Christ is the Lord ,it is not to say every time people in the new testament called Jesus \"Lord\" they recognized his divinity ,but church formally confess that Jesus is Lord ,we are affirming the biblical teaching that Jesus Christ is God .', 8, '2020-10-27 01:30:34', '2020-10-27 18:27:12', NULL),
(2088, 574, 878, 'In the last couple of centuries , many theologians have readly accepted that jesus was human, but they have questioned his divinity , but the early centuries of the church , it was least as common for people to question the humanity of Jesus , to demonstrate that Jesus was a full huamn being , we will speak three broad features of his humanity , here we will discus only his human experience, \r\n Several of Jesus experience prove that he was truly human because only human beings have such experience , Jesus was convinced by the holy spirit , and born of the virgin mary , he suffered under Pontius Pilate , was crucified , died, and was buried, he descended in to hell , the third day he rose again from the death, this experience affirm atv least aspects of Jesus \'humanity \'his genaration, his body his soul, and his resurrections ,  Jesus miraculous conception dose is to ensure that he was fully divine as well as fully human, but it not make him less than fully human, it is true that conceptiojn is miracle ,perhaps one of the great mircle that redemptive history has ever known , and yet from the point of jesus conception forward , his gestation and devolopment in the womb is like any birthing prosses .', 8, '2020-10-27 01:46:28', '2020-10-27 18:27:12', NULL),
(2089, 574, 879, 'The English word\" Christ \"is a translation of the Greek word Christos, which in turn is a translation of the Old Testament Hebrew word Mashiach or messiah, meaning \'anointed one\' the days of the old testament , term \"anointed one \"was abroad term that could be applied to anyone who God appointed to serve him in a special capacity ,one of the most important uses of the term \'anointed one\' in the old testament applied to the descendants of David that served as kings over Israel and Judah , \r\naround the captive time of Israel and Judah many prophets foretold that God would send a great \"messiah\" or \"anointed one \" in the future , he wold be the great king , descended from David, who would restore and reunite the kingdoms of Israel  and Judah , \r\n  The new testament speak of jesus as the Christ over 500 places , it almost gose without saying that from a christian point of view , he is great Messiah that the old testament anticipated , there are two passages in John,s gospel where jesus is called messiah.John.1:41, and 4:25-26.', 8, '2020-10-27 02:02:07', '2020-10-27 18:27:12', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(2090, 574, 880, 'When we say that Jesus has a humane nature , we mean that he possesses all the attributes and traits are essential to being human , things like physical human body and a rational human soul, it is important for every Christian to understand at least the rudimentary aspects of Jesus human nature ,faithful Christian theology has consistently maintained that Jesus is fully human in every respect :he has body, and soul, he was subject to sickness ,injury and death, he has normal physicals limitations, and so on, But Jesus is different , he was born without sin, and lived a perfect sinless life , \r\nChrist humanity has many implication for the way we live as his followers , Jesus had two nature, two distinct nature , a human nature and divine nature , both these natures are entire and whole ,just as the nature of the father is entirely divine , and the nature of human being is entirely human , Jesus posses every atributes that is essential to divine  and every attributes that is essential to humanity , \r\nmore over Jesus two nature are distinct from each other , he dose not have a hybrid nature that combines both divine and human attributes.', 8, '2020-10-27 02:19:03', '2020-10-27 18:27:12', NULL),
(2091, 570, 886, 'The New Testament speaks many times of the church using the Greek word ekklesia.  it is used to identify the gathered nation of Israel. Deuteronomy 9:10\r\nThe Greek word ekklesia is commonly translated \"church\" which indicates that the assembly of Israel was the Old Testament equivalent and predecessor to the New Testament church.\r\n1 peter 2:9 Peter quoted from several old Testament passages that spoke of the nations of Israel and he applied Israel\'s special names to the old Testament church.\r\nI Romans 11, Paul used two metaphors to talk about the relationship between the Old Testament assembly of Israel and the Christian church. he spoke of them a st the batch of dough and the olive tree.\r\nPaul said that the Old Testament assembly was the first fruit of the same batch of the dough from which the New Testament church had been made.\r\nSecond Paul said that the Old Testament was the root of a tree and the New Testament church was the branch of the tree.', 8, '2020-10-27 17:43:04', '2020-10-30 02:39:39', NULL),
(2092, 570, 887, 'Jesus built his church in a way that  relied on but also advanced the Old Testament church.\r\nHe mentioned the church by the name ekklesia on three occasions Mathew 16:18, 18:17\r\nThe word oikodomeo translated here as build  can refer either to building something brand new or rebuilding that exists.\r\nIn Mathew 18:17, Jesus was talking about church discipline.\r\nIn the context of Jesus ministry, the only church that existed was Jewish synagogues.\r\nJesus called them church.\r\nIn the minds of Jesus and Matthew, like Paul, the church of New testament was a development of Israel\'s old Testament\'s assemblies.\r\nThe new Testament presents Jesus as the fulfillment of God\'s promise to Israel Romans 8:1-4\r\nJesus is the founder of the New Testament t church the ne who brought the restoration and renewal that transformed the failing Old testament church into the new testament church.', 8, '2020-10-27 17:56:31', '2020-10-30 02:39:40', NULL),
(2093, 570, 888, 'One important implication is that there is fundamental continuity between Israel in the old Testament and the Christian church in New Testament.\r\nPurpose:\r\nthe history of the world fall in to three stages. creation fall and redemption\r\nThe rest for history makes up the stage if redemption, in which God is working to restore humanity to perfect condition and through humanity to restore creation.\r\nThis redemption of humanity and creation has always been the purpose for God\'s church in both testaments.\r\nBelievers and unbelievers:\r\nRemember in Old Testament and new Testament both the believers are never perfect. in old Testament, some were faithful  and obedient but some rebelled.\r\n same ways in New Testament, there are always a mixture of unbelievers and believers in our churches\r\nObligations:\r\nThe people of God in both testaments were given the responsibility of loving God, spreading his kingdom throughout the world, and bring him in glory.\r\nDeuteronomy 6;5.6\r\nMathew 22:37', 8, '2020-10-27 18:11:41', '2020-10-30 02:39:40', NULL),
(2094, 570, 889, 'The word catholic means \"universal\" or including all Christians in all congregations .\r\nthe word catholic translates the Latin word catholicus, which in turn derives from the Greek word preposition kata nd the adjective holos which means whole or complete. it is a a description of the unity that exists between all churches that faithfully follow Christ.\r\nso, when the apostles creed speaks of the catholicity of the church it does not have in mind and organization of all Christian congregations. rather, it is talking about the unity of the holy spirit that exists between all legitimate Christian churches despite our organizational differences . it was meant to extend the name church to every Christian congregation.\r\n1Corinthians 1:2', 8, '2020-10-27 18:19:57', '2020-10-30 02:39:40', NULL),
(2095, 570, 890, 'we can define the visible catholic church as some world wide fellowship of all people in covenant with God under the headship of Christ. This fellowship is one of the Spirit rather that of church government\r\nthe three marks  to enable Christians to distinguish visible catholic church\r\n1. first mark is preaching the word of God\r\nGod has given the bible to the whole visible church and the holy Spirt to help us understand the whole Bible.\r\n2.The second mark is the right administration of the sacraments of baptism and Lord supper. it is the privilege and responsibility of every congregation within the visible church to  administrate the sacraments according to the church.\r\nMathew 28:19, 1 Corinthians 11\r\n3. The third mark of the visible catholic church is formal church discipline such as excommunication Matthew 13:24-30\r\ndiscipline is intended both to perfect the church and to drive the offended to repentance.', 8, '2020-10-27 18:34:07', '2020-10-30 02:39:40', NULL),
(2096, 575, 881, 'to explain the holy spirit\'s divinity we will look in two direction . on the one hand we will see the apostle creed affirms belief in the spirit\'s divinity and on the other hand biblical basic for creed\'s teaching ,\r\n The apostle\'s creed dose not explicitly state that the holy spirit is divine , but it implicitly affirms the spirit\'s divinity in at least two ways , first trinitarian structure equate the Holy spirit with the father and the son in important ways , second creed\'s description of jesus conception indicates that the holy spirit is divine , Structure: when we approach the creed form the perspective of the doctrine of God , we mentioned that the apostle creed acan be viewed as consisting on tree main section, each beginig with term i believe , in the third section summeriz belief in the holy spirit , and its active ministries .the creed was divided according the tree person of God,Jesus conseption : the apostle\'s creed saying jesus christ is son of God, was conceived by the Holy spirit , the statement dose not explicitly declare that holyb spirit is fully divin, but it strongly imlis this belif , holy sprit is equated to the power of the most high ,', 7, '2020-10-28 01:18:14', '2020-11-05 18:14:43', NULL),
(2097, 575, 882, 'There is great value of recognizing that the faith we affirm today has been consistently affrimed throghout the century , we have to understand the apostl\'s creed teaching about the divinty of the holy spirit , even so our greatest confidence is drawn from scripture , the biblical basis for believing in the divinity of the holy spirit can be demonstrated in many ways , his names, attributes,the works and performance , and the trinitarian formulas that refers to him, \r\nNames ,:the holy spirit is called by a host of names in the bible , some of these name suggest his divinity in  a very implicit manner , other are very explicit manner in calling him divin, and still mothers fall on a continuum between these two extremes , the name that implis his divinity the most implicit ways is the name \"holy spirit \" thenterm holy can be used aspects of creation that are not divine in any ways , the word holy genarally refers to things that are distinct from their common conterparts  because they are special to God in some way, the word \"holy \"dose not by it self indicate that the holy spirit is divine,  with this very implicit names in mind lets lookmat some names that indicate the holy spirit\'s divine in the ways that lies between very implicit , these names includes : the spirit of the lord\" \"the spirit of god\" the spirit of living God\" alos the spirit of Jesus, the spirit of the father , \r\nand another thing is atributtes of the holy spirit is assuring the divinity of the holy spirit ,his communicable attributes and incommunicable atributes .', 7, '2020-10-28 01:36:35', '2020-11-05 18:14:43', NULL),
(2098, 575, 883, 'when speak of the personal attributes of the Holy spirit , we have in mind those qualities he possess that are unique to person , things that can be true about him  if he\'s real person and not simply an impersonal force , the holy has far too many personal attributes for us to catalog them all in this lesson , here we will talks about four examples to demonstrate his personhood , Holy spirit has a will, this is the faculty he uses to plan to desire and to choose , clearly any being that can do these things cannot be a mere force power ,the Holy spirit wants certain people to have certain gifts and other to have other gifts , impersonal forces do not have plans and desires , only person do , the holy spirit must be a person, \r\n The holy spirit also have the attributes of the intelligence , through wich he possesses knowledge and the ability to teach others , he express this intelligence in many ways , such as searching and kwnoing the mind of God , he also gives wisdom and knwoledge , and he teaches , \r\n The holy spirit also have the emotions ,internal feelings and affections that he express in response to others person and events , like his other personal attributes his emotion prove that he is a person, and simply a power , More over the spirit posses what we migt call the attribute of agency , he has a will , the ability to intent things and act on his own accord , and this enabe him to perorfm many action that can only be done by person .', 7, '2020-10-28 01:54:19', '2020-11-05 18:14:43', NULL),
(2099, 575, 884, 'We should being by admiting that there several passage inthe bible where the distinction between the spirit and the other person of the trinity is not entirely clear , holy spirit is identified as the Spirit of God\'s son in Gala 4:6, the spirit of the father in matt 10:20,and he has the several names that highlight the relational connection between the members of the Trinity , rather that their distinctiveness , Three person of the Trinity are only one God , its make perfect sense to think of the holy spirit as the spirit of the father and the son, and the same time insist that he is an entirely distinct person from them, one way to highlight the distinction between the spirit and the other person of the Trinity is to look at passages in the scripture that shown them to intracting with one another in ways that emphasize their differants , \r\nJesus said holy spirit wold not come unless the son first wen away ,John 16:7, clearly the distinguished himself from the spirit by saying that one gose before the other come , each one hand and appointed role , and the role of the spirit would not began until the son had completed his earthly work and ascended in to heaven.\r\nin the same way spirit also dose things that distinguish him from the father , as part of his role as our counselor , the nHoly spirit is our defense attorney , asssisting our prayers by pleading our case befor God.', 8, '2020-10-28 02:11:33', '2020-11-05 18:14:43', NULL),
(2100, 580, 670, 'From biblical theology, we can benefit from reading the early parts of the Bible without knowing how it ends. But if we do not also study the ending of the Bible, the New Testament. The Old Testament raises questions, and hopes, but the answers, resolutions, and fulfillment appear at the end of the scriptures, in the New Testament.  \r\nChristians have tended to follow three main strategies toward exegesis, or interpretation, of Scripture: literature analysis, looking at the Bible as a literary portrait designed to emphasize certain theological perspective;  thematic analysis, looking at the Bible as a minor that reflects our traditional and contemporary interests and questions;  One of the best ways to get at the heart of New Testament biblical theology is to compare and contrast it with what we have learned about biblical theology of the Old Testament.', 7, '2020-10-28 02:13:39', '2020-11-05 18:14:14', NULL),
(2101, 575, 885, 'The relationship between the person of the trinity  have traditionally been described from two different perspectives, theologians have spoken of the onthological Trinity , and the economic Trinity, both of thse perspective on the same Trinity , the father , the son, and the holy spirit , but they emhasize different aspects of the relationships between these three divine person, in christian theology in both ontological trinity and the economic trinity the holy spirit called the third person, he is the third person of the ontological trinity because he is breathed out by the Father who is firt person, and by the son, who is second person, \r\nwith regard to economic trinity the holy spirit is said to be the thierd person because he holds the third rank, being subordinate both to the father and to the son, the scripture indicates his subordination in a number of ways , he is to send given by the father and the son, \r\nof course we say the holy spirit holds the lowest rank from the perspective of the economic trinity , it is important to emphasize that he is till fully God, and he has absolute sovereign authority over every aspect of creation, .', 7, '2020-10-28 02:25:09', '2020-11-05 18:14:43', NULL),
(2102, 580, 671, 'Diachronic development is the way theological structures grew or developed over time. Diachronic development explores how epochal developments took place between major historical periods or epochs. We always come to the scriptures with all kinds of information and ideas and feelings and things that are already priming us, as it were, preparing us for jumping in. And so what a person does come with a lot of synchronic and diachronic background already, having looked at the Bible either formally or informally, either in their younger age or in their later age. So we can look at Bible synchronically, or diachronically. Synchronic or diachronic analysis has no priority over each other.  For example, in Romans 5, a synchronic assessment of Jesus.', 7, '2020-10-28 02:33:31', '2020-11-05 18:14:14', NULL),
(2103, 580, 672, 'One of the best ways to get at the heart of the New Testament biblical theology is to compare and contrast it with what we have learned in the biblical theology of the Old Testament. Old Testament biblical theology and New Testament biblical theology have a mutual interest in God\'s two-fold revelation.  Biblical theologians have pointed out that the New Testament contains all three kinds of word revelation as well. The Gospels report how God spoke through the words of Jesus to reflect on Jesus\' earlier actions. They also report times when  Jesus\'s teaching explained his simultaneous actions, as well as times when Jesus predicted future actions.  The same can be said of authors and characters in the books of Acts and Revelation as well as the New Testament epistles.', 7, '2020-10-28 02:42:56', '2020-11-05 18:14:14', NULL),
(2104, 580, 673, 'Christian eschatology is a major branch of study within Christian theology deals with last things such as eschatology. Broadly speaking, Christian eschatology focuses on the ultimate destiny of the individual souls and of the entire created order based primarily upon biblical texts within the Old and New Testaments.  Preterism, Historicism, Futurism, and Idealism are some of the main approaches that arise from the study of Christianity\'s most central eschatological document, the Book of Revelation, but the principles embodied in them can be applied to all prophecy in the Bible. The alternative method of prophetic interpretation, futurism, and preterism which came from Jesuit writings, was brought about to oppose the Historicism interpretation which had been used from Biblical times.', 7, '2020-10-28 02:57:47', '2020-11-05 18:14:14', NULL),
(2105, 580, 674, 'The direct and dramatic acts of God in the gospel renew the image of God in us by resurrecting us in the image of Christ. No aspect of our personhood, including our personality, is left unscathed. Through faith, our whole being dies and rises with Christ, including those unique qualities and characteristics that make us. As we rise with Christ, even our personalities are redeemed and regenerated and renewed and reformatted. How obvious this renewal depends on how blatantly and observable our personalities have been hijacked by sin. Either way, our personalities are then yielded to the Holy Spirits as we seek to obey our Lord and Master with all our heart, soul, mind, and strength.', 7, '2020-10-28 03:07:59', '2020-11-05 18:14:14', NULL),
(2106, 576, 886, 'The concept of the church in the new testament  actually finds its roots in the Old Testament ,many would think that the church started in the day of Pentecost, when Jesus went up to heaven,and he poured his spirit on the disciple ,this is a misunderstanding of the nature of the church , The new testament speaks many times of the church using the Greek word ecclesia, but this term was derived from the Septuagint ,the Greek translation of the Old testament ,in the old testament ekklesia , and its hebrew counterpart is frequently used to identify the gatherd nation of Israel, we see this in Deuteronomy 9:10,31:30,\r\nEven in the new testament where ekklesia has become technical term reffering to the church the word is still used to reffer to the assembly of old testament Israel, the greek word translated assembly is ekklesia, wich is more commonly translated \"Church\" this indicate the assmbly of Israel was the old testament equivalent and predecessor to the new testament church, \r\nof course this is not to say that the new testament church is precisely the same as Israel\'s old testament assemblies , they are connected , but they are different as well .', 8, '2020-10-29 01:15:53', '2020-11-05 18:11:06', NULL),
(2107, 576, 887, 'There can be no denying that when Jesus came , his earthly ministry had a dramatic impact on the world and on the people of God , it is with good reason that many theologians have noted that jesus did note simply perpetuate the old order , including his old Church ,Jesus only mentioned the church by the name ekklesia on three occasion recorded in the gospel .in fact these are the only times the word ekklesia appears anywhere in Matt .Mark , Luke or john , all these tree passages are in the gospel mof Mathew 16:18, \"i will build my church, \" The word oikodomeo \'translated here as \"build\" can refer either to build somthing brand new , or to rebuild and restoring what already exist , in the orginal context of jesus ministry , the only church that existed was jewish synazgogues scatterd throughout the region and the temple in jerusalem , these were distictivly old testament forms of Israel\'sassemblies ,but jesus called them \'church\' \r\nas we look at the continuity between the old testament and new testament churches ,it is important to recognize the central role that jesus plays in tying these two churches together.the old testament church relationship to jesus is at its essence at the heart the same as the new testament church\'s relationship to jesus christ,', 8, '2020-10-29 01:33:28', '2020-11-05 18:11:06', NULL),
(2108, 576, 888, 'when we realize that jesus ordained the new testament church as the restorationnand the development of the old testament Israel , one important implication is that there is fundamental continuity between the israel in the old testament and the church in the new testament , on a practical levels we should expect the community of God\'s people in the new testament  to reflect its old testament roots, some things are different , and the new testament takes care to point out thses changes , but the new testament also teaches that the church is very much like israel, \r\nthere are too many points of continuity for us to mention them all, but it is worth taking the time to list tree of them explicitly, first ,there is great contuinuity of purpose between old testment church and new testament church, :theologians often summurize the history of the world terms of tree stage , Creation, fall, and redemption, in the stage of creation wich is described in Gen 1-2,God created evrithing, and in one special part of the world , he formed the garden of Eden, second inthe stage of fall, which is recorded in Gen:3, humanity rebelled against to God, the rest of the historuy makes up the stage of redemption , \r\nBelievers and unbelievers : the old testament church was never perfect , most of them rebelied aganest to God in unbelieve and fell under his divine curse .the same way the there are always unblivers mixed among the believers in our church, .', 8, '2020-10-29 01:51:37', '2020-11-05 18:11:06', NULL),
(2109, 576, 889, 'Our discussion of the term catholic will divide into three parts , definition of the word \'catholic\' , catholicity of the visible church, and catholicity of invisible church, \r\nThe word catholic means universal , including all Cristian in all congregation , the word \"catholic\" translate the Latin word catholicus , which in turn derives from Greek preposition \'kata\' and the adjective \'whole \' or complete , as we know the apstle creed we have today developed from early baptismal creed , at the time these early creed were written the various christian churches around the world had not yet come together under a single overarching church government , so when apostle\'s creed talking about the catholicity its dose not having in mind an organization of all christian congregation , rather its talking about the unity of the holy spirit that exist between all legitimate christian churches , \r\nwhen we combin our understanding of catholicity with our understanding of the visible church , we can define the visible catholic church as :one world wide fellowship of all people in covenant with God under the headship of christ, obviously thgis fellowship is one of spirit rather than of church goverment , when we comine our understanding of catholicity with our understanding of in visible church , we can define the invisible ctholic church as: all people from all ages who have been united to Christ for salvation.', 8, '2020-10-29 02:09:46', '2020-11-05 18:11:06', NULL),
(2110, 576, 890, 'When we combine our understanding of catholicity with our understanding of the visible church , we can define the visible catholic church as : one world wide fellowship of all people in covenant with God under the headship  of christ , obviously this fellowship is one of spirit rather than of church government , ther is no single denomination whose government extend over all christian congregation , rather unity of the visible Christian church is based on the fact that the church is in covenant with the same God and under the covenant headship of the same christ ,\r\nhistoricaly the visible church has traced its catholicity in a variety of ways , in some tadition it is traced through church government , the church expand as it is multiples its self, \r\nbut generally protestant have emphasized that the unity of the entier church rest in our faith in Christ and the work of the spirit, rather than in the succession of ordained ministers and priest , for this reason new congregations can arise where unoty of ministares and priests , \r\nthe marks of the church are still important for us to consider todays, they help us to ensure that our own congregation remain within the bounderies of the visible catholic church in covenant with under the headship of Christ .', 8, '2020-10-29 02:25:36', '2020-11-05 18:11:06', NULL),
(2111, 581, 932, 'The doctrine of the Trinity teaches that there is one God- one divine essence- and all three members of the Trinity are equally and fully God. However, this biblical truth is not fully and explicitly revealed in the Old Testament. Instead, much of the Christian doctrine of the Trinity comes from the New Testament. Old Testament is incomplete revelation. God didn\'t reveal himself all at once. Now we are speaking of the third person of the Triune God that we come to know more fully in light of New Testament revelation, but just as much about God when we speak of him as the spirit of God in the Old Testament, as it is more revealed in New Testament passages like Matthew 28, Ephesians 4:1-6 & 2 Corinthians 13- where it is brought together in a clear way. New Testament is especially unfolding who is our Savior as the eternal Son of God but that\'s also true of the Holy Spirit as we see more a distinction of the Spirit in the New Testament.', 8, '2020-10-29 15:46:33', '2020-10-30 02:40:10', NULL),
(2112, 581, 933, 'Revelation chapters 1 and 4 say that the one who sits on the throne is God the Father. And John 1 tells us that the Lamb is the Word of God who became flesh- Jesus Christ, the son of God. Both these passages clearly teach Jesus\' uncreated divinity. In Revelation 5, John used the imagery of both a lamb and a lion to describe Jesus. In Revelation 5, John is weeping because no one is worthy to open the scroll and he knows the scroll holds the secret to God\'s future. An angel announces that there is one who is worthy, Lion of the tribe of Judah, which is a symbol of royalty. Instead he sees a lamb, symbol of sacrifice, symbol of suffering. And there\'s a beautiful picture of Jesus who is the conquering King, he is the Messiah, who accomplishes salvation by suffering and dying as the sacrificial Lamb. So, the Lion who is the Lamb is the beautiful picture of who Jesus Christ is as Lord, as sovereign as King. So, a powerful picture of who Jesus is and how he accomplished our salvation. Revelation 5 places Jesus in the category of divine. He isn\'t one of God\'s creatures. Instead he\'s equal with God. And as God\'s divine Son, he will conquer all his and our enemies when he returns.', 8, '2020-10-29 16:01:51', '2020-10-30 02:40:10', NULL),
(2113, 581, 934, 'The first chapter of John, and the first verse in particular, has been used throughout the history of the church as proof that Jesus is God the Son, the second person of the Trinity. He is God and has been with God since the beginning. He\'s also involved in the creation of all things. And because he\'s involved in the creation of all things, he himself must be uncreated. He is the eternal and uncreated Creator. \"What God was, the word was.\" in essence, what the Greek is doing is it\'s saying that in terms of his essence, in terms of what he is, the word is identical to God, and in the last few words of John 1:1, \"and the word was God\", say in the most concise way possible that the second person of the Trinity is equal in authority, in worship, in attributes as the first person of the Trinity, and yet they are not the same person. John 1:1 is a verse that affirms the deity of Christ. He is fully God himself, that he is a divine associate and he is fully God himself.', 8, '2020-10-29 16:12:09', '2020-10-30 02:40:10', NULL),
(2114, 581, 935, 'Searching and knowing is an attribute of a distinct, self aware personality who is in a loving relationship with other self aware personalities. This necessarily implies that the Spirit of God is a person, distinct from the person of God. If the Spirit of God were simply God\'s impersonal attribute or his impersonal force in action. In John 14-16, we read about Spirit doing things that only a person would do. He will advocate like Jesus, and the Spirit goes on to prosecute the world concerning sin and righteousness and judgement, just like Jesus did. The Spirit is like a witness just like we are witness. Jesus tells us what the Holy Spirit does..He teaches us, reveals all truth, guides us, comforts us, leads us and further we see the Holy spirit has emotions. He is grieved. Like Paul in Ephesians says that Don not quench the Spirit in 1 Thessalonians. So, the Spirit is identified as a distinct person.', 9, '2020-10-29 16:28:09', '2020-10-30 02:40:10', NULL),
(2115, 581, 936, 'Scripture teaches that Jesus is the true and living God. Both Paul and John understood this. But one of the great mysteries of the Trinity is that Jesus is not only fully God, he is also fully human. And it is through his humanity- through his life, death and resurrection- that we are saved. And because the human Jesus is also the eternal God, equal in power and glory to the Father, we can trust that he is worthy and able to redeem us from our sins. Jesus has to a man is that he has to represent us. He must be tempted in every point like as we are. He must be the second man, the last Adam, but he must also be God, because only God can forgive sin, because God is the one who has been sinned against in Adam. in 2 Corinthians 5 it talks about how God was reconciling the world to himself in Christ, as Christ becomes the perfect substitute for us. Because he is fully human yet without sin, he can be our complete substitute. Therefore the Scriptures are clear that Jesus is both God and man. He\'s the second person of the Trinity, God the Son. And Jesus is God, we can freely worship him and adore him for all his glory, power and goodness that he bestows on us every day.', 9, '2020-10-29 16:38:30', '2020-10-30 02:40:10', NULL),
(2116, 577, 891, 'Christian who believe in the bible recognize that one of the main reason Jesus died was to solve the problem created by sin ,Sin separates us from God\'s blessing and place us under his cures ,and there is no way thate we can over com this problem by ourselves .this is what we mean when we talk about the problem of sin, sin condemns us and apart from christ we have no way to save our selves from its presents or its consequense ,\r\nmostv of us familier with events record in Gen 3, the account of whe n our first perents Adam and Eve rebelled against God by eating the forbidden fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, from a biblical point of view this act was not an isolated event , it caused the entier human race to become guilty of sin, and to be corrupted by the sin, Theologians commeonly refers to this event as humanity\'s fall  into sin, or simply the fall ,\r\nscripture indicates after the Adem and Eve sinned ,god judged and cursed entire human race ,this curse efected every aspects of their beings ,its immediately resulted thge spiritual death that spoken of throughout the scripture , it is also produse the curruption in our beings , both body and soul.and it ultimately lead us to physical death, Finnaly sin earned humanity suffering under God\'s judgment in hell, .', 8, '2020-10-30 01:18:12', '2020-11-05 18:10:39', NULL),
(2117, 577, 892, 'In his mercy God was not willing to let entire humanity to remaining under the curse of the sin, he still planed for the humanity to fill and rule over the earth, and turn it to the kingdom worthy of his presents , so he send a redeemer to solve the problem of sin, and the redeemer was his son, Jesus Christ .\r\n    as a work of divine grace , forgiveness involves all three person of trinity , the father , the son, and the holy spirit , \r\n   Forgiveness being with the father because he was one that planned , the new testament explicitly teach us that the father sent the son in to the world and appointed him as the redeemer , the new testament also teaches that the father authorized the Jesus\'s empowerment as the redeemer of his people , as promised to accept Jesus sacrifice on the cross as payment of sin,\r\n  The divine grace that accomplished our forgiveness also involved the son, whom is our redeemer ,the fulfilment of the father promise , the son was sent into the world , become incarnate as Jesus as long awaited messiah , in order to atone for human sin, Jesus atoned for sin by dying on the cross in place of sinners , he received the divine curs that had been warrened by our sin, and his perfect righteousness was credited to our account , so that we would be continued not as sinners , but as obedient children of God.\r\n   The holy spirit is the person of trinity who actully applies the forgivness to our lives , the father laid the plans the son accomlished the atonement ,but our sins are not forgiven until the holy spirit dose his work,.', 7, '2020-10-30 01:35:59', '2020-11-05 18:10:39', NULL),
(2118, 577, 893, 'Scripture clearly taches us that God dose not forgive the sin of every person, some people are forgiven ad some are not, from the human perspective the reason is that the porous of forgiveness ordinarily involves and element of individual responsibility , generally spiking those people that fulfill these responsibilities are forgiven but those that shirk these responsibilities are not, \r\nscripture speak abut the two conditions for the forgiveness , in scripture faith is multifaceted concept but this context when we speak of faith in God , we have in mend, acknowledgement of God\'s divine sovereignty loyal submission to him, and trust that he will show us mercy for sake of our redeemer Jesus Christ, \r\nsome times Christian fall into distinguish between a means of grace and a basis of grace , as result they mistakenly think that means of grace can be used to earn grace ,or even to force God to be gracious to us , so its important to distinguish clearly between a means and a basis ,we might summarize these different by saying that a basis is the ground or merit on which an action or consequents is based , where as means is a tool or mechanism for bringing that action or consequence to pass .', 7, '2020-10-30 01:53:24', '2020-11-05 18:10:39', NULL),
(2119, 577, 894, 'God created human beings to consist of physical bodies and non physical souls , some traditions have maintained that each human beings also possesses a spirit in addition to a soul, before our fall into sin our bodies and our souls were unaffected by sin and its carpeting powers, but when Adam and eve fell into sin, sin corrected not only their souls but also their body , and this correction of their bodies ultimately resulted in their physical death , when Adam and Eve sinned against God he cursed them both , and the part of his cursed was that they would be mortal, they would eventually die and return to dust , because all human being descend from Adam and eve ,\r\nsin affected Adam and Eve in both spiritual and physicals ways ,just like adam and eve our bodies are also corrupted by sin, this corruption result in physical hardship, sickness and eventually death , in some sense physical death is a blessing to believers because we are taken directly into the presents of Christ , but in a more fundamental sense physical death is tragic .it\'s a universal humane experience , but its also horribly unnatural , God did not humanity for death, he created us for life , and our salvation wont we complete until Christ return and redeems our bodies .', 7, '2020-10-30 02:11:37', '2020-11-05 18:10:39', NULL),
(2120, 577, 895, 'We will consider the redemption our bodies in three stage , first the things believers experiencing during our present life on earth, :Christians normally talk abut the redemption of our bodies in terms of our resurrections on the last days , the bible actually teach us the salvation of our body being with the indwelling of the holy spirit when we first come to faith, and our bodies continue to benefits from the holy spirit indwelling presents throughout our lives , especially through the process of sanctification , the sanctification of our body is similar to the sanctification of our souls , the holy spirit set apart for God and purifies us , \r\nsecondly :intermediate state of our body , after the beginning of the redemption of our bodies in the present life of the believers the process continues during our physical death, when we die our bodies are temporarily separated from our souls, this stage often called the intermediate state ,the state between our lives on the earth now , and lives we ll have in the resurrection, during the intermediate state our soul indwelling with Christ in heaven, \r\nand another thing is new lifeform bodies will receive new , perfect life when they are restored to life in the general resurrections ,', 8, '2020-10-30 02:28:20', '2020-11-05 18:10:39', NULL),
(2121, 583, 752, 'उत्तर = प्ररितो के काम  की पुस्तक पवित्र आत्मा के ऊपर गहरे धर्म विज्ञान को प्रस्तुत करती है यहां उसे एक ऐसे व्यक्ति के रूप में वर्णित करती है जो कि कल ईशा को परिवर्तित जीवन यापन करने और संसार में सुसमाचार प्रचार करने के लिए सशक्त करता है यहां वर्णित करती है कि उसने प्ररितो और आरंभ कि कल ईशा के अन्य अंगों के सेवक आई को मान्यता देने के लिए कई चिन्ह और आश्चर्य कर्म का प्रदर्शन किया यह गवाही देती है कि उसने मसीह को उत्साह से भर दिया जो कि विरोध और सताओं का सामना कर रहे थे संक्षेप में प्रेरित के काम  की पुस्तक यहां विवरण देती है कि पवित्र आत्मा वह है जो कि सुसमाचार और राज्य के फैलाओ के लिए योग्य बनाने की सामर्थ्य देता है और लोगों को धर्मी जीवन यापन करने के लिए सशक्त करता है पवित्र आत्मा प्ररितो के काम  की पुस्तक को मैं विभिन्न तरीकों से कार्य किया हम अपने ध्यान को कलीसिया पर उसके प्रभाव को तीन स्थानों में देखने के द्वारा केंद्रित करेंगे सबसे पहले हम पवित्र आत्मा को पेन्तेकुस्त  के दिन से पहले देखेंगे दूसरा हम पेन्तेकुस्त  के दिन यरूशलेम में आत्मा के उड़ेल जाने की जांच करेंगे और तीसरा हम पेन्तेकुस्त  के बाद आत्मा के कार्य की खोज में करेंगे आइए सबसे पहले हम प्रेरितों के काम  की पुस्तक को देखेंगे जो की आत्मा को पेन्तेकुस्त  से पहले का विवरण देती है।\r\n\r\n\r\nपेन्तेकुस्त से पहले :-\r\n\r\n\r\nप्ररितो के काम 1:3-11 लूका ने यहां वर्णित किया है कि यीशु ने उसके पुनरुत्थान और स्वर्गारोहण  के मध्य 40 दिनों का समय प्ररितो  कोशिश यता देने में व्यतीत किया और जैसा कि हम प्रेरितों के काम 1:3 मैं पढ़ते हैं जैसा कि हम देखेंगे कि यीशु की राज्य के बारे में स्वच्छता का एक महत्वपूर्ण तत्व यह था कि पवित्र आत्मा एक विशेष तरीके से प्रेरितों  के ऊपर शीघ्र आ जाएगा।\r\nपेन्तेकुस्त  से पहले पहुंच आत्मा के बारे में हम यीशु की शिष्य ताऊ को दो पहलुओं को छोड़ेंगे पहला हम पवित्र आत्मा के आगमन के समय को देखेंगे और दूसरा हम उसके आगमन के उद्देश्य के ऊपर ध्यान केंद्रित करेंगे आइए सबसे पहले यीशु की पवित्र आत्मा के आंगन आगमन के बारे में दिए गए शिष्यता  के ऊपर ध्यान दें।\r\n\r\n\r\nसमय :-\r\n\r\n\r\nप्ररितो के काम 1:4-8 मैं दिए गए यीशु के शब्दो को :\r\n ध्यान दें कि जब यीशु ने आत्मा के आने वाले 32 माह की घोषणा की तो प्रेरितों  नहीं यहां पूछा कि क्या यीशु इसराइल के राज्य को पुनः स्थापित करने वाला था इस्राएल के राज्य की स्थापना की अस्तित्व से कई आधुनिक पाठकों के लिए अपरिचित है इसलिए हमें इसे समझने के लिए थोड़ा रुकना चाहिए।\r\n पुराने नियम के भविष्य दुख अदाओं ने यहां भविष्यवाणी की थी कि क्योंकि इसराइल और यहूदा के पास इतने ज्यादा थे जिसके परिणाम स्वरूप परमेश्वर उन्हें प्रतिज्ञा की हुई भूमि से निर्वासित कर देगा और उन्हें विदेशी शासकों के अत्याचार के आधीन कर देगा पुराने नियम की भविष्यवाणियों के ऊपर आधारित होकर यहूदियों ने यहां विश्वास किया कि परमेश्वर बाद में उनके पापों को क्षमा करते हुए मसीह को उसके लोगों को पुनः स्थापित करने के लिए उन्हें वापस उनकी भूमि पर ले जाने के लिए और उनके ऊपर राज्य करने के लिए भेजेगा दाऊद का वंश होने के नाते मसीह इसराइल और यहूदा के ऊपर राज्य बन कर आएगा और इस पृथ्वी पर परमेश्वर के राज्य को प्रतिज्ञा की हुई भूमि में केंद्रित करते हुए परिवर्तित कर देगा जहां पर लोग अनंत काल और आशीष जीवन का आनंद मनाएंगे पहली शताब्दी तक इसराइल ने सैकड़ों वर्षो तक न्याय का सामना किया और बड़ी लालसा से इस्राएल के राज्य की पुनः स्थापना के लिए एक राजनीतिक मसीह के लिए आने की प्रतिज्ञा किए इसलिए जब हम प्रेरितों  नहीं यहां सुना कि यीशु स्वर्ग में रोहित होने वाला था तो उन्होंने यहां आशा की कि वहां पुराने नियम की भविष्यवाणी को जाने से पहले पूरा करेगा इसलिए ही उन्होंने उसे इसराइल की पुनः स्थापना के बारे में पूछा परंतु फिर भी यीशु ने यहां से शताब्दी की अचानक से होने वाली इस्राएल की राजनीतिक पुणे स्थापना की प्रसिद्ध प्रतीक्षा गुमराह करने वाली थी और पुराने नियम की भविष्यवाणी का पूरा किया जाना पूरे संसार में सुसमाचार के फैलाव और मसीह के महिमा में भरे हुए पुनः आगमन के द्वारा होगा।\r\nपरन्तु फिर क्या प्ररितो  यीशु के द्वारा पवित्र आत्मा के बपतिस्मा में के प्रति कहे गए वाक्यों को प्रतिउत्तर में राज्य की पुनर्स्थापना के बारे में पूछा ठीक है एक बार फिर से प्रेरितों  पुराने नियम की भविष्यवाणी के बारे में सोच रहे थे पुराने नियम के कई संदर्भों में यहां भविष्यवाणी की गई है कि जब न्याय पूरा हो जाएगा तो परमेश्वर अपनी आत्मा को स्थिति से उड़े लेगा जैसा कि पहले कभी नहीं उड़ेला गया है।\r\nयशायाह 44:3-4\r\n यहां पर यशायाह  ने पुनः स्थापना की बात यह कहते हुए कही है कि परमेश्वर उसके आत्मा को भूमि के ऊपर उड़ेलेगा।\r\n पुराने नियम की भाषाओं ने यह घोषणा की थी कि मसीहा के आगमन से पहले इसराइल जिसे शास्त्रों ने पांच और भ्रष्टाचार और मौत का युग कहां है मैं जीवन यापन करेगा और उन्हें यहां घोषणा की कि जब मसीहा आएगा तो वहां एक नया युग का शुरुआत करेगा जिससे शास्त्रियों ने आने वाला यू कहां ऐसा युग जिसमें परमेश्वर के शत्रुओं का न्याय होगा और उसके लोग अनंत और अपरिवर्तनीय तरीके से ध्यान करेंगे पुराने नियम के बहुत दुख अदाओं ने कभी भी सुनिश्चित नहीं बताया कि यहां प्रतिक्रिया कितना समय लेगी परंतु ज्यादातर शास्त्रियों ने यहां आशा की कि यहां अचानक से हो जाएगी।\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nउद्देश्य :-\r\n\r\n\r\n एक बार फिर से यीशु के प्रेरितो को प्रेरितों के काम 1:8 मैं कहे हुए शब्दों को सुनिए:\r\n इन शब्दों में यीशु ने प्रेरितों  को आत्मा के बपतिस्मा के बारे में नए तरीके से सोचने के लिए पुनः निर्देशित किया राज्य की अंतिम आवश्यकता की आशा देने की तुलना में आत्मा को उड़ेला जाने वाला था ताकि वह प्रेरितों  को मसीह के लिए धर्मी और विश्वास योग्य गवाह होने के लिए सशक्त करें जो कुछ यीशु ने कहा उस पर ध्यान केंद्रित करते हुए आत्मा कि सेवक ik2 आयामों को खोल दे सामर्थ्य और धार्मिकता भरी हुई गवाही सबसे पहले यीशु ने उनके शिष्यों को कहा कि वह आत्मा के बपतिस्मा में के द्वारा सामर्थ्य को प्राप्त करेंगे आत्मा का सामर्थ्य के साथ होना पुराने नियम में एक सामान्य बात है जिसे अक्सर परमेश्वर की आत्मा में आश्रित व्यक्ति प्रस्तुत किया गया है जो कि इब्रानी वाक्य रूआख इलोहीम का अनुवाद है यह इब्रानी अभिव्यक्ति परमेश्वर की ओर से आने वाली शामत साली हवा या ऊर्जा की शक्ति का संकेत देती है पुराने नियम में परमेश्वर का आत्मा विस्तृत रूप से परमेश्वर की इच्छा को पूरा करने के लिए संसार में  सामर्थ साली तरीके से कार्य करता था।\r\n पवित्र आत्मा की शामत नाटक के तरीकों से लोगों के जीवन में प्रकट होती थी उदाहरण के लिए जब परमेश्वर का आत्मा नियायियो अध्ययन 14-15 मैं सिमरोल के ऊपर उतरा तो सिमरन ने आश्चर्यजनक संसारी कारनामों को प्रकट किया जिसके कारण इसराइल ने परिस्थितियों के ऊपर महान विजय को प्राप्त किया आत्मा की सामर्थ्य के अतिरिक्त यीशु ने यहां भी उल्लेख किया है कि आत्मा उसके शिष्यों को धार्मिकता भरी हुई गवाही देने के योग्य बनाए गए यहां संगठन भी पुराने नियम में दिखाई देता है कई अवसरों पर परमेश्वर ने आत्मा ने उसके लोगों को शहर पूर्व और प्रभावी ढंग से परमेश्वर के बदले में बोलने की सामर्थ दी उदाहरण के लिए मीका 3:8 के  इस संदर्भ में में मीका ने समझाया है कि आत्मा ने उसे सच्चाई बोलने के लिए योग्य किया और यज्ञ भी उसका झूठे बहुत दुख तारों ने विरोध किया था इसलिए जब यीशु ने उसके प्रवृत्तियों को कहा कि वह उन्हें पवित्र आत्मा के साथ बपतिस्मा देखकर उसके गवाह होने के लिए संदर्भ देगा तो उसने यह संकेत दिया कि आत्मा उनमें कार्य कैसे ही करेगा जैसे कि पुराने नियम में अन्यों के द्वारा कार्य किया था पवित्र आत्मा प्रेरित हों के संदेश की सच्चाई को प्रमाणित करने के लिए उनमें सामर्थ्य के कार्यों को भी प्रगट करेगा और वे जो उनका विरोध करते हैं उन्हें बोलने के लिए शब्द देगा और उन इसमें कोई संदेह नहीं है कि आत्मा के यहां प्ररितो तो के काम की पुस्तक में बार-बार प्रगट हुई है ।', 9, '2020-10-31 03:41:28', '2020-11-05 18:10:12', NULL);
