(2739, 720, 823, 'Moses drew connection between himself and Noah in the motif of violence\r\n. the work of both Noah an Moses was to deliver people from the violence. \r\nMoses pointed to the fact that both he and Noah had been delivered from water deaths by means of Ark or teavh. \r\nthe importance of divine covenants also establishes Noah as a precursor of Moses. Moses was chose to lead the people of Israel once a special covenant with Yahweh as they came to Munt Sinai. the central role of judgement through water also establishes a fourth connection between the the two men.\r\nin the fifth place , God sent wind to drive back the waters in both the days of Noah and the days of Moses. sixth connection appears in the emphasis put on animals. just as God ordained for Noah to bring animals into the promised Land, God also ordained that Moses should bring animals into the promised land. seventh the theme of divine remembrance also joins Noah and Moses. God declared to Moses that he delivered Israel form Egypt because he remembered his covenant. Divine remembrance also played a vital role in the flood and in the exodus. blessing of nature also associates Noah and Moses', 9, '2021-11-01 18:07:11', '2021-11-17 04:12:14', NULL),
(2740, 720, 824, 'inauguration of the kingdom: Moses emphasized in Genesis 6:19-11:9\r\nChrist accomplished a great salvation. \r\ncovenant: Christ brought deliverance to his people by means of covenant that rescued them form the judgement of God. Nah played a special role as the mediator of covenant and Moses drew upon the fact as he explained his won ministry to Israel. the New testament teaches that Christ is our deliverer because he mediated a new covenant when he came to this earth. Jesus delivered those who trusted him from judgement by mediating the new covenant through his blood on he shed his blood on the cross. \r\nvictory: in addition to bringing a new covenant , Jesus earthly ministry fulfilled the theme of victory in holy war. Mises focused on the theme of holy . Paul described Christ\'s victory at the inauguration of the kingdom in Colossians 2:15 \r\nJesus not only delivered through his new covenant, but he was also victorious over his spiritual forces of darkness in his death resurrection.\r\nfollowers if Christ looks to Christ\'s earthly ministry as the beginning of the final victory promised long ago in the book of Genesis.', 9, '2021-11-01 18:18:46', '2021-11-17 04:12:14', NULL);
