(2741, 720, 825, 'inauguration :\r\ncovenant:\r\nthe new testament teaches that Christ is our deliverer because he meditator a new covenant then he came to this earth:\r\nvictory: Paul described Christ\'s victory as the inaugural of the kingdom. Colossians 2:15\r\nJesus not inky delivered through his new covenant , but he was also victorious over the spiritual forces of darkness in his death and resurrection.\r\ncontinuation: perspectives reacted directly to the importance of baptism and spiritual warfare in the Christian life.\r\nbaptism: \r\nspiritual warfare: New testament passages mainly teach that Christians today are at war with evil,\r\nconsummation:   \r\nfinancial cataclysm: in a even greater way when Christ returns in glory, there will be a cataclysm that utterly disrupts the world.\r\nfinal battle:\r\nin Christ God has delivered us from the tyranny of sin, Just as he delivered the primeval world through Noah, but he has also set us on a  path that requires a period of conflict of struggle as we wait for the day. When Christ brings ultimate victory to his people.', 8, '2021-11-01 18:31:57', '2021-11-17 04:12:14', NULL),
(2742, 722, 962, '2 Timothy 2:15 says Apostle Paul referred to the fact that understanding New Testament Theology often requires hard work. worker  is translated from Greek ergates, a term that often referred to physical laborers.  we need to work hard in terms of learning that language , in terms of learning how genre works, how historical narrative works differently from poetry or differently from personal correspondence.  \r\ninspiration and authority. \r\nto keep myself motivated, I daily read scriptures, meditate upon it, look for meanings, contextual meaning, literal meaning. then I look for background. I refer to different commentaries. I pray about it. I memorize it.\r\nThe Scriptures really reflect a covenantal relationship with God, God\'s gracious initiative to communicate with is but also our responsibility, our response to his Word.', 8, '2021-11-02 17:48:47', '2021-11-17 04:11:15', NULL),
(2743, 722, 963, 'Most evangelical Christians believe in what has been called organic inspiration. this description indicates that it\'s impossible to separate the work of God\'s Spirit and the work of the human authors of Scripture. According to this view, the holy Spirit moved human authors to write and supervised and directed their works as result the words of Scripture are the works of God at the same time , the Holy spirit used the personalities, experiences outlooks, and intentions of human authors as he guided their writing. so the words of Scripture are also very much words of its human authors. the third view best reflects Scripture\'s own testimony about the nature of inspiration\r\nRev Ric Rod heaver says \" men wrote as the Holy Spirit carried them along. its not dictated. it\'s not some message that has no connection to the struggles of the human experience. Peter acknowledged that god\'s Spirit inspired Paul\'s letters. Peter also indicated that this inspiration was organic. one of the most significant inclinations of organic inspiration is what it means to our study of new Testament theology.  Scriptures are true and reliable.', 9, '2021-11-02 18:03:32', '2021-11-17 04:11:15', NULL),
(2744, 722, 964, 'Christians today serve the same God that Christ\'s followers did in the first century. the scriptures teach that God is immutable or unchangeable. because we serve the same immutable god, we should expect there to be many similarities in what god expected from his people in the New Testament and what he expects from us today. just like the original audiences  of the new Testament, we live after Christ\'s death. we have been raised with Christ in his resurrection. just like first century believers. Despite the historical distance that separates us from the days of New Testament, the immutable Creator God has established these kinds of epochal . We find many similarities of culture between our times and New Testament times. we still wear clothes, enjoy art have families ,establish governments and punish crimes much like New Testament times, people today are same, world is same so we can easily apply New Testament texts the audiences , the  and other human figures in the New Testament were like image of god, just like we are today. they were rational and reasoned like us , they reacted with joy and sadness, much like we do today and like us they were fallen images of god who needed redemption in Christ.', 8, '2021-11-02 18:21:04', '2021-11-17 04:11:15', NULL),
(2745, 722, 965, 'relevance of the Bible even though there are the discontinuities between our day and the New Testament age:\r\nthe New Testament was written during the time when god\'s people were transitioning between old and New Testament faith. for this reason  ,any of the issues. despite the historical distance that separates s from the days of the New Testament the immutable Creator has established these kinds of epochal continuities so that we can apply the New Testament to our day.\r\nthe Scriptures are a revelation of God, a revelation of God and god\'s acts in a history. \r\neven though there are discontinuities, we serve the same God, the same Savior Jesus Christ and the same Holy Spirit guides us .\r\nthe New Testament is breathed out by God.', 8, '2021-11-02 18:36:43', '2021-11-17 04:11:15', NULL),
(2746, 722, 966, 'being aware of the continuities and discontinuities between today and the New Testament age helpful for evangelism. \r\nfrom a biblical perspective, there are enough similarities among people for us to be confident that we can learn and apply New Testament theology as we ought. the Scriptures teach that all human beings in New Testament times and today are the same kind of  people. the authors and audiences and other human figures in the new Testament were the image  of God, just like we are today. they were rational and reasoned like us, they reacted with joy and sadness much like we do today, and like us they were fallen images of god, who needed redemption in Christ, they struggled with sin and endured hardship in his fallen world. we are able to connect to people easily. like how Jesus talks to the Samaritan women to bring her husband. there are many similar people even in this world. so people needs salvation at every era. be it then or now.', 8, '2021-11-02 18:50:08', '2021-11-17 04:11:15', NULL),
(2747, 723, 967, 'God has unwavering Sovereignty over all of creation. He is Sovereignly powerful. 1Chronicles 29 :11 and Timothy 6:15speak of the entire creation as God\'s kingdom because God always has ruled and always will rule over all that he has made. \r\nbut in the midst of hard circumstances such as natural disasters, sickness,  poverty , persecution, war and injustice, we human beings are shaken sometimes. but we know that God is enthroned in heaven and nothing happens anywhere, without his foreknowledge. God allows , God permits . but God turns out everything for our good who are called as per  his Will.\r\nall such disasters are a mingle of judgement and mercy, like we see it in the cross of Jesus. it was mercy on us, but judgement of our sins  , which Jesus bore. even by and during these tough times, god awakens souls and turns many to him. We should be  be grateful  for His faithful providence and protection even in such greater troubles like the pandemic era the whole world is going through. even in the midst of all troubles, God is Sovereign  to take care of us all.\r\nHis Sovereignty is our refuge amidst all troubles, no matter the trouble is small , local or international.', 7, '2021-11-06 16:46:48', '2021-11-17 04:10:15', NULL),
(2748, 723, 968, 'God\'s final victory and the defeat of his enemies is the basis of our life. Jesus defeated death by dying. \r\nHe rose up from the dead . and we believe in Jesus Christ and we are saved, we are given a new life. The Spirit of God is given to us a guarantee , as a deposit , He sanctifies us , produces his fruit in our lives.\r\nAnd so we live encouraged and empowered waiting for our Christ\' s return who will finally defeat both human and Spiritual enemies. and will come under the judgement of God.\r\nevery knee will bow one day. Philippians 2. this truth is the hope and anchor of my soul. this truth enables me to live joyfully with him and serve Him faithfully.\r\nGod\'s final victory and defeat  will be the consummation of Christ\'s kingdom. when Christ returns, he will no longer extend mercy to god\'s human enemies too. Satan will be banished form His sight. and we will live a beautiful life.', 9, '2021-11-06 16:59:13', '2021-11-17 04:10:15', NULL),
(2749, 723, 969, 'my childhood was a terrible one, my father being on anti depressants, anyone can imagine how my life would be. we had no Christ in our life. we had no peace at home. domestic violence accompanied by satanic attacks. when I was ten years old, An evangelist named  Mrs. Jacob cam to our house, She gave us Jesus and along with Him came hope, peace and love. My dad was rescued from all sorts of mental illness. that has definitely molded me to be compassionate and understanding other families with similar troubles. to share gospel to them. we were in the clutches of Satan, when We dint know God. but Jesus Set us free.\r\nGod delivered us from a horrible childhood. \r\nthen  in our ministry we had many struggles. \r\nwe lost our child. \r\nGod tested our faith\r\n.two failed pregnancies.\r\nthen God blessed us with two children.\r\nmy brothers were terrible addicted . once I just lost Him. but I went to my brother, prayed to God and Gave him to God\'s hands. God saved him from the clutches of Satan.\r\nGod has delivered me from the stronghold of sin and Satan.\r\nall the deliverance that I had, has made me compassionate, passionate to others. i am considerate while serving others, knowing their struggles . I fast for them. I convince them , share gospel. god does rest things ,', 9, '2021-11-06 17:10:38', '2021-11-17 04:10:15', NULL),
(2750, 723, 970, 'Matthew 13:31-32 says that Jesus taught that God\'s victorious kingdom would begin as something small. like  mustard seed. grow for a period of time, and then reach its final culmination. Jesus outlook on the coming of God\'s messianic kingdom\" inaugurated eschatology this refers to the idea that the work of the Messiah has already been manifested on earth, but the final victory is sill to come., they speak of \" already , but not yet\"\r\n the victory of God\'s kingdom has come already , but not yet in its fulness. this outlook on the victory pf God\'s kingdom offers countless insights into the theology of the New Testament. \r\nJesus has inaugurated the kingdom and we live in a period between inauguration and consummation. when the consummation comes, we live enter into glorious bodies, we will live eternally forever. we still live in theses bodies, we still live in this fallen world. He\'s also reigning in our hearts. the kingdom has come its already, but it is still future. its not yet as well.\r\nthis helps me live a faithful Christian life in this fallen world. since the one who inaugurated and established will also bring it into consummation one day.\r\nGod initiated the victory of the kingdom through Jesus life. death, resurrection  and ascension. \r\nJesus will bring the consummation of the kingdom when he returns in glory.', 7, '2021-11-06 17:25:05', '2021-11-17 04:10:15', NULL),
(2751, 723, 971, 'Jesus\' messianic kingship in the royal titles that the New Testament gives him. the new testament refers to Jesus with the royal titles Christ which means anointed one, the anointed one of God, Jesus in the one who is anointed by God who will save us form the sin \r\na second title attributed to Jesus in the New Testament is royal son of god  or son of the most high. Jesus is the rightful king of Israel. John 1:9. yes we can use it to as an evangelistic tool that Jesus is the son of the Most High, his is the kingdom, he is the king of kings and his kingdom  has no end. \r\nthird royal designation for Jesus\' \" son of David\" God ordained heir of David\'s throne. he is the seed of David, his kingdom has no end, Luke 1:32-33 Jesus is the one who will bring about final , never ending victory of the kingdom of God. we can use these royal titles as an evangelistic tool to convince and convict that Jesus is the anointed one , He is the Messiah, he is the Savior , He is the son of the Most High. he is the seed of David. there is salvation in his name alone.', 8, '2021-11-06 17:38:29', '2021-11-17 04:10:15', NULL),
(2752, 724, 972, 'the New Testament identifies Christ as the New covenant representative . every Jew and every Gentile that God identifies with Christ. Hebrews 9:15 Romans 8:34 and 1Timothy2:5-6. Christ is God\'s chosen representative for the church helps us understand one of the most important characteristics of New Testament theology.  or we can understand that New Testament is Christocentric. every facet of New Testament theology is closely related and ties to the person and work of Christ. we must believe in Jesus for salvation. we must pray and show kindness in the name of Jesus, the church is the body of Christ. because Christ play the central role in New Testament theology because God administers every dimension of life in the New Covenant through Christ as the representative of the church. so this covenant arrangement help s understand New Testament theology in a better  way.', 8, '2021-11-08 17:43:29', '2021-11-17 04:09:28', NULL),
(2753, 724, 973, 'the new testament doctrine of union with Christ points out two sides because we are in Christ every eternal blessing of god has already been assigned to true believers.\r\nTrue believers receive both blessings and curses in this life. As Hebrews 12:1-11 says temporary hardships, failures that happen in our life are God\'s loving . fatherly discipline. theses difficulties sanctifies us and increase eternal blessings we will receive when Christ returns we are identified with Christ in  heaven , and we have received every spiritual blessing . \r\nChrist \'s Spirit work in us , within believers to make us holy. Scripture says that testing is the way God moves us forward in  sanctification. James 1:2,3 every time we are tested and tried , our faith come s out as gold and in light of God\'s kingdom. we shall be greatly rewarded for our faith in him. \r\nthese failures are momentary troubles which are bringing us eternal glory.', 7, '2021-11-08 17:58:12', '2021-11-17 04:09:28', NULL),
(2754, 724, 974, 'as we read the policies of the New covenant, we see that Jeremiah 31:33-34, God said that I will write or put my law in their minds and write it on their hearts.  His promise has come true, when we are regenerated. when we are born again, we are washed by his blood, we are a new creation , we get a new heart, a heart of flesh. the Holy Spirit regenerates our hearts. in the policies of the new Covenant age, God promised to intervene in a such a way that writing his law in our hearts for all of his people.\r\nthough we should meditate and memorize from the Scriptures, but  more than that Holy spirit indwells us and guides us in the right way. it is like the law is written in our hearts. The holy Spirit prompts us when we go and do wrong. \r\nI have seen it in my life, when as a teenager or now in ministry. \r\n a regenerated  heart knows when we do things against God. the holy Spirit convicts us when we sin against god. then we hear the gentle voice of  God and follow Him and make necessary corrections wherever needed. \r\nGod has definitely intervened when I go away from Him , on my own way. Though not knowing all Scripture, we know it by the Spirit of god.', 8, '2021-11-08 18:13:57', '2021-11-17 04:09:28', NULL),
(2755, 724, 975, 'I can definitely fulfill my covenant obligations to God.\r\n First of all being a faithful servant of God, being loyal to Him  in all the responsibilities he has given me be it a wife  or mother or as a missionary in India. \r\nI am serving God as a full time servant, laboring in His vineyard, looking after the believers he has handed me, spreading his good news to those lost ones around me.  I ma fulfilling the duties of a wife, being faithful to my husband, serving him, respecting him, being submissive to him, supporting him, helping him.\r\nI am training my children as joyful mother should. I am being in an example before them , training them in Scriptures.\r\nso these are my present circumstances, I am trying my best with all resources I have to fulfill my covenant obligations to God, by being obedient to Him, loyal to him, by serving him with all my heart, by following the Great commission .\r\nI am fervently praying for my family, nation and church. I am serving God and faithful to  God and obey Him, by serving others and by forgiving them, by accepting them, by loving them.', 7, '2021-11-08 18:29:02', '2021-11-17 04:09:28', NULL),
(2756, 724, 976, 'there are troubles in this world, trials and tests are there present everywhere till the last breath of our life. the blessing that we receive in this life re foretastes of the eternal blessings that will come at the consummation of the kingdom. Hebrews 12:1-11 tell us temporary hardships are God\'s loving , fatherly discipline. these difficulties sanctify us and increase the blessings we will receive when Christ returns.  \r\nthe promise that we will receive the eternal inheritance in the glorious new creation , is the anchor of hope in all our tough circumstances. we may get sick, may be sick to death, we have lost our dear ones, we have bore many losses financially, many easy gains, bore many pains, insults, persecutions. \r\nwe are looked down upon by many friends and relatives. all because we are in Christ. but our inheritance in the glorious new creation, the life with God Almighty is the only thing we hold on to in our toughest trials.  and this motivates us like nothing and I live to motivate others with the same hope to persevere.', 8, '2021-11-08 18:41:44', '2021-11-17 04:09:28', NULL),
(2757, 726, 962, 'in 2Timothy 2:15, the apostle Paul indicated that understanding New Testament theology oftten requires hard work. worker is translated from Greek ergates, a term that often referred to physical laborers. we need to work hard in terms of learning that language, in terms of learning how genre work, how historical narrative works differently from poetry or different from personal correspondence. Inspiration and authority. I keep myself motivated in my endeavors to understand . I give myself to study because the New Testament is breathed out by God.. the epochal , cultural and personal continuities and discontinuities between New Testament times and ours require s to devote ourselves to understanding and applying New Testament theology. \r\nI daily read scriptures, look for meanings, contexts, background, contextual meaning, literal meaning, I refer to commentaries. I memorize and pray about it. I continuos meditate upon it the scriptures', 8, '2021-11-09 17:45:42', '2021-11-17 04:08:29', NULL),
