(2772, 727, 971, 'Jesus messianic kingship in the royal titles that the New Testament gives him, the New Testament refers to Jesus with royal titles Christ which means anointed one, the anointed one of God, Jesus in the one who is anointed by God who will save us from the sin.\r\na second title attributed to Jesus  in the New Testament is royal son of God or son of the most high. Jesus is the rightful king of Israel. John 1:9 yes we can use it to as an evangelistic tool  that Jesus is the Son of the Most high, his is the kingdom, he is the king if kings a nd his kingdom has no end. third royal designation for Jesus\" Son of David\" God ordained heir of David\'s throne. he is the seed of David his kingdom has no end. Luke 1:32 Jesus is the one who will bring about final, never ending victory of the kingdom of God. we can use these royal titles as an evangelistic tool to convince and convict that Jesus is the anointed one. He is the Messiah, he is the savior, he is the seed of David, there is salvation , there is salvation in his name alone.', 7, '2021-11-12 18:39:58', '2021-11-17 04:07:35', NULL),
(2773, 730, 905, 'Paul did not have the same relationship with every Colossians Christan, ... Then we focus in church and individual\r\n\r\nChurch- colo 2:1 deeply for them nonetheless, \r\nNevertheless, we are able to study we find that Paul relationship with the Colossians from the Paul\'s letter.. We read Paul had an indirect relationship with the Colossians through representives, such as his Colossians friend epaphras, Philemon, and onesimus, and his messagers tychicus\r\nThey don\'t met face to face.. They most relationship with in correspondence\r\n1:9 we see Paul prayers for Colossians\r\n\r\nIndividual\r\n Paul have a numbers of friends in Colossian.. Philemon, apphia, archippus \r\nMost of Paul friend seem to have association in some way with Philemon but whatever their relationship to one another it is clear that Paul had closer relationship with these friend then he had with the church in colosse in general. But as his letter to the Colossian showe it is also clear that his relationship with these friend', 8, '2021-11-13 16:21:31', '2021-11-17 04:06:24', NULL),
(2774, 730, 906, 'Colo 2: 1-4 Paul word here indicated that the Colossians value mystery, wisdom and knowledge  all of which Greek philosophy and religion typically valued, \r\nPaul say true mystery and wisdom and knowledge were found only in Christ. And not in pagan religion\r\nPaul target pagan philosophy in 2:8 colo\r\nThe false teacher in colosse tried to mix the church teaching with Greek traditional that were supposed to bring wisdom and strength believe against temptation, \r\n\r\nJewish law\r\nColo 2:16  \r\nEvidence the false teachers in colosse stressed certan practice derived from the old Testament law. Jewish calendar scuh a religion festival new moon, and sabbath day, \r\nIn Colossians Paul wrote against abuse of mosaic Law  he did not writing agant the law of itself. \r\n\r\nSpiritual beings\r\nThe fale teachers cleam to have received vision from angels, and on this basic they encourage others Christan to complete the proper ritual so that they might receive similar', 7, '2021-11-13 16:41:34', '2021-11-17 04:06:24', NULL),
(2775, 728, 972, 'the new testament identifies Christ as the New Testament representative . every Jew and gentile that God identifies with Christ. Hebrews 9:15the fact that Christ is God\'s chosen covenant representative for the church helps us understand one of the most important characteristics of New Testament theology. New Testament theology is Christocentric. every facet of New Testament theology is closely tied to the person and work of Christ. The New Testament teach that we must believe in Jesus for salvation. we pray and show kindness in the name of Jesus. the church is called the body of Christ. Christ play this important role in New Testament theology because of God administer every dimension of life the new covenant through Christ as the representative of the church. so this covenant arrangement is a great help in understanding the New Testament theology.', 9, '2021-11-13 16:49:28', '2021-11-17 04:05:47', NULL),
(2776, 730, 907, 'First is. Paul relationship with the Colossians church in general and with individual within the church. And second thing is investigation some of the problem in Colossian that concerned Paul. \r\nLooking at relationship with the Colossian \r\nSome other reason is.. False teachers inter in church... So paul teache true word of God in Colossian letter', 5, '2021-11-13 16:52:16', '2021-11-17 04:06:24', NULL),
(2777, 728, 973, 'we deal with failures in light of God\'s kingdom purposes.  the New Testament doctrine of union in Christ. we suffer a lot sometimes, we fail a lot but these are building us to eternal happiness in God\'s kingdom. this tests and trials in the form of failures purify us each day and sanctify us each day to eternity.\r\nthe temporary hardships sanctify us and increase the eternal blessings we will receive when Christ returns. Rev 21:6-8. our failures make us humble and we depend and trust God more, which leads to foretastes of the eternal blessings in God\'s kingdom.\r\nfailures will be there , but our loyalty to god and his kingdom will remain same. James 1:2-3 says that testing is the way God moves us to sanctification.', 8, '2021-11-13 16:59:09', '2021-11-17 04:05:47', NULL),
(2778, 728, 974, 'as we read the policies of the New covenant, we see that Jeremiah 31:33-34, god said that I will write or put my law in their minds and write it on their hearts. his promise has come true, when we are regenerated, when we are born again, we are washed by his blood, we are a new creation , we get a new heart, heart of flesh. the Holy Spirit regenerates our hearts in the policies of the New covenant age, God promised to intervene in such a way that writing his law in our hearts for all of his people. we should read the word, meditate upon his promises, memorize  the Word of god, but the Holy Spirit indwells in us, guides us , motivates us , corrects us, in eth way of god. it is really like God has written the law in in our hearts. we with the born again life live with a new and different better renewed mind.\r\nin our ministry while preaching, while teaching, while encouraging, we can definitely see how His promise to intervene and write his law in our hearts have come true', 8, '2021-11-13 17:08:50', '2021-11-17 04:05:47', NULL),
(2779, 730, 908, 'False teachers were trying to persuade the Colossians church to worship cosmic spiritual power. \r\nBut Paul teach insisted that Christ is king of all creations and that he possess all perfection and authority.  \r\nColossians 1:15 -20 Paul teach Christ supremacy\r\nAnd most of these details contrast with false teachers in Colosse. \r\nHe spoke of Christ as the image of God colo 1:15 , 16 supreme Lord \r\nFalse teachers looked to the planets and elements as the image of God, Paul point to Christ as the image of God \r\n\r\nPaul say Christ as a firstborn over all creations, again Paul chose his word carefully to refut the false teachers \r\nPaul said Christ was the firsborn over all creations, he meant that Christ was the one who possessed the birthright of the father, not that Christ was born or creations before all other, he did not mean that Christ was part of creation. But that Christ was Lord over it  that false teachers had no power or authority to give any blessing to anyone.', 6, '2021-11-13 17:11:54', '2021-11-17 04:06:24', NULL),
(2780, 728, 975, 'fulfilling my covenant obligations to God is the primary responsibility of a Christian life. I am a Pastor, serving God in parts of North India, I have completely dedicated life to God. \r\nIt is my obligation to take care of my sheep that is the people God has entrusted in my hand, by teaching them , by guiding them, by correcting them . I am also a husband and a Father. my primary duty is also to lead the family to a better Christ-centered life in their daily life. \r\nobeying His word, being loyal to Him in our trials and tests, fulfilling our responsibilities faithfully and joyfully in our daily circumstances is very important in the sight of God. \r\nso serving Him faithfully with all that he has given eagerly and joyfully in our daily life.', 9, '2021-11-13 17:20:25', '2021-11-17 04:05:47', NULL),
(2781, 730, 909, 'Paul argue that because Christ was superior to the false God. Christ ministers were superior to those who served the false gods \r\nColo 1:22- \r\nChrist\'s ministers are superior because they preach that actually reconcile believe to God. \r\n\r\nThe false teachers encourage Colossians people to placate demons, and perhaps they also offered reconciliation with God. But in reality, no reconciliation ever took place for them because their so called Gospel had no power to save. \r\nPaul point to his own Altruism. Speaking of his suffering on behalf of the church Colo 1:24\r\n\r\nPaul say superior empowering of Christ minister, speaking of the fact that God gave power to his ministers, Paul did not labor in his own strength. Rather. God empowered and motivated Paul to work and to suffer as his apostle', 8, '2021-11-13 17:24:41', '2021-11-17 04:06:24', NULL),
(2782, 728, 976, 'there are troubles in this world and trials are there present everywhere till the last breath of our life. the blessing that we receive in this life are foretastes of the eternal blessings that will come at the consummation of the kingdom.  Hebrews 12:1-11 tell us temporary hardships are God\'s loving fatherly discipline , these discipline, these difficulties sanctify us and increase the blessings we ill receive when Christ returns.\r\nthe promise that we will receive the eternal blessings works as the anchor of our soul. the inheritance in the glorious creation is what we are looking for in our present and momentary troubles\r\nthis motivates us to g that extra mile and take that extra step, even though sometimes each steps seems heavier  for us, but the eternity, the presence of god, seeing Him face to face gives us the courage to do everything for god and bear all these  pain. everything struggle is worth it.\r\nthis motivates me and others to persevere.', 8, '2021-11-13 17:30:36', '2021-11-17 04:05:47', NULL),
(2783, 731, 910, 'A number of modern scholars have suggest that paul did not actually write this letter. But when we see ep 1: 1 it writen was by Paul \r\nNow it is true that in early church some false teachers forget letter under the name of other people. \r\nBut whenever the church discover a letter to be a forgery, they rejected it. Listen to Paul\'s teaching on this matter in 2 thessa 2:1-3\r\nBeyond this Ephesians closely resembles pauls other letter in both doctrn and language. The connection are especially strong with Colossians, which should not surprise us since Paul probably wrote them both at about the same time These connection are so powerful and natural that even crediting it to anyone else', 7, '2021-11-14 16:14:00', '2021-11-17 04:04:16', NULL),
(2784, 731, 911, 'Normally Paul tailored his letter to address the specific problem of a relatively localized group of people whom he know directly or personally. But in Ephesians he did something different. He responded to the problem of several churches in different locations, many of which he had never met. \r\nPaul purpose in writing this letter was to deal with the problem of all these church\'s. But his strategy was not to address each issue individually. \r\nTwo many things - 1) kingdom of God, 2) several challenges to the church in terms of God\'s kingdom. Let\'s look first at the theme of the kingdom of God', 9, '2021-11-14 16:25:27', '2021-11-17 04:04:16', NULL),
(2785, 731, 912, 'The background to Paul epistle to the Ephesians, we are in a positions to survey the structure and content of Paul letter to the church in Ephesus. \r\n1) salutation\r\n1:1-2  say by the will of God. This reference God\'s will identifie Paul as God official represent so that Paul word carry divian authority\r\n2) praise\r\n3) prayer\r\n\r\nAudience\r\n1.original audience of the letter to the Ephesians\r\nSecondary  audience, especially the church of the lycus valley', 8, '2021-11-14 16:41:10', '2021-11-17 04:04:16', NULL),
(2786, 731, 913, 'Praise-\r\nEphesians 1: 3- 14 this Paul canonical letter in which the salutation is followed by such a section of praise to God. Typically Paul followed his salutation with a personal reference or greetings. \r\nBut we seen no personal reference of any type in the epistle to the Ephesians\r\nWe focus on such as it\'s a strong theology  through these verses, explicitly honoring the work of the father, the son and the holy Spirit\r\nPrayer\r\nEphesians 1:15- 23 when we see Paul prayer... \r\nPrayer as 3 part \r\nHis thankful for believers\r\nPetition that the holy Spirit would enlighten them \r\n An extended explanation of the enlightenment\r\nHonoring work of the father the son and holy spirit vers 17 \r\nGod\'s sovereignty rule, which includes his power and authority, God benevolent, which consist of the good things\r\nVers 19\r\nVers 18 Paul prayer Christ\'s glorious inheritance in the saints, which is the hope', 7, '2021-11-14 16:59:19', '2021-11-17 04:04:16', NULL),
(2787, 731, 914, 'Citizenship\r\n1) Ep 2:1-3 focus on the fact that fallen human being are born into the kingdom of darkness and are enemies of God by natur. \r\nEp 2:4-10 the way Gid grants us citizenship in his kingdom by transferring us from the kingdom of darkness to the kingdom of light\r\nEp 2:11-22 The nature of our citizenship in the kingdom of light\r\n\r\nAdministration\r\nEp 3:2-7 Paul say his apostolic authority in relation to the administration of God\'s kingdom. \r\n     God appointed Paul to be his official representative on earth. His apostle. And this Apostleship made paul word Authorvitvt, as it had been spoken by God himself \r\nWisely Paul say in the  administration of the kingdom did not end with his assertion of authority but with a prayer. \r\n\r\nCode of living\r\nThis code for living in the kingdom contain many different instructions. \r\nEp 5\r\nGod\'s kingdom is to be as a morally pure as possible. It is to reflect the characters of it\'s king. And this is for the benefits of the whole kingdom. After all, God blessing and reward moral purity.', 8, '2021-11-14 17:19:18', '2021-11-17 04:04:16', NULL),
(2788, 731, 915, 'Ep 2: 19 -22 . Paul say the Gentiles Christan were full citizens in God\'s kingdom, with equal status of Jewish Christan citizens. \r\nMain fact Paul say every Christan being as a stone in this structure of this kingdom of God\r\nNow the goal of this building was to because God\'s dwelling so that God could live in the midst of his people. \r\nWe Christan build God\'s kingdom today, we must focus on the big picture of honoring God and living in his presence. And of striving to increase Christ glory rather than our own.', 7, '2021-11-14 17:30:58', '2021-11-17 04:04:16', NULL),
(2789, 731, 916, 'God\'s kingdom of the demons and fallen humanity. But eventually Jesus will return. And when he does. He will deliver final judgment against his enemies. Forever crushing their ability to resist him. The present age of sin and death, we have the upper hand in the battle against the demon forces. As we see our king is already seatsed in power and authority above them, and we are seated with him. God has already seatsed in power and authority above them. \r\nThe church is God\'s prize we are the treasure he has fought for and won from the kingdom of his enemies. We are the people God control history to serve,', 7, '2021-11-14 17:42:56', '2021-11-17 04:04:16', NULL),
(2790, 732, 917, 'First. Philemon, second Philemons slave  Onesimus a number of people\r\nPhilemon- Philemons himself appear to have been actively involved in ministering to other believers in colosse. For instance, in Philomen 7 Paul spoke of the way philomon had lovely refreshed the heart of other believers. \r\nBible does not explain how Paul come know philemon. Many people say Paul second minister journey he meet him. \r\nOnesimus\r\nAccording to philemon 16 Onesimus was philemons slave, ... But we don\'t know what kind of slave\r\nWitnesses\r\nPaul mention apphia and archippus in the letter address, found in philemon 1-2 \r\nThe mention of apphia as Paul sister\r\nBut simplely say that she is a believers but since she is distinguished from the rest of the church, it is likely that she was a member of philemons household', 2, '2021-11-15 16:18:08', '2021-11-17 04:02:01', NULL);
INSERT INTO `descriptive_answers` (`id`, `assignment_id`, `question_id`, `answer`, `mark`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(2791, 732, 918, 'It\'s is no secret that some workers are not good worked.. That some servant not good servant.. Onesimus was one of these people.. And his failure whether slothful, negligent or malicious, angered his master philemon.. So much so that onesimus had greatly feared punishment from philemon. \r\nPhilemon 18 mention many say Onesimus had stolen from philemon.. Which was a command crime among household slave... In any cases philemon had a right angry.. But trying to solve this problem to wrote this letter for philemon', 7, '2021-11-15 16:30:09', '2021-11-17 04:02:01', NULL),
(2792, 732, 919, 'Paul did not immediately agree to mediate between Onesimus and Philemon. After all Onesimus was both qn unbeliever and an unprofitable slave, and philemon was a good, loving man. \r\nPaul preaching gospel with Onesimus, he became a newborn in Christ.. Onesimus repentance of all his sin.. Onesimus became a new man and dedicated himself to ministering to the apostle in prison. And Paul in turn, cared deeply for this new child of God, and grew to love him as a son\r\nPaul send Onesimus back to philemon because he wanted any gift from Philemon to be voluntary rather than compulsory, and because be wanted philemon and Onesimus to be reconcile as brother in Christ', 7, '2021-11-15 16:43:12', '2021-11-17 04:02:01', NULL),
(2793, 732, 920, '1) Paul as Advocate 8-10 \r\nIn this passage Paul spoke as a weak elderly man in need of help, and to those who are familiar with his strong writing style in other letter\r\n2) Onesimus as petitioner\r\nPhilemon 11-13 \r\n3) Philemon as a master- 14\r\nPhilemon authority from onesimos\r\n\r\n4) God\'s role as providential ruler of the universe 15-16\r\n5) Paul\'s petition itself  17 -20\r\n6) Paul Statment of confidence that the petition would be granted - 21', 5, '2021-11-15 16:57:40', '2021-11-17 04:02:01', NULL),
(2794, 732, 921, 'Philemon 17-18 he appealed to Philemon for a personal favor as if Paul himself were the one who needed Philemons grace. He did not argue the onesimos deserved to be restored to Philemon. \r\nPhilemon 20 we Paul hoped that Philemon would so respect Paul that he would extened mercy to Paul\'s spiritual son onesimos. And si in his petition, Paul asked Philemon to ministry to the apostle by showing kindness to his son, \r\nPaul asked for mercy for onesimos', 7, '2021-11-15 17:08:14', '2021-11-17 04:02:01', NULL),
(2795, 733, 922, 'Paul had planted the church in philippi during his second missionary journey, around the year A D 49- 50\r\nIn philippi, Paul\r\n    Gained his first European convert\r\n    Was jailed for a exorcism\r\n    Led the Philippin jailer to a professional of faith in Christ \r\nThe church was poor and not always able to help Paul financial, but when they had opportunity, they gave to him generously\r\nPaul referred to philippi as his dear friend ( 2:12-4:1)', 0, '2021-11-16 17:17:54', '2021-11-16 17:17:54', NULL),
(2796, 733, 923, 'The church loved Paul, and they regularly helped him with financial gift according to philippi 4\r\nPhilippi also send gift close to the time that he wrote his letter to them. Listen to Paul ( 4.10) \r\nPaul say they also his close friends\r\nGreek word agapetos\r\nAnd when we see relationship with believers in philippi we understand there friendship so deeper... Lydia, jailor... We have seen caring supportive relationship between Paul and the Philippin, we should turn to the details of the apostles suffering in prison.', 0, '2021-11-16 17:29:48', '2021-11-16 17:29:48', NULL),
(2797, 733, 924, 'Important of perseverance in 1:27-2:18 the help for perseverance that ministers provide in 2: 19- \r\nPaul own exp.. Of perseverance in 3\r\nAnd finally his instructions regarding challenge to perseverance in Christan faith and practice \r\nThe Philippins suffering were distressing  and painful, but they were not beyond God\'s control. On the contrary Gid himself had planned third suffering as a means of blessing them. And therefore. It was vital that they planned their', 0, '2021-11-16 17:43:11', '2021-11-16 17:43:11', NULL),
(2798, 733, 925, '1. Salutation\r\n  Paul is the primary author of this letter \r\n2.Thanksgiving\r\n   Paul present a fairly standard statement of thanks speaking\r\nThe joy, philippi have brought to him\r\nHis expectations for their ultimate salvation\r\n3.prayer\r\nPaul prayer is packed with statement that reflect the emphasis of the entire letter\r\nMake proper judgment\r\nPerform good work\r\nPersever in faith and practice\r\nBring glory and praise to God\r\n4. Body \r\nPaul let philippi know how much loved them and how thankful he was their friendship and ministery', 0, '2021-11-16 17:52:41', '2021-11-16 17:52:41', NULL),
(2799, 733, 926, 'Paul recognition that the Philippines minister to him had helped him to persevere at many stage of his ministery\r\nWe can learn much from the way the Philippines minister ministering to Paul by providing material support. There are multitude of Christan through the world who\'s have grateful material need\r\nIn myself our  ministering life Face many problems.. But always God prepared many people to help our needs.. \r\nOur relationship between people we also help others like Paul word in philippi..', 0, '2021-11-16 18:07:14', '2021-11-16 18:07:14', NULL),
(2800, 734, 962, 'In 2 Timothy 2:15 the apostle Paul referred to the fact the understanding new testament theology often require hard work Listen to what Paul told Timothy \r\nMany dimension of new testament theology are quite simple. But Paul made it clear that understanding scripture is not always easy. Timothy was to be a worker.. Who correctly handles the word of truth.. The Greek term translated worker.. Is ergates a teram that often referred to physical labour Paul metaphor indicated that grasping the theology of the new testament often requer hard labour. But if studying new testament theology is so difficult..', 5, '2021-11-20 15:49:12', '2022-01-15 15:14:08', NULL),
(2801, 734, 963, 'Romantic inspiration. The holy Spirit inspired biblical writers in the same way secular poets or musical might be moved to write \r\n\r\nMechanical inspiration. The holy spirit essentially dictated the Bible, and human writer passively record what he said\r\nOrganic inspiration. Holy spirit used the personalities experience outlook and intention of human author as he guided their writing.. \r\n\r\nPeter acknowledge that God\'s spirit inspired Paul\'s letter but he also indicated that this inspection was organic\r\n1.Explicit assertion. This is the text itself and it can reach us a great deal about new testament theology\r\n2. Theology presupposes we have to study the authors background and theological beliefs\r\n3.Implicit purpose. The implications the authors expected their audience to infer from their text', 6, '2021-11-20 16:07:36', '2022-01-15 15:14:08', NULL),
(2802, 734, 964, 'When followers of Christ first begin to read the new testament they\'re usually drawn to it\'s relatively basic teaching. They read things like Jesus is Lord, Repent and believe the Gospel, love one another and a host of other essential teaching. They don\'t have to consider much about the historical circumstances, personality and purpose of new testament author. For all practical purposes... \r\nN. T writing nearly 2000 years ago. And for this reason. It\'s language. Concept, custom and tradition are different from what we experience in our morden world. But at the same time. If we give ourselves to the study of these matter we can see that new testament still  connects to our world in many ways \r\nIn our life new testament book also connect.. Because when I facing problem I have solution in nt book', 6, '2021-11-20 16:26:59', '2022-01-15 15:14:08', NULL),
(2803, 734, 965, 'There are many epochal continues between our day and the days of the new testament. One of the best ways to see these connection is to realize that Christan today serve the same  God that Christ follow did in the first century. Traditional systemic theoloan often point out how the scripture teach that God is immutable, or unchangeable they focus on this unalterable attributes, his eternal plans and his covenant oaths in numbers 23\r\nIs 46, James 1:17 and because we serve the same immutable God we should expect there to be many similar in what God expected from his people in NT and what he expect from us today', 7, '2021-11-20 16:39:16', '2022-01-15 15:14:08', NULL),
(2804, 734, 966, 'From a biblical perspective there are enough similar among people fir us to be confident that we can learn and apply new testament theology as we \r\nThe out her  audience and other  human figure in new testament were the image of God  we today.. They were retional and reasonl like us. \r\nEvery culture on earth is shaped by the natural of human being and the physical, mutual... But always gospel is gospel... Gospel always same .. But when we present in front of people in different ways... We have many way to spread gospel in this time.. But new testament time only preach and writing letter..', 4, '2021-11-20 16:56:46', '2022-01-15 15:14:08', NULL),
(2805, 735, 967, 'The passage  1 chr 29:11 1.timo 6.15\r\nSay God always has ruled and rule all over the universe.. We keep the passage.. That is script speak of God\'s sovereignty as taking place on two level.. In heaven and on earth\r\nIn the many challenge for God kingdom. But the scripture indicat time and again that the end God will have victory over valley who have opposed him. His image will success in filling and having dominion over the the earth, and the wonder of God kingdom will be revealed everywhere. And at that time', 3, '2021-11-21 16:24:13', '2022-01-15 15:18:48', NULL),
(2806, 735, 968, 'The belief that God would defeat not only human enemies. But also spiritual enemies was supported through out the old Testament scripture. For instance in exodus 12 God say of definitng not only  the Egyptian. But the gods of the Egyptian as well. In 1 Samuel 5:1 Gid made war with the Philistines and also defeated their false God dagon. This is why Isaiah 21:9 coupled the defeat of Babylon with the destruction of Babylon gods\r\nOld testament passage like hagg 2:6 zech 9 ez38 were intrpct in Jewish apocalypse literature as prophet about the grat cosmic war in which the Messiah would lead the armies of God in victory over the nation\'s and the evil spirits who ruled over them. In this way \r\nMessiah would defeat all of God\'s enemies and would deliver all of God people into his glorious, worldwide kingdom.', 6, '2021-11-21 16:40:14', '2022-01-15 15:18:48', NULL),
(2807, 735, 969, 'In myself I don\'t have many things.. But facing some particular problem in our lives.. Some have sickness... But God\'s victory truly I see in my sickness situation.. We know that God give that our lives\r\nAfter this type of situation we must proclaim in faith and belief.. Praying attitude..and Live with Jesus\r\nSome time we facing financial problems.. But our God always give victory in this subject.. \r\nSome time we say what my calling.. Why God call me in his ministry.. But when we take his miracle in our lives , we understand our God Almighty God..', 5, '2021-11-21 16:52:04', '2022-01-15 15:18:48', NULL),
(2808, 735, 970, 'We have miracle represented the blessings if the kingdom that Jesus brought to earth\r\nJesus attention to social justice represesend important blessing of the kingdom.. So we fearless live in this fallen world because our Lord with us\r\nThe greatest blessing in the inauguration of God kingdom was the gift enteral salvation colo1:13\r\n\r\nThe outpouring of the holy Spirit was the one blessing of the world to come given to all believers 2.cor 1:21 holy Spirit always with us.. So we must understand what is wrong and what is right in Christan life..', 5, '2021-11-21 17:04:30', '2022-01-15 15:18:48', NULL),
(2809, 735, 971, '2 corporate 1:21, 22 , ep 1:14 both passage indicate that the Holy Spirit is Christ\'s \' seal of ownership on us\' \' he is a deposit, guaranteeing what is to come in \r\nJesus Christ is delivered people in there crisis.. When we preach gospel we say Jesus Christ is give victory all your problems.. Manly our sin.. \r\nOur God as a God samarthan.. So we preach Jesus Christ is a Samaritan', 3, '2021-11-21 17:16:48', '2022-01-15 15:18:48', NULL),
(2810, 736, 972, 'The new testment repeatedly identify Christ as the new covenant representative, God engaged him in special ways on behalf of church every jew and Gentile that God identifies with Christ. As we read in Hebrew 9:15\r\nThe fact that Christ is God chosen covenant represent for the church help us understand one of the most important character of new testment theology help many biblical interpretation have noted, new testment theology is christocentric in other words ever fact of new testment theology is closely tied to the person and work of Christ. But why is this true \r\nHave seen that God administration his kingdom through covenant representative, and specific through Christ in the new covenant, we should turn t\r\nWe must know that Jesus Christ only way in heaven... We have not any other option', 5, '2021-11-22 15:46:09', '2022-01-15 15:21:10', NULL),
