(758, 23, 'When considering the range of prayers included in the Book of Psalms, one can note that the psalmist even confessed his anger before God.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2017-12-19 07:28:58', '2017-12-19 00:28:58', 1, 1),
(759, 23, 'We get to know ourselves by studying philosophy.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2017-12-19 07:30:20', '2017-12-19 00:30:20', 1, 1),
(760, 23, 'Prayer is convincing God to give us what we want.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2017-12-19 07:31:29', '2017-12-19 00:31:29', 1, 1),
(761, 23, 'There are three dimensions of prayer: prayers of the understanding, prayers with sighs too deep for words, and prayers with the Spirit.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2017-12-19 07:32:27', '2017-12-19 00:32:27', 1, 1),
(762, 23, 'Among the different kinds of prayers prayed by Jesus while on earth, one is His prayer of submission to His Father’s will.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2017-12-19 07:33:26', '2017-12-19 00:33:26', 1, 1),
(763, 23, 'In the “Lord’s Prayer,” Jesus taught us to pray “Thy kingdom come” which acknowledges the kingship of Christ.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2017-12-19 07:34:16', '2017-12-19 00:34:16', 1, 1),
(764, 23, 'The “Lord’s Prayer” ends with a doxology.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2017-12-19 07:35:07', '2017-12-19 00:35:07', 1, 1),
(765, 23, 'In Jesus’ High Priestly prayer, He prays only for His disciples.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2017-12-19 07:37:08', '2017-12-19 00:37:08', 1, 1),
(766, 23, 'Worship is essentially service. This type of service is reverential, respectful, adoring, and in awe before God.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2017-12-19 07:38:57', '2017-12-19 00:38:57', 1, 1),
(767, 23, 'The merging of worship and witness means that we give a testimony that is consistent with our walk—we walk our talk.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2017-12-19 07:39:48', '2017-12-19 00:39:48', 1, 1),
(768, 23, 'At the end of the Creation week, God rested from His labors because He was fatigued.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2017-12-19 07:40:38', '2017-12-19 00:40:38', 1, 1),
(769, 23, 'Rest is a sacred symbol in the mind of God, and as believers we should respect that.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2017-12-19 07:41:26', '2017-12-19 00:41:26', 1, 1),
(770, 23, 'The believer’s future rest will be in heaven—the rest from all labor.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2017-12-19 07:42:04', '2017-12-19 00:42:04', 1, 1),
(771, 24, 'The Pastor is a _______________, __________________________, and ______________________________.', 'Shepherd, Father and Friend', 'Elder, Friend and Brother', 'Pastor, Shepherd and Friend', 'Pastor, Elder and Overseer', '', 'Pastor, Elder and Overseer', 0.00, '2018-02-23 00:10:27', '2018-02-22 17:10:27', 1, 1),
(772, 24, 'The important task of a Christian counselor is to _________________________________.', 'Listen and be calm', 'Surprised on every story.', 'Rebuke them and teach them', 'instill Hope', '', 'instill Hope', 0.00, '2018-02-23 00:15:23', '2018-02-22 17:15:23', 1, 1),
(773, 24, 'What actually works during your Counseling session?', 'Knowledge about Word.', 'Experience of your counseling', 'Your personality to handle the issue.', 'Power of God.', '', 'Power of God.', 0.00, '2018-02-23 00:17:05', '2018-02-22 17:17:05', 1, 1),
(774, 24, 'The Acrostic used for Forming and Adopting a Biblical Counseling Model is __________________________.', 'POWER', 'PEACE', 'PREACH', 'PRAYER', '', 'PREACH', 0.00, '2018-02-23 00:33:47', '2018-02-22 17:33:47', 1, 1),
(775, 24, 'Cognitive aspects of Biblical counseling is ______________________________________________________________.', 'Recognition of thoughts and their Effect on the Life.', 'Recognition of responsibility and their works on the life.', 'Recognition of failure and their affects on the life.', 'Recognition of Success and their effects on the life.', '', 'Recognition of thoughts and their Effect on the Life.', 0.00, '2018-02-23 00:46:07', '2018-02-22 17:46:07', 1, 1),
(776, 24, 'Basic epistemological assumption: Human reason is more fundamental, comprehensive, technical and contemporary than _______________________________.', 'Knowledge', 'Faith', 'Revelation', 'Wisdom', '', 'Revelation', 0.00, '2018-02-23 05:13:52', '2018-02-22 22:13:52', 1, 1),
(777, 37, 'The better we are able to understand the language of the Bible, the closer we will come to understanding the message of the Bible.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:17:34', '2018-10-10 21:17:34', 1, 1),
(778, 37, 'Lexical studies focus on the core meanings of words and how they are put together in a sentence to communicate more complex thoughts.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:18:34', '2018-10-10 21:18:34', 1, 1),
(779, 37, 'Etymology means the “shape of words.”', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:19:10', '2018-10-10 21:19:10', 1, 1),
(780, 37, 'Morphology means the “origin and development of words.”', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:19:51', '2018-10-10 21:19:51', 1, 1),
(781, 37, 'In English, a noun is the name of a person, place, or thing. In Greek, the special label for nouns is the case.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:20:29', '2018-10-10 21:20:29', 1, 1),
(782, 37, 'Nouns in Greek have gender.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:21:00', '2018-10-10 21:21:00', 1, 1),
(783, 37, 'The tense of a verb conveys the time referent of the action in the sentence.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:21:43', '2018-10-10 21:21:43', 1, 1),
(784, 37, 'The subjunctive mood of a verb means “a command.”', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:22:11', '2018-10-10 21:22:11', 1, 1),
(785, 37, 'When one studies the meaning of the Greek word for “conformed,” one gets the imagery of a soft wax being pressed into a mold shaped like the “world.”', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:22:49', '2018-10-10 21:22:49', 1, 1),
(786, 37, 'Semantic range refers to “the number of meanings that a word can have over time and in any given setting.”', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:23:22', '2018-10-10 21:23:22', 1, 1),
(787, 37, 'Syntax refers to relationships of words to other words in the sentence.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:23:58', '2018-10-10 21:23:58', 1, 1),
(788, 37, 'Syntax does not help determine if a metaphorical, or nonliteral use of the word is present.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:24:31', '2018-10-10 21:24:31', 1, 1),
(789, 37, 'Parallelism is a syntactical element where the important words in the verse are arranged in an “X” pattern.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:25:08', '2018-10-10 21:25:08', 1, 1),
(790, 37, 'In a Greek sentence, the words that come first carry the most emphasis.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:25:41', '2018-10-10 21:25:41', 1, 1),
(791, 37, 'Syntax of thought involves the interrelationship of thoughts to other thoughts.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:26:13', '2018-10-10 21:26:13', 1, 1),
(792, 37, 'In order to responsibly interpret the Scriptures, one should follow this order: (1) note the overall context, (2) focus on key words, and (3) note ambiguities.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:26:59', '2018-10-10 21:26:59', 1, 1),
(793, 37, 'There are four areas of contextual analyses: (1) historical context, (2) social context, (3) cultural context, and (4) religious context.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:27:36', '2018-10-10 21:27:36', 1, 1),
(794, 37, 'Pragmatics is the study of grammar, syntax, and linguistics.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:28:17', '2018-10-10 21:28:17', 1, 1),
(795, 37, 'There are three worlds which illustrate the history of Biblical studies: (1) the world behind the text, (2) the world within the text, and (3) the world in front of the text.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:28:54', '2018-10-10 21:28:54', 1, 1),
(796, 37, 'Sitz im Leben is the “setting-in-life of the text.”', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:29:24', '2018-10-10 21:29:24', 1, 1),
(797, 37, 'Christianity was born in the womb of Judaism.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:29:55', '2018-10-10 21:29:55', 1, 1),
(798, 37, 'The event which had the greatest effect on Jewish history (not recorded in either the Old or New Testaments) was the military conquests of Julius Caesar.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:30:30', '2018-10-10 21:30:30', 1, 1),
(799, 37, 'The following are prominent people groups in Judaism: Pharisees, Sadducees, Essenes, Zealots, and Herodians.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:31:04', '2018-10-10 21:31:04', 1, 1),
(800, 37, 'Rabbinical literature is constituted by three main literary works: (1) The Mishnah, (2) The Talmud, and (3) The Midrashim.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:33:54', '2018-10-10 21:33:54', 1, 1),
(801, 37, 'There is ambiguity surrounding the author of the Fourth Gospel.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:34:24', '2018-10-10 21:34:24', 1, 1),
(802, 37, 'The Ras Shamra texts is an example of Old Testament comparative literature.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:34:53', '2018-10-10 21:34:53', 1, 1),
(803, 37, 'Stoicism is a philosophy of Cicero.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:35:21', '2018-10-10 21:35:21', 1, 1),
(804, 37, 'A primary principle of interpretation during the Apostolic period was being able to show literal fulfillment of Old Testament prophecy.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:35:55', '2018-10-10 21:35:55', 1, 1),
(805, 37, 'The first letter from Paul to the Corinthians is not the canonical 1 Corinthians.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:36:24', '2018-10-10 21:36:24', 1, 1),
(806, 37, 'Corinth was at one time a Greek city-state and then was reestablished as a Roman colony by Nero in 44 B.C.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:36:57', '2018-10-10 21:36:57', 1, 1),
(807, 37, '1 Corinthians: (1) whether to eat meat offered to an idol, (2) whether to eat at a temple of a false god, and (3) matters concerning the Lord’s Supper.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:37:35', '2018-10-10 21:37:35', 1, 1),
(808, 37, 'Paul had a philosophy of ministry, but he did not have a definite missionary strategy.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:38:09', '2018-10-10 21:38:09', 1, 1),
(809, 37, 'The following are all examples of the diversity of Biblical literature: narratives, law codes, poetry, letters.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:39:36', '2018-10-10 21:39:36', 1, 1),
(810, 37, 'At times, God inspired through the use of a secretary; for example, Jeremiah’s secretary, Baruch.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:41:01', '2018-10-10 21:41:01', 1, 1),
(811, 37, 'God never wrote Scripture with His own hand.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:41:32', '2018-10-10 21:41:32', 1, 1),
(812, 37, 'Scripture is God’s Word and therefore it cannot be properly interpreted, preached, taught, or applied without the present ministry of the Holy Spirit.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:42:08', '2018-10-10 21:42:08', 1, 1),
(813, 37, 'The majority of Pentecostals are located in the margins of society, but they constitute 21 percent of organized global Christianity.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:42:42', '2018-10-10 21:42:42', 1, 1),
(814, 37, 'The initial phase of Pentecostalism was dubbed “Classical Pentecostalism.”', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:43:15', '2018-10-10 21:43:15', 1, 1),
(815, 37, 'The next phase of Pentecostalism was called the “Third Wave.”', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:43:43', '2018-10-10 21:43:43', 1, 1),
(816, 37, 'There are five principal motifs of Pentecostal theology. They are (1) justification by faith, (2) sanctification by faith as a second definite work of grace, (3) baptism in the Holy Spirit, evidenced by speaking in tongues, (4) healing of the body, provided in the Atonement, and (5) the premillennial return of Christ.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:44:54', '2018-10-10 21:44:54', 1, 1),
(817, 37, 'Theology means “study of God.” Therefore, when reading Scripture theologically, the reader/believer is encountering the living God.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:46:00', '2018-10-10 21:46:00', 1, 1),
(818, 37, 'When a Pentecostal reads the Scripture, he reads with an eye open toward the plain meaning of Scripture; he is never open to multiple meanings in the texts or meanings that might show him something new.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:46:50', '2018-10-10 21:46:50', 1, 1),
(819, 37, 'The expectation of the return of Christ is paramount in Pentecostal theology.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:47:27', '2018-10-10 21:47:27', 1, 1),
(820, 37, 'When John wishes to identify the literary genre of the Book of Revelation, he refers to it as a prophecy.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:48:01', '2018-10-10 21:48:01', 1, 1),
(821, 37, 'Pentecostals accept the Bible by faith as the Word of God which will speak directly to their lives.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:48:40', '2018-10-10 21:48:40', 1, 1),
(822, 37, 'The fear of the Lord is at least an initial requirement in the interpretation of Scripture for Pentecostals. They believe they will encounter God when they read the Bible.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:49:14', '2018-10-10 21:49:14', 1, 1),
(823, 37, 'The greatest witness to the truth of the Bible comes from an academic argument alone.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'False', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:49:43', '2018-10-10 21:49:43', 1, 1),
(824, 37, 'The Incarnation tells us that Christ came to be a sacrificial offering.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:50:10', '2018-10-10 21:50:10', 1, 1),
(825, 37, 'In defense of the Bible as a complete canon, one could ask the following question: “What new revelation could possibly add anything of importance to the present content of the Bible?”', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:50:37', '2018-10-10 21:50:37', 1, 1),
(826, 37, 'The Bible is the instrument of salvation.', 'True', 'False', '', '', '', 'True', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:50:57', '2018-10-10 21:50:57', 1, 1),
(827, 38, 'It is in the __________________of the Word of God that we find the answers to life’s toughest questions.', 'Poetry', 'Authority', 'Prophecy', 'Drama', '', 'Authority', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:53:31', '2018-10-10 21:53:31', 1, 1),
(828, 38, 'The Bible is all the following except_____________.', 'The divine source of doctrine', 'A means of divine reproof', 'A text of instruction in righteousness ', 'A textbook to be used when studying mythology and gods', '', 'A textbook to be used when studying mythology and gods', 0.00, '2018-10-11 04:55:38', '2018-10-10 21:55:38', 1, 1),
(829, 38, 'God’s Word has the authority to require_____________of its readers.', 'Obedience ', 'Poetry', 'Drama', 'None of the above', '', 'Obedience ', 0.00, '2018-10-11 05:06:13', '2018-10-10 22:06:13', 1, 1),
(830, 38, 'Referring to the Word of God, ___________said “it is the power of God to salvation.”', 'Jesus', 'Matthew', 'Paul', 'John', '', 'Paul', 0.00, '2018-10-11 05:06:59', '2018-10-10 22:06:59', 1, 1),
(831, 38, 'When interpreting the Word of God, one should ask all the following questions except___.', 'Did God expect me to read this?', 'What does this text mean?', 'What does this text mean to me?', 'What does this text mean to my congregation or to my class?', '', 'Did God expect me to read this?', 0.00, '2018-10-11 05:08:45', '2018-10-10 22:08:45', 1, 1),
(832, 38, 'All of the following are barriers to understanding when interpreting the Word of God except_____________.', 'Language', 'Culture', 'Tradition', 'Body Language', '', 'Body Language', 0.00, '2018-10-11 05:09:52', '2018-10-10 22:09:52', 1, 1),
(833, 38, 'Hermeneutics is a ________________, with principles that govern the process of interpretation.', 'Humanities', 'Science', 'Religion', 'Form of music', '', 'Science', 0.00, '2018-10-11 05:10:55', '2018-10-10 22:10:55', 1, 1),
(834, 38, 'Hermeneutics can be considered as_____________for Biblical interpretation.', 'Principles', 'Principals', 'Ideas', 'Illustrations', '', 'Principles', 0.00, '2018-10-11 10:14:57', '2018-10-11 03:14:57', 1, 1),
(835, 38, 'All the following are considered common abuses and weaknesses when interpreting the Bible except________________.', 'A consistent hermeneutical system of beliefs', 'Excessive use of symbolic approaches', 'A desire for novelty in preaching', 'A lack of training in Biblical languages and literature', '', 'A consistent hermeneutical system of beliefs', 0.00, '2018-10-11 10:22:07', '2018-10-11 03:22:07', 1, 1),
(836, 38, 'Emphases to bring to the interpretation of Scripture are the following five “H’s.”', 'Holiness, heart, hope, Holy Spirit, healing', 'Holiness, heart, hope, Holy Spirit, hearing', 'Holiness, heart, heaven, Holy Spirit, hearing', 'Holiness, heart, hope, Holy Spirit, homiletics', '', 'Holiness, heart, hope, Holy Spirit, hearing', 0.00, '2018-10-11 10:23:26', '2018-10-11 03:23:26', 1, 1),
(837, 38, 'Biblical interpretation involves not only the intellect but also the_________________.', 'Id', 'Olfactory senses', 'Affections', 'None of the above', '', 'Affections', 0.00, '2018-10-11 10:24:21', '2018-10-11 03:24:21', 1, 1),
(838, 38, 'After Pentecost, we are no longer spectators to the plan of God, we are_____________ in it.', 'Planners', 'Designers', 'Bystanders', 'Participants', '', 'Participants', 0.00, '2018-10-11 10:25:24', '2018-10-11 03:25:24', 1, 1),
(839, 38, 'Jewish tradition gives the honor to ____________of being the first Biblical interpreter.', 'Esther', 'Ezra', 'Eli', 'Enoch', '', 'Ezra', 0.00, '2018-10-11 10:27:34', '2018-10-11 03:27:34', 1, 1),
(840, 38, 'There are three motivations which are central to the writing of the Pentateuch. They are______.', 'The uniqueness of Israel’s God; the character of the covenant; the holiness of God.', 'The uniqueness of Israel’s God; the character of the ark; the holiness of God.', 'The uniqueness of Israel’s God; the character of Jacob’s vision; the holiness of God.', 'The uniqueness of Israel’s God; the character of Adam; the holiness of God.', '', 'The uniqueness of Israel’s God; the character of the covenant; the holiness of God.', 0.00, '2018-10-11 10:28:51', '2018-10-11 03:28:51', 1, 1),
(841, 38, 'A comprehensive________cannot be written.', 'Pentateuch', 'Musical Score', 'Law', 'None of the above', '', 'Law', 0.00, '2018-10-11 10:29:41', '2018-10-11 03:29:41', 1, 1),
(842, 38, 'God’s Word applies to___________.', 'The Jews', 'The generation of the Old Testament', 'The generation of the New Testament', 'Every generation', '', 'Every generation', 0.00, '2018-10-11 10:30:51', '2018-10-11 03:30:51', 1, 1),
(843, 38, 'One principle suggested by reinterpretation is that “there is a____________in the\r\naccuracy of predictive prophecy.', 'Doubt', 'Trust', 'Legacy', 'Uniqueness', '', 'Trust', 0.00, '2018-10-11 10:36:14', '2018-10-11 03:36:14', 1, 1),
(844, 38, 'Looking at the historical record of the Bible, we see a prophetic view of history from\r\nwhich of the following two perspectives?', 'Horizontal and Vertical', 'Horizontal and Aerial', 'Aerial and Earthly', 'Vertical and Earthly', '', 'Horizontal and Vertical', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:13:28', '2018-10-15 19:13:28', 1, 1),
(845, 38, 'When the prophets read the patriarchal history, they saw the personal events in the lives\r\nof the patriarchs as ________________events.', 'Renaissance', 'Postmodern', 'Theological', 'Modern', '', 'Theological', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:14:27', '2018-10-15 19:14:27', 1, 1),
(846, 38, 'All deliverances are symbolized in the______________.', 'Exile', 'Apocalypse', 'Feast of Lights (Hanukkah)', 'Exodus', '', 'Exodus', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:15:51', '2018-10-15 19:15:51', 1, 1),
(847, 38, 'All the following are uses of the Old Testament in the New Testament\r\nexcept__________', 'Referring to Old Testament people, authors, or events', 'Referring to the time of the Maccabees', 'Referring to Old Testament narratives', 'Instructional use of the Old Testament in the Epistles', '', 'Referring to the time of the Maccabees', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:17:41', '2018-10-15 19:17:41', 1, 1),
(848, 38, 'Typology regards scriptures as factual. All the following statements are true\r\nexcept_____.', 'God uses typology for purposes of prediction.', 'Typology can be a person, such as Aaron who was a type of Christ as a priest.', 'Typology is the excavation of ancient ruins.', 'Typology can be an event, such as the ark was a type of salvation through Jesus.', '', 'Typology is the excavation of ancient ruins.', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:18:42', '2018-10-15 19:18:42', 1, 1),
(849, 38, 'All of the following reflect the permanence and literalness of God’s covenant with David\r\nexcept_________.', 'Solomon', 'Jeremiah', 'Amos', 'Abraham', '', 'Abraham', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:19:23', '2018-10-15 19:19:23', 1, 1),
(850, 38, '______________is the fulfillment of the Davidic promise.', 'Jesus', 'Solomon', 'John the Baptist', 'Elijah', '', 'Jesus', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:20:11', '2018-10-15 19:20:11', 1, 1),
(851, 38, 'The Qumran community interpreted the Scripture according to their own community.\r\nThey lived during the____________time period.', 'Modern', 'Postmodern', 'Premodern', 'None of the Above', '', 'Premodern', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:20:56', '2018-10-15 19:20:56', 1, 1),
(852, 38, 'Rebekah drawing water from the well could be saying that we need to go to the well of\r\nthe Holy Spirit to find Jesus Christ. This is an example of___________.', 'Proverb', 'Allegory', 'Metaphor', 'Simile', '', 'Allegory', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:21:38', '2018-10-15 19:21:38', 1, 1),
(853, 38, 'Interpretation in the Middle Ages was tradition-centered and fourfold. All the following\r\nare part of the fourfold interpretation except_________.', 'Literal', 'Allegorical', 'Moral', 'Alliteration', '', 'Alliteration', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:22:19', '2018-10-15 19:22:19', 1, 1),
(854, 38, 'In the postmodern period, all the following are true except_________.', 'Science has been questioned', 'The Bible is not the center of attention, rather the reader of the Bible is the center of attention', 'There is not just one meaning of truth or Scripture, but multiple meanings.', 'Postmoderns are interested in preserving the true meaning of the Bible.', '', 'Postmoderns are interested in preserving the true meaning of the Bible.', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:23:21', '2018-10-15 19:23:21', 1, 1),
(855, 38, 'The inductive study method includes the following__________.', 'Observe the facts in the text', 'Interpret the meaning of the text', 'Apply the message of the text', 'All the above', '', 'All the above', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:24:16', '2018-10-15 19:24:16', 1, 1),
(856, 38, 'When one is observing the facts in the text, he should read the entire book___________.', 'At one sitting', 'At least three times', 'Both A & B', 'Only A', '', 'Both A & B', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:25:08', '2018-10-15 19:25:08', 1, 1),
(857, 38, 'When reading the book a second time, one should do all the following except_______.', 'Outline the book', 'Determine the genre', 'Look for the cultural traditions', 'Look for religious symbolism', '', 'Outline the book', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:26:03', '2018-10-15 19:26:03', 1, 1),
(858, 38, 'When reading the book a third time, one should do all the following except_________.', 'Determine the author’s intent', 'Outline the book', 'Observe facts', 'Relate the context of this book with the whole Bible.', '', 'Observe facts', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:26:59', '2018-10-15 19:26:59', 1, 1),
(859, 38, 'Semantic patterns, literary patterns, theological patterns are all things one should look for\r\nwhen doing a ____________reading of an entire book.', 'First', 'Third', 'Second', 'Fourth', '', 'Third', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:27:35', '2018-10-15 19:27:35', 1, 1),
(860, 38, 'Outlining a book should be done during the___________reading of the entire book.', 'First ', 'Second', 'Third', 'Not at all', '', 'Third', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:29:48', '2018-10-15 19:29:48', 1, 1),
(861, 38, 'When interpreting a narrative in the Bible, one should look at four basic elements: plot,\r\ncharacterization, setting, and_____________.', 'Point of View', 'Figure of speech', 'Date', 'High Point', '', 'Point of View', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:31:40', '2018-10-15 19:31:40', 1, 1),
(862, 38, 'The final element of the plot is the_________________.', 'Rising tension', 'Climax', 'Denouement', 'Conflict', '', 'Denouement', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:33:47', '2018-10-15 19:33:47', 1, 1),
(863, 38, 'All of the following are literary devices contained in the narrative\r\nexcept______________.', 'Imagery', 'Tone', 'Poetic justice', 'Plot', '', 'Plot', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:34:28', '2018-10-15 19:34:28', 1, 1),
(864, 38, 'There are three kinds of words to study when doing a word study. They are__________.', 'Significant words, ambiguous words, paradoxical words', 'Significant words, ambiguous words, theological words', 'Significant words, ambiguous words, ironic words', 'Significant words, ambiguous words, foreign words', '', 'Significant words, ambiguous words, theological words', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:35:28', '2018-10-15 19:35:28', 1, 1),
(865, 38, 'The ultimate goal of a Bible study is______________________.', 'To take the application and present it to the people.', 'To make yourself more aware of Biblical history.', 'To enhance your own knowledge of Greek influences.', 'To expand your own knowledge of literary devices used in narratives.', '', 'To take the application and present it to the people.', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:36:21', '2018-10-15 19:36:21', 1, 1),
(866, 38, 'Comparison/Contrast is where two or more ideas are developed in an alternating pattern, according to similarity or dissimilarity. All the following are examples of comparison/contrast except______________.', 'Adam to Christ', 'Simon the Pharisee to the sinful woman', 'Story of Creation to the Lord’s Prayer', 'The works of the flesh to the fruit of the Spirit', '', 'Story of Creation to the Lord’s Prayer', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:38:48', '2018-10-15 19:38:48', 1, 1),
(867, 38, 'The core concept of “Rightly Dividing the Word” is___________________.', 'Communication', 'Observation', 'Alliteration', 'Poetic Justice', '', 'Communication', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:40:24', '2018-10-15 19:40:24', 1, 1),
(868, 38, 'There are two major elements in “rightly dividing the Word.” They are______________.', 'Divine accommodation and discernment', 'Divine accommodation and Spirit-inspired interpretation', 'Divine accommodation and speaking in tongues', 'Divine accommodation and a knowledge of Greek', '', 'Divine accommodation and Spirit-inspired interpretation', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:41:11', '2018-10-15 19:41:11', 1, 1),
(869, 38, 'The transcendent mind of God accommodated our human limitations by way of\r\n_______________________________.', 'Divine Revelation', 'Symbols', 'Narratives', 'None of the Above', '', 'Divine Revelation', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:41:50', '2018-10-15 19:41:50', 1, 1),
(870, 38, 'The following figure of speech is an example of a simile___________.', 'God is a burning fire.', 'Jesus is the Bread of life.', '“For as the rain cometh down . . . so shall my word be.”', '“The trees went forth on a time to anoint a king over them.”', '', '“For as the rain cometh down . . . so shall my word be.”', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:42:44', '2018-10-15 19:42:44', 1, 1);
INSERT INTO `objective_questions` (`id`, `exam_id`, `question`, `option1`, `option2`, `option3`, `option4`, `answer_option`, `answer`, `marks`, `updated_at`, `created_at`, `created_by`, `updated_by`) VALUES
(871, 38, 'The following figure of speech is an example of a metaphor____________.', '“The kingdom of God is like . . .”', '“There were two men in one city', '“But the olive tree said unto them . . .”', '“Ye are the salt of the earth.”', '', '“Ye are the salt of the earth.”', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:43:59', '2018-10-15 19:43:59', 1, 1),
(872, 38, 'Paul says that we are “the body of Christ.” This is an example of what figure of speech?', 'Metaphor', 'Simile', 'Parable', 'Proverb', '', 'Metaphor', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:44:42', '2018-10-15 19:44:42', 1, 1),
(873, 38, 'All of the following are types of parables except______________.', 'Judgment', 'Kingdom', 'Apocalyptic', 'Growth', '', 'Apocalyptic', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:45:25', '2018-10-15 19:45:25', 1, 1),
(874, 38, 'As a literary genre, proverbs are classified as___________________.', 'Drama', 'Wisdom Literature', 'Narrative', 'Gospel', '', 'Wisdom Literature', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:46:12', '2018-10-15 19:46:12', 1, 1),
(875, 38, 'The following four areas are all principles of interpretation of the proverbs:', 'Scriptural context; social and cultural contexts; balance; metaphor.', 'Scriptural context; social and cultural contexts; balance; alliteration.', 'Scriptural context; social and cultural contexts; balance; plot.', 'Scriptural context; social and cultural contexts; balance; climax.', '', 'Scriptural context; social and cultural contexts; balance; metaphor.', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:47:00', '2018-10-15 19:47:00', 1, 1),
(876, 38, 'Allegory consists of a series of__________joined together by a common theme or story.\r\nEach item in the allegory stands for something in particular.', 'Similes', 'Metaphors', 'Types', 'Proverbs', '', 'Types', 0.00, '2018-10-16 02:47:42', '2018-10-15 19:47:42', 1, 1),
(877, 66, 'In a time of crisis, people usually go first to their____________.', 'Secular counselor', 'Pastor', 'Psychic Reader', 'Neighbors', 'option2', 'Pastor', 0.00, '2019-11-21 03:24:39', '2019-11-20 20:24:39', 1, 1),
(878, 66, '_____________is our model for attending behavior.', 'Jesus', 'Sigmund Freud', 'Carl Rogers', 'Neighbors', 'option1', 'Jesus', 0.00, '2019-11-21 03:24:39', '2019-11-20 20:24:39', 1, 1),
(879, 66, '“Rewording or rephrasing the essence of what has been said” is the definition for______.', 'Attending Behaviour', 'Empathy', 'Clarification', 'prarphrasing', 'option4', 'prarphrasing', 0.00, '2019-11-21 03:24:39', '2019-11-20 20:24:39', 1, 1),
(880, 66, '“Communicating your understanding of the counselee’s feelings” is the definition for____.', 'Empathy', 'Sympathy', 'Reflection', 'Paraphrasing', 'option3', 'Reflection', 0.00, '2019-11-21 03:24:39', '2019-11-20 20:24:39', 1, 1),
(881, 66, 'One rule of counseling is “Speak___________; listen a lot.', 'Boldly', 'Extensively', 'Little', 'Distinctly', 'option3', 'Little', 0.00, '2019-11-21 03:24:39', '2019-11-20 20:24:39', 1, 1),
