(3503, 1, '2017-05-18 16:30:25', '2017-05-18 20:30:25', '[vc_row content_placement=\"top\" parallax=\"content-moving\" parallax_image=\"3291\" u_row_style=\"1\" u_row_paralax=\"0\" u_row_scheme=\"1\"][vc_column][u_heading]Graduate Certificate in Ministry[/u_heading][vc_column_text]<span style=\"color: #000000;\">The Graduate Certificate in Ministry is a One-year Bible <a style=\"color: #000000;\" href=\"http://www.frit.org.in/graduate.html\" target=\"_blank\">training program.</a> The aim of the graduate certificate is to equip candidates with a non-theology background to prepare themselves for postgraduate study as a means of developing research skills appropriate to theology and divinity. The Graduate Certificate of Ministry requires 16 credit points for graduation. The aim of the course is to guide students in a systematic manner to the acquisition of the body of coherent knowledge that is the classical discipline of theology as a means not only of preparing men and women for the responsibility of communicating Christian knowledge but also for advanced <a style=\"color: #000000;\" href=\"http://www.frit.org.in/graduate.html\" target=\"_blank\">degrees in</a> theology and ministry.</span>\n\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\">In addition consideration will also be given to other factors such as maturity and motivation, and the likelihood of satisfactory completion of the <a style=\"color: #000000;\" href=\"http://www.frit.org.in/graduate.html\" target=\"_blank\">academic requirements</a> of the course. Students may articulate to the Graduate Diploma of Divinity or Graduate of Divinity or Master of Divinity.</span>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Admission Requirements</span></h3>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\">The Graduate Diploma provides a two-year <a style=\"color: #000000;\" href=\"http://www.frit.org.in/graduate.html\" target=\"_blank\">program of study</a> for all who has <a style=\"color: #000000;\" href=\"http://elittee.com/trinity/certificate-program/#\">completed</a> 12th Standard with no formal qualifications in theology, Plus…One year of Ministry experience</span>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Or</span></h3>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\">Graduate in any discipline</span>[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_column_text]\n<h3>Graduate Certificate in Ministry</h3>\nThe Graduate Certificate in Ministry is a One-year Bible <a href=\"http://www.frit.org.in/graduate.html\" target=\"_blank\">training program.</a> The aim of the graduate certificate is to equip candidates with a non-theology background to prepare themselves for postgraduate study as a means of developing research skills appropriate to theology and divinity. The Graduate Certificate of Ministry requires 16 credit points for graduation. The aim of the course is to guide students in a systematic manner to the acquisition of the body of coherent knowledge that is the classical discipline of theology as a means not only of preparing men and women for the responsibility of communicating Christian knowledge but also for advanced <a href=\"http://www.frit.org.in/graduate.html\" target=\"_blank\">degrees in</a> theology and ministry.\n\nIn addition consideration will also be given to other factors such as maturity and motivation, and the likelihood of satisfactory completion of the <a href=\"http://www.frit.org.in/graduate.html\" target=\"_blank\">academic requirements</a> of the course. Students may articulate to the Graduate Diploma of Divinity or Graduate of Divinity or Master of Divinity.\n<h3>CURRICULUM OF GRADUATE DIPLOMA IN MINISTRY</h3>\n<h4>YEAR 1</h4>\n<table class=\"doc_list\" border=\"0\" width=\"930\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" bgcolor=\"#578a9d\" width=\"640\"><strong>1st SEMESTER</strong></td>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" bgcolor=\"#578a9d\" width=\"290\"><strong>Credit Hours</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"640\">ntroduction to Old Testament</td>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"290\">4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"640\">Introduction to New Testament</td>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"290\">4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"640\">Life &amp; Ministry of Jesus Christ</td>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"290\">4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"640\">Book of Acts</td>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"290\">3</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table class=\"doc_list\" border=\"0\" width=\"930\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" bgcolor=\"#578a9d\" width=\"640\"><strong>2nd SEMESTER</strong></td>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" bgcolor=\"#578a9d\" width=\"290\"><strong>Credit Hours</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"640\">Contemporary trends in Mission</td>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"290\">3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"640\">Major World Religions</td>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"290\">3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"640\">Theology 1</td>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"290\">20</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"640\"><strong style=\"color: #000;\">TOTAL CREDIT HOURS</strong></td>\n<td align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"290\"><strong style=\"color: #000;\">41</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h4>Admission Requirements</h4>\nThe Graduate Diploma provides a two-year <a href=\"http://www.frit.org.in/graduate.html\" target=\"_blank\">program of study</a> for all who has <a href=\"#\">completed</a> 12th Standard with no formal qualifications in theology, Plus...One year of Ministry experience\n<h3>Or</h3>\nGraduate in any discipline[/vc_column_text][/vc_column][/vc_row]', 'Certificate Program', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '2928-autosave-v1', '', '', '2017-05-18 16:30:25', '2017-05-18 20:30:25', '', 2928, 'http://elittee.com/trinity/2928-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
